window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_FEY_EVOLUTION_MERCHANT_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":2701,"title":"Chapter 2701 Breakthrough!","paragraphs":["2701 Breakthrough!","However, all 12 of them had the same thought: it was impossible for a leopard to change its spots. As long as they remained rulers of the Freedom Federation, their ruthless natures could resurface at any time.","It was unlikely that the rest of the Freedom Federation’s royalty would listen to the Mirror God and God of Fools now that their power did not threaten them.","The Freedom Federation had planted the seed of its downfall long ago. It was hard to change its trajectory once the seed had been planted.","The heads of the Azure Federation’s 12 aristocratic families had another reason for gathering in the Radiance Federation aside from showing their respect to the Moon Empress.","Now that the Freedom Federation was under the Radiance Federation’s control, there was no question that the Radiance Federation would supply more resources to the Freedom Federation.","This was understandable. If they were the ones calling the shots, they would also divert more resources to the factions under their control.","The Azure Federation had no means of resisting the dead spirits crisis.","Given that they needed to be fully reliant on the Radiance Federation, the best course of action would be to submit.","The heads of the Azure Federation’s 12 aristocratic families were prepared to offer their loyalty to the Radiance Federation.","After the second Major Federation Union meeting ended, the 12 of them sought a private audience with the Moon Empress.","The Moon Empress was not at all surprised by this.","Frankly, she had been waiting a month for them to do this. They were offering their loyalty later than she had expected.","It was not just the Azure Federation. Many federation leaders who were part of the Major Federation Union decided to ally with the Radiance Federation by becoming its subsidiaries.","The Radiance Federation had become the heart of the human territories and strategies.","The Moon Empress did not have a lot of time to facilitate the Radiance Federation’s adjustment of these federations’ mindsets.","However, now that they were in the midst of the disaster that was the dead spirits crisis, the Radiance Federation maintained this model of interaction with the other federations. This would ensure that after receiving resources, these federations would do their best to work with the Radiance Federation to tackle the dead spirits crisis.","...","The Radiance Hundred Sequence selection was still ongoing.","None of the teams had reached the main area and joined a leader.","However, almost a day had passed. According to the schedule of the test, the dead spirits crisis had officially begun.","One after another, Dead Spirits Wells popped up in the test ground. An ocean of dead spirits burst out from the Dead Spirits Wells and began spreading out in all directions. Among their ranks were dead dimensional lifeforms that injected death aura into the ground and contaminated the earth.","The concentration of death aura in the air was so high that it almost seemed as though the air had solidified.","The vast ocean of dead spirits stunned the Star Web audience.","Both low-rank spirit qi professionals and regular people did not have the chance to witness such a sight in their daily lives. During the dead spirits crisis, they could only stock up on resources and seek protection from stronger experts.","The setting of this Radiance Hundred Sequence selection allowed those who did not have the opportunity to interact with the dead spirits directly to understand the true horrors of the dead spirits crisis.","Aside from shock, the spectators also felt incredibly glad and powerful. They were lucky to have the members of royalty protecting the Radiance Federation.","The Spirit and City Guards were also dedicated to protecting the citizens and tirelessly fought the dead spirits. All of the spectators’ level of respect and admiration for the Radiance Federation’s troops reached a new high.","The audience was watching from the outside and was in a state of frenzy.","However, those in the midst of the dead spirits crisis had been negatively affected by the explosion of dead spirits, regardless of whether they had directly encountered the dead spirits. The explosive wave of dead spirits caused the participants to be submerged in death aura.","Due to the difference in each person’s physiques, the members of Yang Nuanxin’s team all had different resistance to death aura.","Previously, those with weaker resistances were still able to barely hold on. But now, all of them were showing clear signs of deterioration. Their faces were pale, and blood seeped out of their eyes, noses, and ears.","Yang Nuanxin was extremely resistant to the death aura because of the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane. Although the concentration of death aura was higher than before, she could endure because the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane cleansed the air around her.","The other two spirit qi professionals who were slightly capable of cleaning death aura from the environment were unquestionably outdone by Yang Nuanxin. The area covered by the rain summoned by the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane was completely clean.","This resulted in competition arising in the team of more than 1,000 people. Every single one of them hoped to be nearer to Yang Nuanxin. The area covered by the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane became a resource that the people on the team needed to fight over.","Previously, Yang Wenpeng saw Yang Nuanxin as nothing more than a brat from a collateral branch of his family that he could dictate as he pleased.","Yang Wenpeng gathered all of his close comrades in the team before instructing Yang Nuanxin and the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane to stick with him.","Yang Nuanxin was extremely unwilling to do that. There was no doubt that she preferred her friends over Yang Wenpeng and his close subordinates.","They took care of her when she was still in school, and she received significant help from them.","Now that she was capable, she definitely preferred to help them.","At first, Yang Wenpeng only wanted her to join his team.","The two teams only united because Du Xing made a concession.","The people from Du Xing’s team were already extremely upset with Yang Wenpeng’s actions.","In the half a day that he had been leading them, he had forced all of the work of doing combat and clearing the dead spirits out of their path to the people who were originally from the other team.","He would only continue doing the same during the latter portion of the dead spirits crisis.","All of them were members of the younger generation who were participating in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. The level of their power did not differ greatly.","Yang Wenpeng’s actions incited the rage of many members of the team.","The strapping young man next to Du Xing roared, “Yang Wenpeng, just how shameless are you? Is this how you’re going to lead the team!?","“The Cleansing Rain Sky Crane can lower the concentration of death aura in the environment by bringing forth a shower of rain. But you are only keeping the rain over yourself. The death aura is harming the other members of the team!","“There are many members from your team who are going to collapse at any time. Can’t you see them?”","Yu Rui abhorred wickedness. There was nothing he detested more than injustice.","Yu Rui was Yang Nuanxin’s teammate, and he felt uncomfortable seeing her being forced into a corner.","He knew that saying something now would lead to conflict blooming within the team. There was also a high possibility that the spectators would think of him as short-sighted and narrow-minded.","However, he could not hold on anymore!","Immediately after Yu Rui spoke, ten more members echoed their own displeasure.","Once unhappiness was triggered, it would grow and spread swiftly.","Du Xing was also displeased with Yang Wenpeng’s actions. He resented Yang Wenpeng with his entire being.","Still, it could be said that compared to Yu Rui, Du Xing had a better sight of the big picture.","Du Xing knew that this test involved all of them doing their best to battle the dead spirits.","Any infighting in a team would lead to horrible effects. There was a high chance that this would result in the complete destruction of the team.","Du Xing was about to say something to stop the storm from brewing when he heard a voice with an instigating tone say, “It’s true that the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane is not spreading road over the entire team but only the few hundred people at the center. I agree that the Yang team is being selfish. But we have to understand where they are coming from.","“They have also made significant contributions in order to lead us. Otherwise, we wouldn’t have been able to kill all the dead spirits from the second group we encountered!”","Wei Haodong was the one who had spoken.","He sounded as though he was trying to play the role of the peacemaker, but he was essentially speaking nonsense.","It was easy to ask them to understand where Yang Wenpeng was coming from. But how were they actually supposed to do that? All of them were competitors. They were rushing to the key areas together so they could look out for each other. It was not truly because they wanted to be led by someone.","The first few statements were not sufficient to cause widespread discontent. But what Wei Haodong said made Yang Wenpeng into enemy number one.","The second wave of dead spirits had been ferocious, and there were far more dead spirits than in the previous wave.","Frankly, battling the waves of dead spirits did not necessarily have to lead to such a result.","There were a few spirit qi professionals in the team who were skilled at scouting. All of them had already used their feys to clearly investigate the environment.","They had discovered the presence of dead spirits and reported this to Yang Wenpeng. He could have instructed the team to avoid the dead spirits.","However, Yang Wenpeng wanted to exhibit his heroism and insisted on leading his team into the fray of dead spirits.","This had caused more than 400 members to lose their lives and be eliminated from the selection.","Yang Wenpeng’s authority was thereby shaken.","This was fine when there was no internal conflict. However, once conflict arose, it would cause Yang Wenpeng to run up against resistance.","“Yang Wenpeng, you only managed to become the leader because you are one of the older people on the team. When the team was formed, you were part of it and fought for the leadership position.","“This is not because of your strength but because of the trust that others put in you. However, you have let us down! Since you don’t care whether we live or die, we should just get rid of you.”","As more and more voices of disgruntlement rose, Wei Haodong’s lips curled, and he remained silent.","Since he had already stirred up the winds of discontent, saying something else now would make him as stupid as Yang Wenpeng.","Du Xing frowned at Wei Haodong. This was the second time that Du Xing was seeing Wei Haodong drive a wedge between members of the team.","Although Wei Haodong’s action seemed smart, it could not be any dumber. He was even a larger cancerous tumor to the team than Yang Wenpeng was.","Moreover, Wei Haodong could only play tricks and was not actually intelligent.","Since Du Xing was able to see through Wei Haodong’s actions, the Star Web audience had an even better view.","Even if there was only a small group of people watching his team and who had noticed Wei Haodong, news of what he did would spread quickly.","Du Xing really wanted to know how Wei Haodong felt when he found out that his careful scheming had entrapped himself and caused his rating on Star Web to be tanked.","Wei Haodong had accurately grasped Yang Wenpeng’s bad-tempered personality. After being publicly challenged by so many people, he would definitely blow his top!","It was just as Wei Haodong expected.","Yang Wenpeng immediately summoned his two main feys.","Two black and muscular leopards with sleek bodies appeared in front of him before releasing two ear-splitting roars.","The two leopard-species feys released the aura of Platinum/Fantasy feys.","Yang Wenpeng’s power could be considered top-notch amongst the participants of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. He was also naturally gifted.","Otherwise, he would not have been able to comprehend two Willpower Runes despite only being a little over 20 years old.","However, this did not give any advantage to him during this test.","Night Leaning Moon just happened to be watching Yang Wenpeng’s team.","When she saw that he, as the team’s leader, had summoned his feys to threaten his team members, Night Leaning Moon said seriously, “Go and check how this person managed to gain eligibility to participate in the selection. How could he fill a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence with such a character?","“Go and check on the one who started the commotion as well. It looks like we need to tighten our restrictions on the Radiance Hundred Sequence’s eligibility criteria!”","The people in this team were weak and exhausted. Many of them were covered with injuries.","All of them were in a ‘lone wolf’ state.","In such a state, their mental conditions were very sensitive, and they lost a lot of confidence in the test.","Many of them were not threatened by Yang Wenpeng. Instead, they summoned their own main feys in order to protect themselves.","The members of the teams who benefited from sticking with Yang Wenpeng had no choice but to help him and ensure that he remained the leader after this conflict ended.","Wei Haodong, the instigator, blended into the crowd.","Du Xing let out a sigh.","The waves of dead spirits had already popped up all over the test ground. The best evidence of this was the rising concentration of death aura in the air.","This was the worst time for such conflict to break out.","Du Xing said reproachfully, “The waves of dead spirits have already appeared. We are joining forces to look out for each other during the journey and give each other the best chances of surviving until we make it as the final candidates.","“Don’t lose sight of our initial goal! This conflict is getting in the way of our journey. The wave of dead spirits could drown us at any time!”"]},{"number":2702,"title":"Chapter 2702 Surging Dead Spirits!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2702 Surging Dead Spirits!","One of the main motivations for Du Xing’s action was his sense of responsibility. He had been the leader of the team that later joined forces with Yang Wenpeng’s team.","There was not much that Du Xing’s team could have done, given the strength in numbers that Yang Wenpeng’s team had.","But now, Du Xing needed to take responsibility for the team that he had decided would join Yang Wenpeng’s team.","Otherwise, he would never be sticking his neck out at such a moment!","Yang Wenpeng was fuming.","His rage had been mostly directed at the group of people who had challenged him. But now, they had blended into the crowd.","Yang Wenpeng’s fury had yet to be satiated, and what Du Xing said caused him to fly off the handle.","“Du Xing, don’t forget what you promised when you joined the team! I make the decisions for the team, and you have to listen to me! They were the ones causing trouble. But instead of helping me to quell them, you are trying to tell me what to do.","“Who gave you the right to do such a thing? If you continue running your mouth, you can leave this team and take on the waves of dead spirits up ahead on your own!”","Most of the people in the team did not want such a conflict to break out. Each youth who made it as a participant of the Radiance Hundred Sequence was the cream of the crop. They were grateful that Du Xing was trying to step forward to stop the conflict by preventing the confrontation from escalating.","Du Xing’s words were an olive branch to Yang Wenpeng.","Alas, not only did Yang Wenpeng reject the olive branch, but he even blamed Du Xing, who had offered it to him.","Yang Wenpeng’s actions did not sit right with the crowd.","When Du Xing heard what Yang Wenpeng said, he knew there was no point in trying to say anything else. Also, he did not want to fight with Yang Wenpeng in the first place. He never wanted to fight over the leadership position of the team.","Du Xing said decisively, “I will leave this team. Do any of you want to leave with me? I welcome anyone. I can’t promise that I will be of much help against the dead spirit waves, but I will definitely do my best and stick by you to the end. I will never abandon you just because the dead spirits prove to be too fearsome!”","While Du Xing spoke, he looked at Yang Nuanxin, and they locked eyes. He immediately looked away.","Du Xing knew of the position she was in. Regardless of anything else, he could not force her to do anything at such a time.","Du Xing came from the main branch of his family and knew of the influence that the main branch of the family had over a collateral branch.","If he insisted on inviting her to leave with him, it would undoubtedly put her on the spot. There was a high chance it would cause her to come under fire from Yang Wenpeng’s temper.","Yang Nuanxin continued to look at Du Xing even after he averted his gaze.","There was not a single part of her that wanted to remain with Yang Wenpeng’s team.","Firstly, she hated being coerced. This cousin from the main branch of her family couldn’t care less about her and saw her as nothing more than a tool.","Furthermore, she knew that if she stayed with Yang Wenpeng, her Cleansing Rain Sky Crane would only be allowed to clear the death aura around Yang Wenpeng and his cronies, regardless of how outstanding her fey’s death-aura-clearing abilities were. This would seriously affect her standing in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","Du Xing’s words struck a chord with many people, and almost half of the team walked over to him.","Even the original team he had been leading before the union of the two teams had not consisted of this many people!","With almost 500 people clustering around him, Du Xing’s camp now rivaled Yang Wenpeng’s camp.","This tip in the scales caused Wei Haodong—the originator of the disgruntlement—to panic.","He had secretly caused trouble to drag Yang Wenpeng down and take over the team.","But now, the team had split, and he could no longer become the leader of a team of more than 1,000 people even after dragging Yang Wenpeng down.","This unanticipated outcome was completely the fault of Du Xing.","Wei Haodong redirected his hatred to Du Xing.","As long as he could get rid of Du Xing, the newly formed team would lose their leader and have no choice but to rejoin the other team. At that point, he would be able to make use of Yang Wenpeng’s selfishness and bad temper to cause conflict within the team and push Yang Wenpeng out.","With this thought, Wei Haodong yelled, “You have to think carefully. The members of the team who are able to clear death aura are all on this side. If you leave, you will die from being infected by all the death aura you take in, even if you don’t encounter another wave of dead spirits!","“Yang Wenpeng’s management of the team does have many issues. We can reduce his authority and select a few people to co-manage the team together.","“Du Xing, it’s clear that you have great influence and can even tear apart the team with a raise of your hand. I’m sure you’ll be able to become one of the managers!”","Wei Haodong had brought up both sides of the coin and distorted the facts.","The one thing that Yang Wenpeng cared the most about was his authority in the team. His words undermined Yang Wenpeng’s authority and were no different from plunging a dagger into Yang Wenpeng’s chest, setting his fury alight!","At the same time, he used Du Xing’s leadership and protection over the team to subtly suggest that he was seeking to gain authority.","Those standing behind Du Xing felt the latter was manipulating them!","Du Xing realized what Wei Haodong was trying to do and was about to rebuke him when Yang Wenpeng snarled, “If you choose not to side with me, you will suffer eventually! Don’t come crying to me then!”","At this point, Yang Wenpeng took a deep breath.","“Yang Nuanxin is a distant cousin and has no choice but to listen to me. If you join me now, you will be able to receive the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane’s protection. I will give you 30 seconds to ponder your decision.”","Yang Nuanxin had been suppressing her anger, and it was bubbling within her.","She had already betrayed her friends and had been forcefully recruited by Yang Wenpeng.","But now, Yang Wenpeng was using her as a bargaining chip and even sounded as though he was looking down on her for coming from the collateral branch of the family.","Yang Nuanxin took two steps back and summoned her other fey, the Cutting-Wings Sword Swan.","She grabbed the Cutting-Wings Sword Swan’s feet, and it carried her over to Du Xing.","The Cleansing Rain Sky Crane moved over to join Du Xing’s side so it could follow its contractor.","Yang Nuanxin did not instruct the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane to protect only the side she was on. Instead, she instructed it, “Bring rain down on everyone. Try to cover every person!”","After giving her instructions, she said coldly, “Yang Wenpeng, I was wrong from the beginning. I shouldn’t have allowed myself to be threatened by you during the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. I wasted so much time allowing my friends to be forced to join you and watch you go off your rocker. You are selfish and unsuited to control a team!","“As for those around you, none of you thought of sharing your resources in a time of crisis but are fighting over it instead. None of you are fit to become a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence!”","Yang Wenpeng seemed easygoing but hit the nail on the head when she lost her temper. Naturally, she shocked Yang Wenpeng and all the people around him.","Yang Wenpeng never expected Yang Nuanxin to side with his opponent. She had even turned around to stab him by saying that he did not have the character befitting of a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence!","Her words would definitely catch attention once it was broadcast.","But as angry as he was, Yang Wenpeng still had clarity of mind. Hence, he did not begin insulting and threatening her.","Du Xing understood Yang Nuanxin’s reasons for making her previous choice and did not blame her at all.","If she had sided with him, then Yang Wenpeng would definitely have used his status as a direct descendent of the main branch to make things difficult for her family.","This was a common occurrence. There were many collateral branches that were relegated to grunt work after offending the main branch. Some even ended up eliminated by the main branch.","Yang Nuanxin had just opposed Yang Wenpeng and thrown down the gauntlet.","This would become one of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection’s biggest pieces of news.","As long as someone paid attention to this matter, the Yang family’s main branch would not make things difficult for Yang Nuanxin’s collateral branch, even if she did not manage to clinch a position in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Yang Wenpeng was easy to anger and could only see what was right in front of him. He was not capable of much higher-order thinking.","However, the other members of the Yang family’s main branch would not allow Yang Wenpeng to do as he pleased.","Moreover, Du Xing saw promising potential in Yang Nuanxin.","Given that most feys were unable to do anything against death aura, Yang Nuanxin’s ability to clear death aura using the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane made her worth nurturing.","Yang Wenpeng glared at Yang Nuanxin maliciously, and she could not stop herself from feeling a chill run up her back.","At that moment, soft sounds could be heard in the distance. They were not coming from individual entities but were clearly coming from an enormous group.","“Oh no! There is a wave of dead spirits rushing here from the south! We must leave as soon as possible! There are millions of dead spirits in this wave, and there’s no way that our team will be able to handle such an army! Why is luck so bad? Why did we have to encounter such a giant wave of dead spirits?”","The scouts’ shrieks immediately halted the internal conflict in the team.","The millions of dead spirits would easily swallow a team of more than 3,000 people. Only teams that consisted of more than 5,000 people would be able to stand a chance.","However, trying to take them on by force would not lead to a positive result.","They were initially unaware of whether they were going in the right direction. Now, they had no choice but to go in the opposite direction from the wave of dead spirits.","Since this sudden disaster outbreak had stopped the conflict, Yang Wenpeng was still the team leader and had yet to be replaced.","However, those who chose to side with Du Xing would no longer listen to Yang Wenpeng’s instructions. They were only going to listen to Du Xing.","The team was only maintained because Du Xing took the high road and invited Yang Wenpeng to issue instructions.","Previously, Yang Nuanxin was helping Yang Wenpeng, and his main group of subordinates did not have to face the threat of the death aura.","But now that Yang Nuanxin was siding with Du Xing, the faces of Yang Wenpeng’s close subordinates were slowly becoming paler, and blood began oozing out of their eyes and noses.","All of them were participants of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. The people around Yang Wenpeng were willing to bootlick him when he was able to provide them with benefits. But now that he could no longer do so, all of them began thinking of betraying him.","Yang Nuanxin’s importance to the team heightened when they directly took on dead spirits.","Du Xing was well aware of this.","He did not ask Yang Nuanxin to protect him exclusively. Instead, he saw her as an important combat resource for the team. Thus, he assigned ten support-type spirit qi professionals to her to help her recover her energy.","The Cleansing Rain Sky Crane produced rain continuously and serviced the entire team.","This not only referred to the 500 people around Du Xing, but even those who had not decided to join him received Yang Nuanxin’s protection.","Regardless of how strong the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane’s cleansing abilities were, it was only a Platinum fey.","With the inclusion of Yang Nuanxin, many of the participants were affected by the death aura.","But with the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane around, the group could continue moving forward.","Du Xing led the group in assigning their positions. They managed to avoid the wave of dead spirits by moving in a C formation.","Given that the dead spirits were currently exploding out of the Dead Spirits Wells continuously, a wave of millions of dead spirits was insignificant.","The scouts in the team sent their avian-type feys further and discovered a few groups of millions of dead spirits. Once those groups of dead spirits encountered each other, they would fuse after a small scuffle.","After the scouts discovered the tens of millions of dead spirits, they immediately lost the courage to continue moving forward.","The team could already sense the violent tremors even before hearing the scouts’ reports.","When Yang Wenpeng said that he would do the same as Du Xing did to avoid the tens of millions of dead spirits, Du Xing suddenly felt the urge to leave the team.","Any person who had been part of an adventurer group knew how to use the C formation to avoid an enemy.","When an adventurer group was trying to avoid small groups of dimensional lifeforms, they often employed the C formation.","However, the C formation was only suitable for avoiding such small to medium enemy groups.","There was no way they could form a diameter large enough to cover a wave of tens of millions of dead spirits.","They would definitely end up clashing with the dead spirits.","The only way they could survive now was to try and charge directly through and pray that one of the leaders was nearby.","After Yang Wenpeng issued the order, Du Xing pointed forward and said, “If anyone wants to achieve better results in this test instead of dying here, charge forward with me! Try your best to coordinate your feys and prevent the dead spirits behind from catching up.”"]},{"number":2703,"title":"Chapter 2703: Truly Lucky!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2703: Truly Lucky!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Du Xing ignored the reactions of the others and summoned his main fey, the Burning Ground Yak.","He leaped onto the Burning Ground Yak’s back and rushed to the front.","Most of the Radiance Federation’s younger generation had experience with surviving in the wild.","After last year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, where the test had been changed to a survival format, many members of the Radiance Federation’s younger generation went to train in the wild over the past year.","Many people noticed that Yang Wenpeng was a bumpkin. Although the elders in his family had brought him out to train in the wild, he had not paid attention to the knowledge involved in surviving in the wild. Otherwise, he would not be unaware of the fact that a C formation was not suitable for avoiding a large group of enemies.","Rather than staying here and suffering and dying with Yang Wenpeng, they stood a better shot of surviving by going with Du Xing.","Given the circumstances, there were no better options.","Thus, those who realized their circumstances left the team with Du Xing and rushed forward.","Yang Nuanxin grabbed the teammate next to her, who was about to leave with Du Xing, and said, “Little Dong, give me a ride on your Nimble Moose. I’m leaving with the rest of you! The Cleansing Rain Sky Crane will be able to protect us during our journey.”","The young man Yang Nuanxin addressed as Little Dong helped her up onto the Nimble Moose’s back. He also intentionally sat behind her to prevent her from slipping off.","Qin Dong and Yang Nuanxin were good friends, and he could understand that she was in a difficult position.","Hence, just like Du Xing, he did not force her to stay with them when Yang Wenpeng was trying to poach her.","“Nuanxin, now that you have made your decision, let’s hurry up and catch up with Big Brother Xing! Otherwise, he won’t be able to join him! With the possibility of encountering dead spirits at any moment, it will be better for us to find strength in numbers.”","Although Qin Dong was speaking with Yang Nuanxin, he did not slow down his actions. Rather, when Yang Nuanxin first told him that she wanted to leave, he instructed the Nimble Moose to charge forward. He was afraid that Yang Wenpeng would try to stop her and prevent her from leaving.","Qin Dong was not making a mountain out of a molehill.","He knew how important Yang Nuanxin was to the team.","The best way for Yang Wenpeng to secure his control over the team would be to control Yang Nuanxin and utilize the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane as his signature.","It was true that this was how Yang Wenpeng felt, but he had acted too slowly. By the time he instructed his fey to get close to Yang Nuanxin, she was already seated on the Nimble Moose and had dashed far away.","There was no question that the people who left his team to join Du Xing felt hostility towards him.","Yang Wenpeng dared not send his fey too far.","When Wei Haodong saw this, he was so enraged that he wanted to scream.","He had sowed discord in the team to take over the leadership position.","But now, the team had separated, and there was no meaning in becoming the leader of Yang Wenpeng and these few hundred people.","While Wei Haodong was in the midst of disappointment, a black figure flew toward him and slammed into his back. Two giant forces also immobilized his fey.","When Wei Haodong recovered from the impact, he saw Yang Wenpeng staring at him coldly and with menace.","Wei Haodong shouted, “Yang Wenpeng, why did you attack me? The dead spirits are about to reach us. Why aren’t you instructing your men to flee? We are a team of comrades. Don’t you care about the consequences of attacking me?”","Wei Haodong assumed that because they were all here to participate in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, they would never do anything that clearly harmed their image unless they were lunatics.","Yang Wenpeng was not a lunatic. But he had just suffered a chain of blows.","At first, he was in the glorious position of leading a team of more than 1,000 people. But now, that large team had broken apart. He had also lost Yang Nuanxin’s Cleansing Rain Sky Crane, which caused his authoritative aura to suffer further.","Yang Wenpeng knew that although there were only 300 to 400 people left in his team, they would never allow themselves to be fully controlled by him again.","He had fallen to this position because of Wei Haodong’s provocation. Du Xing would never have had to step forward if he had not tried to provoke him.","Yang Wenpeng could never sit by and watch Wei Haodong take over as leader of the team.","“Of course, I am going to lead us away from the sea of dead spirits. Don’t forget that I was the one who suggested we hide from the dead spirits. You have been continuously stirring discontent in the team and pulling us down. I must teach you a lesson! You can stay at the back of the group and use your feys to clean up after us.”","The moment Yang Wenpeng spoke, the black leopard’s tail, which was akin to a steel whip, landed on Wei Haodong’s body.","The whip did not seem strong, but it still caused the bones in Wei Haodong’s knees to crack. As a result, he could still stand but not walk quickly.","Yang Wenpeng also used his feys to cause serious damage to Wei Haodong’s feys.","Wei Haodong’s chest tightened. He knew that Yang Wenpeng could not kill him directly out of consideration of his own image. He was trying to use this method to eliminate Wei Haodong by leaving him to die at the hands of the waves of dead spirits.","The immense rage caused Wei Haodong to glare at Yang Wenpeng with bloodshot eyes.","“Yang Wenpeng, aside from the slight amount of power you possess, you are nothing but a jerk! A hopeless jerk! Du Xing managed to avoid the swarm of thousands of dead spirits by retreating in the C formation, so you copied him to take on millions of dead spirits. You must be mad!","“You attacked my fey and me and stole my ability to flee. Do you really think a black-hearted fool like you will be able to make it into the Radiance Hundred Sequence? Wake up and get real!”","Wei Haodong felt refreshed after saying that.","The hosts and audience on Star Web must have seen all the twists and turns that had happened to their team.","He had revealed the harm he suffered at Yang Wenpeng’s hands in front of so many people.","Even if he couldn’t get back at Yang Wenpeng in this test, the consequences of his actions that would come after the test would be the ultimate revenge.","It was true that birds of a feather flocked together.","Wei Haodong thought he had hidden his provocative methods well. He had no clue that the audience watching from a bird’s eye view had seen it all clearly.","The conflict in this team had generated passionate comments on Star Web.","The matter became even larger of a sensation once Poison Beauty picked up on it.","The more popular a host was, the less suitable they would be to express their seemingly objective opinions on Star Web, which was a public platform. This was because a person’s opinions were almost always subjective, and expressing them would lead to many negative consequences.","Poison Beauty always kept this in mind.","However, after watching everything that had transpired from her bird’s eye view, she had the right to express her opinion as a host who had been specially invited as a commentator.","The Radiance Hundred Sequence selection was an honorable event.","The Radiance Federation intentionally used the participants’ names as their identification tags.","“Wei Haodong incited discontent in his team and is a malignant tumor to the team. A person like this would harm any team that he is part of. However, his actions also exposed Yang Wenpeng’s issues.","“Who knows how many people the evil dictator Yang Wenpeng has bullied in real life? He actually publicly coerced his cousin from a collateral branch of his family and maliciously attacked other participants.”","Because of her personal experiences, Poison Beauty felt more disgusted with Yang Wenpeng than Wei Haodong.","Poison Beauty also came from a collateral branch and was constantly bullied by an older male and female cousin from the main branch.","Later, her father managed to use his capabilities to form a connection with a powerful chamber of commerce. This allowed them to finally break free from the control of the main branch.","After joining this chamber of commerce, Poison Beauty’s father built two merchant groups.","However, the chamber of commerce eventually went bankrupt, and Poison Beauty’s family only managed to stay afloat by relying on the two merchant groups. At the very least, Poison Beauty did not have to worry about having food to eat and clothes to wear.","However, Poison Beauty needed to earn her own resources to nurture her feys and could not rely on her family for much help.","Later, because she was matched with Lin Yuan on Star Web and fought a few battles with him, she managed to become a popular Star Web host.","It was only after signing a contract with the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce to help them with their sales that Poison Beauty finally gained financial freedom.","When the main branch found out that she was thriving, they immediately contacted her.","Poison Beauty only had one stance toward them—to get rid of any plans to leech off of her!","After Yang Nuanxin was overwhelmed by Yang Wenpeng’s status as a direct descendant of the main branch, Poison Beauty felt a sense of relatability to her.","This was why Poison Beauty intentionally mentioned the part about the main branch of the family coercing the collateral branch.","She hoped she could use her influence to help Yang Nuanxin avoid any negative repercussions from Yang Wenpeng.","Lu Shuang was partnering with Poison Beauty for this live stream. She also shared her thoughts about this matter. Her words were full of harsh judgment toward Yang Wenpeng and Wei Haodong.","Lu Shuang had been part of an adventurer team in the past.","She left the team after six months because there were people in the team who were constantly stirring trouble.","By that time, Lu Shuang could already support herself through her channel.","She did not want to be forced to participate in unnecessary socializing and become embroiled in negativity. Hence, she decided to leave the team.","Lu Shuang and Poison Beauty’s judgments of Yang Wenpeng and Wei Haodong were met with boisterous agreement.","[Returning on Wind]: People like that are disgusting! Who hasn’t encountered dictators and trouble-stirring jerks in their own lives? People like that aren’t fit to become part of the Radiance Hundred Sequence!","[Hopping Tall Mountain]: I can’t be bothered to waste my thoughts on such people. I would rather pay attention to Yang Nuanxin’s Cleansing Rain Sky Crane. Aren’t the Creation Masters doing research into feys that can treat death aura? Why don’t the Creation Masters focus their efforts on the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane? The Cleansing Rain Sky Crane’s ability to cleanse death aura is amazing!","To the Moon Empress and the entire Radiance Federation, Yang Nuanxin’s Cleansing Rain Sky Crane was the biggest surprise to come out of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","It was evident that the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane had mutated from another fey.","There were many reasons for a fey to undergo a mutation.","Unless the external factors were fully replicated, reproducing or creating the mutation was not guaranteed.","The Moon Empress wanted to meet with Yang Nuanxin personally after the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection ended. She would ask Yang Nuanxin and the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane to stay with her for some time to examine her fey.","If she could recreate the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane’s mutation, she could keep one above each city.","The regular people of the Radiance Federation would thus not have to worry about being killed by the death aura when Tower Canon brought out even more moves.","As the topic gained traction, Du Xing and Qin Dong were mentioned. Du Xing especially received significant praise.","[Not Like the Past]: Du Xing is truly a good captain! He didn’t want to engage in conflict while they were in the middle of the journey and chose to give up his authority. When his people were being disadvantaged, he stepped up to fight for them.","[I Hope to be Smoke]: What does he mean by using a C formation to avoid the dead spirits? I think even I’m better than Yang Wenpeng when it comes to surviving in the wild! Du Xing made the right choice. Given the circumstances, charging forward is the only option!","[Love Eating Sweet Beans]: Luckily, Du Xing and the rest aren’t too far from the main area. Judging by their current direction, they will be able to reach Lord Lin Yuan!","Poison Beauty read many similar comments saying that Du Xing and the rest were very lucky.","However, she did not share their sentiment.","The audience felt that Du Xing was lucky because he could join Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had become a symbol of faith in the Radiance Federation, so anyone who had the chance to make contact with him saw themselves as lucky.","But in Poison Beauty’s opinion, Du Xing’s luck came from Yang Nuanxin’s decision to join his team.","In order to properly comment on the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, she intentionally went to experience the dead spirits and stayed in an environment concentrated with death aura for some time. Thus, she was well aware of the impact that death aura had on the human body.","As the dead spirits continued cropping up in the test ground, the concentration of death aura also rose.","If Du Xing and the rest did not change their direction, they would be almost 500 kilometers away from Lin Yuan. However, they would be able to reach Lin Yuan’s sea of flowers in another 300 kilometers!","Without the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane to cleanse the death aura in the area, less than 1/10 of the almost 700 people in Du Xing’s team would be able to make it to the sea of flowers.","Poison Beauty did not think that Yang Nuanxin made her decision because of Du Xing’s charisma. She believed that Yang Nuanxin did so because of how she felt toward her friends.","In this aspect, Yang Nuanxin was doing much better than the Poison Beauty of the past!"]},{"number":2704,"title":"Chapter 2704 Saved by the Sea of Sand!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2704 Saved by the Sea of Sand!","However, Yang Wenpeng managed to control himself.","He still had some restraint after the wave of impulsivity passed.","If he used his feys to kill Wei Haodong immediately, the nature of his actions would change.","Given Wei Haodong’s current situation, there was no way he could survive the waves of rampaging dead spirits. Once the waves of dead spirits swallowed Wei Haodong, Yang Wenpeng’s goal would be met.","Yang Wenpeng sensed the tremors below him intensifying. He waved his arm in a large arc.","“Let’s immediately move sideways to the right and try our best to avoid the wave of dead spirits! Those in charge of scouting should investigate the positions of the dead spirits so we can avoid them in the C formation!”","Yang Wenpeng did not care if these people were truly willing to follow his direction. There was no way they had chosen to stay because they wanted to steal the leadership position from him like Wei Haodong did.","Yang Wenpeng believed that as long as he could lead the team to avoid this wave, his image as a leader would be boosted.","At that moment, a hoarse voice coming not too far from Yang Wenpeng said, “Big Brother Peng, our team no longer has any scouts! The spirit qi professionals who were in charge of scouting all left with Du Xing.”","Yang Wenpeng froze.","He understood the meaning behind the scouting spirit qi professionals leaving him.","Originally, most of them had been following him. There was no reason to assume they were closer to Du Xing.","This happened because those scouts did not think they could escape the wave using the C formation.","But he was already stuck there. He could not change the plan now.","Furthermore, even if he wanted to change the plan, he would not know what to change it to.","Luckily for him, those who had not left had yet to lose all hope in him. They were also those who did not have many opinions on their own, as well as those who had yet to see the reality of the dead spirits wave.","The team of more than 300 people truly intended on moving in a C formation and hoped that this would allow them to avoid the tens of millions of dead spirits.","...","Lu Shuang sighed and told the audience in the live-streaming room, “You will all soon see how a wave of dead spirits swallows a group of more than 300 people. I did not expect Yang Wenpeng to push on with the C formation to avoid the dead spirits. He didn’t pick up his survival skills properly but wants to call the shots. He is not only harming himself but also the entire team!”","Even if these over 300 participants who chose to follow Yang Wenpeng managed to survive the wave of dead spirits, they would never be able to get a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence. A few of them did possess decent power, but they did not have much brains.","Aside from exhibiting the outstanding capabilities of the younger generation, they wanted the regular people to understand the perils of the dead spirits.","Poison Beauty said sternly, “We should be moving our view away, but I think we should all understand what a wave of dead spirits is like. We need to understand this disaster that affects our life and see the difference between the dead spirits and dead dimensional lifeforms.”","Lu Shuang could not help but compliment Poison Beauty when she heard that.","Poison Beauty was becoming increasingly mature as a host. She was also more daring than Lu Shuang and said many things that Lu Shuang would never dare to say.","Lu Shuang was afraid that saying something wrong would attract consequential trouble. But now, she had Poison Beauty to help her to say all that she held herself back from saying. This expanded the range of content of her broadcast.","Lu Shuang could not help but think, I can work with Poison Beauty more in the future.","...","Yang Wenpeng led his team and tried to avoid the dead spirits wave in a C formation.","Technically, they had executed a textbook version. But regardless of how well they executed it, it was useless because the application was wrong.","It was not long before Yang Wenpeng’s team clashed against the surging wave of dead spirits.","Every dead spirit moved at different speeds. Thus, the general shape of the wave changed every second.","It was as though the wave of tens of millions of dead spirits had noticed a delectable meal.","Yang Wenpeng felt his heart sink into despair.","The closer his team got to the wave of dead spirits, the higher the concentration of death aura in the air around them.","The team members’ teeth, noses, ears, and eyes were all infected by death aura and began leaking blood. A few of their faces even ended up covered with bloody scabs.","People became dizzy when they were both mentally and physically tired.","Over 300 people lost their lives, just like a stone thrown into the sea, with no noticeable impact, among the tens of millions of departed spirits.","Du Xing’s team up ahead was not in any better state than Yang Wenpeng’s team.","It required energy to use their feys to charge forward at full speed.","These feys would also be affected by the death aura.","Du Xing and the rest slowed down continuously as their bodies and minds deteriorated.","Yang Nuanxin’s Cleansing Rain Sky Crane flapped its wings gently and summoned a thin curtain of rain atop the group.","However, Yang Nuanxin persisted.","Du Xing looked at the ghastly pale Yang Nuanxin, who was still pushing forward and using the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane to summon rain.","He then looked ahead at the desolate land and said, “Nuanxin, because of your fey, you have the most potential out of all of us. Qin Dong’s Nimble Moose is also the fastest of all our feys. It can also capture wind elements while running to reduce its energy depletion and raise its speed. So just take care of yourself and Qin Dong. Both of you should try your best to survive!”","Du Xing looked at the teammates around him, who were already showing signs of collapsing. He knew that even if Yang Nuanxin continued using the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane to take care of all of them, it was unlikely that all of them would make it.","Aside from being infected by death aura and their health suffering, their awful conditions were the result of being completely drained of energy.","Du Xing could sense that the vibrations under his feet were growing stronger. This meant that the dead spirits were getting closer.","If Du Xing was more selfish, he could use Yang Nuanxin to try to save himself. However, he did not do so.","Meanwhile, an eyeball formed from sand watched all of this from nearby.","After hearing what Du Xing said, the eye’s gaze lingered on him.","When Yang Nuanxin heard that, she was about to shake her head, but he continued. “Nuanxin, you should be aware that you have the greatest need to perform out of all of us. Your performance will save your family. Otherwise, Yang Wenpeng will definitely take action against you and your family!","“Qin Dong, I’m sorry things are hard for you too. If you didn’t have to stick with the team, the Nimble Moose would already be another 100 kilometers ahead.”","Qin Dong pursed his lips tightly and looked deeply into Du Xing’s eyes. “Big Brother Xing, the slower the Nimble Moose runs, the less energy it uses.”","Qin Dong lowered his head and said, “Nuanxin, you can make the decision. I’ll stay with you if you choose to remain with the team. I wouldn’t have lasted this long without your Cleansing Rain Sky Crane anyway.”","Qin Dong did not say that to console Yang Nuanxin. He had laid out his circumstances reasonably.","Because the Nimble Moose exchanged wind elements with the environment through its skin, the death aura had a more serious effect on it than on other feys.","Qin Dong’s body was not in good shape. His body was seriously affected when he first entered the test ground.","When Yang Wenpeng forcefully pulled away Yang Nuanxin, Qin Dong would intermittently cough up large amounts of blood.","Since Yang Nuanxin enabled him to make it this long, Qin Dong was willing to leave the decision to her.","Du Xing knew that he had reached the end of the line and was willing to help others who actually stood a chance of surviving.","However, the other participants did not want Yang Nuanxin to leave until all hope was truly lost, regardless of how arduous their journey was.","“Du Xing, what are you doing? We were willing to follow you when you clashed against Yang Wenpeng. What gives you the right to send Yang Nuanxin and Qin Dong off alone now? We know that you are on good terms with Qin Dong. What else does he bring to the table aside from his fey that is slightly fast? We all know that the Nimble Moose’s combat ability is extremely low.”","Du Xing did not say anything after being reproached. He also did not try to explain himself.","It was true that these people only left Yang Wenpeng’s team because they were following him.","Regardless of whether it was because of his charisma or because they realized that Yang Wenpeng’s proposed C formation was doomed for failure, Du Xing was grateful.","However, he never tied himself to Yang Nuanxin.","When he charged ahead alone, he never took into consideration whether she would be able to catch up.","It was Yang Nuanxin who decided to ask Qin Dong to give her a ride.","Du Xing was doing what he was doing because the team was about to fall. As the leader, this was the best decision for the team. If all of them died there, they would truly lose all hope.","If he was really selfish, he would have tied himself to Yang Nuanxin at the beginning and given her a ride on his own fey.","Yang Nuanxin knew that it would be difficult for the team to hold on. But she still did not want to abandon them.","However, what Du Xing said at the end touched her. Even if she did not think for herself, she had to think for her family.","“Big Brother Dong, my Cleansing Rain Sky Crane will cover your Nimble Moose. Order the Nimble Moose to rush ahead at full speed!”","The moment Yang Nuanxin’s words left her lips, a female voice shouted from nearby, “Thank you for helping us for so long!”","This girl used her two Fantasy Breed feys to shoot a beam of light blue light at the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane, forming a white imprint on its body.","Yang Nuanxin immediately sensed the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane being replenished with energy.","When the girl’s Fantasy Breed feys were done using their abilities, one collapsed on the ground while the other seemed dead.","Yang Nuanxin cupped her hands together in a fist and bowed to the girl before dashing away with Qin Dong on the Nimble Moose.","If the team was seen as a unit, this girl had essentially breathed life into their final spark of hope.","Those who were cold-hearted might see this action as stupid, but this action was heralded as a spirit of sacrifice.","Without Yang Nuanxin, the people in this team grew increasingly weaker, and the sounds of aggression from the dead spirits grew louder.","Du Xing turned to look at the astonishing wave of dead spirits. He pressed his hand to the ground with agony in order to prevent his weak body from being shaken by the tremors.","At that moment, a pool of quicksand appeared under Du Xing’s feet and sucked him in.","The sand did not crush Du Xing. Rather, a small room was created out of metal. He could move freely within the space.","The space had no death aura, and Du Xing and his feys’ spirits could begin recovering.","As the wave of dead spirits advanced, more pools of quicksand appeared below the participants. One of them was the girl whose feys had replenished the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane’s energy.","After a moment of confusion after being sucked into the pools of quicksand, these people suddenly remembered that Lin Yuan had used this move in the battle against Liu Jie!","Lin Yuan was one of the assessors of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","When this thought struck them, these people were overcome with excitement. Lin Yuan’s action was not against the rules.","As one of the main assessors of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, Lin Yuan wielded significant authority in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and could decide which participants he wanted to keep.","These were all the people Lin Yuan had decided to save.","These people were all shining lights. It would be a loss to the Radiance Federation if they were eliminated.","This especially applied to Du Xing. Lin Yuan could see the makings of a leader in him.","If Du Xing could not become a member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, he would receive invitations to join organizations like the Spirit Guards.","Lin Yuan was prepared to snatch Du Xing from the Spirit Guards and nurture him as a member of Sky City’s reserve strategic team.","...","Yang Nuanxin’s Cleansing Rain Sky Crane had recovered a significant amount of energy. With the Nimble Moose’s support and speed, Yang Nuanxin was relieved of significant pressure.","The Nimble Moose was also able to take advantage of its speed.","As a support-type fey, the Nimble Moose was always raising its speed. When it ran at full force, it was much faster than a wave of dead spirits.","Yang Nuanxin could clearly tell that the sounds of the dead spirits behind her were growing softer.","All of a sudden, she realized that the environment around her had a very low concentration of death aura.","Before she could bring this up to Qin Dong, she saw a wild and savagely beautiful sea of flowers up ahead."]},{"number":2705,"title":"Chapter 2705: The Radiance Hundred Sequence’s Final Trial!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2705: The Radiance Hundred Sequence’s Final Trial!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Yang Nuanxin and Qin Dong instinctively rubbed their eyes when they glimpsed the ferocious yet beautiful sea of flowers. For a moment, they thought that they were imagining what they were seeing.","But soon, their emotions turned to delight.","Yang Nuanxin was Lin Yuan’s fan. Although Qin Dong was not considered Lin Yuan’s fan, he had always silently supported Liu Jie.","He had also witnessed how Lin Yuan had stunningly used the sea of flowers to swallow the sea of dimensional lifeforms.","Qin Dong had watched the recording of the previous year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence selection numerous times.","They were able to see this sea of flowers because they were not far from Lin Yuan. As long as they could make contact with it, it would mean that they were under Lin Yuan’s protection.","This sea of flowers was lethal for the dead spirits, but it was an umbrella of protection for the participants. As deadly as the sea of flowers was, it would never harm the participants.","Although the support-type spirit qi professional had depleted her roots to help the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane, it had already run out of spirit qi.","Yang Nuanxin recalled the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane with damaged roots and","said, “Big Brother Dong, Lord Lin Yuan’s sea of flowers can clear death aura.","The concentration of death aura is very low here. I’ll store the Cleansing Rain","Sky Crane away so it can recover.”","Qin Dong said seriously, “Nuanxin, don’t use the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane unless you absolutely need to. After we join Lord Lin Yuan’s team, try your best to display the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane’s abilities to the greatest extent.","“You aren’t skilled at combat. Aside from the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane, your other feys lean toward functional-type. As a result, you can’t compete with the others in direct combat. You can only stand out by using your feys’ abilities!”","There was no need for Qin Dong to say these to Yang Nuanxin. They might seem like teammates, but they were actually competitors in this test.","He told Yang Nuanxin these because he wanted to thank her for her help and because he did not want to see her suffer retribution from Yang Wenpeng after the test.","Many of the members of the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence selection were able to attain opportunities that led to bright futures because of their performances during the test.","Because of the dead spirits crisis this year, there was even more attention on the Radiance Hundred Sequence than in previous years.","Yang Wenpeng would be seen as a negative example and be scorned.","Yang Nuanxin had to achieve some results and more attention in order to fend off the consequences of Yang Wenpeng’s fury after the test.","The head of the Yang family’s main branch would never let Yang Wenpeng express his anger, no matter how bad-tempered he was, as long as she had enough status and popularity. This was to protect the Yang family’s reputation.","Yang Nuanxin nodded gravely.","Still seated on the Nimble Moose, Yang Nuanxin turned and looked at Qin","Dong. She locked eyes with his resolute ones. “Thank you for your advice, Big Brother Dong. But I don’t think I’ll be able to hold back if I see anyone’s eyes and noses leaking blood after being infected by death aura.”","Qin Dong was not at all surprised by what Yang Nuanxin said.","Both of them were in the same team in high school and later entered the same university. With the inclusion of the two years they spent in university, they had been teammates for five years.","Qin Dong understood her character. She remained her same compassionate self throughout the five years.","Compassion was a virtue, but it might not be beneficial for her in this test.","If they managed to reach Lin Yuan’s sea of flowers soon, it was likely that Yang Nuanxin would suggest that they turn back to inform Du Xing of this.","Qin Dong was terrified of this happening.","When it came to such matters, the stubbornly compassionate Yang Nuanxin would not be able to listen to reason.","However, Qin Dong was sure that if they truly turned back, they wouldn’t just fail to rescue Du Xing, but Yang Nuanxin would also lose her chance of survival.","There was one thing that Qin Dong was sure of—this Radiance Hundred","Sequence selection was very important to Du Xing. Du Xing had used the Radiance Hundred Sequence for the past few years as his goal and motivation for working hard.","Du Xing would never have made such a decision unless he was absolutely certain that he could not hold on.","With his fey that had scouting abilities, Qin Dong was well aware of how fast the dead spirits moved.","The dead spirits would have swallowed Du Xing and the rest in less than two minutes after he and Yang Nuanxin left them.","However, Qin Dong could not explain all this to Yang Nuanxin. Even if he did, she would unlikely agree with his decision.","Regardless of whether it was because they were teammates or the possible existence of any other special emotions between them, Qin Dong did not want to fall out with Yang Nuanxin over such matters.","Qin Dong urged the Nimble Moose to run faster toward the sea of flowers.","When they got nearer to the sea of flowers, they saw the gill-shaped petals of the large red flowers opening and closing continuously, as well as the rows of sharp teeth covering the vines that glinted as the vines moved in the air.","Qin Dong was both shocked and afraid.","Just as Qin Dong was trying to come up with a way to enter the dense sea of flowers, the sea of flowers automatically opened up a path.","The path was winding and led deep into the sea of flowers, but Qin Dong and Yang Nuanxin felt relaxed.","Once they entered the sea of flowers, they would no longer have to worry about the dead spirits and would have successfully reached the second stage of the selection.","The two of them would have the chance to see Lin Yuan up close in Star Web.","Liu Jie was not idle and had been using the army of insects to check on the participants in his vicinity. Likewise, he used the army of insects to save the promising participants.","Long Tao, Xia Qing, and the rest did the same. However, they were only able to save far fewer participants than Liu Jie and Lin Yuan.","Almost all of the members of the younger generation who were capable of making it to the main areas had arrived. Those who were unable to make it had probably already been swallowed by the dead spirits.","Tremors could be clearly felt in the areas covered by Lin Yuan’s sea of flowers and Liu Jie’s army of insects. The concentration of death aura was also climbing in these areas.","Lin Yuan did a headcount of the people in his camp. A total of 47 participants had made it to him.","After communicating his report through the Thoughts Letter Paper, he realized that his group was fairly large.","For example, only 21 participants had successfully made it to Shi Xu.","Lin Yuan sighed to himself. Liu Wencheng had made the test much too difficult","this time!","It had already been very difficult for the participants to find their spots last time.","This time, the size of the test ground had multiplied. It was likely that numerous outstanding talents had died during their journey.","But the harsher the environment, the better the talented individuals that emerged from it.","It could not be denied that Lin Yuan and Liu Jie were also to be thanked for enabling over 300 people to arrive at the main areas.","This was not because the sea of flowers and army of insects had protected them.","As invigilators of the test, Lin Yuan and Liu Jie had to ensure the fairness of the test.","Aside from those Lin Yuan and Liu Jie had decided to save, the rest of the participants competed fairly.","The sea of flowers and army of insects lowered the difficulty of the test by absorbing death aura from the environment to a level that the spirit qi professionals could endure.","If they had not done this, the explosion of waves of dead spirits would have caused the concentration of death aura to rise two to three times its current level.","No matter how strong the physiques of the spirit qi professionals were, their bodies would start to decay once the concentration of death aura in the air around them reached 18% and above.","Liu Wencheng had not expected so few participants to make it to the main areas.","Technically, the duels could begin now that the more than 300 participants had reached the main areas.","However, a test like that was prejudiced.","Liu Wencheng sent Lin Yuan and the rest a message through the Thoughts Letter Paper to tell them to divide the 300 participants into 13 groups.","There was no limit to the number of people in each group. These groups would then be sent out to hunt the dead spirits. Those who survived would equally divide up the number of dead spirits they killed as points.","After a moment of pondering, Lin Yuan realized Liu Wencheng’s intention for this design.","Once the 13 groups were formed, 13 leaders would immediately emerge. These 13 leaders would be the participants with the strongest leadership qualities.","The teams of different strengths would begin hunting dead spirits. Logically, the teams with more members had an advantage.","However, the points they earned were equally divided based on the number of dead spirits their team killed. Hence, the teams with more members would be disadvantaged instead.","Nonetheless, there was still an advantage because it was easier for the larger teams to kill dead spirits. Moreover, the team members who died could not claim points.","This test not only tested for leadership skills, combat power, and execution abilities but also human character.","Lin Yuan felt that using pressure and the temptation of honor to publicly expose the dark side of these youths’ natures was very cruel.","Liu Wencheng was doing this because he wanted to let the intelligent people in the Radiance Federation know that this was a better method of discerning a person’s quality than dueling.","In the world of spirit qi professionals, resources could create geniuses.","With Lin Yuan’s supply of resources, Liu Wencheng was willing to boost the members of the younger generation of high moral standing.","Yang Nuanxin and Qin Dong had not expected to see Du Xing and other members of their team here. But aside from their shock, they were also overjoyed.","“Big Brother Xing, how did you manage to escape the wave of dead spirits?”","Qin Dong walked over to Du Xing and patted his shoulder before looking him over to ensure he had no obvious injuries.","However, Du Xing’s body had yet to recover from being infected by death aura. Hence, he looked very frail.","Yang Nuanxin had already summoned the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane, and it was summoning rain to fall over these 30-odd people to protect them.","The other lucky participants looked at Yang Nuanxin in surprise. They had not expected her to possess such a magical fey! With this fey, she was definitely able to stand out in this test.","Qin Dong sighed deeply. Everything that he had said to Yang Nuanxin had been for naught.","There would only be ten final candidates in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. There were already more than 40 participants in Lin Yuan’s camp. It was likely that the other assessors had a similar number of participants around them.","They still had to continue competing.","If he were Yang Nuanxin, he would have done his best to enable the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane to recover its energy instead of using it to summon the rain with mild healing properties to heal the people infected by death aura.","Mu Yan, who had been part of the final ten ranks of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, re-entered the selection.","She had not expected to be so fated with Lin Yuan. She just happened to charge forward to the area where he was located!","Lin Yuan was still manipulating the sea of flowers, opening multiple paths within it.","At that moment, the crowd heard Lin Yuan say, “All of you can walk down these paths. You will be gathered with the other participants a few hours later. At that point, the final phase of the selection will begin, and the last hundred will engage in a round-robin duel.”","Out of the entire group, the one who was the most familiar with Lin Yuan was Mu Yan. She raised her hand and asked, “Lord Lin Yuan, can you give us some information about the final phase of the selection? We are so fated to have found you and will need to compete with the other participants to decide who the final 100 candidates are. It won’t be a bad idea for us to band together to look out for each other.’","Lin Yuan had already witnessed Mu Yan’s leadership qualities during the last Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","Both Mu Yan and Du Xing were capable of leading teams.","According to the rules, he could give information on the test after Liu","Wencheng decided on the contents of the test.","After describing the final phase of the test, Lin Yuan thought, I wonder who out of these 40 people will end up gathering together?","The few hours they spent walking down the paths would be enough for the potential leaders to compete with each other.","Du Xing’s advantage was that four to five of his original team, as well as Qin Dong and Yang Nuanxin, would side with him.","Mu Yan’s advantage was that she had experience as a member of the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence and was far more reputable than Du Xing. It would thus be easier for her to attract the other participants.","When the Star Web audience learned of the rules of the final stage of the selection, they immediately knew that it would be an exciting battle.","However, this was not what the Star Web audience was focused on. Instead, they were fully focused on watching the sea of flowers and sea of insects clashing with the wave of dead spirits.","When the sea of insects clashed with the wave of dead spirits, it seemed as though both sides were evenly matched.","The bones of the dead spirits were dragged by the Hypha Tapeworms into the carpet of fungi and separated before being turned into energy that would recover the other insects’ injuries and become their source of fuel.."]},{"number":2706,"title":"Chapter 2706: Clash of the Captains!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2706: Clash of the Captains!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The Death -Drawing Bladderworm absorbed all of the death aura.","When Liu Jie’s Death -Drawing Bladderworm encountered death aura, it could demonstrate its competence as an insect-species carcinoma fey.","Lin Yuan’s sea of flowers and Liu Jie’s sea of insects stretched out for hundreds of kilometers. Hence, the effects of the fighting taking place at the boundaries of the sea of flowers did not carry on to the main areas where the participants were located.","As such, the participants had no idea that the dead spirits were locked in a fierce battle with the seas of flowers and insects.","The audience watching all of this with a bird-eyed perspective was essentially watching a 3D movie where three groups of species were battling it out for dominance.","The three species were killing and consuming each other.","The brutal vine ramets born from Red Thorn’s spores saw the dead spirits as a","source of nourishment. In return, the dead spirits utilized their bodies to damage the outer layer of the sea of flowers, attempting to breach it.","Red Thorn’s unique child ramets could disperse spores amid the mass of dead spirits. Once these dead spirits perished, the spores would sprout within their lifeless remains, taking over the territory once controlled by the dead spirits.","The crimson, gill-shaped petals absorbed death aura, causing them to gradually turn purplish-red.","The more the brutal vine ramets attacked the dead spirits, the higher the proportion of death energy in their digestive fluids. This death energy aided Red Thorn in breaking down the dead spirits’ corpses.","As time passed, the flower sea and the camp of dead spirits dwindled rapidly.","It was unclear which side had the upper hand, but the sea of flowers had not yet receded under the onslaught of the dead spirits.","In fact, if Lin Yuan wished to expand the sea of flowers’ size, he could instruct Red Thorn to produce the Eyes of Relinquish to suppress the waves of dead spirits.","At present, each Eye of Relinquish stored enough energy for Red Thorn to generate a flower sea spanning 50 square kilometers.","After Red Thorn evolved, the Eyes of Relinquish became reliable sources of backup energy for Red Thorn, unlike in the past when using all of the Eyes of Relinquish would only enable the sea of flowers to expand to twice its original size.","Undeniably, there was another important reason for Lin Yuan’s sea of flowers being able to restrain the dead spirits, which was that Liu Wencheng had restrained the difficulty of the test when creating the environment. The strongest dead spirit would only be around as strong as a Diamond fey.","Every child ramet Red Thorn produced would be as strong as the strongest possible dead spirit.","There was no question that the battle between Liu Jie’s insect-species carcinoma feys and the dead spirits wave was much more intense and exciting to watch than the one between the sea of flowers and dead spirits.","Liu Jie summoned the Halberd Corner Sky-Defying Rhinoceros Beetle, and it was continuously adding metal-attributes to the insects produced by the insect-species carcinoma feys. The metal attributes significantly raised the insects’ overall power.","Elegance produced insects in a never-ending stream.","Liu Jie kept on using Shield Ladybugs as hosts for the Blade Queen Bee to make Blade Worms.","The primary sources of firepower were the Flowing Plasma Electricity Insects and Electromagnetic Chrysalises.","The Flowing Plasma Electricity Insects spewed out a lot of plasma that formed a gooey substance. This goo had a potent paralyzing effect, causing continuous electrical-type damage to any dead spirits that touched it.","Electrical-type attacks were especially harmful to dead spirits, surpassed only by light-type attacks.","When the Electromagnetic Chrysalises transformed into cocoons, they sped up plasma coagulation and ejection. When they assumed their moth form, they harnessed the plasma in their bodies to control nearby targets through electromagnetic forces.","The Flowing Plasma Electricity Insects and Electromagnetic Chrysalises were the main defenders against the dead spirits.","Meanwhile, Elegance created several batches of Six Treasures Cloud","Dragonflies, which enhanced the other insect-species carcinoma feys.","This boosted the speed, strength, defense, and energy reserves of the other insect-species carcinoma feys, enabling them to unleash more powerful attacks.","Elegance allocated and coordinated the insect-species carcinoma feys so that the carpet of fungi encroached into the dead spirits wave.","As the army of insects battled the dead spirits wave, a few of the insect-species carcinoma feys even captured some of the dead spirits with the intention of using them as food rations for the insect army.","Long Tao, Xia Qing, and the others’ performances could not be compared with the likes of Liu Jie and Lin Yuan. Nonetheless, they were still able to use their individual methods to drive off the dead spirits and demonstrate the incredible capabilities of members of a Radiance Hundred Sequence.","At such a time, all the hosts would be praying to land on the best perspective from which to watch the test. However, in this fight between hundreds of millions of lifeforms, thrilling battles broke out on every corner.","Poison Beauty and Lu Shuang chose the sea of flowers and sea of insects perspectives. This ensured that their channel could cover the two most exciting areas.","The live-streaming rooms that did not have two hosts had no choice but to pick one perspective.","The advantage that Poison Beauty and Lu Shuang’s channel had was thus made clear, and they immediately shot to the top of the ranking.","Poison Beauty and Lu Shuang did not have to spend too much time explaining the battle as the audience could see for themselves the shocking clash between the sea of flowers and sea of insects and dead spirits.","The two of them were not aware of Lin Yuan’s sea of flowers or Liu Jie’s insect-species carcinoma feys. abilities. If they tried to explain what was happening, it was likely that they would make mistakes.","[Fantasy World Nether Flames]: When Lord Liu Jie and Lord Lin Yuan crossed swords, the sea of sand quickly swallowed the insect army. Because of that, I didn’t think much of the insects’ strength. But the insects are now able to take over the dead spirits’ territory!","[Light Beauty Flower]: Lord Liu Jie sure is powerful! He summoned many more types of insect-species carcinoma feys in his battle against Lord Lin Yuan. This means that Lord Liu Jie isn’t even using his full power against the dead spirits!","[Fatty Dragon]: That’s right! Lord Lin Yuan is using the sea of flowers and not the sea of sand to fight the dead spirits. If he used the sea of sand and pools of quicksand, the dead spirits would be immediately dragged underground!","Lu Shuang noticed that many people in the live-streaming rooms were discussing Lin Yuan’s sea of sand and flowers. She also did not know which was stronger.","Lu Shuang felt that even if Lin Yuan did not use the full power of his elemental source-type lifeform in his battle against Liu Jie, Lin Yuan had an important reason for not choosing to use the sea of sand against the dead sprits.","This reason was that the sea of flowers could absorb death aura, but the sea of sand could not! This was why Lin Yuan chose to use the sea of flowers against the dead spirits.","Lin Yuan’s sea of flowers was not only fending off the dead spirits but was also protecting the participants.","“Have any of you noticed that the large dark red flowers in the sea of flowers have turned purplish-red? These flowers have been continuously absorbing death aura. There are also insects in the sea of insects that are absorbing death aura.","“Otherwise, with the death of all those dead spirits, the concentration of death aura in the test ground would have risen to 30% higher than its current level! Do you see that the participants in the sea of insects and sea of flowers haven’t been affected by the death aura?”","Lu Shuang’s words did not stop the other people in the live-streaming room from discussing and comparing the strength of the sea of flowers and sea of sand.","However, they were both Lin Yuan’s feys. Even if the audience racked their brains, the Source Sand would never fight against Red Thorn.","Frankly, the Source Sand had taken full control of the underground of the test ground. The Source Sand was hidden underground.","Once the sea of flowers could not address the danger, the sea of sand would immediately step in.","Lin Yuan always liked to ensure that he had backup plans, even if the activity had a very low level of risk.","Lin Yuan stayed a kilometer behind the participants and walked leisurely. He used the sand ball formed from the Source Sand to observe these 40 participants. He saw that they were beginning to fight subversively after learning of the theme of the test.","Mu Yan was the first to speak. “I’m sure all of you know of me, even if you aren’t familiar with me. My name is Mu Yan and I was Sequence #100 of the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence. I am back in the selection because I didn’t manage to make it to the top 90 ranks in the reranking.","“Lord Lin Yuan said that the participants will be split into 13 teams and be led by leaders in hunting the dead spirits. We don’t know how many participants have gathered in the other areas, but I’m sure that we will be able to increase any advantage we have if we band together!","“In my team, I will do my best to ensure the survival of every member while we’re fighting the dead spirits, and I won’t use any intentional methods to reduce the team’s size or harm the team members’ profits! I swear this on my honor.”","Mu Yan knew that there were likely other members of the team who also hoped to become leaders.","She had prior experience from last year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and knew how to present herself in a way that would allow her to stand out.","The best way to achieve this in this test was to become one of the leaders of the 13 teams.","Yang Nuanxin was the most special participant of those who were gathered there.","Now that the concentration of death aura in the air had been significantly lowered thanks to the sea of flowers, Yang Nuanxin was no longer as important. But she would become pivotal once the hunt for the dead spirits began!","However, Yang Nuanxin and the rest of the people close to her were insistent on revolving around the young man named Du Xing! If Du Xing also wanted to become a leader, Yang Nuanxin would definitely side with him!","With this awareness, Mu Yan did not try to engage with the rest of the participants. Instead, she immediately established her position as a leader and promised to secure the rights of her team members.","Now that they were at the tail end of the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, they were all rivals. Mu Yan could not bring up and hope to bank on her status as a member of the previous year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence.","She had only mentioned her background to provide evidence for her power.","While she spoke, Mu Yan looked around at the crowd with a serious gaze. Eventually, her gaze landed on Du Xing.","When their eyes met, Mu Yan knew he would be competing with her.","This was because after hearing what she said, his brows were knitted and he looked resistant.","Now that she understood her circumstances, Mu Yan spoke up first. “I am willing to become a team leader that leads the team to glory. Who is willing to take on the dead spirits with me? The participants in the other invigilators’ camps might not have asked about the contents of the test like I have. If we form teams first, it will be easier for us to recruit the other participants once we meet up with them!”","To this crowd, Mu Yan was no different from a celebrity.","All of them had watched her battles before the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection began.","She had three Diamond/Fantasy feys and was one of the most outstanding participants. Moreover, with her background, she could easily stand her ground against the leaders of the other teams.","In a test with such a chaotic design, it was likely that only three of the ten members of the previous years’ Radiance Hundred Sequence would be able to survive.","After weighing the pros and cons, many participants chose to join Mu Yan.","When Du Xing saw Mu Yan looking at him, he thought she would extend an invitation to him.","If she did try to invite him, he would definitely turn her down.","His previous experience of acquiescing and joining Yang Wenpeng had ended in deep regret. If he had not led his team in joining Yang Wenpeng’s team, more than twice the current number would have made it there.","It was difficult for Du Xing to trust others again when it came to such matters.","Mu Yan was not an exception despite being a member of the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence!","Aside from these considerations, Du Xing had his own selfish thoughts.","In the past, only the strongest soldiers made it into the Radiance Hundred Sequence. But now, leadership qualities held a higher weight. This was made clear by the complicated test format that the Radiance Sacred Hall had come up with.","It would be easier for him to pull ahead of the others by becoming one of the leaders.","When his eyes met Mu Yan’s, he could tell she intended to compete with him.","If he leveraged Yang Nuanxin’s fey’s abilities, he would stand a chance of winning!","However, most of the people present had chosen to join Mu Yan, and it was difficult to sway them toward leaving her to join him now. If they left a team immediately after joining it, they would come across as lacking team spirit, and their points would be deducted!","In this clash between him and Mu Yan, her clever move had allowed her to claim the upper hand.","Du Xing did not immediately declare his wish to become a leader. Instead, he told Yang Nuanxin, Qin Dong, and the others around him, “All of you have been following me so far. Are you willing to trust me again? We can form a team together.”","Qin Dong and Yang Nuanxin had been Du Xing’s teammates for five years and knew the kind of person he was.","“Big Brother Xing, we would have already joined the other team if we weren’t waiting for you to invite us!”","Yang Nuanxin waved her small fists and said, “Big Brother Xing, let’s create a team! My Cleansing Rain Sky Crane has been recovering. It will be able to recover most of its energy in another few hours!”","Du Xing’s question was a sign that he respected Yang Nuanxin, Qin Dong, and the rest.","Now that he had received their support, Du Xing declared.."]},{"number":2707,"title":"Chapter 2707 Lin Yuan’s Dimensional Wall!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2707 Lin Yuan’s Dimensional Wall!","“My name is Du Xing. I also intend to form a team. Everyone in the team will be an equal, and we will do our best to look out for each other. I swear on my Willpower Rune that all competition will be fair!”","Du Xing knew of his own situation. Unlike Mu Yan, he could not speak of honor and glory.","He had been part of a C-level guild club in the past. But before he could recruit Qin Dong, Yang Nuanxin, and the rest to join him and participate in the tournament, the C-level guild club was bought by a B-level guild club.","The B-level guild club had taken away the C-level guild club’s right to form teams. Hence, if Du Xing and the rest wanted to participate in tournaments, their only option was to participate in the lower-tier league.","Eventually, Du Xing left the guild club and even had to pay a handsome fee to dissolve his contract.","He could not use his accomplishments to drive his recruitment, nor did he proclaim Yang Nuanxin as his team’s signature.","The people present were not stupid and could see the difference in level between the two teams.","The biggest gesture of sincerity that Du Xing could make was swearing on his Willpower Rune that the competition between his team’s members would be fair.","A few participants who had been on the fence eventually chose to join Du Xing after a moment of pondering.","Yang Nuanxin’s irreplaceable abilities were important. Furthermore, he had guaranteed that the team would be a just one.","Mu Yan’s promise had been that she would not try to shave down the size of the team or hurt the members’ profits.","It was plain to see which team was offering more sincerity.","The size of the team might not be shaved down, but My Yan could still use her status as the leader to assign some members to handle the more dangerous or difficult tasks.","Mu Yan had managed to gather more than 20 people, while Du Xing had only managed to gather slightly more than ten.","Mu Yan did not show any displeasure at Du Xing managing to attract some members to his team. Rather, once the teams were formed, she walked over to him and reached out her hand with a smile.","“We have more members in our team, so it’ll be easier for us to look out for each other during combat.”","Du Xing, Yang Nuanxin, Qin Dong, and the rest assumed that Mu Yan was trying to throw down the gauntlet to establish her position as the head honcho.","However, Mu Yan went on to say, “I hope our two teams can work together. We will protect your team members, and your team will share the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane’s ability to clear death aura. But it will be up to the individual teams to hunt for themselves!”","Du Xing was momentarily stunned before he smiled at her with amazement.","She truly deserved to be someone who had stood out in the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and earned a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","With Lin Yuan and Gao Feng in the previous Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, there were truly only eight spots to fight for.","Mu Yan’s actions allowed her to come off as having a better character as well as being more masterful than him.","Once she realized that she would have to compete against him, she decided not to try and push him out but to work together instead. This helped her to protect her team, but it was also a skillful military move.","Yang Nuanxin’s Cleansing Rain Sky Crane was indeed capable of protecting 30 to 40 people, but Mu Yan’s team was much larger than Du Xing’s own, meaning that their hunting capabilities also differed significantly.","When spirit qi professionals worked together, they would be able to produce a multiplier effect.","Du Xing took a deep breath before he reached out his large hand to grasp Mu Yan’s smaller one.","Mu Yan was both trying to cooperate and scheme against him.","Regardless, he needed to take her up on her offer or risk losing the match.","This was a clash between leaders and not as ostentatious as one between fighters. They could have a dagger pressed up to the other’s throat at any moment and without making a sound.","As things stood, he was on the losing side. But once all the participants gathered together, he still stood a chance of tipping the scales!","“Okay, I hope we work well together and hold up our own ends of the bargain!”","Mu Yan’s lips twitched when she heard what Du Xing said.","If people were really fighting in the wilderness, those who trusted each other to keep their promises would be foolish. They needed to watch out for one another, even if they had made promises using Willpower Runes.","But now, they were in a test ground on Star Web, and all of them would keep their promises. They would be scorned for the rest of their lives if they went against their word in front of all the Radiance citizens.","Mu Yan was trying to secretly set up a ploy for Du Xing’s failure.","He would seem petty if he did not agree to work with her. This would damage his impression in the eyes of others.","But now that he had agreed to work with her, she could benefit from the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane.","Once they arrived at the main area and encountered the other participants, she and Du Xing could use the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane as bait to recruit team members!","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow as he watched Du Xing and Mu Yan clash.","He had noticed Mu Yan’s previous year’s performance. She was far more mature now, and it was evident she had grown substantially in the past year.","With her power and leadership skills, there was a high chance she could return to the Radiance Hundred Sequence as long as no unexpected accidents cropped up while they were battling dead spirits.","This year, almost 15 members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence would have to exit, meaning that the competition within the Radiance Hundred Sequence would be flattened.","As long as Mu Yan could return to the Radiance Hundred Sequence, it was almost a sure thing she would make it to the top 90 ranks next year.","As for Du Xing, Lin Yuan did not have much experience with him.","He would only be able to get a better sense of Du Xing’s abilities once all of the participants were gathered together.","...","In the few hours that the sea of flowers and sea of insects had been battling against the dead spirits, the Scholars whom Star Web had specially invited had conducted a detailed analysis of the dead spirits.","Most of the dead spirits were in insect form. The second-most common form was the beast form. The dead spirits in human form were the smallest in number but the most powerful. Many of the dead spirits in human form were able to command the dead spirits in beast form.","As for the specters, they all had relatively the same level of strength regardless of their form. They were immune to physical damage and could only be killed with elemental attacks.","The specters could not only affect the spirits of living creatures but their souls as well. They would even take over the bodies of dead spirits that had died.","As the dead spirits had only recently appeared in the main world, the Scholars were only able to come up with general categories for now. But it would not be long before they could draw up more detailed classifications.","The Radiance Federation had already started producing books related to the dead spirits and intended to incorporate them into the education curriculum from next year onward.","From now on, the grading of Creation Masters would also take their dead spirit knowledge into consideration. It was considered a part of the Fey Observer knowledge.","Once the Scholars examined the dead spirits’ bodies and checked if any part of their body could be useful and thus worth harvesting, any spiritual ingredients that came from their bodies would also become part of the Spiritual Ingredient Analysts’ curriculum.","The dead spirits crisis had only been ongoing for a few months, but it had already disrupted and changed the main world’s culture.","...","The instant the participants from all areas gathered together, the fighting intensified. Both the open and hidden battles put human nature on full display.","Luckily, everyone knew that this was the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and was relatively restrained. Nonetheless, their characters, tempers, and values could all be seen.","When Xia Qing spotted Lin Yuan, she walked over to him and said, “It’s a good thing that you and Liu Jie are here. Otherwise, I would have no idea how to fend off the dead spirits and reduce the concentration of the death aura-saturated air. My Suck Burst Oxygen Toad’s body can’t hold on for too long!”","Lin Yuan first turned to look at Liu Jie and gave him a thumbs up before telling Xia Qing, “Xia Qing, you don’t have to be self-deprecating. Feys will continuously improve while evolving their powers. There is a high chance that your feys will surprise you in all sorts of ways when they evolve to Creation Breed or Immortal Breed!”","Xia Qing smiled in a way that showed she neither agreed nor disagreed with him.","Xia Qing would never lose confidence in her future. She always kept her goals and expectations in mind!","Xia Qing wanted to protect the Radiance Federation just like her grandfather and parents had done.","However, she understood that her future prospects were tied to Lin Yuan. Because of the pure spirit qi and fire-elemental energy she had received from Lin Yuan, she managed to transform her feys’ bloodlines numerous times.","As a general Liu Wencheng had appointed, Lin Yuan had been seriously observing the battles between the participants.","Du Xing had surprised him greatly.","In terms of leadership qualities, Du Xing was just as competent as Mu Yan. Moreover, he was skilled at managing the atmosphere of his team.","Lin Yuan, Liu Jie, Xia Qing, and the other invigilators were not the only ones judging the participants. The audience could also tell which participants were doing better than others.","Lin Yuan did not shift his focus to the subsequent duels after the large-scale selection. Instead, he was concentrating on building the bases in the dimensional worlds’ territories.","Bai Qinghuan had sent a message to him to say that the Land Imps had worked hard and were done building the walls that traversed the five dimensional worlds.","The walls were tightly connected and formed an enormous protective net. They split the main world and the dimensional worlds it had fused with into two. There was now the world within the dimensional walls and the world outside of it.","All of the humans were living within the dimensional wall and were protected by it, while the dimensional lifeforms were all placed outside of the dimensional wall.","After Lin Yuan’s observation, he noticed that it was difficult for the dimensional lifeforms to coexist with the humans because many of the dimensional lifeforms were venomous.","It would take a very long time before the dimensional lifeforms could acclimate to living in the main world and be transformed by the spirit qi.","Selfishly, Lin Yuan also preferred the dimensional lifeforms to be the ones to fight the dead spirits. This would protect the humans while increasing the dimensional lifeforms’ evolution rate.","[Bai Qinghuan]: Young Master, the dimensional world that cuts through this world is much stronger than I expected! There are many spatial traps below the dimensional wall. Once any lifeform outside of the wall steps into the spatial traps, they will be sent to the banishment space created by the Space-Cracking Crystals! I have allocated two Samsara Realm Dictators to guard the banishment space. They will handle the lifeforms sent to the banishment space accordingly.","Ever since Lin Yuan took control of the subterranean world and attained various high-grade metal spiritual ingredients, he used them to accomplish many tasks he could not achieve in the past.","This dimensional wall would not have been built if he had not discovered the Space-Cracking Crystal mineral veins.","[Lin Yuan]: Covering the ground with spatial traps will prevent the dead dimensional lifeforms and dead spirits from crossing over into the human world. But the spatial traps won’t be able to stop them from going over the wall! You should be done building the aerial defenses as well, right?","Lin Yuan had used the dimensional treasures to take absolute control of the dimensional lifeforms.","But after the dimensional worlds were fused with the main world, the dimensional treasures were joined with the main world. This meant that Lin Yuan could not use those dimensional treasures to take control of new dimensional lifeforms.","The dimensional lifeforms continuously reproduced after the dimensional worlds were fused with the main world. As subsequent generations of dimensional lifeforms were born, Lin Yuan’s control over them would diminish.","Low-grade dimensional lifeforms had very low intelligence, so Lin Yuan wanted to prevent them from causing harm to the humans.","When Bai Qinghuan saw Lin Yuan’s message, she hurriedly responded.","[Bai Qinghuan]: Don’t worry, Young Master. I would never send a message to you unless the aerial defenses have been completed! I embedded a large amount of Gravity Secret Silver and Attract Magnetic Force Ores. Together, they magnify the Attract Magnetic Force Ores’ effects!","[Bai Qinghuan]: The dead spirits and dimensional lifeforms won’t be able to cross the dimensional wall unless they are stronger than Creation Breed. The gravitational forces will drag them down. If there are dead dimensional lifeforms and dead spirits that are stronger than Creation Breed, the Attract Magnetic Force Ores’s magnetic field will be triggered and alert the experts close to the wall!","Bai Qinghuan had perfectly accomplished the task that Lin Yuan had given her.","[Lin Yuan]: Qinghuan, take the Land Imps with you and go along the wall to help the weak human federations build their bases. I will send help to you. Don’t forget that your future won’t be limited to this Class 2 world!","Initially, Bai Qinghuan only wanted to receive more tasks from Lin Yuan. If he gave her more tasks, it would mean he acknowledged her.","The more capable people joined Lin Yuan, the fewer opportunities each would get to be sent out on tasks.","But not only had Lin Yuan assigned a new task to her, but he had also given her a promise.","Bai Qinghuan already knew that Lin Yuan had set his sights beyond this world.","Given what he said, he would take her with him when he went to the other world!","...","While Lin Yuan was communicating with Bai Qinghuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper, two figures appeared at the Four Seasons Mountain’s foot. They stared up at the imposing mountain with trepidation."]},{"number":2708,"title":"Chapter 2708 Tower Canon’s Misunderstanding!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2708 Tower Canon’s Misunderstanding!","One of the figures was wearing a light green attire and wrapped out in a shawl with a faint tangerine tinge. Her light green hair hung just past her shoulders, and her delicate, gentle eyes glinted brightly.","She was wearing a headband over her forehead that had five faintly colored gems on it. The stones contained various types of energy. When one looked from the side, the five gems seemed to form a horn protruding from her forehead.","Next to her was a burly figure wearing light green leather and a unique dark green metal battle skirt. The battle skirt hung from his waist, but it did not make him seem feminine at all. Rather, it added a dashing air to his demeanor.","He was holding a folding fan covered with various orchid patterns. However, the orchids did not seem to be in a healthy state and were covered in holes from insect consumption.","When one took a closer look at this man wearing green armor, one would notice that there was a layer of insects clustered tightly together all over his armor. These were the same insects as the one on his folding fan that were consuming the orchids.","These two figures were Third Page Violet Light Green and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid.","Violet Light Green had undertaken an enormous risk by trying to liaise with Epoch God Palace on Tower Canon’s behalf. There was enmity between Tower Canon and Epoch God Palace.","But for the sake of her own profits, Violet Light Green had no other choice.","Now that the dead world’s roots had fused with this Class 2 world, there was no way out for Tower Canon.","Violet Light Green did not want to let things drag on like Second Page Warbler Candle and Fifth Page Falling Rainbow did.","First Page Crimson had been vying for the position of leader of their group.","It was true that Crimson had the strongest capabilities out of all of them.","However, he had yet to earn the trust of the others because he always recoiled at the first sign of trouble and was unwilling to step up to shoulder risk for the sake of the group. This caused his image as the leader to be a shaky one.","Violet Light Green had already steeled herself. But when she arrived at the Four Seasons Mountain’s foot and looked up at the towering mountain, she could not help but be gripped by fear.","In Tower Canon’s last clash against Epoch God Palace, they were all severely injured by a girl and a wave of her hand.","The girl had walked out of one of Epoch God Palace’s palaces. There were a total of four such palaces.","Tower Canon did not have the courage to act recklessly when they faced Epoch God Palace.","Violet Light Green could not figure out why Epoch God Palace had chosen to come to this Class 2 world. Could they have foreseen what was happening and had come with the intention of taking Tower Canon down?","Violet Light Green shook this thought out of her mind.","Cavity Orchid said solemnly, “Violet Light Green, you have already spoken. We won’t be able to avoid meeting the people from Epoch God Palace. It’s true that they are already on the move! Epoch God Palace’s doors are opening for the first time in all these years. We will only be able to carry out our plan if we understand what their plans are!”","Violet Light Green nodded.","Ideally, their objectives did not overlap with that of Epoch God Palace. If they did, the only possible result would be Tower Canon finding an alternative path.","Violet Light Green took two steps forward and tugged on Cavity Orchid’s sleeve.","“Cavity Orchid, of the eight of us, we are on the best terms. I used to encourage you to follow Crimson’s orders because we need a leader. But now, I am fully disappointed in Crimson!”","Cavity Orchid reached out and combed down Violet Light Green’s stray hairs before saying gently, “Violet Light Green, I’ve never had hopes for Crimson, so I can’t say that I’m disappointed in him.","“If we’re talking about disappointment, I’m already disappointed with the entire Tower Canon. We all know what the emergence of the demon insects signifies. Even at such a juncture, no one was willing to step forward.","“When you eventually did, the others decided to sit back and piggyback off of your effort instead of coming with you to communicate with Epoch God Palace. They would definitely take us more seriously if all eight of us came together.”","Violet Light Green had not expected her casual venting to lead to a stream of grievances from Cavity Orchid.","Alas, what could they do? Ever since they fused the dead world’s roots with this Class 2 world, all their fates were henceforth bound to this Class 2 world.","If only they had not been so anxious, they could have returned to the Sky Beyond the Clouds with the dead world’s roots.","There was no need for Epoch God Palace to release the demon insects in order to stop the dead spirits disaster.","The treasure that Epoch God Palace held could separate ley lines. If Epoch God Palace wanted to put an end to the dead spirits crisis, they could extract this Class 2 world’s ley lines before purifying it. Even if they did not manually purify the ley lines, the ley lines would be able to purify themselves as long as they were not enveloped by death aura.","This meant that a third faction from the Sky Beyond the Clouds was present in this Class 2 world.","Optimistically, Epoch God Palace might not be taking action because of Tower Canon but this other faction.","The dead spirits crisis had been progressing for some time.","Epoch God Palace had not taken action at the beginning. They only started to make a move when the demon insects appeared.","At that moment, a powerful force pressed down on Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid. A chilling voice echoed in their ears. “Tower Canon, the insects that crawled out from dirt. You have been hovering around Epoch God Palace for some time. Are you here to try and rob us again?”","Under the crushing pressure, Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid only managed to hold on by releasing their own auras.","This gargantuan force was completely foreign to them. Clearly, it was not coming from the same expert who had injured them the last time.","But it was likely that the source of this force and the expert who had injured them last time had similar levels of power.","This expert had to be part of Epoch God Palace’s upper echelon!","It was as though Violet Light Green had not heard the mocking edge in Autumn’s tone and started to explain, “Tower Canon made a mistake all those years ago. We have learned our lesson. This time, we come with sincerity and would like to have a chat with Epoch God Palace. We hope that both sides will be able to work together to achieve a win-win situation!”","Cavity Orchid added, “That’s right. That incident came about from one of our members making a decision on their own. The rest of us have no intention of making an enemy out of Epoch God Palace!”","Autumn’s figure appeared directly above Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid.","The pair of eyes that resembled that of a phoenix looked down at Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid.","Autumn could not touch Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid until he was certain about whether the two of them had ties to Lord Saint. He also wanted to chat with them to find out more information.","However, Autumn disliked what Cavity Orchid said about Tower Canon trying to rob Epoch God Palace because of the unauthorized decisions of one of its members. He also did not trust Cavity Orchid’s explanation.","Since only one of the members of Tower Canon had decided to steal the Epoch Clock, why had the rest of the Eight Pages gotten involved?","Epoch God Palace had been waiting for Lord Saint’s awakening. Autumn had never been concerned with Tower Canon, the traitors from a Class 3 world.","Lord Saint’s awakening was not only related to this world that had recently been promoted to Class 2. Any factor could have contributed to his awakening.","In Autumn’s view, Tower Canon’s existence was an important factor in triggering Lord Saint’s awakening!","If Tower Canon had not tried to steal the Epoch Clock, Spring would not have lost control and stepped in.","Spring had been extremely self-reproachful because of this. She feared that injuring Tower Canon to the point of near death may have affected Lord Saint’s awakening.","Because he knew all of this, Cavity Orchid and Violet Light Green’s words were meaningless to Autumn.","“Why does Tower Canon want to work with us? We don’t care about this Class 2 world, so there shouldn’t be anything about our actions that is holding you back!”","Autumn’s voice was full of derision.","His revulsion of Tower Canon was not because they were weaker than him.","Power was not the yardstick of a lifeform’s worth. Even ants served their own purpose.","There were many ways to criticize Tower Canon’s existence.","They did not try to prevent their dead world from fusing with the Class 3 world because they wanted to protect their home but because they coveted the Class 3 world’s roots.","They had failed to achieve this but still did not give up. Instead, they brought the dead world’s roots with them and fled to this world. This Class 2 world was now being used as their incubator.","Tower Canon’s goal was to sacrifice all of the lifeforms in this world and use the death aura already present to fuse the dead world with this world.","Tower Canon was an invader, a robber, and a destroyer.","Even if this group was stronger than Autumn, it would be difficult for him to respect them.","Even if Autumn believed Lord Saint had not awakened, he would not side with such a group!","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid could hear the mocking and derision in Autumn’s voice.","However, they were struck by something that he said.","Autumn had said that Epoch God Palace was not focused on this Class 2 world. Did that mean that Tower Canon would not earn Epoch God Palace’s fury by trying to take over this Class 2 world?","If that were the case, they would not need to continue conversing with Epoch God Palace.","In truth, Violet Light Green was very against Tower Canon working with Epoch God Palace. If they worked with Epoch God Palace, Tower Canon would never have any say in decision-making.","Autumn did not know that his words had caused Violet Light Green to land on such a big misunderstanding.","Autumn’s task was to interact with Tower Canon. Now that Tower Canon’s members had initiated contact with him, his task was considered complete.","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid looked at each other and saw delight in each other’s eyes.","“Tower Canon would really like to work with Epoch God Palace. It’s really a shame that we won’t be able to! If Epoch God Palace needs our help in the future, feel free to ask.”","After confirming that Epoch God Palace was not interested in this Class 2 world, Tower Canon was no longer afraid of them. Instead, they could try to form a connection with Epoch God Palace.","Once the dead world’s roots were fused with this Class 2 world, Tower Canon would do its best to promote it to Class 3.","They might need Epoch God Palace’s help in the future.","Autumn did not intend to hold the two members of Tower Canon back.","But just as they were about to leave, a thought struck him, and he stopped them.","The two of them froze and turned around. They did not know why Autumn had stopped them.","Could it be that he had said what he said to distract them?","At that moment, Autumn asked gravely, “Is there a member of Tower Canon who is rapidly transforming?”","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid’s expressions turned stony, and they began to ponder deeply.","There were only eight true members of Tower Canon.","The Eight Pages that roamed the world were only their replacements that held their place while they slept.","There were also the Lead Chanters and Singers in every tower.","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid had never paid attention to these Lead Chanters and Singers.","After the Class 2 world was fused with the dead world’s roots, the Lead Chanters and Singers were turned into dead dimensional lifeforms.","Tower Canon did not have a character that fit Autumn’s description.","The instant he saw Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid’s expressions, Autumn had his answer.","It was likely that Lord Saint was not siding with them.","However, Autumn could not be fully certain. Lord Saint’s transformation might have been hidden extremely deeply.","As Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid left Four Seasons Mountain, they continued mulling over Autumn’s question.","Did this mean that Epoch God Palace was looking for someone who was rapidly transforming?","The youths in this world often encountered various opportunities, and there were many who were rapidly transforming.","Why was Epoch God Palace looking for someone like that?","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid contemplated for a moment and discussed this matter but were unable to come up with a conclusion.","Eventually, the two of them decided to stop focusing on this matter.","Since Tower Canon did not care about this Class 2 world, it was time for Tower Canon to fight back against the demon insects!","The demon insects were indeed a powerful species. Every demon insect empress in her prime had the power to ruin a Class 4 world.","However, this was not the Sky Beyond the Clouds, and there was no pure spirit qi for the demon insects to absorb. Hence, the demon insects’ potential was severely limited. Relative to the potential of the demon insects, this demon insect’s colony was puny.","The demon insects could indeed use death aura as fuel, but there were other dimensional lifeforms in the dead world aside from those that emanated death aura.","Tower Canon had sent out the dimensional lifeforms that could emanate death aura first because they wanted to change the main world’s environment.","The hunters in the dead world were capable of consuming the demon insects.","If they could capture the demon insects’ mother insect and turn her into a dead spirit, Tower Canon would gain another weapon for combat."]},{"number":2709,"title":"Chapter 2709: Myth Breed Golden Wings!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2709: Myth Breed Golden Wings!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","With the entire Radiance Federation watching, the curtain closed on the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","Ten new members filled the last ten ranks of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. Among the ten were Du Xing and Mu Yan, who had been eliminated during the Radiance Hundred Sequence reranking.","Yang Nuanxin and the Cleansing Rain Sky Crane’s ability to drive off death aura allowed her to perform well during the selection. But she did not manage to occupy one of the ten spots.","Nonetheless, after the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection ended, she received an invitation to join the Spirit Guards, and they offered her very generous terms.","After joining the Spirit Guards, Yang Nuanxin would become a specialized expert.","Yang Nuanxin enthusiastically accepted the Spirit Guards’ offer immediately.","Her biggest worry had been Yang Wenpeng seeking revenge on her after the selection ended. Given his temper, just seeking revenge on her would not be enough. He would involve her parents and the entire collateral branch as well.","But now that she had accepted the Spirit Guards’ invitation and was going to be a specialized expert, she had a position as a public official, and Yang Wenpeng could not cause trouble for her.","As long as her family could securely latch themselves to the Spirit Guards, they","would be able to break free from the main branch. At that point, they would no longer be under their thumb!","Mu Yan was over the moon that she managed to return to the Radiance","Hundred Sequence.","She had taken stock of her own circumstances.","Her biggest disadvantage relative to the other members of the Radiance","Hundred Sequence was her age.","She was only 23 years old this year and could not be compared to abnormalities like Lin Yuan, but she was considered one of the youngest members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence. The other members with whom she had to compete were all around 26 to 27 years old.","The three- to four-year gap between them gave them a power advantage that was very difficult for her to overcome.","This left Mu Yan feeling extremely regretful.","She should have listened to her father and waited until she was 25 or 26 years old before she tried out for a spot in the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","There were both pros and cons to joining the Radiance Hundred Sequence early.","The younger one was when joining the Radiance Hundred Sequence, the longer their tenancy would be.","After passing this selection, she just needed to put herself through the wringer for another year. This year’s worth of time would be sufficient to enable her to grow rapidly. It was basically a guarantee that she would be able to make it into the top 90 ranks next year.","Du Xing had yet to regain his senses.","Lin Yuan was the one who had selected him to participate in the final dueling stage.","Otherwise, he would not have made the cut based on his accumulated points.","Every assessor was able to select members of their team to save.","Du Xing thus became the only participant Lin Yuan had saved. This was an unimaginable honor.","During the dueling stage, he was able to counter most of his opponents and only lost one round. He eventually earned the ninth spot in the final ten.","Before participating in the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, he never dared to dream that he would become Sequence #99 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","He knew that invitations from major guild clubs would start streaming in tomorrow once the Radiance Sacred Hall officially declared his position. He would not only be able to become part of the guild club’s main team but also recruit his old teammates into the guild club.","The Radiance Sacred Hall was also going to nurture a Bronze/Legend fey for him that would be tailored to his Willpower Rune.","All he needed to do was complete the Radiance Sacred Hall’s tasks and earn resources, and he would be able to nurture the Bronze/Legend fey.","With access to the provision of such resources, his future was unlimited!","Lin Yuan was a veteran member of the Radiance Hundred Sequence and immediately returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion once the induction ceremony for the new members was completed.","He had left the Mother of Bloodbath in the Return from Faraway to look after Shiny.","Feys with the Barren bloodline were powerful. Logic dictated that the more powerful the fey, the more capable they would be of handling their own World Cleansing to evolve to Myth Breed.","But feys with the Barren bloodline had to tackle much more intense World Cleansings than regular feys. Hence, there was a high chance that they would end up injuring their roots if they tried taking on their World Cleansings on their own, resulting in irreparable damage.","When the Mother of Bloodbath used its full power now, it was able to wield Immortal Breed combat power.","Lin Yuan did not have to worry at all if the Mother of Bloodbath was the one helping Shiny to evolve.","The Mother of Bloodbath had already sent a message through the Thoughts Letter Paper to tell Lin Yuan that Shiny had evolved successfully.","Although there had still been a few bumps during the evolution process, the Mother of Bloodbath deemed Shiny’s evolution to be a perfect one. It also marveled at how comprehensive Shiny’s abilities were.","This caused Lin Yuan to form a conjecture.","As a Heavenly Family Fey, the Mother of Bloodbath had very high standards. It would never praise Shiny if it did not deserve it. Shiny’s transformation had to have truly stunned the Mother of Bloodbath.","But why did the Mother of Bloodbath marvel at how comprehensive Shiny’s abilities were?","The Mother of Bloodbath had already seen Shiny before it evolved to Myth Breed. If it wanted to praise Shiny, it could have done so then instead of waiting until now.","The Mother of Bloodbath’s praise had to mean that Shiny’s abilities had improved again!","Presently, the only area in which Shiny was lacking was its absence of healing abilities. Could Shiny have gained healing abilities when it evolved to Suzerain/Myth?","Frankly, with the Jasmine Lily, there was no need for Lin Yuan’s other feys to gain healing-related abilities because its healing abilities were already sufficiently well- rounded!","Lin Yuan hurriedly entered the Return from Faraway Mansion and saw a golden-haired young man sitting next to the Mother of Bloodbath.","This golden-haired young man looked rather similar to Lin Yuan, but his eyes were wilder. His long golden eyebrows were as sharp as swords, and his hooked nose had an exotic charm. It was clear that this was a fey in human form.","The Mother of Bloodbath said sharply, “You have already evolved to Myth Breed and should be intelligent enough to tell right from wrong. You should be trying to learn manners instead of trying to destroy homes! If I see you trying to ruin the furniture made from jade-textured wood again, I will spank you again!”","Shiny shrunk back its neck. Its face, which resembled Lin Yuan’s own, took on an expression of nervous fear.","Shiny was a feather-winged species fey with the Barren bloodline and could be considered a bird.","The Mother of Bloodbath was a bird-catching spider and was considered the natural enemy of bird-species feys. It posed a big threat to them.","Furthermore, the Mother of Bloodbath’s grade was above that of Shiny.","The Mother of Bloodbath was always kind toward Lin Yuan’s feys and was on very good terms with Chimey and Genius.","At first, the Mother of Bloodbath had been the same way toward Shiny. However, after Shiny underwent the World Cleansing and changed into human form, it crushed many pieces of jade-textured furniture in the Return from Faraway Mansion. It was more mischievous than young human children!","Initially, the Mother of Bloodbath assumed that Shiny was just curious and could not control its own strength. But later, it realized that Shiny saw the pieces of jade-textured furniture as toys it could use to destress.","When it saw Shiny reach out its hand toward the wall hanging that depicted all of Sky City’s important members, the Mother of Bloodbath could not stop itself from forcefully spanking Shiny a few times.","This immediately straightened the mischievous Shiny out.","When the Mother of Bloodbath first saw Shiny’s face that greatly resembled Lin Yuan’s, it felt conflicted about disciplining Shiny.","But it did not take long before the Mother of Bloodbath realized that Shiny and Lin Yuan had completely different mindsets and personalities!","If it did not properly discipline Shiny, it would cause trouble for Lin Yuan!","As Lin Yuan’s Path Protector, it had the responsibility of teaching Shiny as Lin Yuan had left it in its care.","When Shiny spotted Lin Yuan, it immediately pouted and reached out its hand to him.","The Mother of Bloodbath had sensed Lin Yuan’s presence when he was ten kilometers away from the Return from Faraway Mansion,","It told Lin Yuan about everything that had transpired. He had not expected Shiny to be so mischievous.","Lin Yuan always showered affection on his feys, but he would not tolerate his feys causing destruction.","He walked up to Shiny to hug it before saying seriously, “Shiny, do you remember Uncle Hu who made your nest? He painstakingly carved all the pieces you crushed. These are all products of his effort and labor. You must respect the hard work of others! If you like crushing jade-textured wood, I can give you some materials.”","Lin yuan’s expression was stern. A year naa passea since Lin yuan contractea Shiny. However, he could not nurture it because he lacked dragon liver and phoenix blood.","Shiny spent most of its time in the past year playing in the marsh world. It seemed that its carefree lifestyle of the past year had caused it to develop some bad habits.","Lin Yuan intended to stay with Shiny for some time so he could properly educate it.","Shiny hurriedly nodded its small head when it saw Lin Yuan’s stern expression. Shiny did not want Lin Yuan to treat it the same way that the Mother of Bloodbath did.","When Lin Yuan saw it nodding obediently, he ruffled Shiny’s soft golden hair.","To be frank, Shiny was very pleasant in the eyes!","Although Genius also looked like Lin Yuan when it was in its human form, its demeanor was completely different from that of Shiny. Their differing demeanors reminded Lin Yuan of the first and second male leads from the television shows in his previous life.","“Lin Yuan, I am just used to scratching and grabbing. Moreover, the jade-textured wood is very soft, and I momentarily lost myself in touching it. You don’t have to prepare materials for me. I can hold myself back!”","In order to express its resolution, Shiny gently waved its fists.","When Lin Yuan’s expression softened, Shiny affectionately kissed Lin Yuan’s cheek.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Shiny.","[Fey Name]: Golden Wings [Fey Species]: Barren-species/feather-winged-species","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Wind [Fey Quality]: Myth Il","Abilities:","[Snapped Neck Falling Death]: When its sharp claws make contact with a target, the target’s neck will be snapped. At the same moment, the Golden Wings will extract the target’s soul and absorb the soul into its feathers. The soul will imbue the storm patterns on the feathers with intelligence.","[Flowing Wind Claws]: When the wind elements in the Golden Wings’ feathers are released into the environment, it will be able to control the surrounding winds and manipulate it to attack its opponent. The attacked target will feel like it is being slashed by claws. After attacking a target, the Golden Wings will also be able to inject elements into its target through explosions and cause double the amount of damage.","[Rapid Wind Whistle]: By flapping its wings to activate wind-elemental energy, it will simultaneously let out a roar that causes both physical and elemental damage to a designated target. A headwind will also lower the target’s speed. Each time a headwind is released, its own speed will be increased.","[Hurricane Added Protection]: A vicious hurricane shield will be added to one’s own body. Every time elemental damage is inflicted on it, the hurricane shield will absorb the damage before reflecting it. The hurricane shield can also absorb wind-elemental energy from the surroundings to replenish the wind-elemental energy in its body.","[Folded Wings Wind Valley]: With the Golden Wings at the center, an environment charged with wind-elemental energy will be formed.","Wind-elemental energy will be continuously produced in this environment. When it makes a sacrifice to this territory, the wind-elemental energy will be absorbed into its bloodline and trigger a one-time explosion.","[Disappearing Wind Attack]: Its body will be combined with wind elements. Even a slight breeze will be enough for it to hide within. While it is hiding in the wind, it will be immune to damage as long as the wind remains.","[Revived Seasonal Winds]: The wind elements’ state will be changed. The wind elements will gain powerful healing abilities. Targets will be healed wherever the winds exist. They will continue to heal as long as the wind does not stop moving.","Exclusive Skill:","[Unset State]: When interacting with another fey, the Golden Wings can copy the fey’s exclusive skill and triggered abilities. Unset State will then turn into the copied exclusive skill and triggered ability. The abilities can only be switched out once every lunar cycle.","[Wind’s Descendant]: By placing itself as the heart of all wind elements, it will become the eye of a hurricane and control all of the surrounding wind elements. It will become the master while all other winds will become its disciple.","[Summoning Wind Changing Spirit]: Use wind elements to accommodate other elemental energy and turn them into vassals of the wind elements. In extreme environments, the accommodated elemental energy can change its own attributes and allow it to become better affiliated with the environment, as well as use elemental attacks of different elemental types.","Lin Yuan noticed that the Suzerain ability, Revived Seasonal Winds, was indeed a healing ability! But after reading through its effects, he did not think it was a pity that it was a group healing ability.. Instead, he could not be more thrilled!"]},{"number":2710,"title":"Chapter 2710 Tower Canon’s Counterattack!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2710 Tower Canon’s Counterattack!","The Jasmine Lily’s healing abilities could be categorized into close-range and far-range individual entity healing, as well as close-range and far-range group healing.","The Jasmine Lily was not very skilled at far-range group healing.","But Shiny’s Revived Seasonal Winds would imbue the wind elements with healing abilities.","In an environment where the wind was constantly flowing, the targets that Shiny had designated would be recovered.","It would not deplete too much of Shiny’s energy to use wind elements to heal other targets.","Once wind began flowing, it would only grow stronger until a powerful external force restrained it. This meant that Revived Seasonal Winds’ healing effects would only grow stronger.","As long as Shiny was present, the healing effects of Wind’s Descendant would persist.","This far-range group healing abilities would lead to unimaginable effects during large-scale war.","But in Lin Yuan’s opinion, Shiny’s biggest improvement came from its Myth Breed exclusive skill, Summoning Wind Changing Spirit.","Summoning Wind Changing Spirit would allow Shiny to use the wind elements in its body to accommodate other elemental energy and turn them into vassals of wind-elemental energy.","Hence, Shiny could change its own attributes, after which its own abilities would also be altered.","It would then harvest the attributes that would be the most effective against the enemy and use them in its attacks.","While Shiny was changing its attributes, it would be able to tap into the elements’ reactive effects to strengthen the damage it could inflict.","Lin Yuan raised his hand and took out hundreds of fire-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls from his spatial equipment.","Lin Yuan brought the fire-type elemental pearls over to Shiny so it could use Summoning Wind Changing Spirit to absorb them.","The hundreds of fire-type elemental pearls were definitely insufficient for Shiny.","Lin Yuan was not trying to use Summoning Wind Changing Spirit to increase Shiny’s power. He was just trying to see if Wind’s Descendant would change after its attributes were changed.","Shiny in human form absorbed the fire-type elemental pearls like a child eating sweets. Shiny might look like an elegant gentleman, but it was not gracefully eating the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls at all.","It grabbed tens of elemental pearls in fistfuls and swallowed them. It would chew occasionally.","The fire-type elemental pearls burst open in Shiny’s mouth, but none of the fire-elemental energy escaped.","After Shiny was done consuming these fire-type heavenly-maiden-grades, but before Lin Yuan could say anything, Shiny’s aura suddenly changed.","The light and agile wind elements swirling around Shiny changed into fervent fire-elemental energy.","When Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Shiny, he saw that the exclusive skill Wind’s Descendant had turned into Fire’s Descendant.","[Fire’s Descendant]: By placing itself as the heart of all fire elements, it will become a volcano and control all of the surrounding fire elements. It will become the master, while all other flames will become its disciples.","The description of the exclusive skill had completely changed to suit that of fire elements.","Lin Yuan pressed his lips together with suppressed excitement.","Summoning Wind Changing Spirit not only allowed Shiny to gain the abilities of various elements but also allowed it to be the ruler of the elemental territory and suppress other lifeforms belonging to the same element.","If Lin Yuan wanted to battle Xia Qing again, he could change Shiny’s attributes to fire-type. Not only would the territory of fire be unable to cause harm to Shiny, but it would even bolster it.","Shiny stared unblinkingly at Lin Yuan. It could tell from his expression that he was happy with its growth.","Shiny reached out its hand and shook it in front of Lin Yuan.","“Yuan, do you still have the elemental pearls? They will help me to take on more and different kinds of opponents during combat!”","Lin Yuan tapped Shiny’s beak.","“I have more than enough of the elemental pearls. I am only concerned that you won’t be able to digest too many at once!”","Lin Yuan took out large chests full of various types of elemental pearls that the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope had organized. There were around 3,000 elemental pearls in every chest.","Lin Yuan said, “Shiny, go ahead and eat your fill. There are only four types of elemental pearls now—wind, fire, earth, and water. I will provide you with rare elements in the future so you can increase your power.”","Because of Summoning Wind Changing Spirit, Shiny was similar to the Flower Calamity Beautiful Devil in that nurturing it involved absorbing various types of pure elemental energy.","Although Lin Yuan did not use the Flower Calamity Beautiful Devil and Frigid often during battle, they were extremely important to him, and he had not stopped supplying them with resources.","The Flower Calamity Beautiful Devil and Frigid were currently accumulating their power.","After Lin Yuan was promoted to an A-rank spirit qi professional, he did not rush into evolving their grades and qualities because these were not vital to the two of them. The evolution of their bloodlines was the most important!","Lin Yuan intended to wait until their bloodlines reached a certain point before he tried to evolve their grades and qualities. His aim was to use the evolution of their grades and qualities to enable their bloodlines to break through.","The Mother of Bloodbath could not stop the look of envy from spreading across its face when it saw Lin Yuan providing Shiny with resources.","The Mother of Bloodbath was not jealous that Lin Yuan was treating Shiny well.","The Mother of Bloodbath believed that it received even better treatment from Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had even been ready to give up his life for the sake of helping it with its World Cleansing!","The Mother of Bloodbath was jealous that Shiny had access to the best resources from the onset of its life. It thus had a perfect foundation that many other feys of the Barren bloodline did not have. It was truly born with a golden spoon in its mouth!","The Mother of Bloodbath had been watching over Shiny at home and experienced the life of a stay-at-home mother. Hence, it had been unable to watch the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","“Lin Yuan, did everything go well with the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection?”","Lin Yuan shook his head. “Things didn’t exactly go smoothly. It almost failed. Elder Liu was too anxious and set the difficulty of the test too high.”","Although Lin Yuan and Liu Jie’s interference managed to allow the selection to end well, the high bar of difficulty of the test would inevitably have caused some excellent youths to drown in the wave of death spirits due to their bad luck.","Lin Yuan felt that this was a pity.","The Mother of Bloodbath did not understand what Lin Yuan was trying to say. In its opinion, the harder the test, the more outstanding the survivors.","The Mother of Bloodbath was more interested in Lin Yuan rather than the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","The Radiance Knight and Radiance Envoy selections would take place after the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","As one of the contenders for the Radiance Envoys, he needed to head to the Radiance Sacred Hall to watch the Radiance Knight selection.","It was clear that Liu Jie had the potential to be a Radiance Envoy, but he still chose to join the Radiance Knight selection instead. Just like Wen Yu, he would become Lin Yuan’s aide.","Long Tao, Gao Feng, and An He were also participating in the Radiance Knight selection.","Lin Yuan was taken aback by An He’s participation but quickly figured out why he had made that decision.","Lin Yuan, Zong Ze, Gu Lang, and Xia Qing were not the only ones participating in the Radiance Envoy selection. The previous generation of Radiance Envoys would also be participating. They had to knock the previous generation of Radiance Envoys out of their positions.","Just like the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection, the format of the Radiance Envoy selection had also changed.","After Lin Yuan and the rest became Radiance Envoys, they would have to accept challenges from subsequent generations every few years.","The dead spirit crisis occurred after the Major Federation Union was established. It became clear that there would be no Major Federation Meeting. Because the federations now had different levels of power, they did not need to compete or be ranked during the meeting.","The federation envoys were iconic to their federations.","An He struggled to compete with Lin Yuan, Zong Ze, Xia Qing, and the rest, much less try to take on the current Radiance Envoys.","After understanding this, An He decided to give up on aspiring to become a Radiance Envoy. Instead, he set his sights on the Radiance Knight selection.","He felt fully confident in passing.","A day was enough time for Shiny to absorb these elemental pearls.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie needed to stay the night in the Radiance Sacred Hall to take part in the oath-taking of the Radiance Knight selection.","In one of his rare periods of respite, Lin Yuan returned to his room and had a good sleep. This sleep could only be described as rejuvenating.","The next day, just as Lin Yuan was about to head to the Radiance Sacred Hall, he saw that the Moon Empress had personally paid a visit to the Return from Faraway Mansion.","He was well aware of how busy she was. She had just finished presiding over the Major Federation Union meeting and could not even watch the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. She should be in the Radiance Sacred Hall now.","The instant his eyes landed on the Moon Empress, alarm bells rang in Lin Yuan’s head.","It was likely that the dead spirits crisis had taken a turn. There was no other reason for the Moon Empress to appear here at such a time.","Furthermore, this change had to compromise the demon insects’ defense of the main world!","Otherwise, regardless of what happened in the dead spirits crisis, the Moon Empress could have contacted him through the Thoughts Letter Paper or by phone call.","When he saw the austere expression on her face, Lin Yuan asked, “Master, what happened over on the dead spirits’ side?”","Lin Yuan’s voice was full of suspicion.","If the demon insects had encountered a powerful enemy, Keira should have sent him a message about it. But since she had not contacted him, it meant that she could address whatever was happening over on the dead spirits’ side.","The Moon Empress solemnly said, “We intentionally retained 18 Dead Spirits Wells to train our soldiers and didn’t instruct the demon insects to defend these 18 Dead Spirits Wells. Since yesterday, these 18 Dead Spirits Wells have been producing dead spirits at accelerated rates. The numbers doubled within a mere eight hours! Tower Canon must be up to something!”","Lin Yuan immediately understood what was happening.","The Moon Empress had come to see him because she was concerned that Keira would not be able to commandeer the demon insects to handle the expanding dead spirits wave.","But the fact that Keira had not contacted him meant she could handle it.","The dead spirits had to have been injected with an enormous amount of death aura in order to multiply in the short span of eight hours.","Tower Canon would not use up such a large amount of death aura for no reason. This was a clear sign that Tower Canon was launching their counterattack.","The Eight Pages of Tower Canon had been planning for the revival of the dead spirits for a very long time and had to have discovered that the demon insects were fending off the dead spirits wave and protecting the main world.","Lin Yuan would not optimistically assume that Tower Canon could not tackle the demon insects. If Tower Canon had been unable to handle the demon insects, they would not have begun their counterattack after a period of silence.","“Master, I will begin setting up defenses now. I won’t be able to head to the Radiance Sacred Hall to watch the Radiance Knight selection.”","The Moon Empress sighed and reached out to help Lin Yuan adjust his collar.","Lin Yuan still had to be the one to step forward to handle the situation at times like this.","During the initial outbreak of the dead spirits wave, all the lifeforms in the main world, including the Radiance Federation, were unable to handle the disaster even if they joined forces. The sea clans led by the Vast Sea Labyrinth fared even worse than the humans when it came to tackling the dead spirits. From the beginning, it was Lin Yuan who saved the main world time and time again.","It was true then, and it was still true now.","“I have informed the other members of royalty of the changes to the dead spirits wave. The Radiance Knight and Radiance Envoy selections will be postponed.”","The Moon Empress had not made this decision on her own but had come to this conclusion after a discussion with the other members of royalty.","The Radiance Hundred Sequence selection and reranking had already bolstered the confidence of the Radiance citizens.","If they went on to hold the Radiance Knight and Radiance Envoy selections when they were on the cusp of an unknown disaster, it would affect their ability to handle and prepare for the disaster.","Lin Yuan did not say anything. He could not guarantee that he could use Keira to fend off Tower Canon’s counterattack.","He instructed Red Thorn to release the Abyss Great Emperor and stood on its palm. He then ordered it to take him to where the five female demon insects were hiding.","Meanwhile, Keira was greedily absorbing pure spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. She had never been in such a magical paradise before. With this environment, Keira felt that she no longer needed the gems that contained pure spirit qi.","Lin Yuan had to have a powerful source of support in order to possess such a blissful haven.","Once again, Keira reaffirmed that being accepted as Lin Yuan’s servant was the biggest opportunity of her life!","Unexpectedly, Lin Yuan summoned Keira and frowned as he asked her, “You should be aware of the changes that have occurred with the dead spirits wave in the past eight hours. Why didn’t you inform me of this in advance? I told you to report any and all changes to the dead spirits wave to me!”"]},{"number":2711,"title":"Chapter 2711: He is the Saint?","paragraphs":["Chapter 2711: He is the Saint?","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","Lin Yuan’s voice was extremely stern.","If Keira had informed him when the anomaly first arose, he could have made preparations sooner.","He had slept soundly in the Return from Faraway Mansion last night and had not wanted his body to be stressed by other matters.","If he had known about the anomaly sooner, he could have instructed Keira to take him to investigate the situation and come up with a plan of action sooner.","Lin Yuan knew that Keira was not using her full powers to tackle the dead spirits. She had only produced five demon insect eggs.","This had displeased Lin Yuan from the beginning.","However, he had not said anything to Keira because the five demon insects managed to handle the situation.","In actuality, he could guess what Keira was thinking. She was never concerned about the main world and only wanted to return to the","The Sky Beyond the Clouds was where she could expand her species and demonstrate her prowess.","But to Lin Yuan, this world was his home. He also had the desire to venture into the Sky Beyond the Clouds, but he had to ensure the safety of the main world first.","Keira’s expression froze when she heard what he said, and terror soon spread across her face. She could sense Lin Yuan’s rage.","It was true that she had found out early on about the change in the dead spirits wave.","But at the time, she had been anxious to absorb the pure spirit qi from the Spirit Lock spatial zone to strengthen herself. She also assumed that the acceleration in the emergence of dead spirits would not be of any obstruction to the demon insects.","After all, the demon insects could still consume the dead spirits. More food was beneficial for the demon insects.","As a highly intelligent lifeform, Keira could stand in Lin Yuan’s shoes and figure out the reason for his perspective.","It was no wonder that Lin Yuan had placed emphasis on informing him when any changes arose.","Now that she understood this, Keira’s heart sank. This matter was indeed serious.","After pondering further, Keira decided not to explain herself but directly admit her mistake.","“Master, I wasn’t able to fully comprehend what you wanted. I lost myself absorbing pure spirit qi and forgot my responsibility. I will instruct the other demon insects to produce more female insects that can take on the dead spirits.”","Lin Yuan reached out and flicked Keira’s head. “Keira, I hope you won’t disappoint me again! I see no need in nurturing a species that can’t even carry out my directives.”","Red Thorn was seated on Lin Yuan’s shoulder and said, “Yuan, now that I’ve evolved into an eight-winged fairy, I can take control of her and manipulate her abilities to nurture the species! It just so happens that a new Tongue of Relinquish is about to grow.”","A look of excited desire appeared on Red Thorn’s face while it spoke.","Red Thorn’s power was increased when it used the Tongue of Relinquish to take control of powerful targets.","Red Thorn preferred to take control of Keira, who had powerful potential, rather than the Tarot experts.","Red Thorn’s words caused a chill of horror to run through Keira.","This also allowed Keira to realize Lin Yuan was not reliant on her. He had the means to take control of her and utilize her abilities after her death.","In their relationship, she was the one relying on him.","Keira was so nervous that her limbs started to convulse, and she kept her head dipped. She was terrified that Lin Yuan would take Red Thorn up on its suggestion.","Lin Yuan did not engage Red Thorn. Rather, he said seriously to the antsy Keira, “I will give you another chance. Don’t forget that this is your last one. The success of the outcome isn’t important. What’s important is that you follow my orders!”","Keira nodded vigorously.","She took out the dimensional lifeforms she had captured and began laying unhatched demon insect fetuses.","Keira had been so reserved in her production of the demon insect fetuses because it was very difficult to produce new ones. It required an enormous amount of energy. Each time she produced female insect fetuses, Keira needed to use a large portion of her roots.","Luckily, after entering the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Keira realized that it was no longer difficult for her to produce the female insect fetuses. In the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s pure spirit qi-filled environment, she could produce a batch of female insect fetuses every two to three years.","This was much faster than the demon insect empresses in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, who received resources from their demon insect citizens!","If she was able to keep up this production rate in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, her branch of the demon insects would be able to take control of the entire demon insects. She might even be able to become the thearch of the demon insect empresses.","Because of Lin Yuan, Keira was able to see a beautiful future. But she was also fully shackled by him. She would never take his orders lightly again.","“Master, thank you for giving me another chance. From now on, I will carry out your orders with the best methods. I will carve your orders into my Genetic Lock!”","When Lin Yuan decided to give Lin Keira a chance and did not allow Red Thorn to use the Tongue of Relinquish to take control of Keira, Red Thorn felt slightly regretful.","Keira was much better than the stupid Acid Corrosion Queen Bee.","Apart from consuming acid and building messy nests in its Mouths of","Relinquish, the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee was not good for anything else.","Lin Yuan was so displeased with Keira because she had not listened to his orders and because he had already used True Data to check on Keira and found out that she could produce the demon insect females in batches.","Lin Yuan did not relax because Keira intended to produce more demon insect eggs. He was still worried.","It was unlikely that Tower Canon’s counterattack would be affected by the increase in the quantity of demon insects. It was probable that Tower Canon had found a way to counter the demon insects.","It did not take long for the Abyss Great Emperor to take Lin Yuan to where the five female demon insects were situated.","During the entire journey, Lin Yuan remained fused with the Abyss Red Lotus and detected the surrounding environment. However, he had failed to sense two figures watching him from the shadows.","The tall and skinny girl with flowers printed on her skirt said in a soft voice, “Summer, when Tower Canon’s manipulation is taken out of the equation, all of the strange happenings in the main world came from this young man. Do you think he could be the awakened Lord Saint?”","The girl’s voice was hopeful.","Since leaving Epoch God Palace, Spring and Summer had been investigating the main world.","The knights from Epoch God Palace had been continuously supplying them with information. Spring and Summer knew almost everything that had happened in the main world in the last two years.","After filtering through the information, there was no other possibility aside from that young man.","Summer twirled her long dark green hair and said with a faint tremble in her voice, “Normally, we should begin observing the candidates after looking through all that has happened in the world in the past few years. But we don’t have any other candidates and can only continue observing this human young man named Lin Yuan!","“Look at the exotic red flower blooming on the temples of the eight-winged fairy seated on the young man’s shoulder. Doesn’t it resemble the flowers blooming on the strange plant depicted on the wall illustration?”","Summer was all but certain that Lin Yuan was Lord Saint’s reincarnation. How else could a young human take control of the corpse of an Afterlife Realm dimensional lifeform?","The power of an Afterlife Realm dimensional lifeform was beyond that of a Class 1 world. It was also considered exceptional in a Class 2 world.","When a Class 1 world was promoted to Class 2, the concentration of spirit qi would rise and it would be easier for the lifeforms in the world to comprehend world willpowers. As a result, both the humans and feys in this world would undergo rapid improvement in the next few centuries. It would no longer be as difficult to evolve their grades.","The one who had enabled this world to promote from Class 1 to Class 2 was this young man in front of them.","Summer looked at Lin Yuan with a gaze that brimmed with admiration.","However, she felt that it was a shame that she and Spring could not appear in front of Lin Yuan to prevent interfering with Lord Saint’s growth.","Summer was always more cautious than Spring. After reeling in her thoughts, she said, “For now, we can focus on observing this young man. He won’t be able to avoid summoning his feys when he battles Tower Canon. At that point, we will be able to tell if his feys match the ones on the wall illustration. We might even be able to sense Lord Totem God’s aura!”","Spring fell silent for a moment before she said, “I think we should tell Autumn and Winter about our discoveries so they can also learn about the good news. We will also be able to protect Lord Saint while we’re observing him!”","Keira had already issued orders to the five female demon insects before Lin Yuan arrived at the nest so they could come out to greet him.","Currently, the five female demon insects’ mindsets differed drastically.","At first, Keira had relied on Doom the most. But Keira later abandoned Doom when she felt that Doom had failed to demonstrate the might of the demon insects to Lin Yuan. She began relying on the four other female demon insects instead.","The four other female demon insects led insect armies and battled the dead spirits at the borders of the dimensional worlds.","After consuming the dead spirits, their insect armies expanded and were now at least seven times larger than Doom’s own.","Hence, the other four female demon insects steamrolled over Doom.","The five female demon insects had gathered there because they had received Keira’s orders three days ago.","Keira planned on using spirit qi crystals to strengthen the five female demon insects. Otherwise, the five female demon insects would take two to three days to travel and gather together.","The female demon insects were all happily waiting for rewards from Keira.","However, they noticed that Keira had produced more female demon insects.","This made all of the female demon insects nervous. They were worried that Keira would replace them because she found their recent performances unsatisfactory.","At first, Doom and the other four had other discoveries that they wanted to report to Keira. But now, they did not know how to broach the subject. These matters could be considered the first failures of the demon insects in their bid to fend off the dead spirits.","The special dead dimensional lifeforms had killed some of the demon insects they had produced!","However, there were not many of these special dead dimensional lifeforms, and they could not be considered a threat to the demon insects’ advantage over the dead spirits wave.","In a low voice, Keira told Doom and the other four demon insects, “Go and tell Master about the current circumstances of the defeat against the dead spirits.","Don’t leave anything out! Otherwise, I will get rid of all of you immediately.”","As a demon insect queen, Keira did not see these female insects she had produced as her offspring but her tools. Hence, she did not feel any emotional ties to them.","This was especially so now because she had the resources to produce female insects in batches.","Keira’s words caused them to tremble in front of Lin Yuan. They could no longer be concerned about whether this negative piece of news would anger Keira. Angering Keira was better than hiding this news and ending up eliminated!","Due to their Genetic Locks, they had no choice but to listen to Keira’s orders.","“Master, the dead spirits are still able to effectively restrain the dead spirits waves and use the dead spirits waves to reproduce. However, a giant special dead spirit has emerged in the dead spirits waves.","“Based on our observation, we’re confident it’s a kind of dead dimensional lifeform. However, it differs from dead dimensional lifeforms that emit a significant death aura, as it releases only a small amount of death aura. Nonetheless, it can harness this death aura in its attacks. Furthermore, it has the ability to consume demon insects, using them as a source of energy after digestion.”","Keira’s eyes widened.","It turned out that Tower Canon had such capabilities and could dispatch dead dimensional lifeforms that were able to consume demon insects!","Doom and the rest did not have the courage to hide the truth. It was likely that they had only just received this news.","The war between the demon insects and dead spirits was no longer about occupying territory. Both sides had begun viciously cutting each other down.","Keira was afraid that Lin Yuan would think she had kept all this information from him.","If she had found out about what the dead spirits had up their sleeves, she would have informed Lin Yuan about it immediately.","Lin Yuan could not help but frown when he heard that and quickly issued orders to the Samsara Realm Dictators stationed in the dimensional worlds. He ordered them to capture the newly emerged dimensional lifeforms so that he could examine them.","There had to be a fair number of types of dimensional lifeforms.","Lin Yuan was afraid that Tower Canon had more moves to play aside from these dead dimensional lifeforms that could consume demon insects.","“Keira, I will send my subordinates out to capture the newly discovered dead dimensional lifeforms and bring them before you. Instruct the dead dimensional lifeforms born from death aura to consume these new dead dimensional lifeforms’ genes. We must make a proper comparison of these dead dimensional lifeforms!”","The demon insects’ biggest advantage was their ability to absorb the genes of other lifeforms.","As long as they could be combined with the genes of the new dead dimensional lifeforms, the offspring subsequently produced by the female demon insects would be able to overcome the new dead dimensional lifeforms.","Presently, aside from relying on the demon insects, Lin Yuan did not have any other means of fighting Tower Canon.."]},{"number":2712,"title":"Chapter 2712: Sword Pointed at the Radiance Federation!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2712: Sword Pointed at the Radiance Federation!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","It was true that Lin Yuan could produce explosive combat power when he fused with the Abyss Red Lotus, but he could not handle the neverending waves of dead spirits on his own.","Moreover, he would definitely attract Tower Canon’s attention once he exposed his power.","It was likely that Tower Canon already knew of his existence.","Once he revealed his power, he would be showing his hand to the Eight Pages of Tower Canon. This would not do Lin Yuan any good.","Presently, Lin Yuan could only place his hopes in Keira.","Lin Yuan could not help but sigh when he saw Keira continuously producing demon insect fetuses. He still had not accumulated enough power!","In his battle against Tower Canon, Lin Yuan felt as though he was being restrained.","He did not like to put all his eggs in one basket.","If he could protect the main world and defeat Tower Canon, he would need to prepare more secret weapons before heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","After Lin Yuan sent out his orders, all of the Samsara Realm Dictators jumped into action.","When the dead spirits crisis first broke out, all of the lifeforms in the dimensional worlds were affected, aside from the lifeforms in the alien insect dimensional world.","Only when the demon insects entered the scene did the lifeforms in the dimensional worlds get to rest. It also gave the Samsara Realm and Turning Wheel Realm Dictators free time. They had all been waiting for Lin Yuan to give them orders.","If Lin Yuan did not give them new orders, their existence would have no value.","Ever since Wen Yu started managing them, the model of the dimensional worlds’ armies was changed.","When the Samsara Realm Dictators received the news, they immediately relayed the news to the Turning Wheel Realm Dictators, Dictators, and Apostles.","The powerful Dictators and Apostles could use their own source-type power to resist death aura.","The real impact on the dimensional worlds was on the dimensional lifeforms that had yet to become Apostles.","The Dictators and Apostles worked together to capture dead dimensional lifeforms from the dead spirits waves and delivered them to Lin Yuan’s location.","The war between the dead spirits and demon insects was only officially beginning now.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on these new dead dimensional lifeforms.","Lin Yuan saw that the Disaster Transcending Deceased and Saw-Killing Dead Beasts were the best entities for killing the demon insects.","When the Disaster Transcending Deceased absorbed death aura, they would turn into fury spirits and enter the demon insects’ bodies to destroy their souls.","That method of combat allowed the Disaster Transcending Deceased to kill the demon insects endlessly while absorbing their soul energy, thereby raising their own grades.","This method of combat did not deplete any of their own resources and allowed the Disaster Transcending Deceased to kill at least 60,000 demon insects in the short span of an hour. It could construct the reproductive abilities of 1,000 demon insects every minute.","The Saw-Killing Dead Beasts used death aura in a similar way that Lin Yuan used spirit qi to use Spirit Essence Explosion.","When the Saw-Killing Dead Beasts activated death aura, sharp saw-like teeth were formed in their mouths. These teeth had the bite power to easily take the lives of the demon insects.","The Saw-Killing Dead Beasts were not as competent as the Disaster Transcending Deceased when it came to killing the demon insects, but there were many more of the Saw-Killing Dead Beasts.","The demon insects were also able to injure the Saw-Killing Dead Beasts.","However, the Saw-Killing Dead Beasts could recover their injuries by absorbing death aura. They could also consume the corpses of their comrades to reproduce. Hence, the Saw-Killing Dead Beasts’ numbers did not fall even after being attacked by the demon insects for an extended period.","Upon encountering these new dead dimensional lifeforms, Keira addressed Lin Yuan with a serious demeanor, saying, “Master, demon insects have boundless potential for evolution. If we can acquire the genes of these dead dimensional lifeforms, we can certainly create offspring capable of confronting them.","“However, generating targeted offspring is a time and energy-intensive process. Achieving this swiftly will necessitate a substantial energy investment. May I have your permission to transport these dead dimensional lifeforms and demon insect fetuses to the blessed territory to expedite the breeding process?","“I will produce five to ten specialized demon insects designed to combat the dead dimensional lifeforms and then determine which ones perform most effectively against the Disaster Transcending Deceased and Saw-Killing Dead Beasts.","“In the future, I intend to employ this approach each time a new kind of dead dimensional lifeform emerges.”","Keira spoke openly, with no hidden agenda. She wasn’t seeking any personal gain from the Spirit Lock spatial zone; her motive was simply to assist Lin Yuan with his issue.","She had already upset Lin Yuan and was now eager to make amends.","Upon hearing Keira’s words, Lin Yuan felt more at ease.","Her confidence in making such bold claims reassured him.","The Spirit Lock spatial zone had already grown to be half the size of the Xia Region.","While Hu Quan had been working on infrastructure in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, it covered only a small portion of the zone’s vast space.","Lin Yuan could allocate an area within the Spirit Lock spatial zone for Keira to establish her nest and settle down. This would enable him to utilize the abundant and boundless supply of pure spirit qi within the Spirit Lock spatial zone to nurture the demon insects he needed for his purposes.","“Keira, I know you desire the spirit qi in that space. I will allow you to build a nest according to your preferences in that space. You can stay there and focus on producing the demon insects for me! Feel free to let me know if you have any needs.","“Don’t forget to try your best to ensure that the female insects aren’t released. Tower Canon has probably already gathered experts to search for the female insects.”","In Lin Yuan’s opinion, the demon insects’ method of growing their species was","similar to the way that the insect-species carcinoma feys produced their insect","armies.The best way to handle the insect-species carcinoma feys was to capture the mothers and take control of them before moving on to handle the nest. Otherwise, the nest would only become larger unless an enormous amount of power was used to destroy the entire nest.","There was no way that Tower Canon was unaware of how to take control of and eliminate the demon insects.","Keira was overjoyed when she heard this.","The biggest blessing she could receive from Lin Yuan was the creation of a nest for her in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. If she could freely absorb spirit qi of such purity, her branch of the demon insects would be limitless! There was nothing else that Keira could hope for after receiving this blessing.","“Master, don’t worry. I will only send out the female insects with Class 2 and 3","Genetic Locks and keep the rest with me. I won’t let you down this time!”","While Lin Yuan was preparing for battle, Tower Canon was not idle either.","First Page Crimson, Second Page Warbler Candle, and the rest were anxiously waiting for news while Third Page Violet Light Green and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid went to make contact with Epoch God Palace.","Crimson was even prepared to take the rest of Tower Canon with him to hide again if Epoch God Palace refused to give Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid the chance to speak and killed them instantly.","They would then slow down the rate at which the dead world absorbed this Class 2 world’s roots so as to dodge Epoch God Palace’s attention while secretly investigating their objective.","If they came back with good news, confirming that Tower Canon and Epoch God Palace had compatible goals, Tower Canon would need to act swiftly. Their first task would be to eradicate the sudden emergence of demon insects, aiming to seize control of the main world as soon as possible.","After the dead world completely absorbed the roots of the Class 2 world, they could then strategize to advance the dead world to a Class 3 status. They might even consider engaging Epoch God Palace’s assistance at critical moments in exchange for compensation.","Crimson already knew that Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid were upset with them, but he did not care because he saw their fates as being intertwined.","After all these years, they had all formed various grievances against each other, but none could do anything about it or leave.","When Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid returned to Tower Canon and smelled the concentrated death aura, they could not help but think they had just encountered a narrow brush with death.","Regardless of how disappointed the two of them were with Tower Canon, they still told the other Eight Pages about the news they found out from Epoch God","Palace.","Warbler Candle asked doubtfully, “Are you sure that the information is accurate?”","Warbler Candle had asked this because she found it hard to believe that Epoch God Palace would stay in a Class 1 world for so long if they had no plans for it!","Any faction or individual had to have their own logic driving their actions.","If Epoch God Palace did not have any plans for this world, Warbler Candle could not figure out what objective they could have.","Warbler Candle’s suspicions were instinctive.","However, Warbler Candle’s instinctive action angered Cavity Orchid.","Cavity Orchid said coldly, “Warbler Candle, what right do you have to question the validity of our information? If you doubt us, you can head to Epoch God Palace and question them yourselves! Let’s think back to who had shrunk back when the topic first came up!”","Violet Light Green also frowned at Warbler Candle with her eyes full of displeasure and rage.","Warbler Candle must be aware of the giant risks that the two of them had undergone to obtain this news.","If they were even going to question information that was beneficial to them, Tower Canon might as well just shut down!","Eighth Page Eye Shadow also looked at Warbler Candle with displeasure and tried to mediate the situation, “There’s no way Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchard’s information is false. We can now launch our counterattack against the natives of this world!”","Cavity Orchid said coldly, “Hasn’t Tower Canon already begun our counterattack against the demon insects? You already sent out the Disaster Transcending Deceased and Saw-Killing Dead Beasts before we returned. Were you trying to use this method to test Epoch God Palace’s true intentions?”","Cavity Orchid was only one step away from saying that they had used them as bait. However, the other members of Tower Canon all understood that this was really what he was trying to say.","This made Eye Shadow, Sixth Page Wave Glow, and Seventh Page Concubine Winding all feel extremely awkward.","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow had been the one who made this suggestion, and Crimson had decided on it.","Although the two of them had not spoken clearly, Eye Shadow, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding all knew that Crimson had such a goal in mind.","The rest of them had silently agreed to let it happen. This was because they had desperately needed to find out what Epoch God Palace’s intentions were!","Eye Shadow felt slightly apologetic toward Cavity Orchid and Violet Light Green.","Now that Tower Canon had already made their move but Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid had still returned safely, this indicated many things.","Warbler Candle had pointed out doubts despite having no moral high ground. She was essentially giving Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid fodder to lose their tempers.","They would likely have to give Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid more","advantages in their subsequent plans!","Crimson did not respond to what Cavity Orchid said. After all, Eye Shadow had already acted as the mediator.","Crimson changed the subject and said, “Since Epoch God Palace isn’t focused on this Class 2 world, let’s try to fully fuse the dead world’s roots with the Class 2 world within the next week.","“Then, we will all take part in eliminating the forces of this Class 2 world that have been obstructing the dead world from taking over this Class 2 world!”","Crimson paused for a moment before continuing. “Violet Light Green and","Cavity Orchid indeed had a hard time making contact with Epoch God Palace. The two of you can stay in the fortress!”","Crimson could not completely ignore the feelings of the other Pages and had to compensate the two of them in some ways. This decision was his way of making it up to the two of them.","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid scoffed. Crimson’s arrangement did not appease them.","Aside from Epoch God Palace, what other danger could there be in this Class 2 world?","Crimson was being thoughtless if he thought that this would be enough to compensate them.","All of them had been asleep for over 6,000 years. Who didn’t want to stretch their limbs after waking up?","Moreover, they would be able to obtain a large amount of spoils by cleaning out this Class 2 world. If they stayed back to look after the fortress, they would lose the chance to gain these spoils.","Cavity Orchid said through his clenched jaw, “Violet Light Green and I will join this plan. The Radiance Federation is now the core of this Class 2 world. I suggest that all eight of us head to the Radiance Federation and conquer that first.","“This will allow us to save the most time and energy, as well as strike a blow to the rest of the factions. After we take control of the Radiance Federation, Violet Light Green and I will each receive two units of the profits, while the rest of you will receive one unit.”","Rather than coming up with a plan, Cavity Orchid was stating his conditions.","Cavity Orchid’s words caused the other Pages to frown.","Warbler Candle was about to speak when she was interrupted by Crimson,","“Okay, we will divide up the spoils according to what you just said!”"]},{"number":2713,"title":"Chapter 2713: Everything to Ashes!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2713: Everything to Ashes!","Translator: Atlas Studios | Editor: Atlas Studios","First Page Crimson had just finished speaking when Fifth Page Falling Rainbow could not help but say, “Almost all of this Class 2 and dimensional worlds’ resources are consolidated in the Radiance Federation. Another unit of resources is worth immense wealth!","“Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid, the two of you are being too greedy! Is it possible that the two of you have formed an alliance and are trying to claim profits from our group?”","Among the Eight Pages of Tower Canon, Third Page Violet Light Green’s temper was one of the milder ones.","But after hearing what Falling Rainbow said, she almost struck her.","Everyone knew that Falling Rainbow and Second Page Warbler Candle had formed an alliance and were in opposition with the other Pages. How dare she say such a thing?","Crimson said in a low voice, “Enough. Stop fighting. After we take over this Class 2 world, we will need to work together to promote it to a Class 3 world in order to return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds to take our revenge and quench our hatred! I hope that moving forward, we will act without animosity.”","Cavity Orchid snorted when he heard what Crimson said.","Without animosity? How could the animosity left over from thousands of years be removed so easily?","Crimson was just trying to smooth things over with pleasant but insincere words. It was hard not to be disappointed that such words had fallen from his lips.","Violet Light Green did not know what Cavity Orchid was thinking.","She did not think that Tower Canon currently had the power to promote this","Class 2 world to Class 3. It was not easy to promote a Class 2 world to Class 3!","Once this Class 2 world was stabilized, associating dimensional worlds would be derivated.","Tower Canon did not possess sufficient combat power to take on a Class 2 world and its dimensional worlds.","The dimensional worlds of a Class 2 world had Afterlife Realm Dictators. It was also possible for even more powerful experts to appear.","It was improbable that they would be able to promote this Class 2 world to","Class 3, much less return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds to seek their revenge.","Back then, they had to flee their homes like mournful dogs. Crimson had to be aware of how powerful their enemy was.","It would be better to harvest more benefits from this Class 2 world rather than buy into the rosy picture that Crimson was trying to paint.","It was likely that cracks would appear among Tower Canon’s members once they conquered this Class 2 world. Eventually, each of the Eight Pages would claim their own territory and situate themselves as the ruler.","Eighth Page Eye Shadow might seem non-materialistic, but she had actually already formed an alliance with Sixth Page Wave Glow and Seventh Page Concubine Winding. The bond between the three of them was even stronger than that of Cavity Orchid and Violet Light Green.","Regardless, the Eight Pages of Tower Canon were currently partners. Before taking over this Class 2 world, they would stick together even if the harmony was superficial.","Regardless of what Epoch God Palace’s goal was, or whether it was in opposition with Tower Canon’s own goal, Tower Canon had no choice but to remain fearful of Epoch God Palace as long as they existed!","Wave Glow waited for the atmosphere to calm before saying, “Let’s not waste any more time here. We should be focusing on fusing the dead world’s roots with the main world!","“Crimson, you and Warbler Candle woke up first. Eye Shadow was forcefully awakened and is in the weakest state of us all. You and Warbler Candle will be the leaders of this operation while five of us will assist you. Eye Shadow shall be left out for now!”","Crimson and Warbler Candle frowned when they heard what Wave Glow said.","It required an immense amount of energy to fully fuse the dead world’s roots with this Class 2 world.","Given the circumstances, no one was willing to fully drain themselves.","However, Crimson knew that he could not oppose Wave Glow’s suggestion.","Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow had never truly trusted and submitted to him.","With Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid also brewing discontent against him, Crimson did not want to offend the small pool left: Wave Glow, Concubine Winding, and Eye Shadow.","Although he did not make his stance clear, he knew that Warbler Candle was unwilling to partake in this plan.","Just as Crimson expected, Warbler Candle said, “The sequence of our awakenings was planned out from the beginning. There are benefits to being at the back of the sequence! Those at the front of the sequence had to take on more of the danger before we arrived in this world.","“Wave Glow, if you want to prevent Eye Shadow from depleting her energy, you can make up for her share of energy! You are capable of doing so if you want to.","Eye Shadow’s expression did not change when she heard what Warbler Candle said.","She told Wave Glow and Concubine Winding in a gentle voice, “Wave Glow,","Concubine Winding, you don’t have to say anything else. I can handle the depletion from the ritual in my current state. But after the ritual, I will need to go into slumber again and won’t be able to head to the Radiance Federation with the rest of you!”","Wave Glow and Concubine Winding were already boiling with fury before Eye Shadow spoke.","Warbler Candle was too shameless!","Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow were part of the reason they had all had to sleep for over 6,000 years. Warbler Candle did not have the right to say what she just said.","Concubine Winding said with false insecurity, “Since we know that Epoch God Palace isn’t focused on this Class 2 world, we should all continue waiting if the rest of you can’t bring yourselves to agree with Wave Glow’s suggestion.","“We will begin the ritual once Eye Shadow is fully recovered! This will give us time to further infect the Class 2 world with death aura and will save us a lot of trouble later on!”","The ritual required at least six of them to participate.","The three of them were a team. As long as the three of them decided not to participate, the other five would have no choice but to plead with them.","Now that Tower Canon had already devolved to such a state, Wave Glow would not mind if the situation became slightly worse.","Aside from Eye Shadow, Wave Glow also had yet to absorb sufficient energy from the black coffin.","Thus, the three of them were considerably weaker than Crimson and Warbler Candle.","Warbler Candle had been making a fuss about bringing the plan forward and did not consider the conditions of the rest at all.","After she was done speaking, Concubine Winding shot a look at Eye Shadow and Wave Glow. The three of them left the fortress and returned to their own towers.","The other five Pages would have to buckle within the next two days. Even if they did not agree to the conditions that the three of them had, they would have to provide them with a resolution that they were satisfied with!","After Wave Glow and the rest left, the hall in the fortress was chillingly quiet.","Cavity Orchid stood up and said, “Violet Light Green, let’s go too. We don’t have the right to make decisions! Once the rest of you have made a decision, let the two of us know! But don’t forget that you have to preserve mine and Violet Light Green’s profits!”","This was clearly an argument that Warbler Candle had started, but she did not discuss with Crimson after the five members left. Instead, she left the hall with Falling Rainbow. leaving Crimson standing auietlv at his original soot.","A moment later, a menacing expression spread across Crimson’s face.","A dark red tentacle protruded from behind Crimson, and an inauspicious aura that was different from that of death aura condensed on Crimson’s body. The red fog that rose from Crimson’s body caused the air to turn sickly sweet.","But it was not long before Crimson retracted his inauspicious aura.","He looked out of the fortress, his eyes gleaming with a cryptic murderous aura.","Lin Yuan had been worried about the state of the dead spirits wave.","Keira dared not hide anything and told him everything she discovered.","The current ferocity of the dead spirits wave astonished Lin Yuan.","When the Moon Empress first came to see and inform him of the situation, the dead spirits wave could be classified as Class 1. But now, given the number of dead spirits that was flowing out, the dead spirits wave could be classified as Class 4!","Luckily, Keira and the other demon insects were continuing to reproduce.","When the female demon insects consumed the first wave of new dead spirits, which consisted of the Disaster Transcending Deceased and Saw-Killing Dead Beasts, they produced a large number of specialized demon insects that enabled the demon insects to fight back against the dead spirits.","At first, Lin Yuan had been feeling fretful. He worried that given the wave’s ferocity, Keira would be unable to produce specialized demon insects quick enough to handle the wave.","But it did not take long before Lin Yuan realized that he was being overly worried.","After the female demon insects that Keira produced in the Spirit Lock spatial zone consumed the dead dimensional lifeforms’ bodies and gained their genes, they produced specialized demon insects within two short hours!","Currently, the biggest issue was delivering the specialized demon insects.","Aside from instructing Wen Yu to deliver the specialized demon insects with Class 2 and 3 Genetic Locks, he also activated the Apostles and Dictators who were delivering the dead dimensional lifeforms.","After delivering the dead dimensional lifeforms, the Apostles and Dictators would take a batch of specialized demon insects with them.","The battle between the demon insects and dead spirits could be described as fueling war with warfare.","The dead spirits relied on the death aura in the ley lines to emerge, while the demon insects relied on the dead spirits’ bodies to be born.","In the past few days, there was even the intermittent emergence of powerful dead dimensional lifeforms. However, they were quickly dealt with in various ways.","Lin Yuan believed that if this situation continued and Tower Canon saw that they were unable to crush the humans, they would lose their patience and step in.","Lin Yuan didn’t appear busy and wasn’t trying to boost his power. However, the Abyss Red Lotus, which he had connected to Morbius through a Spirit Lock, had been quite active.","After taking control of the five dimensional worlds, the Abyss Red Lotus had been using Lotus Locks the World to take control of the main world’s Continent Vein Cores.","As Morbius’ grades increased, the originally Diamond X/Fantasy V Abyss Red Lotus was now Suzerain X/Myth Il!","[Fey Name]: Abyss Red Lotus [Fey Species]: Abyss red lotus species/abyss red lotus genus","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Fire [Fey Quality]: Myth Il","Abilities:","[Lotus Nirvana]: After making a decision to self-destruct, all the energy in its body will be gathered inside the seed. When the seed sprouts, the life and bloodline will be passed on.","[Splendor of Fire]: Fill the area with fire-elemental energy. All other energies besides fire-elemental energy will be eliminated, and the ability of other lifeforms to control fire-elemental energy will be removed.","[Hellfire Lotus Imprint]: The lotus imprint will place a lock on the target and prevent it from gaining energy. Every layer of lotus imprint added will strengthen the lock on the target’s energy and bloodline.","[Cleansing Aura Lotus Flames]: The flames will transform into a lotus coffin. Choose a space, and the flames will preserve it. Time and fixed entities will be preserved in their current condition.","[Lotus World Law]: Control the core of the world and issue orders to the lifeforms in the world. Those who were defiant would be blocked from receiving energy from that world.","[Hellfire Application]: Combine with other lifeforms and combine the energy of the world controlled by Lotus Locks the World with its own to boost itself.","[Burning Lotus Cleansing Dance]: The body will be burned up into nutrients and turned into a lotus. The lotus will be in a cleansing state. Burning the main body will increase the effects of Hellfire Application and protect the worlds linked to Lotus Locks the World.","Exclusive Skill:","[Red Lotus Hellfire]: A target’s karma, bloodline, and energy will be burned up. The flames will add the Hellfire Lotus Imprint on the target’s body.","[Lotus Locks the World]: When contact is made with the core of a world, the lotus roots will wrap around the world’s core. The core of the world will become an energy source for the lotus while the lotus takes over the world.","[Everything to Ashes]: Fire-elemental energy will nourish the body. All entities and energy can be burned and inject increasingly pure fire-elemental energy into itself. The higher the level of the burned entities and energy, the greater the impact on the roots if internal energy is lacking. (If the impact on the roots is too severe, the utilization of cleansing lotus might be affected).","Lin Yuan was pleasantly surprised by the ability and exclusive skill the Abyss Red Lotus gained. They also gave him more confidence to take on Tower Canon when he fused with the Abyss Red Lotus.","When Lin Yuan used Hellfire Application, the power of the five dimensional worlds would be applied to his body. This was already one of his secret weapons.","But Burning Lotus Cleansing Dance could multiply the combat power of Hellfire Application.","Although this would cause the Abyss Red Lotus to enter the ‘cleansing lotus’ state and lower its grade, Lin Yuan believed that this was worth it as it would significantly raise the upper-bound limits of his power.","Everything to Ashes would allow Lin Yuan to use fire-elemental energy to burn all other entities and energies.","Lin Yuan was not lacking in fire-elemental energy at all. The fire-type Elemental Shellfish spat out heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls almost every second.","As Morbius’ grade continued to increase, the spirit qi produced from the spirit pool also increased in purity.."]},{"number":2714,"title":"Chapter 2714: Battle Against Tower Canon!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2714: Battle Against Tower Canon!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","The elemental pearls spat out by the fire-type Elemental Shellfish now always came with outer radiance. After the Elemental Well purified them, the purity could reach 100%.","Moreover, the elemental dolls had started forming near the Element Well.","If the purity of the fire-elemental energy was the only dependent variable in burning everything in the world to ashes, it seemed that there was no entity or energy that Lin Yuan could not burn to obliteration!","If Lin Yuan had sufficient fire-elemental energy, he would not have to experience the negative effects of Everything to Ashes, and the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots would not be affected!","Lin Yuan was not afraid of clashing directly with Tower Canon, but the Radiance Federation was fixed in its location and could not move. He was very worried that Tower Canon would target the Radiance Federation while he was clashing against them.","Bloodshed and sacrifice would be unavoidable if war broke out between the two sides.","Lin Yuan had the Praying Universe Soul Whale and could ensure that those around him did not lose their lives in this war.","Had the demon insects not been keeping the dead spirits at bay, the dead spirits wave would have already swallowed the entire main world. All the lifeforms in the main world would lose their lives, including the dimensional lifeforms! Only a small number of experts would be able to survive.","But as the dead spirits continued occupying and invading the main world, it was highly possible that the spirit qi would be replaced by death aura.","Spirit qi was released from ley lines. As a result, many energy ores appeared in the process of the ley lines releasing spirit qi.","But with the death aura currently invading the ley lines, the quantity of spirit qi had already lowered considerably.","When death aura leaked out from the ley lines, the existing energy ores would not be affected, but the formation of new energy ores would be limited. Now, there was also the formation of grayish-black crystals that radiated death aura.","If Tower Canon was allowed to succeed in their plan, death aura would become the dominant energy in this world.","At that time, the human experts and powerful feys who depended on spirit qi, as well as powerful Apostles and Dictators who depended on source-type power, would all fall to the disaster created by Tower Canon!","Meanwhile, the dead dimensional lifeforms that depended on death aura would come to dominate the world.","Even if Tower Canon did not manually interfere, Lin Yuan would have to deal with Tower Canon as soon as possible to minimize their impact on the main world.","The humans might seem weaker than Tower Canon, but they had never stopped working hard.","The Scholars were doing research to help the humans increase their understanding of the dead spirits crisis’ impact on the main world.","By causing so much commotion in the Radiance Federation, Lin Yuan had forced Tower Canon to surface.","Epoch God Palace was like a plume of mist. Lin Yuan had yet to catch even a whiff of them, much less find the means to interact with them.","The humans would inevitably have to battle it out against Tower Canon.","Although the humans wanted to rest, Tower Canon was charging at full throttle. Yet, the dead spirits wave was being restrained by the demon insects. Hence, Tower Canon would definitely fight back against the Radiance Federation.","The creation of the Major Federation Union had clearly established the structure of the main world. The Radiance Federation was now the heart of the human camp. Thus, in their counterattack against the humans, Tower Canon would strike the Radiance Federation first.","Over the past few days of fighting, Lin Yuan discovered that the demon insects no longer had the upper hand over the new dimensional lifeforms. Instead, the new dimensional lifeforms were now overwhelming the demon insects.","Due to the existence of a few special dead dimensional lifeforms, the demon insects would be injured and killed.","But each time the demon insects died, a special method that was unique to the demon insects would be activated to disseminate information about the circumstances. Consequently, specialized demon insects would arrive at the scene.","Each time new types of dead dimensional lifeforms were discovered, they were captured and delivered to Lin Yuan, who would then send them to Keira’s nest.","When Keira learned about Lin Yuan’s concerns regarding the dead spirits wave, she came to see Lin Yuan and said with utmost seriousness, “Master, judging from the current situation, any dead dimensional lifeforms that emerge will be nothing more but nutrients for the demon insects, unless they are powerful enough to kill the female insects.","“Every female demon insect with a Class 2 or 3 Genetic Lock will build a nest underground. Once the nests are linked, the insect armies can be combined. The most powerful female insect will lead the insect army, while the weaker female insects will select new locations to build new nests. The nests will be built in deeper locations as the insect army grows stronger.","“In several locations, the nests have already reached the ley lines. If you are worried about the death aura from the ley lines affecting the environment, I can instruct the female insects to send the insect armies to consume and absorb the death aura from the ley lines.","“This batch of female insects is one I produced using death aura as the source of energy. Hence, the staggering death aura in the ley lines is the best nutrition for these demon insects!","“Given the concentration of death aura in the ley lines, with your permission, I","am confident of clearing all of it in less than 200 years! However, to do this,","you will need to allow me to remain in the nest in the blessed area. I require","pure spirit i to produce more female insects!”","Lin Yuan was momentarily taken aback and looked at Keira with amazed shock.","Initially, Lin Yuan thought that this dead spirits crisis would be drawn out for a long time. He had assumed that even after defeating Tower Canon, the dead spirits crisis would continue for at least a few tens of thousands of years.","But it turned out that the demon insects could absorb the death aura in the ley lines!","Once the death aura disappeared from the ley lines, it went without saying that no new dead spirits would emerge.","Keira’s actions would halt Tower Canon’s plans from its source.","As long as Lin Yuan allowed Keira to use the insect army to absorb the death aura in the ley lines, Tower Canon’s Eight Pages would immediately try to search for Keira.","While Keira was reporting this information to Lin Yuan, she had stressed that she needed to remain in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. She was terrified that he would kick her out of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Lin Yuan was aware of what was running through Keira’s mind.","She had already mentioned more than once that she wanted to return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds to fight for dominance against the other demon insect armies.","As a demon insect empress, Keira was extremely ambitious.","Keira was an extremely important subordinate to Lin Yuan. He needed to depend on her to produce demon insects in order to see the main world through the dead spirits crisis.","After Keira had done him such an enormous favor, he was willing to help her when they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Keira was under Lin Yuan’s control, so her power also added to his power.","“Keira, inform me of the locations where the demon insects have made contact with the ley lines.”","Lin Yuan took out a newly updated map and handed it to Keira. This map was a consolidated version drawn up after Lin Yuan combined the main world with the five dimensional worlds.","The areas where the demon insects had spread would be represented in real-time on this updated map.","Keira had also taken part in creating his map.","She quickly used her antenna to point out a few locations on this map.","Lin Yuan’s eyes were immediately drawn to a canyon at the boundary between the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent.","Lin Yuan believed that if the demon insects focused on absorbing the death","aura from the ley lines in that area, the Eight Pages would send at least two of","their members to investigate the situation after they found out about this.","If Lin Yuan set up an ambush there in advance, he might be able to kill two of the Eight Pages.","As things stood, this was the biggest advantage that Lin Yuan could wield.","Thus, Lin Yuan told Keira about his plan.","Keira was very against this.","Her life was securely in Lin Yuan’s hands. If he died, she would lose her life as well. Hence, under no circumstances did she want Lin Yuan to put his life at risk!","In Keira’s point of view, there was no difference between Lin Yuan risking his own life and risking hers.","Nonetheless, Keira did not have the right to go against Lin Yuan’s authority.","All she could do was channel more of the demon insects’ forces to the trap Lin Yuan would set up and cooperate with him.","Tower Canon had been quiet for the past few days. It was likely that they were preparing something as an immense amount of death aura was intermittently injected into the ley lines.","Keira had been trying to guess where Tower Canon came from. It was likely that they were a lost group of woeful dogs that came from a world where death aura was the main source of energy. They were trying to take over this world by force after failing to protect their original world.","There was a high chance that Tower Canon had already fused their world’s roots with this Class 2 world.","Otherwise, regardless of how omnipotent they were, they would not be able to create such a tremendous impact on this Class 2 world.","They sped up the awakening of the dead spirits in this Class 2 world by hundreds of times its original rate.","By draining the death aura from the ley lines, the demon insects were essentially draining the roots of the dead world.","Regardless of how many other critical matters Tower Canon needed to attend to, they could not ignore this matter.","Hence, there was a high chance that Lin Yuan’s plan would be successful!","In the past, Lin Yuan always consulted Wen Yu and Liu Jie before making his decisions. Occasionally, he also sought the Moon Empress’ opinion.","But this time, he made the decision on his own.","This was because the three of them would definitely prefer it if he did not put himself in danger. Additionally, they did not understand the current circumstances.","A wise person avoided perilous situations, and Lin Yuan was not the type of person who liked to put himself in said situations.","However, he could not be overly concerned now.","Once Keira confirmed Lin Yuan’s decision, the people living at the border between the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent felt the ground beginning to tremble. It was as though there was a vast number of lifeforms crawling underground.","Once the sea of demon insects entered the canyon, they began building nests in the direction of the ley line.","Lin Yuan also headed to the canyon with the Abyss Great Emperor.","Lin Yuan was in no rush to dispatch the Turning Wheel and Samsara Realm Dictators. Sending so many Dictators to the canyon would be too ostentatious and would likely set out Tower Canon’s alarm bells.","When Lin Yuan fused with the Abyss Red Lotus and reached that level, he could clearly sense that the Turning Wheel and Samsara Realm Dictators were far weaker than him.","If he brought the Turning Wheel and Samsara Realm Dictators with him, not only would they be unable to help him, but they would even end up losing their lives. This would lower the potential strength of the main world.","The Source Sand formed a sea of sand beneath the canyon, and Lin Yuan hid himself within it.","While hidden in the sea of sand, Lin Yuan could still receive information through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","At that moment, there were two figures directly above the canyon.","The long-haired girl with cold features said softly, “Summer, it looks like Lord Saint is enemies with Tower Canon! The demon insects shouldn’t be a species that can be found in this world. They are under Lord Saint’s control!”","While she spoke, Spring watched the demon insect wave that was rapidly gathering at the canyon. A look of envy appeared on her countenance.","Spring never anticipated that the day would come when she was jealous of the pathetic demon insects.","Lord Saint was utilizing these demon insects while all she could do was watch silently.","When Summer heard what Spring said, she clutched Spring’s hand.","“Spring, even after all these years, you still haven’t learned to properly compose yourself! I expect that we’ll be able to stand before Lord Saint soon.","“Not only does First Page Crimson from Tower Canon have the Blood Consumption Seed’s bloodline, but also the partial bloodline of the Blood species! The Blood Consumption Seed’s bloodline has mutated under the influence of the Blood sDecies. First Page Crimson must have a fair number of secret weapons!","“Although our presence is like that of ashes floating among the falling leaves, we will cause substantial issues for Lord Saint. If Lord Saint can’t defeat First Page Crimson, we will have a reason to appear in front of him!”","Spring and Summer had all but confirmed Lin Yuan’s identity.","This was because Lin Yuan had summoned Genius and Shiny in the past few days, both of which were depicted on the wall illustration next to Lord Totem God.","When Lin Yuan sent the dead dimensional lifeforms into the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Spring and Summer also sensed Morbius’ aura.","The only one in this world who could form a contract with, wield, and control Lord Totem God was Lord Saint!","Back then...","Summer’s expression froze with that thought, and she hurriedly moved her thoughts away. Thinking of that incident was taboo and blasphemous.","Spring lowered her gaze to look at the sea of sand that was filling the canyon. Her expression was one of admiration and hopefulness.","Although Lin Yuan did tell the Moon Empress about his plan because he was worried she would be worried, he still told her about their impending battle against Tower Canon.","The Moon Empress needed to know about this in order to come up with the right plans.","When the Moon Empress heard what Lin Yuan said, she did not know why he said that.","Nonetheless, she still sent out numerous orders that she had already prepared in advance.","She also told the other federations about this news.","Lin Yuan knew that doing so might cause the news to be leaked, but he was not going to fight in the shadows against Tower Canon. He was going to do it openly.","Regardless of what happened, Tower Canon would have to send their members to this canyon. Whether they sent more or fewer members made no difference to Lin Yuan because he was already prepared to use all of his power.","He was already fully prepared for his battle against Tower Canon!","At that moment, Keira’s voice echoed in Lin Yuan’s head. “Master, 150,000,000 demon insects have surrounded this ley line. With just one order from you, they will immediately begin absorbing the death aura from the ley line!”","Lin Yuan resolutely gave Keira the order of confirmation.","On the surface, it looked as though nothing was happening. But beneath the surface, the death aura in the ley line was being filtered.","In a very short period, Lin Yuan could sense the environment around him becoming cleaner..."]},{"number":2715,"title":"Chapter 2715: Death Source Heart!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2715: Death Source Heart!","Translator: Atlas Studios Editor: Atlas Studios","This clean feeling was a shock to Lin Yuan’s spirit as he could feel it being refreshed.","He was both very familiar with and missed this clean feeling.","It was the same feeling that permeated the main world before the dead spirits crisis broke out.","The change that was taking place in the environment while the demon insects were absorbing the death aura filled Lin Yuan with confidence.","At the same time, it astonished the Eight Pages, who were shrouded in a dark gray space enveloped by death aura. All eight pairs of eyes widened.","Tower Canon’s Eight Pages were very divided, and the splitting into four groups was becoming increasingly obvious.","From the surface, First Page Crimson appeared to be the leader of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon. But in actuality, he had lost his authoritative might long ago.","The team comprised of Second Page Warbler Candle and Fifth Page Falling","Rainbow, the team comprised of Third Page Violet Light Green and Fourth","Page Cavity Orchid, and the team comprised of Sixth Page Wave Glow, Seventh Page Concubine Winding, and Eighth Page Eye Shadow were all displeased with Crimson to varying degrees.","This was because regardless of what decision he made, the benefits of at least one team would be harmed. Furthermore, he was innately selfish.","In a large team, as long as the decision maker had sufficient support clustering around them, their characteristics would be minimized. But the decision maker’s characteristics would be magnified in a small team.","But given that Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow’s team was unwilling to cooperate with the requests made by the other two teams, Crimson had no choice but to make compromises when he gave out orders.","It was as though the other seven members of Tower Canon were getting to know Crimson for the first time. None of them expected him to be willing to let go of his own profits for the sake of the other members of Tower Canon.","They were currently trying to split up the enormous pie that was this Class 2 world. This was also the first time that the Eight Pages of Tower Canon were splitting up such a colossal amount of resources.","The other seven members of Tower Canon had no idea what trick Crimson was trying to pull.","But since he was willing to let go of his profits to satisfy the overall team, the seven of them would also be willing to work with him.","Only four days had passed since the members of Tower Canon, with the exception of Eye Shadow, had begun the ritual of fusing the dead world’s roots with this Class 2 world.","Eye Shadow had been allowed to sit out, but she did not just sit back and watch. She remained on the sidelines and contributed what she could to the ritual.","However, her contribution was negligible when compared to the other members.","Wave Glow and Concubine Winding were slightly displeased by Eye Shadow’s actions. In their opinion, she was forsaking their bid for benefits.","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid did not express any opinions. However, clear derision appeared on Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow’s faces.","All Eye Shadow ever did were these superficial displays of benevolence. But in actuality, she was never willing to be the one to take the loss. She came across as non-materialistic because she was able to benefit from whatever Wave Glow and Concubine Winding fought for.","Eye Shadow had clung tightly to Concubine Winding and Wave Glow even when they were still living in the dead world.","However, her contribution was negligible when compared to the other","members.","The way they treated her just did not make sense! Falling Rainbow felt that they treated Eye Shadow even better than Warbler Candle treated her.","During the ritual, all of them were thinking about how to use the resources from this Class 2 world to strengthen themselves. Most of the Eight Pages preferred to use the Class 2 world’s resources to strengthen themselves rather than promote it into a Class 3 world.","But while they were fusing the dead world’s roots with this Class 2 world, Tower Canon’s Eight Pages realized that the extremely high concentration of death aura in the ley lines was slowly flowing toward one direction. This indicated that a part of the ley lines was rapidly losing death aura. Otherwise, it was impossible for there to be such a large impact!","Crimson instinctively looked at Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid questioningly.","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid immediately knew what Crimson was thinking. He suspected that this was the work of Epoch God Palace and that the two of them had brought back false information!","Violet Light Green hissed. “Cavity Orchid and I went to Four Seasons Mountain and met with one of the rulers of Epoch God Palace. He said himself that Epoch God Palace isn’t interested in this Class 2 world! There’s no way our information could be fake!”","Concubine Winding said in a low voice, “If that’s the case, is it possible that","Epoch God Palace is tricking us?”","Cavity Orchid was already harboring intense rage. But now that the information that he and Violet Light Green had risked their lives to obtain was being doubted again, he could no longer bear it.","“You should all be well aware that Tower Canon has neither the ability nor right to take on Epoch God Palace. Violet Light Green and I wouldn’t have had to make the trip if we did!","“If Epoch God Palace is truly interested in this Class 2 world, are all of you brave enough to continue coveting it? It’s more likely that Tower Canon will slink away again and let Epoch God Palace take over. Is it even necessary for Epoch God Palace to try and trick us? There has to be another reason.","“We are already mostly done with the ritual to fuse the dead world’s roots with this Class 2 world. Six of us will be sufficient to handle the rest of the ritual. I suggest that the two of us head to the location that’s losing death aura to investigate the situation. We will know the reason after the investigation!","“If my guess is right, the demon insects are the ones to blame! The demon insects have been locked in a stalemate with the dead spirits. They must be trying to use this in their counterattack.”","The other members of Tower Canon found Cavity Orchid’s analysis to be reasonable.","At that moment, they all felt the tugs of their selfish urges.","Fusing the dead world’s roots with this Class 2 world required a lot of energy.","Meanwhile, investigating the source of the death aura leak sounded like a leisure trip.","Even if the demon insects attained power that was beyond this Class 2 world, they couldn’t defeat the members of Tower Canon.","If the demon insects were truly the cause of the death aura leak, those who went on the investigative trip would be able to capture numerous female insects with Class 1 Genetic Locks. They might even be able to find the main mother!","The main mother would belong to whoever found her.","None of the members of Tower Canon could see a reason to pass up on such an opportunity!","It was just as Cavity Orchid had said. There was no need for Epoch God Palace to play dirty tricks if they wanted to target Tower Canon.","Eye Shadow never preferred direct confrontations and could not help but say, “I have the least energy out of everyone here. I can’t participate in the ritual. I think I’m the best candidate to be one of the two to go on the investigative trip!”","Eye Shadow paused for a moment before she looked at Falling Rainbow and said, “Falling Rainbow’s Tower of Falling Rainbow hasn’t been found. Why doesn’t she come with me? We’ll also be able to search for the Tower of Falling Rainbow.”","On the other hand, Falling Rainbow’s brows were relaxed, and she said, “The Secret of the Dead is in the Tower of Falling Rainbow. It must be found! Without my Secret of the Dead, the dead world’s roots will still be able to be fused with the Class 2 world, but we won’t be able to fully tap into the dead world’s roots and speed up the absorption of this Class 2 world’s roots. I also think it’s best if I go with Eye Shadow.”","Eye Shadow’s lips curled slightly.","By continuing what she had said, Falling Rainbow had added impact to it.","Eye Shadow had her own considerations and plans for making such a suggestion!","The only one partaking in Crimson’s pool of profits was himself.","As the assumed leader of Tower Canon, Crimson could not fight for this opportunity.","If Eye Shadow was the one from her team chosen for this trip, Wave Glow and Concubine Winding would not participate.","Hence, her only options for a partner were Warbler Candle, Falling Rainbow, Violet Light Green, and Cavity Orchid.","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid would be receiving more profits. Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow were displeased that Crimson was willing to offer his share of the resources to fulfill Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid’s request.","If Eye Shadow endorsed Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid, she would inevitably attract hostility from Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow.","Coincidentally, she could use Falling Rainbow’s loss of the Tower of Falling Rainbow as the perfect excuse to suggest that she go with her.","Falling Rainbow was fully in charge of the alliance between her and Warbler Candle.","She could secretly strike up a partnership with Falling Rainbow during their journey.","Unless Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid wanted to give up their additional profits, they would have no choice but to agree to this agreement.","Warbler Candle looked at the frowning Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid before saying provokingly,","“We might be able to share this opportunity if you retract your request for additional profits.”","Warbler Candle’s words caused Crimson’s eyes to flash.","Warbler Candle never agreed to Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid’s requests. Crimson was offering his own share of resources. Thus, Warbler Candle did not have the right to say that.","There was a high chance that Warbler Candle’s words would escalate the already existing conflict.","Crimson hurriedly changed the topic and said, “I still have two of the Death Source Hearts. Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid, it’s true that the two of you took on a risk for the sake of Tower Canon. Once we are done with the ritual, you can each have one of my cherished Death Source Hearts.”","The other members of Tower Canon could not object to Crimson using his own resources to appease Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid.","However, Crimson’s actions caused the other members of Tower Canon to be even more curious and shocked. They did not understand what was bringing out such a large change in him.","Once Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow left, Crimson sensed the environment before saying, “Now that there are only six of us left to conduct the ritual, it will take longer to complete. Hopefully, nothing happens during the process. If so, the ritual will be officially completed within five days!”","The other five members of Tower Canon did not notice that the color of","Crimson’s eyes intensified while he spoke, and his lips had curled menacingly.","Ensconced in the sea of sand, Lin Yuan had his eyes closed as he meditated. He was basically done with all the matters he needed to accomplish. All he could do now was wait for the Eight Pages of Tower Canon to arrive.","Lin Yuan was openly baiting the Eight Pages of Tower Canon because he felt that it would be best to speed up the demon insects’ cleaning of death aura from the ley lines since they could do so.","Additionally, it would effectively cut down Tower Canon’s top combat power.","Lastly, Lin Yuan wanted to keep one of the bodies of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon or capture one of them alive.","He could then use the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to interrogate them or Red Thorn’s Tongue of Relinquish to take control of their body. Both paths would allow him to obtain a significant amount of information about Tower Canon.","Lin Yuan needed to understand Tower Canon’s goal and the dead world.","At that moment, he received information from the Moon Empress through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Moon Empress]: Little Yuan, you are not in the Radiance Federation presently. Does this mean that you are executing a plan? I don’t have any requests to make of you. All I hope is that you will look out for your safety and try to stay away from dangerous situations!","When the Moon Empress received Lin Yuan’s call and confirmed that he was not in the Radiance Federation, she was immediately filled with a foreboding feeling.","At that moment, she hated how helpless she was.","If only she was powerful enough to take on Tower Canon, Lin Yuan would not have to shoulder all of the responsibility on his own!","A wave of warmth washed over Lin Yuan when he saw the Moon Empress’ message.","The past three years felt as long as half of his life.","He had transformed from a weak regular person to a hero who could hold up the world.","Lin Yuan had accumulated ample experience and made many good friends.","Before he rose up and left the nest, the Moon Empress had been the one taking care of him.","Now, it was time for him to take over the mantle from his master and protect the Moon Empress as well as the Radiance Federation!","[Lin Yuan]: Master, you don’t have to worry about me. If things go well, I’ll be able to return to the Radiance Federation to see you soon.","The Moon Empress relaxed when she saw Lin Yuan’s response.","But soon, her chest tightened, and her heart started to hammer.","If things went well, Lin Yuan would be able to return to the Radiance","Federation soon. But what if things didn’t go well? What would happen then? The Moon Empress was intelligent and knew that things not going well in a battle against Tower Canon could only result in death.","If Tower Canon captured Lin Yuan, his life would be worse than death. As worried as the Moon Empress was, her fist slowly relaxed.","If Tower Canon killed Lin Yuan, it would not be long before the rest of the lifeforms in the main world followed.","Rather than being worried, it would be more useful if she supported and prayed for Lin Yuan.","As overwhelmed with emotions as the Moon Empress was, she did not stop issuing order after order in an orderly fashion.."]},{"number":2716,"title":"Chapter 2716 Stacking the Lotus Imprints!","paragraphs":["2716 Stacking the Lotus Imprints!","The Moon Empress was Lin Yuan’s Master and a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty. She needed to take responsibility for every citizen in the Radiance Federation.","If Lin Yuan died at the hands of Tower Canon, the Moon Empress would use her actual body to fend off the dead spirits wave when it closed in on the Radiance Federation.","When the Moon Empress was done communicating with Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper, Purple Love and Ice Flow contacted him through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Purple Love and Ice Flow had heard from the Moon Empress that Lin Yuan would be battling Tower Canon.","[Purple Love]: Lin Yuan, where are you? I will lead all the Heavenly Family Feys from the Heavenly Family Cottage to support you!","[Ice Flow]: Lin Yuan, all of the experts from the Vast Sea Labyrinth have gathered. You should be the one to command the battle between the main world’s lifeforms and the dead spirits! Please give us your orders!","Lin Yuan’s lips curled when he saw the messages from Purple Love and Ice Flow that represented the wills of the Heavenly Family Cottage and Vast Sea Labyrinth. He was very pleased with their attitudes.","Their attitudes were a sign that the Heavenly Family Cottage and Vast Sea Labyrinth were ready to sacrifice themselves.","However, he would not need anyone else in this battle. This would be a battle between Lin Yuan and Keira and Tower Canon.","Even experts like Purple Love and Ice Flow would inevitably lose their lives if they participated in this battle.","Lin Yuan responded to Purple Love.","[Lin Yuan]: Auntie Purple, all you need to do is lead the Heavenly Family Feys in helping Master protect the Radiance Federation! I will handle it myself. Even if you come, you won’t be able to help and will end up needlessly sacrificing yourselves!","Purple Love was silent for a long time after she received Lin Yuan’s message. She later looked into the distance and clasped her hands together as she started to pray.","Blood New Moon and White Phoenix looked at Purple Love curiously. They did not understand why she was acting in such a manner. Wasn’t she communicating with Lin Yuan about how they would be fighting back against Tower Canon?","Blue Lotus was the most sensitive and thoughtful of the group. If Lin Yuan had given the Heavenly Family Cottage an order, Purple Love would have informed them of it.","When Blue Lotus saw how formidable Lin Yuan was when he fused the main world with the five dimensional worlds, she knew that there was an uncrossable chasm between him and everyone else.","She had given Lin Yuan her blessing. If something happened to him, she would be alerted immediately through it.","As such, Blue Lotus also placed her hands together and began to pray for Lin Yuan.","A moment later, Blue Lotus heard Purple Love say while choking back tears, “We will remain in the Radiance Federation alongside the Moon Empress to await the return of the hero!”","Purple Love did not know if Lin Yuan would be able to protect the main world from Tower Canon. Nonetheless, waiting for him to return was her way of sending her best wishes.","After praying for Lin Yuan, she led the other Heavenly Family Feys and headed to the Leaning Moon Mountain.","...","When Ice Flow saw Lin Yuan’s message, a flurry of emotions exploded within him.","[Lin Yuan]: All you need to do is look after the sea clans. Leave everything else to the demon insects battling the dead spirits at the bottom of the sea. I will do my best to make everything better.","The sea clans always viewed themselves as above the humans. The Vast Sea Labyrinth never cared about the human factions in the past.","But now, the human factions had saved the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Ice Flow did not know how to express his gratitude.","He could only imagine the weight of the burden that Lin Yuan had to carry in order to make everything better. He was taking it upon himself to try to restore peace to the main world.","Lin Yuan had not given the Vast Sea Labyrinth any orders, but Ice Flow could not sit by and do nothing. Since Lin Yuan had sent the demon insects to protect the sea clans, they would protect the humans!","After discussing the matter with his two brothers, Ice Flow led the experts from the Vast Sea Labyrinth to the sea neighboring the Radiance Federation.","Since Lin Yuan was protecting the sea clans, they would safeguard Lin Yuan’s homeland.","...","After Eighth Page Eye Shadow and Fifth Page Falling Rainbow left Tower Canon’s fortress, they did not immediately head to the location that was losing death aura.","Eye Shadow looked at Falling Rainbow, who was releasing her spiritual energy and trying to pick up a sense of the Tower of Falling Rainbow, and said, “Falling Rainbow, you need to know your priorities. I don’t think you should head to the Startling Lines Continent now to search for the Tower of Falling Rainbow.","“Your book is a treasure from a Class 3 world’s dimensional world. Aside from Epoch God Palace, no other entity in this world can steal such a treasure. Even if an entity from this world stumbles on the book, the book will suck out its soul.”","Falling Rainbow raised her pretty seven-colored eyes and looked at Eye Shadow with irritation. “Eye Shadow, there isn’t anyone else here but us. You don’t have to put on an act in front of me. You definitely aren’t as simple as you seem. If your treasure was lost, you would probably be more frantic than I am now!”","Eye Shadow’s gaze changed, and she smirked mockingly. “Falling Rainbow, how simple or otherwise my thoughts are doesn’t have anything to do with you. You couldn’t even look after your treasure properly and left it in your tower.","“I won’t stop you if you insist on going to the Startling Lines Continent. I can go and clear out the demon insects on my own! I might not be full power, but I won’t have any trouble eliminating the demon insects.","“Crimson, Violet Light Green, and the rest can also sense the death aura being sucked out from the ley lines. I can’t see them being as lenient with you as Warbler Candle is. You will have to use your own abilities to make up for the death aura roots that end up being lost because of a hold-up that you caused!","“I have said all that I need to say. You can decide for yourself whether to listen to me or not.”","Once she was done speaking, Eye Shadow could not be bothered to continue wasting time with Falling Rainbow.","She had already been delayed a day because of Falling Rainbow. She was the one who had suggested investigating the death aura leak and the one who had endorsed Falling Rainbow.","If anything went wrong, she would have to take full responsibility. This implied that she would lose profits.","Eye Shadow did not want to give up any potential profits.","Falling Rainbow was not afraid that the other members of Tower Canon would have objections against her.","Because of that incident, all the other members of Tower Canon, aside from Second Page Warbler Candle, were already displeased with her.","Frankly, Falling Rainbow felt extremely wronged with regard to that incident.","She had made the decision with the silent support of the rest.","However, she had to take on all of the blame because she had been the one to raise the suggestion.","The other members of Tower Canon had been blaming her for that incident ever since, and she had become wholly disappointed in Tower Canon.","The real reason Falling Rainbow changed her mind from heading to the Startling Lines Continent to look for the Tower of Falling Rainbow was that she did not want Eye Shadow to have more opportunities to capture the demon insects. Otherwise, she could not answer to Warbler Candle when she returned.","Falling Rainbow was well aware of how Warbler Candle treated her, so she always treated Warbler Candle decently as well.","Falling Rainbow did not take long to catch up with Eye Shadow.","Falling Rainbow looked at Eye Shadow beside her and said sarcastically, “Eye Shadow, whoever is stronger should call the shots. We will use our capabilities to fight for the female demon insects with Class 1 and 2 Genetic Locks. There’s no need to collect the other demon insects. Let’s handle the rest as we see fit!”","When she saw Eye Shadow frown, a thought struck Falling Rainbow, and she changed her tone, “Actually, why don’t we work together? Once we are done handling the death aura leak in the ley lines, let’s go to the Startling Lines Continent together. The humans have not only been building up the Radiance Federation but the neighboring Startling Lines Continent as well.","“The eight of us have only divided up the resources from the Radiance Federation. Why don’t we empty out the Startling Lines Continent? Crimson, Violet Light Green, and Cavity Orchid won’t be able to protest! What do you think?”","If Falling Rainbow had come out on her own, she would have never dared to do such a thing.","Six of the members of Tower Canon were displeased with her, and her only ally was Warbler Candle. Even if she emptied out the Startling Lines Continent, she could not hold on to the resources.","But if she teamed up with Eye Shadow, she would be part of a pool of profits involving five Tower Canon members.","Even if First Page Crimson, Violet Light Green, and Cavity Orchid were unhappy, they could not act on it.","Eye Shadow was intrinsically greedy. Falling Rainbow was certain that Eye Shadow would not turn her down.","Falling Rainbow silently watched Eye Shadow’s expression change. Eventually, Eye Shadow said firmly, “Since that’s the case, why don’t we split both the work of handling the death aura leak and the resources from the Startling Lines Continent equally? If you agree to this, I will work with you!”","Falling Rainbow’s eyes glinted when she heard that. She was silent for a moment before saying, “This should be the first time we’ll be working together in almost 10,000 years. I hope we will work well together!”","Given that she was stronger than Eye Shadow, Falling Rainbow did not want to agree to Eye Shadow’s request. But if she turned her down, it was highly probable that Eye Shadow would oppose her.","Eye Shadow had Sixth Page Wave Glow and Seventh Page Concubine Winding on her side, while she only had Warbler Candle.","If she occupied more of Eye Shadow’s resources, Eye Shadow could sell her out when they returned and end up receiving 3/8 of the resources from the Startling Lines Continent.","...","It did not take long for Eye Shadow and Falling Rainbow to arrive at the canyon.","The two of them had eliminated many insect armies during their journey.","The moment the two of them glimpsed the canyon, they halted their steps and did not enter.","They could sense billions of demon insects underground, absorbing the ley line’s death aura. This was the source of the ley line leak.","However, the two of them felt disturbed.","Experts always trusted their sixth sense. Their sixth sense was the instinctual culmination of their soul and spirit. Stronger lifeforms had more accurate sixth senses.","The two of them had not felt so uneasy in a very long time.","At the instant that Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow appeared above the canyon, Lin Yuan used his faith power to sense their presence.","Aside from strengthening his divine kingdom, Lin Yuan did not have many other uses for his faith power.","However, Lin Yuan realized not long ago that if he was in the vicinity of a large number of lifeforms that contributed faith power to him, he could use his faith power to detect his surroundings.","The demon insects that Keira produced were all Lin Yuan’s believers.","Lin Yuan could even use his faith power to sense the emotions of these two members of Tower Canon.","It was clear that the two of them had noticed something was off about the environment under them and had hence yet to take action.","One of them was even already thinking about retreating.","After sensing this intention to retreat, Lin Yuan used the Abyss Red Lotus’ ability, Hellfire Application.","In an instant, the energy of the five dimensional worlds and the main world that the Abyss Red Lotus controlled was pumped into Lin Yuan’s body.","Four black roots emerged from the ground and shot toward Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow.","Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow could sense that something was wrong but neither of them had expected to be ambushed!","After Lin Yuan ascertained that there were only two of them, he made his plans.","He would kill one while leaving the other alive. He would kill the weaker one while taking the stronger one prisoner. This would allow Red Thorn and, by extension, him, to take control of another expert.","Furthermore, the stronger member of Tower Canon would probably know more information about Tower Canon.","Lin Yuan used Splendor of Fire at the same time that he used Hellfire Application.","In an instant, fire-elemental energy erupted and enveloped the entire canyon.","Spirit qi and death aura were all pushed out of this space by the fire-elemental energy.","As long as the Abyss Red Lotus was stronger than its target, it would be able to rob and conquer its targets’ control over fire-elemental energy.","Lin Yuan could sense that the Abyss Red Lotus could take complete control of the fire-elemental energy in the environment. This indicated that he was stronger than both of these members of Tower Canon!","Eye Shadow and Falling Rainbow both put up defenses against Lin Yuan’s lethal attacks.","From their auras, Lin Yuan could sense that these two members of Tower Canon were on the same level as him.","This made him both relieved and concerned.","He was glad that he had discovered the Abyss Red Lotus in the abyssal world and used it to help him gain power from the five dimensional worlds’ energies.","Otherwise, with just Eternal Source, who was an Afterlife Realm Dictator, he would not be able to truly take on the Eight Pages of Tower Canon.","It was no wonder that Crimson had not been bothered when he discovered Ancient Ocean and Ink Ocean’s presence. Dictators with such power were of no threat to him.","Due to Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow’s defenses, the Abyss Red Lotus’ four roots did not manage to wrap around them.","However, Lin Yuan had also used Hellfire Lotus Imprint on the two of them.","Hellfire Lotus Imprint would restrict their ability to draw on energy from the environment and seal off their bodies’ existing energy.","The effects of one layer of Hellfire Lotus Imprint were not significant.","But as the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots continued to wrangle with the Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow, the layers of Hellfire Lotus Imprints also stacked up layer by layer."]},{"number":2717,"title":"Chapter 2717 Fall of the Eight Pages!","paragraphs":["2717 Fall of the Eight Pages!","When the Hellfire Lotus Imprints were applied to a target’s body, they would turn into crimson lotus tattoos.","The first layer of lotus tattoos was extremely light, but as the number of layers increased, it looked as though they were engraved on Eighth Page Eye Shadow’s body.","The lotus tattoos might look mysterious and mystical and carry a magnificent power, but Fifth Page Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow became increasingly uncomfortable as the layers of lotus tattoos applied to their bodies increased.","The two of them noticed that not only had the flow of death aura in their bodies stagnated, but they could no longer activate their abilities. As a result, they weakened continuously while fending off Lin Yuan’s attacks.","If Lin Yuan was fighting Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow normally, they would not be in such a sorry state, even if they were truly less powerful than him.","The two of them were at such a disadvantage because Lin Yuan’s ambush had been sudden.","The two of them had been unable to adopt defensive states because they had been unaware of Lin Yuan’s presence. If Lin Yuan had shown himself to the two of them and given them a chance to prepare, they would have been able to flee even if they failed to overpower him!","If the two of them took off in different directions, at least one of them would be able to escape.","If the two sides of experts had agreed to battle, secret ambushes would be extremely despicable.","However, Lin Yuan’s goal was not to battle but to protect the main world.","Falling Rainbow let out a shrill shriek. “Just who are you? Didn’t Epoch God Palace say that you aren’t interested in this Class 2 world?”","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow.","This petite girl with seven-colored eyes had mentioned Epoch God Palace, a topic that Lin Yuan was the most interested in finding out more about.","It just so happened that this was the member of Tower Canon whom Lin Yuan had decided to preserve.","Lin Yuan did not respond to Falling Rainbow’s shriek. It was evident that this Tower Canon member assumed he was a member of Epoch God Palace.","This meant that Epoch God Palace was the only entity capable of possessing such power.","This revelation caused Lin Yuan to be slightly fearful of Epoch God Palace.","If Epoch God Palace’s sights were not set on this Class 2 world, what were they truly interested in?","Spring and Summer were watching this from high up in the sky and blinked.","It had been some time since they left Epoch God Palace.","It was likely that Tower Canon’s members were saying this because they had already paid a visit to Epoch God Palace.","Winter was trying to open a special path from this world to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Hence, Tower Canon’s members must have met with Autumn.","This way of speaking fit with Autumn’s style.","In Autumn’s opinion, Epoch God Palace existed to follow Lord Saint. This meant they were not linked to this Class 2 world at all.","But from the perspective of karma, Lord Saint was rooted in this Class 2 world. Lord Saint’s objective was their will!","Before Autumn met with Lord Saint, he would have no clue what Epoch God Palace’s goal was.","Spring and Summer confirmed that Lin Yuan was Lord Saint and knew that he was enemies with Tower Canon. They had not acted because they were worried about affecting Lin Yuan’s growth.","As things stood, Lin Yuan was showing no signs of being imminently defeated.","Although this Floating World Controlling Honorable Lotus had been stained by fire elements and mutated, karma had brought it to Lord Saint’s side before he had awakened.","The Floating World Controlling Honorable Lotus was an auspicious entity that was kept by Lord Saint’s side constantly. The sacred aura within it was able to purge impurities from souls despite having transformed into fire elements.","The lifeforms from Tower Canon used death aura as their main source of energy so their souls could not be more contaminated.","As the scales of the battle continued tipping toward Lin Yuan, Spring and Summer let out soft sighs.","It seemed that it was still not the right time for them to appear in front of Lord Saint!","Falling Rainbow did not receive any reply to her question. The only response she received was a never-ending barrage of attacks.","In a defensive stance, Falling Rainbow flashed herself behind Eye Shadow before pointing at her forehead.","Soon, a solid stream of energy emerged from Falling Rainbow’s body. The energy pierced the clouds and caused the sky to darken.","A menacing and bizarre figure emerged from Falling Rainbow’s body. The figure transformed into a silhouette that resembled a dark gray rainbow.","The strange silhouette crashed into the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots but did not make even the slightest impact on the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots. Rather, the attacks activated a strange type of energy within the Abyss Red Lotus.","Lin Yuan found the appearance of this type of energy to be very strange.","Could it be that the Abyss Red Lotus was showing signs of evolving while battling the Eight Pages of Tower Canon?","Lin Yuan quickly shook his head.","Instead of an evolution, a more accurate description would be the awakening of its bloodline.","There seemed to be more to the Abyss Red Lotus’ bloodline than what met the eye!","At that moment, Morbius’ voice appeared in Lin Yuan’s ear.","“Partner, I seem to have remembered something! I think I can guess why Tower Canon is carrying out the Sleeper’s Revival plan. I also know the secret behind the world classes!","“Partner, it’s likely that Tower Canon is a marauder from the dimensional world of a Class 3 world. When worlds are being promoted, the main worlds usually win out, and they absorb the dimensional worlds.","“However, there are always a few resistant fellows from dimensional worlds who not only want to break free from their main world but also rob the main world of its place. They refused to give up even after their failure and have brought their dimensional world’s roots with them to try to make a comeback.”","When Lin Yuan heard Morbius’ voice in his head, he began conversing with Morbius, “Partner, if that’s true, what will happen to the Class 3 world?”","Morbius replied in a conclusive tone, “The Class 3 world will forever lose the opportunity to be promoted to a Class 4 world. Tower Canon is trying to use the dimensional world filled with death aura to consume the main world’s roots. This must be the true goal of the Sleeper’s Revival plan!”","Lin Yuan thought, I caught Eighth Page Apoptosis and interrogated him, but I wasn’t able to find out the crux of the issue. It wasn’t because he lied to be but because he was kept from the truth, too. Otherwise, he would not have escaped the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s detection.","As for whether Morbius’ conjecture is fact, I will be able to find this out once I capture the true Eight Pages of Tower Canon!","“Partner, for the good of the main world, this calamity must come to an end as soon as possible! Otherwise, not only will the ley lines be damaged beyond repair, but the tampering with this world’s energy might also cause the appearance of inappropriate dimensional worlds!”","Lin Yuan did not stop his attacks while he was conversing with Morbius. Rather, the attacks became even more ferocious.","Lin Yuan focused more of his attacks on Eye Shadow.","He used the Abyss Red Lotus’ exclusive skill, Red Lotus Hellfire. The Red Lotus Hellfire burned to life on Eye Shadow’s body.","It was not Eye Shadow’s flesh that was being burned, but her karma, bloodline, and energy. This burning was one that led to the utter obliteration of a lifeform’s existence.","As the burning continued, more layers of Hellfire Lotus Imprints were applied to Eye Shadow’s body. The Hellfire Lotus Imprints sealed her body, rendering her no different from an pill furnace!","At that moment, Eye Shadow was still wielding her own energy but was finding it an immense struggle to use the death energy to break through the increasing layers of Hellfire Lotus Imprints. This was because the Hellfire Lotus Imprints could seal the target’s abilities, making it difficult for Eye Shadow to even employ her life-preserving methods.","Lin Yuan only used Red Lotus Hellfire to burn Eye Shadow. He did not use lethal methods against Falling Rainbow.","Falling Rainbow had been battling the black lotus roots as layers of Hellfire Lotus Imprints were intermittently applied to her body.","But at the same time, she watched as the Red Lotus Hellfire burned Eye Shadow.","Falling Rainbow could sense that Eye Shadow’s roots were being rapidly damaged.","Eye Shadow was in a worse state than at the beginning of their slumber.","Falling Rainbow could sense that the person attacking them was going easy on her. Otherwise, her body would not have fewer lotus imprints than Eye Shadow.","Why was she not being burned by the crimson flames?","The gears in Falling Rainbow’s mind turned, and she hypothesized the reason for the enemy’s actions. They likely wanted to use her to gain information on Tower Canon.","Since Falling Rainbow’s life hung in the balance, she had no qualms about betraying Tower Canon.","But if she did end up selling out Tower Canon, would that be enough to guarantee her survival?","At that moment, Falling Rainbow knew that whoever was attacking her and Eye Shadow could not be from Epoch God Palace because the latter already knew everything about Tower Canon.","It seemed that they had underestimated the natives from this Class 2 world!","As she looked at Eye Shadow, who was slowly dying, Falling Rainbow did not feel a shred of sympathy. Instead, she felt strong resentment for Eye Shadow bubbling within her.","If Eye Shadow had not endorsed her for this investigative trip, she would not have been here suffering such fierce attacks and on the brink of becoming a prisoner!","Lin Yuan was reaching near the bottom of the barrel of his store of energy.","Suddenly, a dragon roar reverberated throughout the canyon.","Lin Yuan summoned Blackie and used Spirit Injection to recover his energy.","Since everything was going well, Lin Yuan decided not to use the Spirit Qi Imprint. He also did not instruct the Abyss Red Lotus to use Burning Lotus Cleansing Dance and Everything to Ashes.","Once he used his secret weapons, they would need to enter a long recovery period.","Lin Yuan intended to use his limited resources in the most optimal manner, which meant using them on the other six members of Tower Canon.","Lin Yuan recovered his energy while maintaining his stalemate with Eye Shadow and Falling Rainbow.","Hard work never betrayed the determined.","Soon, Eye Shadow’s soul was burned to ruin.","On the other hand, after being burned by the Red Lotus Hellfire, Eye Shadow’s body had been tempered and was much tougher than it had originally been.","A light emerged from Eye Shadow’s body and took the form of a book.","There was a spectral illusion behind the book.","Lin Yuan immediately recognized this as a Secret of the Dead from the dead world.","The treasure from the dimensional world of a Class 3 was definitely of a higher level than the treasure of a dimensional world of a Class 1 world.","Lin Yuan had accidentally absorbed the treasure from the dead world because he had bumped into it. As a result, he had been in a coma for almost a month.","Although the coma would not cause significant harm to his body, he would be using the fountain of faith in his divine kingdom to take control of and subsume the Secret of the Dead.","But with all that was going on, how could Lin Yuan take the time to go into a sleep state in order to absorb the dead world’s Secret of the Dead?","Lin Yuan used the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots to grab the book before carefully sealing it up. Once he defeated Tower Canon, he would collect all of their Secrets of the Dead!","Now, he needed to deal with this member of Tower Canon with seven-colored eyes.","Lin Yuan knew that it was time for him to show himself.","The sand rapidly roiled in the canyon.","Lin Yuan’s body rose into the air, and he faced Falling Rainbow directly. He asked Falling Rainbow calmly, “I think it’s time for us to have a good talk! Which Page of Tower Canon are you? How should I address you?”","Lin Yuan’s serene tone caused a chill to run up Falling Rainbow’s spine.","This young human had to be brimming with hatred toward her.","Tower Canon saw the lifeforms of this Class 2 world as the fertilizer to spur the growth of the dead spirits. To this Class 2 world, Tower Canon were invaders who had been plotting against them for a long time.","When Falling Rainbow felt the lotus imprints sealing her, she knew that if this young man didn’t like her answer, he would set the crimson flames that burned Eye Shadow on her, too!","“My name is Falling Rainbow. I am the Fifth Page.”","Falling Rainbow did not say anything else after answering Lin Yuan’s questions. She began examining him seriously.","From Falling Rainbow’s actions, Lin Yuan could tell that she was intelligent. Making an enemy of an intelligent being would lead to painful costs.","However, Lin Yuan did like smart prisoners.","Smart prisoners were more aware of how to act appropriately given their circumstances. He would also be able to find more answers to the questions that he had.","“You should be aware of why I let you live instead of destroying your soul. I will give you the chance to say three lines. I hope the three lines will be enough for you to move me.”","While he spoke, fiery Red Lotus Hellfire appeared in his palm.","At first, Lin Yuan had many questions for Falling Rainbow.","But after Morbius regained the most recent portion of its memories, Lin Yuan now had a clear understanding of Tower Canon’s objective.","If Falling Rainbow was sufficiently intelligent, she would be able to pique his interest with the three lines. It would also allow Lin Yuan to find out the direction that would be the best for him to take in order to glean the most information from Falling Rainbow.","Tower Canon could even sense the loss of death aura from the ley lines and had sent experts to investigate it.","They had to be aware that the death aura leak had yet to be addressed and was worsening.","They might even be aware that one of the Eight Pages had already died.","Lin Yuan needed to hasten his interrogation of Falling Rainbow!"]},{"number":2718,"title":"Chapter 2718 Illegitimate Spawn of the Blood Species!","paragraphs":["2718 Illegitimate Spawn of the Blood Species!","Cold beads of sweat began dripping down Fifth Page Falling Rainbow’s back when she heard what Lin Yuan said.","Even First Page Crimson and Second Page Warbler Candle might not be this young man’s match.","Given the circumstances, Tower Canon’s secrets were not significant to this young man.","Falling Rainbow had no doubt that this young man would take her life without batting an eye.","Falling Rainbow pondered for a moment. She believed that only information about Epoch God Palace would be able to pique Lin Yuan’s interest. However, she knew very little about Epoch God Palace and did not know enough to spin out useful information.","Epoch God Palace’s target was not Tower Canon or this main world.","Falling Rainbow remembered that Third Page Violet Light Green and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid had mentioned that a member of Epoch God Palace had asked if anything was special about the main world.","There was no question that this young man was the most special presence.","Hence, Falling Rainbow said loudly, “You are probably Epoch God Palace’s target! With your power, you must have heard of Epoch God Palace’s presence! Eighth Page Apoptosis who went running to seek refuge from you must have told you about them.”","Warbler Candle had intentionally allowed Apoptosis to learn of Epoch God Palace’s presence. Warbler Candle had told Apoptosis about Epoch God Palace exactly because she hoped he would tell the news to the humans and bait them into investigating Epoch God Palace and find out their objective.","Lin Yuan’s eyes widened when he heard what Falling Rainbow said.","Since he was Epoch God Palace’s target, did that mean that they had found out about Morbius?","A chill washed over Lin Yuan’s heart.","In the past, he had always fought his enemies from the shadows while they were out in the open.","But now, he was the one who was out in the open while Epoch God Palace was hidden.","He did not even know anything about Epoch God Palace, yet they had already locked onto him as a target.","Lin Yuan resolved to learn all about Epoch God Palace from Falling Rainbow.","But before that, he needed to verify the truth of what Falling Rainbow was saying.","Lin Yuan instructed the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to release its spores over Falling Rainbow.","Falling Rainbow noticed the appearance of the spores but dared not try to stop them from entering her body.","Epoch God Palace was truly targeting him!","Nonetheless, she had spoken the truth. He was Epoch God Palace’s target.","However, the concept of target that he had was different from what their true intentions were.","Spring and Summer, who were high up in the sky, felt themselves being hit by a wave of awkwardness.","It was good for Lin Yuan to find out about Epoch God Palace. However, Falling Rainbow’s words would cause Lin Yuan to feel hostility toward Epoch God Palace.","If Lord Saint felt hostile toward them and started to resent them, they would be left at a loss!","Falling Rainbow deserved to die!","If Lin Yuan had not taken Falling Rainbow as his prisoner and was not standing before Falling Rainbow, Spring and Summer would have killed Falling Rainbow immediately to stop her from prattling more nonsense to Lin Yuan!","Given Tower Canon’s level, they did not have the right to learn of Epoch God Palace’s true purpose!","“Very good. Your words have temporarily preserved your life. You will now share all the information you possess about Epoch God Palace.”","Falling Rainbow hurriedly asked, “If I tell you everything that I know about Epoch God Palace, will you spare my life?”","Lin Yuan glared frostily at Falling Rainbow and said, “You don’t have the right to negotiate with me. I will end your life now if you are unwilling to comply.”","When he was done speaking, the Red Lotus Hellfire lit up on Falling Rainbow’s body, and her agonized howls filled the air above the canyon.","There was no way that Lin Yuan was going to let Falling Rainbow keep her life.","Falling Rainbow was one of the perpetrators behind the dead spirits crisis that had caused the death of millions of lifeforms in the main world. A being like that did not deserve to be spared!","If Falling Rainbow was unwilling to speak, Lin Yuan would not mind showing her his capabilities.","While the fervent Red Lotus Hellfire was burning her, Falling Rainbow felt the same anguish that Eye Shadow had felt.","The crimson flames burned Falling Rainbow’s body and encroached into her soul.","Previously, Falling Rainbow was trying to set up insurance for herself. But now, she was trying to keep herself alive. If she revealed all that she knew, she would have a higher chance of surviving.","“I can’t say that I’m familiar with Epoch God Palace. All I know is that they have been searching for special entities. Both you and your feys fit the profile of what Epoch God Palace is searching for. They have already begun taking action.”","Lin Yuan waved his hand and extinguished the flames on Falling Rainbow’s body. “Let me ask you. Just how powerful is Epoch God Palace?”","This was the question that Lin Yuan most badly wanted an answer to.","Alas, Falling Rainbow did not give him the answer that he was seeking.","“Epoch God Palace’s power can only be described as unfathomable. It’s a level that is even beyond my imagination. 6,000 years ago, one of the rulers of Epoch God Palace injured all Eight Pages of Tower Canon grievously with just one attack, leaving us with no choice but to hibernate for the past 6,000 years. Otherwise, we would already have died alongside the dead world!”","It turned out that Epoch God Palace was that powerful! One of their members was already more powerful than Falling Rainbow could comprehend!","If that was the case, he would not be able to take on Epoch God Palace even if he fused with the Abyss Red Lotus.","It would be extremely easy for the rulers of Epoch God Palace to kill him if they wanted to.","Although he could take Falling Rainbow prisoner, the fact remained that they were actually on the same level.","This filled Lin Yuan with great perturbance.","But it did not take long for him to compose himself.","The most important matter at hand was to deal with Tower Canon.","Thus, Lin Yuan asked Falling Rainbow in a low voice, “Do the other members of Tower Canon know that one of the Eight Pages has died?”","Falling Rainbow had already decided to answer all of Lin Yuan’s questions honestly.","She did not know what had just entered her body.","But after she gave her reply, white fungal strains grew out of whatever entered her body.","Lin Yuan had not done anything to verify what she said after he saw the white fungal strains. It was likely that they had the ability to ascertain the truth!","Her response would lead to her betraying Tower Canon. Nonetheless, she had already grown disillusioned with Tower Canon and had no qualms about turning against them. Even if the remaining Eight Pages were aware of her difficult situation, they wouldn’t offer assistance.","“It’s unlikely that First Page Crimson and the rest are aware that Eye Shadow is already dead. However, they do know that the death aura leak hasn’t been addressed.”","Falling Rainbow had been trying to find a way to save her life ever since she answered Lin Yuan’s question.","She was well aware of how much this human hated her.","Tower Canon was trying to destroy all the lifeforms in this Class 2 world, making them sworn enemies of all these lifeforms.","If she wanted to ameliorate the hatred in this young man’s eyes, she would have to earn it by contributing value. The best way to do so would be to help this young man eliminate the other members of Tower Canon.","“If you are willing to let me keep my life, I can help you to sow discord within Tower Canon. The Eight Pages are always locked in an intense fight over resources. I will follow your orders, and this will save you a lot of trouble in your endeavor to take down Tower Canon! What do you think of this?”","This was the most attractive bait that Falling Rainbow could think of offering Lin Yuan.","Falling Rainbow did not know what to do in case he did not accept her proposal.","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow and asked, “How will you sow discord among the members of Tower Canon? Is Tower Canon so ununited? You must be aware that my goal is to kill all the members of Tower Canon.","“If you help me to reach my goal, you will have proven your value, and I will give you the chance to continue living! I will also take you with me when I eventually go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!”","Falling Rainbow was overjoyed when she heard that. She finally found a way to keep herself alive!","However, it would not be easy to help Lin Yuan eliminate the other six members of Tower Canon.","She had left for this trip with Eye Shadow. When she returned without Eye Shadow, she could not provide the others with an acceptable explanation!","Once Crimson and the others were done with the ritual to fuse the dead world’s roots with this main world, she would have to answer for Eye Shadow’s absence after three days passed.","Hence, she would have to act before Crimson and the others became suspicious of her in order for her to cooperate with Lin Yuan!","After Falling Rainbow told Lin Yuan about the situation, she said sincerely, “For now, I can’t come up with a plan. But I must return as soon as possible. I will come up with a plan on the way back. You should have the means to place shackles within me. The other members of Tower Canon will not tolerate traitors. The only way I can save myself is to help you!”","Lin Yuan said doubtfully, “It goes without saying that I will take control of you before I let you go. You don’t have to concern yourself with this. If you can’t cooperate with my plan, I will also use my methods to take your life. So don’t think of trying any tricks!”","One of the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots wrapped around Falling Rainbow, and the tip of the root pierced Falling Rainbow’s soul, leaving a black imprint.","Once Falling Rainbow broke free from Lin Yuan’s control, the imprint would instantly begin burning with the Abyss Red Lotus and destroy Falling Rainbow’s soul!","When he was doing this, Lin Yuan waved at Falling Rainbow, indicating that she could leave at any time.","Falling Rainbow did not feel happy in the least as she was about to depart from Lin Yuan’s side. Rather, her heart could not be heavier. Her brain was filled with thoughts about how she could fulfill his orders.","Falling Rainbow always abided by the principle that it was better to cling to a difficult life than to choose death.","If she could go with Lin Yuan to the Sky Beyond the Clouds in the future, she would be able to lead a better life in that wider world than she could being stuck in this Class 2 world!","Before Falling Rainbow left, she told Lin Yuan in a low voice, “I hope that you will instruct the demon insects to stop absorbing the death aura from the ley lines. Otherwise, I won’t be able to answer for my failure when I return. Naturally, I won’t be able to cooperate with your plan either!”","Lin Yuan immediately sent an order to Keira.","Keira relayed the orders to the female insects with Class 1 Genetic Locks, who transmitted it to the rest of the insect army.","The death aura only took a moment to burgeon in the cleaned-up ley line.","“You said that the death of a member of Tower Canon will draw suspicion to you. So I will give you five days. If you can’t be of any help to me after the five days have passed, the black imprint in your soul will begin to burn.”","Lin Yuan took out a Thoughts Letter Paper and tossed it to the Falling Rainbow.","“If you have any information that you want to share with me, you can write it on this paper. I will also communicate my orders through this paper. Your survival depends on whether you can be of value to me!”","Once Lin Yuan was done speaking, he did not continue interacting with Falling Rainbow and left the canyon.","The instant Lin Yuan left the canyon, the insect army under the canyon began to move. They shifted according to Lin Yuan’s movements.","Lin Yuan’s open operation was very successful.","Not only had he killed one of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon, but he had also taken control of another.","This was much more useful than killing Falling Rainbow directly!","It was unlikely that Tower Canon could have ever anticipated such a result!","From the attitudes that Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow had displayed when they arrived at the canyon, Tower Canon could not be less concerned about the human factions. Otherwise, they would have sent more than just two members to investigate the death aura leak.","Lin Yuan had agreed to Falling Rainbow’s suggestion because he wanted the members of Tower Canon to continue maintaining such a mindset.","Even if Falling Rainbow failed to come up with a plan, having a mole in Tower Canon would make it easier for Lin Yuan to learn about their movements!","As Spring watched Lin Yuan departing, she said solemnly, “Summer, Lord Saint has probably misunderstood Epoch God Palace. He really thinks of us as enemies now! I think that we need to do something to change his perception of us!”","Summer said with a sigh, “Spring, that’s a good idea. But how should we go about it? Forget it. For now, let’s just focus on protecting Lord Saint and helping him defeat Tower Canon!","“After he defeats Tower Canon, he will probably try to make contact with Epoch God Palace. If he initiates contact with Epoch God Palace, we will be able to reveal ourselves to him. Then, we will be able to explain ourselves to him. Given his personality, he will understand and forgive us!”","Spring said with a clenched jaw, “First Page Crimson better not disappoint his illegitimate bloodline of the Blood species.”"]},{"number":2719,"title":"Chapter 2719 Gray’s Evolution!","paragraphs":["2719 Gray’s Evolution!","In order to cooperate with Fifth Page Falling Rainbow’s plan, Lin Yuan did not continue instructing the army of demon insects to absorb death aura from the ley line under the canyon.","However, the demon insects did not halt completely.","The demon insects in the other areas of the main world continued absorbing death aura while searching for ley lines.","Lin Yuan learned about the dead world from Falling Rainbow.","First, Tower Canon extracted the death aura that had built up in the main world over the past billions of years and injected it into the ley lines to alter their states. They then used the dead world’s roots to activate the death aura in the ley lines with the intention of enabling the dead world to consume and replace the main world’s roots.","By combining the five dimensional worlds with the main world and promoting it from a Class 1 to a Class 2 world, Lin Yuan played directly into Tower Canon’s benefits! There was much more loot to plunder from a Class 2 world than a Class 1 world.","However, the dead world was only a dimensional world of a Class 3 world.","It was much more challenging for the remnants of the dead world to consume the roots of a Class 2 world than the roots of a Class 1 world. This was why Tower Canon’s plan had been progressing so slowly.","If the main world was still a Class 1 world, the roots of the dead world would have already consumed the roots of the main world.","Aside from continuously sending out dead dimensional lifeforms, Tower Canon had not made any significant moves recently.","If they had not discovered the death aura leak, there was no way that two of the Eight Pages would have stepped out into this world.","This was because Tower Canon had been cowering in fear of Epoch God Palace.","Given that he was Epoch God Palace’s target, it was more likely that they were foes rather than friends.","But when it came to limiting Tower Canon, Epoch God Palace had indeed been of help to Lin Yuan as they helped him to save on time.","Now, all Lin Yuan needed to do was wait to hear back from Falling Rainbow.","Even if Falling Rainbow could not meet his requests, she could report Tower Canon’s movements to him. This would make it easier for Lin Yuan to come up with responses.","From the way that Falling Rainbow and the other members of Tower Canon reacted when he was attacking them, Lin Yuan could tell that the Eight Pages were not on good terms.","The two of them had tried to use the other as shields to hide from the attacks.","If Falling Rainbow and the other members of Tower Canon worked together, they might not be able to win against him in the end, but they would not fall so quickly or miserably!","Hence, there was a high chance that Falling Rainbow would side with him in order to save her own life.","Lin Yuan entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone and went to Keira’s nest.","Hu Quan was leading the over 40 Spirit Craftsmen and almost 400 Land Imps in building the frame of Keira’s nest.","Due to the presence of the immense amount of pure spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, the demon insects could consume the spirit qi as food. If they wanted to replenish their vitality, they could consume the Soldier Ration Radishes, the best vitality source for lifeforms.","Keira’s nest was mainly functional as it served as her individual residence.","The surrounding nests linked together in a teardrop formation were the residences of the female insects.","The entire colony was a giant demon insect production line. Young demon insects with Class 2 and 3 Genetic Locks were born with every passing second.","Once these young demon insects were produced, Lin Yuan would immediately transport them to various parts of the main world to help with the dead spirits crisis.","Previously, the demon insects were mainly developed to target the special dead spirits.","But now, the demon insects were mainly developed to expand the insect army.","The larger the insect army, the faster the cleaning of the ley lines.","Every demon insect was naturally able to clean death aura.","Keira could also use her energy to develop demon insects with ‘shuttle’ functions that made them similar to the Dimensional Light Moth.","Fat Pocket could use the dimensional space in its body to store a large number of insect-species carcinoma feys. The demon insects with shuttle functions could do the same.","However, these demon insects could carry out coordinated transfers while Fat Pocket could not. This significantly raised the maneuverability of the enormous army.","It was because of this that the demon insects could thrive in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Aside from demon insects with shuttle abilities, Keira could produce demon insects with many other types of abilities.","Once Keira obtained the genes of powerful lifeforms, she could attempt to combine the lifeforms’ genes with the demon insect bloodline. This would enable her to produce demon insects with new abilities.","Hu Quan was currently assigning tasks to the Spirit Craftsmen and had not noticed Lin Yuan’s arrival.","Liu Tong, who was next to Hu Quan and watching the Land Imps work, immediately alerted Hu Quan when he noticed Lin Yuan. He bowed to Lin Yuan respectfully and loudly greeted him, “Lord City Lord.”","Hu Quan was a member of Sky City. The Heavenly Craft Pavilion, which he founded, was also under Sky City. It served and provided Sky City with resources just like the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce did.","Just like the members of the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce, the Spirit Craftsmen from the Heavenly Craft Pavilion could not call themselves members of Sky City.","However, six months ago, Hu Quan strongly endorsed Liu Tong to Lin Yuan as a new member of Sky City.","At first, the other Spirit Craftsmen saw Liu Tong as an in-name disciple. Now, they saw Liu Tong as Hu Quan’s disciple.","Lin Yuan had a deep impression of Liu Tong.","Aside from being hard-working and capable, he had a higher EQ than the other Spirit Craftsmen, as well as a sharper eye.","After his time in the marsh world, Liu Tong had also acquired strong management skills. This improved his ability to help Hu Quan manage the other Spirit Craftsmen.","Hu Quan’s craftsmanship was unquestionable. But he lagged far behind Liu Tong when it came to management and organization.","Liu Tong could make up for Hu Quan’s weakness.","Moreover, Liu Tong’s Spirit Craftsman talent was decent. The more time they spent together, the more Hu Quan came to adore Liu Tong!","Lin Yuan smiled and nodded at Liu Tong.","Lin Yuan knew that Liu Tong wanted to express his gratitude. Liu Tong’s set of feys was the best among the federations’ Spirit Craftsmen.","Lin Yuan was the only one in the entire main world that could supply functional-type Bronze/Legend feys suited for Spirit Craftsmen.","The time the Spirit Craftsmen spent in the marsh world had been exhausting, but they had enjoyed a very high quality of life. Most importantly, they had attained substantial hope.","When Hu Quan walked over to Lin Yuan, Keira also left her nest and made a beeline for Lin Yuan.","Hu Quan’s face fell when he saw Keira.","Lin Yuan knew that Hu Quan and Keira did not get along. Hu Quan had already complained to him about Keira multiple times in the short span of a few days!","However, Lin Yuan could not decide who was right and who was wrong.","As a top Spirit Craftsman, Hu Quan preferred inspirational designs over traditional and mundane ones. He always strove for the best aesthetic.","However, the most important factor to Keira was practicality. She preferred functionality over beauty. As such, she could not appreciate Hu Quan’s exquisite designs.","Keira would rather do away with unnecessary touches of beauty that served no purpose and have a wide environment that was conducive to the demon insects’ growth.","The demon insects had night vision, so Keira had rejected the light installations that Hu Quan wanted to build into the roof.","This caused Hu Quan to feel that he was not being included in the construction of the nest.","However, Lin Yuan had tasked him with building the nest.","Hu Quan was afraid Lin Yuan would think he lacked taste and competency once he saw this nest.","“Uncle Hu, Keira’s nest should be almost complete. You won’t have to worry about the construction anymore. You can design the rest of the space however you like!”","A soft expression spread across Hu Quan’s face when he heard what Lin Yuan said.","Hu Quan had put a lot of effort into building this paradise-like space.","Ever since he joined Lin Yuan, the latter had placed great trust in him and was always willing to provide him with opportunities.","Every spiritual ingredient used to construct the base in the Spirit Lock spatial zone would be cause for astonishment in the outside world!","There were numerous occasions during the construction process that he had wasted spiritual ingredients for the sake of the design. But Lin Yuan had been extremely understanding each time.","“Young Master, I have already come up with the design for many other places in this paradise. All I need to do is begin carving! I have also instructed the Land Imps to rebuild the foundation of the underground palace you moved into the paradise. It now sits in the location you specified!”","From this, Lin Yuan knew that Hu Quan had not rested much of late. Otherwise, progress couldn’t be this quick!","Not only had Hu Quan kept himself from resting, but he had overworked the other Spirit Craftsmen as well.","Although Hu Quan and the other Spirit Craftsmen had all contracted Vitality Sloths, they could not work constantly without a break or doing leisure activities!","“Uncle Hu, it will take more than a few days to complete the construction of this space. I’m not in a rush! Art comes from life. The best inspiration will only arise from the united efforts of the entire team!”","After speaking to Hu Quan, Lin Yuan accompanied Keira to the insect colony.","The interior of the nest was bare and resembled a thatched house that had never been renovated. There was a layer of the Soldier Ration Radishes on the ground from which Keira could pick and eat whenever she wanted.","Keira reported, “Master, the dead spirits are not a significant threat. Although new dead dimensional lifeforms continue to emerge, the special demon insects that were previously produced are able to handle these new dead dimensional lifeforms.","“I can now speed up the nurturing of the demon insect army! Additionally, I will be entering a period of slumber during which I will use the energy in my genes to produce more demon insects with shuttle abilities!”","Lin Yuan nodded in agreement with Keira’s plans.","Firstly, Keira needed to nurture the demon insects with shuttle abilities as quickly as possible to speed up removing death aura from the ley lines and return the main world to its original state!","Secondly, Keira could not be of much help in taking on the other six members of Tower Canon. The demon insects existed only to fend off the endless waves of dead spirits and dimensional lifeforms.","Lastly, Keira did not have to be left in an undisturbed state while she was slumbering and nurturing the demon insects with shuttle abilities. If she was truly needed, Lin Yuan could awaken her.","Although this would waste a significant amount of her energy, the energy could be replenished by pure spirit qi! In other words, it would only be a waste of some spirit qi.","The spirit pool in the Spirit Lock spatial zone released a large amount of pure spirit qi every second.","After getting Lin Yuan’s approval, Keira wrapped her arms around herself.","Soon, a special type of vitality began flowing out from her body and formed a convulsing cocoon around her.","At first, Lin Yuan intended to watch the demon insect species’ reproduction process.","But at that moment, a tuft of cloud gathered around Lin Yuan’s body, and he heard Gray’s voice say, “Yuan, I really want to comprehend Willpower Runes!”","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Gray.","[Fey Name]: Sky Clouded Crane","[Fey Species]: Crane species/Red Crane species","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Natural","[Fey Quality]: Legend","Abilities:","[Cloudy Weather]: The body will present itself as a cloud and will be compatible with any weather. The body can absorb the weather. Once the weather is absorbed into the cloud, it will become a new ability. No new abilities will come from evolution.","[Radiance of a Clear Day]: In an area covered by clouds or after changing the weather to that of clear skies, all the lifeforms in the area will be stamped with a clear weather imprint. Friendly lifeforms’ light-type abilities will be able to generate more damage, while enemies will sustain sunstroke, burning, and other negative effects.","[Darkness of a Cloudy Day]: In an area covered by clouds or after changing the weather to that of a cloudy day, all lifeforms in the area will be stamped with a cloudy weather imprint. Friendly lifeforms’ dark-type abilities will be able to generate more damage, while enemies will suffer confusion, fear, and other negative effects.","[Frozen Snowy Day]: In an area covered by clouds or after the weather has been changed to become snowy, all lifeforms will be branded with the snowy weather imprint. Friendly lifeforms will be able to produce more powerful ice-type attacks, and water-type abilities can also become ice-type. Enemies will be frozen, numbed, and experience other negative effects. Fire-type effects will also become less effective.","[Roar of a Windy Day]: In an area covered by clouds or after changing the weather to windy weather, all the lifeforms in the area will be stamped with a windy weather imprint. Friendly lifeforms’ wind-type abilities will be able to generate more damage, while enemies will experience reverse currents, wind pressure, and other negative effects.","[Judgment of Thunder Weather]: An area covered by clouds or has been transformed into cloudy weather will be branded with a thunder weather imprint. When the thunder hits friendly lifeforms, their ability to cause damage will be increased. When the thunder hits enemies, they will feel numbness and other related negative effects.","[Fusion of Rainbow Weather]: Cloudy weather will turn to rainbow weather. The rainbow weather can promote the fusion of other weather and allow them to coexist.","Exclusive Skill:","[Jade Contract]: Condense every type of weather absorbed into a jade. The jade will adorn the feathers. Once the weather turns into the jade decoration, the cloud will no longer carry the aura of that weather. But when the jade decoration is activated, every type of weather will turn into a jade beast."]},{"number":2720,"title":"Chapter 2720 Body of Weather!","paragraphs":["2720 Body of Weather!","Gray had remained in the Spirit Lock spatial zone and absorbed weather from the various plant-type feys that could produce weather.","Moreover, the nourishment from the pure spirit qi allowed Gray to build an exceptional foundation.","Lin Yuan had never felt anxious about evolving Gray’s quality and grade.","If Gray could naturally comprehend Willpower Runes and evolve to Fantasy Breed, it would be very close to Myth Breed.","Lin Yuan had been painstakingly nurturing the Floating Island Whale.","Lin Yuan saw Gray as being linked to Sky Sea. Gray was also a Heavenly Family Fey with an extremely fearsome bloodline.","Sky Sea was not of much help in taking on the dead spirits crisis caused by Tower Canon.","Gray could not be of much help, either. But it could not be denied that Sky Sea was stronger than Gray.","Due to the exclusive skill Sky Sea gained when it evolved to Suzerain/Myth, Sky Sea had become one of Lin Yuan’s most important foundational feys. Not even Genius’ strategic significance could compare to that of Sky Sea.","It seemed that Sky Sea and Gray would only be able to truly shine once they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","“Gray, the Spirit Lock spatial zone isn’t conducive for you to comprehend Willpower Runes. I will take you outside.”","Lin Yuan took Gray out of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","In the endless wilderness, the sand formed a seat behind Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan reclined in the chair and looked expectantly at the tuft of cloud that was Gray. He had accompanied Gray just like this when it transformed into a Heavenly Family Fey.","The weather was clear today, while that night had been snowing.","Many experts in the Royal Capital sensed Gray’s aura and wanted to investigate but were all blocked by the Mother of Bloodbath.","Lin Yuan could even kill the true Eight Pages of Tower Canon and was confident that he would be able to ensure Gray’s safety.","If there was truly an accident, the only possible culprit would be Epoch God Palace.","Lin Yuan was increasingly fearful of Epoch God Palace.","After his interaction with Fifth Page Falling Rainbow, he became aware of how strong Epoch God Palace was.","If they attacked him before he initiated contact with them, he would have no choice but to fight with his life on the line!","Gray used Cloudy Weather and turned its entire body into thin wisps of clouds that enveloped the area.","It did not take long for the willpowers that corresponded to the weather to respond to Gray.","While it was comprehending the Willpower Runes, Gray let out a symphonious cry in harmony with nature.","Seven to eight types of weather phenomena appeared in succession and formed a perfect cohesion that painted a captivating scene.","Gray was not satisfied with taking control of one of the willpowers. Rather, it continuously compressed and tempered the willpowers of all of the weather phenomena so it could absorb all of them.","As Gray’s power grew, it became increasingly greedy during its transformations. But it could not be denied that it would be intrinsically transformed if it succeeded! This would improve Gray’s original foundation!","Gray had been working hard, building up its foundation for this moment.","Gray was not naturally greedy. It used to be content and happy for an entire day by just having the opportunity to fill its belly.","When Lin Yuan discovered Gray, it had been in the worst state out of all of his feys.","Lin Yuan was the one who had brought out this greedy trait in Gray.","But in an environment where there was no lack of resources, feys could be greedy in their increase in power.","Gray could sense that Lin Yuan was quietly watching it.","It intended to give this its best shot for both its own sake and so it would not disappoint Lin Yuan.","Gray activated the bloodline in its body and used it as a medium to absorb all the willpowers associated with weather.","When Heavenly Family Feys activated their bloodlines, there was a high chance that their bloodlines would end up damaged.","Gray was being serious!","Pure spirit qi was beneficial to the evolution of any fey.","Lin Yuan raised his hand and summoned a chest of spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan manipulated the Overlord Sand and crushed the spirit qi crystals so that their highly pure spirit qi could nourish Gray and facilitate the activation of its bloodline.","To win or die trying. It was a fact that feys needed to accept the possibility of undergoing various risks when they evolved their grades and qualities.","As the willpowers in the weather battled each other, Gray would be extremely uncomfortable. However, there was little that Lin Yuan could do to help with this.","He would only step in to help once he was certain Gray could not comprehend the Willpower Runes and risked hurting its roots.","If Gray’s roots were damaged in the process of comprehending Willpower Runes, it would not be able to continue evolving anytime soon!","Luckily, Gray’s foundation was solid, and it was reasonable and would never do anything that overextended itself.","Gray managed to successfully condense its Willpower Rune. This Willpower Rune contained the radiant light of a clear day, darkness of a cloudy day, iciness of snow, roaring of wind, violence of lightning, and beauty of rainbows.","When these various natural phenomena fused together, the resultant Willpower Rune seemed to be able to represent nature itself.","At the instant that the Willpower Rune was produced, Gray’s grade was successfully evolved!","When Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Gray, he saw that Gray’s quality had changed from its original Legend to Fantasy I.","Gray had gained the exclusive skill called Body of Weather.","[Body of Weather]: The body will comprehend the construction of natural phenomena it controls and produce them accordingly. These natural phenomena can be used to aid other targets so they will receive double empowerment regardless of the weather they are experiencing.","Not only could Body of Weather replenish Gray, but it also had strong support effects that could influence a certain area.","Gray could produce weather at will in an area covered by its clouds.","Even if an environment lacked weather, Gray could use its own body to produce the weather and continue increasing its power.","Body of Weather could use natural phenomena to support itself and other targets and provide them with double the empowerment. It could be linked with and be effective in all the weather territories that Gray could produce.","Gray’s territorial abilities could affect a large number of targets.","Lin Yuan gave an order to the recently evolved Gray. He instructed it to use Body of Weather to support the plants in its surroundings.","Lin Yuan realized that Body of Weather could easily support a large number of targets. This would make Gray instrumental in large-scale battles.","Now that Gray had evolved, Lin Yuan did not remain on this grassland with Gray. Instead, he went to the boundary between the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent.","Before Falling Rainbow left, Lin Yuan told her that he wanted her to lure the other six members of Tower Canon to the Startling Lines Continent.","Lin Yuan would be able to minimize the damage to the main world to the greatest extent by battling with Tower Canon at that boundary.","Lin Yuan had set up special infrastructure all over the Startling Lines Continent. It could be said that the Startling Lines Continent’s defense was just as strong as that of the Radiance Federation. Since the infrastructure did not have to take the survival of the citizens into consideration, there were areas in the Startling Lines Continent that had stronger defenses than the Radiance Federation!","Tower Canon had their sights set on the Radiance Federation. Falling Rainbow had emphasized this when replying to Lin Yuan’s questions.","The Eight Pages of Tower Canon had already divided up the potential spoils from the Radiance Federation. They were fully confident that they would be able to take over the Radiance Federation.","The impression was that the Radiance Federation was leading the Startling Lines Continent!","When the other members of Tower Canon went to the Radiance Federation, they would immediately be lured to the Startling Lines Continent once sufficient commotion was caused in the Startling Lines Continent!","Lin Yuan would take the next few days to set up the Startling Lines Continent.","In order to create a large enough commotion to lure the other members of Tower Canon to the Startling Lines Continent from the Radiance Federation, the best plan would be to use Keira, the demon insect queen, as bait.","Falling Rainbow had yet to tell Lin Yuan about her plan.","Once Falling Rainbow told Lin Yuan about her plan, he could come up with preparations according to her plan.","With a mole that was also able to influence the decision-making, it would be much easier to carry out tasks!","Keira was in the midst of producing demon insects with special shuttle abilities. She needed to be in a slumber state now, and Lin Yuan would never send her out at such a time.","However, if the information came from Falling Rainbow, it was unlikely that the other members of Tower Canon would suspect her.","As Keira’s contractor, Lin Yuan could issue orders to all the demon insects while she was slumbering.","The Startling Lines Continent was the place where the demon insect species first started reproducing, so Lin Yuan instructed the demon insects to speed up their digging and search for the ley lines in the hopes of finding the exact locations of the ley lines.","Aside from Keira’s information, instructing the demon insects to absorb death aura from the Startling Lines Continent would also attract Tower Canon’s attention.","The stronger the insects from the Startling Lines Continent, the better he would be able to prove to the other members of Tower Canon that there was indeed a demon insect queen in the Startling Lines Continent.","...","As the millions of demon insects continued digging, all the ley lines in the Startling Lines Continent were uncovered.","There was a layer of special minerals on the ley lines near the Startling Lines Continent.","The minerals condensed into black crystals after being infected by death aura. The death aura in the black crystals was relatively pure, at least 85%.","The demon insects collected the crystals as they were very beneficial to the demon insects that were produced from death aura as the main form of energy.","Now that the demon insects were exposed, they were ready and waiting for Lin Yuan to give them an order. Once he issued his order, the demon insects would immediately begin absorbing death aura from the ley lines.","...","A day later, Lin Yuan finally received a message from Falling Rainbow through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Falling Rainbow]: The dead world’s roots are about to be fused with the main world. Once that happens, the dead world’s roots will consume and subsume the main world’s roots. This will not only increase the release of death aura but also replace the root energy of this world. I will do my best to hide the news of Eighth Page Eye Shadow’s death before taking the others to the Radiance Federation. If they intend on attacking the Radiance Federation, I will do what I can to restrain them!","Falling Rainbow’s idea was essentially useless to Lin Yuan.","This made him very displeased with her.","However, given the circumstances, it was true that it would be difficult for her to propose any suggestions.","Her point about doing her best to restrain them from attacking the Radiance Federation sounded promising, but there was nothing she could do if the rest of them had already made up their minds.","If Falling Rainbow made overly grand promises to Lin Yuan, he would be suspicious of her and wonder if she intended to selflessly sacrifice herself for the sake of the dead world she belonged to.","Morbius’ voice appeared in Lin Yuan’s mind. “Partner, are you really going to let Falling Rainbow go?”","Lin Yuan shook his head. He was only making use of Falling Rainbow to delay enemy forces.","Falling Rainbow absolutely had to die. Otherwise, Lin Yuan would not be able to answer to the lifeforms that died as a result of the dead spirits wave.","Even if he did not kill her, the other members of Tower Canon might do so once they learned of her betrayal.","[Lin Yuan]: What can you achieve by doing your best? Are you really going to be able to stop the members of Tower Canon from attacking the Radiance Federation? Don’t forget that you need to carry out your plan. Bring the other members of Tower Canon to the Startling Lines Continent as soon as possible! Otherwise, you will suffer the consequences!","Once Lin Yuan was done speaking, he put Falling Rainbow out of his mind.","Falling Rainbow’s life was in Lin Yuan’s hands, and she could not afford to cause trouble.","The imprint left by the Abyss Red Lotus on Falling Rainbow’s soul would not only burn her soul but also enable Lin Yuan to keep her on a leash. He could also use this method to ambush the other members of Tower Canon.","Once the imprint on Falling Rainbow’s soul was activated, her soul would become an incubator for the Hellfire Lotus Imprint. When Lin Yuan triggered her soul to explode, the Hellfire Lotus Imprint would be applied to the other members of Tower Canon.","One had to know that the Hellfire Lotus Imprints needed to absorb energy. Falling Rainbow’s soul energy was of a sufficiently high quality that the Hellfire Lotus Imprints applied to the other members of Tower Canon would definitely be able to affect them.","When Lin Yuan triggered the explosion of Falling Rainbow’s soul, he would only severely damage her soul. With her strength, it would not be enough to kill her.","Nonetheless, this would cause the other members of Tower Canon to realize her betrayal.","If they attacked and killed Falling Rainbow, it would have nothing to do with Lin Yuan!","All of Lin Yuan’s plans had gone extremely smoothly in the past. But this time, it would not go according to plan."]},{"number":2721,"title":"Chapter 2721 How High are the Chances of Victory?","paragraphs":["2721 How High are the Chances of Victory?","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow’s head was filled with thoughts about how she could save herself.","This feeling left Falling Rainbow feeling helpless.","Falling Rainbow was certain that she would not be able to envelop the imprint and temper it with her soul energy.","As a powerful lifeform that had lived for many years, Falling Rainbow was rarely at the mercy of others. She had only been restrained and needed to keep her head down when her power had been weak.","Falling Rainbow loathed Lin Yuan with her entire being and wanted nothing more than to destroy him.","But for the sake of her survival, Falling Rainbow had no choice but to be aware of her circumstances and meet Lin Yuan’s requests.","If she had two other members assuredly on her side like Eighth Page Eye Shadow did, it would be very easy to carry out this plan. But she was not like Eye Shadow. She received the worst treatment of all the members.","Moreover, Second Page Warbler Candle, who was on her side, often butted heads with First Page Crimson, Third Page Violet Light Green, and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid.","After some thinking, Falling Rainbow decided that the best way to achieve her goal would be to use the dead Eye Shadow.","Eye Shadow had always kept her Secret of the Dead on her person.","Eye Shadow’s Secret of the Dead had the ability to mask her aura.","Under the cover and protection of her Secret of the Dead, it was almost impossible for the other members of Tower Canon to detect her aura.","Falling Rainbow had always been wary of Eye Shadow because of her Secret of the Dead’s ability.","If she said that Eye Shadow was in the Startling Lines Continent and there were female demon insects there, it was likely that the other members of Tower Canon would ask to meet up with her.","Sixth Page Wave Glow and Seventh Page Concubine Winding would do so out of concern for Eye Shadow. They were on very good terms with her and would definitely be able to tell that this behavior did not fit with her personality.","However, neither of them would suspect Falling Rainbow or even consider the possibility that Eye Shadow was already dead.","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid, who currently possessed the largest pieces of the pie, would also agree to this arrangement. They would assume that Eye Shadow had yet to return because she had discovered astonishing benefits and was trying to keep them all to herself.","As for Warbler Candle, she would go along with this plan even if she had her suspicions. Falling Rainbow was confident of this.","Crimson’s opinion did not matter. His profits were his own. If the rest of the group had made the same choice, he would have no choice but to go along with them.","With this train of thought in place, Falling Rainbow’s tightly wound nerves relaxed slightly.","This feeling of being at the mercy of another was truly horrible!","Back then, the dead world that Falling Rainbow belonged to had been the weaker party.","After freeing themselves from the Class 3 world, they brought their dead world’s roots with them and earned their freedom.","Although they no longer had the status to roam the Sky Beyond the Clouds freely, their lives were still relatively comfortable. At least they led much better lives than they were doing now!","When she sensed that the dead world’s root energy fluctuations beneath her were stabilizing,","Falling Rainbow knew that the ritual to fuse the dead world’s roots with the main world was basically complete.","She had come back at the right time!","Falling Rainbow took a deep breath and composed herself to prevent the other members of Tower Canon from noticing that anything was amiss.","Once she entered the large hall, she saw that all the other black coffins aside from hers and Eye Shadow’s were all wide open.","Crimson and the other members of Tower Canon were currently recuperating in the black coffins.","Falling Rainbow instinctively looked at Eye Shadow’s black coffin. No one would sleep in there ever again!","Wave Glow and Concubine Winding opened their eyes simultaneously and looked at Falling Rainbow.","When they saw that she was alone, Wave Glow frowned and asked in a low voice, “Falling Rainbow, Eye Shadow left with you. Why have you returned alone? Where is Eye Shadow? The ritual is already over. I have made the suggestion to the other members to help to receive Eye Shadow’s roots together.”","Falling Rainbow looked at Wave Glow, and envy and mockery flashed across her eyes. She was very envious of how well Wave Glow and Concubine Winding looked after Eye Shadow. But at the same time, she felt derision toward Wave Glow’s lapdog-like behavior.","“Eye Shadow picked up the trail of female demon insects and headed to the Startling Lines Continent. She really is the kind to forget everything else when she has her eye on profits!","“The Startling Lines Continent is very near to the Radiance Federation. There is a high chance that Eye Shadow’s actions will alert the enemy and catch the attention of the main world’s natives. Eye Shadow and the two of you will have to answer for such a consequence!","“If my Tower of Falling Rainbow wasn’t lost and Eye Shadow hadn’t used her treasure’s power to hide her aura, I would have definitely dragged her back here!”","There was a furious and menacing expression on Falling Rainbow’s face, but her heart was only filled with bitterness.","Falling Rainbow had already guessed why she was unable to sense the Tower of Falling Rainbow and Secret of the Dead, Volume Five, Sinking Song. Lin Yuan must have already gained possession of them.","After all, Lin Yuan had easily claimed Eye Shadow’s Secret of the Dead.","Falling Rainbow’s words caused the other Eight Pages of Tower Canon to frown. However, they were all frowning for different reasons.","Wave Glow and Concubine Winding were suspicious of this story. The Eye Shadow that they knew would never act so unreasonably. If she had truly discovered the presence of female demon insects, she could have informed them of this instead of taking the risk of injuring her roots to head there herself.","This was unless Eye Shadow noticed something that was worth taking this risk and Falling Rainbow had yet to notice it.","If that were the case, the two of them would need to meet up with Eye Shadow as soon as possible.","It went without saying that Eye Shadow would swallow a large amount of resources after heading to the Startling Lines Continent. This would cut into Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid’s profits.","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid knew that Eye Shadow was very scheming and was not as innocuous as she appeared.","It was very possible that she would lose control of herself when profits were at stake!","Hence, Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid felt pressed to protect their own profits.","The Eight Pages of Tower Canon had not brought many resources with them when they landed in this world.","It was very challenging for this Class 1 world to promote to Class 2. Hence, the resources that did exist in this world were of the utmost importance to the Eight Pages of Tower Canon. The more resources they gained, the more things they could do with them and the faster they would be able to increase their power.","“We have completed the ritual. Although we have all depleted a significant amount of our roots and energy, we will be able to recover in just a few days.","“I suggest that we head to the Startling Lines Continent now. We will be able to meet up with Eye Shadow, capture the female demon insects, and destroy the Radiance Federation before divvying up the Radiance Federation’s resources. We will then begin taking over the rest of the resources in this world. After taking over the resources, we can rest and sleep for some time.","“I am sure all of you have sensed that the world wall where Epoch God Palace is located is active. There is a high chance that Epoch God Palace is trying to break through the wall to create a path from this world to the Sky Beyond the Clouds! They will probably leave this world then. This will also give us a way to return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.”","Violet Light Green’s Secret of the Dead had an ability related to boundaries. The world wall could be seen as a boundary formed from willpowers.","Violet Light Green had been in a very good mood these past two days because she had noticed this.","At first, she had not intended to tell the other Eight Pages about this discovery. But, given the circumstances, revealing this news would increase her importance to the group.","If Eye Shadow truly collected a large amount of resources, they would also be able to force her to spit them all out.","Out of the entire group, Warbler Candle was feeling the most troubled.","When she saw that Falling Rainbow had returned on her own, she knew that something had gone wrong with this operation. Otherwise, Eye Shadow would not have been able to slip away completely undetected by Falling Rainbow, even with her Secret of the Dead’s ability.","After waking up, Warbler Candle had intentionally tampered with the supply of energy to the black coffins. She had siphoned some of the energy from the other black coffins to Falling Rainbow. This was part of the reason why Eye Shadow had almost been unable to wake up.","The rest of the group thought that Falling Rainbow was in a weakened state, but Warbler Candle knew that this was false.","If they had truly discovered the female demon insects, Falling Rainbow should have been the one to get her hands on them first!","Even after thinking for a long while, Warbler Candle was unable to understand this.","Could it be that Falling Rainbow had killed Eye Shadow for the sake of profits?","Warbler Candle quickly shook her head. The probability of this was extremely small because Falling Rainbow needed to consider the consequences.","If Falling Rainbow really killed Eye Shadow, it would disrupt the superficial unity that Tower Canon had struggled to form.","Wave Glow and Concubine Winding would definitely confront and battle it out with Falling Rainbow.","Falling Rainbow hated inconvenience and risk.","After the clash against Epoch God Palace, Falling Rainbow had become even more averse toward risk.","After frowning for a moment, Crimson’s eyes turned red.","It was as though an aura was about to awaken within his body.","This aura was strangely beautiful, and it immediately caused his gaze to turn peculiar. Lethal aura was emanating from his gaze.","At that moment, Crimson heard Violet Light Green say, “Epoch God Palace seems to be staying in this Class 2 world because they are searching for an unusual lifeform. One of their rulers asked me and Cavity Orchid about it.","“I think that we should search for such entities while we’re splitting up the resources in this world. If we are able to present it to Epoch God Palace, we will have done them a favor! Even if this doesn’t turn our relationship into an amicable one, it will reduce some of the misunderstandings between us.”","Violet Light Green’s words were like a valve that had been turned and caused the strangely beautiful red hue to disappear from Crimson’s eyes.","The two fists hidden under Crimson’s robe were tightly clenched.","The other members of Tower Canon next to Crimson noticed the change in his aura. After they observed him for a few moments, Crimson finally said, “Since you are all in agreement, let’s head to the Startling Lines Continent! We’ll also search for any unusual lifeforms in this world!”","When it came to unusual beings, Crimson was an unusual being himself.","Since finding out about Epoch God Palace’s objective, he had been afraid that he was their target. As a result, he had tried his best to hide his exceptional traits to prevent himself from catching Epoch God Palace’s attention.","After all, based on what Violet Light Green had said, it was likely that Epoch God Palace would be leaving this Class 2 world. If there was anything he wanted to do, he could wait until they left!","It would be better for him to lay low now and play things safely!","However, this meant he would have to suffer and endure the company of these morons for some time.","Regardless of how the profits from this world were divided, this Class 2 world and dead world’s roots would all become his incubator!","Falling Rainbow was very surprised by Crimson’s decision. When did he start becoming so trusting?","Falling Rainbow was already prepared for Crimson to ask her a list of questions. She had even rehearsed her answers. However, she had not been able to use any of them.","After thinking for a long while, Falling Rainbow could not figure out what was wrong.","If Crimson had noticed something, he would not have allowed this operation to proceed.","Nonetheless, she had accomplished the task Lin Yuan had given her. Her life should be safe now that she had accomplished this task, right?","...","Lin Yuan had spent the last two days setting up the Startling Lines Continent. Thick Soil City had already been shifted onto Lift Marsh. It had taken the millions of people living in Thick Soil City far away from the Startling Lines Continent.","Before the battle between the main world and Tower Canon came to an end, Lift Marsh would continue floating around the sea in the vicinity of the Radiance Federation.","The experts and Dictators from the Vast Sea Labyrinth and the water world would protect Lift Marsh.","Meanwhile, the Land Imps started to rebuild the area where Thick Soil City used to be located. They built a transit station between the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent.","From now on, the Startling Lines Continent would become the Radiance Federation’s gate.","When Wen Yu and Liu Jie found out that Lin Yuan was in the Startling Lines Continent, they immediately rushed to him.","They already knew that he had clashed with Tower Canon.","“Young Master, the base in the Startling Lines Continent is complete. How high are our chances of victory in the upcoming battle against Tower Canon?”"]},{"number":2722,"title":"Chapter 2722 The Attacking Tower Canon!","paragraphs":["2722 The Attacking Tower Canon!","This question had come from Wen Yu.","She was not the type to be restless and impatient. These words did not fit with her personality.","Wen Yu had asked that because she was worried for the entire main world as well as Lin Yuan.","As someone whose skills lay in internal governance, all she could do now were managerial and organizational tasks. She could not help Lin Yuan in battle.","In this aspect, Wen Yu could not compete with Liu Jie.","All she wanted to do now was share Lin Yuan’s burdens. That was all.","After hearing that, Lin Yuan was silent for a moment before he said resolutely, “I have set the Startling Lines Continent as the location for the battle against Tower Canon. The Startling Lines Continent will be where the lives of the Pages of Tower Canon come to an end!","“Judging from the current situation, we stand a good chance of emerging victorious over Tower Canon! The only thing we need to worry about is the Pages fleeing during the battle. It will be difficult to get our hands on them once they’ve fled.”","While Lin Yuan was battling Fifth Page Falling Rainbow and Eighth Page Eye Shadow, he got a general understanding of the power of the true Eight Pages of Tower Canon.","Falling Rainbow had already told Lin Yuan that her power was considered average among the Eight Pages.","If Lin Yuan fused with the Abyss Red Lotus, he would be able to keep the other six Pages down. Moreover, he had other secret weapons he could tap into.","But once the Pages of Tower Canon decided to flee during their battle, they could use their comrades as cover in order to do so.","If the Pages fled, they would undoubtedly cause horrifying disasters throughout the main world. It would be child’s play for them to leave a string of devastated federations in their wake.","Even if they decided to go into hiding instead of causing a commotion, they would become a malignant tumor.","Unless Lin Yuan was able to reach a new level of his fused state with the Abyss Red Lotus, it would be very challenging for him to search for and capture the scattered Pages.","Lin Yuan was well aware that his increase in power depended on his fusion with the Abyss Red Lotus and was bolstered by the dimensional worlds and Continent Vein Cores that the Abyss Red Lotus controlled.","But now, there were no more dimensional worlds and Continent Vein Cores for Lin Yuan to take control of.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie relaxed when they heard that.","According to Lin Yuan, he would not be in great danger regardless of what happened.","Neither Wen Yu nor Liu Jie thought it was important whether the Pages escaped.","They had not even expected Lin Yuan to give such an answer, and they believed he would be able to subdue Tower Canon.","Liu Jie and Wen Yu looked at each other, and there was a hint of shame in their eyes. Both of them still did not understand Lin Yuan’s power well enough.","Lin Yuan did intend to go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds but would be entering a state of seclusion in the main world before he made the trip.","Both of them planned to go into seclusion with him so they could increase their power to the greatest extent. Otherwise, once they arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, they would be useless to Lin Yuan!","If the Pages truly escaped while battling Lin Yuan, the demon insects that were constantly reproducing could be sent out to search and capture them.","Lin Yuan would be able to receive information regardless of whether the demon insects discovered where the Pages were or if they killed the demon insects.","Even if he could not capture the Pages quickly, it would only be a matter of time!","Wen Yu and Liu Jie discussed Lin Yuan’s plan for taking on Tower Canon with him. He told them about the ambush he had set up.","Wen Yu said, “Young Master, since Falling Rainbow is now your tool, I think we should make good use of her!","“If the Pages truly escape during your battle, they will definitely regroup. You can let Falling Rainbow flee during your battle. She will think that you are letting her go and will become a secret weapon that you can activate after the Pages have fled!","“Aside from Falling Rainbow, there are only six other official Pages of Tower Canon. Due to their differing personalities, they will definitely make different decisions when battling you. Some of them will want to battle you, while others could decide to flee after witnessing your power!","“If Falling Rainbow flees first, it is highly likely she will leave with her allies with whom she shares profits. This will allow you to get a sense of the different camps among the Eight Pages! If Falling Rainbow flees, it will also keep the other Pages from suspecting her.”","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up when he heard what Wen Yu said.","She was right! If he could use Falling Rainbow once, he could use her twice!","Lin Yuan felt a substantial amount of pressure taking on the remaining six Pages of Tower Canon.","If it was possible, he did not want to reveal more of his secret weapons.","After all, Epoch God Palace had yet to appear.","During the clash between the main world’s lifeforms and Tower Canon, Epoch God Palace was observing from the shadows.","Lin Yuan was in no hurry to tell Falling Rainbow about this information. Instead, he told Wen Yu and Liu Jie seriously, “Wen Yu, Big Brother Liu, I have a very important task for you. You should be aware that the main world is in such a state because the ley lines have been infected by death aura.","“Fortunately, the infection can be reversed! As long as the demon insects can find the ley lines, they can absorb the death aura. Keira has been commandeering the demon insect species.","“However, the demon insects with Class 3 and below Genetic Locks are even less intelligent than three-year-old children and are unable to react appropriately to information. The two of you will head out to search for the Radiance Federation’s underground ley lines. When the battle against Tower Canon is complete, we will begin clearing out death aura, starting from the Radiance Federation.","“If things go well, we will be able to put an end to this dead spirits crisis in the next few centuries and enable the main world to return to its original clean state!”","According to Falling Rainbow, Tower Canon had already fused the dead world’s roots with the main world.","Once the death aura was all cleaned, the dead world’s roots would become fertilizer for the main world’s roots.","At that time, not only would the damage in the main world be recovered, but it might be able to receive unexpected blessings!","Liu Jie and Wen Yu wanted to remain by Lin Yuan’s side and accompany him. As his retainer and assistant, they both wanted to tackle obstacles with him.","However, the task that Lin Yuan gave them was just as important.","They were the only ones to whom Lin Yuan could assign this task.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie nodded as they said, “Young Master, leave this matter to us. We will definitely do our best to work with the demon insects to search for the location of the ley lines in the Radiance Federation!”","Wen Yu and Liu Jie had interacted with numerous dimensional lifeforms and knew that the Land Imps could not only sense mineral veins but were able to detect ley lines as well. If they brought the Land Imps with them to search for the ley lines, they would be able to save a significant amount of time!","When he saw that Wen Yu and Liu Jie’s expressions were not as austere as they had been, Lin Yuan said in a low voice, “Aside from Tower Canon, there is another group called Epoch God Palace. I don’t know much about Epoch God Palace. I don’t know if they are friends or foes. Before we learn what Epoch God Palace’s true intentions are, we need to be on our toes and stay on guard!”","Lin Yuan’s expression was very serious while he spoke.","He learned from Falling Rainbow that it was highly likely that he was Epoch God Palace’s target.","Lin Yuan had no way of verifying if what she had said was true because she also did not know much about Epoch God Palace.","Tower Canon and Epoch God Palace’s interactions were limited to the singular clash that had taken place more than 6,000 years ago.","Lin Yuan only learned the reason for Tower Canon going into hiding after Falling Rainbow’s explanation.","Given that they had forced Tower Canon to go into hiding, Epoch God Palace had, in a way, protected the main world. Otherwise, the main world would have been conquered by the Eight Pages of Tower Canon long ago!","If he was not Epoch God Palace’s target, Lin Yuan would feel no animosity toward them.","Nonetheless, once Lin Yuan eliminated Tower Canon, he would focus on searching for Epoch God Palace before initiating contact with them.","After Wen Yu and Liu Jie left, Lin Yuan went to the Startling Lines Continent.","He took out the Thoughts Letter Paper and told the Moon Empress about his situation.","Given that he had almost 100% confidence in defeating Tower Canon, Lin Yuan wanted to give the Moon Empress peace of mind.","Spring and Summer had been watching and protecting Lin Yuan from afar. When they heard what he said, they felt afraid and uncomfortable. At the same time, their resentment for Falling Rainbow deepened.","Ever since Epoch God Palace landed in this Class 1 world, they had been hiding in order to minimize their impact on it. They had ignored all the ups and downs that the main world had undergone.","If Tower Canon had not sought them out and disturbed them, thereby affecting Lord Saint’s awakening and triggering Epoch God Palace’s wrath, they would have only emerged from the mountain for the first time a few days ago.","It was true that Falling Rainbow was fearful of Spring. She was the one who had slapped Falling Rainbow and crushed half of her body.","What right did Falling Rainbow have to say that Epoch God Palace was targeting Lord Saint?","Even if Epoch God Palace was truly targeting Lord Saint, their meaning of target was different from how it was currently being interpreted!","It was all Autumn’s fault for blabbing in response to Third Page Violet Light Green and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid’s question. Autumn should be the one to explain all of this to Lord Saint!","Spring and Summer had been around the perimeter of this Class 2 world.","All the lifeforms in this world were blessed to have Lord Saint’s presence in it!","As this world continued to develop, its name would eventually resonate throughout the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","...","Seven figures raced across the surface of the sea.","Sixth Page Wave Glow and Seventh Page Concubine Winding both had grim expressions as they sensed their surroundings. Neither of them could pick up even a hint of Eye Shadow’s presence.","Although the rest of them could not sense Eye Shadow when she used her treasure’s ability to mask her aura, it seemed unlikely that she was making her aura constantly! She needed to deplete her energy to mask her aura!","Eye Shadow had yet to recover her roots. How could she sustain such a long period of depletion?","Falling Rainbow knew that Wave Glow and Concubine Winding were very suspicious of her. However, she did not intend to give them any sort of explanation.","After all, once they arrived at the Startling Lines Continent, her lie would be exposed, and the other Pages would see that she had betrayed them.","Giving them an explanation now would not affect the result. Falling Rainbow could not be bothered to waste the effort!","Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid were not worried about Eye Shadow’s safety. They did not care whether Eye Shadow died.","If she was truly dead, they would be able to claim a larger share of the resources from the main world. This would be extremely beneficial for them.","The two of them were very concerned that Eye Shadow had hidden some previous resources. This would prevent them from claiming their full share!","Regardless, once they found Eye Shadow, Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid would insist on inspecting her to ensure that she had not hidden precious resources.","Second Page Warbler Candle had remained by Falling Rainbow’s side.","When she saw Falling Rainbow’s frown deepening, Warbler Candle said, “I need Falling Rainbow to accompany me to retrieve something. We will meet up with the rest of you on the outskirts of the Startling Lines Continent, at the boundary of the marsh world and this world!","“Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid, the two of you can go first to investigate if you’re in a hurry. Regardless of what Eye Shadow has collected, we will support you in forcing her to spit it all out!”","Warbler Candle grabbed Falling Rainbow’s wrist.","Falling Rainbow sighed.","Warbler Candle knew her too well. She had to have noticed something off about her actions.","She needed to put more effort into thinking of how she should respond to Warbler Candle’s questions in order to appease her.","With her life currently in Lin Yuan’s hands, Falling Rainbow could not be bothered to consider Warbler Candle’s feelings!","After all, Warbler Candle would die eventually while she would be heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Violet Light Green, Cavity Orchid, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding did not try to restrain Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow.","Warbler Candle commonly called Falling Rainbow away when such things happened.","However, they were all working together now, and Warbler Candle’s action seemed rather divisive.","On the other hand, Warbler Candle’s action could be understood.","First Page Crimson looked up and down at Falling Rainbow and Warbler Candle before saying, “If you’re going to leave, hurry up and go! We will wait here for you to return. If you haven’t returned after a day has passed, we will assume you have given up your share of this Class 2 world’s resources!”","After speaking to Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow, Crimson turned and told Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid, “I know you are worried. Any additional resources that Eye Shadow has swallowed will belong to all of us. We won’t allow Eye Shadow to get away with anything! I’m sure Wave Glow and Concubine Winding will understand.”"]},{"number":2723,"title":"Chapter 2723 Evolving Silver Corona’s Bloodline!","paragraphs":["2723 Evolving Silver Corona’s Bloodline!","First Page Crimson stated his opinion and decision.","But this time, no one opposed him.","This was not because they were now willing to submit to him but because he had offered benefits that satisfied most of them without cutting into the profits of the minority.","As such, all of them were willing to offer him some courtesy. They could also use his words to maintain the peace.","Second Page Warbler Candle silently agreed to what Crimson said and pulled Fifth Page Falling Rainbow with her in the direction of the fortress.","Warbler Candle had questions for Falling Rainbow. She did not actually need to retrieve anything. Hence, the two of them did not need a full day’s worth of time.","Warbler Candle also did not try to pick up something she could use to keep up pretenses with the other Pages of Tower Canon.","Warbler Candle had yet to find the opportunity to speak privately to Falling Rainbow. The other Pages of Tower Canon could also guess Warbler Candle’s reason for leaving with Falling Rainbow.","Third Page Violet Light Green and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid looked at each other. Both of them felt that there was a high chance that the alliance between Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow would crack.","Warbler Candle was going to stop being a lapdog and stand on her own two feet!","After moving sufficiently far away from the other Pages of Tower Canon, Warbler Candle stopped, and her grip tightened around Falling Rainbow’s wrist.","“Falling Rainbow, we have known each other for millennia. You know full well how I feel about you. I hope you won’t lie to me! I am going to ask you now. Where has Eye Shadow gone?”","Falling Rainbow’s expression did not change when she heard what Warbler Candle said. However, her heart wavered.","It was true that Warbler Candle had taken good care of her all this time. She had stuck by her even when the other Pages of Tower Canon had ganged up on her!","As cold-hearted as she was, Falling Rainbow did have genuine feelings toward Warbler Candle. It could be said that Warbler Candle was the only member she cared for and hoped would survive.","But so what if she cared?","Lin Yuan’s goal was to use her to destroy all the Pages of Tower Canon.","If Lin Yuan refused to let Warbler Candle live, she would have no choice but to relinquish her life.","Falling Rainbow could not do anything about Warbler Candle’s death. There was no need for her to be overly concerned about someone who was already marked for death.","As such, Falling Rainbow said, “Warbler Candle, why are you asking me this? Do you think I’m lying to you? Do you think I killed Eye Shadow? I don’t have my dimensional treasure, but Eye Shadow has hers. If we really ended up fighting and she used her treasure against me, I would not have had much of an advantage!","“Don’t you have even this much trust in me after the millennia we’ve spent together? You know even better than me the kind of person Eye Shadow is. I suffered considerably on this trip with her! Once we find her, I will definitely make her pay!”","For her own sake, Falling Rainbow did not tell Warbler Candle the truth. She knew that once Warbler Candle found out the truth, she would abandon her immediately, regardless of how good of a relationship they had.","After all, she was about to trade the entire Tower Canon for her own life!","To put it simply, she had turned her back on Tower Canon and Warbler Candle.","Although Warbler Candle was suspicious of her, she would not lose trust in her. As long as she put on an act, she would be able to deceive Warbler Candle!","She needed to take Warbler Candle back with her as soon as possible to prevent any unexpected outcomes.","Presently, there was something that bothered Falling Rainbow.","It bothered her that Crimson had requested all of them to act together. It seemed as though he wanted to keep them all bound together.","This thought did not sit right with Falling Rainbow.","Warbler Candle stared at Falling Rainbow for a moment without saying anything. She eventually decided to place her trust in Falling Rainbow.","Aside from asking Falling Rainbow exactly what had happened, Warbler Candle had called Falling Rainbow out because she had something she wanted to say to her.","“Falling Rainbow, you interacted a fair amount with Crimson after awakening. Have you noticed that he seems different from before?”`","Falling Rainbow’s expression froze. She had noticed this some time ago. However, she had not told anyone else about this and brushed it aside as unnecessary worrying.","But when they were conducting the ritual, Falling Rainbow noticed that Crimson’s dead dimensional lifeform roots had changed. As a result, his power composition was no longer cohesive with the rest of them!","Crimson had to have noticed this as well. Otherwise, he would not have given her, Violet Light Green, and the rest the authority to oversee the ritual together with him!","In the past, Falling Rainbow would definitely have had a proper discussion with Warbler Candle after she brought up something like this.","But now, Falling Rainbow could not be bothered to think about such matters.","What happened to Crimson no longer had anything to do with her. It would soon become Lin Yuan’s problem.","Frankly, Falling Rainbow would prefer if Crimson killed Lin Yuan rather than Lin Yuan destroying Tower Canon.","Once Lin Yuan died, he would no longer be able to control her.","“It’s true that Crimson’s actions are deviating from my expectations. But after slumbering for 6,000 years, it is possible that he has changed in some way. Crimson’s bloodline has always had more potential than the rest of us. That’s why we elected as the First Page!","“Warbler Candle, don’t think too much about such things. If you really want to analyze this, wait until we’re done with this operation and have divided up the main world’s resources.","“Didn’t we all speculate that Crimson was keeping a secret weapon? If this is true, he will have to reveal it if we draw back slightly during the battle against the main world!”","After conversing with Falling Rainbow, Warbler Candle slowly let her guard down.","Without Epoch God Palace’s presence forcing Tower Canon to unite, Tower Canon would already be squabbling over the division of the profit pie that was the main world!","It was highly likely that these current teammates would end up being her enemies. It would not hurt to put a dent in their power now, so it would be easier to deal with them once they eventually became her enemies.","Warbler Candle discussed her ideas with Falling Rainbow.","Falling Rainbow sounded as though she was conversing with Warbler Candle, but her mind and heart were someplace else.","She had only made this analysis to placate Warbler Candle.","Once they arrived at the Startling Lines Continent, her longtime comrades would be reduced to ashes by crimson flames.","...","When Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow rejoined the group, Crimson ordered that they continue their journey.","The longer they sensed their surroundings, the more certain Sixth Page Wave Glow and Seventh Page Concubine Winding were that something was wrong. Even after all the time that had passed, they were still unable to catch even the faintest hint of Eighth Page Eye Shadow!","There was no way that this was normal.","Given Eye Shadow’s condition, she would never be able to sustain the utilization of her Secret of the Dead for this long. This was unless she was doing so at the cost of her roots.","Eye Shadow would only be willing to injure her roots if something was endangering her life.","Falling Rainbow had to be lying!","However, the two of them could not guess what Falling Rainbow’s motive could be.","Falling Rainbow had lost her dimensional treasure and was incapable of killing Eye Shadow. Hence, the two of them did not consider the possibility that Eye Shadow had been killed.","The more they thought about it, the messier their thoughts became.","All they wanted to do was rush to the Startling Lines Continent as soon as possible to meet up with Eye Shadow.","The two of them had voiced their opinions and made their requests to Crimson multiple times. However, he had turned them down every time.","This made Wave Glow and Concubine Winding increasingly upset with Crimson. They almost pulled out their weapons in a fit of fury!","Luckily, Warbler Candle and Falling Rainbow returned just in time.","Otherwise, Wave Glow and Concubine Winding might have attacked Crimson.","It was said that one never cared about things that were irrelevant to oneself. Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid acted no differently from when they were watching a show.","During the journey, Falling Rainbow received a message from Lin Yuan.","Falling Rainbow let out a sigh of relief when she saw that he had a new assignment for her.","She was terrified that Lin Yuan would order her to kill her comrades. It was not because she felt affection for them but because she was worried she would eventually be targeted by them in retaliation and suffer grievous injuries.","But now, Lin Yuan had instructed her to instigate the other members to flee with her.","Fleeing when things were looking bad would not only remove suspicion from her but also ensure her safety.","Falling Rainbow had already guessed that Lin Yuan was doing this because he wanted to separate the Pages of Tower Canon and divide and conquer them.","Falling Rainbow hoped that Crimson would not follow her when they fled.","If Crimson pulled out all the stops and used all his secret weapons against Lin Yuan, Falling Rainbow would benefit regardless of who emerged as the victor!","...","Lin Yuan did not make many more preparations in the Startling Lines Continent. Instead, he calmed himself and waited to receive Tower Canon.","The Radiance Federation and the rest of the main world were waiting to hear news of his victory.","Keira had awoken not long ago. She had nurtured the first batch of special shuttle demon insects.","Based on his experiments, each shuttle could cover a distance of around 5,000 kilometers.","Each trip required a certain amount of energy. The energy could be accumulated through the consumption of flesh and spirit qi.","After a day of shuttling, any corner of the main world could be reached.","Every shuttle trip would be able to carry around 20,000,000 demon insects. This was not a large number. But as long as there were a few female insects with high-class Genetic Locks, the insect army would be able to reproduce and grow.","After Keira woke up, Lin Yuan sent her back to sleep so she could produce more special demon insects with shuttle abilities.","Keira would not be able to offer much help in the subsequent battle against Tower Canon.","Lin Yuan could also control the demon insects and order them as he pleased.","Every female insect that Keira produced was extremely respectful toward Lin Yuan.","Recently, among all the feys that Lin Yuan had contracted, the biggest beneficiary was Silver Corona, who was stationed at the bottom of the sea, clearing out the corpses of the dead spirits.","If there were any corpses of dead dimensional lifeforms that were difficult to handle, the Vast Sea experts and the water Dictators would toss the corpses into the sea of bone lotus flowers. The corpses would then become fertilizer for the bone lotus flowers.","Silver Corona had finally reached Diamond X/Fantasy V.","It had slowed down its grade and quality evolution rate because it had been focusing on tempering its bloodline.","It also intended to evolve its bloodline from six wings to eight wings like Red Thorn had done.","Red Thorn had always been a large source of pressure for Silver Corona.","Because of Red Thorn’s possessiveness over Lin Yuan, Silver Corona had to back off whenever Red Thorn appeared.","Silver Corona felt the same affection for Lin Yuan.","Although Silver Corona and Red Thorn appeared to get along well, Silver Corona did not like Red Thorn’s possessiveness.","When Red Thorn had still been a six-winged fairy, Silver Corona had sensed Red Thorn’s pressure. Now that Red Thorn had evolved into an eight-winged fairy, Silver Corona had no choice but to avoid Red Thorn.","This motivated Silver Corona to evolve its bloodline at the same time that it evolved to Myth Breed.","If the dead spirits crisis had not arrived, Silver Corona would have never been able to evolve its bloodline to such a degree, regardless of how much time passed!","But now that the dead spirits crisis was here, all the dead spirits in the main world were resources that fuelled Silver Corona. It was using these resources to trigger the evolution of its fairy bloodline.","Initially, Lin Yuan wanted Silver Corona to evolve its grade and quality as quickly as possible. But after understanding Silver Corona’s conviction, he decided to support its ambition.","Besides, evolving its fairy bloodline would also aid in Silver Corona’s subsequent increase in power.","Currently, Silver Corona’s sea of bone lotus flowers was already larger than the Startling Lines Continent.","Silver Corona reached out to Lin Yuan and requested that he help it with its breakthrough.","According to the information from Falling Rainbow, Tower Canon was still at least a day away from reaching the Startling Lines Continent.","This was enough time for Silver Corona to evolve.","The commotion caused by Silver Corona would also raise Tower Canon’s expectations.","With these thoughts in mind, Lin Yuan agreed to help with its evolution.","Lin Yuan traveled through a few nodes using Node Transportation and arrived at the edge of the sea.","He deftly leaped into the sea.","Due to his merman thearch bloodline, Lin Yuan was much more mobile underwater than on land.","He intended on accompanying Silver Corona during its transformation!"]},{"number":2724,"title":"Chapter 2724 Lotus Territory Fairy Shadow!","paragraphs":["2724 Lotus Territory Fairy Shadow!","Lin Yuan was a spirit qi professional, but he vastly differed from the traditional spirit qi professional.","Regular spirit qi professionals could only contract three to five feys at the very most. They also had the time to watch all their feys grow. They interacted with their feys on almost a daily basis.","Although Lin Yuan was a spirit qi professional, he had contracted at least ten feys.","Furthermore, he had his own tasks to occupy his time, and it was inevitable that he would neglect his feys at times.","Nonetheless, Lin Yuan was always there with his feys when they were evolving.","Silver Corona was very shy and an overthinker.","Lin Yuan was certain that Silver Corona wanted him to be there during its transformation.","This evolution to Myth Breed would be the most important step in Silver Corona’s life! Once it evolved into an eight-winged fairy, Silver Corona’s future would be limitless!","The water current clustered around Lin Yuan as though he was a magnificent thearch. Lin Yuan could sense the control he wielded over the sea.","Because of the demon insects nurtured by Keira to be suitable for clearing out death aura and dead spirit corpses from the sea, the sea was much cleaner than before. The lifeforms from the sea clans could return to swimming freely like they used to.","As Lin Yuan looked around at the lifeforms from the sea clans, he realized that almost all of them were contributing faith power to him. This meant that the sea clans had developed faith in him after he rescued them.","Many of these lifeforms had low intelligence and were unable to volunteer the contribution of their faith power.","This indicated that the Vast Sea Labyrinth had fulfilled their promise to him.","The fountain of faith in Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom was full and showed signs of transformation.","Lin Yuan could also sense that his divine kingdom was on the cusp of a change.","The mist surrounding the divine kingdom had become thinner, and the silhouettes of new sights could be seen past the mist.","It did not take long for Lin Yuan to reach Silver Corona.","The seemingly endless sea of bone lotus flowers dancing in the water had a cold beauty about it.","The sea of bone lotus flowers did not have any life of their own. But once they sensed Lin Yuan’s arrival, they all began stretching out towards him.","Silver Corona appeared next to Lin Yuan and flapped its three pairs of wings.","Unlike their usual interactions, Lin Yuan did not touch Silver Corona or hold it in his hand.","He could sense the exquisite power in Silver Corona’s body.","If this power strengthened any further, Silver Corona’s body would crumple under the burden.","At that moment, Silver Corona was in extreme agony.","Silver Corona silently fixed its resolute eyes on Lin Yuan. At the same time, it smiled with elation over his arrival.","Silver Corona activated the energy in its body, and the energy that it unleashed stimulated its surroundings.","A terrifying black vortex appeared on the surface of the sea. There were silver flashes in the black vortex, and it was very different from the World Cleansings of other Fantasy Breed feys.","Silver Corona was a water-type carcinoma fey and only became a fairy after the Fairy’s Heart transformed it. It could be said that Silver Corona was a lifeform that never should have appeared in this world.","When a lifeform like this evolved, the willpower of nature would do its best to eliminate such a lifeform.","The World Cleansings from a Class 2 world were stronger than that of a Class 1 world.","However, despite the increased strength, World Cleansings were no big deal to Lin Yuan.","He released the Abyss Great Emperor, which stood on the surface of the sea and was ready to block the World Cleansing’s attacks on Silver Corona’s behalf.","Without interference from the World Cleansing, Silver Corona could concentrate on using its weak fairy body to complete its bloodline transformation.","...","After around five to six hours passed, Lin Yuan noticed that all the energy in Silver Corona’s body had been tempered.","The sea clans had been constantly tossing the corpses of the dead dimensional lifeforms into the sea of bone lotus flowers. Yet, it was insufficient for Silver Corona.","Lin Yuan took out spirit qi crystals and water-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","He had no lack of elemental pearls as they were produced in an endless stream.","However, he was almost running out of spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan did not have the time now to help the spirit qi professionals to evolve their feys’ grades and qualities. But once he had settled Tower Canon, he would be able to obtain spirit qi crystals in one gargantuan net.","After Silver Corona received the pure spirit qi and water-elemental energy from Lin Yuan, the aura in its body began showing more signs of transformation.","Lin Yuan did not mind expending more resources for the sake of Silver Corona’s evolution!","...","After almost 12 hours passed, Lin Yuan sensed that Silver Corona’s aura had changed.","Presently, Silver Corona’s aura was on the same level as that of Red Thorn.","But if they were compared in detail, Silver Corona was still slightly weaker than Red Thorn.","Silver Corona’s bloodline had transformed.","Based on the communication he received from Silver Corona, the World Cleansing was complete.","The Abyss Great Emperor had perfectly defended against the World Cleansing, and the World Grace would soon land on Silver Corona’s body.","The instant the World Grace landed on Silver Corona’s body, Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Silver Corona.","[Fey Name]: Sea Burial Lotus Flower (Silver Corona)","[Fey Species]: Water Willow/Water Bone Lotus","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Fairy","[Fey Quality]: Myth I","Abilities:","[Spotted Coral]: When trained according to the spots on the coral jade, different effects are generated.","1. Nurture Spot Style: Nurture the spots that were absorbed from the spotted coral jade in the Bone Lotus Flowers. The Bone Lotus Flowers will use a living being’s life and soul to nurture the spots and give them vitality. The spots with vitality can use the living being’s original strength to increase the strength and stamina of the Bone Lotus Flowers.","2. Burial Spot Style: Place the spots in between the Bone Lotus Flowers. The spots will eat the Bone Lotus Flowers and become bone insects. The bone insects will retain the spot’s abilities and can deal with attacks on the Bone Lotus Flowers according to the abilities. The external lifeforce will be absorbed, and when the external lifeforce is still weak, their soul can also be absorbed.","[Bone Powder Mist]: The Bone Lotus Flowers will vomit out the living being’s bones that could not be digested. The bone powder will fly up into the sky and stay in the coral spots once it reaches a set thickness of layer.","[Blood Bone Insect Drunk]: While the bone insects are eating, they will enter a drunken state. When they’re in a drunken state, they will not feel any pain. The circulation of their root power will also slow down.","[Blooming Lotus]: The Bone Lotus Flowers’ structure will change and split into main lotuses and branch lotuses. The branch lotuses will strengthen combat power, while the main lotuses will lose all combat power. Every time the main lotuses bloom, the spots will use the vitality they absorbed to produce a skeletal insect. The skeletal insect can consume them to repair the damage done to the body.","[Arrival of Grant of Death]: When the hermit’s dead servants cannot stand up against the enemies, they will change into the grants of deaths that place death penalties on the targets’ souls.","[Soul Parasite Rebirth]: The soul will be hosted in the main lotus. The main lotus will make a copy of the aura of the lifeform’s soul and vitality. When the target’s body and soul are damaged, the main lotus can be sacrificed while absorbing vitality and soul power to enable the target to be reborn. Once reborn, the target will be in a very weak state, and its soul and roots will also be diminished.","[Lotus Territory Fairy Shadow]: The fairy bloodline in its body will be used to nurture lotus fairies in the sea of Bone Lotus Flowers. When the lotus fairies attack targets, there is a chance that the target will die instantly. The lifeforms killed by the lotus fairies will be turned into lotus puppets, and they will retain a portion of the targets’ abilities from when they were alive.","Exclusive Skill:","[Hermit’s Dead Servant]: The Bone Lotus Flower will absorb the target’s body when attacking it. 1% of the target’s power will be injected into the target’s soul to cause the target to be pregnant with its dead soul. The dead soul will consume itself, and when the Bone Lotus Flowers gain 36 hermit dead servants, every hermit dead servant will be able to create a layer of mist over the Bone Lotus Flowers.","[Rotted Bones into Fireflies]: Both vitality and death aura will be absorbed simultaneously. The vitality will turn into fireflies that will mend the sea of Bone Lotus Flowers. The death aura will increase the strength of every Bone Lotus Flower. If there is a pile of rotting bones below the Bone Lotus Flowers to supply nutrients to them, as long as the main lotus is alive, rotting lotuses will be produced from the rotting bones, and energy will be saved!","[Lotus Territory Symbiosis]: All of the lifeforms in the territory will be classified as one entity, and their lives will be linked together. When individual targets are attacked, the lotus territory will take on some of the damage. Before the lotus territory is destroyed, the individual targets will continue to live.","Silver Corona had indeed become a Suzerain I/Myth I eight-winged fairy and became part of the new history of the fairy bloodline.","However, because Red Thorn had evolved before Silver Corona, the creator of this new history was Red Thorn and not Silver Corona.","Lin Yuan had already carefully analyzed the Diamond Silver Corona’s abilities. It could be described as well-rounded.","Soul Parasite Rebirth was a functional-type ability with revival effects.","The Suzerain ability, Lotus Territory Fairy Shadow, allowed Silver Corona to use its bloodline to produce lotus fairies that could cause instantaneous death, and it could be linked with Hermit’s Dead Servant.","The probability of instant death was very low, but it was the most powerful of the special effects and rarely manifested in feys.","Silver Corona could produce more than one lotus fairy with its fairy bloodline. All it needed was time to recharge its bloodline, and it would be able to produce a large number of lotus fairies.","Silver Corona could order the sea of flowers to transform the lifeforms killed by lotus fairies into lotus puppets. The lotus puppets would be able to retain some of the abilities from when they were alive.","This would also enable Lin Yuan to pick out targets with special abilities from the invaders of the sea of flowers and turn them into lotus puppets as a means of obtaining their abilities!","This would allow him to manually expand Silver Corona’s sea of flowers’ abilities, thereby removing all limits to Silver Corona’s breakthroughs!","The Myth Breed exclusive skill, Lotus Territory Symbiosis, was a defensive ability. Objectively, there were pros and cons.","Lotus Territory Symbiosis would link all the lifeforms in a territory and allow them to share damage.","But when a few individual targets were suffering damage, all the lifeforms would be affected as long as the strength of the damage was enough to destroy the lotus territory!","However, as Silver Corona’s power and grade continued to improve, the strength of the sea of bone lotus flowers would also increase, and there would be more and more lotus puppets. It would be a challenge for a target to destroy the entire sea of flowers by targeting individual entities, then!","If there was a lifeform that possessed such an ability, this expert would easily be able to destroy the entire sea of flowers even if Lotus Territory Symbiosis and its negative effects did not exist!","When objective factors were excluded, Silver Corona’s Lotus Territory Symbiosis was a benefit.","Silver Corona opened its eyes while Lin Yuan was browsing through its data.","Previously, Silver Corona had seven-colored eyes. But now, its eyes were as white as the sea of flowers. However, its pupils were still seven-colored. This not only allowed Silver Corona to retain its charm but also made them more hypnotic than before.","The horns on Silver Corona’s head that were in the shape of a crown had morphed into the shape of a lotus. A part of it also curved downward and formed seven-colored bone lotuses on Silver Corona’s back.","White lotus petals enveloped Silver Corona’s body and eventually formed a white lotus dress that draped over its body.","After evolving, Silver Corona’s attire became exceptionally beautiful. Its back had four pairs of translucent wings adorned with seven-colored patterns. These patterns gave the illusion of four pairs of seven-colored eyes when viewed from behind.","Silver Corona excitedly examined its body and sensed its transformed bloodline.","Now that it was an eight-winged fairy, it did not have to back off when Red Thorn was around Lin Yuan!","Silver Corona used to get along well with Red Thorn. It only stopped contacting Red Thorn after the latter evolved into an eight-winged fairy. After all, the dominance of the fairy bloodline intrinsically dictated that only fairies of the same bloodline level could become friends.","From now on, Silver Corona could continue being friends with Red Thorn!","Lin Yuan left Silver Corona at the bottom of the sea so it could continue absorbing death aura and consuming the corpses of dead dimensional lifeforms.","Lin Yuan returned to the Startling Lines Continent to await Tower Canon.","At that moment, Keira’s voice appeared in Lin Yuan’s head, “Master, it will be easy for you to use death aura to nurture this fairy. All you need to do is situate this fairy’s sea of flowers on the ley lines, and a few special demon insects will push out death aura from the ley lines. All the death aura can go toward nurturing this fairy!”"]},{"number":2725,"title":"Chapter 2725 Facing Tower Canon Head On!","paragraphs":["2725 Facing Tower Canon Head On!","“If this fairy absorbs all the death aura from this Class 2 world, its bloodline will be able to reach ten wings at the very least! In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, ten-winged fairies are also considered to be elites!”","Delight spread across Lin Yuan’s face.","He never expected the demon insects produced by Keira to be able to manipulate death aura.","If that were the case, the death aura harming the main world could be channeled toward defending the main world.","This main world was where the roots of Lin Yuan’s current life lay. If the main world was in danger, he would definitely do all he could to protect it.","Silver Corona was not the only fairy Lin Yuan had that could absorb death aura. Red Thorn could also consume death aura and use it to strengthen its own energy.","There was an immense amount of death aura in the ley lines. It would not be difficult to evolve an eight-winged fairy to a ten-winged one.","However, it would be tough to evolve it into a twelve-winged fairy! He might still fall short even after using all the death aura in the ley lines.","Hence, Lin Yuan could attempt to use the death aura to evolve Silver Corona and Red Thorn to ten wings instead.","Lin Yuan treated all his contracted feys equally and did not show favoritism towards any of them.","But in truth, Red Thorn’s abilities trumped Silver Corona’s.","Ever since Red Thorn gained the Tongue of Relinquish, its place in Lin Yuan’s arsenal became irreplaceable.","The entity that enabled Red Thorn to produce the Tongue of Relinquish was a dead dimensional lifeform from the dead world.","The same dead dimensional lifeform had yet to appear again.","Lin Yuan intended to search for it once he defeated Tower Canon. He wanted to try using it to enable Red Thorn’s Tongue of Relinquish to evolve again!","Although Lin Yuan did not know what secrets the hidden Epoch God Palace had up their sleeve, he would not stop moving just because there was a powerful enemy in the shadows. He still had to make preparations for the future.","Previously, Lin Yuan was very displeased by Keira’s arrogance and focus on increasing her own power. But ever since he expressed his displeasure to her, she had been doing her best to make amends. Keira now invested her entire being into carrying out Lin Yuan’s orders.","“Keira, all you need to do now is produce the shuttle demon insects as quickly as possible. It will take at least 20 shuttle demon insects to transport the other demon insects and clear the death aura from the main world.","“In the past, you lacked resources. But now, I am here to supply you with resources. Do not waste my investment!","“When we get to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, there will be many species like the demon insects who need spirit qi. Your performance in this task will determine if I will continue nurturing you, as well as my subsequent opinion of you. You should know what to do!”","It sounded as though Lin Yuan was threatening Keira. But this was how he genuinely felt.","Lin Yuan would only spend his resources nurturing subordinates who could be of help to him.","Once he arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would have plenty of choices of species to channel his resources into!","Even if Lin Yuan did not make this explicit to Keira, she was fully aware of this.","“Master, don’t worry. All you need to do is give me two weeks, and I’ll be able to produce at least 25 shuttle demon insects! Each of the 25 shuttle demon insects will be able to transport at least 200,000,000 demon insects and temper death aura rapidly.","“When clearing an environment of death aura and funneling death aura out of the ley lines, the demon insects can also discreetly clear out the lifeforms from this world who have been infected by death aura and are now releasing death aura of their own!","“Master, are you aware that Class 3 worlds will be classified based on the different attributes of their roots?","“Let’s take this Class 2 world as an example. It will develop into a world composed of spirit qi, vitality, and elemental energy. When a world like this consumes the dead world’s roots, it only needs to consume the world root power. The dead root power that proliferates death aura will need to be eliminated! Otherwise, the death aura will clash with the vitality!","“I suggest that you pick a dead dimensional lifeform with potential and nurture it with the dead root power. After being nourished by the dead root power, the dead dimensional lifeform will be able to mobilize the power of a Class 3 dimensional world. After that, it won’t be long before you gain a powerful soldier!","“Many factions in the Sky Beyond the Clouds use this method of utilizing a dimensional world’s root power to create servants.”","Being a demon insect from the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Keira possessed a lot more information than Lin Yuan.","Her worlds opened new horizons for him and gave him a general understanding of the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","It turned out that there were distinctions between a world’s roots.","Based on Keira’s behavior, Lin Yuan could be certain that pure spirit qi was also a very precious resource in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The dead world was a Class 3 dimensional world, but it did not contain spirit qi.","It was unlikely that there were many worlds in the Sky Beyond the Clouds that contained spirit qi.","It went without saying that he did not have verification for these conjectures. These were nothing more than his guesses.","With Keira under his control, Lin Yuan could ask her anything he was unsure of.","“Keira, give me more details about the distinctions in world energy. I am very interested in this!”","Keira was stunned when she heard what Lin Yuan said. She did not understand why he was asking her for such basic knowledge.","Lin Yuan possessed far too many resources. Keira would never expect him to be a native of this world because his resources excelled past the level of a Class 1 world that had only recently been promoted to Class 2.","Keira saw Lin Yuan’s question as a type of test.","“Master, if your world evolves into a Class 3 world, its Class 3 world energy system will be considered Level 1. There are very few worlds with such energy systems, and real experts usually protect them. These worlds will usually supply resources to these true experts!","“Class 3 worlds will automatically be linked to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, so you should come up with a way to protect this world before it is promoted to Class 3. Otherwise, this Class 3 world will definitely be targeted, and someone will try to rob it from you!","“Level 1 worlds are given this classification because they contain spirit qi. The higher the concentration of spirit qi, the higher the ranking of this Level 1 energy system!","“Level 2 worlds do not have spirit qi, but their lifeforms must be able to supply a large amount of faith power. The world must also be supported by another special type of energy like elemental energy, vitality, or death aura. Most worlds have Level 2 energy systems.","“Level 3 energy systems come from desolate worlds that have lost their energy roots after being plundered and wrecked. Whenever the various universes discover worlds like this, they are turned into dueling grounds. Large factions that need a place to fight to the death to resolve grudges hold their battles there.”","Lin Yuan now had a simple understanding of the classifications of world energy.","He now knew that he needed to accumulate sufficient power to protect the main world before he promoted it to Class 3!","During his conversation with Keira, Lin Yuan noticed that his fountain of faith was rapidly filling up with faith power. The glowing dots that nourished the faith power started fluttering within the shrine.","Lin Yuan realized that there were an uncountable number of lifeforms in the main world that were currently praying. They were praying that he could defeat Tower Canon and restore peace back to the main world.","These lifeforms consisted of humans, feys, and the sea clans.","At that moment, Lin Yuan felt an unprecedented assurance.","There were times when being a protector was a blessing!","...","Fifth Page Falling Rainbow intentionally sent Lin Yuan a message two hours before Tower Canon arrived at the Startling Lines Continent so he could make advance preparations.","Rather than Tower Canon defeating Lin Yuan, Falling Rainbow hoped that Lin Yuan would be able to finish off Tower Canon.","Before Tower Canon defeated Lin Yuan, he would definitely detonate the imprint on her soul and end her life along with his.","But if Lin Yuan defeated Tower Canon, she would stand a chance of survival!","During the journey, Sixth Page Wave Glow and Seventh Page Concubine Winding never stopped asking her about Eighth Page Eye Shadow and requested she confirm the direction that Eye Shadow had left in.","Eventually, Third Page Violet Light Green and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid also began looking at her suspiciously.","Falling Rainbow believed that if she did not have Second Page Warbler Candle on her side, Wave Glow and Concubine Winding would have pulled her away to question her together.","Yet, Falling Rainbow did not feel pressured by all this. She was waiting for the moment that Tower Canon clashed with Lin Yuan.","After all, according to Lin Yuan’s task, all she needed to do was flee with someone.","If she fled, Warbler Candle would definitely leave with her. Once she brought one person with her, she would have accomplished Lin Yuan’s task, and he would have no reason to blame her.","When First Page Crimson sensed the aura from across the sea, he exclaimed, “There is an eight-winged fairy in this Class 2 world! It looks like this Class 2 world has a fair number of secrets! I am curious to find out where this Class 2 world is getting its resources from. How did it manage to produce an eight-winged fairy after producing a fairy!”","Crimson’s words piqued the interest of the other Pages.","The more resources this world had, the happier they would be.","This eight-winged fairy would eventually belong to one of them.","A fairy bloodline that could reach eight wings had to be outstanding. They would benefit immensely regardless of whether they nurtured this fairy themselves or sold it when they returned to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Falling Rainbow did not look excited. Rather, traces of fear and scorn appeared on her face. She knew why the aura of an eight-winged fairy had appeared across the sea. This eight-winged fairy had to belong to Lin Yuan.","It was likely that Lin Yuan was also the reason behind an eight-winged fairy appearing in this Class 1 world before it was promoted to Class 2.","Lin Yuan currently saw Tower Canon as his prey. Yet, these morons next to her were all coveting the eight-winged fairy!","Warbler Candle had been observing Falling Rainbow’s expression. When she noticed the derision and fear, she became certain that something was wrong with the Startling Lines Continent!","Moreover, Falling Rainbow was aware of this problem. Otherwise, she would not be this afraid!","It seemed that Falling Rainbow had not been honest with her!","At that moment, Warbler Candle felt her heart grow cold.","However, she did not call out to Crimson to stop because she badly wanted to know what Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow were up to!","Warbler Candle would never have imagined that Eye Shadow was already dead.","...","Lin Yuan stood in the Startling Lines Continent. This time, he did not hide in the shadows and set up an ambush for Tower Canon. Instead, he intended to take on Tower Canon directly!","Eye Shadow’s body had become more durable after the Red Lotus Hellfire tempered it. Meanwhile, Red Thorn had already used the Tongue of Relinquish to take control of Eye Shadow’s body.","However, Eye Shadow’s body was too strong, and it took time to take full control of it. Otherwise, Eye Shadow’s tempered body would be Lin Yuan’s biggest weapon in this battle against Tower Canon.","By now, Lin Yuan could already sense seven powerful auras charging in his direction. One of these auras belonged to Falling Rainbow, who was under his control.","Lin Yuan had already released his aura and was the only human in the Startling Lines Continent alongside the demon insects.","As he stood on the Abyss Great Emperor’s palm, he was the most eye-catching symbol in the entire Startling Lines Continent.","As he looked at the seven figures, Lin Yuan was finally witnessing the full force of the Pages of Tower Canon.","Wave Glow and Concubine Winding released their own pressure and used it to cover the entire Startling Lines Continent. They were not trying to exhibit their might but were trying to get a response from Eye Shadow.","Although Eye Shadow was retracting her aura, she would never remain hidden after sensing their auras!","Wave Glow and Concubine Winding were unbothered by Lin Yuan and the Abyss Great Emperor. An abyss demon that had only just evolved to the Afterlife Realm was no threat to them. As for the human, he was no different from a clown to them!","The natives of this world were overestimating themselves. Instead of hiding like the demon insects, they were trying to take on Tower Canon directly!","If not for the fact that they could not sense Eye Shadow, Wave Glow and Concubine Winding would begin toying with Lin Yuan first to pass the time.","Crimson was the first to awaken and had looked into the situation in the human world.","As the expressionless Crimson looked at Lin Yuan, he said in an androgynous voice, “You must be the one who enabled this Class 1 world to promote to Class 2! Your actions have helped Tower Canon. However, you shouldn’t be helping us because it will only lead to your death!”"]},{"number":2726,"title":"Chapter 2726 Fighting With Tower Canon!","paragraphs":["2726 Fighting With Tower Canon!","Lin Yuan looked at First Page Crimson, and his gaze swept across the other Pages of Tower Canon.","Lin Yuan hated Tower Canon because they wanted to destroy the world he had been born into.","Unlike Tower Canon, he did not need to communicate with them. But since Crimson had expressed his stance, Lin Yuan needed to do the same on behalf of all the lifeforms in the main world.","“Tower Canon represents the dead dimensional spirits. If the lifeforms oppose Tower Canon, won’t you be surrounded by enemies when you go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds? The world promotion is the result of the main world’s lifeforms’ hard work. How is it related to Tower Canon?”","Crimson’s expression did not change, but Fourth Page Cavity Orchid said mockingly, “At the end of the day, the result of your hard work will be collected by Tower Canon!","“It looks like you have some power. Why don’t you join us? Once we take over the main world, we can make you the leader of an area that will supply us with the main world’s resources.","“But in order for you to join us, you need to change your life state. The smell of the living is too difficult to stand.”","Lin Yuan’s calm expression turned cold.","Based on what this tall member of Tower Canon said, Lin Yuan found out about Tower Canon’s plans for the main world. They intended to take over the main world and harvest its resources.","Given how much the Pages detested the aura of the living, it was likely that Tower Canon would turn all of the lifeforms into dead spirits, transforming the main world into an area of the dead.","This member of Tower Canon’s words fit with what Fifth Page Falling Rainbow had said.","Cavity Orchid smirked mockingly when he saw Lin Yuan’s cold expression. He was no different than an ant in his eyes. What right did an ant have to express his displeasure?","Dark purple death aura condensed in Cavity Orchid’s left hand, and it turned into a serpentine and rough bone spear. There were millions of small gray insects crawling around on the bone spear.","Cavity Orchid flew over to Lin Yuan with his spear brandished.","Cavity Orchid’s attitude toward Lin Yuan was like that of a child who had found a fun toy. He did not intend to kill Lin Yuan immediately. He only wanted Lin Yuan to understand his might so he could admire Lin Yuan’s look of despair.","The black cavity insects on the bone spear would pierce Lin Yuan’s bones and suck out his marrow while the insects bore into his bones.","Cavity Orchid believed that the pain would definitely be enough for him to hear this human plead for mercy.","The other Pages did not try to stop him.","Crimson and the others knew of Cavity Orchid’s personality.","Cavity Orchid looked like a gentleman but was a violent cad from the inside out.","When Tower Canon began dividing the Radiance Federation’s resources, it was likely that Cavity Orchid would kill most of the lifeforms in the Radiance Federation as he ‘played’ with them.","Falling Rainbow stared at Cavity Orchid’s back.","Cavity Orchid did not try defending himself as he drew near to Lin Yuan. It would not be long before Lin Yuan dealt him a lethal blow.","Although Falling Rainbow had not experienced being pierced by the black roots, she had witnessed the black root piercing through Eighth Page Eye Shadow’s body.","Each time the black roots made contact with the body, a seal would be applied to the body. As the seals stacked up, one would lose the ability to draw energy from the environment. Moreover, one’s own body would also be locked away.","The others were a little far from Lin Yuan, and he could not reach them as easily.","With this thought, Falling Rainbow shouted, “Cavity Orchid, I have my eye on this human! An Afterlife Realm abyss demon isn’t a common sight in this Class 2 world! Why should I hand him over to you?","“Wave Glow, Concubine Winding, I can confirm that Eye Shadow is in the Startling Lines Continent! It’s likely that she has hidden her aura because of this human. This human has to be somewhat capable. Otherwise, he would not dare to face us directly.”","Once Falling Rainbow was done speaking, she flew toward Lin Yuan and looked as though she intended to fight for him.","Second Page Warbler Candle usually worked together with Falling Rainbow. But this time, she did not react to Falling Rainbow’s actions.","Given Warbler Candle’s understanding of Falling Rainbow, she would never be interested in an abyss demon.","When they were in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Falling Rainbow hated living creatures more than the rest of them did. Any lifeform that entered her territory would earn her ire.","Now, she claimed to be interested in a human and abyss demon. What a joke!","Although Warbler Candle did not respond to Falling Rainbow, Third Page Violet Light Green, who was allies with Cavity Orchid, flew toward Falling Rainbow intending to stop her.","Sixth Page Wave Glowe Glow and Seventh Page Concubine Winding were only concerned about Eye Shadow’s safety.","When Wave Glow and Concubine Winding thought about how Eye Shadow’s unusual behavior could be related to this human, they immediately moved toward him so they could question him.","Lin Yuan was very happy with Falling Rainbow’s adaptability to the situation.","Falling Rainbow had pushed four Pages to move toward him. This created a prime opportunity for him to strike. Moreover, none of these four Pages had their guard up.","Just as Cavity Orchid’s bone spear was about to make contact with him, Lin Yuan reached out his hands and fused with the Abyss Red Lotus.","Soon, black roots sprouted from his palms and shot toward Cavity Orchid.","Numerous black vines also emerged from his feet and wrapped around Violet Light Green, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding.","Lin Yuan did not bother with Falling Rainbow. She was already under his control and was of no threat to him.","Lin Yuan needed to do his best when tackling these four members of Tower Canon.","Now that he had reached this step, Falling Rainbow’s presence did not have much more value, and Lin Yuan could not be bothered to continue putting on an act with her.","At the instant that he fused with the Abyss Red Lotus, the terrifying aura exploded from within him and suppressed the Pages.","Cavity Orchid’s bone spear slammed into Abyss Red Lotus’ roots, which then wrapped around the bone spear. At the same time, the gray cavity insects rapidly crawled onto the roots.","The roots that emerged from the ground formed a cage in the sky.","Unless these Pages fled immediately, it would be difficult for them to escape the cage formed by the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots later!","The members of Tower Canon were shocked by Lin Yuan’s sudden display of power.","Not even Crimson had anticipated a human to exhibit such overwhelming power!","It was as though the entire world’s wills had been applied to this human.","When Cavity Orchid’s bone spear made contact with the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots, he felt an immense power travel through the spear and slam into his body. This caused him to be hit by a wave of numbness.","At that moment, the bone spear was completely enveloped by the black roots.","Yet, Cavity Orchid did not panic. Instead, he smiled menacingly. His true secret weapon was the cavity insects on the bone spear.","The gray cavity insects could consume virtually anything and had already begun chomping on the black roots.","Cavity Orchid was certain that his cavity insects would be able to eat away at the black roots.","Before Cavity Orchid had the time to issue orders to the crawling cavity insects, crimson flames ignited all over the black roots.","Lin Yuan had used the Abyss Red Lotus’ exclusive skill, Red Lotus Hellfire.","The gray cavity insects stood no chance against the Red Lotus Hellfire, and it did not take long before they were burned to ashes.","The Red Lotus Hellfire traveled up through the bone spear. In a very short span of time, Cavity Orchid felt the might of the Red Lotus Hellfire.","This ability could burn the target’s karma, bloodline, and energy. Furthermore, Hellfire Lotus Imprints were being added to Cavity Orchid’s body.","With his plethora of combat experience, Cavity Orchid intended to abandon his bone spear and move further from Lin Yuan. He would then work with the others to fight back against Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan’s abilities were far too unorthodox, and Cavity Orchid could clearly sense that his bloodline was being locked away.","Lin Yuan did not have the time to tangle with Cavity Orchid.","Aside from Cavity Orchid, Lin Yuan was going to keep at least another two members of Tower Canon.","Lin Yuan used Cleansing Aura Lotus Flames.","The intense flames formed a lotus coffin around Cavity Orchid. In almost no time, Cavity Orchid was cocooned.","The lotus coffin formed by Cleansing Aura Lotus Flames was a jail formed by the power of the cleansing flames. Space and everything else that was considered an existence would be preserved in its original state.","Lin Yuan needed to take control of Cavity Orchid first, as it would make it easier for him to handle the others.","This opportunity was rare. After a moment of hesitation, Lin Yuan used the Abyss Red Lotus’ Myth Breed exclusive skill, Everything to Ashes, to use the fire-elemental energy purified by the Element Well to replenish himself.","The purer the fire-elemental energy used in Everything to Ashes, the more of the target’s energy would be burned.","Lin Yuan used the purest possible fire-elemental energy to replenish the Abyss Red Lotus.","Its flames could now burn anything and everything. All Lin Yuan needed to do was continuously supply it with pure fire-elemental energy. Otherwise, the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots would be severely injured, and it might even become unable to use Lotus Nirvana.","Lin Yuan only targeted Cavity Orchid with Everything to Ashes.","Although there were more than ten mouths of spirit springs that sped up the production of water in the Element Well, Lin Yuan did not want to waste the Element Well’s water.","Reality was not a game, and the Eight Pages of Tower Canon were not the final boss.","Each drop of the Element Well’s water that he wasted represented the loss of precious foundational resources.","Aside from Tower Canon, Epoch God Palace was still hiding in the shadows, and this was a big source of headache for Lin Yuan.","When Falling Rainbow saw that Lin Yuan had not aimed any attacks toward her, she became alarmed.","Violet Light Green, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding could not tell from the situation that something was wrong.","But Warbler Candle and Crimson, who were standing further in the distance, could see the situation clearly.","Falling Rainbow gnashed her teeth and slammed her body into one of the roots burning with the Red Lotus Hellfire. The Red Lotus Hellfire spread to Falling Rainbow’s body, and she looked to be in a very sorry state.","Since Lin Yuan was not going to put on an act with her, she would have to put more effort into her performance. At the very least, she could deceive those around her.","As displeased as Wave Glow was with Falling Rainbow, she still intended to use her own death aura energy to extinguish the Red Lotus Hellfire on Falling Rainbow’s body.","Grayish-purple death energy ignited all over Concubine Winding’s body.","The death energy moved toward Lin Yuan like a mystical mist.","Lin Yuan scoffed and took a step forward with his left foot.","A flame lotus bloomed at his feet.","The flame lotus had a diameter of three meters, and the overlapping petals perfectly enveloped Lin Yuan.","The brilliant crimson flames burned the mist of death energy.","Lin Yuan squeezed his right hand forcefully, and the black roots in the sky locked together tightly. Violet Light Green, Concubine Winding, and Wave Glow now had no way to flee.","Falling Rainbow turned to glance at Warbler Candle and Crimson.","Warbler Candle’s eyes were full of shock and disappointment, while Falling Rainbow was unable to discern the meaning behind Crimson’s gaze. It was clear that both of them had noticed that something was off about her.","Since she could not deceive them, Falling Rainbow intended to earn Lin Yuan’s favor.","Falling Rainbow screamed, “I might have lost my secret of the dead, but my death energy still has safeguarding effects. I can help you to endure the flames by burning my roots. Hurry up and kill this human! I won’t be able to fend off the flames for too long!”","At this juncture, no one would turn down the offer from someone who was willing to deplete their own roots to protect them.","There were already Hellfire Lotus Imprints on Violet Light Green, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding’s bodies.","The one who took up the responsibility of defending them would have to endure the application of many lotus imprints. The special energy that formed the lotus imprints might not disappear after this human was killed, so the three of them surrounded Falling Rainbow in a triangular formation.","Lin Yuan knew that this was Falling Rainbow’s way of sending him a signal.","During his battle against Tower Canon, Lin Yuan realized that they had very special abilities. Moreover, they could complement each other, unlike Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow, who schemed against each other when he ambushed them.","If this persisted, it would be difficult for Lin Yuan to capture them even if he did manage to attain victory by using his secret weapons.","Lin Yuan intended to make good use of this opportunity that Falling Rainbow had created.","The black roots spiraled down from the sky and sailed toward Falling Rainbow.","All of this happened in the blink of an eye.","Warbler Candle yelled, “Disperse quickly!”","Violet Light Green, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding’s attention did not shift to Warbler Candle after her shriek. Instead, the three of them continued to stockpile power to launch a lethal attack against Lin Yuan!"]},{"number":2727,"title":"Chapter 2727 Mutated First Page Crimson!","paragraphs":["2727 Mutated First Page Crimson!","One could not be distracted in a battle of this caliber. Any distraction would result in irreparable consequences.","Warbler Candle reassessed Falling Rainbow’s strange behavior.","Falling Rainbow only began acting strangely after her trip with Eye Shadow.","Falling Rainbow had said that Eye Shadow had gone to the Startling Lines Continent. It was clear that she had lied to lure all of them here.","It was likely that Falling Rainbow was being forced against her will by this human. Warbler Candle did not know what method this human was using to keep her under his thumb. Otherwise, Falling Rainbow would have never decided to betray Tower Canon.","This was because Falling Rainbow represented Tower Canon’s profits and was a beneficiary of their vested interests.","The instant Lin Yuan displayed his power, WWarbler Candle guessed that Shadow was already dead.","She had done so much for Falling Rainbow, yet the latter had betrayed her.","She had sought out Falling Rainbow during their journey. Falling Rainbow had not been honest with her, even in a private conversation with only the two of them. This meant that Falling Rainbow wanted to work together with this human to kill her.","After this became clear to her, Warbler Candle made a painful decision. Warbler Candle turned and told Crimson, “Crimson, judging from the current situation, we must join the battle. Otherwise, Violet Light Green and the rest will be in serious danger!”","Once Warbler Candle was done speaking, she intended to strike.","She thought that Crimson would step in to stabilize the situation.","It was true that Crimson was the strongest out of the eight of them. Moreover, his Secret of the Dead was very skilled at fending off elemental energy.","However, Warbler Candle did not expect Crimson to not only not take action but also stop her.","“Warbler Candle, don’t be impulsive. You should be aware that Falling Rainbow has betrayed us. After this storm settles, I will personally kill this traitor. I hope you won’t stop me then!","“As for Violet Light Green, Cavity Orchid, Wave Glow, and Winding Concubine, two of them are blinded by profits while the other two are led by their emotions. They must learn a lesson from this fight!”","When Warbler Candle heard what Crimson said, sheWarbler Candle felt her heart being overcome by a chill. She instinctively looked away from Crimson.","When she looked back at him, she found his gaze to be foreign. It was as though this was the first time she was seeing him.","As Tower Canon’s leader in name, Crimson’s actions did not align with Tower Canon’s profits. They also did not fit with his usual style of actions.","This human had already demonstrated his power. The black roots could wrap around Fourth Page Cavity Orchid’s arm and even leave cracks in the bone. This meant that the black roots would also be able to ruin the bodies of Violet Light Green and the rest.","The crimson flames could burn the insects on Cavity Orchid’s body to ashes.","Violet Light Green, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding were now being attacked by the sky-covering roots because Falling Rainbow conned them. They were not going to end up in any better of a state than Cavity Orchid.","Yet, CCrimson was calling all this a lesson!","Could Crimson be planning on sleeping for another 6,000 years after their four comrades battled against this human?","CCrimson had to have a reason behind this decision.","Regardless of what the specific reason was, it was fundamentally no different from that of Falling Rainbow.","If a difference had to be found, it would be that Falling Rainbow had no choice because she was under duress. On the other hand, Crimson was doing this only for himself.","With this thought, Warbler Candle suddenly realized why Crimson had calmly shared his profits with Violet Light Green and Cavity Orchid. He must have already intended on getting rid of a few members of Tower Canon.","Perhaps Crimson never had any plans to evolve this Class 2 world to Class 3 and return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","When Warbler Candle pulled Crimson away, she saw him glance at her with amusement. But he did not do anything else.","Warbler Candle did not understand where Crimson’s confidence was coming from. Why did he believe that he could defeat this human?","This human had to have secret weapons prepared in order to have the courage to take on Tower Canon.","This was the first time that the humans were initiating an attack on Tower Canon!","Although Warbler Candle had some substantial conflicts with the other Pages, she did not want these companions with whom she had spent thousands of years to die.","With this thought, Warbler Candle sacrificed her Secret of the Dead, and a candle burning with a black flame appeared in her hand before beginning to attack the roots.","Since Falling Rainbow wanted to cause trouble, she would protect Wave Glow, Concubine Winding, and Violet Light Green on Falling Rainbow’s behalf. At the very least, she would be able to take on this attack.","Wave Glow, Concubine Winding, and Violet Light Green were accumulating energy in preparation to launch a lethal attack at this human. The three of them were unable to defend themselves while they were stocking up on energy.","Lin Yuan sensed the might of the attack from these three Pages, but his expression did not change in the slightest.","Lin Yuan now had two options.","His first option was to enter the Spirit Lock spatial zone and dodge the attack with this method.","However, there was a drawback to this method, which was that he would not be able to address the current situation after dodging the attack. Tower Canon could end up escaping.","If that happened, Lin Yuan would only be able to capture Cavity Orchid, who was sealed in the lotus coffin.","That meant his plan would have failed!","If the other five Pages, aside from Falling Rainbow, fled, it would be difficult for Lin Yuan to search for and capture them.","Hence, Lin Yuan was not going to hide in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. He was going to face the attacks from these three members of Tower Canon.","Another Page had joined the battle. Lin Yuan felt that he needed to use Burning Lotus Cleansing Dance to magnify the effects of Hellfire Application. He also instructed the Abyss Red Lotus to protect this world’s root energy.","In an instant, Lin Yuan’s aura amplified and reached a new level.","At that moment, Crimson’s expression changed. He began looking at Lin Yuan with fear as he put up his guard. His eyes started to flash with red light.","Falling Rainbow did not anticipate Lin Yuan to have more power to exhibit.","Based on the power that Lin Yuan was currently demonstrating, Violet Light Green, Cavity Orchid, Concubine Winding, Wave Glow, and Warbler Candle would definitely die at Lin Yuan’s hands.","She could use this opportunity to leave a good impression on Lin Yuan.","Falling Rainbow’s body flashed, and she pressed her palm forcefully on the back of Violet Light Green, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding’s heads to vibrate their soul fires.","As a dead dimensional lifeform, Falling Rainbow knew where her companions’ weaknesses were.","Falling Rainbow’s attacks caused the three of them to stop stockpiling energy.","The three of them shot out their attacks of less-than-full energy, and their souls entered a dizzy and sluggish state.","This dizzy and sluggish state would not last for too long, but it would still prevent the three of them from fending off Lin Yuan’s attacks.","After doing that, Falling Rainbow gnashed her teeth and tapped into the last vestiges of her roots before moving toward Warbler Candle to stop her from saving the three of them.","Warbler Candle’s attacks were being directed at the black roots in the sky.","If she ambushed Warbler Candle, she would definitely be able to cause serious injury to Warbler Candle’s roots.","This would help Lin Yuan to capture Warbler Candle as well.","Lin Yuan would definitely remember her actions.","If Warbler Candle was allowed to save Violet Light Green, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding, it would not be easy for Lin Yuan to handle the four of them.","Lin Yuan would be in danger if the three of them worked together to attack him.","In the meantime, three lotus coffins appeared in front of Lin Yuan.","The three lotus coffins moved toward Violet Light Green, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding’s attacks, sealing the attacks within the lotus coffins.","At that moment, Lin Yuan used Blackie’s Spirit Qi Imprint, which he had not used in some time.","In an instant, half of the sea of spirit qi had been used up.","The spirit qi maintained the lotus coffins’ cleansing of the three attacks.","Lin Yuan had not used Spirit Qi Imprint in almost a year. Blackie had also been storing up spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Falling Rainbow’s actions went beyond Lin Yuan’s expectations.","Not only did she create an advantageous situation for him, but she also injured three members of Tower Canon. She had even been willing to attack Candle.","It could be said that if Lin Yuan truly managed to kill these four Pages, half of the credit would go to Falling Rainbow.","Warbler Candle watched FFalling Rainbow’s attack heading toward her and screamed, “Falling Rainbow, you’ve gone mad! Regardless of what this human has on you, you still have the chance to turn back now!”","Falling Rainbow looked at Warbler Candle with a complicated gaze. A bitter, apologetic smile appeared on her face.","If there was any other way, Falling Rainbow would not have wanted to attack Warbler Candle. However, she did not have any other choice.","Lin Yuan had placed an imprint on her soul that could explode with the crimson flames and burn her soul to nothing. Once she stepped out of line, Lin Yuan would not hesitate to end her life. There was no turning back for her now!","When Falling Rainbow’s attack hit Warbler Candle and dissolved her Warbler Candle protection over Violet Light Green and the rest, Falling Rainbow did not continue fighting Warbler Candle. Instead, she took a large step backward for fear of causing Lin Yuan to misunderstand. She was nothing to him!","If she was within the attacking vicinity of the black roots, Lin Yuan might take the opportunity to kill her.","Falling Rainbow did not trust Lin Yuan, but she did not resist. The only option she had was to trust Lin Yuan.","The crimson flames shackled Violet Light Green, Wave Glow, and Concubine Winding, and their bodies began burning.","Layers of Hellfire Lotus Imprints appeared on the three of their bodies.","Once the three of them regained clarity, they immediately started to flail with agony.","The three of them used their root power and managed to break three of the roots with brute force.","Lin Yuan sighed softly. It seemed that he had applied too few Hellfire Lotus Imprints on the three of them!","If he had applied more Hellfire Lotus Imprints and used the Hellfire Lotus Imprints to lock their bloodlines and energy, they would not have been able to break free from the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots!","Nonetheless, it would be very difficult for the three of them to escape the cage of roots created by the Abyss Red Lotus.","At the beginning of this fight, Lin Yuan had used the Abyss Red Lotus’ Splendor of Fire to fill the environment with fire-elemental energy. The fire-elemental energy had eliminated all other types of energy and cut off other lifeforms’ abilities to use fire-elemental energy.","Now, aside from fire-elemental energy, all that was left was a small amount of death aura.","The members of Tower Canon were releasing the death aura so it could not be dispersed.","But as the layers of Hellfire Lotus Imprints increased, it would become increasingly difficult for them to control the death aura in the environment.","As Lin Yuan sensed the Abyss Red Lotus’ condition, he knew that he could not drag this on for much longer.","This was because the Abyss Red Lotus’ Burning Lotus Cleansing Dance was continuously burning the Abyss Red Lotus’ body for nutrients. If this was prolonged, the Abyss Red Lotus’ roots would be injured.","Unless it was absolutely necessary, Lin Yuan did not want the Abyss Red Lotus to reincarnate.","Lin Yuan had yet to use the Abyss Red Lotus’ Platinum ability, Lotus Law World. It would use the world controlled by the Abyss Red Lotus as the core to issue orders to all the lifeforms in that world. Those who did not listen would be stripped of their ability to continue drawing energy from the world.","According to what Falling Rainbow had said, Tower Canon had fused the dead world’s roots with the main world. The dead world’s roots were now a part of the main world’s root energy. They would use this method to infect and take over the main world’s root energy!","Hence, Lin Yuan, who controlled the five dimensional worlds and main world’s energy cores, could issue orders to the Pages of Tower Canon, who were not part of the main world. He could then use Lotus Law World to take away the Pages’ ability to draw energy from the main world.","The instant Lin Yuan used Lotus Law World, Crimson sensed the change. As a result, Crimson’s eyes immediately turned red.","Crimson stopped suppressing the strange and evil energy in his body and allowed the strong blood energy to flow out.","Falling Rainbow looked in the direction of Violet Light Green, Concubine WindingFalling Rainbow, and Warbler Candle.","When they sensed the bizarre aura coming from Crimson’s body, all of them prepared to react.","At that moment, they heard a mesmerizing chuckle coming from his throat.","Soon, bright red tentacles emerged from his companions’ throats. When the tentacles emerged, the Pages’ faces began to show signs of aging."]},{"number":2728,"title":"Chapter 2728 Crimson’s True Bloodline!","paragraphs":["2728 Crimson’s True Bloodline!","Third Page Violet Light Green, Fifth Page Falling Rainbow, Second Page Warbler Candle, and the rest let out five grunts.","They had remained silent when the Red Lotus Hellfire burned them. But now, it seemed that the bright red tentacles had touched their limit of restraint.","Dead dimensional lifeforms were different from lifeforms in that dead dimensional lifeforms used death aura to temper their souls and manipulate their bodies.","Their bodies would only show signs of aging if their souls were unable to move their bodies, causing death aura to leak out from their bodies.","It looked as though the tentacles were emerging from their bodies, but the tentacles were not absorbing the energy in their bodies but the energy in their dead souls.","After the bright red tentacles appeared, they wrapped around the bodies of the Pages of Tower Canon.","It was as though the tentacles had a life of their own as they dragged Warbler Candle, Violet Light Green, Falling Rainbow, and the rest over to Falling Rainbow.","The blood mist emanating from Crimson’s body had the same roots as the bright red tentacles.","At that moment, Warbler Candle, Violet Light Green, Falling Rainbow, and the rest knew that they had fallen for Crimson’s scheme.","Falling Rainbow felt unbelievably wretched.","She had betrayed Tower Canon to save her life which was under Lin Yuan’s control.","But in actuality, without her realizing, her life had already fallen into Crimson’s hands.","It turned out that Crimson only ever saw them as tools.","Apparently, they had woken up after 6,000 years because Crimson was frightened by Epoch God Palace and felt pressed to hide himself.","Crimson was exposing himself now because Lin Yuan’s display of power had forced him into a corner.","If he did not attack them, he would be attacked by Lin Yuan.","Warbler Candle was feeling just as troubled as Falling Rainbow.","She had been furiously devastated over Falling Rainbow’s betrayal. Yet, unbeknownst to her, Crimson had already been plotting against her for some an unimaginable amount of time.","She had not picked up on the tentacles’ presence at all before they started absorbing the death aura from her soul.","Warbler Candle yelled, “Crimson, what is the meaning of this? We have been together for thousands of years and built Tower Canon together. Are you going to take our lives?”","Soon, Violet Light Green, Sixth Page Wave Glow, and Seventh Page Concubine Winding’s angry cries echoed that of Warbler Candle.","Falling Rainbow had already lost all hope.","If Lin Yuan ignited the imprint on her soul, he could help her to tackle the tentacles.","Yet, he did not do so.","This meant that he had no intention of letting her go free.","There was no reason for Crimson to be bothered by the screams and questions of his previous companions. Instead, he looked at Warbler Candle and the rest mockingly.","Soon, the blood mist that had emerged from Crimson’s body completely swallowed Warbler Candle, Falling Rainbow, Violet Light Green, and the rest.","When Crimson acted, Lin Yuan suddenly sensed Eye Shadow and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid’s bodies changing.","It was as though something had come alive in Eye Shadow’s body. However, she had lost her soul, and the Red Lotus Hellfire had fully tempered it.","Moreover, there were many layers of Hellfire Lotus Imprints on her body. Hence, whatever had come alive did not manage to exit her body and remained stuck even after struggling intensely for some time.","Lin Yuan sensed a strange bloodline power from the entity within Eye Shadow’s body.","The bloodline power had a very similar level to the mermaid bloodline, meaning that it belonged to a powerful species.","This bloodline also had a powerful persistence.","Lin Yuan hurriedly summoned Eye Shadow and re-placed the Red Lotus Hellfire in her body before adding more layers of the Hellfire Lotus Imprints to strengthen his seal on Eye Shadow’s body.","Cavity Orchid, who was stuck inside the lotus coffin, was reacting much more violently.","The bright red tentacles had protruded from his body and restrained him. The Red Lotus Hellfire was already burning his soul and it was eventually destroyed as the struggle continued.","Normally, once a dead dimensional lifeform’s soul was destroyed, it would no longer be able to move.","But at that moment, a bright red tentacle took hold of Cavity Orchid’s body and began using bloodline energy to sustain movement in Cavity Orchid’s limbs. Cavity Orchid’s body started to flail violently.","Luckily, the Hellfire Lotus Imprint could also seal away bloodlines.","As the layers of Hellfire Lotus Imprints sealed away this bloodline power, Cavity Orchid’s body could not break out of the lotus coffin.","When Lin Yuan saw this, he gained an understanding of the strength of the bright red tentacles.","As long as there were enough Hellfire Lotus Imprints, they would be able to lock the bloodline power. This meant that the Abyss Red Lotus’ bloodline was on the same level of Crimson’s bloodline.","This gave Lin Yuan confidence.","Lin Yuan poured a bottle of fire-elemental energy that had been purified in the Element Well on the Abyss Red Lotus’ flower core.","The Abyss Red Lotus activated Everything to Ashes and used it to burn the bright red tentacle manipulating Cavity Orchid’s body.","Lin Yuan would eventually have to burn up this bright red tentacle!","He thought, 800 ml of fluid fire-elemental energy that has been purified in the Element Well should be enough to remove the bloodline power in Cavity Orchid’s body.","This bloodline power was of a relatively high level, and Lin Yuan could not assuredly allow Red Thorn to come into contact with it.","Control and cooperation were interlinked. Red Thorn used its own bloodline to cooperate with and control the bodies of other lifeforms. Once this bloodline’s controlling abilities were stronger than that of Red Thorn, the latter might end up as the one being controlled instead.","Once the Hellfire Lotus Imprint was placed on a target, it was very difficult to remove. The only way to remove it was to use energy to dissolve the seal.","Given that the Abyss Red Lotus’ bloodline was more elite than that of Crimson, it would be extremely difficult for Crimson to remove the lotus imprint!","Lin Yuan who was controlling the lotus imprint could sense that Crimson was absorbing the energy of the other members of Tower Canon.","Due to the bright red tentacles, Crimson was able to directly fuse with the flesh of the other members of Tower Canon, and he began rapidly absorbing their energy. As he continued to absorb their flesh, his body underwent accelerated transformations.","This could only be bad news for Lin Yuan.","Once Crimson absorbed the bodies of the other Pages, along with the energy in their souls, his power would undoubtedly evolve.","This transformation could become a threat to Lin Yuan.","But luckily, Lin Yuan had his own secret weapons.","Although Crimson could become a threat to Lin Yuan after consuming the other Pages, Lin Yuan did not try to stop Crimson’s actions.","This was because after absorbing them, all the Hellfire Lotus Imprints on their bodies would be transferred to Crimson.","Even if Crimson was able to sense the presence of the Hellfire Lotus Imprints, he would not consider them too much of a threat before Lin Yuan instructed the Abyss Red Lotus to activate them.","Crimson used his soul to envelop the souls of the other Pages and forcefully combined them.","The seal that Lin Yuan placed on Falling Rainbow’s soul would also be absorbed into Crimson’s soul.","Once he confirmed that all the Hellfire Lotus Imprints had been transferred, Lin Yuan used the energy in his body and used Lotus World Law again to steal some of the energy that Crimson had extracted from the main world.","Next, he used Cleansing Aura Lotus Flames to form more than 20 lotus coffins, forming a circular shape around Crimson.","The crimson flames in the lotus coffins ferociously burned the blood mist.","The Red Lotus Hellfire and blood mist crashed together, resulting in an ear-splitting explosion.","Meanwhile, the Red Lotus Hellfire depleted most of Lin Yuan’s energy.","The blood mist was able to resist the Red Lotus Hellfire. However, the blood mist also depleted faster than the Red Lotus Hellfire did.","Since Lin Yuan’s only remaining opponent was Crimson, this would be his final battle against Tower Canon. He needed to attack his opponent while ensuring his own survival.","At that moment, Lin Yuan entered combat mode and put all thoughts of Epoch God Palace out of his mind.","Even if he was truly Epoch God Palace’s target, he did not care if this battle allowed them to see through his methods.","In truth, the members of Epoch God Palace were watching his battle against Crimson. However, their mindsets were completely different from what he was thinking.","Spring and Summer’s eyes twinkled with amazement. Both of them knew that Lin Yuan had risen up within the short span of three years. For him to grow from a regular person to the person he was today in just three years, he truly lived up to being Lord Saint!","The two of them felt extremely disdainful toward Crimson’s bloodline.","“Summer, this illegitimate seed of the Blood species actually has the opportunity to meet with Lord Saint face-to-face. This is truly the highest honor he could ever receive! I never expected the illegitimate seed of the Blood species to be able to fuse so perfectly with the dead dimensional lifeform bloodline!”","Summer said softly, “Aren’t the people from Supreme Heavenly Abode always saying that the Blood species should be relegated to the same category as death energy? When the Blood species bloodline is fused with death aura, the bloodline level is not only maintained but will even be nourished by the death aura.","“Aside from the Blood species bloodline, that member of Tower Canon also possesses a hint of the Abyssal Beast bloodline. The Blood species on its own could never have such parasitical abilities!”","At that point, Summer’s voice turned stern and serious.","“Spring, regardless of what happens, I am always ready to step in to help Lord Saint. Aside from parasitical abilities, the Abyssal Beasy bloodline probably also allows Crimson to use void teleportation. I don’t want Lord Saint to suffer or be injured! As Lord Saint’s followers, how can we watch him become injured?”","When she saw that Spring was about to speak, Summer continued with her serious tone. “Spring, I know what you want to say. You have your considerations, but I also have my own determination.","“Lord Saint needs to have his own path of growth. With his current power, his growth won’t be significantly affected even if we interfere. If you are worried, you don’t have to act when I do.”","Summer had a gentle disposition. But once she made her decision, no one aside from Lord Saint could change her mind.","Summer had been punished in the past by the Totem God after speaking out of turn.","The two of them had walked their journeys together. If Summer wanted to step in, she could not stand by and watch.","With this thought in mind, Spring said softly, “You go and protect Lord Saint. I will keep an eye on Crimson and prevent him from fleeing. No matter what happens, we will end up showing ourselves to Lord Saint today! Falling Rainbow’s words have caused Lord Saint to mistakenly think of Epoch God Palace as the enemy. We should assuage this concern of his!”","The two of them came to their decision while the blood mist around Crimson fully disappeared.","Previously, Crimson’s body had been fully enveloped in his rose-red robe. But now, he revealed it.","Lin Yuan was stunned when he saw Crimson’s face.","He assumed that Crimson’s body would become monstrous after he absorbed the other members of Tower Canon. Yet, the body he revealed from under the robe was extremely handsome.","The long golden hair that framed his face billowed in the wind and had faint blood-colored specks. This did not make the long golden hair seem strange. Rather, it added an air of dignity!","He also had long narrow eyes, bloodless lips, and a tall body that wore an attire intricately adorned with gems.","This made Crimson the appearance of a prince in an ancient castle from Lin Yuan’s previous life.","The bright red and transparent tentacles sprouted from Crimson’s back and danced around wildly in the air.","The tentacles’ aura was fully suppressed by Crimson’s elite arrogance.","Lin Yuan saw Crimson’s lips curl slightly, and sharp fangs slid out from Crimson’s lips, shining like diamonds under the sunlight.","Lin Yuan was not shocked because Crimson had revealed his body but because Crimson’s facial features bore some similarity to the images Lin Yuan had seen when he received the New Thearch’s Scale’s legacy.","Lifeforms that looked like Crimson had ruined the mermaids and killed a mermaid thearch.","Those lifeforms were called the Blood species.","Lin Yuan was slightly confused. How did a member of the Blood species become mixed up with a dead dimensional lifeform?","Based on Crimson’s aura, the death aura in his body had already fully changed into blood energy.","Crimson had spent all his time with the other members of Tower Canon. How could they not have realized the change in the root energy in his body?","While Lin Yuan was working through his suspicions, Crimson said mockingly, “I don’t think you anticipated your actions to turn out to be helpful to me. In truth, I noticed you long ago. You were making use of Falling Rainbow while I was making use of you. I buried seeds in Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow’s bodies so I could use them as my eyes.”"]},{"number":2729,"title":"Chapter 2729 Dagger Palm Piercing From the Back!","paragraphs":["2729 Dagger Palm Piercing From the Back!","At that point, Crimson paused, and the mocking expression became even more evident on his face.","“You are already aware of many of Tower Canon’s secrets. You probably know that the fake Eight Pages were nothing more than puppets I put in place for appearances. Didn’t you expect that I would have some sort of restraint or control over these puppets?","“I allowed Eighth Page Apoptosis to escape with so much information, some of which even included information about Epoch God Palace, because I wanted to use him to keep an eye on you!","“We actually met a long time ago. So, in a way, we are old friends! Old friends shouldn’t fight immediately after meeting. Let’s have a chat. You must be very curious about me. It just so happens that I feel the same way! Why don’t you trade some secrets with me before surrendering your life?”","Lin Yuan knew that based on his observations, Crimson probably thought very lowly of him and saw him as nothing more than an easy target. Otherwise, he would never make such a speech!","It was likely that Crimson did not register him as a threat at all.","In terms of aura, their auras were of a similar level.","Crimson’s certainty that he could defeat Lin Yuan had to mean that he was hiding an extremely powerful secret weapon.","This worried Lin Yuan.","However, he also had secret weapons that he had yet to use.","It was true that there were many things that he wanted to find out about.","Although killing Crimson and destroying Tower Canon would reduce it to nothing more than a piece of the main world’s history, Lin Yuan did want to learn more about who was truly pulling the strings.","Crimson had been watching him through the blood-colored tentacles he had planted in the other members of Tower Canon.","This meant that there had to be a blood-colored tentacle in Apoptosis’ body.","Luckily, three months ago, Lin Yuan had killed Apoptosis after discovering that he was causing widespread harm by consuming the vitality of living people in order to enable his sacred source lifeform’s Stars to break through.","Otherwise, if Apoptosis was still in the Radiance Federation now and under the control of the bright red tentacle, he would definitely wreak havoc in the Radiance Federation!","Lin Yuan did not know if the bright red tentacle had benefited Apoptosis’ body in any way. If it enabled Apoptosis’ body to reach a new level, there were very few people in the Radiance Federation with the power to take him on.","“You’re right. Regardless of who ends up dead, I need to obtain information on Tower Canon.”","Crimson let out a low throttle of laughter. “Tower Canon? That’s me! I am the only member of Tower Canon left!”","While he spoke, Crimson looked at the ground around his feet. “You probably want to know why Tower Canon wants to take over this Class 2 world.”","Lin Yuan snarled, “Weren’t you watching me through Falling Rainbow and Eye Shadow? You should already be aware that Falling Rainbow has told me everything.”","Crimson extended a slender finger and wagged it at Lin Yuan. “I told you. I am Tower Canon now! If their thoughts aligned with mine, how could they end up as fodder for my bloodline awakening?","“I see no value in the dead world’s roots! Now that my bloodline has been activated, I would rather absorb spirit qi than the dirty death aura. Spirit qi truly has a splendid taste. I now know why the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ universes are ruled by those fellows who use spirit qi as their roots!”","Lin Yuan frowned when he heard what Crimson said.","Crimson’s goal was completely different from what Falling Rainbow had claimed it to be!","Falling Rainbow had said that they were trying to use the dead world’s roots to occupy this Class 2 world’s roots so they could recover their home.","Yet, Crimson saw the dead world’s roots as his tool and the other members of Tower Canon as sacrifices to activate his bloodline.","However, he had failed in the past because he lacked power.","In this respect, it could be said that Lin Yuan had helped Crimson.","Previously, Lin Yuan saw Tower Canon as an enemy who was trying to rob the main world. He had to kill the Eight Pages of Tower Canon because they stood on opposing sides.","But now, Lin Yuan saw Crimson as callous scum who had no qualms and was willing to destroy relationships.","Relationships were extremely important to Lin Yuan, and he could not understand how Crimson could lay a hand on comrades he had spent the past few millennia with.","Lin Yuan had sensed the sorrow and disbelief Violet Light Green, Falling Rainbow, and Warbler Candle felt before they died.","Warbler Candle, Violet Light Green, Falling Rainbow, and the other members of Tower Canon had been too seriously injured to fight back against Crimson. However, the Hellfire Lotus Imprints in their bodies could strike back against Crimson.","“If my guess is right, your bloodline is linked to the Blood species. However, your bloodline isn’t pure. The real members of the bloodline don’t have those tentacles!","“The Blood species prioritizes bloodline above all else. With your current bloodline, it’s unlikely that you’ll be accepted by the other members of the Blood species even if you do return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!”","Lin Yuan’s words hit Crimson’s sore spot, and anger spread across his face. But he quickly suppressed his rage.","Crimson did not respond to what Lin Yuan said because he believed that doing so would be admitting that he agreed with Lin Yuan. He would be admitting that he would never be accepted by the Blood species!","As a possessor of the Blood species bloodline, Crimson had always been proud of the fact that his father was a member of the Blood species. However, due to some circumstances, he also ended up in possession of the Abyssal Beast bloodline.","For other species, being able to combine the Abyssal Beast bloodline with their own was an enormous blessing.","But for the Blood species that valued bloodline over everything else, mixing bloodlines was the highest form of blasphemy.","Crimson always hated the Abyssal Beast bloodline in his body because it prevented him from being acknowledged by the Blood species.","Yet, without the Abyssal Beast bloodline, he would never have been able to use the other members of Tower Canon as his sacrifices.","Although Crimson did not respond to what Lin Yuan said, the latter could still sense that Crimson’s aura had changed.","At that moment, Crimson was incensed. Otherwise, his emotions would not be fluctuating so vigorously.","The imprint that had been on Falling Rainbow’s soul was now on Crimson’s soul.","Once a person lost their temper, they would also lose their sense of rationality.","Before Crimson could speak, Lin Yuan released his mermaid thearch aura.","“Since you used Apoptosis, Falling Rainbow, and Eye Shadow to spy on me, you should know that my bloodline has reached the mermaid thearch level!","“My bloodline is much purer than yours! Once I arrive at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, I will be acknowledged by the mermaid species while you still continue to be a pariah of the Blood species. You will still be nothing more than trash abandoned by the Blood species for having three types of bloodlines in your body!”","Lin Yuan was not a mean person. He was always extremely courteous toward others and was very uncomfortable saying such abrasive words. However, he could still utter them against an enemy!","Lin Yuan had hit Crimson’s sore spot multiple times. To the Blood species, there was no greater insult than having their bloodline attacked!","Crimson still had a fair number of questions for Lin Yuan. But now, he was in no mood to ask anything. After all, he would be able to dig out Lin Yuan’s secrets after killing him.","Crimson glared murderously at Lin Yuan as many blood-colored tentacles burst out from his body.","The tentacles rolled toward Lin Yuan and became entangled with the Abyss Red Lotus’ black roots.","The tentacles were enveloped in a special spatial energy that was very resistant to fire-elemental energy.","The Red Lotus Hellfire could not cause immediate damage to the blood-colored tentacles. However, it could deplete the spatial energy that enveloped them.","Once Crimson realized this, his expression shifted slightly, and he prepared to draw back these tentacles.","Although the tentacles existed as a form of energy, they were still a part of Crimson’s body. Once they were damaged, it would affect Crimson’s roots.","If Lin Yuan was even capable of damaging the Abyssal Beast’s abyssal energy, he had to have reached that level!","Crimson hurriedly dispelled his anger and turned serious, thinking, I shouldn’t have tried to use the abyssal tentacles I attained from the mutation of the Blood species bloodline to battle with Lin Yuan before properly understanding his power.","Lin Yuan intended to utilize all his secret weapons to kill Crimson. Hence, there was no way he would allow Crimson to draw back his tentacles.","Lin Yuan could sense that these tentacles were very important to Crimson. Otherwise, he would not have injected so much energy into these tentacles.","The blood mist spread out into the surroundings, and the entire Startling Lines Continent was shrouded in the blood mist.","However, the Red Lotus Hellfire was applied on Lin Yuan’s body, and it prevented the blood mist from getting close to him.","Still, he noticed that the blood mist could transform the elemental energy in the environment into blood energy that Crimson could absorb.","Lin Yuan had seen this ability in the dream realm when he was receiving the New Thearch’s Scale.","The Blood species turned water-elemental energy into blood energy and barraged the mermaids.","Nonetheless, there were two sides to all energy transformations.","Due to Lotus Law World, the fire-elemental energy in the surroundings was extremely pure and was also under the Abyss Red Lotus’ control.","Hence, the fire-elemental energy would be transformed at a very low rate. Crimson might be able to absorb energy faster than he transformed it!","Lin Yuan had made ample preparations before this battle and had used all the water in the Element Well to concoct pure fire elements.","As such, he took out a bucket of fire-elemental energy and poured it over the Abyss Red Lotus’ flower core.","The Red Lotus Hellfire rolled over the blood mist in a terrifying manner.","The crimson flames on the Abyss Red Lotus’ black roots turned a brilliant scarlet and rose to the sky, filling the sky with lotus patterns.","When the fierce scarlet Red Lotus Hellfire made contact with the abyssal energy on the tentacles, the abyssal energy quickly melted away like ice.","After the abyssal energy was burned away, the crimson and golden Red Lotus Hellfire burned the bright red tentacles to the point of deformation.","Crimson let out a few grunts of pain.","Lin Yuan could sense that Crimson was quickly gathering the energy in his body. It was clear that he was preparing to launch a counterattack.","Crimson had decided to put an end to this battle swiftly because he could sense that the Red Lotus Hellfire was placing Hellfire Lotus Imprints on his body through his tentacles.","If the Hellfire Lotus Imprint only sealed energy and Crimson was prevented from transferring energy between his body and the surroundings, he would not be as panicked as he was now. The key point was that the lotus imprints could also seal his bloodline.","The Blood species was fundamentally different from dead dimensional lifeforms.","Dead dimensional lifeforms used death energy as their cores and to fight, while the Blood species used their bloodline power to activate energy.","If his bloodline was sealed, Crimson’s ability to use his power would be affected.","At that moment, Lin Yuan activated the Hellfire Lotus Imprint in Crimson’s body. Once the Hellfire Lotus Imprint appeared, Crimson’s bloodline was immediately locked.","At the same time, the imprint on Crimson’s soul ignited with ferocious Red Lotus Hellfire that began ravaging Crimson’s soul.","Lin Yuan had used all the directly accessible methods against Crimson. If they were not enough, he would have to tap into other secret weapons!","Before he came to know of Epoch God Palace, Lin Yuan had every intention of using all his secret weapons against Tower Canon.","Although using his secret weapons would come at a cost, he would have plenty of opportunities to collect more secret weapons in the future.","But with Epoch God Palace’s presence, Lin Yuan had to preserve some of his secret weapons during combat so he would not be completely vulnerable when he eventually faced Epoch God Palace.","Crimson already guessed why so many Hellfire Lotus Imprints had appeared in his body. There were even seals on his soul. They must have come from Warbler Candle, Violet Light Green, and Falling Rainbow.","Crimson felt as though he had just fallen for Lin Yuan’s trap.","He could clearly tell that Lin Yuan did not understand the Abyssal Beast’s bloodline. Otherwise, he would not have left out naming the Abyssal Beast’s bloodline when mocking his bloodline!","With this thought, Crimson decided to use his Abyssal Beast bloodline to ambush Lin Yuan.","There were many experts in the Sky Beyond the Clouds who were assassinated by members of the Abyssal Beast species.","The Abyssal Beast species was skilled at overcoming their relative weakness to achieve victory.","Crimson’s body suddenly disappeared from within the Red Lotus Hellfire and appeared behind Lin Yuan.","Crimson used his palm as a dagger and slashed down on Lin Yuan.","At that moment, an explosive scream filled the space."]},{"number":2730,"title":"Chapter 2730 I am the Saint?","paragraphs":["2730 I am the Saint?","“Do you really think trash like you deserves to lay a hand on Lord Saint?!”","Due to the Hellfire Lotus Imprints, Lin Yuan could sense Crimson’s presence. The Hellfire Lotus Imprints had essentially placed a brand on Crimson’s body, allowing Lin Yuan to locate Crimson if he used any hidden attacks.","However, Crimson had moved too quickly, and Lin Yuan had been completely unable to react. He could feel a powerful force rushing toward his back.","However, despite being able to sense Crimson’s location, he was unable to do anything to stop him because Crimson was moving too quickly for Lin Yuan to be able to react in time to stop him.","He could already feel a powerful force rushing toward his back.","Lin Yuan had no doubt that Crimson would be able to pierce through his heart.","Due to the Jasmine Lily’s existence, Lin Yuan could use its Vitality Imprint to activate his genetic model and grow a new heart.","However, Lin Yuan was afraid that Crimson would plant the disgusting tentacle in his body.","Not even the official members of Tower Canon were able to break free of the tentacles’ control.","Although Lin Yuan had ways to protect his soul, he did not have the confidence to fend off these bizarre tentacles.","But after this cry, the immense force behind Lin Yuan disappeared abruptly.","Lin Yuan turned quickly and saw a skinny girl with long hair standing in front of him. Her finger was pointed and positioned on Crimson’s palm.","Not only was the finger easily blocking the palm, but it was also blocking the force that had been rushing toward him.","Lin Yuan heard the girl say in a clear and cold voice, “You, illegitimate seed of the Blood species, you should know who I am. You sure are brave!”","Lin Yuan watched as the girl’s finger made a gentle chopping motion.","Crimson’s hand was promptly cut off by this girl’s finger!","Crimson looked at this girl with fright and tried to back away.","However, with a slight hook of this girl’s finger, Crimson’s body was frozen, and a few small flowers bloomed on his body.","Crimson shrieked, “Isn’t Epoch God Palace’s target someplace aside from this world? Tower Canon made a trip to clarify this with you! Why are you going against your word?”","The rage intensified on Spring’s face.","Once worlds reached a certain level, they would begin invading and plundering each other. Many worlds strengthened themselves by consuming other worlds.","Hence, Spring was apathetic toward the destruction of worlds and the extinction of lifeforms.","Crimson thought that she was targeting him because Epoch God Palace had lied to them. He had no idea that they were the ones who had misinterpreted the significance of Epoch God Palace’s existence.","If Epoch God Palace had not seen numerous new totems appear on the wall illustration in the sacred hall, thereby confirming that Lord Totem God was awake and that there was no need for them to continue laying low, Lord Saint might have been hurt by Crimson’s attack. It might have even impacted Lord Saint’s reincarnation.","The more she thought about it, the more afraid she became. However, Spring did not unleash a lethal attack on Crimson. Instead, she restrained Crimson before turning and bowing respectfully to Lin Yuan with her eyes full of reverence.","“Greetings, Lord Saint!”","Before Lin Yuan could react to Spring’s greeting, another girl appeared in front of him and bowed just like Spring had done.","As confused as Lin Yuan was, he knew that he was the ‘Lord Saint’ the two female experts were referring to.","Lin Yuan was frozen.","These two girls had saved him, but he felt as though they had gravely misunderstood something.","Lin Yuan did not have any memories of being the Saint. Naturally, he did not see himself as the reincarnation of the Saint either.","It was clear that the two female experts had made a mistake about his identity.","However, this was a good opportunity for Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had been worried that Epoch God Palace would be an enemy. He had heard from Fifth Page Falling Rainbow that Tower Canon had been forced into slumber for 6,000 years because of Epoch God Palace.","The female expert had recognized him, and she also had the power to defeat Crimson easily. She had to be one of the rulers of Epoch God Palace!","The ruler of Epoch God Palace was acting this respectfully toward him because she had mistaken his identity.","Did this mean that he would be able to control Epoch God Palace by taking the place of this Saint?","However, Lin Yuan did not feel even a hint of optimism.","Identity theft came with risks.","Lin Yuan did not know when the members of Epoch God Palace would realize that he was not the Saint.","As Lin Yuan looked at the two female experts kneeling on the ground before him, he could not decide between immediately assuming the identity of Lord Saint and interacting with these two experts in his actual confused state.","Now that Spring and Summer were in close proximity to Lin Yuan, the two of them could see the Totem God on his wrist.","Lord Totem God could only appear on the Saint.","The two of them had become certain of Lin Yuan’s identity long ago. Hence, after greeting him, Summer began seriously explaining, “Lord Saint, you probably don’t know who we are. It’s true that we shouldn’t be appearing in front of you! But now that you’re in danger, we have no choice but to reveal ourselves! If you want to assign blame, Spring and I are willing to take the blame!”","When Crimson saw such mannerisms, he began looking at Lin Yuan with terror.","This was the way that a follower greeted a master.","Crimson did not know what the identity of the Saint signified, but he knew that only the top experts from the universes had the ability to reincarnate! Only those experts had the power to gather followers.","Could it be that this human, who they were calling the Saint, was one of those reincarnated beings? This was the only way to explain everything that was happening!","If Epoch God Palace was a faction that was following an entity, it explained why they had been lying under the radar in the main world for such a long time!","Epoch God Palace had not gone against their word. He was the one who had offended them.","In an instant, Crimson’s heart sank.","If Lin Yuan was allowed to decide whether he lived or died, there was no way that Lin Yuan would allow him to continue living!","Even after hearing what Summer said, Lin Yuan did not think of himself as the Saint.","Instead, he now knew how to approach them.","Lin Yuan took a deep breath and prepared himself to put on an act.","This was when he heard the female expert who had protected him say in a gentle voice, “Lord Saint, do you have any doubts about your identity? You are wearing Lord Totem God.","“We confirmed your identity based on Lord Totem God’s aura! So you don’t have to worry that we are mistaken about your identity! Once we head back to Epoch God Palace, we will be able to use the Returning Saint Pool to shine on your birth horoscope! That will authenticate your identity!”","Lin Yuan was about to become immersed in his act. But when he heard what Spring said, his body froze, and his expression changed.","He lifted his hand to look at Morbius on his wrist.","Could it be that Morbius was the Totem God? This did seem possible!","The exclusive skill that Morbius gained after evolving to Myth Breed allowed it to produce the totem seeds.","As his lifelong companion, he always wore Morbius on his person.","Lin Yuan assumed that wearing Morbius as an accessory was very discreet. Yet, this expert from Epoch God Palace was still able to sense Morbius’ aura.","Although Lin Yuan did not believe what Spring said, he knew that there was no need for this female expert who had saved him to lie to him. If she wanted to capture him, he would be incapable of resisting! Since he could not resist, it went without saying that he stood no chance of overpowering her!","After understanding this, Lin Yuan questioned his identity for the first time.","Could it be that he was truly the reincarnated Saint?","It was true that he came to the fey world from another world.","However, he had not made any significant waves in his previous life and had even died an untimely death.","He could not ascertain his identity just by thinking about it.","Lin Yuan believed that he needed to head to Epoch God Palace to use the Returning Saint Pool to shine his birth horoscope and confirm if he was truly the Saint.","Aside from confirming his identity, Lin Yuan was also curious about the Returning Saint Pool. It was able to shine a person’s birth horoscope and enable a lifeform to become a birth horoscope expert!","Currently, Lin Yuan was only an A-rank spirit qi professional.","After the Returning Saint Pool shined on his birth horoscope, his and all his feys’ powers would increase. He would no longer be limited by his spirit qi professional rank.","At that time, Morbius’ power would also elevate rapidly.","Not only would the Spirit Lock spatial zone grow larger again, but Lin Yuan’s overall power would also increase at an unbelievable rate.","“I am willing to head with you to Epoch God Palace to allow the Returning Saint Pool to shine on my birth horoscope. But before that, I need your help with something. Help me to take full control of Crimson!”","Spring and Summer remained kneeling in trepidation when they heard what Lin Yuan said.","“Lord Saint, receiving orders from you is a blessing to us. You don’t need to ask for our help. Working for you is only right!”","Spring and Summer tapped Crimson’s body, and he was immediately imprisoned between them. Crimson could not even move one of his fingers.","Spring and Summer would not give Crimson the chance to speak before Lin Yuan gave him permission to do so.","This was because they felt that Crimson was too lowly of a lifeform to deserve to communicate with Lin Yuan. They also did not want the Crimson to utter any uncouth words in front of Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan could see from Crimson’s gaze that he had many things that he wanted to say. However, he did not want to give Crimson the chance to say them.","There was no need to communicate with someone who wanted to destroy the world and attack him! The only option for Crimson was death!","At first, Lin Yuan wanted to find out more about Epoch God Palace from Crimson.","But now, it seemed that Epoch God Palace was more likely a friend than foe. It was possible that they would become his subordinates and lend their strength to him after his identity was proven!","Lin Yuan raised a hand, and Crimson was enveloped in ferocious Red Lotus Hellfire.","Under Spring and Summer’s control, Crimson could not use his own power to defend himself!","As the Red Lotus Hellfire burned Crimson’s body, layers of Hellfire Lotus Imprints accumulated on his body.","Crimson’s body was extremely important to Lin Yuan. After tempering Crimson’s body and destroying his soul, he would use Red Thorn’s Tongue of Relinquish to take control of Crimson’s body.","At that point, Crimson would become his strongest general!","He would be better off obtaining Crimson’s body and using it to strengthen himself rather than allowing Spring and Summer to eradicate him!","Although it seemed that the experts from Epoch God Palace would protect him, Lin Yuan would rather increase his own power than be protected by others. Increasing his own power was fundamental.","Lin Yuan tempered Crimson for three days before he finally managed to destroy Crimson’s soul.","Spring and Summer helped Lin Yuan significantly in the past three days.","A lifeform that used its bloodline as its energy source could host a portion of its soul in its bloodline. It would then be able to use its bloodline to revive itself after its souls were destroyed.","Spring and Summer yanked out the soul that Crimson had hidden in his bloodline. Otherwise, even if Lin Yuan killed Crimson’s soul, the remnant of his soul energy in his bloodline would reject Red Thorn when it tried to take control of him.","Lin Yuan felt satisfied as he stored Crimson’s body. He turned and said, “I need you to give me two days to prepare. Two days later, I will go with you to Epoch God Palace.”","Spring and Summer knew how attached Lin Yuan was to this Class 1 world because they had taken it upon themselves to understand his entire life journey.","It was obvious that he was going to use these two days to tend to this attachment.","Spring said softly, “Lord Saint, you are free to decide whenever you want to head to Epoch God Palace. You don’t have to set a time with us. We will be following you so you can leave for Epoch God Palace whenever you wish. If you want to address the death aura in this world, we can help you!”"]},{"number":2731,"title":"Chapter 2731 Master, Everything is Going Well!","paragraphs":["2731 Master, Everything is Going Well!","Lin Yuan’s eyes lit up.","This expert from Epoch God Palace had the means to help him clear out all the death aura in the ley lines! He could not ask for anything better!","Given their capabilities, they would be able to do a much better job of clearing death aura from the ley lines than the demon insects!","The faster death aura was cleared from the ley lines in the main world, the better it would be for the lifeforms in the main world.","However, rather than just getting rid of the death aura, Lin Yuan would rather divert the death aura to Silver Corona and Red Thorn so they could consume it to evolve their bloodlines.","“If that is true, I shall thank the two of you in advance now. Is it possible for you to funnel the death aura in the ley lines to a specific location? I would like to use the death aura to evolve two of my feys.”","Spring hurriedly replied, “Your request can be met easily. All we need to do is inject and direct some of our own energy into the ley lines to manipulate the direction of the death aura while we’re clearing it! Do you plan on using the death aura to strengthen the fairy beneath this continent?”","Lin Yuan nodded.","These two girls from Epoch God Palace came across as thoughtful and competent individuals. They were able to understand his intentions without him needing to provide much explanation.","At the same time, he gained a new understanding of their powers.","They were able to use their energy to funnel the death aura in the ley lines of a Class 2 world. Just how powerful did they have to be to be capable of such a feat?","After 6,000 years of infection, the death aura had already taken root in every corner of the ley lines. The death aura had even formed a large amount of minerals around the ley lines.","Lin Yuan did not know what the members of Epoch God Palace would do to him if he was not the Saint.","But if he was confirmed to be the Saint, he would gain the protection of numerous experts with such power.","This would make him much more confident in both protecting the main world and when he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","“You’re right. The fairy beneath this continent is indeed one of the targets for strengthening that I have in mind. How long will it take you to direct all the death aura in the main world to that location?”","Spring and Summer fell silent when they heard Lin Yuan’s question. After a pause, they said, “Lord Saint, it is tough for us to answer your question. We will definitely be able to funnel the death aura faster than the eight-winged fairy’s rate of absorption. So the exact time depends on your eight-winged fairy’s rate of absorption.”","“If you’re willing to give us time, we can compress the death aura in the ley lines into crystals. Then, you can collect the crystals and feed them to the fairy whenever you wish!”","“Your demon insects can absorb death aura, but they are far too slow. Furthermore, while they are absorbing the death aura, they will inadvertently affect the ley lines. The roots of this Class 2 world will have to be significantly depleted in order to recover damaged roots.”","Once they were done speaking, power rose from Spring and Summer.","At that moment, Lin Yuan was still fused with the Abyss Red Lotus.","The auras emanating from Spring and Summer were not targeted at Lin Yuan, but he could still feel enormous pressure from them. He could even feel the effects of the pressure on his divine kingdom.","Lin Yuan had never felt this feeling before.","Spring and Summer injected this solid power into the ley lines, and it rapidly began flowing through the ley lines. While it flowed, the energy extracted death aura and gathered it toward the Startling Lines Continent.","When Lin Yuan saw this, he summoned Red Thorn.","Once Red Thorn appeared, it began flying around Lin Yuan while sniffing him. It could pick up Silver Corona’s scent clearly.","On the one hand, Red Thorn was happy for Silver Corona that it managed to successfully evolve its bloodline. However, it was also irked that Silver Corona had the audacity to become more intimate with Lin Yuan after its evolution and even left its scent on him.","Red Thorn had already used its fairy bloodline to issue a warning to Silver Corona. However, Silver Corona had bypassed its warning after its evolution.","Since they were both Lin Yuan’s feys, Red Thorn would not be so reckless as to engage in conflict with another one of his feys. But this did not mean that Red Thorn could condone Silver Corona’s actions.","Red Thorn knew that Lin Yuan had summoned it because he wanted them to absorb the death aura together.","Since they had this setting of fair competition, Red Thorn intended to compete with Silver Corona. It wanted to see which one of their bloodlines transformed first after absorbing death aura.","Lin Yuan was unaware of all these thoughts running through Red Thorn’s mind. He had no idea that Red Thorn was always secretly comparing itself to Silver Corona.","Lin Yuan handed First Page Crimson, Eighth Page Eye Shadow, and Fourth Page Cavity Orchid’s bodies to Red Thorn before saying seriously, “Red Thorn, when you begin absorbing the death aura, use the death aura to first speed up the time taken to take control of these bodies!”","Red Thorn nodded earnestly. It had a great interest in taking control of the bodies of the Eight Pages of Tower Canon.","A thought suddenly struck Red Thorn. “Yuan, when you go to search through Tower Canon’s nest and take possession of their resources, I hope that you’ll help me to search for the Gardener Konjac that you previously fed me.","“The Gardener Konjac is very beneficial in enabling my Tongue of Relinquish’s abilities to evolve! If it’s possible, it will be best if we can get our hands on the Gardener Konjac’s seeds so we can try cultivating it ourselves!”","Lin Yuan nodded solemnly.","Lin Yuan already intended to ask Tower Canon about the Gardener Konjac.","Fifth Page Truth had mentioned that the Gardener Konjac was a kind of konjac that Second Page Warbler Candle had nurtured. It was a dead plant-type fey that was very rare in the dead world.","Even while she had been sleeping for 6,000 years, Warbler Candle had used her puppetry abilities to manipulate her puppets to look after the Gardener Konjac. She had even contributed a portion of her root energy.","As a result, the Gardener Konjac had to be thriving!","Now that all the members of Tower Canon were dead and Warbler Candle had been absorbed by Crimson, Lin Yuan had no one he could ask about where the Gardener Konjac was planted.","Regardless, Warbler Candle and the other members of Tower Canon had no reason to destroy the Gardener Konjac before they left. Hence, the Gardener Konjac had to still be growing somewhere in the main world!","The two female experts from Epoch God Palace had to know where Tower Canon’s nest was located.","If Lin Yuan searched Tower Canon’s old residence, he would undoubtedly be able to find the Gardener Konjac that Warbler Candle had painstakingly nurtured.","Lin Yuan could set aside a sealed off space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone dedicated to nurturing the Gardener Konjac. He would then be able to use it to strengthen Red Thorn’s Tongue of Relinquish!","Out of all of Red Thorn’s abilities, its Tongue of Relinquish was the most helpful to Lin Yuan as his power increased at an accelerated rate.","After Red Thorn was done speaking with Lin Yuan, it left and headed to the bottom of the sea. It summoned its main body from the Spirit Lock spatial zone and produced a sea of flowers at the bottom of the sea.","Red Thorn and Silver Corona then began absorbing death aura from the bottom of the sea.","After Summer observed the rate at which Red Thorn and Silver Corona were absorbing the death aura, she said, “Spring, I can direct the death aura on my own. If you stay here and use your energy to direct the death aura with me, there will be no one to stay with Lord Saint to protect him. Lord Saint is probably going to head to the Radiance Federation.”","Spring slowly dispersed her energy and left Summer to funnel the death aura in the ley lines on her own.","Before they found Lin Yuan, everyone in Epoch God Palace spent all their time thinking about and missing the Saint.","But now that they had found Lin Yuan, Spring and Summer had the same thought, which was to ensure Lin Yuan’s safety.","This was in spite of the fact that there was no other lifeform in the main world that could threaten Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan told Summer with a smile, “Summer, sorry to trouble you. It’s true that I am going to the Radiance Federation.”","Lin Yuan previously asked Spring and Summer to give him two days because he did not know that they had already confirmed that he was the Saint.","He was going to use the two days to explain his situation to the Moon Empress.","Although the dead spirits crisis had yet to come to an end, no more changes were going to crop up, and it had entered its ending stage.","Just like how the Radiance Federation and the rest of the main world had to make extensive preparations before the dead spirits crisis began, they would also have many tasks to attend to after the dead spirits crisis ended.","As the core of the main world, it would be best if the Radiance Federation could begin its preparations first.","Aside from telling the Moon Empress about his news, he was going to inform the Heavenly Family Cottage and Vast Sea Labyrinth about this.","Lin Yuan was also going to awaken Keira and issue new orders to her.","Now that Summer could allocate the death aura in the ley lines while clearing out the death aura, Keira no longer had to rush to produce the demon insects with shuttle abilities.","Just as Summer had said, the demon insects would definitely impact the ley lines to a certain extent while clearing the death aura.","Keira had informed Lin Yuan of this in advance. But at the time, Lin Yuan did not have any other options aside from using Keira to clear out the death aura in the ley lines.","However, now that he had a method to clear out death aura from the ley lines without causing any damage to them, Lin Yuan would prefer to preserve the main world’s ley lines.","Due to the change in plans, Lin Yuan had to assign new tasks to Keira.","Currently, Keira’s main job was to use the demon insects she produced to eliminate the dead dimensional lifeforms.","With the demon insects’ combat capabilities, the current volume of demon insects was already sufficient.","Lin Yuan could do his best to remove all signs of any dead dimensional lifeforms from the surface of the main world. If he achieved this, both the human world and the dimensional worlds would be able to regain peace.","Two days was enough for Lin Yuan to accomplish these two tasks.","However, Spring and Summer were in no rush and were willing to give him however much time he needed to do the tasks he needed to finish.","Thus, Lin Yuan would definitely be returning to the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan knew the Moon Empress well. She would only be able to lay her worries to rest when she saw him in the flesh.","Recently, Lin Yuan had been busy fighting the dead spirits crisis and had not had the time to help the spirit qi professionals whose feys were stuck at their current grades to break through.","He did not know how long it would take for him to head to the Epoch God Palace and use the Returning Saint Pool to light up his birth horoscope.","Lin Yuan could not hold back these experts from increasing their power and keep them waiting for him. Hence, he needed to help them break through their feys’ grades before he went to Epoch God Palace.","This would also allow Lin Yuan to collect a large quantity of spirit qi crystals and golden ley line pearls.","Once his birth horoscope was awakened, Lin Yuan’s feys would need to break through as well. Stocking up on the spirit qi crystals would definitely be helpful!","After he harvested the spirit qi crystals and golden ley line pearls, Lin Yuan could give a portion of them to the Moon Empress so she could continue increasing the Radiance Federation’s overall power.","Increasing the Radiance Federation’s power was not only to enable the Radiance Federation to take on the dead spirits crisis.","After the sixth epoch would be the seventh epoch, then the eighth and the ninth epoch.","No one knew when the next calamity would descend. In the face of uncertain catastrophes, the only thing they could do was increase their power.","As the Radiance Federation and the main world grew stronger, their ability to resist risks would also rise.","Lin Yuan was never the type to let down his guard. However, he did not feel much suspicion toward Epoch God Palace, Spring, and Summer.","He had already experienced Spring and Summer’s powers. Both of them were more powerful than he had imagined.","Either of them could kill him easily. They could even destroy the entire main world without leaving any survivors.","Experts like this did not need to use any underhanded tricks against him!","Spring stood half a meter behind Lin Yuan.","“Lord Saint, when you leave for the Radiance Federation, I will hide by your side to protect you. Don’t worry. My presence won’t cause any inconvenience to you!”","After she spoke, Spring’s figure disappeared.","Lin Yuan tried his best to sense his surroundings but could not detect Spring at all.","He summoned the Kill Food Sky Butterfly and climbed aboard its back before heading to the Radiance Federation.","While he was traveling to the Radiance Federation, Lin Yuan excitedly sent a message to the Moon Empress.","[Lin Yuan]: Master, everything is going well on my end! Tower Canon has been dealt with! The death spirits crisis is also about to come to an end.","The Moon Empress had been keeping the Thoughts Letter Paper in her hand in the hopes of receiving a message from Lin Yuan as soon as he sent it.","When the Moon Empress read his message, she instinctively relaxed. But she soon became nervous again.","It was not that she did not believe what Lin Yuan said. He would never lie about such matters. Tower Canon was definitely destroyed, and the dead spirits crisis was coming to an end.","However, Lin Yuan did not explain the situation clearly. He had to have paid an enormous price in order to obliterate Tower Canon and put an end to the dead spirits crisis.","The Moon Empress did not just want the disaster to be over. She wanted Lin Yuan to return.","At that moment, the Moon Empress received another message from Lin Yuan.","[Lin Yuan]: Master, I will be arriving back at the Radiance Federation soon. I will report the details of the situation to you then!"]},{"number":2732,"title":"Chapter 2732 Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress’ Meeting!","paragraphs":["2732 Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress’ Meeting!","The Moon Empress was finally able to relax fully when she saw Lin Yuan’s message.","By saying that he was arriving back in the Radiance Federation soon, it meant that Lin Yuan was safe and unharmed.","This was two pieces of good news for the Moon Empress.","However, she did not share the information immediately. She wanted to wait for Lin Yuan to return to the Radiance Federation and hear the details of the situation from him before she made any further arrangements.","Although Tower Canon had been destroyed, the dead spirits crisis was still ongoing.","The dead spirits crisis was disastrous for the entire main world.","This calamity was a wake-up call for the Moon Empress.","Although the main world used to encounter dimensional rift openings, the federations lived under relative peace. The only friction came from the scuffles between individual federations that only depleted the individual federations’ strength and never made them more of a threat than they already were.","If the Radiance Federation had maintained a readiness to tackle any risks, it would not have had such a tough time at the beginning of the dead spirits crisis.","If it was possible, the Moon Empress did not want to eliminate every single dead spirit immediately. Instead, she wanted to use them to train the main world and increase the power of the main world’s federations.","The Moon Empress planned to hold discussions with the Vast Sea Labyrinth’s leaders.","The sea clans were stronger than the humans, but they also needed to participate in this training.","The Moon Empress was prepared to use the next few decades to fundamentally improve the main world.","Aside from having exceptional power, this year’s Radiance Hundred Sequence also possessed outstanding leadership skills.","The Moon Empress was going to give Liu Wencheng many resources so he could personally raise the power of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Mystic Moon had been sticking by the Moon Empress’ side.","Cold Moon remained on the outside to disseminate the Moon Empress’ instructions while Mystic Moon stayed in the Radiant Moon Palace so he could pay close attention to the Moon Empress’ plans and assist her in organizing everything.","The Moon Empress had remained in a state of worry ever since Lin Yuan left the Radiance Federation a week ago. The ever-steady Moon Empress was only able to maintain her usual composure when she was busy with work. At any other time, she was filled with anxiety.","But now, the anxiety vanished from the Moon Empress’ face and was replaced by excitement and delight.","Mystic Moon knew that Lin Yuan had sent updates about his situation.","Usually, the Moon Empress did not ask many questions when Lin Yuan said that he would be returning soon. But this time, she could not stop herself from asking.","[Moon Empress]: Little Yuan, how long will it take you to reach the Radiance Federation?","When Lin Yuan saw the Moon Empress’ message, he realized just how concerned she was for him.","[Lin Yuan]: I should be arriving at the Radiant Moon Palace at around 2:00 p.m. tomorrow!","Normally, Lin Yuan could travel back to the Radiance Federation directly through the Space Tunnel in the basement.","However, he had moved the underground palace to the Spirit Lock spatial zone, causing the Space Tunnel to lose its effects.","Since the Ethereal Jellyfish could grow more main tentacles after the Space Tunnel was removed, Lin Yuan did not actually suffer any real losses.","Before he returned to the Radiance Federation, Lin Yuan was going to instruct Lift Marsh to bring Thick Soil City back to the Startling Lines Continent before sending the Land Imps to fortify Thick Soil City’s base.","After Tower Canon was destroyed and the main world returned to a state of peace, the Startling Lines Continent was going to become the Radiance Federation’s gate to the rest of the world.","Luo Lan, Yi Huailong, and Jin Qianxun, who ruled over the three federations that made up the Startling Lines Continent, all sent Lin Yuan messages. They hoped that the Divine Wood, Iron Hammer, and Great Lush Federations could return to the Startling Lines Continent.","With their abilities and experience, they were easily able to recognize the Startling Lines Continent’s strategic significance.","Firstly, Lin Yuan had invested numerous resources into the Startling Lines Continent and turned it into a virtually impenetrable fortress.","Furthermore, there was an abundance of resources in the Startling Lines Continent, and it was also the Divine Wood, Iron Hammer, and Great Lush Federations’s home.","The three of them wanted to continue their development in their home.","The Divine Wood, Iron Hammer, and Great Lush Federations were all fully under Lin Yuan’s control.","There was no question that allowing these three federations to continue developing in the Startling Lines Continent was the best option.","Luo Lan had sought Su Yiren’s opinion before sending her request to Lin Yuan. Su Yiren supported Luo Lan in fighting for such an opportunity.","If the dead spirits crisis could come to an end without any more trouble cropping up, Su Yiren would also lead the people from the Dark and Sand Island Continents back to their original continents.","However, Su Yiren knew that Lin Yuan was busy with many matters and stressed to Luo Lan not to rush Lin Yuan.","Since they could not offer him any help now, they should not be adding to his burden either.","It was true that Lin Yuan was very busy of late and did not have time to attend to these trivial matters.","Wen Yu was also busy. Thus, Lin Yuan could not assign her to take care of these trivial tasks.","Lin Yuan had already issued orders to Lift Marsh.","When Lift Marsh brought Thick Soil City back to the Startling Lines Continent, Lin Yuan would instruct it to deliver the demon insects to the boundaries between the main world and the various dimensional worlds.","...","Lin Yuan did not rest while he was riding on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly. Instead, he took out the Thoughts Letter Paper so he could attend to all the tasks that had piled up of late.","It did not take long for him to see the requests sent by Luo Lan, Yi Huailong, and Jin Qianxun.","After a moment of silence, Lin Yuan decided to agree to allow the three of them to take the Divine Wood, Iron Hammer, and Great Lush Federations back to the Startling Lines Continent so they could continue their development.","The Startling Lines Continent was not small. The three federations continuing their development there would not prevent the Radiance Federation from using the Startling Lines Continent as its gate. Rather, the three federations’ presence would help to save the Radiance Federation a lot of trouble.","Lin Yuan had already overhauled these three federations, and they could be considered his direct subsidiaries. He did not have to worry when they were in charge of watching the Radiance Federation’s gate.","Moreover, aside from the Radiance Federation, Lin Yuan had given most of his resources to the Divine Wood, Iron Hammer, and Great Lush Federations. Hence, the three federations’ overall power would only grow.","Although they could not compete with the Freedom Federation and Azure Federation now, they had solid positions among the second-tier federations.","These three federations were on close terms now because they were all under his control. Although they could not be considered united, they were able to carry out his strategies together.","Lin Yuan sent replies to three of them.","Yi Huailong relied on Yi Huailu, who was a Class 5 Creation Master, to rapidly increase his own power.","Yi Huailong could clearly sense that as the Divine Wood Federation’s overall power rose, he needed to increase his own power in order to secure his position as the ruler of the Divine Wood Federation.","If his power could not match his position, naysayers would emerge to undermine him. Yi Huailong was worried that if these negative sentiments spread and reached Lin Yuan, the latter would swap him out.","Jin Qianxun also had the same thoughts.","However, Jin Qianxun did not have a Class 5 Creation Master by his side and did not have a convenient avenue he could use to increase his power like Yi Huailong did.","It was true that Jin Qianxun had ties to Weng Queji, who was a Class 5 Creation Master. However, Weng Queji only served Lin Yuan and did not cater to him.","Hence, Jin Qianxun could only do his best to develop the Great Lush Federation and demonstrate his value to Lin Yuan.","Compared to Yi Huailong and Luo Lan, Jin Qianxun lacked confidence. This was because he was acutely aware of how he had managed to take the seat of the ruler of the Great Lush Federation.","Luo Lan had not done much to develop the Iron Hammer Federation recently. She had nurtured a few royal attendants who were capable of helping her handle appropriate tasks.","Luo Lan had been focusing most of her energy on helping Su Yiren to manage the Sand Island citizens.","After Su Yiren migrated, it was very difficult for her to manage the Sand Island citizens.","After all, she did not have much time to spare after handling the tasks involved with managing the Dark Federation.","Luo Lan’s help took significant pressure off of Su Yiren.","Naturally, Su Yiren was touched by Luo Lan’s help.","Su Yiren knew that Yi Huailong, Jin Qianxun, and Luo Lan were secretly competing with each other.","In spite of that, Luo Lan was willing to help her, which was enough to prove the genuity of their sisterly bond.","Before Su Yiren formed ties with others, she was constantly judging the value of others.","Luo Lan was very skilled at managing federations.","The Iron Hammer Federation’s previous king had nurtured Luo Lan as his successor because he recognized her talent.","However, Luo Lan lacked perseverance and ambition. Hence, it was highly unlikely that Lin Yuan would take her with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Normally, Su Yiren only liked to make friends with people of value.","However, regardless of what happened in the future, Luo Lan would always be her sister.","...","Luo Lan and Jin Qianxun had received Lin Yuan’s response almost at the same time, and both of them were over the moon.","After receiving Lin Yuan’s message, Luo Lan relayed the news to Su Yiren.","Su Yiren had already expected Lin Yuan to agree to her and the rest’s requests.","Su Yiren sent her reply to Luo Lan.","[Su Yiren]: Once I’m done with the tasks I have on hand, I will help you to develop the Iron Hammer Federation like I used to. Luo Lan, thank you for all the help you’ve given me!","After Su Yiren understood Lin Yuan’s goal, she stopped limiting her sights to the main world. She also wanted to go with him to explore worlds beyond the main world.","Su Yiren intended to properly nurture her 14 poppy fruits so they could temporarily manage the Dark and Sand Island Continents in her place.","Eventually, she would have to nurture another group of talents.","The 14 poppy fruits were part of the Absolute Love Poppy’s abilities. If she left the main world, she would have to take the 14 poppy fruits with her.","...","Wo Lun had also sent many messages to Lin Yuan.","He had been extremely excited recently.","As a marine federation, the Violent Wind Federation lacked mineral resources. They also had to source for lumber resources from islands on their outskirts. Hence, they were very constrained in the resources they needed to build boats and vessels.","Wo Lun had not felt this way when he was in such environments in the past.","It was only after he received the wood materials and metals from Lin Yuan that Wo Lun realized his breadth of resource interactions in the past had been far too limited!","With so many resources that he had never encountered before now in his possession, Wo Lun could build designs that he never could have imagined in the past.","It did not take long before Wo Lun made a discovery.","[Wo Lun]: Leo, I noticed that jade-textured wood can perfectly prevent rotting caused by seawater. It works best with sea mulberry wood that has water elements applied to it! If jade-textured sea mulberry wood is used to cover the bottom of the boat and Strong Floating Iron is used to build the frame, the boat will be able to travel to every corner of the seas in the main world! Fey storage boxes are also able to store living resources. As for a motor, feys that can release lava and tamed aquatic lifeforms are all good options! I believe that the main world will enter a great marine era once the dead spirits crisis is over.","Wo Lun sent his message to Lin Yuan after serious thought. He did not casually relay his thoughts.","The establishment of the Major Federation Union made Wo Lun aware that it was now necessary for the federations to become united!","The Island Whales could be used to form the links between the human federations.","However, the Island Whales were much too rare. Hence, there were not enough of them to meet the needs of all the federations.","If the boats and vessels could traverse the seas with ease, they could become the regular mode of marine transportation!","The federations that did not have the Island Whales would have no other choice.","The federations that did have the Island Whales would also be willing to sell their specialty goods and obtain rare foreign resources.","Lin Yuan controlled the water world dimensional lifeforms and was on good terms with the Vast Sea Labyrinth.","The water world dimensional lifeforms, sea clans, and humans were all on cooperative terms because of the dead spirits crisis.","After the dead spirits crisis ended, it was unlikely that the sea beasts would attack the humans’ boats.","The only thing that the humans needed to tackle was the natural obstacles of the sea’s environment.","After some pondering, Wo Lun believed that he needed to share his thoughts with Lin Yuan.","...","When Lin Yuan received the message from Wo Lun, he silently praised Wo Lun’s foresight.","In actuality, Lin Yuan had given the spiritual ingredients from the dimensional worlds and the jade-textured wood to Wo Lun because he wanted to enact such positive changes in the main world.","Lin Yuan would definitely have detailed discussions with Wo Lun about this matter. Hence, he did not send a thorough reply to Wo Lun.","As he looked out at the silhouette of the Radiance Federation in the distance, Lin Yuan was filled with an overwhelming sense of accomplishment and belonging.","Lin Yuan instructed the Kill Food Sky Butterfly to land on the borders of the Radiance Federation.","The Radiance Federation’s border had many spatial nodes that Lin Yuan had set up using the Ethereal Jellyfish’s tentacle node.","He could travel much faster using them than flying on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly!","...","Lin Yuan did not return to the Return from Faraway Mansion to clean up—his body was immaculate. Even if he did not shower and wash himself, he would remain in an extremely clean state.","Instead, he immediately went to the Radiant Moon Palace.","From the moment he appeared in the Radiant Moon Palace’s inner palace, he locked eyes with the Moon Empress.","Mystic Moon was standing behind the Moon Empress.","When Lin Yuan used the spatial nodes to travel, no obvious spatial fluctuations appeared in the locations he traveled to.","Hence, it was likely that the Moon Empress and Mystic Moon had been waiting there for him.","Lin Yuan reached out and pressed down the stray hairs on his head as he told the Moon Empress with a smile, “Master, just like I said in my message on the Thoughts Letter Paper, everything is going well!”"]},{"number":2733,"title":"Chapter 2733 Four Beasts Territory’s Conflict!","paragraphs":["2733 Four Beasts Territory’s Conflict!","The moment Lin Yuan was done speaking, he saw the Moon Empress stride over to him before enveloping him in a bear hug!","This was not to say that Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress were on bad terms, but the Moon Empress rarely showed her emotions so outwardly. Normally, she would just adjust his collar or pat his shoulder.","From how unrestrained she was in expressing her emotions now, Lin Yuan knew that she had been worried sick about him!","Lin Yuan gently reached his arm around her back and patted it. “Master, it’s all over!”","The Moon Empress only released Lin Yuan after a beat had passed.","She looked him up and down. It was only when she was certain that he was completely fine that she said solemnly, “Little Yuan, from now on, even if I can’t be of help in whatever you’re doing, you cannot wait until the last second to update me! Even if I can’t help you, I can share your burden!”","The Moon Empress was being extremely sincere.","When the dead spirits crisis began, the Moon Empress experienced helplessness for the first time. This helplessness made her aware that there was no end to increasing one’s power!","In her youth, she was accustomed to doing her best. But after she became a Class 5 Creation Master and subsequently a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty, she stood at the top of the world and undoubtedly slowed down her increment of power. From then on, she stopped focusing her energy on increasing her power.","She only redirected her focus back to increasing her power when she was injured during her battle with the Freedom Federation’s royalty, and it became imperative that she achieve a breakthrough in order to extend her lifespan!","In the past, the Moon Empress believed she had come upon this realization far too late.","But as she thought about how Lin Yuan had taken each step on his journey of growth, the Moon Empress felt that being able to come to this realization, regardless of timing, was a blessing!","Firstly, she now had an endless lifespan, so her previous delay would not have any impact on her increasing her power in the future.","Moreover, she had obtained a large leg up from Lin Yuan in terms of increasing her power. He had provided her with treasures that she could not produce on her own despite being a Class 6 Creation Master. It was through the resources she obtained from him that the Moon Empress had been able to make progress in advancing her level.","When Lin Yuan heard this, it became one of the rare moments that he found himself disagreeing with what the Moon Empress said.","Lin Yuan shook his head gently at the Moon Empress.","“Master, I have already increased my power. In the past, you had to shelter me from everything and shoulder all the pressure on your own. Now, it’s my turn to protect you! Rest assured, I won’t allow you to fall into peril so easily. I won’t make you this afraid and worried again!”","Lin Yuan spoke earnestly.","To him, there was no senior he felt closer to than the Moon Empress. She was as important to him as Chu Ci was.","Although Morbius and his own special characteristics could be credited for his growth thus far, the Moon Empress’ involvement had been instrumental as well.","Without the Moon Empress, it was likely that he would have been killed by Cheng Wu.","“Little Yuan, you have already grown up. You are now my shelter and the protector of the main world. But don’t forget that nothing is more important than your safety!”","From Lin Yuan’s words, the Moon Empress felt cared for and looked after. These feelings were both amazing and warming to the Moon Empress.","Mystic Moon was very happy for the Moon Empress when he heard what Lin Yuan said.","He could not help but think of Wen Yu.","Wen Yu’s growth had also far surpassed Mystic Moon’s expectations.","After thinking for a moment, Mystic Moon walked out of the inner palace so he could leave the space to Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress.","All this time, Spring had been watching from the shadows to ensure Lin Yuan’s safety.","She was both thankful and respectful toward the Moon Empress.","She was grateful for the help that the Moon Empress had given Lin Yuan. In a way, it could be said that the Moon Empress had sped up the Saint’s awakening.","Moreover, teachers were respected figures in both the main world and Sky Beyond the Clouds. The Moon Empress would carry the title of ‘Saint’s Teacher’ for the entire life. The title would make her the most venerated figure in the entire Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Once the Moon Empress was certain that Lin Yuan was in perfect health, she began to ask him for details.","“Little Yuan, tell me about the current circumstances in detail. This will make it easier for me to issue orders accordingly.”","Lin Yuan said seriously, “Master, I have killed all the real Eight Pages of Tower Canon. I will be staying in the Radiance Federation for a few days before leaving on a long trip. When I next return to the Radiance Federation, I will organize and collect the resources left by Tower Canon.","“We can safely say that the threat to the main world posed by the Eight Pages of Tower Canon has been fully eliminated. It’s true that the dead spirits crisis persists, but I will send the demon insects to handle it.","“Once the demon insects are done, the dead spirits crisis will no longer have any impact on the lifeforms in the main world. Based on the current quantity of demon insects, there are enough of them to effectively stop the dead dimensional lifeforms from breaching the surface.","“Although there is still death aura in the ley lines, the humans living on the surface will be able to return to the lifestyle they led before the dead spirits crisis broke out.”","Lin Yuan’s words allowed the Moon Empress to gain a complete understanding of the current situation.","For the regular people, the dead spirits crisis had been concluded.","The demon insects’ handling and elimination of the dead spirits would be subsequently carried out in the depths of the underground.","The shift in circumstances caused the Moon Empress to be hit by a wave of realization. From its onset until today, the dead spirits crisis had only been going on for two months.","The Moon Empress had braced herself to lead the Radiance Federation in tackling the dead spirits for a few thousand years. She never expected the dead spirits crisis to be fully suppressed almost immediately after it began!","The Moon Empress remained silent for a moment before asking, “How long will it take the demon insects to clear out the death aura from the ley lines?”","There was no need for Lin Yuan to hide anything from the Moon Empress.","His identity as the Saint would not be confirmed beyond a shadow of a doubt until he went to Epoch God Palace and the Returning Saint Pool enlightened his birth horoscope.","“Master, it will take the demon insects around 200 years to fully treat the environment underground. However, using the demon insects to clear out death aura from the ley lines will leave an impact on the ley lines. Any damage to the ley lines will also be damage to the main world’s potential.","“Luckily, I have a way to clear out death aura from the ley lines without damaging it in any way. If everything goes well, my plan will be complete within two years.”","The Moon Empress was astonished to hear that.","Clearing the death aura was no small feat! The Moon Empress could have never imagined that the death aura could be fully cleared out from the ley lines within two years.","The Moon Empress did not ask Lin Yuan what his methods were. Since Lin Yuan had said it, it meant that his plan was definitely viable!","The Moon Empress still wanted to use the dead dimensional world to train the humans and sea clans. She told Lin Yuan about her thoughts.","Lin Yuan found her idea to be achievable. It was true that using the dead dimensional lifeforms to train the main world’s lifeforms would substantially increase the combat power of the main world’s lifeforms.","At that moment, Spring’s voice appeared in Lin Yuan’s ear, “Lord Saint, Summer will direct the death aura to the vicinity of the Startling Lines Continent. If the crystals formed from the death aura are buried, they will create an area conducive for the dead dimensional lifeforms’ survival.","“It will be easy to create such a training ground. You can extract a portion of the dead world’s roots and inject it into this area to create a territory of death. With the support from the root power, various types of dead dimensional lifeforms can be produced!","“This territory of death can be created both on land and in water to suit your needs. If you intend to create this territory of death, I will send the servants from Epoch God Palace’s Spring Palace to handle this matter.”","Once again, Lin Yuan felt the deep respect and sincerity that Spring held for him.","She was very willing to help him to solve all the problems he encountered.","This behavior meant that Spring had no doubt that he was the Saint!","Since Spring had a very good method to solve his issue, Lin Yuan did not have to come up with a solution on his own.","Instead, he shared Spring’s plan with the Moon Empress.","All the Moon Empress needed to do was to create the territory of death.","Setting up territories of death around the main world would become prime training grounds for the humans, sea clans, and dimensional lifeforms!","Lin Yuan’s mind was not focused on the main world.","The Heavenly Family Cottage and Vast Sea Labyrinth represented the top power of feys. He needed to tell them that Tower Canon had been destroyed.","However, it would be better for the Moon Empress to handle the follow-up tasks.","“Master, I have some things to do back in the Radiance Federation, but I won’t be staying for too long. Before I leave, I will give you a large batch of resources that you can use to develop the Radiance Federation.”","The Moon Empress nodded.","The Moon Empress really wanted Lin Yuan to stay in the Radiant Moon Palace so they could have dinner together. However, Lin Yuan was not the only one who did not have time. The Moon Empress also did not have time to spare.","The Moon Empress was much busier than Lin Yuan.","Half an hour later, she would have to head to the Radiance Federation’s imperial court to deliver this good news.","The main world had indeed entered the sixth epoch, but it was not as filled with hardship as they had anticipated. The initial struggles were about to be gone.","In the future, the bitter struggles would turn into sweet fruits that would nourish the entire main world.","During this half an hour, Lin Yuan told the Moon Empress in detail about what had happened in the past two days, as well as his plans for the main world.","...","When the Moon Empress left for the Radiance Federation’s imperial court, Lin Yuan went to a manor in the north district of the Royal Capital. This manor housed all the spirit qi professionals who were waiting for Lin Yuan to help them with their feys’ breakthroughs.","When Lin Yuan arrived at the manor, he realized that there were far more spirit qi professionals than he had expected!","When a large group of people gathered together, friction was inevitable. This was especially so because these people all came from different factions.","The first thing to greet Lin Yuan was exactly a violent fight.","Seven spirit qi professionals had split into three teams and were fighting each other.","Two of their feys could already change into human form.","This fight between emperor-class experts was being watched by many spirit qi professionals in the manor.","One of them was a burly middle-aged man dressed lavishly, and he bellowed, “Spirit Snake Ravine has gone too far! Don’t assume that you can occupy the four manors just because you have some connections to Coiling Dragon’s Valley! Those four manors have the best positions. Spirit Snake Ravine can only take two of them at the very most. You must hand over the rest!”","Once the burly man was done speaking, an elderly woman dressed in a purple robe said angrily, “Four Beasts Territory is much more overbearing! Not only have you taken over our residence, but you are also trying to steal Spirit Snake Ravine’s residence!","“The residences were specially allocated when we first arrived here. You were given four rooms as well. Everyone knows that the resources are allocated based on the number of rooms. The person in charge of allocating the rooms didn’t allow us to fight amongst each other! Today, we will take back the rooms you stole from us!”","Once this elderly lady was done speaking, the elderly man who represented Spirit Snake Ravine snapped, “What do you mean Spirit Snake Ravine is being overbearing? You need to get one thing right. Four Beasts Territory is the one who first started looking for trouble. Even if we end up brawling, we will never release even a single room to you!","“It’s true that Spirit Snake Ravine works with Coiling Dragon’s Valley, but there are only business ties between us. We are not affiliated with Coiling Dragon’s Valley. Aside from Coiling Dragon’s Valley, we are working with other factions as well.","“Gao Huan, restrain yourself! Don’t forget the reason that we’re all gathered here! If Four Beasts Territory continues to cause trouble, you will definitely be punished!”","The burly middle-aged man scoffed.","“Four Beasts Territory isn’t the only one fighting over the rooms. Don’t you know that there are many factions fighting over the rooms as well? Shouldn’t the factions who are most frequently fighting over the rooms be the ones who receive punishment instead?”","At first, Lin Yuan thought that Four Beasts Territory had started the conflict.","Four Beasts Territory had almost been wiped out by Whale Ocean Commerce and had been left with less than 1/5 of their initial number of experts. Although they had the help of allies, they had already fallen out of the ranks of the top factions.","If Four Beasts Territory was trying to fight for resources, they must want to restore their status as a top faction!","However, if Four Beasts Territory was the only faction that was causing trouble, Lin Yuan would definitely punish them harshly.","But based on what the members of the other factions said, Lin Yuan realized that fighting over the rooms happened frequently in this manor.","Anger bubbled within Lin Yuan.","If his memory was accurate, this manor was being managed by Cultivated Garden."]},{"number":2734,"title":"Chapter 2734 Coiling Dragon’s Valley to the Rescue!","paragraphs":["2734 Coiling Dragon’s Valley to the Rescue!","Cultivated Garden was also in charge of distributing resources to all the factions.","Lin Yuan intended to investigate what plans the manager from Cultivated Garden had. Why was he encouraging the factions to fight and steal rooms from each other?","This was a negative competition that did not benefit the Radiance Federation at all. When the factions fought so viciously with each other, the Radiance Federation’s internal unity was significantly lowered!","This was the last thing that Lin Yuan wanted to see happen, yet it was exactly what was happening.","Lin Yuan had not expected this to happen.","With so many of the Radiance Federation’s factions fighting with each other over the rooms, there was no point in doling out punishment.","Instead of punishing the factions, it was more important that Lin Yuan eliminate the sources of the dispute.","Hence, Lin Yuan took out the Thoughts Letter Paper and sent a message to Tian Feng, the member of royalty who managed Cultivated Garden. Lin Yuan invited Tian Feng to personally come down to the manor in the north district after the imperial meeting.","Lin Yuan had interacted with Tian Feng a few times in the past and knew of his character.","Tian Feng always put the Radiance Federation first.","After the dead spirits crisis began, Tian Feng released a significant portion of his personal resources as part of the aid efforts.","Lin Yuan greatly respected Tian Feng’s actions.","However, the fights in this manor were not a small matter.","Rather than Lin Yuan handling the employees from Cultivated Garden, it would be much more appropriate for Tian Feng to handle this matter!","Tian Feng was currently in the imperial meeting and would not be back anytime soon.","Lin Yuan was in no rush about this matter.","Lin Yuan decided to continue observing the situation in the manor so he could give Tian Feng a detailed explanation when he arrived, and so he could see how the fight over the rooms progressed!","Since the resources were allocated based on the rooms, the employees from Cultivated Garden in charge of the manor were allowing the factions to fight over resources!","Resources directly affected a faction’s foundations.","These factions were willing to spill blood for the sake of building up their foundations!","Since he was going to watch how the fights progressed, Lin Yuan did not reveal himself.","The tension between the people from Spirit Snake Ravine and Four Beasts Territory magnified, and they were on the brink of drawing their swords.","Based on their numbers, Four Beasts Territory seemed stronger than Spirit Snake Ravine.","However, Spirit Snake Ravine had allies.","With help from their allies, they would be able to restrain the people from Four Beasts Territory and cause them to lose manpower.","There were many factions who were spectating the commotion.","Four Beasts Territory and Spirit Snake Ravine did not immediately begin brawling. But this was not just because they were measuring their potential losses but also because they were wary of the spectating factions.","All of the factions were aware of the logic of becoming too preoccupied with a minor issue and failing to recognize a more significant hidden problem.","None of them wanted to be taken over by other factions because they had become too severely injured in this fight over rooms.","The middle-aged man named Gao Huan from Four Beasts Territory cursed to himself when he saw the people from Spirit Snake Ravine resolve themselves to hold onto their rooms.","Spirit Snake Ravine was hedging their bets on him not having the courage to make the move and blow up the matter!","It was true that the experts from the various factions started out peaceful in the first two weeks that they arrived at this manor in the north district of the Royal Capital.","There were very few members of each faction who had come to this manor because only the spirit qi professionals who needed help with their feys’ breakthrough needed to be there.","At first, the members of the various factions all intended to network with each other.","Although they were still able to receive resources daily and the experts from the factions were unwilling to cause trouble when they were unable to call for backup, the Moon Empress eventually started to distribute an abundance of resources to the factions. They were all resources that these factions had never dared to dream of in the past!","These resources caused the spirit qi professionals whose feys’ grades had been restrained to attain breakthroughs.","As a result, more and more experts arrived at the manor, and the experts from the same factions naturally banded together.","When there was a power imbalance between the factions in the manor, the competition for resources emerged.","At first, the factions had been very wary of each other. They were afraid that causing trouble in the manor would displease the manager and cause them to lose their supply of resources.","Aside from power, factions needed craftiness in order to develop.","The leaders of the factions in the manor directed all their craftiness toward the manager of the manor.","As the resources were willingly being given up, the manager of the manor decided to turn a blind eye. It was because of this attitude that the competition gradually became more violent.","Gao Huan had come with a mission.","After Gao Huan told his family about this situation, they instructed him to secure two more rooms.","It had not been long since Four Beasts Territory started rebuilding.","In the past, Four Beasts Territory had been a top faction, but their power was now comparable to some veteran factions. There were even some top-ranked veteran factions who stopped expressing respect toward Four Beasts Territory.","Hence, Four Beasts Territory felt a great urgency to increase their power and use this to prove their position in the Radiance Federation.","With this thought, Gao Huan raised his hand and summoned his fey.","After Gao Huan summoned his fey, the other experts from Four Beasts Territory did the same. The weakest of these feys were Myth Breed, and a number of them were Fantasy Breed.","After Gao Huan instructed the other experts from Four Beasts Territory to summon their feys, the people from Spirit Snake Ravine became nervous and summoned their own feys.","The people who were spectating this commotion were stunned by this shift in events.","If this conflict persisted, the scale would grow too large!","The various factions knew that the Radiance Federation’s royalty did not want the factions to fight each other in deadly brawls. Otherwise, they would not have distributed resources directly but encouraged the factions to compete for them instead!","It was obvious that the members of royalty wanted to increase the overall power of all factions rather than just the power of the top factions.","The manager of the manor was fully responsible for the conflict escalating to this extent.","The manager was permitting such conflict because he wanted to receive a kickback from them.","In the past few months, the manager had received at least tens of billions of Radiance dollars worth of resources.","This manager wanted to obtain a kickback but did not dare to allow the matter to blow up too much. Once it caught the attention of the members of the royalty, the nature of the situation would change.","This manager could not afford to be on the receiving end of the members of royalty’s fury!","This manager was acting this courageously because he knew that the members of royalty were all focused on the dead spirits crisis.","The dead spirits crisis would persist for thousands of years.","As the dead spirits crisis carried on, the members of royalty did not have the bandwidth to pay attention to this matter. Otherwise, regardless of how brave this manager was, he would never dare to do such a thing!","Tian Feng was always very strict when it came to managing Cultivated Garden. Once his actions were discovered, it was highly likely that this manager would be ousted by Tian Feng.","A relatively young man in the crowd said loudly, “Are you really going to throw all caution into the wind to fight? If you anger Lord Mang Shui, both your families will have to pay the consequences! Those who are spectating should just continue watching. Don’t join the fray and end up dragged into the consequences!”","The man’s tone was very serious, and it was clear that he blamed the people from Four Beasts Territory and Spirit Snake Ravine. He made it sound as though their fight would affect all of their profits!","However, the conflict between Four Beasts Territory and Spirit Snake Ravine had already reached a highly sensitive point. Neither side could appear weak now. At that moment, any side that backed down first would become a laughingstock.","Gao Huan was silent for a moment, but he eventually decided to go ahead with the fight.","This was not the first time that Four Beasts Territory was fighting over the rooms.","The one managing this manor was Mang Shui, one of the four envoys of Cultivated Garden.","The previous head of Gao Huan’s family had private ties with Mang Shui and had helped him in the past.","Although Four Beasts Territory’s previous family head had been killed by Whale Ocean Commerce, Mang Shui did not forget about their old ties.","Four Beasts Territory kept up their ties with Mang Shui and had offered him significant benefits in the past month.","Even if this fight displeased Mang Shui, he was more likely to vent his anger on Spirit Snake Ravine.","The only thing about Spirit Snake Ravine that concerned Four Beasts Territory was their relationship with Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","From his observations, Gao Huan noticed that the people in the manor who were from Coiling Dragon’s Valley did not seem to have any intention of helping Spirit Snake Ravine.","Coiling Dragon’s Valley had not interfered during any of Spirit Snake Ravine’s previous clashes against other factions.","This had led Gao Huan to think that Coiling Dragon’s Valley and Spirit Snake Ravine were not as close as he initially imagined.","With this thought, Gao Huan decided to strike first.","A battle broke out in the manor in the north district.","The repercussions of conflict spread out in all directions. But luckily, the experts in the manor were all powerful and would not be overly impacted by the aftermath.","Long Zhuo stood in the crowd with his hands behind his back. His brow was knitted as he watched the confrontation between Four Beasts Territory and Spirit Snake Ravine.","An elderly man who stood by the side hurriedly said, “Young Master, don’t be impulsive! You don’t need to get involved in this fight! You must be aware that this fight will only lead to terrible consequences!","“If the dead spirits crisis wasn’t still ongoing in the main world and occupying the attention of the members of royalty, the manor would already have been tidied up by the authorities! Once this matter gets out, there will be nowhere for Mang Shui to turn. Even Lord Tian Feng will be implicated in Mang Shui’s actions!","“Coiling Dragon’s Valley is currently one of the top three factions in the Radiance Federation. We are standing toe-to-toe with the Cage of Brahma Insects. We have Lord Lin Yuan backing us, and our position is unshakable. We shouldn’t be getting involved in unnecessary conflict!","“If you’re going to act recklessly, I will have to report this to the First Young Master and the head elder of the family!”","This elderly man knew that this fight was akin to a beehive. Poking it would only result in one getting stung. There were no benefits to be reaped at all!","In Coiling Dragon’s Valley, Long Tao was destined to be the Young Leader from the moment he was born. There was no higher position in Coiling Dragon’s Valley than the one he held.","Meanwhile, in spite of his impressive talent, Long Zhuo could not touch Long Tao’s position in the family.","There had been an incident in the past when Long Zhuo tried to rise up and topple Long Tao and suffered because of this transgression. After his failure, Long Tao did not begrudge him. However, Long Zhuo’s position in Coiling Dragon’s Valley was never what it once was or could have been.","If Long Zhuo joined the conflict and blemished Coiling Dragon’s Valley’s reputation, he would have an even tougher time in the Long family. It was possible that he might never be able to become an elder of the family even if he did manage to become an emperor-class expert!","This elderly man was a direct senior of Long Zhuo’s branch of the family. Otherwise, he would never offer Long Zhuo such advice at this moment.","Ever since Coiling Dragon’s Valley became one of the three major factions in the Radiance Federation, their share of the pie of benefits only grew.","As the Young Leader of Coiling Dragon’s Valley, Long Tao received the biggest share of the pie. However, there were enough resources left over to distribute to the other juniors in the family.","There were a fair number of juniors in every branch of the Long family. Once one junior was relegated to being a pariah, the other juniors would be able to receive significantly more resources!","Long Zhuo was able to survive because of his extremely strong combat abilities. Because of this, the family continued to nurture him even after he failed to usurp Long Tao’s position.","The elderly man did not want Long Zhuo to waste his talent, nor did he want his branch of the family to lose such an outstanding junior.","Long Zhuo ignored the elderly man’s cautionary words and snarled, “I might not be the leader of the members of Coiling Dragon’s Valley who have gathered in this manor, but all of you are aware of the goal of resource allocation here in the manor.","“I have told Big Brother Tao about the situation in the manor. He said that if serious conflict breaks out, I should lead the rest of you in putting a stop to it and preventing any further negative effects. Now, you will all go ahead and restrain the people from Four Beasts Territory and Spirit Snake Ravine!”","If Long Zhuo had issued the orders under his own name, those who were present would definitely have ignored him. But now that he had invoked Long Tao’s name, the implications had changed completely!","Since his birth, Long Tao was destined to be the Young Leader of Coiling Dragon’s Valley. He had also taken on a large portion of the responsibilities of the head of the family. His will represented the will of the entire Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","They could not afford to get on the wrong side of Mang Shui, an envoy of Cultivated Garden, but Long Tao could.","But when did Long Zhuo and Long Tao get on such good terms? He had actually communicated with Long Tao privately!","None of the elders from Coiling Dragon’s Valley who were present believed that Long Zhuo could be lying. If he was lying, he would not be able to shoulder the subsequent consequences!","Lin Yuan’s expression of rage did not fade when he saw the reaction of Coiling Dragon’s Valley. Yet, his lips curled into a smile!"]},{"number":2735,"title":"Chapter 2735 Mang Shui’s Wrist!","paragraphs":["2735 Mang Shui’s Wrist!","When Zhao Xiaochun and the other members of the Dragon Gate Guild Club’s main team first encountered Long Tao, they all found him to be strict, cold, and unapproachable. But after spending more time with him, this impression was soon disproven.","Long Tao was strict when it came to carrying out tasks, but he was a very sweet person who always thought about his friends outside of work. This made him seem as though he had a contrasting personality.","Because of this reason, Fang Duoduo and Zhao Xiaochun, who were also members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, felt great affection for their leader.","Long Tao and Lin Yuan first met in the Radiant Moon Palace on Leaning Moon Mountain.","At first, Long Tao had not thought much about Lin Yuan.","The young were susceptible to hubris. This especially applied to Long Tao, who used to be Sequence #3 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","But after meeting on Leaning Moon Mountain, the memory of Lin Yuan was seared into Long Tao’s mind.","Mystic Moon had acted far more familiar and favorable toward Lin Yuan than anyone else.","He and Cheng Rui had been asked to spar with the tea attendants while Lin Yuan became the Moon Empress’ disciple without doing anything.","From this, Long Tao had known that the Moon Empress had been leaning toward Lin Yuan from the start. He and Cheng Rui had just been there to go through the motions.","Despite knowing that Lin Yuan had to be extraordinary to be picked by the Moon Empress, Long Tao still felt indignant and constantly sought out opportunities to compete with Lin Yuan.","Long Tao only became friends with Lin Yuan through his second identity, ‘Black’.","As a young and talented elite, it was difficult for Long Tao to feel respect and admiration for another.","He had only started paying attention to and developing a positive impression of Black because he had saved Millstone Town, which was right outside of Ascending Dragon City.","After Long Tao learned about Millstone Town’s situation, he knew that the insect tide would have devoured the town if Lin Yuan had not been there to protect them. All the residents of the town would have ended up as food for the sea of insects.","This young man had been clearly capable of fleeing but had stayed where he was. Hence, Long Tao had badly wanted the opportunity to get to know Black.","Serendipitously, Chen Hongfeng from the Dragon Gate Guild Club’s reserve team, whom Long Tao always had his eye on, had happened to be matched with Lin Yuan.","It had just so happened that the Dragon Gate Guild Club’s main team had one empty spot to fill, and Long Tao had decided to recruit Black.","At that time, Black had only been beginning to make a name for himself on Star Web and had yet to exhibit any outstanding power. Long Tao had also invited Black with the intention of nurturing him.","As the Young Leader of Coiling Dragon’s Valley and the Dragon Gate Guild Club being one of the top B-level guild clubs, he had many opportunities to join the ranks of A-level guild clubs. Hence, Long Tao had been filled with confidence.","However, Black had turned him down.","Later, Long Tao had led all the members of the Dragon Gate Guild Club to the outskirts of the Royal Capital, where the contained dimensional rifts were located, so they could train.","They had happened to encounter that incident there, and he had also been able to meet Black in real life.","From that battle, Long Tao had gained a full understanding of Black’s power and begun viewing him as a friend.","Otherwise, as one of the top-ranked members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence, Long Tao would never have allowed his dedicated reporter to work with Tian Ningning to hold a press conference to promote Black!","Long Tao and Lin Yuan’s friendship had started from Lin Yuan’s identity as ‘Black’.","Hence, his feelings toward Lin Yuan remained pure even after he learned of Lin Yuan’s true identity.","Subsequently, he received help from Lin Yuan time after time again.","When Lin Yuan produced treasures like the Golden Lotus Brocade Pearls, he had been willing to trade them with Coiling Dragon’s Valley and had allowed Coiling Dragon’s Valley and Dark Clouds Bird Shrine to be the first two factions to get their hands on these resources.","From then on, Coiling Dragon’s Valley developed rapidly.","Coiling Dragon’s Valley could be considered one of the top three factions in the Radiance Federation now because of the foundation they had created with those precious resources.","Lin Yuan had also provided precious resources like the law crystals to help Long Tao’s father and grandfather increase their powers. They also enabled the Long family to produce their first Immortal expert.","It could be said that Lin Yuan was the biggest reason Coiling Dragon’s Valley managed to become one of the top three factions in the Radiance Federation.","Long Tao was well aware of how much Lin Yuan had done for him, and he had always been extremely grateful to Lin Yuan.","But at the same time, he knew that he had no means of being of help to Lin Yuan.","Everyone had friends who were doing better in life. Aside from transferring resources between each other, friends also offered each other genuine relationships.","The members of Coiling Dragon’s Valley who had gone to the manor were reporting the situation in the manor to him.","Long Tao knew that Lin Yuan was currently fully focused on dealing with the dead spirits crisis.","The members of royalty’s attention was also fixated on the dead spirits wave.","The original plan was to hold the Radiance Knight and Radiance Envoy selections immediately after the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection. However, they had been postponed. This made Long Tao aware that something urgent had cropped up.","It was because the members of royalty were not paying attention to the manor in the north district that people like Mang Shui were able to take advantage of the situation and have the audacity to do such things.","There was no way for Long Tao to correct Mang Shui’s way of thinking.","Mang Shui was one of Cultivated Garden’s envoys, and Cultivated Garden was under Tian Feng’s jurisdiction. Hence, Mang Shui possessed a position of a similar level to Zuo Ming and You Zhe of the Spirit Guards.","As long as Mang Shui did not go overboard, Long Tao believed that it would be better to wait for Tian Feng to discover and handle Mang Shui on his own! This way, Tian Feng would not be humiliated, and Coiling Dragon’s Valley would not be negatively implicated.","Given Coiling Dragon’s Valley’s current status, targeting an envoy from Cultivated Garden openly in front of other factions would lead to significant repercussions.","However, as per Lin Yuan’s wishes, Long Tao had picked out one of the members from Coiling Dragon’s Valley who was present in the manor. The person he had selected was Long Zhuo.","Long Tao stressed to Long Zhuo that at the sign of any bloodshed in the manor, he had to step in immediately to put an end to it.","The manor in the north district had been set up at Lin Yuan’s request. Although Cultivated Garden was the one in charge of managing the manor, any incidents would be traced back to Lin Yuan.","As Lin Yuan’s friend, Long Tao did not want Lin Yuan’s reputation to be damaged.","As for his reason for picking Long Zhuo, who had tried to take over his position in the past, it was because Long Tao had decided to concentrate on increasing his own power.","Hence, he planned on nurturing a few close confidants in his family who would replace him in managing Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","Long Zhuo met Long Tao’s requirements in all aspects.","This arrangement was Long Tao’s way of testing Long Zhuo.","Long Tao had seriously discussed his thoughts with Long Zhuo.","Since he was a child, Long Zhuo felt that his fate was an unfair one and had only been trying to claim some authority within Coiling Dragon’s Valley. Now that Long Tao was willing to voluntarily hand over authority to him, Long Zhuo’s desires were satisfied.","Once an ambitious person’s desires were satisfied, he would turn into a handy tool","Long Tao was not worried that Long Zhuo’s desires would grow in the future and that he would become dissatisfied with the power he had been given.","Long Tao would use his feys to control Long Zhuo and the others he picked to ensure that he would retain full control over Coiling Dragon’s Valley even while he was focusing on increasing his individual power.","Hence, Long Tao did not have to be worried when he used Long Zhuo and the rest and he was also willing to invest resources into them.","Apart from from his ambition, Long Zhuo had an upright outlook and had a strong sense of righteousness.","Thus, Long Zhuo was very displeased with Four Beasts Territory trying to use brute force to take the resources of the other factions.","After Long Zhuo issued his order, Coiling Dragon’s Valley’s experts summoned their feys and quickly took control of the conflict.","Gao Huan, who was leading Four Beasts Territory, never expected the people from Coiling Dragon’s Valley to get involved in this fight.","Gao Huan asked fearfully, “What does Coiling Dragon’s Valley mean by this? Are you trying to help Spirit Snake Ravine with whom you have ties?”","The factions present in the manor had complicated relationships. Many of them had ties with each other. This was why they had chosen to keep to themselves at first, and it was rare for a faction to forcefully stand out on behalf of another faction.","If Coiling Dragon’s Valley insisted on coming to Spirit Snake Ravine’s aid, they would be ruining the unspoken rule here.","Before Long Zhuo could speak, a cold voice said from nearby, “It sure is rowdy here! Why are all of you gathered here? Don’t you have anything else to do? There are people supplying you with resources every day. Don’t you know how to use these resources to strengthen and raise your grades?”","The tall and skinny man who spoke was wearing brown attire with green embroidered patterns of flora and fauna. He shot his gaze at the people from Four Beasts Territory and Spirit Snake Ravine first. But he quickly shifted his gaze away to frown at Long Zhuo.","Although he did not say anything, his aura suppressed that of the members of Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","The tall and skinny man was using this demeanor to express his displeasure.","This man was the manager of this manor, one of the envoys from Cultivated Garden – Mang Shui.","If Long Zhuo was facing someone of Mang Shui’s status on his own, he would already be trembling in his boots.","However, he now had the support of Long Tao and the entire Coiling Dragon’s Valley. Hence, he was able to retain his composure even when facing someone of Mang Shui’s outstanding status.","Moreover, Long Zhuo spoke first to Mang Shui, “Lord Mang Shui, you are tasked with managing this manor. Although you are working under Tian Feng’s name, you are actually working for Lord Lin Yuan. You have silently permitted the factions to fight over resources and caused the experts here to all be on guard. The conflict between the factions has escalated. If you don’t properly manage the atmosphere in the manor, issues will probably crop up in the future!”","Mang Shui’s brows were tightly furrowed.","He glared at Long Zhuo while he began to think.","What intentions did this member of Coiling Dragon’s Valley have?","Coiling Dragon’s Valley had to have the support of someone in order to rise to become one of the Radiance Federation’s top three factions.","A trivial member of Coiling Dragon’s Valley like Long Zhuo had to be backed up by someone in order to be brave enough to say such words!","Mang Shui mulled over this. He believed that the Radiance Federation’s members of royalty were unaware of this matter. If they were, he would already have been called out and questioned by Tian Feng!","After pondering further, Mang Shui concluded that Coiling Dragon’s Valley was doing this to threaten him and attempt to obtain profits from him.","Mang Shui had a large amount of resources to allocate, but they could not go into his own profits.","If he could work with Coiling Dragon’s Valley and receive kickbacks from them, he would be able to receive even more resources than he previously could.","Mang Shui decided that it would be better to prevent the problem from growing. He would seek Long Zhuo out for a private negotiation later.","“It’s true that the atmosphere in the manor is worsening. From now on, if any factions want to fight with each other, you are prohibited from getting help from other factions. Any faction that does otherwise will have 30% of their resources docked for the next three months. Today, Spirit Snake Ravine found helpers. Since I only just put this rule in place, I will give them a small punishment as a lesson. I will take back their two rooms and reallocate them in the future! If anyone from Spirit Snake Ravine can’t swallow this arrangement, you can come and see me about it.”","When Lin Yuan, who was hiding in the shadows, heard what Mang Shui said, his brow furrowed deeply.","Mang Shui was adept at seizing opportunities, and it showed through even in his speech.","First, Mang Shui agreed with what Coiling Dragon’s Valley said in order to placate them. Then, he used his new rule to punish Spirit Snake Ravine, who had received help from Coiling Dragon’s Valley, so that he could establish his authority amongst the other factions.","It was likely that he would try to start a conversation with Long Zhuo in private. His attitude then would be a far cry from what it was now.","If Mang Shui really wanted to punish Spirit Snake Ravine, he could have confiscated Spirit Snake Ravine’s resources.","However, Mang Shui was sending hints that Spirit Snake Ravine could seek him out. Clearly, he wanted to obtain under-the-table benefits from them.","At this moment, Lin Yuan received a reply from Tian Feng through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Tian Feng]: Little Yuan, have you arrived at the manor in the north district? Why are you asking me to head there? I have just finished attending the imperial meeting and will be able to arrive at the manor in five minutes at the most. Mang Shui is very capable. If you have any urgent issues, you can let him handle them!","Lin Yuan did not send a reply to Tian Feng’s message. Instead, he stored the Thoughts Letter Paper away.","As the member of royalty in charge of Cultivated Garden, Tian Feng turned out to be a bad judge of character and had caused such a serious issue.","It was likely that this incident would lead Tian Feng to reassess his subordinates.","Lin Yuan prioritized character over abilities.","In this world, people of outstanding character did not lack in abilities either.","At first, after hearing what Mang Shui said, Lin Yuan had been ready to step in.","But since Tian Feng would be able to arrive in five minutes, it would be better to let him handle it personally.","When Long Zhuo heard what Mang Shui said, he silently praised Mang Shui. He had not left anything out in his speech.","It was clear that Mang Shui wanted to change the atmosphere in the manor and take away any reason Long Zhuo could use to target him.","If he continued to target Mang Shui, he would go against Long Tao’s arrangement and cause trouble for the Long family.","Mang Shui had been observing the expressions on Long Zhuo’s face.","When he saw Long Zhuo’s fury subside, Mang Shui changed his tone and said, “Since bad influences have appeared and factions of the likes of Coiling Dragon’s Valley have been made uncomfortable, any faction that causes trouble in the next week will lose a room’s worth of resources. You should all use this incident to reflect!”"]},{"number":2736,"title":"Chapter 2736 Leave it to Iron Prison!","paragraphs":["2736 Leave it to Iron Prison!","A cold streak flashed across Mang Shui’s eyes when he spoke.","This cold glare was not pointed at Long Zhuo and Coiling Dragon’s Valley. However, his words had fully targeted Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","It was clear that Mang Shui’s words were trying to suppress Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","The other factions who were present would definitely aim their anger at losing a portion of resources toward Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","Today’s incident had indeed blown up to slightly too large of a degree. Even Mang Shui felt slightly concerned.","He had already been ready to step in to put an end to the conflict, but the people from Coiling Dragon’s Valley had beaten him to it.","Coiling Dragon’s Valley’s actions were not only a slap to his face as they questioned his ability to manage the manor but also jeopardized his authority in the manor.","If he did not compromise, the factions present would all think he was afraid of Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","This would not be beneficial in his future management of the manor. If he lost his authority and other factions gained the courage to threaten him, he would no longer be able to obtain any resources!","From the beginning, Mang Shui knew that his actions were not right and that he was exploiting a loophole!","At first, he had been very afraid of his actions leading to negative consequences and did not dare to openly encourage the factions to compete with each other.","But once he got a taste of the benefits, his greed tempted him to desire more and more.","As an envoy of Cultivated Garden, Mang Shui was an important figure in the Radiance Federation.","However, he had earned more profits in the past week than he had in the past year.","It was said that valuables could be found in peril. Mang Shui was willing to take on risk for the sake of such wealth!","Hence, Mang Shui stood his ground even against Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","A murderous glare appeared in Lin Yuan’s eyes.","Lin Yuan had not been paying attention to this manor. He had been too preoccupied with tackling Tower Canon and had even put his life on the line in the matter.","Although he had not been focused on the manor, this did not mean he was fine with the current arrangement.","When Lin Yuan told the Moon Empress that he wanted to set up the north district manor, he had stressed that the resources had to be distributed fairly. The resources given to each room daily had to be equal.","Lin Yuan did not remember giving anyone the authority to siphon these resources!","Long Zhuo’s heart sank when he heard what Mang Shui said. He knew Mang Shui was trying to keep Coiling Dragon’s Valley down.","Long Zhuo had already sensed the various factions around him looking at him differently.","Coiling Dragon’s Valley could not back down at such a time.","If Coiling Dragon’s Valley retreated and this impacted the other factions’ profits, this would generate hostility toward Coiling Dragon’s Valley.","This would not be advantageous for Coiling Dragon’s Valley’s future deals with the other factions.","Although Coiling Dragon’s Valley was one of the top three factions in the Radiance Federation, its main business was nurturing dragon species feys and its Creation Master role. Hence, it needed to trade with other factions to obtain resources.","Creation Master resources used to be the most precious resources in the Radiance Federation. But now that Lin Yuan had distributed a large amount of Creation Master resources, the Radiance Federation’s factions were able to receive a large amount of high-class Creation Master resources in a short period of time. Hence, factions with Creation Master roles were all impacted.","Long Tao only told him to stop the conflict in the manor but had not told him to use Coiling Dragon’s Valley to earn the ire of hundreds of factions.","Rather than making the other factions displeased with the Coiling Dragon’s Valley, it would be better to push back against Mang Shui to the end.","There was right and wrong to every matter. Long Zhuo believed that Mang Shui did not have the courage to blow up this matter to too far of an extent. Mang Shui would only suffer once this matter escalated to an uncontrollable degree.","Regardless of how protective Tian Feng was of his own people, he would never protect Mang Shui, who had committed such a grave error!","With this thought, Long Zhuo said something that caused the jaws of everyone present to drop.","“Lord Mang Shui, it’s true that you are the manager of this manor. All of us factions greatly respect you and are willing to support you in your job. I have been keeping a question to myself. Did the members of royalty agree to allow the factions to viciously fight with each other over resources?”","Long Zhuo’s words caused Mang Shui’s expression to become even stormier.","Long Zhuo did not give Mang Shui the chance to speak and continued. “I am even more curious to know if the members of royalty have given you the authority to siphon resources.","“It would be fine if the siphoned resources have been stored away as a form of punishment, but I heard that they had entered your pockets instead. I even heard that you’ve used them to strengthen your feys.”","Long Zhuo’s heart was racing while he spoke.","In the past, he never had the chance to talk back to a figure like Mang Shui.","However, as a disciple of the Long family, Long Zhuo needed to make the best decision for Coiling Dragon’s Valley regardless of how nervous he was.","Long Zhuo did not have to care about how much his words impacted Mang Shui.","When Mang Shui targeted Coiling Dragon’s Valley, he did not leave Coiling Dragon’s Valley with a foot to stand on.","All the factions who were present knew what Mang Shui was doing. However, none of them expected Long Zhuo to lay it all out bare. Long Zhuo’s words had left Mang Shui fully and publicly vulnerable.","For Coiling Dragon’s Valley to have the confidence to take on Mang Shui, they had to have a source of support.","It was not wise to cross an envoy of Cultivated Garden!","When Mang Shui heard what Long Zhuo said, his face turned red, then white. Even after a few moments had passed, no response fell from his lips.","Regardless of how daring Mang Shui was, he would never dare to claim publicly that Tian Feng had given him the authority to siphon resources.","It would be fine if he had not already spent the resources because he could just replace them. Alas, he had already spent all of them and could not replace them even if he wanted to.","Previously, Mang Shui wanted to teach Coiling Dragon’s Valley a lesson. He had not expected Coiling Dragon’s Valley to fight back so strongly against him.","He was momentarily flummoxed about how to go on from here.","At this moment, an angry and authoritative voice resonated from above the manor, “Mang Shui, have you forgotten what I told you when I sent you here to the manor?”","When he heard this voice, Mang Shui trembled, and his head snapped upward. This was when he saw a heavy-set elderly man looking at him with utter disappointment.","Mang Shui squeaked, “Your Excellency Tian... Tian Feng, you...”","When Tian Feng heard Mang Shui address him, he growled, “Don’t call me Your Excellency. Because of your actions, I am too humiliated to receive such a greeting. Tell me! What did I tell you when I gave you this assignment?”","The five envoys of Cultivated Garden were Tian Feng’s closest subordinates. They had been with him for decades.","Although Mang Shui had not been with him for the longest time, he had the most well-rounded capabilities and was the most clever.","But now, it was evident that Mang Shui had used his cleverness in all the wrong places.","Not only had Mang Shui broken his trust, but he had also damaged his reputation.","Tian Feng’s anger was not strongly linked to the fact that Mang Shui had hurt his image. It was more so that Tian Feng felt that he had failed to recognize character, let down the Moon Empress’ trust in him, and wasted the resources Lin Yuan had provided to the Radiance Federation.","Just like how Mang Shui did not know how to answer Tian Feng, the latter did not know how to answer the Moon Empress and Lin Yuan.","Mang Shui recovered from his shock.","He knew Tian Feng’s personality well. Unless he managed to find a reasonable explanation, there was no way that Tian Feng would let him off.","Alas, even after racking his brain, Mang Shui was unable to come up with an explanation for himself.","When Tian Feng saw that Mang Shui still had yet to reply to him, a tangible pressure and lethal force enveloped Mang Shui, breaking Mang Shui’s train of thought.","Mang Shui gnashed his teeth. “You told me to allocate resources fairly and prevent the factions from fighting over resources. You also said to watch over the people in the north manor and restrain anyone who tries to increase their feys’ powers on their own.”","The members of the factions who were present had not expected Tian Feng to come to the manor, much less see him needle one of his own envoys from Cultivated Garden.","When the people present heard what Mang Shui said, they understood why Tian Feng was this incensed.","Tian Feng’s fury was valid. Mang Shui had fully gone against what Tian Feng had asked for. It could be said that he had done the complete opposite.","Tian Feng had told Mang Shui to remain fair and prevent arguments from taking place. Yet, for the sake of his selfish desires, Mang Shui had instigated fights and unjust happenings.","Tian Feng looked at Mang Shui with narrowed eyes and was silent for a moment. Then, he proceeded to ask Mang Shui why he had done what he had done, punctuating each word.","When Mang Shui heard what Tian Feng said, his throat closed, and he prepared to beg for mercy.","Tian Feng was emotional and especially had a soft spot for his old subordinates.","But before Mang Shui could speak, a light and pleasant voice rang out from beside Tian Feng, “Tian Feng, the result of this matter is already clear. You don’t need to ask for a reason.”","Everyone present instinctively lifted their heads and saw a young man standing behind Tian Feng.","This young man had a calm expression, but his eyes were betraying the absolute deadly intent that he was actually feeling.","This young man was Lin Yuan, who had just become Sequence #1 of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","The regular people in the Radiance Federation might not be aware of the extent of Lin Yuan’s achievements. Still, the factions all knew that Lin Yuan was the one who had enabled the fusing of the main world with the dimensional worlds.","They also knew that he was the one who was protecting the lifeforms in the main world and fending off the dead spirits crisis. All of them were only able to receive resources here in this manor because of Lin Yuan.","It could be said that Lin Yuan was the protector of the main world and had every right to stand next to Tian Feng. In fact, he even deserved to stand in front of Tian Feng!","However, Lin Yuan maintained the respect he felt for Tian Feng.","This made Lin Yuan seem even more respectful and well-mannered!","Tian Feng did not sense Lin Yuan’s aura when he arrived and did not expect Lin Yuan to have arrived at the mansion long ago.","Tian Feng had come to the manor because of the message he had received from Lin Yuan.","It was likely that Lin Yuan was already present in the manor when he sent the message.","Lin Yuan had not stepped in to put a stop to the conflict out of consideration of his pride. He wanted to give him the chance to deal with Mang Shui on his own.","Mang Shui’s error was far grievous. He could only erase his mistake by personally eliminating Mang Shui.","Tian Feng was very thankful for the consideration Lin Yuan was showing him.","Frankly, Tian Feng could guess the reasons for Mang Shui’s actions. It was because he had succumbed to the temptation of the mountain of resources at his fingertips.","He had also taken advantage of the calamity that was the dead spirits crisis to exploit a loophole.","His actions were beyond deplorable.","While everyone was trying their best to increase the Radiance Federation’s power, Mang Shui was a parasite that was trying to empty out the Radiance Federation.","At the instant that a deadly glare appeared in Tian Feng’s eyes, he decided to end Mang Shui.","He had asked for Mang Shui’s reasons because he wanted to hear an explanation. It was to express how wholly disheartened he was.","Tian Feng turned to look at Lin Yuan and was about to bow to express his apology when he saw Lin Yuan bow respectfully to him like a junior would to a senior. Then, Lin Yuan shook his head gently.","A few of the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s spores landed on Tian Feng, and Lin Yuan spoke to him through the spores.","“Uncle Feng, everyone experiences a failure of judgment at times. Aside from Mang Shui, it’s no one else’s fault that he fell to temptation and made such a decision. It has nothing to do with you, so you don’t need to blame yourself too much!","“Now that we’ve arrived at the tail end of the dead spirits crisis, you will need to continue helming Cultivated Garden!”","Lin Yuan understood why Tian Feng blamed himself.","The respect that Lin Yuan felt for Tian Feng was sincere.","Firstly, Tian Feng had been working hard for the sake of the Radiance Federation’s development and had even sacrificed a large portion of his own wealth.","Lin Yuan would also feel crushing sadness if he had misjudged someone.","However, he did not want Tian Feng to lose self-confidence over this incident.","It was impossible for Tian Feng to miss Lin Yuan’s meaning.","Tian Feng patted Lin Yuan’s shoulder and hissed to Mang Shui, “Mang Shui, I will be handing you over to Iron Prison, and he will be dealing with you personally. Your actions have made you worse than the dead spirits. You must pay the price for your greed!”","A sprig of fresh branches appeared from behind Tian Feng. The branches extended towards Mang Shui and encased him.","Iron Prison was the most terrifying member of royalty to all the factions of the Radiance Federation. He managed the prison, and the Sin Cleansing Pool was also under his jurisdiction.","If Tian Feng handed Mang Shui over to Iron Prison, he would likely end up buried under the Sin Cleansing Weeping Willow after serving his punishment.","Later, the Radiance Federation would send out an announcement about Mang Shui’s sentencing.","When Tian Feng restrained Mang Shui immediately after arriving, the other factions present realized that Tian Feng had been aware of Mang Shui’s wicked deeds.","Tian Feng had been instructing Cultivated Garden to issue resources to the regular people in the Radiance Federation to prevent the Radiance Federation from collapsing due to a lack of influx of resources.","Although this incident was related to Tian Feng’s arrangement, his present actions allowed Tian Feng to win back the respect of all the factions present.","Tian Feng used his sacred source lifeform to lock up Mang Shui and did not give Mang Shui any opportunity to come up with excuses.","Lin Yuan escorted Tian Feng out. After Tian Feng left, Lin Yuan was in no hurry to depart. Instead, he flashed himself next to Long Zhuo."]},{"number":2737,"title":"Chapter 2737 Lin Yuan’s Enormous Harvest!","paragraphs":["2737 Lin Yuan’s Enormous Harvest!","When Lin Yuan first came to this world, he was a regular person who was familiar with the dark and warm sides of the world. He did not have the attitude of an elite at all.","But as he continued to grow, he established and became the leader of Sky City. Eventually, he started protecting the entire main world.","In spite of his young age, he already gave off the pressure that usually came from an elite leader.","Elite leaders needed to know when to reward and punish appropriately.","Mang Shui had paid an excruciating price for his greed.","Long Zhuo and the rest of Coiling Dragon’s Valley would receive rewards from Lin Yuan because of their decision.","Long Zhuo and the other experts from Coiling Dragon’s Valley hurriedly bowed to Lin Yuan.","Long Zhuo almost lost strength in his legs and ended up kneeling in front of Lin Yuan. He did not feel such pressure even from his grandfather, an Immortal expert.","Although they were nervous, Long Zhuo and the other experts from Coiling Dragon’s Valley knew that he was not here to reproach Coiling Dragon’s Valley but to reward them.","The people present all knew that Lin Yuan was fully responsible for Coiling Dragon’s Valley being able to enjoy its current glory.","Lin Yuan shifted his gaze away from Long Zhuo and the other members of Coiling Dragon’s Valley to the other experts who were present.","Next, Lin Yuan said seriously, “Mang Shui used to manage this place. You all just heard Tian Feng’s expectations assigned to Mang Shui. The latter was the one who took it upon himself to fall to his selfish desires and breed a negative environment of stealing and fighting.","“In the future, someone new will come to this manor to lay down the rules for all of you.","“Coiling Dragon’s Valley stopped this commotion from getting out of hand and prevented bloodshed. I am going to give Coiling Dragon’s Valley 1,000 heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls! I hope that there will be no more fights over resources in the manor from now on!","“Mang Shui has paid for all the previous mistakes. If anything similar happens again, the factions causing the problems will lose the right to continue obtaining resources! It goes without saying that without resources, you will not need to continue remaining in this manor!”","Lin Yuan nodded at Long Zhuo before rising into the air.","With a wave of his hand, the Abyss Great Emperor appeared next to him.","Lin Yuan landed on the Abyss Great Emperor’s palm.","“I came here to help all of you to break through your grades. Once I’m done and you leave this manor, make sure to relay my words to your families!","“I am providing so many resources to you without asking for repayment because I want to bolster the Radiance Federation’s overall power and enable us to work together to take on any crises that arise in the future.","“I don’t want the resources to cause you to fight amongst yourselves and erode the power that we put so much effort into building up!”","Lin Yuan was still a young man. He was still a ways away from becoming a real adult. Nonetheless, no one questioned his might.","Even Mang Shui who Tian Feng had just dragged away to the Sin Cleansing Pool had supplied Lin Yuan with faith power in the past and was considered one of his believers.","A large portion of the people present already regarded Lin Yuan as their faith.","Long Zhuo had just received a reward from Lin Yuan and said bravely, “Lord Lin Yuan, how will we overcome the World Cleansing?”","Lin Yuan activated Morbius’ Pure Land of Bliss, and a large sea of white sand appeared below the manor.","Lin Yuan declared loudly, “Every person stepping on the sand and is within the sea of white sand will be sending their feys to undergo the World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation together.”","Lin Yuan’s words astonished everyone present.","The World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation were all disasters for feys and caused the deaths of many feys.","The same went for spirit qi professionals.","Many spirit qi professionals chose to join large factions because they were unable to handle their feys’ World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation on their own.","Rather than saying that they were seeking the protection of these large factions, they were hoping that the experts in the factions would help their feys to overcome the World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation to enable their feys’ qualities and grades to evolve.","Every expert saw such difficult trials as requiring a careful approach.","Yet, Lin Yuan was going to help these Myth Breed and Creation Breed feys to evolve all at once!","The sea of white sand expanded, and there were at least tens of Myth Breed and more than ten Creation Breed feys within the sea of sand.","The World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation’s overlapping forces were beyond the imagination of those who were present!","However, no one doubted Lin Yuan’s words. Instead, they did what Lin Yuan said and triggered the World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation.","A hundred holes appeared in the sky.","The terrifying scene in the sky rivaled that of the dead spirits crisis.","Various types of World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation descended from the sky.","Just as the experts from the various factions thought that they were about to be destroyed by these forces, they saw the demon Lin Yuan was standing on lash out a whip of fire.","The flames and wind from the whip decimated the energy within the World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation.","The whip of flames absorbed the energy within the World Cleansings and Trials of World Creation before channeling all the energy into the Abyss Great Emperor’s body.","As an Afterlife Realm Dictator, these Myth Breed and Creation Breed level attacks were a piece of cake.","The World Graces and Creation World Ley Lines fell from the holes in the sky and nourished the newly evolved feys.","Because of the Pure Land of Bliss, Lin Yuan collected a mountain of spirit qi crystals and golden ley line pearls.","Lin Yuan had severely underestimated the number of experts in the manor.","Although Lin Yuan was evolving them in groups, he ended up staying at the manor for three days.","Spring watched Lin Yuan silently, her presence practically nonexistent.","As Spring watched Lin Yuan use the Pure Land of Bliss to accumulate resources, nostalgia appeared in her eyes.","It was as though she was looking past Lin Yuan into the eons that had already passed until she stopped on a certain stalwart figure.","Spring’s expression was usually as cold as ice as the seemingly never-ending days passed.","But ever since she discovered Lin Yuan, the smile had yet to leave her face.","Spring and Summer already told Lin Yuan that he could make whatever decisions he wanted without worrying or rushing.","Ever since they confirmed that Lin Yuan was the Saint, Spring and Summer would be willing to silently and steadfastly wait by his side even if he wanted to remain in the Radiance Federation for the next few decades.","In the few days that Lin Yuan spent evolving experts’ feys in the manor, Iron Prison sentenced Mang Shui for his actions.","While he was sentencing Mang Shui, Iron Prison’s expression became increasingly stony.","Iron Prison thought, It’s a good thing that Lin Yuan has put an end to the dead spirits crisis so we no longer have to be distracted by it. Otherwise, Mang Shui’s actions would cause unimaginable impacts.","As time passed, the conflicts would morph into resentment and become irreparable. It would be too late to try and fix things then!","Mang Shui had interacted with Iron Prison many times. Iron Prison’s impression of Mang Shui was that he was a very principled person.","It was because Mang Shui was so principled and detailed that he managed to catch the attention of someone as strict and intolerable as Tian Feng!","Based on Mang Shui’s actions, there was no need to imprison him in the Sin Cleansing Pool. People like him did not deserve to live.","Iron Prison icily glared at Mang Shui before asking, “Mang Shui, when you were acting based on your greed, did you ever stop to think that you would end up in this state?”","Iron Prison felt his heart grow cold when he saw that Mang Shui was only begging for mercy and had not once admitted to his mistakes.","His hand turned into a dagger, and he chopped Mang Shui into two.","The Sin Cleansing Weeping Willow sensed the blood and twisted its roots around Mang Shui’s body.","The blood stained the Sin Cleansing Pool red.","Slowly, the red was dissolved in the pool, returning to its usual clarity.","Mang Shui’s actions had given Iron Prison the answer he was looking for. Mang Shui had not thought about the consequences at all!","This was because Mang Shui never expected the dead spirits crisis to come to an end so abruptly.","All Mang Shui did was take advantage of the crisis for his own personal benefit.","A person like this repulsed Iron Prison. But at the same time, Iron Prison felt reminded that as a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty, he needed to open his eyes to clearly assess anyone he tasked with important assignments!","Lin Yuan did not immediately check on his resources after helping all the experts in the manor to evolve their feys’ grades and qualities.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope, who managed the Spirit Lock spatial zone, would organize and check the resources in his stead.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope ate heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls daily. Hence, its ability to control wind elements grew stronger, and it could organize resources more quickly.","After a discussion with the Moon Empress, Lin Yuan decided not to just inject resources into the Radiance Federation.","The entire main world had received resources from Lin Yuan.","Hence, the human federations, sea clans, and Heavenly Family Cottage all had experts who were ready to evolve.","By providing the main world with resources, Lin Yuan constantly planted fruit trees. The trees would continuously mature and bear fruits that Lin Yuan would eventually harvest.","Lin Yuan had received many more times the resources that he had ever received in the past.","Lin Yuan had not been supplying resources to the main world for long. He was only just getting started.","After the dead spirits crisis was quelled and the lifeforms in the main world no longer had to worry about the dead spirits, the main world would enter a stage of rapid development.","Before Lin Yuan left the main world, the main world would be like a treasure trove that he could constantly draw resources from.","Compared to other lifeforms, humans had very short lifespans. However, in their fleeting lifespans, they could create unimaginable value. As time progressed, human experts distinguished themselves time after time again.","Lin Yuan was in no rush to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Instead, he intended to remain in the main world for some time so he could nurture more experts for the main world. This would be his way of making one last contribution to the main world’s prosperity before he left.","On the way back to the Radiance Federation, Lin Yuan conversed in depth with Spring.","He learned that Epoch God Palace had a path to the Sky Beyond the Clouds that could be opened at any time. However, once they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he could not return to this main world again!","The resources in this main world would become Lin Yuan’s capital when he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Hence, his investments into the main worth would bring equitable returns!","However, Lin Yuan was not only supplying such a large amount of resources to the main world for his own sake.","After traveling to various areas in the main world to gather resources, Lin Yuan would come up with a plan of action.","During his journey, he would meet with Liu Jie and Wen Yu.","Nothing else in the main world could threaten Keira and the demon insects.","Rather than sending Liu Jie and Wen Yu to manage the demon insects, it would be better to instruct Keira to release the female insects with Class 1 Genetic Locks. Using the female insects with Class 1 Genetic Locks to manage the alien insects would be much more convenient.","After releasing Liu Jie and Wen Yu of such responsibilities, they could help Lin Yuan develop an effective strategy for organizing the dimensional worlds.","Lin Yuan would definitely be strengthening the bond between the main world and dimensional worlds before he left the main world.","The Moon Empress had entered her busiest phase. She was even busier than when the dead spirits crisis had first begun.","The main world could currently be described as an environment containing numerous tasks that were waiting to be addressed.","After the Moon Empress was assured of Lin Yuan’s safety, there was nothing for her to worry about.","She could communicate with Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper in her spare time.","Traveling all over the main world did not make Lin Yuan tired at all. Rather, he was filled with a sense of extreme satisfaction.","It could be said that Lin Yuan harvested a mountain of resources wherever he went.","The Moon Empress helped Lin Yuan to collate all the resources he had supplied to the main world and told him about the resources in a message on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Lin Yuan came to a conclusion with his rough calculations.","With every unit of resources he invested, he obtained 67 times the returns. This meant that every spirit qi crystal he invested would lead to 67 spirit qi crystals worth of profits.","This gave Lin Yuan even more resources to invest in the main world.","Lin Yuan could spend spirit qi crystals freely to evolve his feys and raise his overall power.","He could try to evolve all his feys to the World Emperor and divine kingdom level before he left for the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth was helping Lin Yuan to gather experts from the sea clans who were ready to break through.","Lin Yuan would have to stay here for some time.","He decided to use this opportunity to increase the Perfect Touch Wisteria’s power.","Due to its ability, Green Vine’s grade had no limits.","If Lin Yuan invested his copious resources into Green Vine, it would be able to reach World Emperor grade and divine kingdom level.","With this thought, Lin Yuan summoned Green Vine.","Ever since Green Vine made contact with the human world, it gained a preference for doing activities in its human form.","Green Vine knew that Lin Yuan would help it evolve its grade. It was so excited that it started to cling and paw lovingly at Lin Yuan. Once it was sated, Green Vine returned to its original form."]},{"number":2738,"title":"Chapter 2738 Honor Absent Palace Above All!","paragraphs":["2738 Honor Absent Palace Above All!","Green Vine’s current body could be described as sky-encompassing. Its eight vines seemed to form a cage around the sky.","This was especially so for the vines that used Swallow Same Source to consume entities far beyond Green Vine’s level. Thus, Green Vine’s might completely surpass that of a Sovereign X/Eternal XII lifeform!","The vine that had absorbed the five golden snake scales was swinging above the others, its serpentine shape looming over the ground.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Green Vine.","[Fey Name]: Perfect Touch Wisteria","[Fey Species]: Strong armor wisteria species/long wisteria species","[Fey Grade]: High Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Eternal XII","Abilities:","[Forbidden Growth]: After contracting any lifeform, it can break the limit that comes with the contract. As long as it has sufficient energy, it will be able to continuously increase its power. When it has absorbed the maximum amount of energy, it will be able to comprehend a required Willpower Rune.","[Peak Sturdiness]: A large amount of the absorbed energy can be used up to increase the durability of the vines. When injured, the energy can also be used to repair the vines.","[Long Vine Application]: Choose two vines that will be applied to one vine. The vine with the two vines applied on it will be able to gain the two vines’ abilities.","[Paralyzing Vine Sap]: When damage is sustained, the vine sap with paralyzing effects can be sprayed out from the wound.","[Brutally Pushing Out of Soil]: When faced with the opponent’s defenses, the seeds’ sprouting strength can be activated to help to break past the opponent’s defenses.","[Root’s Parasitic Restraints]: Pick a target and the target’s body will become soil where roots will grow. The roots will absorb the target’s vitality to cause harm to the target.","[Splitting Illusionary Spikes]: When the illusionary spikes pierce a target’s body, the illusionary spikes will turn into a seed that will germinate in the target’s body and produce even more illusionary spikes.","[Avoidance Wedge]: Every time the Perfect Touch Wisteria is injured, a wedge will grow over its surface. Every three layers will turn into a sharp spike that will be able to increase the vines’ effects while boosting them.","[Combined Vines Defense]: Pick a target to apply to and help it to defend against external attacks. The Perfect Touch Wisteria’s own vitality will be sacrificed to protect the target it is applied to.","Exclusive Skill:","[Swallow Same Source]: Every vine will have the same grade and quality, but they can be separated to act as individual entities. Every vine can consume something and take control of its attributes. The swallowed entity cannot be spat out, but an even higher-level item can replace it. (Once it gains attributes, the vine cannot be separated again.)","[Broken Vine Replacement]: When a vine is destroyed during combat, another vine can be picked to take on the damage instead to save the first vine.","[Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn]: The energy within the vines can be gathered at a certain spot. An illusionary thorn composed of energy will sprout from this spot. The illusionary thorn will be undetectable.","[Tactile Vine Wood World]: All of the wood-type energy and vitality stored within the vines will be released. The wood-type energy and vitality will transform into a large number of vines. The vines will intertwine and form a world of vines. The main body will fuse with this world to attack targets. Before the wooden world is broken, all the damage sustained by the main body will be reduced and shouldered by the wooden world.","[Entire Body Medium]: Sacrifice the item that the vine had absorbed and release the source of the item through a medium. The released source will not have any knowledge but will possess all of its original power. (Compare the proportion of energy that the source comprises of within the item to determine how long the released source will be able to remain outside.)","[Vine Tempering Garrotte]: Use the long vines to garrotte other lifeforms. If the target’s bloodline is more elite than that of the Perfect Touch Wisteria, it can absorb the target’s bloodline to strengthen its own bloodline. This will also strengthen every vine that has absorbed an entity through Swallow Same Source.","After sensing Green Vine and the aura of the vine, Spring materialized next to Lin Yuan and asked with narrowed eyes, “Lord Saint, where did you find these five snake scales? The Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake’s secret treasure shouldn’t exist in this world!”","Spring would not question Lin Yuan if he had obtained five of the Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake’s scales. However, the Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake’s secret treasures were completely different from its scales.","Divine-kingdom experts produced the secret treasures by tempering their root power and faith power.","The secret treasures were as important to divine-kingdom experts as sacred source lifeforms were to Class 1 world experts. Many divine-kingdom experts would rather die than let their secret treasures go.","Ignoring the fact that a divine kingdom Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake would never appear in a Class 1 world to start with, it was also impossible for it to appear in a Class 1 world that had promoted to Class 2!","Lin Yuan’s world was part of the East Universe, which was under Honor Absent Palace’s rule.","There was no way that she would be unaware of a Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake arriving in the main world!","The only possibility was that this Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake was an inspector in charge of supervising the lower worlds. For some reason, this inspector had taken advantage of his assignment from Honor Absent Palace and released his own secret treasures into this world in order to spy on it.","The most likely event from the past few centuries to catch the inspector’s eye was the birth of the faeries!","The thought caused fury to burgeon in Spring’s eyes.","They had locked themselves in Epoch God Palace all this time because they were worried about affecting Lord Saint’s awakening.","But the divine-kingdom expert from Honor Absent Palace went so far as to release his own secret treasures!","The consequences would have been unthinkable if Lord Totem God had not been sufficiently awakened and failed to absorb these secret treasures!","The anger in Spring’s eyes allowed Lin Yuan to sense her concern for him.","All this time, Lin Yuan had been unaware of what the five dark golden scales were. Apparently, they were the Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake’s secret treasures!","Given that Spring had a name for the five snake scales, it was clear that she was well acquainted with them.","When he was with Spring, Lin Yuan did not need to keep his guard up and could ask her whatever questions he had. She would never hide anything from him. If she wanted to keep secrets from him, she would not have appeared and brought up the Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake!","“Spring, I don’t know much about the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Can you tell me about how the Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake is viewed in the Sky Beyond the Clouds?”","Spring hurriedly replied, “Lord Saint, the Sky Beyond the Clouds is just a colloquial name. It refers to the area under the North, South, East, and West Universes. This world you’re in is located in the East Universe. If this world and its seas are together compared to the East Universe, this Class 2 world is like a drop of water in the sea!”","Spring had chosen her metaphor intentionally. She wanted to give Lin Yuan a proper understanding of the Sky Beyond the Clouds and was not exaggerating in the slightest.","When Lin Yuan heard what Spring said, he could not prevent shock from blooming on his face.","He had asked Fifth Page Falling Rainbow and Keira about the Sky Beyond the Clouds. However, they were restricted by their levels and did not have a comprehensive understanding of the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","But from what Spring said, Lin Yuan now truly understood its vastness!","“Aside from the North, South, East, and West Universes that make up the Sky Beyond the Clouds, countless abyssal domains surround the Sky Beyond the Clouds. These abysses are much larger than the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Innumerable species hide in the abysses and attack the Sky Beyond the Clouds often.","“If you head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds from this Class 2 world, you will end up directly in the East Universe. In the East Universe, Honor Absent Palace stands above all the other factions.","“Based on these secret weapons, this Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake has already reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom. A figure like that is trivial in Honor Absent Palace but is considered a notable expert in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!”","After hearing this, Lin Yuan gained a thorough understanding of the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ circumstances.","This was the first time that he was hearing the names of factions from there.","Based on Spring’s expression and tone, Lin Yuan could tell that these five dark gold snake scales should never have appeared in this world.","However, these five dark gold snake scales had helped him significantly! He saw them as his final killing move.","Lin Yuan could use Green Vine’s Entire Body Medium to summon the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake. When its secret treasures were used as the source for the summoning, the Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake could be maintained for a very long time.","However, Lin Yuan had not expected First Page Crimson to have such a strong ambushing ability.","If Crimson had not ambushed him, Lin Yuan would have considered using the five dark gold snake scales to summon the Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake through Entire Body Medium during the battle.","Spring did not tell Lin Yuan about her plans.","Once they went to the East Universe, Spring was going to pay a visit to Honor Absent Palace.","If not for Lord Saint, two of the Sky Beyond the Clouds’s four universes would have been destroyed back then. The East Universe would have been one of the two destroyed universes!","Lin Yuan longed to gain more information on the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","He possessed the mermaid thearch bloodline, and it just so happened that he could ask Spring about the mermaids and Blood species.","Before evolving from Sovereign X/Eternal XII to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, Green Vine needed to cross two large levels in the form of the birth-horoscope and spirit-fire levels.","Even if it was constantly supplied with resources, this process would still take considerable time!","Lin Yuan waved over two king-class mermaids in the distance.","After being called over by a mermaid thearch, these two king-class mermaids anxiously bowled in front of Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan instructed the two king-class mermaids to carry over the spirit qi crystals he had prepared for Green Vine.","Lin Yuan summoned chest after chest filled with spirit qi crystals that the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope had organized. There were about 10,000 spirit qi crystals in each chest.","After Morbius evolved to Suzerain/Myth, the amount of spirit qi in each spirit qi crystal multiplied by many times!","The two king-class mermaids’ bodies trembled with excitement. They never imagined that they would be picked by Lin Yuan and given the chance to serve him.","King-class mermaids were the equivalent of Turning Wheel Realm Dictators. They had a similar magnitude of power to birth-horoscope experts.","The two of them could handle the task of feeding resources to the evolving Green Vine!","Lin Yuan asked Spring seriously, “You say that I’m the Saint. You should be able to sense that aside from the human bloodline, I possess the mermaid bloodline in my body. Is there anything you can tell me about the mermaids and Blood species? I am very interested in them!”","It went without saying that Spring could sense the mermaid bloodline in Lin Yuan’s body.","In the past, she did not think much of the mermaid species. It was only after she discovered the mermaid bloodline in Lin Yuan’s body that her opinion of the mermaid bloodline improved.","Spring was already certain that Lin Yuan was the Saint.","Aside from sensing Morbius’ aura, Lin Yuan’s physique was another point of consideration.","His body did not absorb spirit qi from the environment when he circulated spiritual power. Instead, he could purify the spirit qi.","This body composition fit with Lord Saint’s ‘Body of All Spirits’.","However, Lin Yuan only exhibited the preliminary version of the Body of All Spirits.","The Saint who possessed the Body of All Spirits could absorb any bloodline into his own bloodline, as well as evolve the various bloodlines at will.","Rather than saying that Lin Yuan possessed the mermaid bloodline, it was more accurate to say that the mermaid bloodline was blessed to be evolved in his body!","Although Spring remained by Lin Yuan’s side, she could not reveal much about his affairs.","Luckily, Lin Yuan had specifically asked about the mermaid and Blood species’ bloodlines. She could give him a detailed description of them.","“Lord Saint, there are different Species Rankings in the four universes. The Mermaid and Blood species are on three of the Species Rankings. In the West Universe’s ranking, the mermaids rank much higher than the Blood species.","“But in the North Universe’s ranking, the Blood species ranks above the mermaids. In the East Universe, their rankings are very competitive! The mermaid bloodline in your body should have come from a branch of the East Universe’s mermaids.”","Spring paused before continuing. “In my opinion, the Blood species’ bloodline is deadlier than the mermaids’. However, the mermaids control the seas. They are the only bloodline that can stand toe-to-toe against the faeries!","“However, unlike the Blood species, the mermaids aren’t keen on expanding and prefer to enjoy their days in the beautiful seas. Hence, most of the battles between the mermaids and Blood species are started by the Blood species.","“In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, your mermaid thearch bloodline will be able to advance with ease.”","Spring did not say this because it was easy to evolve the mermaid bloodline but because she trusted the composition of Lin Yuan’s body."]},{"number":2739,"title":"Chapter 2739 Domain Mountain-Class!","paragraphs":["2739 Domain Mountain-Class!","Otherwise, there was no way for Lin Yuan’s bloodline to improve to such a degree in such a short span of time in this world that lacked the mermaid bloodline!","Currently, the only bloodline that Lin Yuan had absorbed was the mermaid bloodline.","When he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and encountered other species, he would probably be able to absorb their bloodlines!","If the bloodline in Crimson’s body had been pure, Spring would likely have hinted to Lin Yuan to try taking control of the Blood species’ bloodline.","Normally, once a lifeform absorbed the bloodlines of more than two species, the two bloodlines would definitely clash in their body, creating an explosion that resulted in the death of that lifeform. It was impossible for a body to handle two bloodlines repelling each other.","However, Lin Yuan’s Body of All Spirits could smoothly carry and absorb various bloodlines.","Not only would the bloodlines not clash against each other in his body, but they would even bolster each other and lead to links and positive reactions.","Hence, absorbing the bloodlines of multiple bloodlines in his body only had upsides for Lin Yuan!","The most impressive part of the Body of All Spirits was that Lin Yuan could use the bloodline as an energy source when he wanted to abandon the bloodline. He could sacrifice the bloodline for a similar one and help the new bloodline to evolve. As a result, his previous effort into nurturing the first bloodline would not go to waste.","Aside from being curious about the mermaid and Blood species’ bloodlines, Lin Yuan was also curious about the Abyssal Beast bloodline Spring had mentioned.","Crimson had almost successfully ambushed him because he possessed the Abyssal Beast bloodline! If Spring and Summer had not stepped in in the nick of time to protect him, Lin Yuan could not say for certain how the battle would have ended.","“Spring, you recognized the Abyssal Beast bloodline in Crimson’s body. What kind of level does the Abyssal Beast bloodline represent in the Sky Beyond the Clouds? How does it compare to the mermaid and Blood species’ bloodline?”","Spring had already been anticipating this question from Lin Yuan.","The Abyssal Beast bloodline was multifaceted. In fact, it was much more complicated than the Βlood and mermaid bloodlines! However, it was extremely inferior.","Nonetheless, it would still take a long time before Lin Yuan’s fey could evolve. Spring said seriously, “Lord Saint, do you remember I mentioned the endless abyss I mentioned exists outside of the Sky Beyond the Clouds? The Abyssal Beast is the general name for the lifeforms in the endless abyss that possess spatial abilities but don’t belong to a specific species.","“Most of these lifeforms have tentacles and multiple eyes. Their bodies come in various shapes and sizes. The Abyssal Beast bloodline in Crimson’s body is considered a very average one. Moreover, the share of Abyssal Beast bloodline in Crimson’s body had been rather small. Otherwise, he would not have been able to keep up appearances as a member of the Blood species.","“There are many species that became terrifying and ferocious after the Abyssal Beast bloodline tainted their bloodlines. By comparison, Crimson had not inherited many of the Abyssal Beast bloodline’s unique abilities. His speed of ambushing you wαs not even half as fast as that of World Emperor Abyssal Beasts when they warp space!","“Because of their strong abilities to warp space, the Abyssal Beasts are very common in all four universes of the Sky Beyond the Clouds. There are many powerful species and factions who train the Abyssal Beasts as pets or tame them for riding.","“The average Abyssal Beast is not worth much. One can easily purchase an Abyssal Beast as long as one is sufficiently strong. However, it is not easy to tame the Abyssal Beast. Subjugating one requires resources, and it is much more costly than just buying one. A few experts and members of factions like to train the Abyssal Beasts into pets and for riding as a form of showing off their resources and prestige.","“The Abyssal Beasts gather around the Sky Beyond the Clouds because they love energy like spirit qi and absorb all types of energy, including elemental energy, vitality, death aura, and even faith power. After absorbing them, the Abyssal Beasts’ body will change accordingly! With the resources you possess, you can easily cultivate and breed the Abyssal Beasts.”","If the Sky Beyond the Clouds was compared to the main world, the abyss around it was akin to the dimensional worlds around the main world.","Once he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, there was no way that Lin Yuan would sell foundational resources like spirit qi crystals and elemental energy. Lin Yuan needed them to create a production chain that would provide him with a never-ending supply of resources.","Lin Yuan could nurture the Abyssal Beasts as a business. However, he could only come up with the details after he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and observed the situation on the ground.","After her explanation, Spring noticed Lin Yuan looked like he had more to say. She hurriedly said, “Lord Saint, if you want to hear about Sky Beyond the Clouds, I can tell you all about it. The Sky Beyond the Clouds is a place where all species fight for dominance. However, the strength of the species is not determined based on the Species Ranking because the Species Alliance draws up the ranking.","“The Species Alliance is unaware of many existing species. For example, the faeries did not join the Species Alliance of late, but they are still considered one of the top ten species based on their previous achievements.","“The Blood species likes to fight and always prepares seriously for the Species Alliance. Hence, their ranking might be higher than what their true power reflects.","“Although the faeries don’t like to fight, they won’t allow other factions to overtake them on the Species Ranking. Hence, they don’t neglect their performance on the Species Alliance either.","“Before I came to this Class 1 world, I heard that the dominant factions of the four universes intend to deploy their individual species into the Species Alliance. I don’t exactly know how this plan will be carried out. But if this plan is successful, the Species Alliance’s influence will surpass that of other alliances and become the most influential alliance in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. The competition within the Species Ranking will intensify and be seen as the standard!”","She had spent far too much time hidden in this world. Hence, Spring could only use her general impression to describe the circumstances of the Sky Beyond the Clouds. It was possible that her explanation significantly deviated from the actual circumstances!","Lin Yuan was aware of this. However, a rough understanding was understanding nonetheless.","Spring’s words solidified his resolution to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and run wild.","While Spring and Lin Yuan conversed, Green Vine continued increasing its power.","Spring was not overly amazed by Green Vine’s extraordinary nature.","All she felt was that Green Vine was very lucky.","Green Vine only had such achievements because it just happened to fall into Lin Yuan’s hands, and Lin Yuan just happened to be willing to provide it with resources. If it had fallen into anyone else’s hands or had to grow in the wild, there was no way it would have achieved such transformations!","A lifeform like this that required more resources than other lifeforms was not a reasonable existence to begin with.","Moreover, the faerie bloodline, metals, and Divine Retribution Ashes Scale Snake’s secret treasures were entities that no one else in this world would be able to provide Green Vine!","By remaining by Lin Yuan’s side, Green Vine had outstanding achievements in its future! It would likely become famous throughout the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Spring spent two days patiently describing and painting a picture of the Sky Beyond the Clouds for Lin Yuan. As a result, despite never having been to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan now had the knowledge of a frequent visitor!","At that moment, Spring sensed Green Vine’s aura and said seriously, “Lord Saint, your fey will be able to evolve to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom very soon! Once a lifeform reaches this level, it will undergo a reincarnation into a new life. So, no matter what happens, you don’t have to be worried. I will be here to step in and help if necessary!","“This abyss demon you sent out has already reached World Emperor grade. Since it’s a lifeform from a Class 1 world’s dimensional world, it won’t be able to develop a divine kingdom. It won’t be able to properly protect this fey!”","Spring enjoyed staying by Lin Yuan’s side and was willing to work for him. Now, she finally had a chance to offer him help.","If the Abyss Great Emperor could protect Green Vine, Spring would never dare to suggest carrying out tasks for Lin Yuan. This was because it would be the equivalent of trying to flatter and butter him up. Followers like her were prohibited from such actions!","Lin Yuan gasped to himself, thinking he had taken too large of a bite.","Lin Yuan could enable Green Vine to evolve so smoothly because of Entire Body Medium. Additionally, it was also because he had Spring by his side.","Lin Yuan was certain that Spring would not stand by and watch Green Vine fall into danger.","Regardless of what happened today, Green Vine was going to evolve.","Lin Yuan gave half of his accumulated resources to Green Vine. He was well aware of its spirit qi needs because he took stock of all the resource needs of his feys.","Green Vine waved its vines around as it absorbed the spirit qi.","Each breath of spirit qi Green Vine absorbed caused its aura to intensify significantly. This meant that it was difficult for Green Vine’s body to absorb more energy.","All the energy that Green Vine absorbed was presented through its appearance.","Just as Spring had said, Green Vine’s time to evolve was there!","Lin Yuan sensed that the Eternal Heart in Green Vine had been ignited. This was not because it had been set aflame by an external attack but was a self-combustion.","It was not just Green Vine’s Eternal Heart that had been ignited. The emerald green spirit fire that had been forming in Green Vine over the last day was also slowly being burned. This was a sign that a spirit-fire lifeform was about to die.","If Spring had not given Lin Yuan a heads-up, Lin Yuan would be worried about Green Vine’s situation. But since Spring had mentioned that Green Vine would need to experience a reincarnation into a new life before it could reach World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, Lin Yuan laid his worries to rest.","Lin Yuan would be an eyewitness to Green Vine’s transformation!","It could be said that Lin Yuan was the one who had created Green Vine’s transformation!","After Green Vine evolved to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, many of Lin Yuan’s doubts would be dispelled!","Lin Yuan only had a general idea of the divine kingdom.","Lin Yuan confirmed that the shrine in his soul was a divine kingdom when he used True Data.","However, based on the definition of human spirit qi professional ranks, he was an A-rank spirit qi professional.","He had not even become an A-rank spirit qi professional when he obtained his divine kingdom.","This was all very confusing for Lin Yuan.","Once Green Vine gained its divine kingdom, Lin Yuan would see if there were any differences between his own divine kingdom and that of Green Vine despite still being unsure of how he gained his own divine kingdom.","Lin Yuan could sense the agony that Green Vine was in.","The burning of its Eternal Heart and spirit fire caused Green Vine to become extremely weak.","But just like waxed and waned plants, they would eventually explode with shocking vitality.","Spring gasped to herself as she watched Green Vine.","Green Vine was truly born with a golden spoon in its mouth!","Ever since he began nurturing Green Vine, Lin Yuan only provided it with the best resources.","Other feys at the gate of World Emperor/Divine Kingdom would not experience their Eternal Heart burning for this long, and their spirit fire would have already been burned away.","It was unlikely that any other lifeform in this world had evolved to this level.","In the words of the Sky Beyond the Clouds, this level was called the ‘Spirit Master’s Nirvana’. After this transformation, the spirit master’s body would create a miniature divine kingdom. The divine kingdom would become the core of its body’s energy, and its energy would transform!","Once the divine kingdom was created, it would be able to receive and absorb faith from other experts.","Only experts who had reached the Divine Kingdom level would be able to destroy the soul of such an expert, as the divine kingdom would protect their soul and spiritual energy during combat.","The development of the divine kingdom would even bring benefits to divine-kingdom experts.","Compared to the divine kingdom, which was broken into detailed categories, the World Emperor grade was just a general concept.","Only divine-kingdom experts were able to reach the World Emperor grade, so they were designated into smaller categories.","In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, they were called domain mountain-class experts.","Presently, there were less than 30 living domain mountain-class experts in the entire Sky Beyond the Clouds!"]},{"number":2740,"title":"Chapter 2740 Divine Kingdom Ability: Bloodline Abundant Harvest!","paragraphs":["2740 Divine Kingdom Ability: Bloodline Abundant Harvest!","Green Vine was silently enduring this singular biggest transformation in its life. It trusted Lin Yuan to ensure its safety. All of this suffering would eventually culminate in its grade and quality evolution!","At that moment, Green Vine could sense that its soul was transforming from the inside out. This transformation was very foreign to Green Vine.","However, this change did cause Green Vine’s soul to come into contact with a mystical space.","When Lin Yuan checked on Green Vine’s condition, he saw that its aura had changed enormously in the span of an instant.","Previously, its aura was very similar to that of the Abyss Great Emperor. But it was now clearly more powerful and profound than the Abyss Great Emperor’s aura!","Spring stepped in front of Lin Yuan for the first time.","“Lord Saint, you don’t have to worry even if a big commotion occurs later. When a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom expert evolves in a Class 2 world, they will definitely attract a lot of attention to this Class 2 world.","“This Class 2 world’s wills will also naturally reject the Perfect Touch Wisteria. These are all obstacles to its evolution, and I will be here to remove them!”","While Spring was speaking, Green Vine’s life seemed to be extinguished. Its Eternal Heart was burned to destruction, and its spirit fire had stopped burning.","Yet, the aura in its soul was becoming increasingly strong and concentrated!","The main world’s sky resembled a choppy sea. Streaks of black and purple scars appeared in the sky, and it looked as though the entire sky had cracked open.","All of the phenomena in the sky were directed at Green Vine.","This was similar to when Night Leaning Moon used her 10 Stars sacred source lifeform to trigger celestial phenomena.","All the lifeforms in the main world could see the phenomena in the sky.","These phenomena were just as startling as the dead spirits crisis. It might even be more astonishing than the dead spirits crisis!","After all, the dead spirits crisis came from underground, and the main world’s lifeforms were able to get a clear look at underground happenings. However, they were able to observe the sky clearly.","Lin Yuan was receiving a stack of messages through the Thoughts Letter Paper. Most of them contained questions about the phenomena in the sky.","The dead spirits crisis had just ended, and most of the leaders of factions in the main world were still mentally drained. Any blow would be enough to shock them.","Moreover, the current phenomena in the sky were truly staggering.","As time went by, more energy accumulated in the sky. If the energy was unleashed on the earth, it would annihilate most of the bases on the main world and at least 1/3 of the lifeforms!","Even if the dead spirits crisis was allowed to proceed unrestrained, it would not cause such destruction in such a short span!","Lin Yuan replied to the Moon Empress first.","[Lin Yuan]: Master, don’t worry. There are no problems, and everything is going well! The phenomena in the sky are triggered by one of my feys undergoing a breakthrough. Once it has evolved, the phenomena will disappear on their own!","Lin Yuan did not hide anything from the Moon Empress and told her the truth.","The Moon Empress was taken aback.","She had assumed that this was either part of the aftermath of the dead spirits crisis or the work of a hidden faction that was more powerful than Tower Canon!","She had never expected such force to come from the evolution of one of Lin Yuan’s feys!","If that were the case, there was no need for the Moon Empress to be concerned. Given her understanding of Lin Yuan, he had to have made advance preparations for his fey’s evolution.","An increase in Lin Yuan’s fey’s combat power benefited the Radiance Federation and all the humans.","Lin Yuan sent the same reply to Wen Yu and Liu Jie as he did to the Moon Empress.","However, he did not send such detailed explanations to others. All he said was that the phenomena taking place in the sky would not negatively impact the world.","Now that Lin Yuan had accounted for the phenomena in the sky, the factions in the main world were no longer as concerned about the subsequent effects.","It was said that there was always someone to catch you when the sky fell. To all of the factions, Lin Yuan was the one who would catch them! Since Lin Yuan was there as a safety net for them, there was no need for the leaders of other factions to be worried!","...","Iron Prison announced the sentencing and results after dealing with Mang Shui.","Tian Feng did not have any objections.","Iron Prison also had not considered Tian Feng’s feelings at all.","He never considered others in his actions. Moreover, he knew that if Tian Feng truly cared about Mang Shui and wanted to save him, he would not have handed Mang Shui over to him!","Mang Shui needed to be eliminated to give a proper warning to those who had dishonest intentions.","These people might not necessarily be blinded by greed like Mang Shui was.","After the dead spirits crisis came to an end, the Radiance Federation would undergo an overhaul.","Although the dead spirits crisis had lasted for a short time, it had still left an enormous impact on the entire main world!","Lin Yuan was also preparing to divide the benefits. The benefits would allow the main world’s factions to at least double their power.","When the resources were being distributed, greed would surge within many factions. This kind of greed would have a large influence on the Radiance Federation.","This warning would remove at least 30% of the potential greed.","If there were any factions that did not rein in their greed after witnessing what happened to Mang Shui, Iron Prison would not show them any mercy!","Tian Feng usually protected his own interests and covered up for others’ shortcomings. However, his actions usually aligned with Iron Prison’s in matters of great importance.","If Tian Feng continued to overlook shortcomings regarding such matters, the impacts would be overwhelmingly negative! It would also cause Iron Prison to doubt Tian Feng’s worthiness as a member of royalty!","...","The Moon Empress immediately quelled the concerns about the phenomena in the sky and began taking the first steps in changing the Radiance Federation.","Even after the Moon Empress was done issuing most of her orders, the phenomena in the sky had yet to cease. Rather, they seemed to have changed significantly.","This current could not be compared to its initial stage!","Nonetheless, the Moon Empress was not worried. Instead, she was shocked at the power of Lin Yuan’s fey that was currently evolving!","This evolving fey had already surpassed the level she currently comprehended.","In the past, it was always her replying to Lin Yuan’s questions.","The Moon Empress still believed that there was a need to hold question-and-answer questions. But from now on, she would be the one asking, and he would be the one answering!","The Moon Empress had a strong desire for knowledge and wanted to learn about everything she did not know.","...","In the past two days, Lin Yuan watched Spring fend off attack after attack for Green Vine. However, she did not fully fend off the attacks, only enough so that a portion could be left for Green Vine to train its body.","Green Vine’s main body was destroyed and recovered repeatedly. Each time it recovered from destruction, its body’s durability was fundamentally improved.","Green Vine’s miniature divine kingdom had already formed.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Green Vine.","[Fey Name]: Perfect Touch Wisteria","[Fey Species]: Strong armor wisteria species/long wisteria species","[Fey Grade]: World Emperor (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","[Forbidden Growth]: After contracting any lifeform, it can break the limit that comes with the contract. As long as it has sufficient energy, it will be able to continuously increase its power. When it has absorbed the maximum amount of energy, it will be able to comprehend a required Willpower Rune.","[Peak Sturdiness]: A large amount of the absorbed energy can be used up to increase the durability of the vines. When injured, the energy can also be used to repair the vines.","[Long Vine Application]: Choose two vines that will be applied to one vine. The vine with the two vines applied on it will be able to gain the two vines’ abilities.","[Paralyzing Vine Sap]: When damage is sustained, the vine sap with paralyzing effects can be sprayed out from the wound.","[Brutally Pushing Out of Soil]: When faced with the opponent’s defenses, the seeds’ sprouting strength can be activated to help break past the opponent’s defenses.","[Root’s Parasitic Restraints]: Pick a target and the target’s body will become soil where roots will grow. The roots will absorb the target’s vitality to cause harm to the target.","[Splitting Illusionary Spikes]: When the illusionary spikes pierce a target’s body, the illusionary spikes will turn into a seed that will germinate in the target’s body and produce even more illusionary spikes.","[Avoidance Wedge]: Every time the Perfect Touch Wisteria is injured, a wedge will grow over its surface. Every three layers will turn into a sharp spike that will be able to increase the vines’ effects while boosting them.","[Combined Vines Defense]: Pick a target to apply to and help it to defend against external attacks. The Perfect Touch Wisteria’s own vitality will be sacrificed to protect the target it is applied to.","[Climbing Vine Armor Transformation]: Its body will transform into an armor, and its body will be linked to the target’s energy source. In its armor state, its bloodline will be boosted, and the effects will show after the armor state is removed.","Exclusive Skill:","[Swallow Same Source]: Every vine will have the same grade and quality, but they can be separated to act as individual entities. Every vine can consume something and take control of its attributes. The swallowed entity cannot be spat out, but an even higher-level item can replace it. (Once it gains attributes, the vine cannot be separated again.)","[Broken Vine Replacement]: When a vine is destroyed during combat, another vine can be picked to take on the damage instead to save the first vine.","[Energy Gather Illusionary Thorn]: The energy within the vines can be gathered at a certain spot. An illusionary thorn composed of energy will sprout from this spot. The illusionary thorn will be undetectable.","[Tactile Vine Wood World]: All of the wood-type energy and vitality stored within the vines will be released. The wood-type energy and vitality will transform into a large number of vines. The vines will intertwine and form a world of vines. The main body will fuse with this world to attack targets. Before the wooden world is broken, all the damage sustained by the main body will be reduced and shouldered by the wooden world.","[Entire Body Medium]: Sacrifice the item that the vine had absorbed and release the source of the item through a medium. The released source will not have any knowledge but will possess all of its original power. (Compare the proportion of energy that the source comprises of within the item to determine how long the released source will be able to remain outside.)","[Vine Tempering Garrotte]: Use the long vines to garrotte other lifeforms. If the target’s bloodline is more elite than that of the Perfect Touch Wisteria, it can absorb the target’s bloodline to strengthen its own bloodline. This will also strengthen every vine that has absorbed an entity through Swallow Same Source.","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Bloodline Abundant Harvest]: When the divine tree growing in the divine kingdom consumes a corpse and its bloodline, fruits bearing the bloodline power will grow on the tree. The concentration of bloodline power in the fruit will be linked to the faith power supplied to the tree by the divine tree. The more faith power is supplied, the stronger the concentration of bloodline power in the fruits.","Lin Yuan saw that Green Vine was now a World Emperor I/Elementary Divine Kingdom expert. The grade of its divine kingdom was miniature.","Normally, Green Vine’s transformation would be complete.","But the attacks descending from the sky were full of prying intentions.","It was likely that Begin Lady and Celestial Sight’s evolutions into faeries had caught the attention of an expert from the Sky Beyond the Clouds, and this expert was now trying to interfere with this evolution.","There was no way that Lin Yuan could use the Abyss Great Emperor to fend off any of these attacks.","Lin Yuan could guess how Green Vine’s evolution to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom would end up if Spring was not here to help!","After all the attempts to spy were stopped by Spring, Lin Yuan said seriously, “Thank you, you—”","Before Lin Yuan could finish speaking, Spring had fallen to her knees from the moment he thanked her.","“Lord Saint, I am your follower. Serving you is only the right thing to do! Your thanks gives me panic!”","Spring’s reaction vexed Lin Yuan. He did not want an expert like Spring to produce such a reaction toward him at any time.","Clearly, he could not be too polite toward the members of Epoch God Palace from now on!","When Spring saw Lin Yuan move to help her up, she hurriedly stood up on her own. Shame and humility hung on her face.","Lin Yuan could sense that Spring was supplying him with a sea of faith power. The faith power from Spring alone made up 10% of all the faith power in his divine kingdom!","This was enough to show just how devout her faith was!","Previously, Lin Yuan was unable to sense the faith supplied by Spring because she had used a method to suppress her transmission of faith power."]},{"number":2741,"title":"Chapter 2741 The Six Major Divine Kingdom Abilities!","paragraphs":["2741 The Six Major Divine Kingdom Abilities!","The faith power that Spring was supplying Lin Yuan astonished him. He never imagined a lifeform would ever supply him with such a volume of faith power.","But at the same time, he could sense that she was intentionally hiding many things from him.","Lin Yuan did not interrogate her about this because this volume of faith power already answered the question he had.","He knew that he could trust Spring unconditionally!","It was likely that the other members of Epoch God Palace were also supplying him with such an immense amount of faith power!","Lin Yuan could not begin to guess what he had done in his previous life to earn this much faith from these lifeforms.","He believed that all these questions would eventually be answered. At that time, he would know everything that he wanted to know!","“Spring, you must know where Tower Canon’s vestiges are. Once we are done helping Green Vine evolve, I will take a trip around the main world’s factions and seas to harvest resources and look at the damage done by the dead spirits crisis!","“Once I’m done with the trip and have cleared out the resources left behind by Tower Canon, I’ll go with you to Epoch God Palace. This visit should tell me a lot of information I don’t currently know, right?”","Spring was silent for a moment before she said seriously, “Lord Saint, the birth horoscope you will be enlightening is the one from your present life. If you want to know more about the past, the four of us can tell you what we know once we’re all gathered together.","“A large reason for our existence is to keep records of your happenings and circumstances. But it goes without saying that you can choose not to dig into your past. After all, your current and past lives are separate!”","Lin Yuan nodded.","He still thought it was ridiculous for him to be the reincarnation of the Saint, but he did not disbelieve it. If he was not the reincarnation of the Saint, why would Epoch God Palace go so far for his sake?","Spring’s attitude toward him was an indication of how the rest of Epoch God Palace would treat him.","However, if the choice was truly up to him, Lin Yuan did not want to chase after his past memories. He would rather live life to the fullest now!","While conversing with Spring, Lin Yuan read through the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Green Vine’s True Data.","The new World Emperor ability was called Climbing Vine Armor Transformation.","Climbing Vine Armor Transformation was similar to Tool Transformation for other feys, but it would not cause Green Vine to transform into a tool. Instead, it would transform into an armor of vines that Lin Yuan would put on and would link their bloodlines.","When Green Vine was in the armor state, its bloodline would be boosted by Lin Yuan’s bloodline. This boost would only take effect after Green Vine stopped using Climbing Vine Armor Transformation and was no longer an armor of vines.","This was an ability that linked Lin Yuan and Green Vine.","However, this would not be a significant improvement for the current Green Vine.","When Lin Yuan came into contact with dragon-species feys in the past, he realized that his bloodline did not reject the dragon-species feys’ bloodlines. He could sense that if he absorbed the dragon-species bloodlines, they would become a part of him and have no negative impact on his mermaid bloodline.","Green Vine’s ability Climbing Vine Armor Transformation gave Lin Yuan the incentive to use his bloodline to absorb even more bloodlines.","Presently, Lin Yuan did not know if this idea was feasible.","Green Vine returned to Lin Yuan’s side after it completed its transformation.","Lin Yuan suddenly sensed that because of their contract, he had a faint link to Green Vine’s divine kingdom.","Because of this link, Lin Yuan no longer resisted the temptation of Green Vine’s divine kingdom.","Lin Yuan sensed his consciousness entering a narrow space.","This space was desolate. It was even more barren than when the Spirit Lock spatial zone first started out.","It was clear that this was Green Vine’s divine kingdom.","There was a small tree sprout growing in the ground.","From True Data, Lin Yuan knew that this tree sprout was a result of Green Vine’s Bloodline Abundant Harvest.","After feys reached the Divine Kingdom level, they would not gain any new exclusive skills. Instead, they would gain something called the divine kingdom ability.","It was clear that every lifeform’s divine kingdom ability was linked to their life and abilities.","Green Vine’s divine kingdom ability was linked to its bloodline.","The tree sprout growing in this small space was the divine tree growing in Green Vine’s divine kingdom.","The divine tree could consume the bloodlines of dead lifeforms to produce fruits with the bloodline powers. The concentration of bloodline powers in the fruits was linked to the aura of faith power supplied by the divine kingdom to the divine tree. The more faith power was supplied, the stronger the bloodline powers in the fruits!","Green Vine’s divine kingdom ability was a production ability. This type of ability would be useful to both Lin Yuan and Green Vine.","Spring also saw through Green Vine’s divine kingdom ability and did not look surprised.","Lin Yuan had nurtured it. Regardless of how outstanding its divine kingdom ability was, it would seem ordinary to Spring.","Although Spring did not express shock after seeing Green Vine’s divine kingdom ability, she knew that it would definitely send waves through the Sky Beyond the Clouds once Lin Yuan arrived there.","Bloodline Abundance Harvest could strengthen a lifeform’s bloodline.","Many species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds used bloodline power as their main source of power and the measure by which they ranked the various species.","Moreover, Green Vine’s Bloodline Abundance Harvest could support Lin Yuan when he used his Body of All Spirits to absorb the bloodlines of other species.","Now, Lin Yuan understood the difference between his divine kingdom and Green Vine’s divine kingdom.","The fountain of faith had not even formed in Green Vine’s divine kingdom.","Green Vine’s divine kingdom would only expand once it attained a large amount of faith power and produced the fountain of faith.","Green Vine could represent regular feys.","Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom was much more advanced than Green Vine’s divine kingdom. He would only be able to discern the exact size of the gap after observing the development of Green Vine’s divine kingdom.","Spring knew that Lin Yuan was unaware of the distinctions between the divine kingdom abilities, and began to explain, “Lord Saint, all divine kingdom lifeforms will gain divine kingdom abilities. As their divine kingdom develops, not only will they gain more divine kingdom abilities, but the abilities will strengthen continuously as well.","“Amongst all the divine kingdom abilities, the domain-types are the most exceptional. This is because domain-type divine kingdom abilities can influence the divine kingdoms of other lifeforms!","“The major factions will seek after every lifeform with domain-type divine kingdom abilities. The factions are all willing to invest resources into these lifeforms. After investing resources into this lifeform, they will be able to receive significant profits after its power evolves!","“Compared to combat-, defense-, and control-type divine kingdom abilities, production-type are very variable. The combat-, defense-, and control-type divine kingdom abilities can easily be categorized based on their potential. Once the potential has been decided, it won’t change unless an opportunity arises to change this divine kingdom ability.","“But production-type divine kingdom abilities are able to produce varying amounts of resources. Some production-type divine kingdoms are useless and negligible, while others can complement domain-type divine kingdom abilities or even surpass the domain-type divine kingdom abilities!","“Green Vine’s Bloodline Abundant Harvest deserves to be deemed equal to domain-type divine kingdom abilities. Faith power is a very precious type of energy. Aside from you, anyone else is unlikely to possess this much faith power to grow the bloodline fruits.","“The most scorned type of divine kingdom ability in the Sky Beyond the Clouds is the expanding-type. This kind of divine kingdom ability mainly targets the divine kingdom’s development. But in order to develop a divine kingdom, sufficient power is a prerequisite, followed by sufficient resources to sustain the divine kingdom.","“It’s difficult for others to increase their own power and obtain resources. Even the species that are brimming with resources are unwilling to spend them on an ostensibly bottomless hole. There are six main types of divine kingdom abilities. The others are categorized under these six!”","Spring’s explanation gave Lin Yuan a full grasp of divine kingdom abilities.","Green Vine’s divine kingdom ability was essentially useless in the main world because there was no way for Lin Yuan to get his hands on a large number of corpses from different species. It would only be useful in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","After Red Thorn and Silver Corona’s powers increased, Lin Yuan needed to swap out the weapons controlled by the Tongues of Relinquish and Silver Corona’s sea of flowers.","Those that did not meet his standard could be buried in Green Vine’s divine kingdom!","Green Vine’s successful World Emperor/Divine Kingdom evolution allowed Lin Yuan to know he could also use his resources to evolve his other feys to this level.","However, he would first have to head to Epoch God Palace’s Returning Saint Pool to enlighten his birth horoscope.","Lin Yuan now knew the difference between his own divine kingdom and that of other lifeforms.","...","After storing Green Vine in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Lin Yuan started helping the sea clan experts evolve.","Once again, Lin Yuan harvested a large pile of spirit qi crystals that he could tap into whenever he saw fit.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope, which managed the Spirit Lock spatial zone, started working hard again!","Spring continued to protect Lin Yuan from the shadows to prevent any harm from coming to him. Regardless of how powerful he became or whether he was capable of solving his issues, Spring saw it as her duty to safeguard him. She took her role of being his follower with utmost seriousness.","The lifeforms from the sea clans had witnessed Green Vine’s evolution and had unending respect for Lin Yuan.","Moreover, Lin Yuan had the mermaid thearch bloodline. Hence, the sea clan lifeforms naturally felt affection for him.","There were many more sea clan lifeforms than humans.","Lin Yuan did not provide the sea clans with too many resources.","The Vast Sea Labyrinth gave the order that all sea clan experts who were Fantasy Breed and above had to seek Lin Yuan’s help before evolving their grades and qualities. This was why so many sea clan lifeforms that needed to evolve had gathered together.","The potential of the sea was on display.","Lin Yuan sought out Ice Flow.","He interacted with Ice Flow the most out of the three rulers of Vast Sea Labyrinth.","Aside from Ice Flow, Lin Yuan also called over Silver Umber Black, Light Green Umber, Blue Umber, and Red Beauty to assist Ice Flow in distributing the resources.","After the incident in the manor in the north district of the Radiance Federation’s Royal Capital, Lin Yuan no longer gave away his trust as easily.","With the four emperor-class experts helping Ice Flow distribute the resources to the sea clans, Lin Yuan could accumulate resources while ensuring the resources he spent did not go to waste.","Lin Yuan felt very wealthy and assured when he gathered resources from the sea.","During his journey, Lin Yuan investigated the various happenings across the main world.","Lin Yuan thought, It’s a good thing that I handled things in the nick of time!","If he was any later, the death aura would have infected the energy ores and altered them. Without the energy ores, the foundation of the entire world would be shaken.","Now, after Summer extracted the death aura and the demon insects consumed it, the death aura’s effect would be eliminated.","Lin Yuan spent almost seven months collecting the spirit qi crystals. If he returned to the Radiance Federation during the seven months and harvested resources from there, he would possess even more spirit qi crystals than he did now!","Spring did not even bat an eye at Lin Yuan’s wealth.","This wealth would be enough to stun any faction in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, but it was nothing to the Saint.","Back then...","Lin Yuan’s gathering of resources triggered a memory for Spring.","She wanted to speak but eventually chose to keep her mouth shut.","Lin Yuan received a message from the Moon Empress that said that many federations wanted to use the Major Federation Union to situate themselves in new locations. Hence, many human federations had decided to migrate after the dead spirits crisis was quelled.","It was not convenient to collect resources at such a time.","Hence, Lin Yuan decided that it was time to search for the remnants of Tower Canon!"]},{"number":2742,"title":"Chapter 2742 Reincarnation Gold Jade!","paragraphs":["2742 Reincarnation Gold Jade!","“Spring, where are the remnants of Tower Canon? They should contain a resource that I urgently require. I need to search for these resources in the vestiges of Tower Canon.”","“If you head in this direction, you will eventually be able to see an island in the sea. There is a castle on the island. The entire island can be considered Tower Canon’s old nest!","“However, there is more to the island than what meets the eye. The bottom of the island has been altered to be linked to the ley lines. Tower Canon has injected the roots of a Class 3 world’s dimensional world into this Class 1 world.","“The Class 3 world’s dimensional world’s roots continue to affect this Class 1 world even after it was promoted to Class 2. It’s clear that Tower Canon has been nourishing this Class 3 world’s dimensional world’s roots.","“After you’ve collected all of the Secrets of the Dead and combined them into tomes, you will probably be able to control and manipulate the dead world’s roots. At that point, you’ll be able to use the dead world’s roots to specifically nurture a type of dead dimensional lifeform.”","Lin Yuan nodded.","Keira had already told him that, just not in this much detail.","There was no question that Lin Yuan was going to take control of the dead world’s roots. He already knew that the dead world and main world’s root energies repelled each other, causing the bond between the two world’s roots to be tenuous.","Hence, if Lin Yuan could use the dead world’s roots to nurture a special dead dimensional lifeform, he would be able to avoid unnecessary waste!","The dead spirits crisis brought disaster to the main world. Yet, Lin Yuan did not truly detest these lifeforms. Rather, the battles against the dead spirits allowed Lin Yuan to see the strength of these lifeforms.","Lin Yuan was very willing to learn about all types of lifeforms.","However, Lin Yuan still did not know which type of dead spirit he was going to strengthen with the dead world’s roots.","Keira had captured almost every type of dead dimensional lifeform and analyzed their roots.","If Lin Yuan sought Keira’s opinion, she would definitely be able to give him an answer he was satisfied with.","He summoned the Kill Food Sky Butterfly and flew southwest where Spring had pointed towards.","Meanwhile, in Epoch God Palace...","A handsome young man and elderly man began trembling after listening to what the girl in front of them said. Tears sprang to both of their eyes.","“Summer, are you sure that your information is sound?”","When she heard what the elderly man said, Summer knew that Winter was overwhelmed with surprised delight. Otherwise, he would never doubt her!","Moreover, she would never falsify information regarding Lord Saint!","She and Spring had slowly confirmed Lin Yuan’s identity. Still, tears filled their eyes the moment they became certain.","Summer told Autumn and Winter with utmost seriousness, “It’s true that we’ve found Lord Saint. He is wearing Lord Totem God on his wrist. There’s no mistaking this! Spring is currently sticking by Lord Saint’s side to protect him. I only returned to let the two of you know about this.”","At this point, Summer turned to Autumn. “You previously came into contact with Tower Canon. It was Lord Saint’s enemy and has been completely wiped out. With Spring by Lord Saint’s side, no harm can come to him.","“Soon, I must return to the Startling Lines Continent to funnel the death aura in the ley lines, so I can’t stay for long.","“Autumn, it won’t be long before Spring brings Lord Saint back to Epoch God Palace so the Returning Saint Pool can enlighten his birth horoscope. Since you have nothing better to do, why don’t you help Winter to open the path to the Sky Beyond the Clouds?”","Neither Autumn nor Winter had any issues with Summer’s arrangement.","Both of them were wondering when Spring would be able to bring Lin Yuan back to Epoch God Palace. They badly wanted to stand in front of him and greet him.","They had waited for such a long time. But now that they knew they were about to meet him, they became impatient.","...","Summer did not stay in Epoch God Palace for long. She left for the Startling Lines Continent immediately after delivering the news to Autumn and Winter.","During her time in the Startling Lines Continent, redirecting the death aura in the ley lines, Summer observed Red Thorn and Silver Corona. She supplied them with pure death aura at a rate that matched their rate of absorption.","Additionally, Summer used her own methods to increase the purity of the death aura.","It would take a very long time for these two eight-winged fairies to evolve their bloodlines by absorbing death aura.","Summer decided to inform Lin Yuan of this when he went to Epoch God Palace.","Even if the two fairies were supplied with a large amount of death aura, they also needed to be supplied with a large amount of pure spirit qi in order to raise their chances of successfully evolving their bloodlines.","With Lin Yuan’s body, pure spirit qi was a common good.","...","Lin Yuan and Spring never stopped conversing during their journey. The more they spoke, the more comfortable they became with each other.","This made Spring feel as though she was receiving special favor.","For example, Lin Yuan had handed her a piece of roasted meat when he had his meal.","Spring was so thrilled that she did not know what to do with herself!","As Lin Yuan looked at the azure sea below him, he once again sensed vigorous signs of life.","Spring paused to sense the sea before saying, “Lord Saint, you should be able to sense that all the death aura has been drained from the ley lines below this sea. This means that we are very near to Tower Canon’s old nest!","“Although the Eight Pages of Tower Canon are dead and the Chanters under their control would have already died along with them, this does not mean that there are no more dangers in their old nest. If you need anything, you should leave it to the Afterlife Realm Demon or me!”","He had almost been assassinated by Crimson during their battle and did not see Tower Canon’s old nest as a safe place at all.","Lin Yuan had experience clearing out a faction’s treasure trove after conquering it. Each time, his harvest had been plentiful.","But Lin Yuan was really looking forward to clearing out Tower Canon’s old nest.","Standing on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s back, Lin Yuan could already make out the silhouette of the island.","There were various colored gems embedded on the surface of the island. Each one of these gems was considered priceless in the outside world. Yet, these fist-sized gems were scattered on the beach like worthless garbage. These gems would be excellent both as accessories or used in potions.","There was no reason for Lin Yuan to let these gems go to waste.","Lin Yuan instructed the Kill Food Sky Butterfly to land on the edge of the island, and the Source Sand’s main body appeared by his feet.","The Source Sand began rapidly generating sand. It produced Close Guard Sand that changed the environment of the ground under them, and the sand soon began spreading out underground.","The Source Sand was skilled at searching and gathering resources, so it collected all the gems on the ground.","In the blink of an eye, the Source Sand had covered the entire island.","Aside from these gems, the Source Sand did not collect anything else from this island.","As the Source Sand dug deeper, Lin Yuan noticed that the gems and sand were just for superficial appearances. After a depth of 30 meters, the Source Sand hit a rock layer that had been fortified. The rock extended deep under the island and probably reached the bottom of the sea.","Lin Yuan instructed the Source Sand to break this layer of rock. However, he realized that the Source Sand did not have the ability to do so.","After thinking for a moment, Lin Yuan decided to enter the castle first. He would investigate the space under the island later.","Spring clearly knew something about this and began explaining. “There are so many gems accumulated here because Tower Canon intentionally sent people out to gather these resources.","“Unlike lifeforms with the giant dragon bloodline, dead dimensional lifeforms aren’t interested in shiny trinkets. Tower Canon has likely been using these gems as a vessel for a special energy source. They are using these materials from fey corpses to extract wills and laws. Then, they used the wills and laws to speed up the fusing of the dead world and main world’s laws.”","Lin Yuan understood what Spring was trying to say.","The wills and laws comprehended by feys came from the main world. Using them as mediums would indeed be able to speed up the fusing of the two worlds’ roots.","Lin Yuan could easily use the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen to collect these wills and laws. Hence, he had no need for the vessels that Spring had mentioned.","However, not everyone had the Sacred Sword Wielding Queen.","This type of vessel would be very beneficial to Lin Yuan both in the main world and in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","After entering the castle, Lin Yuan and Spring found the interior to be very dark and dank.","The eight black coffins were continuously sucking out the light from the environment.","The only light in the castle came from the chains of birth horoscopes hanging from the ceiling.","Lin Yuan pointed at the birth horoscopes and a stream of sand wrapped around these makeshift lanterns.","The sand rapidly started to break down the birth horoscopes, as well as the Eternal Hearts, Immortal bodies, and the like that also comprised the lanterns.","These lanterns in the castle could be described as the graves of experts.","If a birth-horoscope expert died and learned that their birth horoscope was going to be used as a lightbulb, how would they feel?","Spring had never come to Tower Canon’s old nest before. She did not know that the interior decoration would be so simple.","Spring pointed at the eight black coffins and exclaimed, “The Eight Pages of Tower Canon actually found a resource like the Reincarnation Gold Jade! They even turned the Reincarnation Gold Jade into eight vessels for their own benefit and left their individual imprints on them.”","Spring had been curious to find out why Tower Canon had managed to awaken 6,000 years after she severely injured them.","It turned out that it was due to these eight black coffins made of Reincarnation Gold Jade!","By any reasonable standard, the Eight Pages of Tower Canon were already dead.","Lin Yuan had battled the Eight Pages of Tower Canon, but the soul imprints they had placed on the Reincarnation Gold Jade had yet to disappear.","As long as the Reincarnation Gold Jade was supplied with sufficient energy, the Eight Pages could use the remnants of their souls to reincarnate even after hundreds or thousands of years had passed!","The Reincarnation Gold Jade was viewed as a treasure in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. How did those dead spirits get their hands on it? It seemed that the Eight Pages of Tower Canon had a fair number of secrets of their own!","It was likely that these secrets would slowly be revealed as they explored more of the castle.","When Lin Yuan heard what Spring said, the words ‘Reincarnation Gold Jade’ were seared into his brain.","Before Lin Yuan could speak, Spring took it upon herself to remove the marks on the eight black coffins left by Tower Canon.","It was only at this moment that the Eight Pages of Tower Canon truly died.","Lin Yuan was silently shocked when he saw this.","Luckily, these black coffins made of Reincarnation Gold Jade did not have warning alarms.","Before the imprint was activated, it would be in a state of primal chaos. Otherwise, he would have been exposed when he killed Eye Shadow!","“Lord Saint, you can store away these five items made of Reincarnation Gold Jade. From now on, you can leave the imprints of other lifeforms on these five vessels made of the Reincarnation Gold Jade.","“If the chosen lifeforms die, they can be reincarnated in this vessel! This revival does not refer to just that of the physical body. The soul can also be revived with all the previous memories intact!”","At that point, Spring could not stop herself from warning Lin Yuan. “Lord Saint, the Reincarnation Gold Jade is not without its drawbacks. Once a soul forms a contract with it, the Reincarnation Gold Jade will be imprinted on the lifeform’s soul until they are killed and their soul is destroyed!”","Lin Yuan nodded.","Lin Yuan stored the eight coffins in the spatial equipment. He would pick suitable people to place imprints on the black coffins made of Reincarnation Gold Jade later.","Almost everyone around Lin Yuan had formed contracts with the Lifespan Mice. Those that had yet to do so would eventually be able to. Hence, those around him all possessed virtually endless lifespans and did not need to use the black coffins made of Reincarnation Gold Jade to extend their lives.","As such, the best use for the eight black coffins would be to give them to his companions, who were always out on dangerous missions. This would be a form of safety net for them!","Suddenly, an idea popped into Lin Yuan’s head.","“Spring, since these eight black coffins are just vessels made of Reincarnation Gold Jade, can I repurpose the Reincarnation Gold Jade into vessels of different sizes?”","Each black coffin was almost three meters tall and could fit three people with no issues.","If the vessel was made smaller, more vessels could be made from the same volume of material!","If anyone else had asked Spring this, she would say that it was impossible.","However, Lin Yuan had the Totem God with him, and the Totem God could easily melt down all the metals in the world!"]},{"number":2743,"title":"Chapter 2743 The Death Demon Concubine Beast’s Opportunity!","paragraphs":["2743 The Death Demon Concubine Beast’s Opportunity!","If Lin Yuan used Morbius’ ability to melt this Reincarnation Gold Jade, he could turn the Reincarnation Gold Jade into spatial equipment of various sizes!","However, Spring felt that there was no need for Lin Yuan to do this because it would be a waste of the Totem God’s energy.","The Totem God’s energy was much more valuable than the Reincarnation Gold Jade.","Furthermore, once he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, there would be other metal spiritual ingredients of the same level as the Reincarnation Gold Jade. It was considered average among World Emperor metal spiritual ingredients.","After pondering for a moment, Spring told Lin Yuan softly, “Lord Saint, the resources you possess are limited by this Class 2 world and Tower Canon’s dimensional world’s levels. Once you arrive at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, you will realize that there are far more precious treasures!","“I advise you to wait until your horizons have been broadened by the Sky Beyond the Clouds before making any further plans.”","At this point, Spring hastily bowed to Lin Yuan. She believed that as his follower, she had overstepped the boundaries by giving him a suggestion.","Lin Yuan was the type to listen to the opinions of those around him. This was especially so after he accepted this identity.","It went without saying that Lin Yuan would not listen to these opinions blindly. After hearing them, he would do his own deep contemplation.","Lin Yuan found her words to be reasonable.","With his horizons constrained by not being there himself, he could not properly grasp the entire scope of the Sky Beyond the Clouds regardless of how much information he learned.","Lin Yuan still had not decided who he would give these eight black coffins made of Reincarnation Gold Jade.","These eight black coggins were not urgent resources to him. As such, he decided to store them away for now.","The Source Sand rummaged through the hall, and Lin Yuan emptied the castle of almost all of its resources.","Spring softly told Lin Yuan, “Lord Saint, this castle is only meant to exhibit these eight black coffins. After the Eight Pages of Tower Canon woke up, they moved all their resources into their respective towers.","“I will go with you to organize the resources in those towers before heading below the castle to organize the situation there! Tower Canon slept for 6,000 years. They depleted their resources continuously while using their black coffins to recover their injuries.","“Moreover, it took a substantial amount of resources to combine the dead world’s roots with the main world’s roots. I don’t think Tower Canon has much resources left. If Tower Canon had a large amount of resources, fusing the dead world’s roots with the main world’s roots wouldn’t have taken so long.”","Lin Yuan nodded when he heard that.","Lin Yuan had not hoped to gain a large amount of resources from Tower Canon’s old nest.","If Lin Yuan was fully fixated on resources, he could have plundered resources from the main world, like the Eight Pages of Tower Canon had done.","Not only did he not do this, but he even used his own resources to foster the main world’s development.","Lin Yuan mainly wanted to search for Tower Canon’s towers and the Gardener Konjac’s ortets.","Tower Canon had used metals that were at least on the same level as the Reincarnation Gold Jade to build the towers.","Morbius had already broken down Fifth Page Falling Rainbow’s tower into its metal materials, and they were stored in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","...","Lin Yuan and Spring did not take long to sweep through the towers. Although the profits were not significant, there were still profits nonetheless!","Lin Yuan found many spiritual ingredients that contained pure death aura.","These spiritual ingredients did not have any benefits for the main world, so Lin Yuan decided to feed these spiritual ingredients to Silver Corona and Red Thorn.","Lin Yuan then melted down these towers.","Morbius was only calcifying the metals. If it did not activate the metals’ abilities, it did not have to use up much energy.","After cleaning out these towers, Lin Yuan shifted his attention to the base of the castle.","There was a dark door to the entrance of the castle’s first floor. The dark door was sealed tightly and could only be opened by energy that contained death aura.","Spring did not wait for Lin Yuan to take action and punched through the dark door with her left fist. The door shattered with a thunderous bang.","When Spring smashed the dark door, she sensed the death aura that radiated endlessly from below the door. This death aura could cause violent spiritual fluctuations and would have a large impact on a lifeform’s body and intelligence.","Compared to pure death aura, this death aura that contained a large number of dead souls was far more precious!","Spring circulated the energy in her body, and a vortex of wind appeared in front of her.","Spring began compressing the death aura that contained dead souls.","“Lord Saint, let me go on ahead to block any possible dangers! You can stay here to collect resources!","“This circular space extends deep into the ground and ends very close to the ley lines. The deeper you go, the more concentrated the death aura that contains these dead souls.","“If you don’t clean this place, this death aura and the pure death aura will culminate in new types of dead dimensional lifeforms in a few years and they will begin spreading anew.","“There is a piece of knowledge that all experts of the Sky Beyond the Clouds are aware of. After fighting dead dimensional lifeforms, one must clear the battleground immediately after the battle ends, regardless of how bad one’s injuries are.","“There are a few famous cases in the Sky Beyond the Clouds where there was no time to clear the corpses of dead dimensional lifeforms and the remaining dead souls. As a result, the dead spirits rose up again and launched a successful counterattack!”","On his way here, Lin Yuan saw that one level had been turned into a garden. However, the garden did not have a pleasant appearance at all.","Spring was continuously collecting the death aura in the environment. Hence, the concentration of the death aura was falling, and a few plants that relied on the death aura withered.","The only living plants in the garden were those with large leaves covered with scars that Lin Yuan was familiar with.","Lin Yuan found these startling scars to be fascinating.","These plants were the Gardener Konjac that enabled Red Thorn’s Tongue of Relinquish to mutate.","The Gardener Konjac was a fey that could depend on death aura or spirit qi to survive.","Lin Yuan had encountered the Gardener Konjac’s seeds not only in Ji Feng’s body but also obtained one from Whale Ocean Commerce.","It could be said that Lin Yuan understood the Gardener Konjac well.","Lin Yuan instructed the Source Sand to carefully dig around the Gardener Konjac’s roots before he summoned four Hundred Questions Beasts and instructed them to store the Gardener Konjac away.","Lin Yuan did not intend to let Red Thorn consume the Gardener Konjac immediately. Instead, he was going to use a few of the Hundred Questions Beasts to analyze it before nurturing it. Then, he would be able to feed the Gardener Konjac to Red Thorn regularly.","Through this, it was likely that the Tongue of Relinquish would be able to evolve continuously!","If the day came that the Gardener Konjac was no longer able to help the Tongue of Relinquish evolve, Lin Yuan could just destroy the Gardener Konjac!","If the Gardener Konjac could not be of help to him, Lin Yuan would not allow a plant like that to continue living in the main world’s environment. Once the Gardener Konjac was allowed to spread, it would wreak as much havoc as a carcinoma fey!","...","This trip to collect Tower Canon’s resources had met Lin Yuan’s expectations. He felt no motivation to send the Source Sand to look for more resources.","Lin Yuan communicated with his feys in his mind.","He noticed that Genius had been so busy of late that it was no longer as clingy as it used to be.","Instead, Merciful Soul frequently called him out for a chat.","Although Lin Yuan had robbed Merciful Soul from Lu Ou, he had already formed a contract with it.","Lin Yuan treated Merciful Soul the same way that he did his other feys. He did not make it feel like it was any different from the others.","While Lin Yuan was chatting with Merciful Soul, Spring suddenly said, “Lord Saint, I know how Tower Canon managed to activate the dead spirits crisis! I used to think that they were able to do so because the dead world’s roots were healthy and relatively complete. But it turns out that I was wrong. Tower Canon was collecting calamity and turning it into curses. They were cursing the ley lines to weaken them and make them more susceptible to being infected by death aura.”","Spring was about to describe a solution when she saw Lin Yuan raise his hand and summon a strange small beast.","Lin Yuan let Merciful Soul out, and it immediately pounced onto his shoulder and wrapped its tail around his neck before nudging his face with its own soft one.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Merciful Soul.","[Fey Name]: Death Demon Concubine Beast","[Fey Species]: Demon concubine beast species/faceless beast species","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Curse/Spiritual/Soul","[Fey Quality]: Myth II","Abilities:","[Death]: Make a judgment on the target’s willpower, soul, spirit, and mind power. If the judgment decides that the combined power of the four powers is weaker than it, the lifeform will not be able to attack it.","[Heart Words Cross Disaster]: Placing a voiced curse on the target. The strength of the target’s spiritual energy will determine the strength of the curse. Under the influence of the curse, if another curse is placed on the target’s mind, the effects of the curse will multiply, and the target’s soul will start to corrode.","[Demon Concubine’s Promise]: The Death Demon Concubine can turn its heart into a pill that can be gifted to a target. The target will become the Death Demon Concubine’s dependant, and their lives will be tied together.","[Heart Stolen Soul Photographed]: After Disaster Heart curses the target’s soul, it can enter the target’s body and use its soul to control the target’s body.","[Deepened Curse Imprint]: Magnify the effects of the curse on the target and bewitch the target’s mind, soul, and spiritual energy simultaneously.","[Steal the Fate of a Nation]: If it can influence the fate of a country that sits upon a certain area of the earth, the fate can be stolen. The price of this ability is the burning up of one’s lifespan.","[Demon Concubine’s Chaos]: When affecting the fate of the nation that the territory belongs to, a chaotic destiny can be injected into the territory. The chaotic destiny will cause all the lifeforms on the ground to be afflicted by bad luck. The effects of the bad luck will be linked to the strength of the chaotic destiny.","Exclusive Skill:","[Faceless Appearance]: Set a target and absorb its bloodline, spiritual energy, and soul. It will then assume the appearance of the target and obtain all of its abilities.","[Fate of Chaos]: Absorb the fate of the ground it is present on. The fate can be used to enhance the effects of its abilities.","[Payment in Life]: Use its lifespan to investigate the lifespans of other targets. If its own lifespan is sacrificed, it can take away another’s lifespan by touching the target.","Merciful Soul had reached Suzerain X/Myth II. It was a rare curse-type/spiritual-type/soul-type fey.","Merciful Soul was skilled at using curses and could bring misfortune to others. But at the same time, calamity and curses were the best nourishment for it.","If what Spring said was true, Merciful Soul would be the biggest beneficiary of this trip to Tower Canon’s old nest.","Spring was slightly stunned when she saw Merciful Soul.","This was firstly due to Merciful Soul’s abilities. It was rare to come across a fey like Merciful Soul that could absorb calamity and change the fate of an environment. Feys with such abilities were also rarities in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Spring was curious to see what divine kingdom ability Merciful Soul would gain after it evolved to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom. Given Merciful Soul’s current state, it was likely that its divine kingdom ability would be related to curses and fate.","Moreover, Spring had seen the image of Merciful Soul on the wall illustration in her palace.","Otherwise, she would never show such an expression regardless of how outstanding a Suzerain/Myth fey was.","When she saw that Lin Yuan was about to send Merciful Soul to absorb the calamity and curse power around the dead spirit pools in front of them, Spring hurriedly said, “Lord Saint, I suggest that you leave the calamity and curse power alone for now. They will not dissipate after being sealed here.","“You can send your fey to absorb the calamity and curse power after the Returning Saint Pool enlightens your birth horoscope. This will not only facilitate the evolution of your fey’s bloodline but the strength of this calamity and curse power might even enable your fey to reach World Emperor/Divine Kingdom!”","Lin Yuan pursed his lips and asked Spring, “How long will it take for me to head to Epoch God Palace and enlighten my birth horoscope in the Returning Saint Pool?”","Lin Yuan had asked Spring the most pressing question in his mind."]},{"number":2744,"title":"Chapter 2744 Choice of the Priority Birth Horoscope!","paragraphs":["2744 Choice of the Priority Birth Horoscope!","The main world was in the midst of rebuilding after the dead spirits crisis. All sorts of issues could crop up at such a time that would require Lin Yuan to step in to address them.","It would take too long if he used the Returning Saint Pool to cleanse and enlighten his birth horoscope. It was likely that the main world would have already changed drastically by the time he was done.","As things stood, Lin Yuan could not leave the main world alone.","Moreover, he still had resources to collect from the main world’s lifeforms. He would be using the resources he collected from the main world’s lifeforms to return benefits to them. If he fell into a state of slumber, this positive circulation of resources would halt.","Spring seriously told Lin Yuan, “Lord Saint, the Returning Saint Pool is root energy compatible with your body. Bathing in the Returning Saint Pool will improve your body.","“The enlightening of your birth horoscope is only a side effect of improving your body and won’t take too much time. You will only need to spend less than a month bathing in the Returning Saint Pool. Once you emerge from the Returning Saint Pool, you will realize just how incredible your body has become!”","Spring could not tell Lin Yuan all this if he did not ask. But since he had asked, Spring could not give him a detailed explanation.","It went without saying that Spring was only divulging all this information because she was certain that Lin Yuan was the Saint. If Lin Yuan was not the Saint and entered the Returning Saint Pool, the energy in the Returning Saint Pool would short-circuit his body and cause it to explode.","The Body of All Spirits was one of the five pinnacle body types. It contained more energy than regular feys could even fathom.","The energy in the five pinnacle body types repelled each other and could never be properly fused!","Lin Yuan relaxed when he heard that.","He could spare a month.","After the Returning Saint Pool enlightened his birth horoscope, his feys would be able to evolve their grades and qualities without limits.","He would wait until then to allow Merciful Soul to absorb the calamity from here so it could evolve.","After that, he could begin his second round of resource collection and use the spirit qi crystals he harvested to evolve the powers of his other feys.","As Morbius’ grade increased, the number of feys it could spirit lock increased as well.","However, Lin Yuan was in no rush to spirit lock these feys. He would wait until he arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds before he made subsequent plans.","“Spring, I’ve made my decision. Take me to Epoch God Palace! I want to enlighten my birth horoscope!”","Delight spread across Spring’s face.","“Lord Saint, if you want to head to Epoch God Palace, allow me to lead the way! Summer has probably already told Autumn and Winter about you. They should be close to exploding with impatience now!”","Of the four rulers, Winter was slightly stronger than the rest, but the other three had comparable levels of power.","Lin Yuan could not wait to arrive at Epoch God Palace and meet with the rest of his followers.","Firstly, meeting with Autumn and Winter would allow Lin Yuan to gain a large amount of faith power that he could use to develop his divine kingdom.","Furthermore, they were part of his pillars of strength.","Before he made contact with the members of Epoch God Palace, Lin Yuan had been conservative in making his plans for his development in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. He was wary of being targeted.","But now, although he would still develop his power cautiously, he no longer had to worry about being targeted in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Even if he did catch negative attention from a faction, Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter would step in to handle the trouble.","Lin Yuan enjoyed the feeling of having powerful followers to protect him. This would resolve a considerable number of concerns in future tasks.","Although he had decided to go to Epoch God Palace to enlighten his birth horoscope, Lin Yuan and Spring continued to clear out the space below Tower Canon’s basement.","Lin Yuan collected a fair volume of resources from the castle, but they were only useful to dead dimensional lifeforms and were too niche.","Lin Yuan would have to wait until he took control of the dead world’s roots and decided on a lucky dead dimensional lifeform to nurture before these resources could be used.","Just as Spring predicted, the bottom of the castle reached the ley lines.","The main world’s ley lines were originally milky white and emanated a lustrously pure spirit. But after being infected by the dead world’s roots, the ley lines had turned grayish-black and radiated the cold and barren loneliness of death.","Spring paused next to the ley lines for a moment before she said with a smile, “Lord Saint, it’s just as I predicted. Tower Canon indeed lacked the power to fuse the dead world’s roots with this Class 2 world’s roots!","“It’s a good thing that you evolved this Class 1 world to Class 2. Otherwise, the complete fusing of the dead world’s roots with the main world’s roots would have caused severe damage to the main world’s roots. Even if they are separated later on, there will still be problems with the main world’s roots.”","Lin Yuan’s eyes flashed before he asked, “Spring, based on what you just said, does this mean that it’s still possible to extract the dead world’s roots?”","Spring pressed her hand on the ley line and said a moment later, “Lord Saint, give me five days, and I’ll be able to fully extract the dead world’s roots. You can temporarily store the dead world’s roots after being extracted.","“After enlightening your birth horoscope in the Returning Saint Pool, you can then pick a dead dimensional lifeform and nurture it with the dead world’s roots!”","Lin Yuan knew that the death aura in the ley lines would lose their source once Spring extracted the dead world’s roots.","A thought struck Lin Yuan, and he asked, “What if I don’t use the dead world’s roots to nurture a dead dimensional lifeform? Instead, I’ll feed it to my two feys. What do you think?”","Spring shook her head, saying seriously, “Lord Saint, I know you want the two fairies to evolve their bloodlines. The two fairies are able to absorb death aura as a source of energy. That’s why I suggested that you use the death aura to nurture them!","“However, the dead world’s roots are very different from death aura. If you use the dead world’s roots to nurture your two feys, their fairy bloodlines might mutate and their future development might be affected.","“The best way for fairies to increase their power is for them to absorb fairy bloodlines stronger than their own. Fairy bloodlines are easily obtainable in the Sky Beyond the Clouds through trading with factions. If you still want to nurture your two fairies then, you can use your resources to trade for fairy bloodlines with a powerful faction!”","As such, Lin Yuan discarded the idea of using the dead world’s roots to nurture Red Thorn and Silver Corona.","There was a dead dimensional lifeform called the Parasite Death Dark Infant. When it was triggered, it would mutate two to three times in succession. It was a dead dimensional lifeform that mutated easily!","The Parasite Death Dark Infant would attach itself to other lifeforms and begin using its own root energy to decay the main body’s roots. Then, it would take over the body and gain control over the host’s soul and mind.","The Parasite Death Dark Infant had very strong imitating abilities. After taking over its target, it would retract its own energy and imitate an energy similar to the target’s own. This made it very difficult for other lifeforms to notice the Parasite Death Dark Infant’s presence.","There were many good choices for targets among the dead dimensional lifeforms.","Lin Yuan thought about choosing the Parasite Death Dark Infant because his next trip to the Sky Beyond the Clouds would also be his first one, and he did not know anything about the place. The Parasite Death Dark Infant would allow Lin Yuan to take control of other targets there and use these targets to gain information.","Rather than being attracted by the Parasite Death Dark Infant’s power, he was interested in its abilities.","For the past few months, Lin Yuan’s main objective was collecting resources.","People from all over the main world wanted to interact with Lin Yuan, but he did not have the time to speak with every single one of them.","For the next few days when Spring was absorbing the dead world’s roots, Lin Yuan could find the time to speak with these people.","These people were not looking for Lin Yuan because of urgent matters. If they were, Lin Yuan would have replied to them regardless of how busy he was.","The Moon Empress sent a weekly message to Lin Yuan to confirm his condition. This weekly correspondence had become embedded into their relationship.","...","After a long voyage, Wo Lun finally arrived at the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan had asked the Moon Empress to be at the harbor to receive Wo Lun.","Wo Lun was even more useful for the main world’s development than Lin Yuan was!","While Lin Yuan was the main world’s protector, Wo Lun was the driver of structural change in the main world!","With the power of the Radiance Federation and the relationship between the humans and sea clans, the change to human voyage could take place without any issues.","In just the short span of a few decades, there would be no imbalance of power between the federations.","Boats were a tool that could easily be used to conduct migration and resource trading.","This would allow all the federations to enter a period of rapid development.","Lin Yuan thought deeply before deciding on the main world’s development.","Different regions in the main world produced different resources.","Some of these resources were not compatible with human existence. Nonetheless, humans stubbornly insisted on staying there.","The development of trading would save these impoverished regions and would allow the main world’s lifeforms to be connected through their resources.","In Lin Yuan’s previous life, the trading of live resources led to the introduction of invasive species. However, this would not happen in the fey world.","There were differences in power between feys that deterred overt fights.","The biggest issue with trading was the possibility that it would lead to invasions.","The yoke of authority was securely in the hand of the Radiance Federation. It had the power to prevent such invasions from taking place.","Wo Lun had communicated any and all ideas he had to Lin Yuan.","After pointing Wo Lun in the right direction, Lin Yuan did not interfere with Wo Lun’s plans.","If Wo Lun’s ideas were constrained, his creativity would not surpass that of Lin Yuan’s previous life.","Lin Yuan never assumed that a world’s development would immediately take the best and optimal form.","It was possible that Wo Lun’s creativity would surpass the development of the world in Lin Yuan’s previous life!","This world’s oceanic development was only just beginning. Everything was still in the early stages.","For the next few thousands of years, the people from this world would explode with boundless imaginative creativity that was linked to oceanic development.","With the Moon Empress’ level and intelligence, she understood the importance of oceanic development. Without Lin Yuan having to provide too much of an explanation, the Moon Empress placed great importance on Wo Lun’s presence.","The Moon Empress would provide Wo Lun with an abundance of resources.","The main world’s territory expanded when it was promoted to Class 2. When the main world was combined with the five dimensional worlds, the humans gained a large amount of land to develop.","The Moon Empress encouraged the federations to develop the land and expand themselves.","The Radiance Federation’s territory would also expand.","...","After the Moon Empress found out about the matter of Mang Shui, she did not comment on account of Tian Feng.","However, she began taking a personal interest in the manor in the north district. She also sent a tea attendant, five moon envoys, and Mystic Moon to personally check and ask about the manor’s situation. This would guarantee that a similar situation never took place again.","The Moon Empress had interacted with Mang Shui in the past. Her impression of him was that he was careful and cautious while also being capable and thoughtful.","Without such a disposition, Mang Shui would not be so heavily used by Tian Feng, the most eccentric of all the members of royalty. People who could catch his eye had to be a cut above the rest.","Tian Feng was also aware of the importance of the manor in the north district. He had sent Mang Shui there because he felt that Mang Shui was reliable.","However, Mang Shui had changed beyond Tian Feng’s control.","This allowed the Moon Empress to witness how temptation and desire could change a person. Once such a change took place, it would lead to extremely negative consequences unless it was reigned in in time.","This change usually took place in those who possessed power.","The Moon Empress would be investing a lot of energy into this issue from now on.","There was no one better than Iron Prison to handle this matter.","However, there was no question that Iron Prison could not handle this alone.","Night Leaning Moon was also suited for this type of job.","However, as the Chief Guard of the Spirit Guards, Night Leaning Moon was always extremely busy. She did not have time or energy to spend on this matter.","After thinking for a moment, the Moon Empress decided to set up an organization in the main world where its members would keep others in check."]},{"number":2745,"title":"Chapter 2745 Higher Faeries!","paragraphs":["2745 Higher Faeries!","Given the current circumstances, the entire main world would be split into four factions. They were the human-led federations, the sea clans under the Vast Sea Labyrinth, the feys in the Heavenly Family Cottage, and the dimensional lifeforms led by the Afterlife Realm Dictators.","With the main world’s factions as complicated as they were, it was impossible for the vast main world to be supervised by just one or two people. A small number of people would be unable to oversee the entire main world, and it would be inevitable for incidents of favoritism to arise.","Unfairness was the beginning of devolution into chaos.","With such circumstances, the best method would be to pick representatives from each faction and allow the factions to keep each other in check. This method would be the most effective at preventing unfairness.","However, this endeavor was not simple and required a significant amount of effort.","Nonetheless, the Moon Empress was willing to invest her time and energy into this matter.","Once this group was functioning smoothly, the main world would enjoy an extended period of balance and peace.","There were more than 37,000 human federations. It was clear that it was impossible to pick representatives from each federation.","When trying to establish fairness, there were other considerations aside from fairness itself.","If the humans sent out thousands of representatives, it would be too complicated for them to look after each other.","Ever since the Major Federation Union was established, the federations no longer cared about the Major Federation Meeting.","Nevertheless, the Moon Empress felt there was still a need to hold the Major Federation Meeting.","After the dead spirits crisis came to an end, the entire world would enter a period of martial prosperity.","The Moon Empress planned to raise the rewards for the Major Federation Meeting.","The Major Federation Meeting would be hosted by a different human federation every three years instead of being held on an uninhabited island like it used to be.","As long as there were boats that could be used for long voyages, the Major Federation Meeting would bring new human traffic to the federations and boost their tourism industry.","In the past, there was only tourism in the big cities of each federation. But now, any federation chosen to be the host would be able to receive substantial profits. Hence, all the federations would be clamoring to host the Major Federation Meeting.","Becoming a federation envoy was the highest honor for a member of the younger generation in a federation. They should not become symbols of an era.","With this thought, the Moon Empress sought out Iron Prison.","...","Lin Yuan had picked up on the incident in the north manor in time and used the method of handling Mang Shui to send a warning to all those who had similar thoughts. However, the incident still left a significant impact on the Radiance Federation. After all the fighting they had recently done, there were many factions who continued to be ready to brandish their swords at any moment.","Negative incidents of factions fighting with each other had been breaking out, and Iron Prison was constantly dealing with them.","If the Moon Empress did not seek him out in these two weeks, Iron Prison would go and see her about this matter.","Iron Prison was always aware of the gap between him and the Moon Empress.","Despite both of them being members of the Radiance Federation’s royalty, she used to be a Class 5 Creation Master and was now a Class 6 Creation Master.","During imperial meetings, the Moon Empress, Chef Supreme, and the Bamboo Monarch sat on the same level as the other members of royalty. But in actuality, the three of them were of a higher status than the other members of royalty.","This was especially so now that the Moon Empress was supplying all of the Radiance Federation’s resources. Her disciple was also the one who enabled the main world to evolve.","Hence, Iron Prison changed the attitude he took toward the Moon Empress to one of respect.","It went without saying that Iron Prison’s respect did not only stem from the Moon Empress’ strength but also because he acknowledged her.","Otherwise, not only would he refuse to submit to her, but he would even stubbornly oppose her!","...","When the Moon Empress saw the state that Iron Prison was in, she poured out a cup of tea for him before saying solemnly, “Iron Prison, I have focused on dealing with the dead spirits crisis of late and neglected the management of the Radiance Federation. You must be aware of the Radiance Federation’s circumstances! I hope that you’ll tell me everything as it is.","“After the dead spirits crisis ends, the most important matter will be that of the Radiance Federation’s internal management. I don’t want any similar incidents to appear again in the future. I also don’t want the Radiance Federation’s factions to always be ready to attack each other!”","Iron Prison understood the Moon Empress’ meaning. He also knew why the Moon Empress had come to see him.","Iron Prison said seriously, “It won’t be easy to change the current situation among the Radiance Federation’s factions. We can ensure that the factions won’t clash again but can’t dissolve the resentment and animosity that has already built up.","“You might not be aware of this, but there are many factions that are fighting even more ferociously than in the manor in the north district. Blood was spilled in many other places.","“There are factions declaring blood feuds against each other daily. It has gotten so serious that I was forced to close the ultimate fighting ground! It will take at least a few decades to comb out all the relationships between the factions and restore the previous state of harmony!","“Dealing with Mang Shui was indeed a way of warning some people, but this warning is far from enough. A longer period of control and management is still necessary.”","Iron Prison’s tone became sterner as he continued. “The resources from your disciple are far too startling. Even we members of royalty have never had the opportunity to receive such resources, much less the other factions!”","After hearing what Iron Prison said, the Moon Empress knew that there was no need for her to elaborate because Iron Prison shared her thoughts and could understand her meaning immediately after hearing her decision.","“Iron Prison, I’ll give you two years. In these two years, first sort out the combative environment among the factions. Two years later, I will establish a mutual supervision group made up of factions across the main world. You will represent the group from the Radiance Federation.","“With your abilities, two years should be enough to accomplish this! If you agree, I will announce this decision at the imperial meeting three days later.”","Iron Prison could sense the trust that the Moon Empress had in him.","Iron Prison was well aware of his bad temper. Aside from Cicada Song, Iron Prison did not have deep ties with the other members of royalty. It could be said that he had the worst interpersonal ties among all the members of the Radiance Federation’s royalty.","Later, when the Moon Empress’ lifespan was endangered, Iron Prison decided to use his own sacred source lifeform to extend her life. It was only then that their relationship improved.","The Moon Empress still did not like Iron Prison, but this did not mean that she did not admire his character.","The Spacetime Elder had given Iron Prison such an arrangement in the past because it prevented his talents from going to waste. The Moon Empress was going the same now.","There were many members of royalty with free time. However, the Moon Empress deemed Iron Prison to be the most suitable of the lot.","She believed that he would be willing to take on this task.","“Moon Empress, I have no reason to turn down this task you’re giving me! I will make sure to get the Radiance Federation’s surface layer under control. Enabling the Radiance Federation to come off as peaceful isn’t a challenge for me at all!","“The method of keeping each other in check is effective at managing not only the entire main world but the Radiance Federation as well! I will pick some elites from the members of royalty’s subordinates and manage the Radiance Federation through them. The elites belonging to the camps of different members of royalty will also supervise each other.”","After he was done speaking, Iron Prison did not stay long. He did not even finish drinking the cup of tea the Moon Empress had poured out for him.","This did not bother the Moon Empress because she knew that this was just his personality.","Iron Prison did not have much of an EQ, but he did have the character befitting of a member of royalty.","The Moon Empress intended to have a talk with Tian Feng after the next imperial meeting ended. She was going to tell him not to overly blame himself for his erroneous decision but to focus on the future development of the Radiance Federation instead!","This dead spirits crisis allowed the Moon Empress to see the importance of Cultivated Garden.","Cultivated Garden was the source of supply for the Radiance Federation’s foundational resources. These foundational resources could not be replaced by high-quality resources.","High-quality resources were beneficial for spirit qi professionals who already had some power, while low-quality resources were meant for the millions of regular people who lived in the Radiance Federation.","The burden of responsibility on Tian Feng’s shoulders was a very heavy one!","Tian Feng was not the kind of person who could be convinced through advice. Once he became bogged down by his thoughts, it would take some time for him to regain his footing!","...","While the Moon Empress was handling the Radiance Federation’s affairs, Spring had finished gathering the dead world’s roots. She stored them inside a special amber bottle.","Spring placed this bottle in Lin Yuan’s hand and said earnestly, “Lord Saint, the dead world’s roots are of a very high level. It will have a large impact on lifeforms below the Divine Kingdom level. Do not use the dead world’s roots on other lifeforms without careful consideration.”","Lin Yuan nodded seriously, making a mental note of Spring’s words.","“Spring, I will seek your help when I decide to use the dead world’s roots to nurture or strengthen other lifeforms! I already have a target in mind.”","Spring could tell that Lin Yuan trusted her, and she could not help but smile brightly.","“Lord Saint, you can give me instructions whenever you want as long as you need me!”","After removing the dead world’s roots from the ley lines, Spring used her energy to seal Tower Canon’s castle. She would immediately be alerted if anyone tried to enter the castle.","Spring knew that Lin Yuan was going to use the calamity in the castle to strengthen Merciful Soul in the future!","Lin Yuan followed Spring to Epoch God Palace.","...","With Spring leading the way, Lin Yuan arrived at the entrance of Epoch God Palace very quickly.","As he looked at the mountain with the four seasons clearly distinguished on it, Lin Yuan could not help but feel both a sense of familiarity as well as amazement.","The Snow Celestial Mountain had been far from as majestic and mystical as this mountain.","Spring saw Lin Yuan looking at Four Seasons Mountain and said seriously, “Lord Saint, this Four Seasons Mountain has the potential to become a higher faerie. However, even after being promoted to a Class 2 world, this world can’t handle the Heaven’s Trial of a higher faerie.","“If you want to take this Four Seasons Mountain with you when you leave for the Sky Beyond the Clouds, there will be no need to continue suppressing the Four Seasons Mountain’s bloodline, and it will be able to evolve into a higher faerie.","“The appearance of a higher faerie in the Sky Beyond the Clouds will immediately lead to a meeting with the people from Faerie Institution. Then, you’ll be able to use Four Seasons Mountain to become acquainted with Faerie Institution.","“Although Faerie Institution is a faction made up of faeries, they have never been against interacting with other factions. But if any harm comes to a faerie, they will bring down their wrath with no mercy. Faeries are the strongest species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. This is largely related to the unity of the faeries.”","Lin Yuan looked at Four Seasons Mountain in surprise. He had not expected it to not only have the potential to evolve into a higher faerie but already be ready for the evolution!","The only reason it had yet to evolve was that its grade was being suppressed.","Lin Yuan really liked listening to Spring talk about the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Although he was present in the main world, this allowed him to gain a better understanding of the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan was very willing to interact with Faerie Institution when he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Through his interactions with Celestial Sight and Begin Lady, Lin Yuan had a very good impression of the faerie species. Moreover, it seemed that his body composition naturally attracted faeries.","At that moment, Lin Yuan sensed two powerful auras emanating from within Epoch God Palace. These two aura were heavily permeated by emotion.","Normally, experts with such auras should not appear now.","Summer was currently extracting death aura from the Startling Lines Continent’s ley lines.","The only entities in Epoch God Palace who were willing to reveal their auras to Spring were Autumn and Winter, who were also rulers of Epoch God Palace.","Autumn and Winter were also followers of the Saint. It was clear that they were releasing their auras in response to his arrival.","While Lin Yuan was thinking of the right way to address Autumn and Winter, two figures appeared and knelt in front of him. They performed the same greetings that Spring and Summer did when they first showed themselves to him.","Just as Lin Yuan was about to help Autumn and Winter up, Spring said softly, “Lord Saint, let them finish their greetings! They have been waiting for many epochs to pass just to see you!”"]},{"number":2746,"title":"Chapter 2746 The Returning Saint Pool!","paragraphs":["2746 The Returning Saint Pool!","Spring understood how Autumn and Winter were feeling.","They were feeling the same way she felt when she first saw him.","Autumn had been blaming himself recently, especially after he heard Summer talk about Lin Yuan.","Tower Canon had almost assassinated Lord Saint, and his life was almost in danger of coming to an end! This information caused Autumn’s heart to start thumping rapidly.","Autumn was Epoch God Palace’s first representative to contact Tower Canon. He truly regretted not eliminating Tower Canon then and giving them the opportunity to harm Lord Saint later!","Winter was the first of the followers to join Lord Saint’s side.","When he saw Lin Yuan and sensed Morbius’ aura on Lin Yuan’s wrist, Winter could not prevent tears from springing to his eyes.","After sincerely greeting Lin Yuan, the two of them stood up and joined Lin Yuan behind Spring.","Regardless of how overwhelmed they felt, the two of them restrained themselves. As followers, they did not have the right to initiate communication with Lin Yuan! They could only engage with him when he asked them questions.","Lin Yuan did not have social anxiety, especially when he was aware of the status of Autumn and Winter.","Lin Yuan immediately asked, “Where is the Returning Saint Pool? Take me there now. Firstly, I need to enlighten my birth horoscope to verify my identity. Secondly, I need to increase my power as soon as possible.”","When Spring followed Lin Yuan, she responded immediately to his questions. But now, she gave Autumn and Winter the opportunity to communicate with Lin Yuan instead.","Autumn was the first to speak. “Lord Saint, the Returning Saint Pool is at the center of the four palaces. If you want to head there, I will take you immediately!”","Autumn immediately began leading the way.","Normally, Autumn was very respectful toward Winter, who was an elder. He always gave way to him.","But now that he had the chance to interact with Lin Yuan, Autumn was not going to give way like he usually did. Rather, he seemed to have competitive intentions.","Winter took out a crystalline object.","This crystalline item looked solid but moved between a wispy cloud-like state and a tangible state in Winter’s palm.","Winter carefully held up this crystalline item in front of Lin Yuan.","“Lord Saint, this is pure soul energy that I tempered using my soul. Any lifeform can absorb it. The lifeform might not benefit from absorbing the soul energy and might even be negatively affected.","“I’m not trying to ask you to absorb my soul energy. You can use this energy to activate the Returning Saint Pool’s water. This will shorten the time taken for you to enlighten your birth horoscope!”","Spring and Summer looked at Winter poignantly.","Winter was the strongest of the four of them. He was also the only one who had reached the level of being able to temper his soul into a nourishing supplement.","Winter began tempering his soul when Epoch God Palace first arrived in this world.","This energy was a heartfelt gesture from him.","Lin Yuan frowned slightly but did not immediately reach out to receive the soul energy.","Firstly, Spring clearly said that it would only take him around a month to enlighten his birth horoscope in the Returning Saint Pool. A month was not a long time for Lin Yuan, and he could spare the time. Hence, he did not need to shorten the time it took to enlighten his birth horoscope.","This item that Winter had condensed from his soul had to be very precious to him.","“Winter, if you absorb the item in your hand, will it be able to evolve your soul because the energy came from your own soul? Or will there be drawbacks?”","Winter was slightly stunned. Lin Yuan’s words allowed Winter to see that this iteration of the Saint had a very different personality from the previous one.","The previous Saint would never turn down such an offering. Yet, despite this being their first meeting, this Saint was already thinking for his sake.","Regardless of how his personality changed, it made no difference to Winter as long as it was confirmed that Lin Yuan was the Saint.","Winter said candidly, “If I absorb this ball of soul energy, my soul will be significantly nourished. I will be able to heal 2/3 of the damage my soul suffered from being tempered.”","Lin Yuan told Winter sincerely, “If that’s the case, you can absorb this item! Don’t do anything like this that harms yourself again. Even if you want to help me, you don’t have to do it by depleting yourself.”","While he spoke, a thought struck Lin Yuan. Throughout their journey together, he had not asked Spring what resources she used to increase her power.","Now that Spring, Autumn, and Winter were in front of him, Lin Yuan admired the beauty of Epoch God Palace while asking, “Spring, Autumn, Winter, what kind of resources do you usually need to increase your power?”","In this enormous main world, there did not seem to be any resource that was of a particularly high level. The resources that Lin Yuan produced on his own had already reached the peak of the main world.","It seemed as though he could also secure a monopoly over the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Autumn had already communicated with Lin Yuan. Although Autumn really wanted to continue interacting with Lin Yuan, he decided to give the chance to Winter.","Winter said seriously, “Lord Saint, the four of us have very different body compositions. But as long as we have sufficient pure spirit qi, our bodies will be able to evolve however we like.”","Lin Yuan did not immediately take out the spirit qi crystals because he did not know the purity of the spirit qi that Winter was referring to.","Lin Yuan would not assume that the spirit qi he produced could meet Winter’s expectations.","Although Lin Yuan had the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Green Vine, he could not fathom Winter’s level.","“What is the percentage purity of spirit qi that you require?”","Spring, Autumn, and Winter all understood Lin Yuan’s intent. It was clear that he wanted to provide them with resources.","In this regard, Lin Yuan was the same as the previous Saint!","Spring, Autumn, and Winter were all Lin Yuan’s followers. It was normal for followers to use their master’s resources.","Winter did not beat around the bush and said, “What we need now is to increase the purity of this world to 94% and above, then begin absorbing the spirit qi.","“Spirit qi that is less pure than that won’t benefit our power. Instead, it will contaminate our bodies and increase the impurities within our bodies! Because of this reason, our faction has been increasing our power very slowly. I am the only one who has achieved a breakthrough.”","Lin Yuan was surprised to hear this, but at the same time, he relaxed.","He had not expected an expert of Winter’s level would only require spirit qi with a 94% purity. This was much lower than the concentration of spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Lin Yuan normally used spirit qi of at least 98% purity to evolve his feys!","This allowed Lin Yuan to recognize just how powerful Morbius was.","Lin Yuan took out four wooden chests. The heavy chests thumped when they landed on the ground, each containing 10,000 spirit qi crystals.","“During the time that I’m in seclusion, the three of you can each take a wooden chest and use the spirit qi crystals within it to evolve yourselves! One of you will deliver the fourth wooden chest to Summer.”","Normally, he would not have given away these many resources regardless of how generous Lin Yuan was. He was only giving away such a large amount of resources now because he was certain they were his followers.","Just like how Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter needed to verify Lin Yuan’s identity, Lin Yuan also sensed solid faith power flowing into him from Autumn and Winter the moment he met them.","Faith power could not lie.","The four rulers of Epoch God Palace were Lin Yuan’s strongest combat power. The stronger they were, the more protection Lin Yuan would have in the future.","Moreover, 40,000 spirit qi crystals did not put a large hole in Lin Yuan’s pocket.","Lin Yuan would continue to supply the four of them with spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan was only providing them with 10,000 spirit qi crystals this time because he wanted to gauge the ability of spirit qi crystals to enable experts like Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter to evolve!","Spring, Autumn, and Winter performed a ritual of respect toward Lin Yuan.","Each of them picked up a chest filled with spirit qi crystals.","The three of them were only able to reach their current level of power because they used the resources they received from the Saint. The Saint was also the one who had helped them to activate their body compositions.","The three of them were very familiar with spirit qi crystals.","After such a long time, the four of them could finally receive this level of resources again!","With these spirit qi crystals, they could finally increase their power again despite being in a Class 2 world.","Spring was silent for a moment before she picked up the last box of spirit qi crystals on the ground.","“Lord Saint, I will deliver the spirit qi crystals to Summer while you head to the Returning Saint Pool to enlighten your birth horoscope. Then, I will stay to gather the death aura in the ley lines with Summer.”","Lin Yuan nodded.","Autumn had already led Lin Yuan to the cross between the four large palaces.","There were white jade pillars erected here. Each pillar was draped in a special veil. The layers of gauze floated in the wind and shrouded the space between the pillars.","As Lin Yuan stood here, he felt his soul shudder. Something within the space was calling him forward.","Autumn bowed and made an ushering gesture.","“Lord Saint, this is considered forbidden ground. Aside from you, no one else is allowed to enter. If you want to enlighten your birth horoscope, all you need to do is step in. While you’re enlightening your birth horoscope, the water in the Returning Saint Pool will temper your body and soul.","“You have already tempered the impurities in your body, spiritual energy, and soul, so you should know about the pain you will need to endure during the process. If you can’t endure the agony, you can call us in to help you.”","Lin Yuan shook his head.","As long as his life was not in danger, he could handle pain. He was not the type to shy away from agony and hardship.","Rather, he appreciated the opportunity to temper his body, spiritual energy, and soul.","Lin Yuan looked forward to the growth he would receive from the Returning Saint Pool. Once he enlightened his birth horoscope, he would be able to distinguish himself even among the older generation!","Not many of the Radiance Federation’s members of royalty had enlightened their birth horoscope.","Luckily, Lin Yuan was there to provide resources to the members of royalty, and it would not be long before another birth-horoscope expert emerged from the Radiance Federation’s members of royalty.","Lin Yuan stepped through the layer of gossamer. The nearer he walked to the Returning Saint Pool, the more he felt a sense of innate intimacy. It was as though he was facing himself.","At that point, Lin Yuan no longer doubted that he was the Saint.","The tent was spacious, and the main space was very wide. There was a large pool that had yet to transform into a spirit pool at the center of the space.","It was clear that this pool was the Returning Saint Pool that was going to enable him to enlighten his birth horoscope.","Lin Yuan quickly stepped forward, and the Returning Saint Pool turned a beautiful amber that resembled a pool of tea.","Lin Yuan squatted down and placed his hand in the pool. He noticed that the pool was almost the exact same temperature as his body.","Rather than seeming like water, the pool water seemed like an entity that would not contaminate his hair and skin.","Even if Lin Yuan sank his entire arm into the pool, his sleeve remained dry after he lifted his arm out.","Lin Yuan could sense that a portion of the abilities in the pool water had entered his body through his palm.","A warm and comfortable wave washed over Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan jumped into the Returning Saint Pool.","The depth of the Returning Saint Pool just happened to reach right below his nose.","Lin Yuan was able to breathe comfortably, even with his mouth closed.","At the instant that he jumped into the Returning Saint Pool, the amber fluid sprayed jets of fluid resembling flower petals while Lin Yuan seemed to be the flower’s core.","The amber fluid moved outward around Lin Yuan, and streams of amber fluid formed mysterious patterns.","Lin Yuan’s eyes were currently open as he watched the changes take place.","But it was not long before he clenched his jaw tightly.","Lin Yuan felt warm and comfortable when a wisp of energy within the Returning Saint Pool entered his body. But when buckets of the energy were pouring into his body, he felt as though he had turned into a sealed jar.","Not only was his body growing increasingly warmer, but he also had to endure piercing pain shooting through his spirit and soul.","This pain was only climbing.","At first, the pain seemed like the pricks from needles. But in less than two minutes, Lin Yuan felt as though his soul and spirit were being ground by something.","Lin Yuan clenched his fists tightly as he silently endured all this.","He knew that his spirit and soul were only feeling this way because they were being destroyed and reconfigured over and over again, thereby evolving through this process.","Normally, the pain in his soul and spirit were more excruciating than the pain in his body. But in the Returning Saint Pool, the pain of Lin Yuan’s body was much more intense than the pain of his soul and spirit!"]},{"number":2747,"title":"Chapter 2747 Above Sacred Source 12 Stars!","paragraphs":["2747 Above Sacred Source 12 Stars!","Lin Yuan’s body was like a piece of soap that was melting in the Returning Saint Pool.","Lin Yuan was using this method to trade the energy within himself and that of the Returning Saint Pool.","It was as though the Returning Saint Pool was a part of Lin Yuan’s body.","It was both itchy and agonizing for Lin Yuan’s body to constantly melt and be remolded.","Pain was an endurable feeling to gnash one’s teeth and endure as long as one was strong enough.","However, itchiness could easily cause a person’s willpower to crumble.","Anyone who had experienced being cut by a knife knew that the itchy part of wound healing was much more salient than the pain.","Lin Yuan’s body was being externally remolded but the itchiness permeated his entire power.","Even with Lin Yuan’s willpower, he could not help but let out a groan.","Lin Yuan’s body shuddered under the pain and itch.","Lin Yuan had never been in such a sorry state ever since he arrived in this world.","Lin Yuan bit his lip forcefully to stave off the itchiness. His teeth almost immediately tore his lip. Fresh blood dripped from Lin Yuan’s lips and spread out in the Returning Saint Pool.","Lin Yuan had not noticed that his blood had turned golden-red. The golden-red blood even had a jade-like sheen.","Lin Yuan curled up his body, hugged his legs, and sank to the bottom of the Returning Saint Pool in this fetal position.","When he instinctively entered this state, he felt the pain and itch alleviate considerably.","However, the exchange of energy between the Returning Saint Pool and his body sped up significantly.","It did not take long before Lin Yuan clearly sensed that his body had improved.","When Lin Yuan circulated his energy, he realized that in the short span of an hour, the energy in his body now circulated at more than seven times its original speed.","Moreover, the energy could spread to many more channels in his body.","When Lin Yuan circulated his energy, the rate at which spirit qi was purified in his body also increased substantially compared to before.","At the same time, Lin Yuan could sense that his two souls were showing signs of fusing. Lin Yuan was certain that this was due to the Returning Saint Pool.","It was likely that two souls did not fit with the usual conditions for a birth horoscope expert.","Now that the two souls were showing signs of fusing, it seemed that it was an inevitability.","Indeed, a lifeform’s birth horoscope represented its fate. There should not be the existence of two fates in a stable lifeform.","However, Lin Yuan felt the twinge of dilemma.","The existence of two souls allowed Lin Yuan to contract more sacred source lifeforms. Lin Yuan was concerned that he would be forced to lower the number of sacred source lifeforms he could contract once his souls were fused.","Spring allowed Lin Yuan to understand something: even experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds contracted sacred source lifeforms, and they were also limited in the number of sacred source lifeforms they could contract.","The 12 Stars of sacred source lifeforms were the mechanism by which lower-class worlds categorized the strengths of sacred source lifeforms.","At the Sky Beyond the Clouds, there was another way to distinguish the levels of sacred source lifeforms.","After sacred source lifeforms broke through past 12 Stars, they would reach a level called Divine Kingdom Banner. It was divided into ten levels. It was given this name because sacred source lifeforms needed to have their own divine kingdom in order to break through past 12 Stars.","The experts whose sacred source lifeforms had yet to reach the divine kingdom would not be able to experience such a breakthrough!","Hence, being able to contract sacred source lifeforms was also a good thing in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","While these thoughts were running through Lin Yuan’s mind and he was awash in conflicted feelings, Morbius’ voice appeared beside Lin Yuan’s body.","Morbius was no longer in a semi-solid state when it materialized in reality.","In terms of looks, it was almost an exact carbon copy of Lin Yuan. Morbius had a colder and sterner expression if they really had to be compared in detail. Its eyes were not as gentle as that of Lin Yuan.","“Partner, fusing your two souls to awaken your birth horoscope won’t weaken the quality of your two souls. Instead, they will be improved. At that time, you will still be able to contract more sacred source lifeforms than the average person!","“When your two souls become one, they will become more resistant to damage when you’re in danger! This is a good thing for you. Based on my unlocked memory, it’s true that you’re the reincarnation of the Saint.","“I am also the Totem God they are referring to. I know what you’ve been worried about. Being a reincarnation doesn’t mean that you have to become someone else. As the Saint, you can continue being as kind as you’ve always been. The only thing that has been combined is your memories from both lives.","“Those memories have always been in you. You should be hoping that you won’t have anything holding you back in the road ahead and can march forward to wherever your heart takes you!”","After speaking, Morbius injected a portion of its root energy into Lin Yuan’s body.","Morbius’ main body on Lin Yuan’s wrist released a blinding reddish-brown light and seemed to transform into a fish that began swimming around the Returning Saint Pool.","When Morbius injected its root energy into his body, Lin Yuan’s mind throbbed.","Much of the pain and itch had disappeared.","However, Lin Yuan could tell that they had not truly disappeared but were being shared by his companion Morbius. Morbius was also experiencing the same pain and itchiness he was feeling.","“Partner, I can do more than share the good times with you. Let me share the pain with you. This won’t affect the awakening of your body composition in the slightest! I really want to walk alongside you, just like how you’ve been helping me to evolve my grade!","“The energy in the Returning Saint Pool is only just beginning to be activated. You will still have to remain here in the Returning Saint Pool for a very long time and will have to endure an extended period of pain. So you better compose your mind now.","“Otherwise, you might run out of steam and fall into a state of slumber! If that happens, the Returning Saint Pool won’t be able to evolve your spirit and soul!”","Morbius’ words touched Lin Yuan. It felt good to have a companion to walk through life with.","Lin Yuan took out spiritual ingredients that could bolster the spirit and held them in his mouth.","After the Returning Saint Pool enlightened his birth horoscope, his power would skyrocket.","In the eyes of the main world, an A-rank spirit qi professional was the equivalent of an emperor-class expert.","But once an expert awakened his birth horoscope, he would gain power beyond the Eternal level. At that point, Lin Yuan would have crossed over the Creation, Immortal, and Eternal levels!","It was highly possible that such an opportunity only came along once in a person’s life! Hence, Lin Yuan was going to do everything he could to grab ahold of it.","Even if the pain in his body, soul, and spirit increased to five times its current level, and he had to remain here for five months, Lin Yuan would press on without hesitation.","Lin Yuan was confident of this even if he was alone, much less now that he had Morbius’ support!","Time slipped by day by day.","During this time, Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter were using the resources provided by Lin Yuan to increase their powers while they waited for Lin Yuan to emerge from the Returning Saint Pool.","Once Lin Yuan stepped out of the Returning Saint Pool, his Body of All Spirits would be fully awakened. At that point, he could use his body to control any species’ bloodlines.","Their Body of Four Seasons could be linked to the Body of All Spirits once it was awakened. At that time, they could transfer their energy to the Body of All Spirits and enable the Body of All Spirits’ bloodline to be tempered.","The four of them preferred to be of help to Lin Yuan rather than staying by his side to protect him.","After absorbing the last spirit qi crystal, Autumn opened his eyes. He could not remember the last time he absorbed spirit qi of such high purity!","Even in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, only Lin Yuan could coordinate his body composition with the Totem God to produce spirit qi of such high purity.","With his body nourished by such pure spirit qi, Autumn could feel that the locks on that gate were finally budging.","When Winter absorbed the last spirit qi crystal and opened his eyes as well, Autumn glanced in the direction of the Returning Saint Pool and asked Winter with a hint of concern in his voice, “Winter, Lord Saint must endure considerable pain while using the Returning Saint Pool to enlighten his birth horoscope and awaken his Body of All Spirits. Do you think—”","Before Autumn could finish speaking, he was sharply interrupted by Winter, “Autumn, don’t forget your place. All you need to do is fulfill the tasks of your station! Don’t think about other things you don’t need to consider!","“There is no way that Lord Saint will fail to enlighten his birth horoscope and awaken his body composition. There’s no need for you to worry! I have already opened the path to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","“Once Lord Saint steps out from the Returning Saint Pool, he can decide to go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds at any time. I know you are the most anxious of the four of us to return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","“But you have to understand one thing, which is that Lord Saint is the one who decides when and if we’ll return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. We cannot use our actions or words to influence him toward any sort of decision. You should be aware of this!”","All of them had different personalities. Winter and Autumn had spent countless epochs together, and Winter knew Autumn’s character well.","Autumn would never do anything that harmed Lin Yuan. As his follower, he shared the same attitude and thoughts as the rest of them.","However, Autumn’s personality needed to be slightly mellowed.","Lord Saint needed steady people by his side.","Autumn nodded ardently when he heard what Winter said.","It was not true that Autumn had not improved in the slightest after all the epochs that had passed. He was also constantly growing.","Autumn was always aware of his own issues.","When he interacted with Spring, Summer, and Winter, Autumn consciously worked on correcting his issues.","Although he had not caused any direct trouble for Lin Yuan, it was true that he had affected Lin Yuan’s judgment.","A small smile appeared on Winter’s face when Autumn nodded.","“Spring has gone to help Summer handle the death aura in the ley lines. It won’t take the two of them long to work together to gather all the death aura in the ley lines. The people we’ve sent out have already fully understood this Class 2 world’s circumstances. You are aware of how Lord Saint feels toward the natives of this world.","“I think that Lord Saint will remain in this world for almost a century to help it to develop. Rather than thinking about going to the Sky Beyond the Clouds now, we should think about how we can help Lord Saint to develop this Class 2 world!","“Before we confirmed Lord Saint’s identity, you could take this Class 2 world lightly. But now, this Class 2 world is Lord Saint’s homeland. Given our understanding of Lord Saint, this place will eventually become the sacred ground of the Sky Beyond the Clouds!”","A month passed in the blink of an eye. During this month, Lin Yuan endured a mix of pain and itchiness. There were countless instances where he was on the brink of giving up.","It was just as Morbius said. The first day’s pain and itchiness were nothing but a small appetizer. In the subsequent days, the agony increased by at least three times of that of the first day!","Luckily, he had Morbius there to share the load with him and endure the month together.","Now, Lin Yuan had successfully awakened his body composition and enlightened his birth horoscope. He was now a certified birth horoscope expert!","The amber fluid returned to its original transparency when Lin Yuan stepped out of the Returning Saint Pool.","If Lin Yuan did not control his body, the spirit qi would have gathered around his body like a tsunami to nourish him.","Furthermore, after his body was tempered and condensed, his two souls had fused into one.","A birth horoscope with 12 dots of light circled Lin Yuan’s soul. The birth horoscope embedded itself above his divine kingdom and shone like a gem above the divine kingdom.","Lin Yuan could clearly sense that the quality of his soul had improved. Additionally, his spiritual energy had been significantly improved.","Lin Yuan enjoyed this feeling of an improved body. The current condition of his body made him feel like the past month of agony had been worth it!","The mermaid thearch bloodline in his body was no longer entangled with his own bloodline.","Lin Yuan’s bloodline was now the main pillar while his mermaid thearch bloodline was only a small branch. It was as though the mermaid thearch bloodline was nothing compared to his bloodline!"]},{"number":2748,"title":"Chapter 2748 The Jasmine Lily’s Evolution!","paragraphs":["2748 The Jasmine Lily’s Evolution!","This feeling was very strange for Lin Yuan.","Previously, the mermaid bloodline dominated his own bloodline.","But now, his bloodline had been improved in the Returning Saint Pool and was suppressing the mermaid thearch bloodline. It was as though he could now manipulate the mermaid thearch bloodline at will.","Previously, Lin Yuan still had some suspicions about whether he was truly the Saint as Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter claimed.","But now, it was ascertained that he was indeed the Saint.","Lin Yuan turned to look at the now colorless Returning Saint Pool.","The moment Lin Yuan saw his reflection in the Returning Saint Pool, his entire body froze.","His facial appearance had not changed drastically and still resembled his previous self. However, his features and bone structure had changed slightly in the Returning Saint Pool.","Previously, his features and bone structure were considered near-perfect. But now, they were absolutely exquisite.","Regardless of how much favor the creator showed a particular lifeform, they would not allow any lifeform to have features and a bone structure similar to the one that Lin Yuan had now.","Lin Yuan already had an extremely outstanding deportment. With the support from his deportment, Lin Yuan’s aura could no longer be described as elite.","The description’ heavenly tyrannical’ was not an exaggeration when it was directed at his features and bone structure.","Lin Yuan took out a piece of casual wear made from moonbeam brocade from his spatial equipment.","Most of Lin Yuan’s clothes were made by Wen Yu, and only a few of them had been sewn by the Moon Empress. This piece of casual wear happened to be one of the few.","When Lin Yuan wore this set of clothes, he looked as though he was draped in moonlight.","Lin Yuan circulated the energy in his body and realized with shock that the amount of spirit qi that passed through his body each second was comparable to the volume of one spirit qi crystal.","After being strengthened by the Returning Saint Pool, Lin Yuan’s spirit qi production ability was now just as strong as Morbius’.","Epoch God Palace sat atop 17 spirit veins. If all of them were mined, hundreds of tons of energy ores would be produced.","One of the reasons for Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter deciding to build Epoch God Palace there was its favorable environment.","Additionally, they wanted to prepare resources for Lin Yuan so he could harvest and use them when they finally found him.","Otherwise, if Tower Canon or the humans happened to discover this place during such a long passage of time, they would definitely begin mining the resources for their own benefit.","Due to the presence of the 17 spirit veins, this environment was highly concentrated with spirit qi.","Lin Yuan did not rush to leave the Returning Saint Pool. He sat down cross-legged on the ground and began carefully examining both the feys he had spirit-locked and those he had contracted.","Feys like Shiny, Genius, Chimey, and the rest needed to absorb other resources aside from spirit qi. Hence, they could not evolve their grades solely using spirit qi or by having pure spirit qi injected into their bodies.","However, this was possible for Blackie and the Jasmine Lily.","The Praying Universe Soul Whale needed to absorb soul energy, while the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom needed to absorb fire-elemental energy.","Lin Yuan had plenty of fire-elemental energy.","Lin Yuan would have regarded soul energy as a rare and scarce resource six months ago. He could not start a war to collect the souls of millions of people just to nurture Rememberling.","But now, with the dead spirits crisis, there was a large number of souls floating around in the main world. After absorbing these souls, Rememberling’s grade and quality would be able to evolve rapidly!","Lin Yuan did not have time to take Rememberling around the main world to absorb energy. However, he could send experts like the Abyss Great Emperor to take Rememberling around the main world. Rememberling would be taken to wherever there was the most number of souls.","Aside from spirit qi and earth-elemental energy, the Source Sand also needed some special earth-type treasures. It was just as difficult to evolve the Source Sand as it was Dark Blue.","It was even more difficult to evolve Purple Afterglow’s grade and quality. It needed at least a few years to stabilize!","Hence, the only feys Lin Yuan had that could increase their power rapidly were the Jasmine Lily and Blackie.","With thατ thought, Lin Yuan summoned the Jasmine Lily first.","He intended to use this elegant environment to evolve the Jasmine Lily and Blackie’s grades and qualities!","Although doing this would lower the concentration of spirit qi in the environment, Lin Yuan believed that Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter would not mind him doing so.","After the Jasmine Lily evolved to Suzerain/Myth and proliferated as well as fasciated, it mutated into an obstinate leaf style.","It was now only around the size of Lin Yuan’s palm.","Even the emperor green jade that Lin Yuan had glimpsed once in his previous life could not hold a candle to the Jasmine Lily’s color.","There was a small bright red main flower on the Jasmine Lily’s short, round, and moist leaves. The top of the main flower looked as though it had been carved from red jade.","There were three Buds of Mountain Jade on the carved red jade flowers. The crystallized Buds of Mountain Jade resembled opal and shone with a mottled glow. They looked even more brilliant than a wildflower-covered mountainside!","Lin Yuan had not had any time recently to address the Jasmine Lily. This was the first time he was summoning the Jasmine Lily in months.","He could not hide the amazement in his eyes.","[Fey Name]: Jasmine Lily (Bud of Mountain Jade)","[Spirit-Lifeform Species]: Crassulaceae genus/Aeonium genus","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Myth II","Abilities:","[Heal]: (Fasciated Flower Stand): Its Heal ability will reverse-heal the target, absorbing its vitality and letting it experience extreme comfort at the same time.","– Crystallized Main Flower: Its Heal ability will reverse-heal the target and absorb a large amount of its vitality.","– Bud of Mountain Jade: Its Heal ability will heal the target and channel rich vitality into it through its Bud of Mountain Jade, restoring the target’s damaged vitality.","[Mountain Jade Imprint]: The Mountain Jade Imprint will compress the pollen and vitality within the Bud of Mountain Jade to combine the two. A special imprint will be formed. When applied to a target, the healing effects will be greatly raised.","[Healing Transfer]: When the Mountain Jade Imprint is healing a target, if the vitality being injected into a target exceeds the amount that the target requires, the vitality will explode and heal the other lifeforms in the area. Alternatively, it can transfer the vitality to other targets that have the Mountain Jade Imprint applied on them.","[Life Protecting Soul]: When a target is being healed, the vitality can form a protective layer over the soul to help the target’s soul defend against external attacks.","[Red Crystal Jade Drain]: When using the Crystallized Main Flower to carry out reverse healing on a target, the effects of draining vitality and the negative impacts to the spirit senses will be magnified. If the enemy target has the Mountain Jade Imprint applied on it, it can drain the target’s vitality.","[Mountain Jade Prayer]: Once the Fasciated Flower Stand is activated, layers of jade will be produced, and the vitality within the body will be rapidly released. There is no distance limit, and the targets with the Mountain Jade Imprint on them will receive healing. This will enable the friendly targets with the Mountain Jade Imprint on them to recover their vitality to the maximum level.","[Revived Muscle and Bone]: If the target’s body has lost its genetic model, the mountain jade fluid in the Buds of Mountain Jade can use the target’s damaged body to analyze and create a replica of its genetic model.","Exclusive Skill:","[Recovery Imprint]: It accumulates the healing energy that is released by the Jasmine Lily during normal times. The contractor can activate the imprint to release the accumulated healing energy.","[Severed Limbs Growth]: It comprehends the arcana of plant growth. Even if one’s gene template is damaged, the rich vitality can allow one to continue to grow slowly.","[Generated Wedge]: Vitality will be poured into the target’s body and used to bless the target. Before the vitality is used up, the target will not die regardless of how serious the injuries it sustains are.","The Jasmine Lily that had been growing in the Spirit Lock spatial zone had already successfully evolved from Suzerain/Myth I to Suzerain/Myth II. It was only a step away from evolving to Myth III.","Lin Yuan was anxious to evolve the Jasmine Lily to Myth III. At that point, it would be able to change into human form!","When the Jasmine Lily evolved to Diamond grade, Lin Yuan confirmed that the Jasmine Lily was male.","Plant type feys could pick their gender when they transformed into human form.","Since the Jasmine Lily had already made its decision, it would not have to struggle with indecision when it transformed like other plant-type feys did.","It would be difficult for Lin Yuan to evolve the Jasmine Lily directly to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","Lin Yuan personally saw Green Vine take on heaven and earth when it reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","The main world’s will had not wanted a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform to appear in this world and restrained the evolution of its own accord. Additionally, meddling from spies outside of this world made the trials even harder to handle!","Lin Yuan would not be alone when he decided to evolve the Jasmine Lily to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom. He would ask Autumn and Winter for help.","Normally, Lin Yuan liked to use spirit qi crystals when he evolved his feys.","But this time, instead of doing that, he picked up the Jasmine Lily with his right hand and circulated the energy in his body.","The Jasmine Lily’s grade and quality began climbing rapidly as though they were being powered by an engine.","As the sea of pure spirit qi was injected into the Jasmine Lily’s body, it became increasingly crystalline!","The World Cleansing appeared above the Returning Saint Pool.","By now, Lin Yuan had summoned the Abyss Great Emperor and was waiting for the World Cleansing to descend.","But in the end, the Abyss Great Emperor did not need to step in as the World Cleansing was intercepted and blocked by Autumn.","Autumn had already anticipated that Lin Yuan would evolve his feys after he was done enlightening his birth horoscope.","Autumn and Winter were already waiting to help Lin Yuan to block these attacks.","Lin Yuan’s lips curved, and he felt even more confident that the Jasmine Lily’s evolution would be successful.","But now, the Jasmine Lily was no longer seated in Lin Yuan’s hand. Instead, it had transformed into a handsome man who was slightly taller than Lin Yuan. This man had short hair that resembled the Jasmine Lily’s short and small obstinate leaves.","The Jasmine Lily in human form not only had jade green hair on its head, but its eyebrows were also the same color. There was a pair of big doe eyes right below its eyebrows.","In terms of its looks, the Jasmine Lily could not match up to Blackie and Chimey. However, it did had a fresh and natural aura that resembled that of Lin Yuan’s own.","Before the Jasmine Lily in human form could say anything to Lin Yuan, the Trial of World Creation descended.","Lin Yuan placed his hand on the Jasmine Lily’s back and said seriously, “Jasmine Lily, the opportunity to increase your power is here! I will do my best to enable you to evolve to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom. Don’t hesitate to tell me if any issues crop up or if you feel uncomfortable in any way. Do not try to endure it on your own!”","The Jasmine Lily shook its head sincerely.","When the Jasmine Lily transformed into human form, its main body transformed into a lantern in the shape of a lotus flower. This was clearly a weapon that the Jasmine Lily’s main body had transformed into.","Lin Yuan was in no hurry to check on the Jasmine Lily’s data. Instead, he decided to wait until its grade and quality were fully evolved before he checked on it.","The Jasmine Lily really liked this feeling of rapid evolution.","Lin Yuan injected spirit qi into the Jasmine Lily’s body so that it could absorb the spirit qi.","It seemed that the spirit qi Lin Yuan produced from his own body was even better than the spirit qi crystals produced by Morbius!","Lin Yuan gazed at the weapon formed from the Jasmine Lily’s main body.","The lantern had a short base that could only be seen from a side view.","The Jasmine Lily was not holding up the lantern with its hand but had hooked one finger through the handle.","The lantern was the same jade green as the Jasmine Lily’s leaves while the center of the lantern was bright red. A blinding white flame burned within the lantern. When the white flame burned, one could sense the solid vitality in the lantern.","It took much longer to evolve the Jasmine Lily than Green Vine.","...","Eight days eventually passed.","Lin Yuan could sense that the now Eternal XII/Spirit Fire Jasmine Lily had reached a gate.","Lin Yuan was not unfamiliar with this gate. He had also encountered it with Green Vine.","Despite having sufficient spirit qi crystals, the Jasmine Lily was still stuck at this gate for some time.","As long as the Jasmine Lily could cross this gate, it would become Lin Yuan’s second World Emperor/Divine Kingdom fey.","The Jasmine Lily would also be able to attain a divine kingdom ability.","Lin Yuan did not rest even for a moment during the eight days.","In the past, his body would be exhausted and on its last legs.","But after emerging from the Returning Saint Pool, Lin Yuan noticed that his body would naturally absorb spirit qi to replenish itself. He would not feel tired unless his body was completely drained of energy."]},{"number":2749,"title":"Chapter 2749 Issues with the Boundary Patrol Envoy!","paragraphs":["2749 Issues with the Boundary Patrol Envoy!","Layers of fluffy clouds clustered together around the top of a palace. The entire palace towered like a mountain and was surrounded by thousands of square meters of various captivating flora and fauna. Purple leaves filled the bows of trees. With each passing breeze, the branches swayed with a hypnotic beauty.","At that moment, a man with short grayish-brown hair was kneeling in the hall, his forehead dripping with cold sweat. His face was scrunched up with anxiousness.","Fan Lou was Honor Absent Palace’s newest Boundary Patrol Envoy and led the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team. Although he was not considered part of Honor Absent Palace’s management level, he did have a respectable status.","Out of the 3,000 Boundary Patrol Teams, the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team was one of the best-performing ones.","Every 10,000 years, Honor Absent Palace renumbered its 3,000 Boundary Patrol Teams. The numbers were assigned according to the ranking the teams had achieved in the past 10,000 years.","At first, Fan Lou wanted to enable the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team to become one of the top five teams.","The Boundary Patrol Envoys that led the top five teams would not only be able to obtain more resources from Honor Absent Palace but could receive an Honor Absent Token.","The Honor Absent Token was a symbol in the East Universe. Even the most inferior white Honor Absent Token symbolized considerable status!","However, the team Fan Lou managed caused trouble a few days ago.","In actuality, every Boundary Patrol Team was dishonest to a certain degree.","The Boundary Patrol Envoys needed to generate income when they patrolled lower worlds.","The members of Boundary Patrol Teams did tedious work and needed some incentive to motivate them.","Honor Absent Palace closed one eye when it came to these matters.","Not long ago, Fan Lou received a letter of resignation.","One of his subordinates had lost his life treasure while supervising a lower world.","Every member of a Boundary Patrol Team was a divine kingdom lifeform who had all activated their divine kingdom abilities.","When their life treasures descended to the worlds, they would cause significant impacts even in a Class 3 world, much less a Class 1 world!","Fan Lou was the type to treasure relationships. Nonetheless, in order to keep the transgression under wraps, he accepted the resignation.","At first, Fan Lou thought about holding a meeting with the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team to discuss this matter and give the other members a warning.","They were in their busy period. Due to an unknown reason, almost 1/3 of the four universes’ fate had been drained.","Fate could be recovered, but it would not be easy to restore the amount of fate to its previous state.","Most importantly, the dominant factions of the four universes and all the species had worked together to investigate this matter but came up empty. This bothered the dominant factions and species of the four universes immensely.","Any misstep at such a juncture could lead to one’s doom.","If he revealed this matter, it was inevitable that it would be leaked to the members of other teams.","The teams were rivals, so they only appeared to be on good terms on the surface. But behind closed doors, they often use dirty tricks to undermine each other.","The team that Fan Lou led had been tripped up by others numerous times.","There was an infinitesimally small possibility of a faerie appearing in a Class 1 world. There was no need to pay attention to such anomalies.","At this moment, Fan Lou regretted not bringing this matter up. If he had strictly and strongly emphasized this matter, there would have been so many members of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team who secretly spied on the Class 2 world when one of its lifeforms evolved to the World Emperor grade the divine kingdom level. They all ended up killed by a lifeform in that Class 2 world!","The Sixth Boundary Patrol Team was now three-quarters of its original size.","It was true that he was the Boundary Patrol Envoy who was the acting leader of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team. However, despite being under his management, the members of the Boundary Patrol Team were not truly his subordinates.","Every Boundary Patrol Guard was an official staff in the territory owned by Honor Absent Palace. If anything happened to a member, it had to be reported and addressed.","Regardless of how capable Fan Lou was, he could not keep such an enormous matter under wraps.","Hence, he had no choice but to seek punishment from Honor Absent Palace.","A seated, beautiful girl toying with a gem in her hand frowned when she heard this.","“What? So many members of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team have died! Moreover, a lifeform in one of the Class 2 worlds under the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team’s jurisdiction has evolved to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom! Fan Lou, I am always generous with you. Are you here to crack jokes with me?”","This girl threw the gem forcefully on her chair’s armrest.","“How could a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform appear in a Class 2 world? The world rules don’t permit the existence of such a lifeform! Is it possible that the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team once again received private benefits from a faction or individual and ended up making a mess?”","Fan Lou’s kneeling body jumped when he heard the sound of the gem slamming onto the chair’s armrest.","He did not know how to explain himself to this beautiful girl.","Fan Lou also found it bizarre and did not understand how a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform could have appeared in a newly promoted Class 2 world. This event indeed went against all reason.","It was true that Fan Lou and the Boundary Patrol Teams he led in the past had accepted benefits from other factions and species.","Each under-the-table operation earned staggering profits for Fan Lou.","Each time he received resources, he would share a portion of it with this girl. This girl had always been the one watching out for him in Honor Absent Palace.","Otherwise, despite being a Boundary Patrol Envoy, Fan Lou would never be assigned to manage such an outstanding team.","“Lordess Kong Huan, even if I did do something extra, how could I ever hide it from you? You have always been taking care of me. Even at the cost of my life, I would never step over the rules! If you don’t believe me, you can investigate personally!","“It’s true that a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform has appeared in a Class 2 world! I don’t know why that Class 2 world’s wills did not restrain this lifeform’s evolution.”","Fan Lou paused before he continued. “Lordess Kong Huan, in truth, this Class 2 world received two Heaven’s Trials even when it was only a Class 1 world.”","When the enraged girl heard what Fan Lou said, she could not stop herself from sitting straighter.","“Fan Lou, you claimed that a Class 1 world managed to produce two faeries. Are you lying to me?”","Fan Lou hurriedly began defending himself, “Of course not! It’s true that a Class 1 world birthed two faeries, and these two faeries successfully overcame the Heaven’s Trials! One of them even successfully evolved into an intermediate faerie!”","Kong Huan stood up.","At first, she intended to investigate and find out what was different about this Class 2 world personally.","However, this Class 2 world had produced an intermediate faerie when it was only Class 1. This matter concerned the powerful Faerie Institution, so Kong Huan could not look into it too deeply.","Kong Huan decided to report this matter. As long as one of the higher-ups took over this report, there would be no need for her to take responsibility for future repercussions!","“Fan Lou, I am aware of everything. You can leave. Remember, do not allow your Boundary Patrol Team to cause any other mishaps! Otherwise, not even I will be able to protect you! I will allocate members to the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team before the assessment!”","Fan Lou relaxed when he heard Kong Huan’s response.","This matter seemed to be very messy but was very simple to address.","The first option was for Kong Huan to throw him to the dogs and allow him to take on all the responsibility and blame. He would then be captured by Honor Absent Palace’s punishment department for questioning and sentencing. Once he admitted to his crime, the executioners would immediately eliminate him.","Many of the Boundary Patrol Team captains who did not have anyone supporting them ended up with such fates.","Alternatively, Kong Huan could take on the blame on his behalf. This incident was not serious enough to shake her position in Honor Absent Palace. However, he would have to compensate her in whatever way she asked for in the future, even if it came at the cost of his life!","When Fan Lou left Honor Absent Palace, he decided that he would hold a meeting and sternly rein in the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team. They should not take off running in the hopes of receiving unconfirmed benefits once anything happened in one of the worlds!","Fan Lou had it all planned out. But when he returned to the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team, he saw that another six members of his team had died. This was exactly the same as what had happened previously.","Fan Lou cared a lot about the image he portrayed. However, at that moment, he could not stop himself from roaring, “Ling Gu, what is the meaning of this? You are the deputy captain of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team. Don’t you know that you are in charge of managing these idiots when I’m not present?”","The skinny and tall man named Ling Gu pulled back his neck and said, “Boss, another World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform has appeared in that Class 2 world! The four of them insisted on checking it out and...”","Before Ling Gu could finish speaking, Fan Lou’s body started to tremble.","Nonsense! They had all gone off the rails!","He had just finished giving his report to Lordess Kong Huan. Now, another four members of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team had died. What was he going to tell her now?","...","Lin Yuan did not know that the Jasmine Lily’s evolution had caused such a giant scene in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","He used True Data to check on the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Jasmine Lily.","[Fey Name]: Jasmine Lily (Bud of Mountain Jade)","[Spirit-Lifeform Species]: Crassulaceae genus/Aeonium genus","[Fey Grade]: World Emperor (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","[Heal]: (Fasciated Flower Stand): Its Heal ability will reverse-heal the target, absorbing its vitality and letting it experience extreme comfort at the same time.","– Crystallized Main Flower: Its Heal ability will reverse-heal the target and absorb a large amount of its vitality.","– Bud of Mountain Jade: Its Heal ability will heal the target and channel rich vitality into it through its Bud of Mountain Jade, restoring the target’s damaged vitality.","[Mountain Jade Imprint]: The Mountain Jade Imprint will compress the pollen and vitality within the Bud of Mountain Jade to combine the two. A special imprint will be formed. When applied to a target, the healing effects will be greatly raised.","[Healing Transfer]: When the Mountain Jade Imprint is healing a target, if the vitality being injected into a target exceeds the amount that the target requires, the vitality will explode and heal the other lifeforms in the area. Alternatively, it can transfer the vitality to other targets that have the Mountain Jade Imprint applied on them.","[Life Protecting Soul]: When a target is being healed, the vitality can form a protective layer over the soul to help the target’s soul defend against external attacks.","[Red Crystal Jade Drain]: When using the Crystallized Main Flower to carry out reverse healing on a target, the effects of draining vitality and the negative impacts to the spirit senses will be magnified. If the enemy target has the Mountain Jade Imprint applied on it, it can drain the target’s vitality.","[Mountain Jade Prayer]: Once the Fasciated Flower Stand is activated, layers of jade will be produced and the vitality within the body will be rapidly released. There is no distance limit and the targets with the Mountain Jade Imprint on them will receive healing. This will enable the friendly targets with the Mountain Jade Imprint on them to recover their vitality to maximum level.","[Revived Muscle and Bone]: If the target’s body has lost its genetic model, the mountain jade fluid in the Buds of Mountain Jade can use the target’s damaged body to analyze and create a replica of its genetic model.","[Life Healing Flower Eye]: Flower eyes will be left on the body of targets. Before the flower eyes are activated, the targets’ injuries will be healed. After the flower eyes are activated, the vitality in the flower eyes will spread outwards like a fountain and heal the area around the target.","[Healing Resonance]: Each time a target is being healed or recovered, the Jasmine Lily receives a certain amount of energy replenishment. If the Jasmine Lily’s energy limit is reached during the resonance process, the healing will achieve explosive effects!","[Spirit Restoration]: The combination of faith power and healing energy will recover the divine kingdoms of other targets. The targets’ divine kingdoms will be nourished and restored.","Exclusive Skill:","[Recovery Imprint]: It accumulates the healing energy that is released by the Jasmine Lily during normal times. The contractor can activate the imprint to release the accumulated healing energy.","[Severed Limbs Growth]: It comprehends the arcana of plant growth. Even if one’s gene template is damaged, the rich vitality can allow one to continue to grow slowly.","[Generated Wedge]: Vitality will be poured into the target’s body and used to bless the target. Before the vitality is used up, the target will not die regardless of how serious the injuries it sustains are.","[Imprint Creation]: All the energy in the Jasmine Lily’s body will be used to create an imprint. The imprint’s effects will be multiplied momentarily.","[Extending Life Returning Light]: A few of its leaves will be sacrificed. The energy in the leaves will enable the target to return to its prime state even if it started on the brink of death. However, the target will also be filled with the Jasmine Lily’s poison, and their vitality will be continuously depleted until it dies.","[Mountain Jade Protection]: The Bud of Mountain Jade will bless and protect the target. When the target is attacked, it will only undertake a small amount of damage, while most of the damage will be blocked by the energy in the Bud of Mountain Jade. The blessing state will be weakened as time goes on. Accordingly, the damage suffered by the target will continuously increase until the target eventually takes on the full extent of the damage.","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Postponed Birth]: The target will be put into a birth state. After the target dies, it will be able to be revived for a temporary period of time. When the birth state is activated, the target will be drained in various ways, and its potential will also be affected."]},{"number":2750,"title":"Chapter 2750 Honor Absent Parliament!","paragraphs":["2750 Honor Absent Parliament!","When a fey evolved from Normal to Elite, to Bronze, then to World Emperor, it would obtain a total of ten abilities. When it evolved from Normal to Legend, to Fantasy Breed, to Myth Breed, then to Divine Kingdom, it would gain a total of six exclusive skills and one divine kingdom ability.","Life Healing Flower Eye was considered a very strong functional-type healing-type ability.","The Jasmine Lily could place flower eyes on a target. Before the flower eye was activated, it would only heal the target. But once the flower eye was activated, it would become a moving healing spring that could heal all the entities in the target’s vicinity!","The Jasmine Lily could use Life Healing Flower Eye on many targets at once. This would allow the Jasmine Lily’s healing abilities to become more comprehensive and multi-dimensional. The Jasmine Lily would be able to heal many targets at once during battle even if Lin Yuan did not summon it directly!","When this healing ability was paired with Severed Limbs Growth, it would reach the peak of healing effects.","Healing Resonance was simultaneously an endurance and boosting ability.","Currently, the Jasmine Lily’s main endurance ability was Recovery Imprint.","However, Lin Yuan used Recovery Imprint as a foundational ability. He would only use such a foundational exclusive skill when the situation was absolutely dire.","Hence, the Jasmine Lily rarely had endurance when it was using its normal healing abilities.","But now that it had Healing Resonance, the Jasmine Lily would receive a certain degree of energy replenishment when it healed other targets.","The Jasmine Lily’s healing could be activated on a large scale. With such large-scale healing, it was easy for the energy in the Jasmine Lily’s body to reach its limit. This would keep the Jasmine Lily’s energy level full, and its healing would be able to produce explosive effects easily.","The explosive effect would cause the healing effects to multiply while using up a small portion of energy. This effectively raised the Jasmine Lily’s healing abilities.","These two abilities brought great joy to Lin Yuan.","The endurance of Healing Resonance enabled the Jasmine Lily to handle the job of meeting Lin Yuan’s healing needs during combat even without relying on the Recovery Imprint.","Lin Yuan could stop using Recovery Imprint as an endurance ability but as a real secret weapon that he would only use when he was on the brink of death. This would give Recovery Imprint the chance to endlessly accumulate vitality!","However, these two abilities could not be compared to Spirit Restoration.","As the environment changed, the definitions of the levels of entities would change.","There were many foundational abilities in the main world that became insignificant in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","However, the Jasmine Lily’s Spirit Restoration would continue to be seen as foundational even in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. It would even be considered one of the top foundational abilities.","This was not because Lin Yuan was overly confident in his fey’s abilities but because Spirit Restoration truly reached this level.","Divine-kingdom lifeforms were the most afraid of their divine kingdoms being damaged. Once their divine kingdoms were damaged, their ability to take in faith power would be affected.","There were methods in the Sky Beyond the Clouds to heal divine kingdoms, but these methods required a large amount of rare ingredients that regular divine-kingdom experts could not afford.","Even if the divine-kingdom expert in question belonged to a large faction, the faction would have to weigh his value to the faction before deciding if they were worth the cost of so many rare resources.","Spirit Restoration would combine faith power and healing energy to heal and nourish damaged divine kingdoms until they were restored to their original states.","When they arrived at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, the Jasmine Lily would be able to use this ability to be of great help to Lin Yuan. This would give him the chance to gain many divine-kingdom expert subordinates.","The divine-kingdom experts under Lin Yuan would not have to be worried about being left vulnerable when their divine kingdoms were injured during battle.","Lin Yuan felt that this ability was even more precious than some divine kingdom abilities.","Aside from abilities, the Jasmine Lily also gained three new exclusive skills: Imprint Creation, Extending Life Returning Life, and Mountain Jade Protection.","Imprint Creation would allow the Jasmine Lily to use all the energy in its body to create an imprint. Its effects could be multiplied temporarily.","When Lin Yuan saw this exclusive skill, he instinctively thought of the Recovery Imprint.","If Lin Yuan used Imprint Creation at the same time he used Recovery Imprint, the latter’s effects would be temporarily raised.","Lin Yuan would then be able to tap into more vitality to use to overcome obstacles.","This increased the strength of Lin Yuan’s secret weapons.","Extending Life Returning Life allowed the Jasmine Lily to sacrifice its obstinate leaves and use the energy in the obstinate leaves to restore a target to its prime even if it was on the brink of death.","The Jasmine Lily was a crassulaceae genus/aeonium genus fey. It could heal targets, but its body also contained extremely potent poison.","There were many people who, out of starved insanity, consumed crassulaceae genus plants and died.","Extending Life Returning Life would allow the target to recover a large amount of vitality, but its body would also become filled with the Jasmine Lily’s poison. Subsequently, the replenished vitality in the target’s body would be depleted.","It was not impossible to remove the negative effects of Extending Life Returning Life. All that was needed was to remove the poison in the target’s body immediately after it was healed.","Presently, Lin Yuan did not have many techniques to neutralize poison.","It was difficult for regular feys to neutralize the poison of a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform.","The only way to find such a fey would be to search in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Frankly, there were also feys in the main world that could neutralize the poison of crassulaceae genus/aeonium genus feys of the same level.","However, there was no way Lin Yuan would evolve another fey to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom just to neutralize the poison. Despite having the resources, Lin Yuan would not be so wasteful!","The stronger Lin Yuan became, the more aware he became that resources needed to be spent wisely! This was the only way to enable him to improve to the greatest extent!","It would not only use the Bud of Mountain Jade to boost targets but also protect targets at the same time. As a result, the targets would only have to suffer a small portion of the damage that was directed at it while most of the damage would be blocked by the energy in the Bud of Mountain Jade.","Although the boosting state would weaken over time and the target would have to suffer an increasing share of the damage, Mountain Jade Protection would defend the target from various forms of damage countless times. This would allow the target to survive a barrage of attacks.","Assault troops were used in various battles. They often had to sacrifice themselves.","Assault troops were a very rare resource in any faction. Only those with absolute loyalty were willing to become an assault troop and assault troops needed to be nurtured using a large amount of resources.","Mountain Jade Protection would ensure the safety of the assault troops to the greatest extent.","Compared to abilities and exclusive skills, Lin Yuan was more excited about the Jasmine Lily’s divine kingdom ability.","Spring had already told Lin Yuan about the different types of divine kingdom abilities.","The Jasmine Lily’s divine kingdom ability, Postponed Birth, was clearly a functional-type one.","Lin Yuan already had more than one revival technique. However, Postponed Birth was the only one that Lin Yuan could use in battle.","Lin Yuan felt that Postponed Birth could complete Mountain Jade Protection.","When the Jasmine Lily used Postponed Birth to put a target in a birth state, the target could be revived within a certain period after its death. It was an amazing ability.","However, these abilities came with negative effects. The negative effects were not directed at the Jasmine Lily but the target that was put in the birth state.","Each time the birth state was activated, the target would be drained in various ways. Its potential might even be severely affected.","Once a target’s potential was affected, its future would come to a screeching halt. It would be even more difficult for powerful targets to advance further. Once their potential was cut off, they might not be able to move forward for the rest of their life!","However, in the Sky Beyond the Clouds where danger was abound, being alive was better than being dead.","This especially applied to assault troops.","It was clear that the Jasmine Lily’s appearance had changed significantly from before. The current Jasmine Lily looked more divine.","The Jasmine Lily walked over to Lin Yuan and transformed back into its original form before landing on Lin Yuan’s palm.","The Jasmine Lily had social anxiety and preferred to appear as its main body rather than its human form. The Jasmine Lily was more comfortable and carefree in its main body!","Lin Yuan played with the Jasmine Lily for a while before he returned it to the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The Jasmine Lily could be nourished by pure spirit qi there.","It was extremely important for recently evolved World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeforms to be nourished by pure spirit qi.","Hence, powerful species from the Sky Beyond the Clouds always fought for blessed territories with a high concentration of spirit qi for the sake of their younger generation. Each time a blessed territory appeared, intense fighting would ensue.","Lin Yuan summoned Blackie.","...","Lin Yuan had no idea that when he summoned Blackie with the intention of evolving it, Fan Lou who was the leader of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team was once again visiting Honor Absent Palace. He was brimming with nervousness as he prepared to meet with Kong Huan again.","Before he came, Fan Lou held a meeting in Honor Absent Palace and repeatedly emphasized the situation.","Normally, Fan Lou would not throw such a big tantrum toward his subordinates.","These people under him all had similar portfolios. As long as they did not make grievous errors, they could all continue being Boundary Patrol Guards. He would still have to give them orders in the future, so offending them was not a smart choice!","All the intelligent Boundary Patrol Envoys had mindsets similar to Fan Lou’s.","The Boundary Patrol Envoys who went on power trips would only diminish the morale of their team and lose support.","However, Fan Lou could not help himself this time.","Fan Lou’s fury caused the members of his team to become terrified. This was not because they were afraid of him but because they also realized the seriousness of this matter. Despite knowing that there was something off about this Class 2 world, they did not dare to investigate it any further!","Benefits were indeed important, but these Boundary Patrol Guards cared more about their lives than benefits! None of them saw their lives as things to toy with!","Fan Lou was nervous and cursed his bad luck. This matter was clearly unrelated to him, yet he had to take responsibility for it.","With so many members of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team dead, Kong Huan was already livid. Now that another four had died, he felt as though he was provoking her! She would definitely blow her top once she found out about this matter.","After he was done with his explanation, Kong Huan might allow him to keep his life, but she would not favor him as heavily in the future!","There were 30 members of every Boundary Patrol Team. Once more than 1/3 of the members were lost, this had to be reported to the Honor Absent Parliament.","This matter had clearly reached the level that necessitated reporting.","Fan Lou had been a Boundary Patrol Envoy for some time. He could not figure out how a seemingly ordinary Class 2 world had become so special!","This matter would definitely gain attention from the bigshots once it was reported during an Honor Absent Parliament meeting.","It was likely that they would all fix their attention on this Class 2 world to investigate and understand its circumstances.","Although this Class 2 world was under the jurisdiction of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team, there was no way he would receive any of the future benefits.","However, receiving benefits did not matter. What mattered was that Fan Lou found out whether this Class 2 world was hiding anything sinister.","How did it manage to cause him to shoulder such a heavy sin? This feeling was not comfortable in the slightest!"]},{"number":2751,"title":"Chapter 2751 The Scheme of Sending Assistance During a Time of Need!","paragraphs":["2751 The Scheme of Sending Assistance During a Time of Need!","Fan Lou was one of Kong Huan’s people, and not many people knew about this.","Kong Huan always took care of herself and her own.","As a member of Honor Absent Parliament, Kong Huan’s decision could influence their decisions to a certain extent.","Kong Huan also had many rivals.","If their relationship was exposed, someone of Fan Lou’s standing would definitely put a dent in Kong Huan’s reputation.","However, those around Kong Huan knew that she fully supported Fan Lou. His past few years of hard work had also brought Kong Huan significant benefits.","Fan Lou had just angered Kong Huan, and she was hurriedly cleaning up his mess.","Why was Fan Lou back again? Was it possible that Fan Lou knew that he had made an error and was trying to get on her good side? It was not easy to appease a hopping-mad Kong Huan!","Kong Mu came from the same species as Kong Huan and served her since they were young.","When Kong Mu saw that Fan Lou was back again, she knew that Kong Huan’s mood would be affected when she saw him again.","Kong Mu walked up to Fan Lou and looked him up and down before saying seriously, “Fan Lou, you should be aware of Lordess Kong Huan’s temperament. If you know that you’ve made a mistake, just make sure not to repeat it again!","“When Lordess Kong Huan sees you again, she will punish you if her anger is still lingering. Don’t blame me for not warning you!”","Kong Mu and Fan Lou were acquainted with each other.","In Kong Mu’s eyes, Fan Lou used to be very intelligent. Why was he acting so stupidly now?","Even with the relationship that existed between Kong Mu and Kong Huan, Kong Mu needed to avoid showing her face to Kong Huan when she made mistakes.","She was doing Fan Lou a favor by giving him this reminder. With her status, it would serve Fan Lou well to listen to her!","Kong Huan had spent less than 1/3 of her time in the past 1,000 years in Honor Absent Palace. For the remaining 2/3 of the time, Kong Mu was the one handling the affairs from Honor Absent Palace on Kong Huan’s behalf.","Fan Lou smiled bitterly before clasping his hands together.","“Your Grace Kong Mu, I know of Lordess Kong Huan’s temper. However, I have a reason that necessitates my meeting with Lordess Kong Huan!”","Kong Mu looked surprised. For Fan Lou to come despite knowing of Kong Huan’s temper, this matter had to be serious!","Based on Fan Lou’s expression, he was not bringing good news. Since it was not good news, there was no need for Kong Mu to participate and put herself at risk of being burned.","Fan Lou never stopped thinking and pondering while he was speaking with Kong Mu. Should he tell her about this matter?","Although Kong Mu was Kong Huan’s servant and would never do anything that went against Kong Huan’s benefits, Fan Lou believed that she would plead for mercy on his behalf as long as Kong Huan’s benefits were not impacted!","As long as he was able to convince her to speak up for him in front of Kong Huan, he would not have to bear the full brunt of Kong Huan’s rage.","As long as he remained a Boundary Patrol Envoy and led the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team, he could earn whatever resources he had to cough up now!","Fan Lou sighed sadly.","He was well aware of Kong Mu’s greedy nature, but he had no choice but to beg her now.","“Your Grace Kong Mu, we have known each other for tens of thousands of years. I have always shown you the greatest of respect. Can I ask for your help this one time? If you are willing to help me, I am willing to give you the harvest of a miniature spirit qi mine for the next 10,000 years!”","Fan Lou’s words were strung together very well. Although he did not explicitly play the emotional card, emotions permeated his words.","He even dangled tempting profits in front of Kong Mu! His heart was pricked by reluctance when he promised such profits to her. He believed that these profits were sufficient to persuade Kong Mu!","There were times when Kong Mu could make decisions on Kong Huan’s behalf. However, all the offerings had to go to Kong Huan, and Kong Mu could only take a very small cut. Kong Huan was not generous, even to longtime servants like Kong Mu!","As greedy as Kong Mu was, she was also smart.","10,000 years of harvest from a miniature mine was not a small sum.","Fan Lou had spent almost all of his assets in order to obtain the rights to develop this miniature spirit qi mine.","The fact that Fan Lou was willing to give her such resources meant that he had committed a serious blunder!","Even with these profits within reach, Kong Mu did not agree immediately. Instead, she cautiously asked, “Fan Lou, it’s true that we have known each other for a long time. But you can’t just ask me for help. You need to tell me exactly what you need help with! I can’t be of help in everything. You need to keep this in mind!”","Since Fan Lou was asking Kong Mu for help, he could not hide the truth from her.","He began to describe the situation in detail.","“Your Grace Kong Mu, you should be aware of my reason for coming to see Lordess Kong Huan now.”","Kong Mu nodded. She was aware of the matter.","She did not think that Fan Lou had done anything wrong, just that he was down on his luck. It was true that there was something off about that Class 2 world!","Kong Huan would definitely investigate that Class 2 world after settling this issue!","There was a case in the past when a few bigshots managed to obtain a fair amount of outstanding resources from a low-class world, enabling them to improve significantly.","When Kong Mu nodded, Fan Lou did not provide more of an explanation and got right to the main point.","“When I returned to my team, another four members had died. This happened because another World Emperor/Divine Kingdom appeared in that Class 2 world. They didn’t learn their lesson from the last time and decided on their own accord to investigate that world.","“I didn’t have the chance to stop them! I hope that you’ll be able to speak up on my behalf in front of Lordess Kong Huan so she doesn’t punish me too heavily!”","Kong Mu was momentarily stunned when she heard what Fan Lou said. She never anticipated such a thing to happen! She was momentarily at a loss about what to say next.","Kong Mu now knew why Fan Lou had returned so soon. This was the reason!","However, once Kong Huan heard of this matter, she would definitely vent all her fury on Fan Lou!","This was not because Kong Huan was unable to understand Fan Lou’s position.","Fan Lou was an innocent who had been dragged into this matter. However, there was no way that Kong Huan would let Fan Lou off easily because this matter caused her to lose unquantifiable profits. She might have also lost a major opportunity!","If a Boundary Patrol Team lost eight or nine of its members, Kong Huan could use her own means to cover up the matter.","But now that another four members had died, this matter absolutely needed to be reported to the Honor Absent Parliament!","Once Honor Absent Parliament found out about this matter, one could only imagine how many people would try to claim a share of the loot.","It was true that Kong Huan was a member of Honor Absent Parliament, but she could not be considered a bigshot. If she truly wanted to punish Fan Lou, it would be because she was upset that she had lost such an opportunity.","Hence, it was not plausible for Kong Mu to help Fan Lou with this matter.","However, Kong Mu did not say this clearly and gave her a verbal tentative agreement.","“I will make a note of this. If Lordess Kong Huan is still angry, nothing I say will work. But once she’s done, I will definitely speak up for you and do my best to help you keep your position as a Boundary Patrol Envoy. You won’t be held back by just one incident!","“You don’t need to give me 10,000 years of harvest from the miniature spirit qi mine. 8,000 years will do. I will also only be taking 70% of the profits! You already say that we are old friends. I care more about helping you than receiving those resources!”","Despite knowing that she could not be of help in any way, Kong Mu still played the old friend card. After all, Fan Lou had no way to check if she did end up helping him. As long as she said she did help, it would mean she had!","After saying that, Fan Lou would owe her an enormous favor if he survived.","If Fan Lou died, his resources would all go to Kong Huan and have nothing to do with Kong Mu.","If she took 10,000 years of harvest from Fan Lou’s miniature spirit qi mine, Fan Lou would eventually become resentful toward her. Fan Lou would become more attached to her if she volunteered to take less profits.","In the future, she could make life easier for Fan Lou as he continued to remain a part of Kong Huan’s camp. Then, he would definitely compensate her with profits of his own!","Kong Mu had used this method to build bridges with many people over the years. She enjoyed the feeling of using her authority to manipulate others.","Otherwise, with Kong Huan’s stingy character, Kong Mu’s power would never have increased so rapidly!","Fan Lou never thought much of Kong Mu in the past. But now, he felt indebted to her. She was essentially sending assistance during his time of need.","Before this, Fan Lou had no idea that being sent assistance during his time of need was such a warm feeling!","When Kong Mu saw the way that Fan Lou was looking at her, she could not help but smile broadly.","Ah! Another fool that was falling to this method of manipulation!","She could only hope that this fool had better luck. If his luck was bad and Kong Huan killed him in a fit of rage, she would have no means of extracting profits from him in the future!","When it came to using emotions to manipulate a person, the crux was hitting the iron while it was hot. Now that Fan Lou was feeling grateful toward her, she needed to deepen this gratitude!","As a member of the Alluring Fox species, Kong Mu was gorgeous.","She walked over to Fan Lou and adjusted the two accessories hanging on the front of his attire.","“Later, try to emphasize that Class 2 world’s uniqueness. Do not lie to Lordess Kong Huan! The more you talk up that Class 2 world, the less likely Lordess Kong Huan will direct her rage at you!”","Fan Lou earnestly took note of what Kong Mu said. She was telling him how to preserve his life.","It could be said that no one knew more about this Class 2 world than Fan Lou.","As long as the Class 2 world was seen as sufficiently exceptional, Fan Lou’s understanding of the Class 2 world would become useful to Lordess Kong Huan.","Kong Mu really hoped that Fan Lou would survive. If he survived, he would become a useful resource to her.","How could an outstanding member of the Alluring Foxes lack a crowd of men around her?","...","Lin Yuan looked at the flying Blackie and checked on it with True Data.","[Fey Name]: Five-Clawed Spirit Dragon","[Fey Species]: Clawed-dragon-species/five-clawed-dragon-genus","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Water","[Fey Quality]: Pinnacle Myth Breed","Abilities:","[Spirit Injection]: Restore a huge amount of spiritual power at once and restore the lost spiritual power over a period of time.","[Spirit Roar]: Let out a roar to control the direction of the flow of spiritual power. It can choose to boost or drain the spiritual power of the targets in a given area.","[Endowment Spirit Rain]: The bloodline can be used to gather the clouds and release rain that contains spiritual power. The targets that make contact with the rain will be able to replenish their lost spiritual power.","[Spirit Channel System]: The spirit qi in the body can be released into the environment. A perfect and invisible channel system will be formed through the spirit qi. The channel system will not only recover its own spiritual power but decrease the rate at which its spiritual power was diminished.","[Spirit Judgment Imprisonment]: Pick a target and judge the concentration of spirit qi within the target’s body. If the concentration of spirit qi in the target’s body is higher than its own, all of the spirit qi in its body will be emptied out. If the concentration of spirit qi in the target’s body is lower than its own, the target’s spiritual power will be imprisoned.","[Spirit Wrath]: The dragon aura will be unleashed. The dragon aura will burn off all of the spirit qi in the area and cause the surrounding environment to be empty of spiritual power.","[True Spirit Five Changes]: Release the dragon claws. Every dragon claw will become a clone. The clones will possess all the abilities of the main body. They will not disappear after being attacked and will share spiritual power with the main body.","Exclusive Skill:","[Spirit Qi Imprint]: The spirit qi that is constantly released to the environment would be stored within the Spirit Qi Imprint instead. It can also drain a small amount of the spirit qi released from other dragon species feys within the surrounding area that does not exceed the fey’s grade and inject it into the Spirit Qi Imprint. It would be branded on the contractor’s body, and the contractor could release spirit qi contained within the Spirit Qi Imprint.","[Spirit Essence Explosion]: Gather the spiritual power into a single point and explode all the energy. The Spirit Essence Explosion can only be applied on places where there is contact with the Spirit Qi Imprint.","[Emperor Spirit Control]: An Emperor Spirit Inscription will be formed within the dragon claw. There can only be one Emperor Spirit Inscription in each claw. Each Emperor Spirit Inscription will allow the amount of spirit qi in the body to be multiplied.","While in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Blackie had successfully evolved from Suzerain I/Myth I to Suzerain X/pinnacle Myth. It was on the precipice of evolving.","Blackie had experienced way too much hardship on its journey of evolving from a regular Spirit-Siphon Goldfish to a five-clawed dragon. Each evolution involved Blackie’s body being reconfigured.","The five-clawed dragon was considered to be excellent.","Lin Yuan was not certain which direction Blackie’s bloodline would take during this evolution."]},{"number":2752,"title":"Chapter 2752 The Main World is Targeted!","paragraphs":["2752 The Main World is Targeted!","Clawed dragons were already a very strong type of main dragon.","Lin Yuan and Spring had not yet discussed Blackie. Hence, Lin Yuan did not have an estimate of how Blackie’s bloodline would evolve. He had no choice but to wait for Blackie to evolve until he did a comprehensive analysis of it.","Based on the level of Blackie’s bloodline, Lin Yuan would be able to make a general estimate of the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ level of dragon-species fey bloodline. This would be very important in helping Lin Yuan to understand the species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Although Spring had not yet introduced the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom dragon-species bloodline to Lin Yuan in detail, she had mentioned that there were hundreds of thousands of dragon species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. None of them dropped below the top 100 in the rankings of any of the universes and even cracked the top ten of the South Universe’s ranking once!","After flying a few rounds in the sky, Blackie changed into human form and landed in front of Lin Yuan.","Unlike the Jasmine Lily, Blackie was more comfortable in its human form. It was a fey that preferred to stay in its human form!","However, Lin Yuan needed to ride on Blackie on most occasions. Hence, it usually accompanied him in its original form.","In its human form, Blackie presented some female dragon traits. However, this did not dampen its dashing demeanor.","Blackie’s aura was elegant, and every movement and smile was gentle.","But compared to its aura, Blackie’s voice was even more gentle. It was so gentle and soft that one would never be able to tell, based on just its voice, that Blackie was a dragon.","In the main world, dragons were the most amorous and emotional type of fey.","They were very strict and picky when it came to choosing a mate. Even after deciding on a mate with whom they had agreed to start a family, they would not hesitate to abandon that mate if a better option came along!","Almost all male dragon-species feys liked mates with gentle dispositions like the one that Blackie had. The female dragons, who were built like muscular tanks and had the dispositions of female warriors, had little to no prospects.","It could be said that Blackie was the ideal dragon of the main world. This was why Blackie was willing to appear in its original form.","Just like how dragons liked to collect wealth and shiny trinkets, they also liked to put themselves on glorious display!","“Blackie, you have always suffered the most out of all my feys. Not even Genius has had as tough of a time as you!","“I don’t know if this transformation will put you through the same experience as the previous ones. But don’t worry. I’ll be able to protect you regardless of what happens, no matter how serious the problem is!”","Lin Yuan spoke confidently. This was firstly because Autumn and Winter were right outside to help him fend off the evolution’s trials.","Additionally, the Jasmine Lily had evolved to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, drastically improving its healing abilities. Lin Yuan could continuously supply Blackie with pure vitality during its transformation to treat any injuries.","Blackie gently hugged Lin Yuan and rested its chin on his shoulder.","For Duan He, there was no difference between supporting his fey and supporting his wife. He only lavished more and more love on his fey of a wife.","Lin Yuan was well aware of Duan He’s thoughts and intentions. He was trying to take advantage of the Sea Demon Snake’s various different personalities to periodically swap out his wife’s personality. Where was the harm in this?","Duan He was Liu Jie’s closest aide during the white-clothed followers’ external training operation. He could be said to be one of the pillars of Sky City. Lin Yuan was more than happy to meet his requests!","Lin Yuan was already used to his feys showing him affection.","Blackie said gently, “Yuan, honestly, I felt like I was going to die during all the previous evolutions! Each time I was certain that I wouldn’t be able to hold on any longer, you pulled me out of death’s grasp!","“This time, my bloodline is once again shackled. My bloodline will only be able to qualitatively improve if I break through the limits of the clawed dragon species! So this time won’t be easy either! As long as I have you by my side, I’m not afraid of evolving!”","Blackie hugged Lin Yuan tighter before letting him go.","Lin Yuan knew that Blackie was fully ready.","Lin Yuan could sense Blackie’s unconditional trust in him. He loved this feeling of being trusted by his feys!","Lin Yuan circulated the energy in his body, and a large amount of spirit qi entered Blackie’s body.","It did not take long for Blackie’s grade to evolve from Suzerain/Myth II to Myth III and then continue to evolve further.","Two dagger fists appeared on Blackie’s white hands. They had very odd shapes, as there were five sharp protuberances on the anterior. They resembled five spread-out dragon claws!","One of the dagger fists was sharp, while the other was thick. They would be able to produce extremely different effects during combat.","Between support and combat, Blackie chose combat.","Lin Yuan had anticipated Blackie to make this choice. Blackie preferred to fight opponents than provide support during combat.","Lin Yuan realized that all the feys he nurtured were ambitious and driven to distinguish themselves. He did not know whether he was supposed to be happy or vexed by this.","Blackie’s pure support abilities were Spirit Injection, Spirit Roar, Endowment Spirit Rain, and Spirit Channel System. Aside from these four support abilities and the exclusive skill, Spirit Qi Imprint, the other abilities and exclusive skills were all geared toward combat!","These four abilities and exclusive skill were already sufficient to provide support during combat!","The exclusive skills that a fey gained from evolving their quality would dictate their development direction.","Most of Lin Yuan’s feys were functional-type, and almost none of them were as strong of a combat beast as Blackie. If Blackie could only evolve into a combat beast, it would make up for this gap in Lin Yuan’s team of feys.","Every spirit qi professional had different directions.","If a spirit qi professional was solely in charge of combat, a combat beast would be the best choice for them.","However, this was not the case for Lin Yuan.","When Lin Yuan picked his feys, he usually leaned toward functional-type ones. They could continue to be the main type of fey that he contracted from then on.","Functional-type feys only had one drawback, which was that they had an enormous requirement for resources.","Given Lin Yuan’s wealth of resources, he could support the needs of these feys.","Morbius’ new exclusive skill, 14 Totem Seeds, would also allow Lin Yuan to pick species to support in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Before Lin Yuan arrived there, he had no way of knowing what species he would be supporting in the future.","...","While Lin Yuan was evolving Blackie, Kong Huan returned to her palace again. Upon returning, she spotted a squirrelly Fan Lou standing there, clearly with something to say.","Kong Huan frowned. She knew that something had definitely happened again! Otherwise, Fan Lou would never dare to show up there!","She did not have a pleasant temper at all, especially when her subordinates had caused her trouble.","There was no way that Fan Lou had come with good news for her.","However, Kong Huan did not get angry before she heard the bad news that Fan Lou brought her. This was because she had already settled the previous matter and already planned on asking Fan Lou a few questions.","Just what was special about this Class 2 world?","Kong Huan had some ideas about this special Class 2 world.","Not only could this Class 2 world birth World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeforms, but it had even killed so many Boundary Patrol Guards!","All of the Boundary Patrol Guards had produced their life treasures. Being employed by Honor Absent Palace was much better than trying to make it on their own in private factions!","There had to be something special about this Class 2 world for all of this to happen.","Kong Huan was increasingly interested in this Class 2 world and really wanted to investigate it.","However, she dared not act recklessly. Despite being much stronger than the Boundary Patrol Guards, she could not guarantee that whatever was in that Class 2 world would not be able to affect her.","“Fan Lou, you should be managing the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team now. Why are you here looking for me?”","As a member of the upper echelon, Kong Huan did not have to ask Fan Lou directly when she needed to speak to him.","If Fan Lou was smart, he would tell her all about the Class 2 world of his own accord.","Kong Huan came up with many possibilities but never expected Fan Lou to bring her news that would ruin her thoughts and plans.","Fan Lou knelt by Kong Huan’s feet and lowered his head to the ground.","When Kong Huan saw this, she immediately knew that he had caused major trouble! Otherwise, he would never act in such a manner! Just what had happened that was causing him to put on such a display?","Kong Huan turned to look at Kong Mu. The latter wanted Fan Lou to explain the situation to Kong Huan. However, Kong Huan did not give Fan Lou the chance to speak but looked at her directly. Now, it seemed that she could not keep herself clean even if she wanted to!","There was no way that she could not respond to Kong Huan.","It would be fine if she did not know anything about the situation. Alas, she knew everything about the matter.","She should not have stayed there!","Kong Mu gnashed her teeth and said nervously, “Lordess Kong Huan, when Fan Lou returned to his team, he found out that another four Boundary Patrol Guards of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team had died. This happened because another lifeform in that world has evolved to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom!”","While Kong Mu spoke, she could sense fury spilling out from Kong Huan. She increased her rate of speech and continued. “Lordess Kong Huan, there are many special traits about this Class 2 world. Fan Lou can tell you about it in detail!","“This Class 2 world is far too dangerous. It led to the deaths of so many Boundary Patrol Guards. Anyone who tries to investigate this Class 2 world will put themselves at considerable risk!”","Kong Mu threw in the last statement to increase her chances of survival. However, she did also speak up on Fan Lou’s behalf.","Fan Lou lifted his head to look into Kong Huan’s furious eyes and voiced his daring guess, “Lordess Kong Huan, I suspect that this Class 2 world is linked to Faerie Institution. Otherwise, it wouldn’t have produced two faeries back when it was still a Class 1 world! One of the faeries even has an intermediate bloodline!”","Fan Lou used his life-preserving safety net right off the bat.","Kong Huan looked visibly shocked when she heard what Fan Lou said.","However, when did the Faerie Institution that came from the South Universe and West Universe gain such a far reach?","Moreover, why did they need to interfere in a Class 1 world? This did not make sense at all!","However, there was no way that Fan Lou would lie to her.","One of the Alluring Foxes’ talents was to discern lies.","When Kong Huan heard what Kong Mu said, she held herself back from crushing to death the idiot Fan Lou, who had ruined her plan.","But now, Kong Huan knew she could no longer suppress his matter.","Once this matter was reported to the Honor Absent Parliament, she would have to head to this Class 2 world with the other executive members and share the loot with them.","The leader of the Boundary Patrol Team in charge of this would act as the guide.","Kong Huan still wanted to keep Fan Lou around so he could gather more benefits for her!","With that thought, Kong Huan suppressed her temper and seriously said, “Fan Lou, all of this started from your management failure. With such an error, you can’t make up for it even by sacrificing your life, much less merely giving up your position as a Boundary Patrol Envoy!","“Now, tell me every morsel of information you know about this Class 2 world. I want to know every detail about this Class 2 world! Then, I will take you with me to the upper domain of Honor Absent Palace to participate in the Honor Absent Parliament.","“You will report this situation clearly to the parliament! I need you to put your best foot forward and try to obtain the opportunity to become the guide! As long as you achieve this, I will forget about your mistake and won’t take your life after this matter is over.","“If you become the guide, you can help me to obtain some benefits from the Class 2 world. Not only will I share some of the benefits with you as a reward, but I’ll even let you keep your position as a Boundary Patrol Envoy!”"]},{"number":2753,"title":"Chapter 2753 Divine Kingdom Ability: Turbid Spirit Cleansing","paragraphs":["2753 Divine Kingdom Ability: Turbid Spirit Cleansing","Kong Huan was saying this to give Fan Lou a burden as well as a chance. This was the only reason she would spare him.","Fan Lou hurriedly lowered his head and said, “Lordess Kong Huan, I will definitely do a good job! My management wasn’t strict enough in the past, but most of the actions were done by the Boundary Patrol Guards on their own accord. As long as it’s something I can accomplish, I definitely won’t let you down!”","Although the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team had made a mess of the matter, Kong Huan still believed in Fan Lou’s individual competencies!","Moreover, Fan Lou was fully under her control. Even if she gave him an opportunity and he became the guide for the exploration of this Class 2 world, he would never dare to step a toe out of line!","Faerie Institution was a faction established by higher faeries.","Faerie Institution had been working toward gathering all the faeries and protecting their rights.","If a Class 1 world was able to produce an intermediate faerie, that Class 1 world deserved to be called a blessed ground!","As long as the two faeries were born from that world itself, the world’s chances of producing a higher faerie after being promoted to Class 2 world would also be raised!","Due to the strong reputation that Faerie Institution had built over the past thousands of years, the other factions dared not rear faeries like they used to do. They no longer made use of faeries to create positive environments to strengthen themselves.","If they could obtain natural habitats from this Class 2 world that could evolve faeries, they could bring them to the Sky Beyond the Clouds to be nurtured.","Faeries that were not born from natural means were everything to creators. Since they were produced from the creators’ resources, not even Faerie Institution could force them to give the faeries up!","Although another four members of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team had died and this matter needed to be reported to the Honor Absent Parliament, doing so would enable Kong Huan to share some of the risk.","However, Kong Huan was rather despondent.","It was said that wealth and honor were found in danger. Kong Huan could accept taking on some danger in exchange for opportunities.","But now, the right to choose was taken out of her hands.","As opposed to Kong Huan’s melancholy, Kong Mu and Fan Lou were delighted.","Fan Lou had essentially saved his life.","Kong Mu was happy because she had helped Fan Lou with such a big favor and given him a direction for the future. He only managed to move Kong Huan by listening to her advice.","Her receiving the harvests from the miniature spirit qi mine was one matter. More importantly, after Fan Lou used his link to Kong Huan to become the guide for the Class 2 world, Kong Mu would definitely be able to obtain benefits as well.","Without Fan Lou, she would never be able to get her hands on such benefits!","...","Lin Yuan did not notice that after his dip in the Returning Saint Pool, using his body and resources to evolve the Jasmine Lily and Blackie caused such a giant commotion.","Although Lin Yuan did not pick up on this, Autumn and Winter, who were guarding the Returning Saint Pool, did. However, the two of them were unbothered. Rather, they were upset by the spying attempts.","“Through Lord Saint’s wide guidance, we confirmed that he would reincarnate into this Class 2 world. This Class 1 world is in the East Universe.","“Back then, the East Universe was the messiest of the four universes. We didn’t want Lord Saint to reincarnate into an unstable environment so we used the name of Four Seasons Divine Palace to secure Honor Absent Palace’s position in the East Universe and enable them to command the East Universe.","“The species in the East Universe are no longer fighting with Honor Absent Palace. Yet, the East Universe is now trying to target Lord Saint!","“I heard from Spring that Lord Saint has obtained the life treasure of a stupid snake. At that time, we weren’t with Lord Saint. Luckily, Lord Saint is blessed. Otherwise, his reincarnation might have been delayed by the stupid snake’s life treasures’ hidden sabotage!”","Autumn’s expression was full of anger while he spoke.","As a lifeform that had lived for many years, Autumn was Lin Yuan’s follower and servant. However, relative to others, he was an undeniable elite.","Back then, in order to achieve their objectives in the Sky Beyond the Clouds and make it easier for them to serve Lin Yuan, Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter established Four Seasons Divine Palace.","By the time they came to this Class 1 world and established Epoch God Palace as part of their waiting for the Saint to return, Four Seasons Divine Palace had already become legendary in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Regardless of how the epochs changed, Four Seasons Divine Palace would never lose out to Faerie Institution in terms of the might they wielded in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","However, the mention of Faerie Institution could strike real fear, while the mention of Four Seasons Divine Palace was now akin to bringing up a cherished memory.","As a leader, Autumn understood the way that subordinates sought profits for themselves. This was not wrong. However, it should not affect Lord Saint!","While Lin Yuan was evolving Green Vine, Spring did not hold back against the spies. Now, Autumn and Winter were taking the same attitude toward those spies!","In fact, Autumn was even harsher than Spring. She had only killed the fellows that released their life treasures while Autumn obliterated every single entity that was attempting to spy.","There were many times when Winter felt that Autumn was unreliable and did not think things through. But in this matter, Winter did not think that Autumn was doing anything wrong.","If Autumn had not killed these audacious fellows, Spring would have done it.","“Autumn, it looks like Lord Saint intends to continue evolving his feys. There will definitely be more spies coming. You don’t have to pull your punches with them.","“I believe that it won’t be long before some authoritative figures from the West Universe begin paying attention to this matter. Do you think they will break the rules and open a path to this Class 2 world before making their way here?”","Autumn revealed a small smile.","“They will come seeking opportunities. But they have no clue that not coming would be a much bigger opportunity! We made so many preparations for Epoch God Palace. It is still considered part of the West Universe’s authoritative figures.”","Autumn said furiously, “If those fellows are still authoritative figures in the West Universe and are daring enough to descend onto this Class 2 world to attack Lord Saint, they will truly be ungrateful scum! I will definitely kill as many of them as I can get my hands on!”","Winter shook his head.","“Autumn, have you forgotten the right course of action after waiting for Lord Saint for such a long time? If people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds really arrive in this Class 2 world, Lord Saint should be the one who decides what to do next. We don’t have the right to make any decisions!”","The description ‘ungrateful’ was appropriate.","However, the authoritative figures from the West Universe were still ignorant of that.","Those in the West Universe who had the right to know of the legend of the Saint and found out that Lin Yuan was the Saint would put on their most humble demeanor to come to greet him.","Suddenly, a look of surprise appeared on Autumn’s face.","The native dragon-species fey that Lin Yuan was nurturing in this world had evolved its bloodline to the true dragon!","It was rare even in the Sky Beyond the Clouds for a dragon-species fey’s bloodline to reach true dragon at the same time Blackie evolved to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","But when he remembered that it was Lin Yuan nurturing this fey, the surprise vanished from Winter’s eyes.","Lin Yuan witnessed Blackie’s transformation. It could be said that Blackie’s transformation had refreshed his understanding of feys.","Although Lin Yuan had used the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Jasmine Lily to heal Blackie, the latter almost did not make it through its dangerous bloodline transformation.","Luckily, Lin Yuan eventually decided to use the Jasmine Lily’s Vitality Imprint and Recovery Imprint on Blackie.","He also used his body composition to support Blackie.","All of this together enabled Blackie to successfully achieve its transformation.","Blackie remained in its original form during the transformation.","Blackie’s appearance did not change significantly from before, but its black and gold skirt had turned a shining milky white.","Blackie’s aura was even more gentle and graceful than before.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Blackie.","[Fey Name]: Spirit Clawed True Dragon","[Fey Species]: True dragon species/spirit dragon species","[Fey Grade]: World Emperor (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Water","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","[Spirit Injection]: Restore a huge amount of spiritual power at once and restore the lost spiritual power over a period of time.","[Spirit Roar]: Let out a roar to control the direction of the flow of spiritual power. It can choose to boost or drain the spiritual power of the targets in a given area.","[Endowment Spirit Rain]: The bloodline can be used to gather the clouds and release rain that contains spiritual power. The targets that makes contact with the rain will be able to replenish their lost spiritual power.","[Spirit Channel System]: The spirit qi in the body can be released into the environment. Through the spirit qi, a perfect and invisible channel system will be formed. The channel system will not only recover its own spiritual power but decrease the rate at which its spiritual power was diminished.","[Spirit Judgment Imprisonment]: Pick a target and judge the concentration of spirit qi within the target’s body. If the concentration of spirit qi in the target’s body is higher than its own, all of the spirit qi in its body will be emptied out. If the concentration of spirit qi in the target’s body is lower than its own, the target’s spiritual power will be imprisoned.","[Spirit Wrath]: The dragon aura will be unleashed. The dragon aura will burn off all of the spirit qi in the area and cause the surrounding environment to be empty of spiritual power.","[True Spirit Five Changes]: Release the dragon claws. Every dragon claw will become a clone. The clones will possess all the abilities of the main body. They will not disappear after being attacked and will share spiritual power with the main body.","[Spirit Dragon Guide]: Its bloodline energy will become a guide to boost and influence other dragon species lifeforms. The other dragon species lifeforms will thus evolve towards true dragon species/spirit dragon species. The effects will be magnified when used on a lifeform with the same genes and bloodline.","[Spirit Ability Blessing]: Its bloodline will boost the target, which has spiritual power as its root energy. At the same time, the spirit qi capacity and spirit qi activity of multiple targets can be raised.","[True Dragon Spewing Breath]: Dragon breath imbued with its bloodline will be spewed at a target to cause damage to the target. The dragon breath’s attributes will follow that of the Spirit Clawed True Dragon’s pwn. (Water-type True Dragon Spewing Breath effect is obliteration).","Exclusive Skill:","[Spirit Qi Imprint]: The spirit qi that is constantly released to the environment would be stored within the Spirit Qi Imprint instead. It can also drain a small amount of the spirit qi released from other dragon species feys within the surrounding area that does not exceed the fey’s grade and inject it into the Spirit Qi Imprint. It would be branded on the contractor’s body, and the contractor could release spirit qi contained within the Spirit Qi Imprint.","[Spirit Essence Explosion]: Gather the spiritual power into a single point and explode all the energy. The Spirit Essence Explosion can only be applied on places where there is contact with the Spirit Qi Imprint.","[Emperor Spirit Control]: An Emperor Spirit Inscription will be formed within the dragon claw. There can only be one Emperor Spirit Inscription in each claw. Each Emperor Spirit Inscription will allow the amount of spirit qi in the body to be multiplied.","[Calling All Spirits]: Its own spirit qi will be injected into the environment to trigger all the spirit qi in the surroundings to move towards it. If its spirit qi’s ability to control energy is stronger than that of other feys in the environment, the spirit qi in nearby target lifeforms can be extracted.","[Dragon Breath Support]: The energy in the dragon breath will be used to support a body part, either defensively or for combat. Alternatively, various streams of dragon breath can be compressed to launch a powerful attack at the target!","[True Dragon Concealing Spirit]: In an environment full of spirit qi, its own body will be fully fused with the spirit qi environment. Before the spirit qi in the environment disappears, it can hide its presence. In its hidden state, it can rapidly recover its depleted energy.","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Turbid Spirit Cleansing]: Its breath will create a territory in which injured lifeforms will be cleansed by special spirit qi. The lifeforms’ root energy will be transformed into spirit qi.","Blackie had evolved from a main-dragon into a true dragon. Lin Yuan had never heard of this dragon-species bloodline level before and did not know what it implied.","But when Lin Yuan saw Blackie’s divine kingdom ability, he knew it was one of the rarest types, the domain-type.","Furthermore, Blackie’s domain-type ability was very special. It used its own aura to create a territory in which lifeforms that did not have spirit qi as their root energy would be cleansed, and their root energy would be transformed into spirit qi.","In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, spirit qi was the highest form of energy. Most of the upper echelon lifeforms in the Sky Beyond the Clouds had spirit qi as their root energy.","Lin Yuan had heard from Spring that there were treasures in the Sky Beyond the Clouds that could alter a fey’s root energy. Aside from special species like the Blood species, dead lifeforms, and elemental lifeforms on whom these treasures had no effect, these treasures were highly sought after by the other species."]},{"number":2754,"title":"Chapter 2754 Dragon Ascends to the Sky!","paragraphs":["2754 Dragon Ascends to the Sky!","Treasures like this that could alter roots always came with danger and a low probability of success.","Yet, they were seen as foundational treasures in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Compared to these treasures, Blackie’s Turbid Spirit Cleansing was much more advantageous!","Firstly, unlike those treasures, when Blackie’s Turbid Spirit Cleansing created a territory to change the root energy of other lifeforms, the lifeforms’ roots would not be damaged.","Moreover, Blackie’s divine kingdom ability only used up its own energy and faith power. This was not a high cost to change the root energy of other lifeforms.","With this divine kingdom ability, Blackie could create unimaginable value for Lin Yuan.","Aside from this divine kingdom ability, the new abilities and exclusive skills that Blackie gained were also outstanding.","The Sovereign ability it gained was called Spirit Dragon Guide. It enabled Blackie to use its true dragon bloodline to affect dragon-species feys in its vicinity. It would guide all the dragon-species feys’ bloodlines to evolve toward true dragon species/spirit dragon species.","With that ability, Blackie was now a master at nurturing dragon-species feys.","As long as they were within Blackie’s vicinity, any dragon-species bloodline that was below Blackie’s own would benefit. If the dragon-species fey happened to share the same genes as Blackie, the bloodline evolution effects would be magnified!","This immediately led Lin Yuan to think of the Spirit Tide Ink Flood Dragons in Submerged Flood Dragon Lake. All of them used to be Spirit-Siphon Goldfishes.","Lin Yuan had been using the Spirit-Siphon Goldfish’s essence blood to enable their bloodlines to transform, and his efforts were finally showing signs of paying off.","However, it required an unimaginable amount of resource wealth to evolve these Spirit Tide Ink Flood Dragons’ bloodlines to the next level. Lin Yuan did not want to spend such a mountain of resources on the few hundred Spirit Tide Ink Flood Dragons.","Although Lin Yuan possessed a large amount of pure spirit qi now and was willing to spend it, he preferred using the resources to nurture experts rather than the Spirit Tide Ink Flood Dragons. The experts would even be able to repay Lin Yuan with a large amount of spirit qi crystals during their growth process.","But now, Lin Yuan could use Blackie’s bloodline to influence the Spirit Tide Ink Flood Dragons and guide them toward evolving to true dragon species/spirit dragon species.","These Spirit Tide Ink Flood Dragons had a similar gene base to Blackie. As such, their bloodlines would skyrocket.","Once Lin Yuan confirmed the range of efficacy of Spirit Dragon Guidance, he would be able to cultivate and evolve an even larger batch of Spirit-Siphon Goldfish.","Due to environmental limitations, the Submerged Flood Dragon Lake in the Return from Faraway Mansion could not house many Spirit-Siphon Goldfish. But once he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he could create a Spirit Dragon Lake specifically suited to the utilization of Spirit Dragon Guidance.","All he needed was to invest sufficient resources, and he would be able to create a scene of thousands of dragons soaring in the sky.","The spirit qi released by feys with the dragon-species bloodline would be able to increase the rate at which the Spirit Qi Imprint accumulated spiritual power. There were many potential benefits.","The High Sovereign ability, Spirit Ability Blessing, was a blessing ability. However, this blessing did not increase the rate at which targets recovered their spirit qi or their spirit qi activity, but rather the target’s spirit qi capacity.","This form of blessing was very rare.","It could significantly increase the target’s endurance during combat! This was because the target usually needed to evolve their grades in order to increase their body’s energy capacity.","Moreover, Spirit Ability Blessing could target multiple targets at once, thereby raising the strength of an entire team.","True Dragon Spewing Breath was an ability that suited all true dragons.","Dragon breath was the strongest combat technique for all dragon-species feys.","Being a water-type fey, Blackie’s dragon breath would cause obliteration effects.","The breath of water-type true dragons was part of the top three true dragon dragon breaths.","Blackie’s exclusive skills raised its combat abilities to a far greater extent than its abilities did!`","Calling All Spirits allowed Blackie to inject its own spirit qi into the environment and call all the spirit qi in the environment toward it to recover its depleted energy.","This exclusive skill could bring almost unlimited energy to Blackie in an environment brimming with spirit qi.","Aside from being able to recover Blackie’s depleted energy, when Blackie’s own energy had stronger control over spirit qi than the other lifeforms in the environment, spirit qi could be extracted from surrounding targets and absorbed by Blackie.","True dragons naturally possessed extremely high dominance.","Moreover, Blackie was a spirit dragon that excelled at controlling spirit qi! It was very unlikely that feys of the same grade would be able to exert stronger control over spirit qi than Blackie!","Only feys of higher levels would be able to exert stronger control than Blackie.","However, such control could only target lifeforms that had spirit qi as their main energy. If their main root energy was not spirit qi, Calling All Spirits would lose its effectiveness.","Between Dragon Breath Support and True Dragon Concealing Spirit, Lin Yuan favored Dragon Breath Support.","As the strongest form of combat technique for dragon-species feys, dragon breath was very violent in its execution.","Dragon Breath Support would allow Blackie to wield its dragon breath in a wider range of avenues during combat. Its dragon breath could be used as armor or applied to a weapon.","When it was paired with Spirit Essence Explosion, it would be able to generate extraordinary effects.","Additionally, Dragon Breath Support could compress multiple streams of dragon breath to cause added damage to targets. This gave Blackie the ability to fight above World Emperor/Divine Kingdom. The other World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys would be green with envy over this ability!","The Eternal exclusive skill, True Dragon Concealing Spirit, was not bad. It allowed Blackie’s body to be fused into the environment and for Blackie to remain in a concealed state as long as the spirit qi did not disappear. It could even recover its depleted spirit qi while in the concealed state.","This exclusive skill clashed against Spirit Ability Blessing to some extent.","Blackie was already able to use Spirit Qi Imprint to create an environment with a high concentration of spirit qi.","Moreover, Lin Yuan would definitely protect Blackie, a functional-type fey. It was almost impossible for Blackie to ever find itself in danger.","As the Saint of Epoch God Palace, Lin Yuan had Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter protecting him at all times.","While Lin Yuan was observing Blackie, the latter was also serenely surveying itself.","When it sensed the transformation of its bloodline, two gem-like droplets of tears fell from the corner of its eyes. The Spirit-Siphon Goldfish was the most inferior type of dragon-species bloodline. Blackie’s journey thus far had been a tangle of emotions.","However, as a fey that spent a lot of time with Lin Yuan, Blackie did not stand on ceremony with him. Blackie had been with Lin Yuan ever since it gained intelligence. In its eyes, Lin Yuan was no different from its parent.","After Lin Yuan evolved Blackie, he did not intend on nurturing any other feys for the foreseeable future aside from allowing Merciful Foul to absorb the calamity that was sealed off in Tower Canon’s old nest!","Although Lin Yuan had used his own body’s composition to evolve the Jasmine Lily and Blackie, he still used up a considerable amount of its store of spirit qi. His pile of spirit qi crystals was much smaller than before.","Lin Yuan checked the time.","He had spent a little over a month enlightening his birth horoscope in the Returning Saint Pool and almost a month combined evolving the Jasmine Lily and Blackie.","These two months had been spent very fruitfully. Both his own power and foundation had utterly transformed. Lin Yuan really liked this feeling of evolving continuously.","Lin Yuan smiled at Blackie and said, “Blackie, you haven’t had a chance to return to your original form yet. Let me take a look at what your original body looks like now.”","Lin Yuan was certain he would be shocked by the sight of a true dragon.","Blackie let out a loud dragon roar. This dragon roar was clear and elegant but also carried a unique dominance.","Blackie rose to the sky, and all that could be seen was half a tail and a slender leg beneath the misty clouds. There were seven dragon claws on the foot.","Lin Yuan gently stomped his left leg, and six pairs of black wings appeared on his back and carried him up into the sky.","As a birth-horoscope expert, Lin Yuan could fly with ease and was no longer as awkward as king-class experts. However, Lin Yuan was accustomed to using the Source Sand for flight.","Lin Yuan saw Blackie’s curled milky white dragon body that extended thousands of meters. Its whiskers radiantly and majestically adorned its face while resting atop the breeze. Its scales were no longer as sharp as before. Instead, they had a watery transparency.","Lin Yuan was stupefied when he saw the image of Blackie flying.","Autumn and Winter also admired and were amazed by Blackie.","The same thought entered both their minds. This was truly a fey that was personally evolved by Lord Saint. It was remarkable!","Neither of them disturbed the interactions between Lin Yuan and his fey. They only went over to Lin Yuan after he returned Blackie to the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Winter told Lin Yuan everything that had happened and did not hide how the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds had tried to spy on this Class 2 world.","When Lin Yuan heard this, he realized that he had been careless.","While helping Green Vine to evolve, he had witnessed the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds turning their attention to the main world and attempting to investigate the happenings in the main world. Spring had killed all of them.","After that experience, he should not have allowed the main world to continue attracting attention. If an expert from the Sky Beyond the Clouds truly decided to target the main world, this would likely spell disaster for the main world.","When Winter saw the worried expression on Lin Yuan’s face, he knew that Lin Yuan was concerned for the main world’s safety after hearing what he just said.","Winter hurriedly began explaining, “Lord Saint, even if someone from the Sky Beyond the Clouds truly tries to continue spying on or pay a visit to the main world, we will be able to ensure the main world’s safety, so there is no need for you to be worried!","“Even if a scheme is cooking up in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, it won’t come into play immediately. These matters usually require extensive discussions between multiple parties who will eventually collectively send people to this Class 2 world!”","Lin Yuan nodded.","He did not know Winter well. However, he naturally felt a strange closeness to Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter.","Moreover, Winter was very dependable and would never lie to him when it came to such matters.","Spring and Summer were done gathering the death aura in the ley lines. The death aura was gathered below the Startling Lines Continent’s sea, where Red Thorn and Silver Corona would be able to absorb it.","Spring and Summer turned the death aura that could not be collected into death aura crystals. When the death aura crystals were buried in the ground, they could form Dead Spirits Wells.","After returning, Spring and Summer bowed to Lin Yuan upon seeing him.","Lin Yuan pondered for a moment before handing Merciful Soul to Spring and instructing her to take it to Tower Canon’s fortress so it could absorb the calamity there.","Spring had already told Lin Yuan it would take a considerable time for Merciful Soul to evolve by absorbing calamity. It would only be done in three to five years.","Lin Yuan could not spend the next few years in Tower Canon’s old nest just to accompany Merciful Soul while it evolved.","Previously, Lin Yuan intended to wait until he set his spirit fire alight before he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","At the time, he believed he still had a long way to go before he set his spirit fire alight.","However, after emerging from the Returning Saint Pool, he was now a birth-horoscope expert. He was not at beginner birth horoscope either but was only a step away from reaching the spirit-fire level.","Lin Yuan intended to change the entire main world and unite the dimensional worlds with the human world. This would not only enable both sides to become equal but would also raise their individual resistance. Both sides would then begin improving in the right direction.","Lin Yuan needed to expend significant effort in order to change and improve the main world. Recently, he had been fully focused on this endeavor.","Since Lin Yuan had Winter to take care of the spies from the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would no longer have to worry on that front!","Firstly, Lin Yuan trusted Winter. Secondly, it was very likely that the continuous evolution of his feys would startle some bigshots from the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Those bigshots were not as easy to handle as Tower Canon. It was unlikely that Lin Yuan had the capabilities to take them on even if he wanted to.","Unless it was absolutely necessary, Lin Yuan did not want to waste time on matters that were beyond his means.","Once the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds arrived in this world, he would be able to gain a deeper understanding of the Sky Beyond the Clouds through them despite not having been there yet."]},{"number":2755,"title":"Chapter 2755 The Spirit Lock Spatial Zone’s Changes!","paragraphs":["2755 The Spirit Lock Spatial Zone’s Changes!","Half a year had passed since Lin Yuan had dealt with the Eight Pages of Tower Canon.","As the number of feys that could heal death aura increased, many regular people infected by death aura had recovered.","Although the main world had not changed drastically, Lin Yuan’s Spirit Lock spatial zone had changed enormously.","Hu Quan had remained in the Spirit Lock spatial zone to construct and set up the interior.","Lin Yuan had not used Spirit Lock to spirit-lock more feys. Hence, Morbius’ grade had not increased even after the Jasmine Lily and Blackie evolved. The size of the Spirit Lock spatial zone remained unchanged.","After being nourished by the high concentration of spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, the more than 100 Deposit Vegetable Pods that Lin Yuan had planted had successfully changed into human form.","They took over the Medusa Snake Demon’s jobs and were able to take good care of all the plants in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. They were also able to look after the heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls with outer radiance to raise their purity.","Hu Quan was the type of person who liked to immediately materialize his ideas and designs, meaning he was very willing to do rush jobs.","All of the Spirit Craftsmen working in the Spirit Lock spatial zone had contracted Vitality Sloths and could work for 20 hours daily without feeling tired.","Hence, through cooperating with the Land Imps, a new base and structure were completed in the Spirit Lock spatial zone on an almost weekly basis.","Lin Yuan intended to return to the Spirit Lock spatial zone to gain an understanding of all the changes before he began altering the main world.","Upon entering the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Chu Ci barrelled into him and wrapped him in a big hug.","She had done as he said and remained in the Spirit Lock spatial zone to increase her power.","Lin Yuan had told Chu Ci almost nothing about what was happening in the main world, but she knew everything nonetheless.","Chu Ci knew that Lin Yuan had been unable to look after her recently because he had been battling a large faction called Tower Canon.","This battle was linked to the safety of the entire main world.","Chu Ci did not feel a great sense of responsibility or a need to save the world. She never wanted Lin Yuan to take it upon himself to save the world, nor did she feel exceptionally proud that he was the savior of the main world.","All she wanted was for her only family to be able to live happily and healthily, regardless of whether the world was currently in a state of prosperity or catastrophe.","Worry and longing led Chu Ci who normally never showed her emotions to lose control of her composure.","Lin Yuan returned Chu Ci’s hug and enjoyed this warm feeling.","Chu Ci clenched her fists when she heard what Lin Yuan said.","Chu Ci inhaled deeply to get a full whiff of Lin Yuan’s scent. He smelled exactly the same as she remembered. This smell filled Chu Ci with a sense of security.","After separating from the hug, Lin Yuan noticed that Chu Ci was taller than he remembered.","She was at the age where her growth was the most rapid. This growth was not limited to her body but also her mental maturity.","Unlike him, this was not her second life, and she had developed a stable and well-rounded perspective from her previous life.","Lin Yuan was very worried that her thoughts would become twisted after experiencing so much conflict and complications. If that happened, he would have failed as her brother.","“Chu Ci, when I told you about Tower Canon, I mentioned the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Do you have any thoughts about the Sky Beyond the Clouds?”","Chu Ci smiled and shook her head.","“Lin Yuan, anywhere is home as long as you’re there! I am grown up now and have done my best to increase my power. From now on, you must take me with you wherever you go!”","Lin Yuan nodded seriously.","Chu Ci rarely made any requests of him. Whenever she did, it meant that it was a sincere plea.","Firstly, with Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter around, Lin Yuan would not be in much danger even when he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Moreover, the Spirit Lock spatial zone was large enough to house millions of people.","Lin Yuan had no plan to house too many people in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. However, close people like Chu Ci could live in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Regardless of where they were, Lin Yuan could be assured of Chu Ci’s safety as long as she was in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","When Lin Yuan went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would do the same as when he first went to the marsh world and select a suitable location to develop.","His territory would thus become Sky Sea’s base.","Hence, none of the resources Lin Yuan spent on the territory would go to waste, regardless of the quantity. This was because his base was mobile.","Lin Yuan could ensure Chu Ci’s safety in the territory.","Rather than keeping Chu Ci in the main world, her development would undoubtedly be better if she went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds with him.","Chu Ci was still a B-rank spirit qi professional, and her feys were all Diamond X/Fantasy V.","It would take time for her to become an A-rank spirit qi professional.","Lin Yuan did not feel rushed in the slightest.","He had already instructed Chu Ci to form a contract with the Lifespan Mouse, so she now possessed an endless lifespan.","...","Lin Yuan did not go to check on the Spirit Lock spatial zone immediately.","Instead, he spent three days with Chu Ci in the underground palace before he went to see Hu Quan.","Hu Quan had finished the construction of the precious lifeform garden.","Precious lifeforms did not refer to a specific lifeform but all lifeforms that possessed a high value.","Hu Quan had moved all the resources like the Twin Red Pagoda that could ignite the Lifeform Sacrificial Fire and the Soldier Ration Radish, which was considered a foundational resource to the precious lifeform garden.","The precious lifeform garden was not overly large, but it was tended to by 200 Hundred Questions Beasts and 20 Myth Breed Deposit Vegetable Pods. They both looked after and protected the lifeforms in the garden.","The 20 Deposit Vegetable Pods were never swapped out, but the 200 Hundred Questions Beasts worked in shifts. Each day, a new group of Hundred Questions Beasts would come to the precious lifeform garden to take over the previous day’s group.","This ensured that the Hundred Questions Beasts that worked in the precious lifeform garden would not become complacent due to any particular reason and would continue to keenly look out for possible issues in the precious lifeform garden.","The precious lifeform garden had been constructed after a discussion between Hu Quan and Lin Yuan.","Without Lin Yuan’s explicit instructions, Hu Quan would not casually waste resources to turn his designs into reality. This was a trait that Lin Yuan always admired about Hu Quan.","Currently, Hu Quan was making plans for the demon insect nest.","The demon insects were multiplying faster than expected, so the space dedicated to the demon insects had to be continuously expanded.","Hu Quan estimated that if Keira put her whole effort into developing the demon insects, they would take up half the space in the Spirit Lock spatial zone even if some of them were shifted out.","Hu Quan did not want to give Keira so much space. Hence, he was resolutely finding ways to improve the structure and design of the nest.","Hu Quan had been trying to find a way to bring this matter up with Lin Yuan. He could not come outright and say that the large occupancy of demon insects affected his plans for the Spirit Lock spatial zone!","This matter did not trouble Hu Quan for long because when Lin Yuan found out about Hu Quan’s plan, he said, “Uncle Hu, do you remember me instructing the Land Imps to fortify the mobile base when I asked you to build an insect nest for Keira?","“My purpose was to make the demon insect nest easy to move around so it can even be moved out of the Spirit Lock spatial zone. You don’t need to worry about Keira’s situation. Just focus on the designs for the other areas!”","Before his battle with Tower Canon, Keira’s nest was not in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Lin Yuan had only ever promised Keira that he would supply her with pure spirit qi. This was an extremely easy promise to fulfill for Lin Yuan. All he needed was to give her some spirit qi crystals.","If she performed well, Lin Yuan could use his body to supply her with spirit qi.","The demon insects were notorious in the Sky Beyond the Clouds and feared by all the species. The main reason for this was that the demon insects needed to consume the bodies of other species to extract their bloodlines. As such, they consumed all that was in their sight in order to develop their species.","The demon insects that were born without much intelligence and were mainly used as tools lived only to plunder and grab resources.","However, once the demon insects had enough resources to expand their species, they would become more peaceful than other species.","Pre Keira’s words: “With enough to eat and drink, only idiots would be willing to work hard!”","Lin Yuan was unsure how long he would stay in the main world. But he would be here long enough for Keira to turn the demon insects into a powerful species.","It would be best if Keira could produce the second batch of insect eggs before they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Previously, Keira filled all her insect eggs with death aura, which became their root energy. This limited the development of Keira’s demon insects.","Lin Yuan intended to use Blackie’s divine kingdom ability to change the root energy of the female insects with Class 1 Genetic Locks.","This would allow Lin Yuan to test out the effects of Turbid Spirit Cleansing, as well as the drain that it would have on Blackie.","Hu Quan could not contain his delight when he heard what Lin Yuan said.","He could not ask for anything better than to remove the demon insects that did not have a shred of aesthetic sense from the Spirit Lock spatial zone and for him to take full control of the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s design!","Living in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Hu Quan was bathed in pure spirit qi and felt refreshed and energized every day.","He already saw the Spirit Lock spatial zone as his home.","All the feys in the Spirit Lock spatial zone had very high intelligence, and Hu Quan felt at ease around them.","When it came to artistic design, Hu Quan had some insecurities. He believed that an artist should not socialize too much but focus on comprehending beauty and attempting to merge said beauty into their designs.","Lin Yuan understood Hu Quan’s pursuit of beauty. It was evident from his attention to and insistence on the intricacies.","Lin Yuan now had a job he would assign to Hu Quan.","“Uncle Hu, do you remember the Submerged Flood Dragon Lake that you constructed in the Return from Faraway Mansion? I would like you to move it into this space. However, it needs to be much larger than before. It will have to be able to house at least 10,000 flood dragons!”","Lin Yuan expressed his request simply. But after hearing what Lin Yuan wanted, a majestic image unfolded in Hu Quan’s mind!","Thousands of flood dragons flying atop the surface of a lake would make for a breathtaking sight. Hu Quan believed that such a scene could not be done justice by imagination alone and needed to be witnessed in reality!","Even without the help of the Land Imps, Hu Quan could have created the lake Lin Yuan wanted with all the Spirit Craftsmen he had, much less now that he did have the Land Imps’ support.","“Young Master, if we begin work on that lake now, it will take around two months to complete! There was sufficient larimar and amazonite among the resources you previously gave me. They are both treasures and are even better than what was used in the Return from Faraway Mansion!","“However, jade-textured wood shards were used to lay the foundation previously. A large amount of jade-textured wood is produced in this space daily. I suggest that we use this jade-textured wood to cover the bottom of the lake instead!","“On the outside, Sunlight King Lotuses need to be planted at the bottom of the lake for the water to appear transparent. The pure spirit qi nourishing the Spirit Lock spatial zone will enable the jade-textured wood to glow on its own. This will cause the lake to look like the surface of a mirror, and the dragons swimming within it will be seen clearly!”","Lin Yuan smiled. “Uncle Hu, you can come up with a design and make all the decisions about such matters. If you have any other design ideas or need any resources, just contact me through the Thoughts Letter Paper!","“Aside from the main lake, I hope you can create smaller lakes that lead out from the main lake. I will be nurturing some special aquatic feys in these small lakes.”","The Spirit Lock spatial zone had become the main base where Lin Yuan nurtured feys, and he needed to think carefully and thoroughly when it came to the design.","He might be able to discover some excellent aquatic fey species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds."]},{"number":2756,"title":"Chapter 2756 Treecastle in the Sky!","paragraphs":["2756 Treecastle in the Sky!","Lin Yuan continuously perfected Sky City’s structure.","In the eyes of other factions, these seemed to be giant secret establishments. But in actuality, they were not even Sky City’s core.","As Morbius’ grade continued to increase, the Spirit Lock spatial zone continuously grew larger.","The Spirit Lock spatial zone perfectly realized all the ideas and plans that Lin Yuan had. It was now Sky City’s core.","As long as Lin Yuan wanted to, he could move Sky Sea and Lift Marsh into the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The construction of the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s interior had become a top priority. From now on, Lin Yuan would nurture various feys and species in the Spirit Lock spatial zone that were rare in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Hence, Lin Yuan would rather spend more resources now than have to alter the Spirit Lock spatial zone later.","Hu Quan was very serious about his work and took the same attitude toward leading the team. Having to redo the work when there were no issues with the design was the greatest disrespect to Hu Quan and the other Spirit Craftsmen!","Hu Quan barked out a few delighted laughs.","Ever since he began working for Lin Yuan, Hu Quan had been very satisfied and carefree.","There was nothing that a Spirit Craftsman was more afraid of than having their resources limited, as this would restrict their inspiration.","With Lin Yuan, not only had Hu Quan’s inspiration never been limited, but he was frequently enlightened by the new resources that Lin Yuan gave him access to as well.","As a result, Hu Quan had broader horizons. He also came to understand that in order for a Spirit Craftsman’s class to be raised, they required not just skill and experience but, more importantly, an elevated mind.","Hu Quan had his reasons for using jade-textured wooden planks rather than jade-textured wood shards to cover the bottom of the lake.","Amazonite had the ability to purify water. With the spirit qi’s nourishment, amazonite could produce water that was as blue as the sky and completely absent of impurities.","When larimar was embedded at the bottom of the lake, it would generate water currents. Larimar was essential in creating a comfortable environment for nurturing water-type dragon-species feys.","The larimar created very tough water currents that would strengthen the dragon-species feys’ bodies. This gave them more strength when they swam.","If jade-textured wood shards were used to cover the bottom of the lake, the churning of the water currents would create some turbidness in the water.","But if jade-textured wooden planks were used to cover the bottom of the lake, Hu Quan could alter the genetic model of the wooden planks to suit the environment at the bottom of the lake.","When light shone on the bottom of the lake, rays of light were reflected. If the water was absolutely clear, even looking at the lake from a close distance would allow one to see thousands of flood dragons dancing in the sky.","Hence, aside from striving for perfection in his designs, Hu Quan never forgot to do his best to minimize the cost that Lin Yuan incurred.","Lin Yuan shook his head.","Genius had not stopped reporting Hu Quan’s progress to Lin Yuan.","Genius had given its input on both the breeding room for the army of Hundred Questions Beasts and living areas for the cats.","Hu Quan had essentially received an order and built the breeding room and living areas according to Genius’ specifications.","Both the breeding rooms and living spaces were functional bases.","Anything was fine as long as it was what Genius wanted!","With Hu Quan’s designs and as long as he was not shackled, the functional bases could also be turned into works of art!","“Uncle Hu, I don’t need to go and see it. Aside from the lake, you can make use of the upper area of the Spirit Lock spatial zone. This will maximize its utilization!”","Lin Yuan’s words stunned Hu Quan and opened up new potential ideas.","However, Hu Quan did not have any inspiration or thoughts at the moment.","He just could not find a way to make use of the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s upper area.","Hu Quan knew that whenever Lin Yuan brought up an idea, he did so after having given it some thought. Lin Yuan was not the kind to shoot from the hip and ignorantly toss tasks to his subordinates.","After ensuring he did not have any ideas, Hu Quan asked, “Young Master, what are your ideas for using the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s upper area? There is no limit to its height, so it is truly worth using it.","“I did some tests and found the concentration of spirit qi in the sky to be comparable to that on the ground. It will make a conducive environment to nurture avian-type feys. However, avian-type feys will need to stop to rest. Even if they have sufficiently high intelligence and know not to defecate while in the sky to avoid polluting the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s environment, they will need a place to rest.”","Lin Yuan smiled. “Uncle Hu, you lived in the Divine Wood Federation for some time as well. Have you forgotten about the special plants that are used as treecastles there?","“Let’s take the Prosperous Chamber of Commerce’s Hollowed Tamarix as an example. After the Hollowed Tamarix evolves to Myth Breed, it will be able to grow up to tens of thousands of meters tall. The Hollowed Tamarix can lower the external pressure to ensure that lifeforms can live comfortably within it. It is also able to store sunlight, and the backs of its leaves will subsequently release the sunlight.","“I learned from Elder Weng that the Creation Breed Hollowed Tamarix can grow to almost 50,000 meters tall. If we want to make use of the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s sky, our best option will be to nurture the Hollowed Tamarix! The light in the Spirit Lock spatial zone is currently supplied by the jade-textured wood. However, the sunlight requirements for all the feys in the Spirit Lock spatial zone are being met.","“Gray’s clear weather and Chimey’s sun can both be situated in the sky to illuminate the Spirit Lock spatial zone. It won’t take long to fill the Hollowed Tamarix’s leaves with energy. The interior of the Hollowed Tamarix can house people while its branches can be used to rear avian-type feys, as well as insect-, spider-, and beast-species feys that live in trees.”","The main reason Lin Yuan wanted to make use of the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s sky was that he wanted to maximize the use of the energy. This would ensure that the spirit qi produced by the spirit pool would not accumulate in the Spirit Lock spatial zone and potentially cause the spirit pool’s rate of production of energy ores to slow down.","Energy ores were not considered to be very valuable in the main world, and it was the same in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","The spirit qi mineral veins were as precious as they were in the Sky Beyond the Clouds because the spirit stones mined from the spirit qi mineral veins had a purity of more than 40% and could be directly absorbed by lifeforms.","The same could not be said for that of the main world.","There were also many energy ores in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, and they were used as tradeable currency by low-class lifeforms.","Hence, it was necessary for the spirit pool to maximize its distilling ability.","Lin Yuan’s words caused Hu Quan’s eyes to light up.","Planting many tall tree castles in the Spirit Lock spatial zone could indeed increase the utilization of its upper area.","Technically, there was no sky in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. Lin Yuan was essentially creating one using the tree castles.","The area above the tops of the trees could also be used, as long as the tops of the trees were not crushed.","Hu Quan never suspected Lin Yuan’s ability to nurture feys.","The Spirit Lock spatial zone was essentially a giant treasure trove.","The Deposit Vegetable Pods in the Spirit Lock spatial zone had not been specially nurtured. They evolved into human form after five to six months of absorbing the pure spirit qi there.","The Hollowed Tamarix would definitely be more difficult to nurture than the Deposit Vegetable Pods.","However, it would be able to reach Creation Breed very quickly if it was planted in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Moreover, the army of Hundred Questions Beasts under Lin Yuan were all high-class Creation Masters.","When Hu Quan learned of this secret, he could not believe everything that was in front of his eyes! This secret overhauled his understanding of the sacred profession of Creation Masters.","However, Hu Quan would not reveal this secret.","Hu Quan also knew that he would not have the chance to reveal this secret. Lin Yuan would never let him leave again after he began working in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. Otherwise, regardless of how much Lin Yuan trusted him, he would never share so many secrets with him!","Others might see this as a loss of their freedom, but Hu Quan saw this as Lin Yuan giving him a chance. It was a chance for him to map out this Eden of a world!","“Young Master, I will create a garden used to nurture the Hollowed Tamarixes. Once they have grown to maturity, I will arrange them in the Spirit Lock spatial zone! They do not let in sunlight easily. Jade-textured wood will still be needed to illuminate the top of the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","“I will pick some jade-textured wood and carve them into the shape of stars and place them on the branches of the Hollowed Tamarixes. This way, those who look up from the ground will be able to see the gleaming constellations!”","Lin Yuan nodded and replied, “Uncle Hu, the jade-textured wood is a resource that we can produce very quickly. Do whatever you want without worrying about the amount of jade-textured wood that you have to use. If you don’t have enough wood, I will send Listen to collect some and deliver it to the Spirit Lock spatial zone.”","Lin Yuan always held the idea of family close to his heart. This did not refer to people but to a place he was familiar with.","It was true that the Return from Faraway Mansion was Lin Yuan’s home in the Radiance Federation. But he could not shift the Return from Faraway Mansion to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. The Spirit Lock spatial zone would thus become his proxy home.","The Moon Empress, Liu Jie, Wen Yu, Su Yiren, and the rest would all be going to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","They would all be living in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, and Lin Yuan could rest easy!","After telling Hu Quan about his requests, Lin Yuan took a general stock of the situation in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Keira was still asleep, and Lin Yuan did not wake her up.","After settling the matters in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Lin Yuan decided to focus on the main world as a whole and begin making alterations to the main world.","Lin Yuan took out the Thoughts Letter Paper but did not contact the Moon Empress immediately. Instead, he contacted Wen Yu.","He could not ask his master to give him a report of the circumstances. It was easier and more convenient to communicate with Wen Yu and Wo Lun than the Moon Empress.","Ever since the death aura disappeared from the ley lines, Wen Yu started helping Lin Yuan to organize and gather information from all over the main world.","Wen Yu was Lin Yuan’s companion and one of the three founders of Sky City. She could tap into the channels of information in the main world and quickly organize all of the information.","Wen Yu was undeniably capable. But she was only able to collect so much information in the short span of a few months because of the Source Paper’s exclusive skill, Hear Heaven’s Secrets.","[Lin Yuan]: Wen Yu, how is Wo Lun doing with his boats and plans?","Wen Yu looked surprised and happy when she saw the message from Lin Yuan.","[Wen Yu]: Young Master, you are finally out of seclusion! With the Moon Empress’ support, everything on Wo Lun’s side is going very smoothly. The Radiance Federation’s major cities will soon be able to begin using boats for trading! The only setback is that with all the options of spiritual ingredients that you’ve given Wo Lun, the boats are constantly being rebuilt. Luckily, the rebuilt boats have crazily high demand from the other federations and are sold almost immediately after being built.","Wen Yu felt that it was rather a waste to swap out the boats that had only been in use for less than two months. After all, the new fleets were not significantly better than the previous ones.","Moreover, the sea clans were now on good terms with the human factions, while the water world’s lifeforms were perfectly under Lin Yuan’s control. They would never pose a threat to the humans who used the boats for trade.","Hence, the change in the new boats’ capabilities should not use up so many resources!","After a moment of silence, Wen Yu told Lin Yuan about her thoughts.","Lin Yuan was the one who supplied the obscene amount of resources that Wo Lun was wasting.","The waste of billions of Radiance dollars worth of resources caused Wen Yu’s chest to ache.","Lin Yuan smiled and shook his head after reading Wen Yu’s thoughts.","Firstly, he could produce a large amount of resources quickly.","Moreover, the innovation of the boats would determine the main world’s main mode of trading in the future. Any amount of resources that was spent was a necessity.","Wo Lun dared to do all this because he had received Lin Yuan’s approval.","Moreover, the other federations were there to take over the eliminated boats.","If this situation was prolonged, all the federations in the main world would eventually have sufficient boats for trading.","The Radiance Federation would be the first to receive the cutting-edge boats. This ensured that the Radiance Federation would remain the leader of the pack regardless of what changes took place in the future!"]},{"number":2757,"title":"Chapter 2757 The Destroyed Dimensional Wall!","paragraphs":["2757 The Destroyed Dimensional Wall!","Lin Yuan would not call himself selfless, but he had indeed used numerous resources to develop and break ground on this enormous main world as well as protect all of the humans, sea clans, and dimensional lifeforms in it. He had caused the plan that Tower Canon had carefully woven together to fail to achieve its goal of destroying the main world.","Most of Lin Yuan’s ties to the main world were with Radiance citizens. In everything that he did, he would fulfill his priority first.","[Lin Yuan]: Wen Yu, this is actually a good thing for the main world and the Radiance Federation. Our resources come from the entire main world as well as the dimensional worlds. If these resources are used to build fleets of boats that service the dimensional worlds and main world through enabling trade, the main world will enter a period of rapid development.","[Lin Yuan]: This is critical for a Class 2 world! It isn’t bad for every federation to have their own culture. The flow of trade will allow the individual federations’ cultures to interact, and this will continuously make up for any gaps in each federation’s culture.","When Wen Yu saw the contents of Lin Yuan’s messages, she realized that she was too short-sighted.","Just as Lin Yuan said, if the main world’s federations were enabled to trade using the boats, there would be no more separation within the main world, and the human federations would not be prevented from interacting with each other because of geographical constraints.","Humans never stopped gaining new desires.","The weaker federations would definitely choose to ally with larger federations in the hope of improving their development. But if they were able to interact culturally and had the financial means, despite the presence of the Major Federation Union, to keep violence from breaking out, the smaller federations would definitely form ambitions to overthrow the larger federations.","These were all factors of unease and instability.","Wen Yu felt that she needed to tell Lin Yuan about these destabilizing factors since she had thought of them.","Lin Yuan was not at all surprised by the message that Wen Yu sent him. Given her intelligence, she was fully capable of thinking to such an extent. However, this was still far from sufficient!","Lin Yuan had utilized the Lifespan Mouse, allowing numerous experts with endless lifespans to emerge. However, as Lin Yuan ventured into the Sky Beyond the Clouds and time progressed, the prevailing tranquility in the main world was not sustainable.","This remained true despite the efforts of the Major Federation Union to maintain peace. It wasn’t a lack of trust in the Moon Empress’ preparations, management, or the Major Federation Union’s control over the main world.","The reason lay in the fusion of the main world with the five dimensional worlds. Over time, Lin Yuan’s influence over dimensional lifeforms would diminish, and the treasures from the five dimensional worlds would lose their efficacy. Consequently, the new dimensional lifeforms operated beyond Lin Yuan’s control.","In the past, there was only source-type and faith power in the dimensional worlds. But after being nourished by the spirit qi from the main world, the new dimensional lifeforms would acquire spirit qi as their energy source.","In terms of potential, the new dimensional lifeforms undoubtedly had more!","These new dimensional lifeforms would slowly replace the old dimensional lifeforms.","Those that were superior would eliminate those that were inferior. Only the strong would survive. This was the underlying principle of this world, and it applied to the sea clans as well!","The collaboration between the sea clans and humans would last for at least the next few hundreds or even thousands of years.","However, after tens of thousands of years had passed, the sea clans and humans would resume their fighting and disputes.","The human factions were not the only ones who needed the resources that were traded through sea trade. The sea clans needed them as well. The strong sea clans that were not restrained would definitely attack the humans over the resources.","This was only something that Lin Yuan came to understand after reaching a certain level. He felt that he needed to find an opportunity to break down and explain this matter to Wen Yu as it would be extremely beneficial for her critical thinking and broadening her horizons!","Once he had expanded her mindset, Wen Yu would be able to analyze issues with a wider and more objective mindset. Naturally, this would lead her thinking skills to improve exponentially!","[Lin Yuan]: Wen Yu, we still need to continue doing everything we can to support Wo Lun. Additionally, tell Wo Lun to take in more disciples and pass on his skills just like Uncle Hu did. Wo Lun comes from the Violent Wind Federation. There should be a fair number of people from there who are capable of building boats. We can use the Radiance Federation’s name to recruit and hire adventurers from the Violent Wind Federation who are capable of building boats!","There were many aspects of Wo Lun, and his boat-building skills were not something Wen Yu understood.","But since Lin Yuan had given the order to fully support Wo Lun, it went without saying that Wen Yu would follow Lin Yuan’s instructions to the tee.","After asking the question that he most wanted an answer to, Lin Yuan sent another message.","[Lin Yuan]: I previously asked you to collect and gather information on the five dimensional worlds. How is that going? Have the root energy of the new dimensional lifeforms shown signs of shifting?","Had Lin Yuan not asked about Wo Lun first, she would have reported the circumstances of the five dimensional worlds to him first.","[Wen Yu]: Young Master, we have underestimated the pace of change in the dimensional worlds. Currently, numerous descendants of lifeforms from the abyssal, water, alien insect world, and even the previously averse to spirit qi marsh world, are exhibiting a surprising sensitivity to spirit qi. What’s more, many of these mutations are hereditary, passing down through generations. This development has sparked intense debates in the dimensional worlds.","[Wen Yu]: Numerous Apostles and Dictators view these newly emerged lifeforms, possessing spirit qi, as anomalies and potential energy sources. Up to now, I have merely observed and documented the unfolding situation, refraining from any interference. I am awaiting your guidance on the appropriate course of action.","Lin Yuan paused for a moment before he responded.","[Lin Yuan]: This is a necessary stage that needs to take place after the fusion of the dimensional worlds and the main world. If we issue an order to Samsara Realm Dictators to forbid the other Dictators and Apostles from laying a hand on the new lifeforms with spirit qi as their root energy, the destabilizing elements will build up in a short span regardless of whether the Samsara Realm Dictators obediently carry out the order.","[Lin Yuan]: As opposed to that, we should allow the five dimensional worlds to go through the changes naturally. After all, the lifeforms with spirit qi as their root energy will eventually increase in number, and there will definitely be a change of hands in the yoke of authority!","Wen Yu knew that Lin Yuan wanted to improve the unity between the main world and dimensional worlds. The best way to do this would be to increase the number of dimensional lifeforms that had spirit qi as their energy source.","Wen Yu had been with Lin Yuan for a long time and was used to taking a judicial and administrative mindset when she analyzed issues.","Now, Lin Yuan was showing her an indirect way of examining issues.","After mulling over it, Wen Yu realized that this way of thinking could indeed unite the main world and dimensional worlds in a stable manner.","However, it would take considerable time for everything to play out naturally.","Natural development was always the best choice.","At that moment, Wen Yu felt that she could understand why Lin Yuan wanted to wholeheartedly support Wo Lun and the building of boats. He must have already predicted the extent of the main world’s derivation and the impacts that would unfold in the main world’s future!","Lin Yuan was already Wen Yu’s role model, and she had learned most of her methods from him.","But she never expected that even now, there was still so much that she did not understand about him.","She had only picked up one way in which he viewed issues.","[Wen Yu]: Young Master, Bai Qinghuan supervised the construction of the dimensional wall that separates the main world from the dimensional worlds and which prevents the invasion of the dimensional worlds into the main world. When creating this wall, she did not anticipate the dimensional lifeforms to slam into the dimensional wall so relentlessly. Several parts of the wall are showing signs of damage and need to be fixed by the Land Imps! Bai Qinghuan asked me to seek your opinion on this!","After Bai Qinghuan was done supervising the building of the Radiance Federation’s defenses, Lin Yuan placed her at the boundary between the main world and dimensional worlds.","The dimensional wall was the biggest project undertaken by Bai Qinghuan to date. She was well aware of the labor and effort that had gone into the project.","But now, so soon after its completion, the dimensional wall was showing signs of damage.","It would be fine if the dimensional wall was damaged as a result of the dead spirits crisis, but the truth was that it was damaged by the dimensional lifeforms.","Because of this, Bai Qinghuan could not explain herself to Lin Yuan. She did not even dare to report the matter to Lin Yuan herself and sought help from Wen Yu.","Bai Qinghuan never believed herself to be important to Lin Yuan, especially after she saw how many capable people Lin Yuan had in his orbit. Wen Yu, Liu Jie, Su Yiren, Listen, Qin Yu, and Hu Quan were all gifted individuals!","She could indeed be of great help when it came to battle coordination.","But after the dead spirits crisis ended, the main world entered a period of prolonged peace, and Bai Qinghuan’s abilities were no longer applicable.","As someone who lacked a sense of security, Bai Qinghuan was the most afraid of not being needed.","Recently, she had been in a state of constant nervousness.","Wen Yu had been observing all of Bai Qinghuan’s behavior. However, she had not said anything to Bai Qinghuan because she was Lin Yuan’s assistant and could not direct him toward any decisions.","Moreover, during the time that Lin Yuan had relied heavily on her, she had been arrogant and conceited.","This change in Bai Qinghuan greatly displeased Wen Yu.","Wen Yu guessed that Lin Yuan would not put Bai Qinghuan on the spot.","The dimensional wall had been built with the intention of defending against the dead spirits and not the dimensional lifeforms.","Lin Yuan wanted to unite the main world and dimensional worlds.","The dimensional wall would either be changed or deconstructed so the spiritual materials could be repurposed into other infrastructure projects.","With a large number of Land Imps, repurposing the dimensional wall would not come at a high cost.","If Lin Yuan was willing to divert 200,000,000 Land Imps to this endeavor, they would be able to deconstruct the dimensional wall in a little over 20 days!","It would take the Land Imps much less time to deconstruct the base than it had taken them to build it.","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow.","He pondered over the matter and guessed that new dimensional lifeforms were the culprits that damaged the dimensional wall. The dimensional lifeforms that were fully under his control would never do such a thing!","If even Wen Yu could guess what Bai Qinghuan was thinking, it went without saying that Lin Yuan could do the same.","Lin Yuan had heard from Return to Ruins about Bai Qinghuan’s behavior during the building of the bases that linked the dimensional worlds and main world.","Return to Ruins found Bai Qinghuan’s demeanor to be over the line.","Otherwise, Return to Ruins would never have brought up this matter to Lin Yuan with the insinuation of complaining about Bai Qinghuan when he knew that she was his subordinate!","In her pursuit of quick progress, Bai Qinghuan had even eliminated several Land Imps that were moving too slowly.","Bai Qinghuan was a native of the Divine Wood Federation and was influenced by its culture. Hence, she carried the aristocratic degeneration as a member of the Divine Wood Federation’s elite.","Lin Yuan believed that he could use this opportunity to get Bai Qinghuan back on the right track.","[Lin Yuan]: Wen Yu, I intend on taking Bai Qinghuan to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. With her ambition, it is not suitable for her to remain in the main world. Her abilities will come in handy there. But I intend on placing her under you in the future. You can handle this matter!","Lin Yuan never needed to be overly explicit when he spoke to Wen Yu. She was always able to understand his meaning.","After reading the Thoughts Letter Paper, Wen Yu paused before she responded.","[Wen Yu]: Bai Qinghuan isn’t to blame for this matter. However, with the matter of the dimensional wall, it won’t be appropriate for her to lead the team of Land Imps that deconstruct the dimensional wall. Return to Ruins is free. Why don’t we send him to lead the team while Bai Qinghuan supports him? Once Bai Qinghuan returns, I am sure that she will obediently work under me!","When Lin Yuan saw the message from Wen Yu, he could not help but sigh to himself.","Wen Yu had managed many matters and was now familiar with the procedures.","Return to Ruins had pent-up rage against Bai Qinghuan. When he worked under her, he had not been able to protect the Land Imps under him, and she had not extended any courtesies to him.","Now that Return to Ruins was the one leading the team, it went without saying he would vent all his anger.","During this assignment, Bai Qinghuan would understand that every dog had its day.","In the future, she would be more restrained in her actions.","Return to Ruins had reached the Afterlife Realm and was the strongest of the three Dictators from the subterranean world.","It was also necessary to bear with his way of doing things.","The Land Imps were selfish, shallow, and petty.","If Return to Ruins had to continue suppressing his rage, it would inevitably lead to bumps in the road in the future."]},{"number":2758,"title":"Chapter 2758 Reopened Dimensional Rift!","paragraphs":["2758 Reopened Dimensional Rift!","An outstanding person with internal governance talent needed to have broad horizons. Lin Yuan could not be overly focused on the few subordinates under him. Otherwise, it would undoubtedly lead to issues in the team!","He liked talented people but did not like those who were arrogant and abused their power to unreasonably grab benefits for themselves.","There were issues with Bai Qinghuan’s supervision of the construction project. If he did not take this opportunity to understand this and she was let off easy, there was no guarantee that she would not cause trouble for Lin Yuan again in the future!","After ending his discussion with Wen Yu, Lin Yuan contacted the Moon Empress.","The main world was currently in a state of peace and calmness. There would be no more trouble in the main world for a very long time.","However, the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ spying into the main world would put the main world in danger.","According to Autumn, the four universes were in conflict with each other.","The four universes had agreed on a rule. Even if they were warring with each other, they would never lay a hand on worlds that were Class 3 and below.","The low-class worlds were the bricks that made up the entire system of the Sky Beyond the Clouds. If the low-class worlds did not exist, they would lower the combat power of the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ experts.","If experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds were allowed to interfere with the operation of the low-class worlds, a light consequence would be that the low-class worlds’ evolution would be affected and cause them to be stuck at their grade without being able to progress even at the point of extinction. A heavy consequence would be the direct collapse of the worlds!","The dominant factions from the four universes would not allow the members of other factions to interfere with the low-class worlds. However, they could play some tricks in the low-class worlds to obtain some profits.","Once the Sky Beyond the Clouds decided to target a low-class world, they would come up with a reason to legitimately suppress the low-class world.","Winter had promised Lin Yuan that the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds who came to the main world would not leave any impact on the main world.","Lin Yuan believed Autumn and Winter but could not risk the Radiance Federation being put in any danger.","Lin Yuan intended to send Summer to the Radiance Federation to protect it while Autumn would accompany him to collect spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan would be the only one who collected the spirit qi crystals. No one else could perform this task in his stead. Spirit qi crystals were his most precious resource!","Although Lin Yuan had activated his body composition and could inject pure spirit qi into the bodies of targets by placing his hand on their bodies and circulating the energy in his body, his body composition was his secret and was irreplaceable!","The Moon Empress was the highest level of management of the human factions.","Lin Yuan needed to let the Moon Empress know of these matters so she could be mentally prepared at the very least.","With Summer protecting the Radiance Federation, no issues would crop up.","If Lin Yuan had not evolved three of his feys to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, something like this would never have happened!","If the Moon Empress received such news before learning about his abilities, she would definitely be panicked.","But now, Lin Yuan carried the heavy responsibility of protecting the main world.","With the guarantee from Lin Yuan, the Moon Empress would not have to worry about possible dangers.","Firstly, even if the Moon Empress focused on this matter, she would not be able to stop the dangers even if she racked her brain.","Moreover, there were many things that the Moon Empress needed to do and decisions she needed to make.","Rather than focusing on issues she could not solve, it would be better for her to focus on issues that were more meaningful.","[Lin Yuan]: Master, the dimensional lifeforms are merging rapidly with the main world. I will generate natural sparks in the dimensional worlds without direct interference. The entire process will be deliberately prolonged. Humans won’t be adversely affected by these developments, but I believe it’s crucial for us to prepare in advance for the integration of the dimensional worlds and the main world.","[Lin Yuan]: As spirit qi becomes the fundamental energy for dimensional lifeforms, humans can attempt to form contracts with many of these lifeforms. We must shift the antagonistic perception between humans and dimensional lifeforms. However, it’s essential to note that reducing hostility doesn’t imply that humans should let their guard down against dimensional lifeforms.","[Lin Yuan]: My plan involves manually creating several dimensional rifts and reinforcing them with minerals infused with spatial energy. If the human federations wish to open dimensional rifts in their territories, they can submit requests to us. I propose opening multiple dimensional rifts in each city to enhance the quantity and resilience of the City Guards.","The Moon Empress’ eyes lit up when she heard what Lin Yuan said.","She had been thinking about the best way to train the Radiance experts.","If the dead dimensional lifeforms were used to train the Radiance Federation’s men, the endurance of the dead spirits crisis would become extremely important.","But now, Lin Yuan had extracted all of the death aura in the ley lines.","If the humans had not created the Dead Spirits Wells, it would be very unlikely for the dead spirits to appear in the main world again. This would significantly deflate the potential effects of using the dead spirits to train the Radiance troops!","After the dimensional world fused with the main world, no more dimensional rifts opened in the main world.","The dimensional rifts were always an excellent way for the humans to train their combat powers. It could be said that the youths from most federations had experience training and hunting in the dimensional rifts.","Lin Yuan was capable of creating many dimensional rifts and handing over the authority to the Radiance Federation to do so.","This increased the leverage that the Radiance Federation had over all the human federations. In the future, the other federations would need to acknowledge the Radiance Federation’s leadership position in order to open dimensional rifts in their own federations.","[Moon Empress]: Little Yuan, your idea will be very helpful for humanity! What is the cost of manually creating the dimensional rifts? I would like to start in the Radiance Federation’s major cities before slowly expanding outward. We will meet the Radiance Federation’s needs first before thinking about the other federations.","Lin Yuan was silent for a moment.","He did not know how much it would cost to open a dimensional rift.","Lin Yuan asked the Samsara Realm Dictators from the various dimensional worlds to help make estimations for the various classes of dimensional rifts.","But since the Moon Empress had asked him for numbers, Lin Yuan would definitely collect the information diligently. After a moment, Lin Yuan organized the data and handed it to the Moon Empress.","Aside from the substantial amount of resources required to open Class 5 dimensional rifts, it also required a significant amount of resources to open Class 4 dimensional rifts.","As for Class 6 dimensional rifts, they could not be opened regardless of the amount of resources spent.","In the past, the dimensional worlds and main world overlapped with each other. But now, they were combined.","The dimensional rifts were very similar to the Space Tunnels. However, the Space Tunnels could not cause the space to overlap, and this significantly raised the difficulty level.","Lin Yuan had excavated sufficient resources from the subterranean world to create millions of dimensional rifts.","The main world’s federations would definitely not require so many dimensional rifts.","Moreover, the dimensional rifts only needed to be opened on land.","The sea clans were getting along swimmingly with the dimensional lifeforms.","They had a close affiliation with water-elemental energy and spirit qi. Even the Dictator sea beasts were able to temper their bodies with spirit qi to slowly subsume spirit qi into their bodies.","The mermaids came from the Sky Beyond the Clouds and were naturally affiliated with spirit qi.","But without spirit qi, they had no choice but to use source-type power to strengthen themselves.","Now that they had spiritual power, all of the mermaids transformed in a very short period of time.","Lin Yuan thought to himself that it was possible that the water world dimensional lifeforms and sea clans would be fully united in the next few thousand years and live harmoniously in the sea.","The situation in the sea could not be compared to the situation on land.","Although the Major Federation Union maintained order on land, there were still undercurrents of instability during this time.","Meanwhile, all of the lifeforms in the sea had become close to the mermaids.","Mermaids used to exist in the main world. Otherwise, the Goddess of Mercy would not have been able to evolve her mermaid bloodline to king-class after gaining the mermaid bloodline.","Back then, the sea clans of the main world had all been treating the mermaids as gods.","The mermaids were as capable as the Heavenly Family Feys when it came to controlling water elements. Once their bloodline reached king-class, they would even become stronger than the Heavenly Family Feys at controlling the sea!","The sea clans put the mermaids on a pedestal. Even Ice Flow and the other leaders of the Vast Sea Labyrinth were extremely respectful toward Dazzling Silver, Light Green Umber, Blue Umber, and the other emperor-class mermaids.","...","After Lin Yuan recounted the recent events and sent the data, the Moon Empress was over the moon.","She was aware that Lin Yuan possessed the mermaid thearch-class bloodline.","After Lin Yuan left the main world, the mermaids would also carry on his will.","Once the sea clans’ faith was applied to the mermaids, the mermaids would soon replace Vast the Sea Labyrinth as the leaders of the sea clans.","As a result, regardless of how the water world dimensional lifeforms and sea clans changed over time, the mermaids would be able to promise that the lifeforms from the sea clans would not clash with the humans.","The Moon Empress and Lin Yuan no longer perceived resources in the same way they used to.","In the past, the Moon Empress’ knowledge utterly surpassed that of Lin Yuan.","The first time Lin Yuan had entered the Radiant Moon Palace’s treasure trove and seen the thousands of bottles of potions and exquisite resources stacked together, he had felt as though his eyes were being opened for the first time.","But now, the difference between their experiences was even larger than that of Lin Yuan and the Moon Empress in the past!","When the Moon Empress fully understood Lin Yuan’s store of resources, she knew how she was going to negotiate with the other federations who wanted to open dimensional rifts in their own territories.","...","Ever since Lin Yuan picked Autumn to remain by his side, the smile had yet to leave his face.","Autumn had handsome and stony cold features. His eyes had the dashing elegance of autumn wind. In the words of Lin Yuan’s previous life, he was classically handsome!","Now, his lips were curled into a broad smile. But this did not clash with his chiseled coldness. Rather, it gave the air of brilliant chrysanthemums blooming at the height of autumn!","While remaining by Lin Yuan’s side, Autumn supplied him with faith every second.","Lin Yuan could sense genuine sincerity and trust from Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter.","...","Two years had passed since Lin Yuan began taking Autumn around with him to collect spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan had spent the entire two years traveling.","For his own convenience, Lin Yuan had asked Liu Jie to instruct the Land Imps to build teleportation arrays and ten teleportation nodes in Thick Soil City while collecting the spirit qi crystals.","From then on, all the experts in the main world who were ready to evolve would be transported to Thick Soil City through these ten teleportation nodes.","Once Liu Jie was done overseeing this matter, Lin Yuan would no longer have to run around the main world in order to collect the spirit qi crystals!","For the past two years, Lin Yuan had been waiting for the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds to arrive.","It was just as Winter had said at the beginning.","The deaths of many Border Patrol Guards in the Sky Beyond the Clouds who supervised the low-class worlds would definitely attract the attention of Honor Absent Palace.","However, there had been no movements in the past two years, and Lin Yuan felt as though they were all talk and no action.","Autumn knew what Lin Yuan had been thinking for the past two years.","Autumn said calmly, “Lord Saint, the low-class worlds are under the protection of the world rules, and time passes much slower than in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. In the two years that you’ve spent in this Class 2 world, only around 20 days have passed in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","“The larger the faction, the more degenerate their internal affairs. If the upper management of Honor Absent Palace learns of this matter, they will definitely begin fighting like dogs! But regardless of how slow the fighting progresses, someone will come within six months!”","Lin Yuan raised an eyebrow—that explained everything!","Time passed in the main world at a different rate than it did in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. The difference was more than ten times!","In these two years, aside from collecting resources, Lin Yuan had also been seriously observing the development of the main world.","Today was Lin Yuan’s 21st birthday. He was now an adult.","The Radiance Federation had returned to the same state as before the dead spirits crisis.","Various classes of dimensional rifts had opened in various areas of the Radiance Federation.","After the Radiance Federation took control of these dimensional rifts, they became the Radiance Federation’s main training grounds. The Dead Spirits Wells had the same function.","After the dimensional rifts opened in the Radiance Federation, the 12 aristocratic families of the Azure Federation immediately contacted the Moon Empress in the hopes that dimensional rifts could also open in the Azure Federation.","The Moon Empress first agreed to the Azure Federation’s terms before she offered the same incentive to all the other human federations at the next imperial meeting.","Since the Radiance Federation sat at the helm of the Major Federation Union, they needed to carry a suitable attitude.","The Radiance Federation needed to treat all the federations equally.","While Lin Yuan was waiting for the visitors from the Sky Beyond the Clouds to arrive, there was finally news from Merciful Soul’s side!"]},{"number":2759,"title":"Chapter 2759 The Death Demon Concubine Beast’s Divine Kingdom Ability!","paragraphs":["2759 The Death Demon Concubine Beast’s Divine Kingdom Ability!","After absorbing calamity for so long, Merciful Soul was finally beginning to evolve to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom!","Merciful Soul’s abilities and exclusive skills were extraordinary.","It was the only curse-type/spiritual-type/soul-type fey that Lin Yuan knew of.","In the past, Lin Yuan never used Merciful Soul. But this was not because it could not be of help to him but because its abilities were too domineering.","Steal the Fate of a Nation and Demon Concubine’s Promise would allow it to take over all the fate within a territory, as well as inject calamity into the territory. All the lifeforms in the territory would become entangled in the calamity.","If such an ability was expanded, it would be even more terrifying than the dead spirits crisis.","The dead spirits crisis was terrifying in a structured way, and the fear could be linked directly to the dead dimensional lifeforms.","On the other hand, Merciful Soul was terrifying in an unstructured way. It was a fear that could not be linked directly to anything!","This fear would cause the fear of inferior lifeforms to grow endlessly and create hardship for many.","Merciful Soul had yet to use its ability in the main world, but there was a chance that it would be able to demonstrate its ability in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Even if Merciful Soul was not by Lin Yuan’s side, its evolution would bring him benefits.","Autumn sensed the energy fluctuations coming from Merciful Soul and said softly, “Lord Saint, if this fey of yours evolves to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, it will definitely trigger the opportunists in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. It will likely bring forward their eventual visit. It’s possible that they will arrive soon after your fey evolves.”","Autumn felt significant unease.","In the many years of waiting for the Saint to reincarnate, Autumn had suppressed himself, bringing out a tranquilness in him.","But now that he was by Lin Yuan’s side, all the anxiousness resurfaced.","Lin Yuan’s expression did not change in the slightest.","He had already expected the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds to come to the main world because of his feys’ evolutions. The timing of their arrival made no difference to him.","Even if the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds came, Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter would take up the duty of protecting the main world. With his power, he could not offer much help against the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ experts!","Autumn could sense the energy fluctuations from Merciful Soul, but Lin Yuan could not.","But it did not take long before Merciful Soul’s data appeared in front of Lin Yuan.","[Fey Species]: Demon concubine beast species/faceless beast species","[Fey Type]: Curse/Spiritual/Soul","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","[Death]: Make judgment on the target’s willpower, soul, spirit, and mind power. If the judgment decides that the combined power of the four powers is weaker than it, the lifeform will not be able to attack it.","[Heart Words Cross Disaster]: Place a voiced curse on the target. The strength of the target’s spiritual energy will determine the strength of the curse. Under the influence of the curse, if another curse is placed on the target’s mind, the effects of the curse will multiply, and the target’s soul will start to corrode.","[Demon Concubine’s Promise]: The Death Demon Concubine can turn its heart into a pill that can be gifted to a target. The target will become the Death Demon Concubine’s dependent, and their lives will be tied together.","[Heart Stolen Soul Photographed]: After Disaster Heart curses the target’s soul, it can enter the target’s body and use its soul to control the target’s body.","[Deepened Curse Imprint]: Magnify the effects of the curse on the target and bewitch the target’s mind, soul, and spiritual energy simultaneously.","[Steal the Fate of a Nation]: If it can influence the fate of a country that sits upon a certain area of the earth, the fate can be stolen. The price of this ability is the burning up of one’s lifespan.","[Demon Concubine’s Chaos]: When affecting the fate of the nation that the territory belongs to, a chaotic destiny can be injected into the territory. The chaotic destiny will afflict all the lifeforms on the ground with bad luck. The bad luck’s effects will be linked to the strength of the chaotic destiny.","[Calamity Gathering]: Calamity will be absorbed from the environment. When the calamity is gathered, the curse effects faced by other lifeforms in the environment will be removed and cleansed.","[Calamity Trigger]: This will target calamity in the bodies of lifeforms. The calamity in targets will be triggered, and their fortune value will be lowered. They will encounter accidents and mistakes both in life and in combat.","[Adversity Growth]: At necessary moments, the calamity can be transformed and used as lifespan to elongate its own lifespan. When its calamity is used up and its lifespan is about to come to an end, the calamity can be fully depleted (the fully depleted calamity will need 100 years to be replenished).","Exclusive Skill:","[Faceless Appearance]: Set a target and absorb its bloodline, spiritual energy, and soul. It will then assume the appearance of the target and obtain all of its abilities.","[Fate of Chaos]: Absorb the fate of the ground it is present on. The fate can be used to enhance the effects of its abilities.","[Payment in Life]: Use its lifespan to investigate the lifespans of other targets. If its own lifespan is sacrificed, it can take away another’s lifespan by touching the target.","[Disaster Fortune Application]: A disaster fortune imprint will be applied on the target. The disaster fortune imprint will measure its own calamity to the fortune in the target. If the calamity in its own body is greater than the fortune in the target, it will absorb the fortune in the target while injecting calamity into the target.","[Shared Affection]: The damage suffered can be shared with targets that feel affection for it. The targets that feel affection for it will share the damage it suffers.","[Demon Concubine’s Control]: Each of its eyes carries the ability to control lifeforms. As long as the target’s divine kingdom grade is not more than two grades above its own and the target has less calamity in its body, the Death Demon Concubine Beast will be able to take hold of the mind and spirit of the target that feels affection for it and become its puppet.","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Hardship Transformation]: The calamity and fortune in the divine kingdom can be transformed. The calamity eye and fortune eye will be formed on the Fortune Calamity Tablet in the divine kingdom. The calamity eye can enable calamity to accumulate continuously in the target’s body. The fortune eye will enable fortune to accumulate continuously in the target’s body.","Merciful Soul’s Creation Breed exclusive skill was called Disaster Fortune Application.","Disaster Fortune Application would place a disaster fortune imprint on the target’s body before measuring its own calamity with the target’s fortune. If there was more calamity in its body than fortune in the other party, not only could it absorb the fortune in the target’s body but could also inject its own calamity into the target.","Calamity was intangible.","But as Lin Yuan’s power and level continued to rise, he could not deny the existence of calamity.","Compared to energy and fortune, calamity was on a comparable level to faith power. It was a very rare type of energy.","When Spring saw Merciful Soul, surprise appeared on her face. Merciful Soul could absorb calamity from the environment into its own body, but other lifeforms did not have the ability to absorb fortune from the environment.","Disaster Fortune Application could be linked with Calamity Gathering and Calamity Trigger.","Calamity Gathering strengthened Merciful Soul’s ability to gather calamity from the environment and could remove and cleanse the curse effects experienced by lifeforms in the environment.","The ability to remove curses from a group was a very rare support ability.","According to Spring, there were many species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds that were held in high regard because of their curse abilities. These species were rarely trifled with.","The species with curse abilities were famed and feared for these abilities.","However, in front of Merciful Soul, these species would have no choice but to keep their heads lowered.","Calamity Trigger would trigger the calamity in other lifeforms. The calamity would be used to lower the fortune of targets and turn their fortune values to negative.","When a person was unlucky, they would feel pain in their teeth when they drank cold water and trip when they walked. These misfortune effects would all be triggered in the target, and even living would become a challenge, much less during combat!","The disaster fortune imprint applied on targets by the exclusive skill, Disaster Fortune Application, would allow targets to have more calamity than other energy in their bodies!","Meanwhile, Adversity Growth and Demon Concubine’s Promise could be linked with Payment in Life.","The Lifespan Mouse that Merciful Soul had contracted through Demon Concubine’s Promise would enable Merciful Soul’s lifespan to lengthen endlessly. As such, Merciful Soul’s lifespan became a lethal weapon!","However, the Lifespan Mouse accumulated lifespan at a set rate and could not be evolved.","Hence, after Merciful Soul reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, the help offered by the Lifespan Mouse decreased significantly.","However, Adversity Growth made up for this drawback as it would turn calamity into lifespan.","If it lacked lifespan, it could overdraw on its calamity.","However, overdrawing on its calamity came at a cost.","If Merciful Soul could not replenish its overdrawn calamity in the next 100 years, its lifespan would also come to an end.","This enabled Merciful Soul to have the ability to roll numerous grades to fight.","But now that Lin Yuan had Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter by his side, he would not have many opportunities to send Merciful Soul out even if he was in danger.","The Immortal ability Merciful Soul gained was Shared Affection.","Shared Affection was a self-preservation ability.","When Merciful Soul was attacked, it could share the damage with entities that felt affection for it.","Merciful Soul was capable of breeding chaos and was a beast lifeform.","If many lifeforms felt affection for Merciful Soul, it would be very difficult for it to be killed even by powerful enemies!","The new exclusive skill, Demon Concubine’s Control, could be linked with Shared Affection.","This was the exclusive skill that Lin Yuan favored the most.","Each of Merciful Soul’s eyes could take control of a lifeform. As long as the target had less calamity in its body and its Divine Kingdom grade was not more than two grades above that of Merciful Soul, the latter could attempt to take control of the target.","For two lifeforms to have divine kingdoms that had more than a two-grade gap, they had to have many magnitudes of difference in power. They were not fit to be compared at all.","Yet, Merciful Soul could take control of many of such targets. This was enough to see its potential.","Merciful Soul could create a powerful World Emperor/Divine Kingdom army for Lin Yuan.","While Lin Yuan was checking Merciful Soul’s data, he glanced at Merciful Soul, which had transformed into the form of a beautiful human.","Suddenly, Lin Yuan felt as though his looks could not measure up to that of Merciful Soul.","Its clear doe eyes and slightly curled shapely lips adorned its round head with petite bone structure. It wore a purple and pink dress that did not look gaudy at all. Rather, it could be described as beautifully elegant.","It was a pity that there was too large of a gap between Spring and Merciful Soul. Spring only admired Merciful Soul’s looks and did not feel any other special emotions.","Currently, Lin Yuan was thinking about what level Merciful Soul’s divine kingdom ability could affect.","Merciful Soul’s divine kingdom ability could be seen as a functional- and production-type one.","Merciful Soul could transform calamity and fortune within the divine kingdom with Hardship Transformation.","After Merciful Soul absorbed the calamity from a place of peril and transformed it into fortune before injecting it into the environment, it would have used its own means to create a place of fortune.","Once the power of lifeforms reached a certain level, they would be able to sense danger.","Currently, Lin Yuan could not come up with a use for the calamity eye produced on the Fortune Calamity Tablet in Merciful Soul’s divine kingdom.","Rather than using the calamity eye to increase the amount of calamity in the target’s body, it would be better to use Disaster Fortune Application to place a disaster fortune imprint before injecting a large amount of calamity into the target’s body.","Every lifeform sought fortune.","The fortune eyes on the Fortune Calamity Tablet in Merciful Soul’s divine kingdom could be seen as an excellent spiritual ingredient.","If this spiritual ingredient was sold on the market, many factions from the Sky Beyond the Clouds would fight over it.","However, Lin Yuan did not lack resources. Rather than trading these resources at the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan preferred to keep them for his own use!"]},{"number":2760,"title":"Chapter 2760 Visit from the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","paragraphs":["2760 Visit from the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","The fortune eyes would bring fortune to the Moon Empress, Chu Ci, Wen Yu, Liu Jie, and the rest. It would allow them to encounter even more opportunities while they were increasing their powers.","The increase in fortune would bring immeasurable benefits to a lifeform!","If there was something like the fortune eye in Lin Yuan’s previous life, even a person who was down in the dumps would be able to win the lottery after obtaining the fortune eye and increasing the amount of fortune in their body!","After Merciful Soul evolved to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, Spring would bring it back to the Radiance Federation.","Then, Spring and Summer could protect the Radiance Federation together.","Just as Lin Yuan was preparing to enter the Spirit Lock spatial zone to see how the Wind Speed Rapid Antelope was doing with its organization of the resources, he received a message from Peace on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Peace was an official member of the Astronomical Parliament, and Lin Yuan had invested significant resources into her to enable her to grow.","Each delivery of resources to the Broiling Rock Continent required a large amount of law power.","Luckily, Lin Yuan’s Sacred Sword Wielding Queen had absorbed numerous Law Runes and could make use of the broken Law Runes.","Peace had a merciful heart that wanted to save the Broiling Rock Continent.","However, this also limited her sights to the Broiling Rock Continent. Even now, she was still worried about Green Continent City’s development.","A person’s potential and demeanor determined their future development. The impact of a person’s abilities on their future also rested on their potential and demeanor.","With Peace’s experience and mindset, Lin Yuan believed she was only suitable to being the City Lordess of Green Continent City.","After confirming this, Lin Yuan became somewhat disappointed in Peace.","He had brought this up with Peace in the past.","Although he had never explicitly said he would be taking her with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he had told her he would be giving her opportunities.","Alas, she had not properly made use of these opportunities.","Lin Yuan did not like to force or coerce others, much less try to manually alter their perception and demeanor.","Hence, Lin Yuan had not paid much attention to Peace lately. If Peace had any issues, she would go to Wen Yu for help.","Lin Yuan was rather surprised to see the sudden messages from Peace.","[Peace]: Leo, Green Continent City has officially changed its name to the Green Continent Federation. We have a population of more than 20,000,000 and are still growing! However, many marshes form in the Green Continent Federation’s current location during the monsoon season.","[Peace]: The various plants and animals that die in the marshes will create a poisonous air that limits the Green Continent Federation’s development. Are you able to arrange for a suitable location for the Green Continent Federation’s development where we will be able to lay down our roots permanently?","Peace should not be coming to Lin Yuan over such a matter. However, Wen Yu had not given her a definite response after sending her request to her.","There were very few natives of the Broiling Rock Continent.","Green Continent City had just changed its name to the Green Continent Federation. If a suitable location for development was not found, it would be difficult to expand the Green Continent Federation’s population!","Peace was also unwilling to accept the homeless from other federations.","This was not because she was picky about the Green Continent citizens but because most of the homeless that had been ejected from other federations were bad eggs!","After all, during the crucial stage of a federation’s development, its population was a critical resource. From a certain angle, a population would increase the transfer of resources and represent the labor force.","Peace was afraid that taking these people in would lead to a coup in the Green Continent Federation.","Normally, Wen Yu treated Peace very well. As such, she assumed that Wen Yu’s lack of reply was due to her being too busy. She had no idea her request had wholly disappointed Wen Yu and even caused Wen Yu to look down on her.","Wen Yu felt that Peace, Bu Po, Luo Lan, and Su Yiren had a similar set of circumstances. All of them wanted to use their own capabilities to bring prosperity to their federations.","All of them had been blessed by Lin Yuan.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie had been helping the four of them and treated them equally.","But, during the development of their federations, Bu Po, Luo Lan, and Su Yiren never sought help from Wen Yu.","No one was forcing the four of them to become the leaders of their federations.","Since she was incapable, why did she want to manage a federation?","Moreover, Peace was in a rush to change Green Continent City’s name to Green Continent Federation but had yet to meet the requirements of being called a federation. Green Continent City’s population had not even reached the size of an inferior federation like the Iron Hammer Federation. There were even more people in two Diamond tribes!","At the beginning of the migration, Peace had asked Wen Yu which region would be the most suitable for development.","Wen Yu had seriously responded that the best option would be a place that had four clear seasons, a complex environment, and wide plains. As long as there were four clear seasons, they would be able to nurture special feys.","With these special resources and feys, the Green Continent Federation would not be able to trade with other federations. A region with large plains would be suitable for growing production-type plants. As long as the area experienced a relatively normal level of rainfall, such an area would be able to bring in regular bountiful harvests.","Wen Yu had given Peace the best answer.","However, Peace had not heeded Wen Yu’s advice. This was likely because the Broiling Rock Continent was traumatized by their experience with water scarcity. As such, Peace eventually selected a location with many bodies of water.","Each time rain filled up the bodies of water, they would have no issues obtaining drinking water. However, finding food would become even more of a struggle than when they were on the Broiling Rock Continent!","Wen Yu had already pointed out a path of development for Peace, but the latter had not listened to her. Wen Yu did not want to help her anymore.","In the Astronomical Parliament, Ta Lei lacked talent and could only be the City Lord of Thick Soil City at best. Hence, he dared not hope for too much for himself.","The only other member of the Astronomical Parliament who was single-mindedly focused on the development of their federation was Luo Lan.","Su Yiren and Bu Po had talked with Wen Yu and set their sights on the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Wen Yu felt that Peace had wasted Lin Yuan’s nurturing.","It would be fine if Peace could do a good job of being the City Lordess of Green Continent City and properly manage its development. However, she was unable to accomplish this and insisted on changing Green Continent City’s name to Green Continent Federation.","Wen Yu liked people with ambition—only such people were capable of achievements.","But if capabilities could not match up to ambition, doubling down on one’s ambition would be a stupid choice!","At the end of the day, Peace lacked a sufficient mindset and character.","Wen Yu had guessed that Peace would go to Lin Yuan if she did not receive a response from her. This was not a bad thing as this would give Lin Yuan the chance to understand Peace’s situation.","Wen Yu believed that with her understanding of Lin Yuan, he would definitely help her with her request, especially if it was a matter he could handle easily.","But once he helped her, she would never be able to advance past being the ruler of the Green Continent Federation. Whether the Green Continent Federation subsequently survived or was destroyed would also no longer have anything to do with Lin Yuan.","The truth played out as per Wen Yu’s expectations.","Lin Yuan frowned after seeing Peace’s messages.","In Lin Yuan’s previous life, 20,000,000 people was not a small number at all. But in this fey world, even the Xia Region, where Lin Yuan used to live, had a population of more than 8,000,000! The Xia Region was a very small region in Redbud City.","It was likely that the Green Continent Federation’s name was being spread by Peace herself. The official federations would never acknowledge the Green Continent Federation’s presence!","However, Lin Yuan’s brows soon relaxed.","Everyone chose their own paths. Peace had already chosen her path, so she needed to bear the associated consequences!","Peace was a member of the Astronomical Parliament. Since she had already made her request, Lin Yuan would definitely help her!","[Lin Yuan]: If you want to relocate with the Green Continent Federation, it will be best to head far away from the various dimensional rifts. Look for a place with four clear seasons that is also near to a powerful federation.","Lin Yuan could only tell her about the right spot to pick. He did not have the time to understand the main world’s current map and territories.","After the dead spirits crisis ended, many federations migrated.","Previously, many federations made their choice under duress from the dead spirits crisis.","Even the Azure and Freedom Federations had intentions of migrating back to their original locations.","It could be said a place would change regardless of whether there was a leader facilitating the change.","The Major Federation Union had just managed to establish and sustain the peace.","Lin Yuan could not give the Green Continent Federation special rights when it came to choosing a location as it would interfere with the Moon Empress’ plans.","The Green Continent Federation’s subsequent development would depend on Peace’s individual capabilities.","Having made the decision to embark on the journey to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan shifted his attention toward those who would be joining him, emphasizing their significance over those who opted to stay in the main world.","Peace’s matter was only a small interlude.","After replying to Peace, Lin Yuan immediately went to the Spirit Lock spatial zone to select a few resources.","He would be supplying even more resources to nurture his companions who would accompany him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, as well as the main world’s experts!","...","Lin Yuan did not know that his answer had confused Peace.","Most of the residents in Green Continent City could not even fill their stomachs now.","In regions bordering lakes, the monsoon season rendered the ground damp and soft. While ordinary plants might endure such conditions, their roots would inevitably succumb to rot.","Regret lingered within Peace. Had she only needed Wen Yu’s advice, her current predicament would have been averted.","To the southeast of the Green Continent Federation’s current location, a spot precisely matching Wen Yu’s description existed. This was where the Dense Forest Federation had chosen to establish its roots.","The Dense Forest Federation garnered bountiful harvests every few seasons, sustaining its development and amassing surplus resources for trade with other federations.","Lin Yuan’s response closely mirrored Wen Yu’s. However, Peace couldn’t fathom why Lin Yuan deliberately emphasized the importance of the Green Continent Federation aligning itself with a formidable federation.","The strength of a federation directly correlated with the influence it could wield. A dominant federation naturally asserted control over its neighboring federations.","While the Major Federation Union prevented outright absorption of weaker federations, it didn’t preclude the powerful federation from exerting covert influence over them.","This would be a cause of considerable stress for Peace while she developed the Green Continent Federation.","Peace believed that it would be better to be positioned near a weaker federation than a powerful one! The weaker federations would gather together to increase their overall strength but would not be able to take down each other. They would be able to develop simultaneously for the long term!","Peace’s idea deviated from that of Lin Yuan. This was just like when her idea deviated from that of Wen Yu.","Peace hesitated before she eventually decided to do as Lin Yuan said and relocate the Green Continent Federation to the vicinity of a powerful federation.","Peace did not know if she was making the right choice.","...","With the current situation in the main world, powerful federations would only grow stronger.","It was inevitable that fights would break out among the smaller federations while they were developing.","The Moon Empress had already decided to separate the main world into 17 sections.","The federations in these 17 sections were allowed to compete like they used to.","The Major Federation Union only served to prevent the powerful federations from devouring the smaller ones and not maintain peace in the main world.","The Moon Empress did not announce her decision, so many federations were unaware of this.","With powerful federations holding down the fort in each section, the smaller federations could establish collaborations with them and receive their protection, thereby continuing their development.","If there were many small federations clustered together in a section, they would eventually fight with each other until only the two or three strongest ones emerged victorious.","...","Wen Yu only found out a few days later that Peace had sought out Lin Yuan and that he had pointed her in the right direction.","It was likely that Lin Yuan would completely give up on Peace going forward.","They were all members of the Astronomical Parliament. As long as Peace was not requesting an unreasonable amount of resources from Lin Yuan, he would likely grant her request!","But once Lin Yuan went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Peace would lose this source of support.","The Green Continent Federation that Peace presided over would soon be destroyed.","After all, the Green Continent Federation’s population was far too small and could not be seen as a complete federation. This was especially so because Peace did not possess overwhelming power.","Just as Wen Yu was about to report the information about the various dimensional worlds she had obtained from the Samsara Realm Dictators, Spring and Summer’s eyes narrowed, and they immediately appeared next to Lin Yuan.","Spring and Summer bowed to Lin Yuan before Summer said, “Lord Saint, I sense that this Class 2 world’s wills are being suppressed. The people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds are almost here!","“Don’t worry. Summer and I will protect the Radiance Federation while Autumn and Winter capture them! Given Autumn and Winter’s strength, no harm will be done to this world!”"]},{"number":2761,"title":"Chapter 2761 Uniqueness of the Body of All Spirits!","paragraphs":["2761 Uniqueness of the Body of All Spirits!","When Summer was done speaking, she looked nervously at Lin Yuan.","Her actions could be considered her giving advice to Lin Yuan.","This suggestion sounded good to Summer, but Lin Yuan might not think so. If her suggestion enraged Lin Yuan and earned his ire, Summer would have to suffer the repercussions!","A look of agreement appeared on Spring’s face when she heard what Summer said.","It could be said that Summer had echoed her thoughts exactly.","However, Spring and Summer had different personalities and did not offer suggestions to Lin Yuan like Summer had done.","Lin Yuan began thinking deeply after hearing what Summer said.","It was true that Lin Yuan had intended to remain in seclusion in the main world for some time to increase his and his companions’ strength before heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds to begin a new chapter of his life.","But after his trip to Epoch God Palace, Lin Yuan had emerged from the Returning Saint Pool as a birth-horoscope expert. His strength was now top class in the main world.","It would take a very long time for Liu Jie and Wen Yu to increase their strength.","The Moon Empress was about to set her spirit fire alight.","After setting her spirit fire alight, it would be very difficult for her to become a divine-kingdom expert because of the limits of this Class 2 world’s will. But once she left the Class 2 world and went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, her grade would no longer be restricted by these limits and would truly be able to increase her power endlessly!","It was true that it would be better for him and the Moon Empress to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds than remain in this Class 2 world.","It would not make a difference where Wen Yu, Liu Jie, and the rest increased their strength as he was the one supplying them with their resources.","But now, the Radiance Federation and main world had reached a key stage of development. There were numerous issues that were only just beginning their preparation.","Given Lin Yuan’s understanding of the Moon Empress, she would never head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds at such a juncture. So neither would he!","Lin Yuan could give out spirit qi crystals and heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls at will in the main world to increase the main world’s experts’ strength.","But he could not do that in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. He would have to keep to himself and protect his assets. Otherwise, it would not be long before news of his sea of resources spread like wildfire.","Even with Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter protecting him, being too ostentatious would not benefit his future development.","Hence, regardless of which factors he took into consideration, Lin Yuan would have to remain in the main world for some time.","“Summer, your suggestion is very good. However, I have my own considerations. If we capture all the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds who are targeting the main world’s experts, will it attract more spies to the main world?”","Summer nodded.","“Lord Saint, things will definitely play out as you expect. If many experts are detained in this Class 2 world, Honor Absent Palace will only have two options. They can either pull out and stop concerning themselves with this Class 2 world or send stronger people to spy on this Class 2 world.","“What would you do if you were in charge of Honor Absent Palace? After this wave is over, it’s likely there will be a second wave of visitors from Sky Beyond the Clouds. If you want to change this, you can pick one of us to send to deliberate with the Sky Beyond the Clouds and Honor Absent Palace.","“Alternatively, you can take control of this first wave of visitors from the Sky Beyond the Clouds and use them to send a message to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. With such a message, the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds will no longer pay attention to this Class 2 world!","“But it goes without saying this will mean you will no longer be able to continue evolving your feys in this Class 2 world. Otherwise, it will definitely continue attracting attention from the Sky Beyond the Clouds!”","When Lin Yuan heard that, he had a general outline of understanding.","It seemed that his thinking had been overly simple in the past.","The arrival of the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds was only just the beginning. However, there were ways to make changes to the matter while it was progressing.","Summer had given two options. Lin Yuan was leaning toward the second option rather than the first one.","Lin Yuan did not know exactly how strong the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds were. He could not send Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter to head there on their own.","It would be much better to first take control of this batch of experts!","While Lin Yuan was thinking, Spring said, “Lord Saint, now that you’ve enlightened your birth horoscope with the Returning Saint Pool and activated your body composition, your body composition will improve as your power grows!","“You should have been using your body composition to evolve feys. In a way, you can also be seen as a fey. Your body composition can also help humans to improve rapidly without leading to any negative effects!","“All you need to do is give it a try, and you’ll see that I’m telling the truth. Your body composition can also combine the bloodlines of many species and nurture them. All you need to do is test out these traits that I just spoke of!”","Back when Lin Yuan had only just confirmed his identity as the Saint, Spring would have never dared to say such things to Lin Yuan.","But now that Lin Yuan had enlightened his birth horoscope in the Returning Saint Pool and had made it clear that he did not want to regain his past memories as the Saint, he was in a newly awakened state and it was acceptable for Spring to say such things to him!","Spring could tell from Lin Yuan’s actions and manner he was anxious to raise his companions’ strength.","There was a definite difference between human and regular feys. Spirit qi had a much more obvious effect on feys than on humans.","Rather than wasting these resources, it would be better for Lin Yuan to use his body composition to speed up the increase of his companions’ strength.","Spring felt that if she did not elucidate this clearly and allowed Lin Yuan to learn and experience it all on his own, he might not fully experience the extent of his body composition even by the time he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan looked surprised when he heard what Spring said, and a radiant smile appeared on his face.","Lin Yuan could not be happier.","If what Spring said was right and he could use his body composition to speed up his companions’ increase in power, Lin Yuan would not have to worry about increasing Liu Jie, Wen Yu, Chu Ci, and the rest’s strength!","If he continuously increased their strength, they might even be able to surpass him!","Given their current power, if they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan would have no choice but to keep them in the Spirit Lock spatial zone. They would not be able to roam around outside on their own. Any native expert would be able to compromise their safety!","Lin Yuan intended to find the time to test out the extent to which his body composition could speed up a spirit qi professional’s increase in power.","Once he was done with his tests, he would systematically increase his acknowledged companions’ strength.","Ever since Liu Jie returned to the Radiance Federation, he had been in seclusion so the Insect Queen could take control of new insect-species carcinoma feys.","Ever since Elegance evolved to Suzerain/Myth, its spiritual energy had been steadily growing stronger. It could now take control of many more feys than it originally could.","Wen Yu had just returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion after using the Elemental Paper’s Hear Heaven’s Secrets to organize information.","Upon seeing Wen Yu, Lin Yuan inquired, “Wen Yu, considering your current rank as a spirit qi professional, how long do you think it’ll take for you to achieve S-rank status?”","Wen Yu found herself momentarily uncertain about how to respond to Lin Yuan’s question.","Having recently attained the status of an A-rank spirit qi professional, Wen Yu attributed her swift progress partly to Mystic Moon’s Dragon Pearl Embryo. Additionally, Lin Yuan’s consistent supply of rainbow fish coats for her consumption played a significant role.","Without these contributions, Wen Yu acknowledged that reaching even B-rank status would be considered fortunate at this point.","Wen Yu was well aware of her talent and potential.","There was an enormous gap between an A- and S-rank spirit qi professional. This was why so many people were stuck at emperor-class and were unable to evolve to thearch-class despite the large amount of resources that Lin Yuan was pouring into the main world’s experts.","Wen Yu had used up almost all of the energy in the Dragon Pearl Embryo. She could no longer use it to quickly increase her rank.","When she first started using the rainbow fish coats, the effects had been astounding. But after using them for a prolonged period, the effects would decrease precipitously.","With the help from the rainbow fish coats and her talent, Wen Yu believed that it would be impossible for her to become an S-rank spirit qi professional in the next 20 years.","From Lin Yuan’s words, Wen Yu could sense that he had high hopes for her increase in rank.","As such, Wen Yu was at a loss about how to respond to Lin Yuan.","Was she really going to say that she would only be able to become an S-rank spirit qi professional when she was 40 or 50 years old?","Liu Jie had more talent than her. It should only take him around 15 years to become an S-rank spirit qi professional.","When Lin Yuan saw Wen Yu’s expression, he realized she had misunderstood him.","He smiled and reached out his hand to her. “Wen Yu, give me your hand.”","Wen Yu was stunned and confused about what Lin Yuan’s intentions were.","But she was well aware that Lin Yuan only saw her as a good friend, and there were no romantic feelings between them to speak of.","As Wen Yu matured, she was also able to control her emotions better.","It was true that it would be best for her and Lin Yuan to maintain their state of friendship. This was the most sustainable relationship that could exist between them.","Wen Yu smiled and placed her hand on Lin Yuan’s.","At that moment, Wen Yu felt an energy flow from Lin Yuan’s palm into her body. The energy was warm. Once it entered her body, she felt her body greedily absorbing the energy.","The energy in her body was being strengthened at a visible rate!","Wen Yu gaped at Lin Yuan in shock.","Lin Yuan did not answer Wen Yu’s question but asked her again, “Wen Yu, given the rate at which your power is rising, how long will it take for you to become an S-rank spirit qi professional?”","Wen Yu earnestly sensed the changes in her body before squeaking out in shock,","“Young... Young Master, given the current rate of power increase, I should be able to condense a spirit qi vortex in a day and a half and become a fully-fledged S-rank spirit qi professional!”","Spirit qi professionals condensed spirit qi vortexes to protect themselves. It was a symbolic ability of S-rank spirit qi professionals.","Even with Wen Yu’s intelligence, it took a while for her to recover from her shock.","Lin Yuan’s actions went beyond Wen Yu’s comprehension.","Lin Yuan smiled brightly. “Since that is the case, I’ll help you to raise your rank first so you can become an S-rank spirit qi professional. If you feel any discomfort during the process, I will immediately stop helping you to increase your power. Safety is more important than anything!”","This was the first time that Lin Yuan was using his body composition to increase the power of a human. Although Spring was the one who informed him of this ability, he still needed to test it out for himself.","Lin Yuan was delighted. If he could promote an A-rank spirit qi professional to S-rank in a day and a half, it would not take long for him to increase his companions’ strength!","Once one became an S-rank spirit qi professional, one’s feys’ grades would no longer be restricted. At that point, one would truly be free and have boundless possibilities!","This would give Lin Yuan a reason to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds as soon as possible.","If he could help increase the Moon Empress’ power, she would be able to devote all her time to managing the Radiance Federation and governing the main world.","In just a few years, with the main world’s system working at full capacity, every facet of the main world would be overhauled!","It was rather strange to continue clutching Wen Yu’s hand to increase her power. He only asked Wen Yu to give him her hand because he wanted to test his abilities.","Lin Yuan told Wen Yu to sit on a bench while he sat opposite her and placed his hand on the back of her hand.","Normally, Lin Yuan would not call on Liu Jie while he was in seclusion.","But after spending a day and a half strengthening Wen Yu, he asked her to call Liu Jie.","When Liu Jie saw Wen Yu calling him while he was in seclusion, his chest tightened.","He and Wen Yu mostly communicated through the Thoughts Letter Paper. As such, there was no longer a need to communicate through phone calls.","Wen Yu was calling him despite knowing that he was in seclusion. Could something have happened?","Liu Jie hurriedly asked, “Wen Yu, did Lin Yuan—”","Before Liu Jie could finish speaking, Wen Yu cut him off with a laugh.","Liu Jie was shocked.","He knew that Wen Yu would never joke with him when it came to such matters. This meant that she had truly become an S-rank spirit qi professional.","Just like Wen Yu was aware of Liu Jie’s talent, the latter understood Wen Yu’s talent.","Wen Yu was able to become an A-rank spirit qi professional before him because she used the Dragon Pearl Embryo.","However, the energy in the Dragon Pearl Embryo had been used up. How did Wen Yu accomplish something that should have taken her more than 20 years within only a few days? Could she have encountered a massive opportunity?"]},{"number":2762,"title":"Chapter 2762 Genius From the Past!","paragraphs":["2762 Genius From the Past!","Liu Jie was delighted after making this guess.","There was no longer any unfamiliarity or need to stand on ceremony when it came to Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, and Wen Yu. They were the closest of companions.","In the past, Liu Jie only saw himself as Lin Yuan’s retainer. But as he spent more time by Lin Yuan’s side, his thoughts changed continuously.","Liu Jie now saw himself not just as Lin Yuan’s retainer but also as his companion.","There were only certain circumstances that would cause Liu Jie to change his perspective. For example, if Lin Yuan was in danger, Liu Jie would still use his body to defend Lin Yuan against deadly attacks like he had done in the past.","True friends would not be jealous of each other. It was true that Liu Jie was envious of Wen Yu, but this did not stop him from genuinely being happy for her.","“Congratulations Wen Yu! If you become an S-rank spirit qi professional, it will probably take at least a few decades before I manage to catch up with you!”","When Wen Yu heard this, she knew that Liu Jie had not grasped her meaning.","How could she have the capabilities to increase her spirit qi professional rank so abruptly?","Aside from a small part that came from Mystic Moon, most of what Wen Yu had now came from Lin Yuan.","“Big Brother Liu, how long will you be in seclusion this time? If you aren’t in too much of a hurry, my advice is that you head home. Young Master is the one who increased my grade in a little over a day. When you return, he will do the same for you!”","A look of shock crossed Liu Jie’s face before his breath turned ragged.","He was one of the three founders of Sky City and knew that he was the least useful of the three of them. Lin Yuan could easily swap him out for a subordinate such as Listen and Bai Qinghuan.","In terms of intelligence and strategy, he could not match up to Wen Yu. His martial force was where he had the most improvement. However, not only was he unable to defeat Lin Yuan, but it was also a struggle for him to distinguish himself among Sky City’s experts. Hence, it was difficult for Liu Jie to gain any confidence.","When they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would surely become a burden to Lin Yuan.","Liu Jie was putting all his effort into increasing his power, but this was not an easy endeavor.","Liu Jie could no longer deny his potential. If his spirit qi professional rank could be raised, there would be specific environments where even Lin Yuan would be no match for him.","If Lin Yuan could help Wen Yu increase her power within a day or so, he would definitely be able to help Liu Jie as well.","He had been occupied with being in seclusion and contracting carcinoma feys in the Spirit Guards’ land. However, all of these would be placed below raising his spirit qi professional rank.","Once his spirit qi professional rank was raised to S-rank, Elegance’s grade and quality could be evolved. At that point, he would no longer have to be selective about the insect-species carcinoma feys he contracted and could contract any one of them stored in the Spirit Guards’ land!","“Wen Yu, I’ll come back now. Lin Yuan should not be leaving anytime soon, right?”","Liu Jie’s tone contained anticipation, joy, and hope.","In truth, Liu Jie, Wen Yu, and Lin Yuan had not lived together for a long time. All three of them were busy with their own tasks.","The three of them all had their own tasks to attend to.","With an enemy such as Tower Canon looming over them, they had been leading each day nervously and feeling as though they were tiptoeing on the edge of a knife.","But now that the dead spirits crisis had come to an end and they had defeated Tower Canon, Epoch God Palace was not on hostile terms with Lin Yuan and was even on extremely friendly terms with him.","Given the circumstances, Liu Jie really hoped that he could enjoy simple days with Lin Yuan and Wen Yu in the main world before they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Although power was important to Liu Jie, he also believed that living was the key part of life.","Liu Jie especially missed the feeling of living with his friends and family.","...","Hope also bloomed in Wen Yu’s eyes when she heard what Liu Jie said.","Wen Yu turned to look at Lin Yuan. She knew that his spiritual energy was currently strong enough to hear the contents of her conversation with Liu Jie.","When Lin Yuan saw the hope in Wen Yu’s eyes, he smiled and nodded.","Recently, aside from occasionally collecting spirit qi crystals, Lin Yuan spent most of his time in the Radiance Federation. If he had any tasks that he needed done, he could send out orders. There was no need for him to handle matters on his own.","Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter would handle the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan intended to enjoy life in the Radiance Federation for some time. He would sear memories of his time in the main world into his brain before he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan had not felt much reluctance when he left the Xia Region for the Royal Capital. Instead, all he felt was excitement and hopefulness.","But now that he was about to leave for the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan felt reluctant to depart from the main world.","This thought brought a smile to Lin Yuan’s face.","Since he felt reluctant, he would use the best of his abilities to enable the main world to develop!","When Lin Yuan nodded, Wen Yu smiled radiantly, resembling a blooming crabapple.","“Big Brother Liu, Young Master will be remaining at home for some time. I’m not sure exactly how long he’ll be staying. But don’t forget to buy more ingredients before you return. Young Master and I haven’t had your cooking in a very long time!”","Even if Wen Yu did not give him the reminder, Liu Jie had already planned on buying more ingredients to cook for Wen Yu and Liu Jie.","Suddenly, a thought struck Liu Jie, and he asked, “Is the Mother of Bloodbath at home?”","Wen Yu checked the time before answering, “Sister Love is currently with the team from the Heavenly Family Cottage. They are tending to and settling the various fey species. She will only be able to return six months later at the earliest. So you only have to prepare food for the few of us! I will fetch Little Flower and Little Grass home tomorrow.”","During the next month, Listen, Qin Yu, and the rest would slowly make their way back to the Return from Faraway Mansion.","Since the Mother of Bloodbath was not at home, Liu Jie did not have to worry about the quantity of food he made.","Although Wen Yu also had a large appetite, her appetite was nothing compared to that of the Mother of Bloodbath.","Since Lin Yuan intended on remaining in the Return from Faraway Mansion to rest for some time, Wen Yu also needed to make her own preparations.","After ending the call, Wen Yu poured out a cup of Three Treasures Tea for Lin Yuan and said, “Young Master, Big Brother Liu cares more about increasing his power than I do. He almost exploded with happiness when he found out he could speed up his spirit qi professional rank promotion!”","Lin Yuan knew that Liu Jie was competitive and ambitious. This was especially so after he became certain of his talent. Since then, his desire to increase his power became even stronger than before.","It would take some time for Lin Yuan to use his body composition to evolve feys’ grades.","Lin Yuan was in no rush to help Wen Yu to evolve her feys’ grades. Instead, he gave her a chest filled with spirit qi crystals that she could use for her daily needs.","Rather than using his body composition to evolve Wen Yu’s feys’ grades and qualities, Lin Yuan preferred to help spirit qi professionals to raise their grades.","Lin Yuan was not satisfied with just helping Wen Yu, Liu Jie, and the rest to become S-rank spirit qi professionals. He was going to help them become birth-horoscope experts at the very least.","Wen Yu, Liu Jie, and the rest could evolve their feys’ grades quickly using spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan already had a general plan in mind.","After Lin Yuan returned to the Radiance Federation, he should head to the Radiant Moon Palace first to spend time with the Moon Empress.","But the Moon Empress had gone to the Startling Lines Continent to participate in the first Major Federation Union meeting since the dead spirits crisis had come to an end. She would only be returning two weeks later at the earliest.","Lin Yuan needed to stay in the Return from Faraway Mansion for another two weeks before he could head to the Radiant Moon Palace.","Autumn was currently above the Startling Lines Continent to protect it.","Everyone had selfishness within them.","In order to protect the main world, Lin Yuan would concentrate most of the defensive forces in the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent.","Wen Yu did not bother with courtesies when it came to resources provided by Lin Yuan. She knew she needed to utilize these resources in order to improve her management and building of Sky City.","...","While sitting on the sofa, Lin Yuan stretched out just in time to see Liu Jie striding into the mansion.","Since Liu Jie had also contracted the Lifespan Mouse, his lifespan would not shorten, and his looks would be frozen in their current state.","Hence, even if they were apart for a long time, Liu Jie did not look any different to Lin Yuan.","Liu Jie was always very restrained when it came to his emotions.","Yet, now that he was reuniting with Lin Yuan after such a long time apart, he could not stop himself from giving Lin Yuan a hug.","A hug between brothers needed to be as passionate as possible.","Liu Jie realized that Lin Yuan had grown much taller since they last met. They were almost the same height now.","In terms of looks, he could not even begin to compare himself to Lin Yuan. He would never be able to match up to him!","When they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan would attract attention everywhere he went!","Spring remained by Lin Yuan’s side.","When Lin Yuan and his friends were enjoying and sharing warm moments, Spring and Summer hid their physical selves and auras.","Spring’s body composition allowed her to control all that had just emerged and sprouted. This included new ideas.","After sensing Liu Jie’s thoughts, Spring could not help but nod.","Lin Yuan’s Body of All Spirits would indeed cause him to become the center of attention in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","But this would not just be because of his looks.","The lifeforms in the Sky Beyond the Clouds were very practical. There were many species that could alter their looks after increasing their power. Hence, appearances were no longer something that was permanent.","Even if one’s true looks left a lot to be desired, they could use special lifeforms and spiritual ingredients to change their looks into a perfect facade.","At the Sky Beyond the Clouds, the definition of beauty was determined by one’s bloodline aura. Bloodline aura was even above wealth.","Lin Yuan’s Body of All Spirits could temper any bloodline and apply the bloodline to his own body. As such, there was no lifeform in the Sky Beyond the Clouds that could be compared with Lin Yuan.","However, with Lin Yuan’s elite status as the Saint, he would never compete with other entities in the Sky Beyond the Clouds in terms of attractiveness.","A group of lifeforms from the Sky Beyond the Clouds would receive an unprecedented transformation, which would be enough to alter the future development of their species.","This transformation would come from them joining Lin Yuan.","Spring and Summer felt Wen Yu and Liu Jie were extremely lucky. They were Lin Yuan’s subordinates, yet he saw them as friends. Because of Lin Yuan’s attitude, even Spring and Summer were extremely respectful toward them. After all, followers were beneath friends.","“Lin Yuan, I will go and cook now. It will just be the three of us, so I won’t cook too much. But I promise that I will make your favorites!”","If Wen Yu was the Return from Faraway Mansion’s steward, Liu Jie was the chef.","Not only did Liu Jie have great skills as a chef, but he also remembered the individual tastes of every person.","Lin Yuan and Wen Yu liked to eat meat. They especially liked the meat of the Black Back Mountain Boar but were also fine with beef and lamb. However, Lin Yuan did not like eating fish. Chu Ci shared Wen Yu’s tastes and liked eating tender fish.","Hence, when Liu Jie cooked, he needed to cater to not only Lin Yuan’s taste but also Wen Yu’s taste.","...","Chu Ci was previously in seclusion in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","After Lin Yuan returned to the Radiance Federation, Chu Ci went to see Cold Moon and Cold Moon took her to the Startling Lines Continent to train.","Lin Yuan did not have any objections to this. Cold Moon was Chu Ci’s master and could take charge of molding her. Cold Moon was also capable of protecting Chu Ci.","After Mystic Moon, Cold Moon managed to break through her power as well and was now an Above Eternal expert.","Otherwise, there would be four of them having dinner together in the Radiance Federation today!","Liu Jie did not need Wen Yu and Lin Yuan’s help when it came to cooking.","...","Lin Yuan sat on the sofa and took out all the information that Wen Yu had organized. The mansion’s hall soon filled up with paper.","When Wen Yu saw this, she scratched her head and said, “Young Master, this is only around 1/7 of the total amount of information. I was going to summarize this information after organizing it, but there was no way to do so. Once you’re done reading through this information, you should be able to gain a detailed understanding of the recent happenings in the main world!”","Although Wen Yu could use the Elemental Paper’s exclusive skill to gather information, Lin Yuan could tell from the sheer volume of information she had worked hard to gather.","There was no way that Lin Yuan could read all this information page by page. There were far too many events happening in the main world each day. If Lin Yuan used his eyes to read this information, it would take him around three years to finish. If Wen Yu continued organizing information in these three years, the amount of information would pile up even higher!","Lin Yuan summoned Genius.","After being summoned, Genius was about to cling to Lin Yuan when it suddenly wiggled its nose and meowed in a child-like tone.","“Yuan, I smell red braised meat! I haven’t eaten red braised meat in a very long time! Please include some red braised meat in my meal later!”","Genius appeared akin to a creature sprung from the realms of imagination and fantasy. Its tail billowed and flowed, its form exuding an elusive and celestial air.","However, when it communicated, Lin Yuan observed a Genius adorned with matted fur, possessing a penchant for devouring red-braised meat. Curiously, it consistently recoiled and never dared to consume any when Lin Yuan presented the dish before it!"]},{"number":2763,"title":"Chapter 2763 Return of Ownership of the Deep Harbor!","paragraphs":["2763 Return of Ownership of the Deep Harbor!","Back then, Genius had the intelligence of a child that was around 14 to 15 years old.","At the time, Lin Yuan was responsible for bringing up Chu Ci.","Sending Chu Ci to school and nurturing her feys did not come at a small cost.","The Lin Yuan of then had been riddled with illnesses. He had neither awakened Morbius nor discovered that he had a unique physique. He could only trim the fat when it came to his clothing, food, and comforts of living.","It was usually Auntie Zhang who brought over red braised meat when she came to visit Lin Yuan.","Recently, Genius had been remaining in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, and its diet consisted of the Soldier Ration Radish.","If Genius did not mention it again today, Lin Yuan might have forgotten that it was a glutton in its own right. They shared the same tastes in food as well!","Lin Yuan reached out and patted Genius’ small head.","Genius closed its eyes as it enjoyed the experience of being showered in Lin Yuan’s affection. It turned its head and gently nudged Lin Yuan’s hand before quickly lifting its head to signal that it wanted its chin scratched.","When Wen Yu saw this, she could not help but run her hand down Genius’ back.","Genius was very close with Wen Yu. In truth, Genius had spent even more time with Wen Yu than it did with Chu Ci. Hence, they had a deeper relationship.","“Genius, not only will Young Master prepare a meal for you, but so will I! Besides red braised meat, you will also love the ribs and spicy chicken! I’ll also spoon out a bowl of fish chowder for you.”","When Genius heard that, it left Lin Yuan’s embrace and snuggled into Wen Yu’s arms before the two of them began playing.","For the first time in a long while, Lin Yuan felt the rowdy joy that came with having his feys by his side.","Lin Yuan lifted his hand and summoned Chimey.","After being summoned, Chimey spotted Genius playing with Wen Yu and hurriedly landed on Lin Yuan’s shoulder. Its small head nudged Lin Yuan’s face before it let out a few pleasant chirps.","Chimey was uninterested in the smell of red braised meat that was drifting through the air.","Lin Yuan smiled and said, “Chimey, since you see the past as miserable and your present as happy, I will get some Normal Usnea for you so you can reminisce the taste!”","Sunlight streamed through the windows into the Return from Faraway Mansion, temporarily keeping the space basked in light.","Aside from the fact that the feys in the mansion had all evolved their grades, this scene was no different from a few years ago. The Five Fortune Ranchu Spirit-Siphon Goldfish in the sandalwood longevity fish tank were the best witnesses to this.","Genius circulated its spiritual energy, and the first pile of information began flying around in an orderly manner.","In less than ten minutes, the rain of paper in the room stopped.","After organizing the information, one of the cat tails turned into a strip of light and linked Genius to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan received all the information that Genius had organized. Lin Yuan immediately gained an understanding of the situation in various areas of the main world.","This was not the first time that Wen Yu was seeing Genius use Connected Tails. Genius had also used Connected Tails to transfer most of Wen Yu’s perspectives and knowledge to her.","It could be said that Wen Yu had around the same amount of knowledge as Lin Yuan.","But it went without saying that Lin Yuan had more knowledge than Wen Yu. This was because his knowledge included his own secrets and secret weapons.","Once Genius was done looking through all the information that was present, Wen Yu immediately took out a new set, and Genius repeated its previous actions.","It would take at least two hours for Liu Jie to finish cooking. There were many dishes that needed to be stewed for some time in order to maximize their flavor.","In the time that Liu Jie spent cooking, Lin Yuan finished going through all the information on the events that had taken place in the main world in the past three years!","This included the information on the Green Continent Federation.","Lin Yuan told Wen Yu seriously, “The Startling Lines Continent’s current position is extremely important. It has become the hub of the entire main world. It is also the gateway to the Radiance Federation.”","Wen Yu nodded seriously.","She had been wanting to bring up this matter to Lin Yuan. This was the most important matter at hand.","Due to the rise in importance in the Startling Lines Continent’s position, the harbor Lin Yuan had built outside of the Great Lush Federation became even more critical.","This was especially so because the entire main world was about to begin sea trading.","The harbor had become the best channel for other federations to interact with the Startling Lines Continent.","Lin Yuan had provided all the resources for the construction of the harbor. The Great Lush Federation was only managing it.","However, Jin Qianxun had set his sights on the harbor and had been using it to gain personal benefits.","This matter displeased Luo Lan and Yi Huailong greatly, and they had sought out Wen Yu multiple times.","Yi Huailong had been performing well. After he became the ruler of the Divine Wood Federation, he did his best to develop it.","Yi Huailu had been helping Sky City to concoct potions and could be considered one of its more central members.","As a member of the Astronomical Parliament, Luo Lan was closer to Wen Yu.","Wen Yu had not made her decision immediately after hearing Luo Lan and Yi Huailong’s opinions. Even if Lin Yuan had not brought this matter up, Wen Yu was already intending to ask him about it after this meal.","There was no way that the Great Lush Federation could be allowed to have sole ownership of the harbor.","Lin Yuan had invested more resources into the harbor than the entire Great Lush Federation.","If the Great Lush Federation was allowed to take sole control of the harbor and obtained three years’ worth of profits from the harbor, the Great Lush Federation’s position in the main world and foundational resources would be above that of the Divine Wood and Iron Hammer Federations.","If the three federations were going to develop simultaneously in the Startling Lines Continent, they had to stand on equal footing. Once the balance was disrupted, the Startling Lines Continent’s current structure would be affected. Lin Yuan would not permit such destabilizing factors to appear in the Startling Lines Continent.","Since such thoughts had formed in Jin Qianxun’s mind, it meant that his dishonesty needed to be reined in.","“Wen Yu, when you give out instructions for this matter, inform Jin Qianxun personally. Tell Jin Qianxun about the reasons and repercussions. Then, tell Jin Qianxun to provide me with an explanation. If something similar happens again in the future, you can select a suitable secret aristocratic family from the Great Lush Federation to replace Jin Qianxun.”","When Wen Yu heard that, she knew that Lin Yuan was seething.","He had already given the Great Lush Federation the best space to develop. Yet, Jin Qianxun had not been satisfied.","Although he would not punish the entire Great Lush Federation, he would definitely penalize Jin Qianxun.","They could only hope that Jin Qianxun could learn his lesson and stop foolishly trying to claim profits that did not belong to him!","“Young Master, I’ll arrange everything after dinner. Apart from that, I’d like to seek your opinion on another matter. Once Chef Supreme fulfills the Radiance Federation’s requirements and distributes the Soldier Ration Radishes, coupled with your supply, other federations won’t have to worry about food shortages. Their only obligation would be to provide resources in exchange for the Soldier Ration Radishes.","However, some federations haven’t engaged in this trade, and the Green Continent Federation is one of them. They are also grappling with food scarcity. Do you think it’s advisable to dispatch a portion of Soldier Ration Radishes to assist them?”","Lin Yuan had just replied to Peace through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","He knew that Peace would encounter significant issues after changing Green Continent City to Green Continent Federation. But he had not expected the problem to be so serious. The citizens could not even keep their stomachs full!","Lin Yuan was always aware that the environment in the Broiling Rock Continent was harsh.","Peace was a native of the Broiling Rock Continent and had never received any education. She survived on her own abilities.","It was true that Peace had changed the name of Green Continent City to Green Continent Federation because she wanted to become a member of the elite. But she also hoped to use her own strength to protect the citizens of the Green Continent Federation. Her desire to do so only grew stronger after seeing how powerful the other federations were.","Although Peace would not be going with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan would still step in to help if he knew that she was encountering issues. After all, the citizens of the Green Continent Federation were innocent.","“Wen Yu, send these two Soldier Ration Radishes over. Also, send an experienced teacher to teach Peace the ways of the world, as well as the knowledge that a leader needs to have!","“Have a chat with Peace again three years later to see if her thoughts have changed. If she is still focused on being the Green Continent Federation’s leader, then she shall compete fairly with the other federations.”","Wen Yu pursed her lips. She knew that Lin Yuan was being very generous with Lin Yuan. This was how he was with everyone.","Since Lin Yuan hadn’t provided an alternative, it implied his awareness that, despite three years of education, Peace would persist in making such decisions, transforming from an uninformed ruler into one possessing knowledge.","Currently basking in the bliss of ignorance, Peace would soon confront the harsh realities of the main world, realizing its complexity far exceeded her initial perceptions.","Within the Green Continent Federation, not a single proficient Creation Master existed. The once esteemed Rain Masters had lost their relevance in the face of water abundance yet retained their high-status positions. This stark reality exposed the superficiality of Peace’s governance.","Su Yiren and Luo Lan had received special nurturing and education from a young age.","Su Yiren was able to manage the Dark and Sand Island Continents because she had outstanding intelligence and enviable talent.","Luo Lan had more talent than the average person and was more excellent than her peers. But she still ran up against obstacles and felt trapped often.","Wen Yu did not have any wicked intentions toward Peace. She only found it a pity when she thought of all the effort Lin Yuan had put into nurturing her.","If the resources that Lin Yuan had spent on Peace had gone to others instead, he would definitely have been able to produce a splendid subordinate.","Lin Yuan could nurture Peace thanks to the support of the Astronomical Parliament. Whenever Lin Yuan depleted his resources, Wen Yu played a crucial role. The thought of the laws Lin Yuan had utilized to secure resources for Peace evoked a pang in Wen Yu’s chest.","Once Lin Yuan completed his preparations and issued instructions, Liu Jie emerged from the kitchen carrying a variety of dishes.","Lin Yuan and Wen Yu hurriedly moved to help him, but he waved them away.","“I am all done. All you need to do is eat! I have never been very good with plating. I secretly learned a few of Zong Ze’s plating skills from him when we last tested our skills against each other. I still need to add a few things after the dishes are served!”","Lin Yuan and Wen Yu looked at each other. Since Liu Jie had already spoken, the two of them dutifully sat at the table and watched as Liu Jie brought out dish after dish.","It was true that Liu Jie’s plating skills used to be weak. His dishes looked homely and rustic, and their appeal came from smell and taste.","But now, every one of his dishes looked intricate. They looked so exquisite that Lin Yuan and Wen Yu could not bear to touch them with their chopsticks!","Aside from plating, Liu Jie had another reason for not wanting Lin Yuan and Wen Yu’s help.","Whenever Wen Yu had a meal, she would always fill up her bowl to prevent herself from having to refill her bowl.","The rice that had just been cooked was fluffy and had the best texture. Compressing it in the bowl would affect their taste and the taste of the meal.","With this thought, Liu Jie decided to carefully fill up Wen Yu’s bowl for her.","...","Fan Lou had been walking on eggshells recently as he remained by Kong Huan’s side.","He had come into contact with more bigshots recently than he had over the course of the first half of his life.","Moreover, these bigshots were all unimaginably esteemed. There were even some to whom Kong Huan had to be polite.","Honor Absent Palace was a faction composed of experts of different species. If there was any activity, the powerful species would quickly catch wind of the news.","This matter would undoubtedly lead to enormous repercussions.","The appearance of a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform went against all that was known. This was not to say that something like this had never happened, but whenever it did happen, it indicated that a valuable treasure had emerged.","Aside from feeling nervous and anxious about having to watch his every word in his replies to the bigshots, Fan Lou also felt as though he was holding a secret and was the only one in the know while everyone else was blinded.","Fan Lou had not told anyone besides Kong Huan that an intermediate faerie had appeared in this Class 2 world. All the members of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team who knew of the matter had been secretly dealt with by Kong Huan.","Kong Huan was always merciless when profits were at stake.","Fan Lou was not worried about being under Kong Huan’s thumb because she still needed his help to collect resources from that Class 2 world!"]},{"number":2764,"title":"Chapter 2764 Chaos Wind Demon Wolf!","paragraphs":["2764 Chaos Wind Demon Wolf!","Once the matter was settled, things would have reached a checkpoint.","As long as Kong Huan received resources she was satisfied with, she would have no reason to make use of this subordinate with whom she was in the same boat.","Fan Lou had thought things through well. He had even set up schemes and plans for himself.","Unfortunately, things would never progress the way that wicked people like himself planned.","On the day before they left, Fan Lou was preparing all the resources they needed to bring with them.","As the guide to this Class 2 world, Fan Lou would need to prepare more resources so he could use them to make connections with the bigshots at important moments. Even if he could not make connections with them, he could at least leave a good impression on them. It was possible that a bigshot would be willing to give him a chance and open up a new path for him!","Before Fan Lou could finish organizing the resources, he noticed that Kong Huan had come to his residence.","As the Boundary Patrol Envoy who led the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team, Fan Lou had his own private residence in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. He was the master of his residence, and everyone else was his servants.","Given Kong Huan’s identity and status, she should not come to his residence.","If there were truly any issues, Kong Huan only needed to send out an order, and he would go meet with him.","Her sudden appearance there had to mean that something urgent had happened.","Fan Lou understood better than anyone else just how important Kong Huan’s image was to her. He was not the only Boundary Patrol Envoy who Kong Huan was supporting.","Previously, a Boundary Patrol Envoy had helped Kong Huan with a large favor and received a large reward from her.","Later, that Boundary Patrol Envoy became extremely arrogant. Despite continuing to serve Kong Huan, he no longer humbled himself to the extent that he used to.","This Boundary Patrol Envoy’s actions had enraged Kong Huan, and she immediately stopped supporting and nurturing him.","Moreover, when this Boundary Patrol Envoy took on private jobs, Kong Huan punished him and kicked him out of the East Universe.","The four universes were constantly competing with each other.","After being kicked out of the East Universe and having held an official position in the East Universe, the other universes would never take him in. He would be forced to roam around the abyss as a homeless nomad.","Fan Lou’s smooth development was partially credited to his abilities. But it was also because he was always acutely aware of his place.","Fan Lou knelt on one knee in front of Kong Huan and said humbly, “May I know why you have come to my place of residence? If you needed to speak with me, you could have sent someone to inform me, and I would have rushed to you!”","Fan Lou kept his head low while he spoke.","His demeanor pleased Kong Huan greatly.","It was true that Kong Huan had an urgent matter she needed to discuss with Fan Lou. Otherwise, she would never lower herself to the point of coming to his residence. If word of this matter got out, it would affect her reputation. She would never permit such a thing!","The various representatives from Honor Absent Parliament clashed against each other often. However, they were usually restrained to verbal blows and never reached the point of physical attacks. Once it reached the point of physical attacks, it would be a war between two powerful species","Moreover, the other members of the parliament would also do their best to stop conflict from breaking out.","This was unless the two sides truly reached an irreconcilable point.","Since they were unable to lay a hand on each other and the two sides possessed comparable power, reputation and might were the only weapons they could use against each other!","“Fan Lou, it goes without saying that I came here because I need to speak with you about something. Apart from me, there will definitely be other members of the parliament who will come to speak with you before we set off.","“You need to be clear about whose camp you’re a part of! I hate subordinates who are a slave to their desires and are always dissatisfied with their current position and trying to climb the ladder! You became the guide because I put a lot of effort into promoting you. As long as you do well, you won’t have to worry about living in comfort!","“You have yet to marry an official wife. I will arrange for a match between you and a female from my species. She will help you manage your affairs in your residence! You will also gain the right to participate in meetings held by my species!”","After hearing what Kong Huan said, the kneeling Fan Lou could not help but begin trembling.","Kong Huan had made such promises, to the extent of arranging for him to be married to a female from the Alluring Foxes. He would even gain the right to participate in the Alluring Foxes’ meetings. This was an enormous honor! He would also have the Alluring Foxes’ imprint applied on him, and everyone would be able to see that he was a relative of the Alluring Foxes.","In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, the stronger species held higher statuses.","Hence, the Sky Beyond the Clouds had a very different societal structure to the main world.","As the captain of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team, he had more than 100 unofficial concubines in his residence but had yet to marry an official wife. This was because he had been waiting for just such an opportunity. If he had already married an official wife, he would not be able to grab hold of the opportunity even if it arrived!","“Fan Lou thanks Lordess Kong Huan’s generosity! Don’t worry. You are the only one I’ll serve for the entirety of my life!”","Kong Huan nodded in satisfaction when she heard this and immediately left Fan Lou’s residence.","Fan Lou had been following her for a very long time and had always been extremely loyal. Hence, she was not as worried about him.","Firstly, people were generally aware that Fan Lou was part of her camp. It was unlikely that someone like Fan Lou, who already had a master, would be recruited by others.","Additionally, Fan Lou was relatively timid and would not trust the promises of others unless he knew them well, even if they were also the Honor Absent Parliament’s members.","The promises of others were unreliable. They could turn on their word at any time. As long as they eliminated Fan Lou in secret, no one would find out about their dealings.","The Alluring Foxes were an elite species, and Fan Lou did not deserve to be their relative.","Kong Huan had made Fan Lou such a promise because she also had no intentions of allowing Fan Lou to live.","After Fan Lou helped her to obtain resources from that Class 2 world, many members of parliament might set their sights on this Class 2 world. It would not be beneficial for her image for it to become known she had brazenly broken the rules.","Rather than nurturing someone like Fan Lou, Kong Huan decided to nurture more members of the Alluring Foxes.","Kong Huan had begun nurturing Fan Lou before joining the Honor Absent Parliament.","Now that she was a part of the Honor Absent Parliament and had attained some authority and power, she could begin claiming profits for the Alluring Foxes.","...","Fan Lou only stood up some time after Kong Huan had left.","He felt his heart racing and was full of hope for the future.","At first, Fan Lou had been holding onto some selfishness and wanted to make use of this trip to the Class 2 world to connect with some parliament members. But now, he felt that he only needed to dutifully remain by Kong Huan’s side and do her bidding.","...","Soon after Kong Huan left, Fan Lou received a message from his subordinate while he was in the middle of a meal.","A man wearing a blue fur cloak had come to Fan Lou’s residence. He had an impressive background and did not enter Fan Lou’s residence immediately. Instead, he informed Fan Lou’s subordinate at the entrance that he wanted Fan Lou to come to greet him personally.","The powerful species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds all had their own unique traits.","It was clear with one look that this man was a member of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf species.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had never even entered the top 1,000 ranks of the East Universe’s Species Ranking.","Nonetheless, he was still far from someone whom Fan Lou could afford to offend.","The ranking of the Species Ranking was not only determined by the power of the species’ experts but also by the size of the species.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolf was a branch of the Moon-Worshiping Wolf species and had a rather small population. Otherwise, the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves would definitely be able to enter the top few ranks of the Species Ranking!","When Fan Lou heard that a member of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves was there to see him, he immediately set down his utensils and went to receive this visitor with the utmost respect.","This man wearing a light blue fur cloak finally smiled when he saw Fan Lou’s respectful demeanor.","“Fan Lou, Feng Lin and I are old friends. He mentioned you to me in the past. I am here to see you because you are about to lead the team to that special Class 2 world. I will be going with you. The Lord of my family would like to meet with you before we set off. Do you have time?”","The gears in Fan Lou’s brain immediately started turning when this man from Chaos Wind Demon Wolves mentioned Feng Lin.","Feng Lin was also a captain of a Boundary Patrol Team. He became a relative of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves a few years ago. After doing so, he held a lavish banquet in his residence, which Fan Lou attended.","Fan Lou had not interacted with Feng Lin many times, but they had no hostility between them. As such, it was unlikely that Feng Lin would speak ill of him.","Although this expert from the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves said that he was here to extend an invitation, in actuality, there was no way he could reject it. If he did not agree, the matter would definitely be reported to higher authorities.","“How should I address you? How could I not accept an invitation from Lord Feng Qing?”","With Fan Lou’s agreement, this man from Chaos Wind Demon Wolves said, “Since it is convenient for you, why don’t you come with me now? My name is Feng Xuan. I hope that we will be able to help each other and have a good time with you in the Class 2 world!”","Feng Xuan immediately emphasized the part about them helping each other. Fan Lou immediately understood Feng Xuan’s intention to come to see him.","With Kong Huan’s promise, Fan Lou had already decided to become the relative of the Alluring Foxes, just like Feng Lin had become the relative of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","However, Fan Lou was at a loss about how to turn Feng Qing down. It would not be simple or easy to turn down Feng Qing! He held as much authority as Kong Huan did in the Honor Absent Parliament.","However, he couldn’t feign agreement due to the pressure he felt. If he agreed and word of this spread, not only would he struggle to prove himself to Kong Huan, but also—if he refrained from assisting Feng Xuan in the Class 2 world and Feng Xuan later disclosed his actions to Feng Qing upon their return—he would be guilty of deceiving Feng Qing.","At that moment, Fan Lou once again cursed his luck. He was stuck between a rock and a hard place. A single wrong move, and he would be crushed.","–","Fan Lou went with Feng Xuan to Feng Qing’s palace. This was the first time that he was interacting with Feng Qing face-to-face.","Feng Qing had handsome features, a muscular physique, and a pair of light silver eyes that were full of gentleness and did not carry even a hint of pressure.","Feng Qing chuckled after seeing Fan Lou bow to him, and he said in a gentle voice, “Let’s sit down to chat. You don’t have to be so nervous around me! The Sixth Boundary Patrol Team finding a Class 2 world like this within your jurisdiction is also a gift from you to me!","“Feng Xuan, go and pluck a few Light Wolf Fruits. Envoy Fan, I’m not sure if you are interested in the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf and the Light Wind Wolf species’ bloodline. Three Light Wolf Fruits should be enough for you to obtain a portion of the Light Wind Wolf bloodline’s characteristics.”","Fan Lou was taken aback by Feng Qing’s immediate gift and the way he addressed him.","Fan Lou knew of the Light Wolf Fruit. It was a fruit that Fan Lou would never be able to touch in the past. It was a resource that he could not even buy with money.","Powerful species always had dependent species attached to them.","The Light Wolf Fruit was sacred to the Light Wind Wolves as their ancestors were all buried beneath the Light Wolf Tree.","Members of beast species who consumed the Light Wolf Fruits would obtain traits of the Light Wind Wolves.","Fan Lou just happened to be a member of a beast species.","The Light Wind Wolves’ bloodline would enable him to significantly increase his speed, and wind would become his aid instead of an obstacle.","Kong Huan would be hesitant to give him such a reward even if he asked her for it.","Feng Qing’s generosity touched but also bothered Fan Lou.","When Feng Qing saw that Fan Lou did not turn him down immediately, his lips curled slightly. It seemed that Kong Huan did not treat her subordinates very well or give them generous promises! Otherwise, he would not be so easily tempted by three Light Wolf Fruits.","Feng Qing and Kong Huan were not considered rivals. In fact, the two of them were not linked in any way.","However, Feng Qing would not show mercy when it came to fighting for profits. He was also unafraid of offending Kong Huan.","It did not take long for Feng Xuan to bring the three Light Wolf Fruits over and place them in front of Fan Lou.","Feng Xuan was aware of Feng Qing’s intention.","Given Feng Qing’s identity, it was not appropriate for him to extend an invitation to Fan Lou directly. Hence, Feng Xuan picked an appropriate moment and said, “After consuming the three Light Wolf Fruits, there will be sufficient Light Wind Wolf bloodline power in your body to make you a distant relative of the Light Wind Wolves. You will receive the protection of the Light Wind Wolves.","“If you are willing to help Lord Feng Qing, he will be willing to give you the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves’ essence blood to change your bloodline. That will make you a branch member of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","“This gift will definitely enable your status to skyrocket! I don’t think the master you serve will also be willing to gift you the essence blood of her species, right?”","The three Light Wolf Fruits had only tempted Fan Lou. But the mention of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf essence blood had an effect that went beyond temptation!","Fan Lou lifted his gaze and looked at Feng Qing with his eyes full of hope.","Feng Qing’s tone was no longer as amicable. He said sternly, “The Chaos Wind Demon Wolf essence blood is talk for the future. You will only get your hands on it after you’ve helped me. Additionally, I can personally transform your bloodline so you won’t be put at any risk!”","Feng Qing paused before he continued. “Do you really think that Kong Huan thinks highly of you? The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves do not care about bloodline as much as the Alluring Foxes do. The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves have always had a history of taking in other species. But can the same be said of the Alluring Foxes? Think about the other Boundary Patrol Envoys you used to work with. You should be better aware than anyone else where they are now!”"]},{"number":2765,"title":"Chapter 2765 Kong Huan’s Subordinate Gets Poached!","paragraphs":["2765 Kong Huan’s Subordinate Gets Poached!","Feng Qing had not said much, but each word he uttered hit just the right spots.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were a branch of the Moon-Worshiping Wolf species.","It was said that the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves’ ancestors had abandoned the Moon-Worshiping Wolves’ traditional method of evolving their bloodline and stopped worshiping the moon. Instead, they began using wind elements to temper their bodies.","A species like this that chose to change their bloodline during their development was very capable of taking in other species.","The Alluring Foxes’ dependent species had a much lower status than the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves. The Alluring Foxes were willing to nurture only members of the fox species.","Fan Lou knew that his bloodline did not align with them.","Since both paths led to him becoming a member of a dependent species, it would be better for him to become part of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves rather than the Alluring Foxes’ dependent species.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were extremely protective of their own. In the past, they even got into conflicts with other species on behalf of their dependents.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves was also one of the few species that had dealings with the Blood species, aka Bloodians.","With the Bloodians’ protection, most species did not dare to get on the wrong side of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves. One of these species was the Alluring Foxes.","At first, Feng Qing’s words only riled up Fan Lou’s appetite and caused him to waver in the face of profits. But the latter part of what Feng Qing said caused any willpower Fan Lou had to crumble.","Kong Huan was an Elder of the Alluring Foxes and could decide which dependent species they took in.","However, there was no reason for Kong Huan to strengthen another dependent species for his sake.","Kong Huan looked down on dependent species and took the same attitude toward him.","Kong Huan had gotten rid of all the Boundary Patrol Envoys under her command for various reasons. If she was willing to abandon them, he knew she would do the same to him.","Fan Lou suddenly felt a strong sense of peril.","Even if he continued to do her bidding, he could not guarantee she would treat him well after they returned from the Class 2 world. Would she really do as she promised and give him all those profits?","A mysterious smile appeared on Feng Qing’s face when he saw Fan Lou’s expression.","There was still some time before they set off. If he buried the seed of doubt within Fan Lou, the latter would eventually come back to look for him even if he did not agree to his terms today!","How could he have any sense of security working under Kong Huan?","“Why aren’t you accepting Lord Feng Qing’s generosity? The Boundary Patrol Envoy of the 346th Boundary Patrol Team traded for ten drops of the Wild Billowing Spirit Water from the mermaids for Kong Huan.","“If Lord Feng Qing is willing to protect you, Kong Huan won’t be able to touch you even if she finds out that you’ve betrayed her! You have never stopped providing Kong Huan with offerings, and she doesn’t have anything that she can use against you.","“Kong Huan won’t start a war between the Alluring Foxes and Light Wind Wolves over this grudge. After all, this might bring down the wrath of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves on the Alluring Foxes as well!”","Now that all the pros and cons were laid out in front of Fan Lou, he would have no reason not to join Feng Qing’s camp as long as they gave him a sense of assurance.","Feng Qing had put some effort into his plan to recruit Fan Lou.","If Fan Lou truly joined him and provided him with benefits from the Class 2 world, Feng Qing would not mind helping Fan Lou and turning him into another obedient and useful subordinate.","After Fan Lou heard what Feng Xuan said, he looked up at Feng Qing as though he was resolving to make a serious decision before bowing deeply.","“Lord Feng Qing, I am willing to become a member of the Light Wind Wolves! When we get to the Class 2 world, I will do my best to help you to search for resources. I will also look after Feng Xuan. I hope you will truly be able to protect me!”","Feng Qing scoffed. “Are you doubting my sincerity? Protecting you is a small matter to me! If you are willing, you can eat the three Light Wolf Fruits and change your bloodline before you leave. Then, you can announce to the outside world that you have become a member of the Light Wind Wolves. I will tell the leader of the Light Wind Wolves to respond accordingly.”","Feng Qing’s words set Fan Lou at ease.","Previously, Kong Huan never allowed Fan Lou to let their relationship become known. She did not want him to affect her reputation in case an accident happened.","Yet, Feng Qing was willing to go public with their relationship!","Reputation was extremely important for the members of the Honor Absent Parliament.","There was no need for Feng Qing to risk tarnishing his reputation for the sake of a trivial character like him by making the news public.","As Fan Lou contemplated agreeing to ally with Feng Qing, he was interrupted by Feng Qing’s solemn inquiry, “Kong Huan, though cruel, possesses intelligence and foresight. If the events in that Class 2 world merely involved the evolution of a few lifeforms into World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, she wouldn’t go so far as to suggest you as the guide! There must be undisclosed information. I need to know what that is!”","Fan Lou knew that this was Feng Qing’s way of telling him that he needed to make a declaration.","After being made aware of the pros and cons, Fan Lou had decided to join Feng Qing.","There was no need to continue keeping this secret for Kong Huan’s sake.","Moreover, there was no way that Feng Qing would reveal this secret after learning of it. Kong Huan would not know that he had betrayed her.","Now that he had sorted his thoughts out, Fan Lou said in a pleasant tone, “Lord Feng Qing, your strategy is truly profound! The true meaning is indeed not as simple as it appears to be. Besides having two World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys, there were faeries born in that Class 2 world!”","A look of shock appeared on Feng Qing’s face, but it was quickly replaced by realization.","It was no wonder that someone like Kong Huan, who did not like to use her resources, was willing to spend too much for the sake of Honor Absent Palace. It turned out that faeries had appeared!","A low-class world that could produce faeries was worth investigating, no matter how sizable the cost. The faeries alone represented unimaginable value.","Fan Lou was very skilled at reading someone based on their body language. When he saw the expression on Feng Qing’s face, he knew that Feng Qing was very satisfied with his answer.","If Fan Lou was compelled by his circumstances and was only temporarily siding with Feng Qing, he could keep the latter part of his answer to himself.","But now that Feng Qing had made a promise to Fan Lou and guaranteed he could assure Fan Lou’s safety, Fan Lou was more than willing to prove his value to Feng Qing.","Fan Lou added earnestly, “Lord Feng Qing, this Class 2 world is far more amazing than what I’ve already revealed. It was only just promoted from a Class 1 world to Class 2. Although World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeforms appeared after the world’s promotion, the faeries appeared when it was still a Class 1 world.”","At first, Feng Qing only wanted to search this world in the hopes of obtaining profits. He wanted to see if he would be able to discover a new resource or treasure in this world.","As a member of Honor Absent Parliament, Feng Qing held an extremely high status. Searching for outstanding resources and treasures was not only his hobby but also the method through which he built up his foundational power.","He became especially interested after finding out that there were a few World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys in this Class 2 world.","But he never expected this information to have been intentionally released by Kong Huan.","The deaths of so many people in the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team could not be kept under wraps forever. Even if Kong Huan wanted to hide it, she was incapable of doing so.","However, she had used that information to hide a secret that would shake up the entire Sky Beyond the Clouds.","There were a few bigshots in the Sky Beyond the Clouds who were uninterested in the Class 2 world and had not sent people to join the investigation. But if they found out that faeries appeared in this Class 2 world when it was still Class 1, they would do anything they could to get a piece of the pie!","Feng Qing already decided to send more people to this Class 2 world.","After receiving this news, Feng Qing’s impression of Fan Lou improved significantly.","“Fan Lou, you are great! The information you told me is extremely important. Once the matter is settled, I will arrange for a marriage between you and a member of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves’ dependent species so you can become a relative of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves. You will then have the right to participate in the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves’ meetings!”","Previously, Feng Qing had only promised that Fan Lou would become a member of the Light Wind Wolves. But now, he was promising an engagement between him and a member of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","This was a similar level of generosity to what Kong Huan had offered him.","However, Fan Lou felt more secure in this promise from Feng Qing than the one from Fan Lou.","There were very few members of the Light Wind Wolves. They always cherished their members, so their relatives were much more valuable than the Alluring Foxes’ relatives.","Now that the benefits had piled up, Fan Lou said excitedly, “Lord Feng Qing, I’m not done speaking yet! You are unaware of this, but there is not just one faerie in the Class 2 world. One of them is an intermediate one!”","Feng Qing was already interested in this Class 2 world.","When he heard that there was an intermediate faerie there, Feng Qing could not stop himself from slamming his hand down on the table.","Despite being a superior, he was showing his emotions in front of his subordinates. This was enough to show the extent of Feng Qing’s shock and excitement.","Feng Qing let out two peals of laughter.","“In the past, Feng Xuan was the only one by my side. There are many tasks that are too much for him alone. If you perform well this time, you can join him by my side from now on!”","Feng Xuan could not hide the hostility in his gaze as he looked at Fan Lou. He never expected the Fan Lou he brought there to one day share his authority!","Feng Xuan believed that all the work he had done under Feng Qing had been impeccable. There were no tasks that had been too much for him.","Feng Qing was the type to follow his heart and act as he pleased. If he said that he was going to support Fan Lou, it was very possible he would keep Fan Lou by his side in the future!","Fan Lou had to be relatively capable in order to become captain of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team. It was only his power that was still lacking.","Feng Qing patted Fan Lou’s shoulder, and his gaze softened.","In all the time that Feng Xuan had spent by Feng Qing’s side, he did not know that Feng Qing cared a lot about luck and fortune.","This was the first time that he was meeting Fan Lou, but the latter was already bringing him such enormous fortune. Feng Qing believed that keeping Fan Lou by his side would bring him luck!","Otherwise, Fan Lou would not deserve such support from Feng Qing even if he gained the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf essence blood and bloodline!","There were many members of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf species who racked their brains for a plan that would allow them to remain by Feng Qing’s side.","As a member of the Honor Absent Parliament, there was no way that Feng Qing could personally head to the Class 2 world. The same went for Kong Huan!","A Class 2 world’s world wills had a limit to what they could handle. If overwhelmingly strong experts arrived in a Class 2 world, there was a high chance that said world would collapse.","They could only harvest resources from low-class worlds in secret.","If they wrecked a Class 2 world and the other three universes found out about it, they would work together to exert pressure on the East Universe. Faerie Institution would also look into the matter.","Feng Qing did not want to be dragged into trouble.","Among species of equal power, the Bloodians possessed extremely high dominance.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were on good terms with the Bloodians, and Feng Qing intended to borrow a few World Emperor/Intermediate Divine Kingdom experts from them. This would deepen their connection to the Bloodians.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were in urgent need for resources. The Bloodians’ energy mainly came from absorbing vitality and death energy. Hence, they had a large amount of resources they could trade with the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","Even if the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves obtained faeries, they would have to share them with the Bloodians.","Feng Qing would feel more secure if the Bloodians were involved!","Kong Huan was definitely aware of the information that Fan Lou had just revealed. She also had to have already made her preparations. Hence, he needed to guard himself against her.","“Fan Lou, I have already been sufficiently generous with you. Now, I want you to announce that you’ve joined the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves. You will remain in my palace for the next few days. You don’t have to interact with any outsiders. I will personally settle things with Kong Huan on your behalf. What do you think of this?”","If he was capable of using his authority and offering profits to seduce Fan Lou into joining him, the other members of the Honor Absent Parliament could do the same. Feng Qing had absolutely no doubts about this.","Feng Qing would only feel at ease if Fan Lou remained here until he had to depart.","Fan Lou nodded enthusiastically. “Lord Feng Qing, I will do everything as you say! I will make a record of all the resources found in the Class 2 world and hand it over to you.”","Feng Qing’s suggestion suited Fan Lou perfectly.","If he joined the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves, his peers would be green with envy.","Moreover, Feng Qing would help him to settle things with Kong Huan. This settled all of his worries.","Feng Qing immediately left for Kong Huan’s residence.","Feng Qing believed that Kong Huan also did not want news of an intermediate faerie appearing in the Class 2 world when it was still only a Class 1 world to become known. If she did not want this information to be exposed, their negotiation would go smoothly!","The Alluring Foxes were not as powerful as the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","Hence, despite it being rather unsavory that he had poached Fan Lou, Kong Huan would have no choice but to swallow this injustice!"]},{"number":2766,"title":"Chapter 2766 Give Him a Reminder!","paragraphs":["2766 Give Him a Reminder!","The Startling Lines Continent was less than outstanding before the dead spirits crisis.","In order for a continent to make a name for itself in the main world, it needed to achieve impressive results during the Major Federation Meetings.","However, the Divine Wood, Great Lush, and Iron Hammer Federations had no federation envoys in the past and had been absent from the past few decades of Major Federation Meetings. It could almost be said that they were hiding from the rest of the world.","Aside from the few neighboring continents that were aware of the Startling Lines Continent’s existence, the federations located further away had never even heard of the Startling Lines Continent.","The Radiance Federation had fully overshadowed the Startling Lines Continent.","But now, the Startling Lines Continent was a glittering territory of fortune that was known by every person in the main world.","The Major Federation Union’s headquarters was located in the Startling Lines Continent and all the experts of the main world who wanted to receive resources from the Radiance Federation to increase their power needed to report to the Startling Lines Continent.","The Startling Lines Continent also had a harbor. The boats that the Radiance Federation had eliminated were ready and prepared to begin trading.","The Startling Lines Continent was now a superstar in the main world.","If not for the fact that the Startling Lines Continent did not speak the lingua franca, many experts would have already flooded the Startling Lines Continent as tourists.","The Divine Wood, Great Lush, and Iron Hammer Federations’ officials sent out official notices that they would begin taking in experts three years later. They would use these experts to build up their guard teams and address the safety and peace-keeping issues in the federations.","The younger generation of the Startling Lines Continent’s three federations all contracted feys with the Sacred Wood bloodline.","The Sacred Wood bloodline was vestiges of Begin Lady’s intermediate faerie bloodline.","With Begin Lady’s current power, it could easily allow these feys to evolve to Suzerain/Creation.","The experts who joined the Divine Wood, Great Lush, and Iron Hammer Federations could also contract feys that possessed the Sacred Wood bloodline.","This was an extremely attractive point.","The Startling Lines Continent seemed to be basking in glory and was the hub of the entire world. However, its three federations were mired in contention. This was all focused on the harbor.","...","The ruler of the Divine Wood Federation, Yi Huailong, was currently in a secret room speaking to a man who resembled him but with softer eyes.","“Huailu, I am not thinking too deeply into this. Although you have joined Sky City and Lord Lin Yuan, the Divine Wood Federation is your roots! The Yi family’s establishment is fully within the Startling Lines Continent! I put all my effort into developing the Divine Wood Federation into what it is today. Why can’t I be troubled by the matter of the harbor?”","Yi Huailu could not help but massage his temples. He was well aware of how much effort Yi Huailong had invested into the Divine Wood Federation. He had truly devoted his heart and soul into it.","However, the matter of the harbor was much too serious. Given that the Radiance Federation had placed the eliminated boats in the harbor, it meant that Lin Yuan had not forgotten about the harbor’s existence.","The harbor could not be stolen away due to its geographical location.","Once the harbor was connected to the entire main world, its profits could exceed that of the entire Great Lush Federation!","The Radiance Federation was continuing to deliver the eliminated boats to the harbor. This meant that Lin Yuan had plans to expand the operation.","Yi Huailu believed that if Lin Yuan had expanded the harbor earlier, Jin Qianxun would not have dared to reach his selfish hands into the harbor!","At that moment, Yi Huailu did not know if his brother was too shortsighted or cared so much about the ownership of the harbor because he was hyper-focused on developing the Divine Wood Federation.","“Big Brother, I understand your meaning. However, you might not be aware of this, but I don’t have much speaking authority around Lord Lin Yuan. I can’t be considered one of Sky City’s main members. Even if I was, I couldn’t speak up on your behalf in this matter!”","Yi Huailu was extremely vexed when he spoke, but this was the truth. He did not have the ability to influence Lin Yuan to change his strategies.","Back when he was in the Startling Lines Continent, Yi Huailu believed that the end of the line of pinnacle Class 4 Creation Master. If one was able to become a Class 5 Creation Master, one would be able to stand on the peak and look down on the rest of the world.","But after joining Lin Yuan, he realized just how wrong he was.","Creation Masters did not receive any special treatment from Lin Yuan. Rather, those who were skilled at management stood out.","Yi Huailu was well aware of how much resources he had supplied to Lin Yuan. He had only made a marginal contribution to the resources that Lin Yuan had supplied.","Yi Huailu knew that if he told his brother about the truth, Yi Huailong might not believe him.","Nonetheless, Yi Huailu still needed to say what needed to be said.","Yi Huailong was definitely the type who would ask him to collude and scheme together.","If Yi Huailong sought him out and asked him to do such, Yi Huailu would have to draw the line between them.","Yi Huailong’s heart sank when he heard that. He looked at Yi Huailu with heavy disappointment.","With Yi Huailong’s perception of values, he would never have expected a Class 5 Creation Master to be unimportant.","Yi Huailong was not a Creation Master and did not know of a Creation Master’s resource production abilities.","He contemplated questioning Yi Huailu about whether the family had received insufficient resources over the years because Yi Huailu had allocated them all to Lin Yuan, who then distributed them across the main world.","In a self-centered manner, Yi Huailong believed that even if Yi Huailu had aligned with Lin Yuan, he should prioritize the Yi family’s interests.","As long as the Yi family maintained substantial power, Yi Huailong could enjoy a higher status among Lin Yuan’s subordinates.","Observing Yi Huailong’s expression, Yi Huailu discerned that his brother hadn’t fully grasped his point.","Without delving further into explanations, Yi Huailu opted to reassure Yi Huailong.","“Big Brother, I can’t promise that the harbor will be shared equally among the Divine Wood, Great Lush, and Iron Hammer Federations. But I can promise that the Great Lush Federation will not have sole ownership of the harbor!","“The harbor’s position is extremely critical. It will be the channel through which the Startling Lines Continent trades with the other continents. Even the few harbors in the Radiance Federation can’t compare to the one in the Great Lush Federation in terms of location and environment. The profits will roll in if we can get our hands on that location!","“Big Brother, because of the geographical location of the Startling Lines Continent, the Great Lush Federation will make it into the top 300 at the Major Federation Meeting. As long as the Great Lush Federation continues to develop, the Divine Wood Federation will be able to raise its ranking as well!","“The Divine Wood, Great Lush, and Iron Hammer Federations are all at the forefront of change. There are countless federations who are eyeing the Divine Wood Federation’s position. At such a time, laying low and being restrained will be the best course of governance for you! If you charge ahead in everything, others will misunderstand you as having unsavory intentions!","“Luo Lan is much closer to Lord Lin Yuan than I am. If you can, try to communicate more with her to follow in her lead. I came back this time to give you some Creation Master resources that you can use to nurture the family.","“Big Brother, I will never forget who I am, regardless of where I am. I will also never forget to give resources to the family!”","Yi Huailu spoke with utmost seriousness and expressed his stance to Yi Huailong.","Given Yi Huailu’s character, he would not be bothered to provide an explanation to anyone else. However, Yi Huailong was his brother. If Yi Huailong still did not understand him after this explanation, he would explain himself again!","Yi Huailu knew that Lin Yuan’s goal was not in the main world and that he intended to take a group of people with him to a higher-level world.","Before he witnessed the fusing of the dimensional worlds with the main world and the promotion of the main world, Yi Huailu would not have believed in the existence of a higher world beyond the main world. However, given the circumstances, Yi Huailu could not help but believe.","Lin Yuan still had yet to come to see him. Moreover, it was true that he was not important to Sky City. Hence, it was more likely than not that Lin Yuan would keep him in the main world.","At that time, he might not be able to overly support the Divine Wood Federation but could still strengthen its development and grow its power.","It was true that Yi Huailong had not accepted Yi Huailu’s words. However, Yi Huailu was there to provide resources to the family. As displeased as he was, he did not bring up the Divine Wood Federation again.","Yi Huailong was still concerned about the harbor, but he believed that he needed to contact Luo Lan.","There was no way that Luo Lan would want Jin Qianxun to occupy the harbor on his own!","...","Yi Huailong did not know that Luo Lan had not thought about this that deeply.","Luo Lan had always been open about the harbor’s ownership issues. She believed that it was not an issue that needed to be overly analyzed.","While Lin Yuan was preparing the Startling Lines Continent’s defenses, he had invested almost 1/3 of the resources into the harbor. This was a clear indication of the harbor’s importance to Lin Yuan.","Since then, Luo Lan knew that Jin Qianxun would never be able to retain full control over it.","Luo Lan had reported the matter to Wen Yu because she believed she needed to report her circumstances as a member of the Astronomical Parliament.","Luo Lan, Jin Qianxun, and Yi Huailong had collaborated for numerous years, and her favorable opinion of Jin Qianxun exceeded that of Yi Huailong. She opposed the idea of Jin Qianxun being replaced as the leader of the Great Lush Federation due to reckless scheming.","But once ambition had bred in a person, it could not be dissolved easily.","Luo Lan could not give Jin Qianxun advice when it came to this matter. If she did, it would be seen as her trying to stir trouble.","Some time had passed since she had reported her information to Wen Yu.","Lin Yuan had only just gained some time to rest. Wen Yu would definitely relay the situation to Lin Yuan so he could make the decisions and come up with the plan.","The aides in Luo Lan’s court had been worried about the ownership issue of the harbor and brought up the issue with Luo Lan.","When Luo Lan saw that her aides were still troubled over this matter, she said, “All you need to do is focus on developing the Iron Hammer Federation. You don’t need to think about anything else, so don’t waste your time thinking about this! Otherwise, your thoughts will be led astray!","“The harbor will either end up being shared by the Startling Lines Continent’s three federations or it won’t. With how far the Iron Hammer Federation is from the harbor, how can we even attempt to interfere?”","Luo Lan was silent for a moment before she continued. “Help me pack my things. I will make a rush journey to the Dark Continent. I will be staying there for some time.","“You must send me daily reports on the federation’s internal affairs using that magical paper I gave you. I will give my authorization for any plans through the paper.”","Luo Lan’s aides were shocked when they heard that. She was actually going to leave the Iron Hammer Federation at such a time?","The Startling Lines Continent was currently riding a wave of prosperity, and countless federations wanted to strike up deals with the Iron Hammer Federation.","The aides believed Luo Lan should focus on the Iron Hammer Federation’s development.","Luckily, even if Luo Lan left the Iron Hammer Federation, they could communicate with her through the magical paper and inform her of any developments in the federation.","Luo Lan had thought deeply before she decided to leave for the Dark Continent to help Su Yiren.","Luo Lan had already organized all of the development issues in the Iron Hammer Federation. She had sought Wen Yu’s opinion on many matters. The Iron Hammer Federation was operating well and on the right path.","Even if Luo Lan remained in the Iron Hammer Federation, she would only need to call the shots and make decisions.","Su Yiren had decided to return to the Dark Continent after the dead spirits crisis came to an end.","Aside from the Dark Continent, Su Yiren also needed to manage the people in the Sand Island Continent. Millions of people were seeking shelter in the Sand Island Continent, and there was endless work to be done!","This was the time that Su Yiren most needed her.","Luo Lan was well aware of all the help that Su Yiren had given her in the past. It was now time for her to repay Su Yiren!","When a ruler left their federation, they were most afraid of losing their power within their federation.","This was what had happened to Luo Lan’s father.","However, this would never happen to Luo Lan.","Firstly, Lin Yuan had Lin Yuan’s Eternal weapon by her side.","Additionally, even if the Eternal weapon could not handle those who tried to overthrow her, Lin Yuan, who had been capable of putting an end to the dead spirits crisis, would definitely have the ability to regain power on her behalf!","All those concerned about the harbor ownership were unaware of who truly controlled the Startling Lines Continent. Without knowing this, mulling over the matter would only lead to erroneous and harmful conclusions.","Luo Lan could not tell Jin Qianxun about this upfront, but she could use another method to advise him.","Luo Lan looked up at one of her aides and patted her shoulder.","“Fei Xing, I remember that a year before the dead spirits crisis began, your sister married into the Jin family in order to form an alliance between the Iron Hammer Federation and Great Lush Federation. How is your sister doing in the Jin family?”","Fei Xing hurriedly answered, “My sister is living very comfortably in the Jin family. She attends every important gathering in the Jin family and even helps with the management at times. She does have some sway in the family!”","Luo Lan smiled faintly. “Are you still in contact with your sister? Go and tell her to pay respects to Jin Qianxun and give him some spiritual ingredients as well as a fey! Remember to remind her not to speak too much about other matters.”"]},{"number":2767,"title":"Chapter 2767 The Overstuffed Flower Mink Mouse!","paragraphs":["2767 The Overstuffed Flower Mink Mouse!","Luo Lan was certain that once Jin Qianxun saw these spiritual ingredients and fey, he would understand what she was trying to say. Saying too much would not only be meaningless but could also cause news of their interaction to spread.","Luo Lan did this after thinking through her own considerations.","Firstly, Luo Lan had set her sights on the Sky Beyond the Clouds. If there were any changes to the structure of the Startling Lines Continent, Luo Lan would have to refocus her efforts on managing the Iron Hammer Federation.","Moreover, the new ruler of the Great Lush Federation might not be as intelligent and understanding as Jin Qianxun.","Luo Lan had built up a chemistry with Jin Qianxun and gotten used to his way of doing things. If the new ruler of the Great Lush Federation liked to cause trouble, Luo Lan would have to waste a lot of effort handling him.","A person who was chosen by Lin Yuan would not be obvious about any trouble they were trying to cause. It would be much more challenging to try to handle someone who was trying to cause trouble from the shadows.","Fei Xing thought about this for a moment. But she could not figure out what the spiritual ingredients and fey could be. Since she could not figure it out, she could only ask, “Your Majesty, I hope you will tell me clearly what the spiritual ingredients and fey you would like my sister to prepare so I tell her to get them ready immediately!","“She might have married and moved to the Great Lush Federation, but she is still a member of the Iron Hammer Federation’s Turquoise Tribe and will do what is best for the federation!”","Luo Lan nodded noncommittally.","Back then, this was exactly the reason for picking someone from the Turquoise Tribe to marry into the Jin family. If the member of the Turquoise Tribe who married into the Jin family was unable to work for the Iron Hammer Federation, the marriage alliance would be meaningless.","“The spiritual ingredients and fey I want you to prepare are common. They are the Flower Mink Mouse and a large amount of quince blossom buds. There must be enough quince blossom buds to overstuff the Flower Mink Mouse!”","The Flower Mink Mouse was a fey that was common in the Startling Lines Continent. It was the evolved version of the Flower Branch Mouse.","There were very few people who formed contracts with the Flower Mink Mouse. It had a special habit, which was an insatiable appetite. It was especially weak toward quince blossom flower buds.","The quince blossoms happened to be in full bloom, and there were many Flower Mink Mice with exploded stomachs littered below the quince blossom trees.","Quince blossoms could be found in wild forests and reproduced easily.","Fei Xing knew that there was no way the Flower Mink Mouse and quince blossoms were meant to be gifts.","After pondering for a moment, Fei Xing understood Luo Lan’s intention of telling her sister to present the quince blossoms and Flower Mink Mouse to Jin Qianxun.","When a Flower Mink Mouse saw the quince blossoms, it would begin consuming them in a frenzy and eventually become so bloated that its stomach exploded and it died.","Luo Lan was trying to warn Jin Qianxun not to become like the Flower Mink Mouse over the matter of the harbor’s ownership.","It was said that the human heart was never content, just like a snake that tried to swallow an elephant.","Fei Xing was unsure if her sister would be implicated because of this matter. But even if she did end up implicated, this was a task that her sister needed to complete.","Fei Xing started to leave the hall.","At that moment, she heard Luo Lan say, “You have always had a more agile and intelligent mind than others. You must pay more attention to the management of the court! You are better suited than the others to manage the court meetings. I hope that you will work hard from now on so as not to disappoint me.”","Luo Lan waved at Fei Xing to signal she should pass down her order as quickly as possible.","Fei Xing’s expression did not falter as she departed the hall. But once she exited the hall, her body started to tremble uncontrollably.","Fei Xing could read between the lines of Luo Lan’s remark. Luo Lan intended to rely heavily on her in the future—her words were a clear message!","Luo Lan had been intentionally distributing power and authority in the last few years. Now, she was giving away the authority to manage court meetings.","If she obtained the authority to manage court meetings, she would be second only to Luo Lan when it came to power and authority in the Iron Hammer Federation.","Fei Xing was not stationed next to Luo Lan from the beginning. Rather, she had captured opportunity after opportunity and had been promoted after Luo Lan noticed her abilities.","Luo Lan let out a sigh after Fei Xing left. She saw Jin Qianxun as exceedingly important.","Someone as smart as him would not be so impulsive as to act foolishly.","Jin Qianxun had to have thought deeply and carefully before acting. He also had to have already made preparations to face the associated risks.","Luo Lan hoped that her warning would help Jin Qianxun to see the light.","A supervisor who had received authority should not make independent decisions. It was possible that Jin Qianxun had forgotten this after becoming accustomed to being a ruler.","...","In the evening, Jin Qianxun finished his harbor patrol, a routine he diligently performed to oversee the ongoing construction. His regular checks had become a recent habit, ensuring the harbor’s smooth operation.","Observing the boats arriving and departing from the harbor, Jin Qianxun experienced a sense of elevation, as if he were overseeing everything from a vantage point.","The Island Whales, representing different federations, paid their dues and docked in the harbor. Those who utilized these majestic creatures always took a moment to acknowledge him.","The newfound respect and admiration directed toward Jin Qianxun were sensations he had never experienced before.","It was because he had all these federation managers clustering around him that Jin Qianxun’s mindset began to change slowly.","Jin Qianxun did not employ members of the Jin family while governing the Great Lush Federation because he did not want Lin Yuan to think he was abusing his power for selfish reasons. Instead, he selected excellent managers from various secret aristocratic families who together served as advisors for court meetings.","But it went without saying that Jin Qianxun remained the true and ultimate decision-maker. He would never allow the authority he had jumped through hoops to obtain to leave his hands.","“Your Majesty, another large batch of resources has been invested into the harbor. According to news from the envoys, the harbor is about to be expanded to include the entire outer sea. This will make the harbor even larger than the Great Lush Federation’s six major cities combined!","“May I be so brash as to ask if we will truly have full control over such a harbor? With the continuous stream of resources that we’ve invested into the harbor in the past few years, we could have rebuilt the Great Lush Federation four times! Your Majesty, I don’t think you should hope to have sole control over the harbor.”","This nephew always had a clear grasp of the perspectives of different matters.","However, what his nephew had just said was not something that Jin Qianxun wanted to hear.","Jin Qianxun frowned and yelled, “The issue of the harbor has been mentioned at the imperial meeting more than three times, and a decision has been made. You don’t need to be unnecessarily worried! Leave now. I will go through these documents on my own. You can come back when you have something to report to me!”","When Jin Zhanming heard what Jin Qianxun said, he pursed his lips but did not say anything else. Instead, he left Jin Qianxun’s private room and began standing guard outside.","Jin Zhanming was well aware of Jin Qianxun’s state and guessed that Jin Qianxun would react in such a way after hearing his suggestion.","However, Jin Zhanming had been keeping these words to himself for a long time.","The function he served by Jin Qianxun’s side was to give him some advice during special situations.","The larger the harbor became, the less secure Jin Zhanming felt.","Jin Qianxun had always remained pleasant toward him.","Such a reaction from Jin Qianxun meant that he also shared the same foreboding. However, he intended to take the risk and take a gamble.","With this thought, Jin Zhanming sighed.","A truly dumb person could be given a wake-up call. But if an intelligent person chose to stake everything on a final dice throw, such a person would not turn back unless there was something they were truly worried about!","When Jin Qianxun was alone in his private room, he continuously poured tea for himself. He finished a large pot of tea in a little over ten minutes.","Jin Qianxun placed the teacup heavily down on the table as Lin Yuan’s face flashed through his mind.","Lin Yuan was aware of all that he did.","Lin Yuan was always decisive in his actions and never dragged his feet.","Most times, he was generous and never held back when he invested resources. He also enabled people like Jin Qianxun to truly be able to rule over federations.","But behind all of this, he drew up plans for the federations’ development. The leaders he chose needed to follow the paths he had set to develop their federations.","One of the reasons Jin Qianxun wanted so badly to take control of the harbor was that its existence had allowed him to regain his pride. He greatly enjoyed the feeling of being flattered and fawned on by the other federation envoys.","Furthermore, it was true that the harbor was located within the Great Lush Federation.","However, the harbor had never been developed before Lin Yuan took control of the Great Lush Federation.","Jin Qianxun could not help but be afraid each time he was alone.","If he had nothing now, Jin Qianxun would be very willing to take the gamble. But now, the Jin family had become the Great Lush Federation’s royal family, and he was its ruler. Once he lost, everything he had now would vanish.","At that moment, someone knocked on the door of his private room. Jin Zhanming peeked in before saying softly, “Your Majesty, Jin Lü would like to see you. Are you willing to meet with her?”","Jin Lü was Fei Xing’s sister and had the direct bloodline of the Turquoise Tribe. She had changed her last name in accordance with the Great Lush Federation’s customs because she had married into the Jin family.","Jin Lü represented the friendship between the Iron Hammer Federation and the Great Lush Federation.","Given their friendly relations, the Jin family treated Jin Lü extremely well.","Jin Lü was acutely aware of her circumstances. She never forgot about her identity and did not forget about her roots just because she lived in luxury in the Jin family.","Her behavior pleased Jin Qianxun greatly.","Jin Lü was most likely there to see him pass on a message on behalf of the Iron Hammer Federation.","He and Luo Lan had been sending messages to each other through the Thoughts Letter Paper. Why did she not do the same this time?","“Let Jin Lü in. Zhanming, go and brew a pot of tea and prepare some snacks.”","Jin Zhanming left immediately.","It was clear that Jin Qianxun had sent him on a task at such a time because he did not want him to remain in the room.","He could have served the tea and snacks after Jin Qianxun and Jin Lü were done with their conversation.","Jin Zhanming started to make guesses about Jin Lü’s reason for coming at such a time.","Upon entering the room, Jin Lü greeted Jin Qianxun with a smile and a respectful bow. She had come as a representative of the Iron Hammer Federation, adopting the appropriate demeanor befitting an elite of the federation.","Jin Qianxun waved at Jin Lü to indicate that they should sit next to each other to speak.","Jin Lü did not sit down immediately. Instead, she fixed her determined gaze on Jin Qianxun.","“I just went to take a walk around the harbor and found a Flower Mink Mouse as well as some quince blossom buds.”","Jin Lü took out the Flower Mink Mouse and quince blossom buds she had prepared and placed them on the floor.","Quince blossoms had an extremely strong scent, and it was gaudy to place them in the room. But once the Flower Mink Mouse in the cage caught a whiff of the quince blossom buds, it began chittering loudly and gnawing on the bars of the cage. It started to slam its body against the cage, and signs of injury appeared on its thick fur.","Jin Lü ignored the way that the Flower Mink Mouse’s expression changed after it saw the quince blossom buds and opened the cage.","The Flower Mink Mouse charged toward the quince blossoms. In the short span of a few tens of minutes, it began happily and madly stuffing the quince blossoms down its throat. It did not take long for the Flower Mink Mouse to die in front of Jin Lü and Jin Qianxun.","When Jin Lü saw the Flower Mink Mouse’s round and distended belly that was about to burst, she took out a dagger and gently swiped it across the Flower Mink Mouse’s abdomen. All of the quince blossoms spilled out from its stomach.","Jin Lü pulled a frightened expression and began bowing repeatedly to Jin Qianxun. “Your Majesty, I never expected such a thing to happen. I have disrespected you!”","Jin Lü cleaned up the carcass on the ground before bidding goodbye to Jin Qianxun with a solemn expression.","As Jin Lü was walking out of the private room, she bumped into Jin Zhanming, who was standing by the door and carrying a tray of tea and snacks.","Jin Zhanming was very surprised to see Jin Lü leaving. She had only been there for tens of minutes. That was almost too quick!","Just as Jin Zhanming was about to enter the private room, Jin Lü gently pulled him back and shook her head to tell him not to go in now to bother Jin Qianxun.","Jin Zhanming watched Jin Lü’s lips move and saw that she was mouthing the word ‘harbor’.","Jin Lü nodded and did not say anything else.","She had come to see Jin Qianxun about the issue of the harbor and was a representative of Luo Lan’s stance.","Luo Lan would never advise Jin Qianxun to occupy the harbor on his own. It was likely that she was advising him to stop trying to gain selfish profits from the harbor.","Jin Zhanming did not know if Jin Qianxun would give up his desire to gain sole ownership of the harbor after his conversation with Jin Lü.","Having spent considerable time by Jin Qianxun’s side, Jin Zhanming discerned that among the three federation rulers, Luo Lan held the closest rapport with Jin Qianxun. The probability of him attentively heeding and learning from her was significantly higher!"]},{"number":2768,"title":"Chapter 2768 Kong Huan’s Rage!","paragraphs":["2768 Kong Huan’s Rage!","The Iron Hammer Federation was on the best terms with the Great Lush Federation. The latter’s trade volume with the Iron Hammer Federation was far greater than its trade volume with the Divine Wood Federation.","Although the Startling Lines Continent had entered a state of peace, there was deep resentment between the Divine Wood Federation and the Great Lush Federation. Even if this resentment was not actively mentioned, it was still seared into their citizens’ bones and could not be removed easily.","Hence, even if Luo Lan wanted to scheme against another federation, her target should be the Divine Wood Federation and not the Great Lush Federation.","Waves of fright washed over Jin Qianxun. He struggled to calm down even some time after Jin Lü left.","Given Jin Qianxun’s understanding of Luo Lan, she was open to communication but strongly enforced her stance.","Luo Lan would never intentionally interfere with other federations. She knew that if she did so when the three federations were structured the way they were, Lin Yuan would be displeased when he learned about what she did.","Lin Yuan wanted there to be equality among the three federations because he did not want any federation to fall under the control of another federation.","Luo Lan had to mentally prepare herself before sending Jin Lü to warn him.","The Flower Mink Mouse had been as healthy as it could have been when it was in the cage, jumping around and baring its teeth. But after consuming the quince blossom buds in a mad frenzy, its stomach expanded and broke.","By trying to take sole control of the harbor and claiming benefits for his own federation, Jin Qianxun was just like this Flower Mink Mouse.","At that moment, fear gripped Jin Qianxun.","He ignored everything else and prepared to contact Luo Lan.","After some pondering, he did not use the Thoughts Letter Paper to contact Luo Lan. Instead, he called her over the phone.","Originally, communication in the Great Lush Federation was limited to within the federation. But as Lin Yuan altered the Startling Lines Continent’s infrastructure, he set up numerous special spiritual ingredients that could transmit signals. This enabled calls to be made across the entire continent.","However, after becoming accustomed to using the Thoughts Letter Paper, Jin Qianxun had not used his phone for communication in a very long time.","The messages in the Thoughts Letter Paper were recorded and could be checked. Jin Qianxun did not want evidence of his attempt to take sole control over the harbor to be left behind.","Luo Lan picked up his call very quickly.","She had been waiting for Jin Qianxun’s call ever since she arranged the matter.","Given her understanding of Jin Qianxun, he would respond to her gesture regardless of whether he heeded her advice.","If he had yet to heed her advice, she could still try to persuade him over the phone!","However, if Jin Qianxun insisted on his original plan even after the call, there would no longer be any hope for him.","Luo Lan could thus prepare herself for a change in the Great Lush Federation’s ruler.","“Jin Qianxun, you must be calling me because of Jin Lü. If there’s anything you want to say to me, don’t beat around the bush and just come out and say it! I can keep your secrets as long as it doesn’t disrupt the Startling Lines Continent! If I wasn’t sincere, I wouldn’t have sent Jin Lü to you!”","Luo Lan did not want to argue with Jin Qianxun. Just like how she did not trust him most of the time, he would not be fully trusting of her either. At the end of the day, both of them were rivals.","Hence, they needed to clear the air in order to communicate effectively. This would also bring the two of them closer together.","Now that Luo Lan had expressed such an attitude, she would understand his intention if he showed an unwillingness to continue the topic.","In such a case, she would no longer communicate with him in such a manner again in the future. She might even shove him from the back to quicken his fall from grace.","Jin Qianxun’s expression faltered. He felt certain that she knew something. Otherwise, she would not have sent Jin Lü to deliver trash like the Flower Mink Mouse and quince blossom buds to him.","“You know that I have been trying to take control of the harbor. I want to ask you if you think that by doing so, I am like the Flower Mink Mouse guzzling the quince blossom buds.”","Luo Lan’s straightforwardness led to the right response from Jin Qianxun.","Luo Lan smiled brightly. It seemed that Jin Qianxun intended to form an alliance with her!","If she helped Jin Qianxun and the Great Lush Federation, he would inevitably have to return the favor in the future.","“At least the Flower Mink Mouse could overstuff itself with quince blossoms before it died as a result of its gluttony.","“The harbor is something that the Great Lush Federation should never have tried to covet. In the beginning, 50 Island Whales were immediately invested in the harbor. I thought this was enough to make you see things clearly. I never expected your mind to become clouded by some insincere flattery from the other federation envoys.","“Once the harbor is expanded, the Startling Lines Continent’s three federations combined won’t be able to compare, much less the Great Lush Federation on its own. The harbor is meant to be the Radiance Federation’s gate to the rest of the world. It doesn’t have much to do with the Startling Lines Continent.","“You actually tried to dip your fingers into such an important entity. How do you think Lord Lin Yuan will feel about this? If I were you, I would immediately remove my men from around the harbor and then find the opportunity to explain myself to Lord Lin Yuan. If he decides to step in before that happens, you might lose the opportunity to salvage the situation!”","Buckets of cold sweat began dripping down Jin Qianxun’s back.","Luo Lan had given Jin Qianxun a similar warning in the past. However, she had not been as clear as she was now.","Jin Qianxun had been blinded by his desires back then as well.","But now, as the harbor’s construction came closer and closer to completion, Jin Qianxun realized that the Great Lush Federation did not have the ability to manage the harbor.","Jin Qianxun had already spent numerous lonely nights terrified by this realization.","Now, he no longer felt confident about gambling with his and the Jin family’s future.","“Luo Lan, you are the closest to Lord Lin Yuan. Please help me. What do I need to do to resolve this misunderstanding?”","Luo Lan fell silent instead of responding immediately. It was only when he repeated his question that she said, “I can’t give you an exact answer to this. It depends on your actions! Acting now might not earn the Lord’s forgiveness. But if you don’t act within the next week, you will have to pay the price for your greed!”","Luo Lan hung up upon saying that and stopped concerning herself with Jin Qianxun. She knew that Wen Yu had to be by Lin Yuan’s side now that he had some free time. She would definitely give him unfiltered reports of the recent happenings in the main world.","After learning of what had happened, Lin Yuan would certainly step in to handle the situation.","Luo Lan was still the one reporting to Wen Yu about the situation in the Startling Lines Continent.","...","As Jin Qianxun listened to the static sounds on the other end of the call and mulled over Luo Lan’s final words, he eventually called Jin Zhanming in hastily.","Jin Zhanming was still holding the tray of tea and snacks. Before he could place them on the table, Jin Qianxun said anxiously, “Zhanming, send out my order this instant. All the men stationed around the harbor are to be dismissed immediately. Let the harbor’s workers continue their work as usual! By tomorrow morning, I want it to look like the harbor is separate from the Great Lush Federation!”","Jin Zhanming had never seen Jin Qianxun in such a state. At that moment, his demeanor was slightly unbecoming for the Great Lush Federation’s ruler. However, this also showed just how urgent the matter was.","“Don’t worry, Your Majesty. I will send out your order right now!”","Jin Zhanming immediately went to work.","Jin Qianxun did not wait until the next morning when all of the Great Lush Federation’s forces had retreated from the harbor to contact Lin Yuan. Rather, once he composed himself, he immediately contacted Lin Yuan through the Thoughts Letter Paper.","Jin Qianxun never expected to get a response from Lin Yuan on the same day. Usually, whenever he contacted Lin Yuan, it took a very long time for him to get a reply!","Lin Yuan was not overly interested in what was going on with the harbor because he knew that the harbor and the entire Startling Lines Continent were under his control. If there were any issues, he would cleanly remove the source of the problems.","However, unless it was absolutely necessary, Lin Yuan did not want to swap out Jin Qianxun.","This was because Jin Qianxun had been doing a good job of governing the Great Lush Federation. He was also able to develop it in the right direction. Lin Yuan could not be certain that Jin Qianxun’s replacement would be equally as competent.","Moreover, Lin Yuan did feel some attachment to these people who had been with him for some time. If they committed errors but were able to see and fix their issues, Lin Yuan would give them a chance.","Jin Qianxun was one such example.","Lin Yuan did not know why Jin Qianxun suddenly changed, but all that mattered was that Jin Qianxun was able to see the error of his ways.","Lin Yuan replied to Jin Qianxun.","[Lin Yuan]: I am aware of your previous thoughts and motives. You don’t have to try to spin your ambition in a positive light. Having ambition isn’t a bad thing. However, it needs to be directed toward the correct objectives. If directed towards the wrong objectives, it will only lead to trouble. The Great Lush Federation doesn’t have the ability to take sole ownership of the harbor. I’m sure you have come to realize this.","[Lin Yuan]: In the future, a specific faction will manage the harbor. At the end of the day, the harbor is located in the Startling Lines Continent. The Divine Wood, Great Lush, and Iron Hammer Federations will be able to participate in its management. The three federations will share 30% of the profits from the harbor! This means that you will also need to take up the respective responsibility of managing the harbor!","Lin Yuan did not waste time reprimanding Jin Qianxun. This was the last chance he was giving him.","Wen Yu would send out her instructions tomorrow afternoon. At that time, white-clothed followers would take over the harbor’s supervision.","If the Great Lush Federation maintained control of the harbor upon the arrival of the white-clothed followers, Wen Yu’s directive was clear: eliminate Jin Qianxun immediately.","Jin Qianxun had essentially saved his own life.","Furthermore, Lin Yuan did not have to worry about Jin Qianxun forming harmful ambitions. If he did, Lin Yuan would not offer him any more chances.","After his conversation with Lin Yuan, Jin Qianxun’s gratitude toward Luo Lan increased exponentially. But at the same time, he was extremely happy.","Lin Yuan had decided to give 30% of the profits to the GDivine Wood, Great Lush, and Iron Hammer Federations.","After the harbor was expanded, it would be able to house at least 1,000 Island Whales. Even sharing 30% of the profits would allow each federation to earn enormous wealth!","Jin Qianxun felt that he needed to thank Luo Lan.","...","Lin Yuan was currently holding Merciful Soul.","Even after evolving to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, Merciful Soul still preferred not to be in human form. Rather, it took the form of a small beast that was about the size of the palm.","Merciful Soul wanted to cling to Lin Yuan at every moment.","Genius and Chimey were already very clingy. But neither of them could hold a candle to Merciful Soul.","At the Sky Beyond the Clouds...","In one of the halls of Honor Absent Palace, the ground was covered in a mess. Countless valuable items had been smashed to smithereens.","Kong Huan slammed her hand forcefully on one of the stone pillars in the hall.","Luckily, the stone pillars in the hall were all made of exceptionally sturdy stone. Otherwise, Kong Huan’s hand might have broken the stone pillar apart.","Kong Mu stood off the side. She dared not even take a breath. In truth, she felt every bit as furious as Kong Huan.","Kong Huan had been under the impression she had successfully recruited Fan Lou into her camp and turned this captain of a Boundary Patrol Team into her obedient servant.","She never expected him to betray her and join Feng Qing.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had even publicly announced that they were taking Fan Lou in as a relative.","Fan Lou was the crux of the search of the Class 2 world.","Kong Huan had invested considerable resources and used many favors to enable Fan Lou to become this expedition’s guide.","But now, all that she had spent had essentially become a dowry that she paid to Feng Qing.","Fan Lou did not hold any value of his own. The only reason to explain why Feng Qing saw so much value in Fan Lou was that the latter had revealed extremely important information.","Given that the information had been sufficient for Fan Lou to be taken in by the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves, it had to be related to the Class 2 world.","Meanwhile, since Fan Lou was no longer part of Kong Huan’s camp, how could he still hand over the resources he had promised to Kong Mu?","Kong Mu could not ask for resources from Kong Huan either.","If this matter was revealed, it would affect Kong Huan’s trust in her.","“Fan Lou is truly scum! I must make him pay! He better not think that things will be smooth sailing for him from now on just because he has become a relative of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves!”","Kong Huan’s voice was full of rage, and her fury was so intense that Kong Mu could not help but recoil."]},{"number":2769,"title":"Chapter 2769 Snow-Covered Fox Species!","paragraphs":["2769 Snow-Covered Fox Species!","At that moment, a clear voice echoed from outside the hall. “What Fan Lou is doing is akin to a bird nesting in the finest tree. You only provided Fan Lou with resources so you could earn profits for yourself. So there’s no need for you to be this outraged!”","Kong Huan was not very familiar with this voice. But after thinking for a moment, she recognized the owner of the voice.","Kong Huan narrowed her beautiful eyes.","Feng Qing had poached from her and stolen one of her subordinates. Now, he had come to strut around and reproach her!","Whether Fan Lou could be considered a talented individual was one matter. But what did Feng Qing mean by choosing the finest tree? Did he mean that he was one, but she wasn’t? Or was he trying to brandish the power of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves to suppress the Alluring Foxes?","Now that she was facing an expert who possessed comparable power to her, Kong Huan repressed her flaring fury.","She had guessed Feng Qing’s reason for coming to see her. It was likely he was there to save Fan Lou.","Before Kong Huan’s venture into the Class 2 world, she was under constant scrutiny, unable to act freely. However, Fan Lou would lose his significance in her plans upon her return, and no one would dare intervene or oppose her to defend someone as insignificant as him.","Kong Huan could see no reason for Feng Qing to come to see her for the sake of such an insignificant character.","This made Kong Huan feel that Feng Qing was slighting her!","“Feng Qing, there has never been any hostility between us. We even worked together in a few operations in the past. I never expected you to rob me of one of my subordinates! I was the one protecting the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team all these years. You should be aware of this!”","Kong Huan had deployed the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team in the presence of Feng Qing in a previous operation. Back then, Fan Lou had presented himself as Kong Huan’s servant.","Despite knowing that Fan Lou was her servant, Feng Qing had poached him from her and allowed Fan Lou to join the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","To Kong Huan, this was an insult to the highest degree.","By now, Feng Qing had entered the hall.","When Feng Qing saw Kong Huan’s enraged face, his lips curled slightly.","“So what if I’m aware? So what if I’m unaware? I spent a large sum of resources to poach Fan Lou. He made his choice of his own free will. It has nothing to do with me trying to poach from you!","“With all those profits within reach, even you would reach out to try to grab them! You have poached more people than I have over the years! What? You can poach from other leaders, but I can’t? That doesn’t make any sense!”","It was already a fact that Feng Qing had successfully poached Fan Lou and that the latter was now part of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves. After Fan Lou made his announcement, the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had issued proof of that. There was no way that Kong Huan would be able to get Fan Lou back.","Kong Huan wanted Feng Qing to compromise with her so it would be easier for her to collect resources from the Class 2 world. At the very least, Feng Qing would accept that he was in the wrong and offer her some sort of compensation.","Yet, not only did he refuse to meet her halfway, but he also chose to bite back stubbornly.","This caused Kong Huan’s repressed rage to erupt.","“Feng Qing, you must give me some sort of an answer for this matter! Otherwise, I will make you pay, even if it means I won’t be able to collect resources from the Class 2 world! You won’t make it there if I can’t go!”","Since Kong Huan failed to strike a deal, she threatened him.","With how strongly Feng Qing was standing up for Fan Lou, it was clear he had found out that faeries had been born in that Class 2 world.","Feng Qing wouldn’t give up on his plan to harvest resources from that Class 2 world.","If Feng Qing did not provide her with satisfactory compensation, Kong Huan would rather give up her profits than let him get off scot-free.","She could always tell the other members of Honor Absent Palace about the Class 2 world’s faeries. Once the powerful individuals learned of this, they would definitely become interested.","At that point, Feng Qing would no longer have the right to stir up turmoil!","Feng Qing’s expression did not change when he heard what Kong Huan said. It was as though he did not feel threatened by her words at all.","Feng Qing kept his gaze on Kong Huan’s enraged face as he said calmly, “I have already informed the Bloodians of this matter. They will be sending people to participate in this operation!","“If you ruin the Bloodians’ plan, the Alluring Foxes will experience a repeat of what happened to the mermaids. If that happens, you can’t blame me for not warning you!","“Given your love for the Alluring Foxes, I believe that you won’t reveal this secret! If you are willing to work with me when harvesting the resources, I will share some of the pie with you! I don’t do things in the same overbearing manner as the Bloodians. Otherwise, I wouldn’t have come here to see you!”","After mentioning the Bloodians, every word Feng Qing uttered sounded as though he only wanted what was best for Kong Huan. But in actuality, he was threatening her.","This became especially evident with his mention of the mermaids’ tragedy.","The war between the mermaids and Bloodians had resulted in the mermaids being kicked out of the East Universe’s Species Ranking. The mermaids had yet to regain their prosperity.","The Alluring Foxes’ strength in the East Universe could not be compared to the mermaids, much less the Bloodians!","If this was only a spat between the Alluring Foxes and Chaos Wind Demon Wolves, Kong Huan could take Feng Qing on without being overly worried. But since the Bloodians had been roped in, Kong Huan had no choice but to consider the Alluring Foxes’ safety!","The Bloodians consumed blood, so all species with vitality in their bodies could become their source of food.","If the Bloodians found a legitimate reason, they would be more than willing to conquer the lifeforms with vitality.","To the Bloodians, this was considered hunting.","Honor Absent Palace successfully maintained control over the Bloodians, ensuring they refrained from harming species they had acknowledged.","Honor Absent Palace was the dominant faction in the East Universe of the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Regardless of how strong the Bloodians were, they had no choice but to listen to Honor Absent Palace’s orders.","But if any grudges were formed, or there were any fights over profits, the Bloodians would have a reason to make their move.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had betrayed the Moon-Worshiping Wolves, severing their allegiance. Despite harboring resentment, the Moon-Worshiping Wolves refrained from retaliation, as the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had allied with the Bloodians and secured their protection.","Contemplating the altered situation, Kong Huan opted to control her anger. To ensure the safety of the Alluring Foxes, she reluctantly portrayed a vulnerable facade in the presence of Feng Qing.","Typically, considering her personality, Kong Huan would cease interactions with Feng Qing after feigning vulnerability. However, if the Class 2 realm proved to be rich in resources or harbored valuable treasures, the Alluring Foxes could gain a share of the profits. Any amount would be preferable to leaving with nothing at all!","“Feng Qing, I won’t cause any more trouble for Fan Lou. During this operation, my people will listen to your orders. But I hope that you will keep your promise and provide me with all the resources I deserve!”","Feng Qing was very happy with Kong Huan’s reply.","When Feng Qing saw the indignant but helpless expression on Kong Huan’s face, he was extremely satisfied.","This was not the first time that Feng Qing was mentioning the Bloodians in front of a member of the Honor Absent Parliament. This was a very effective card!","Feng Qing had always been skilled at using his connections to achieve his objectives.","With the looming terror of the Bloodians, there were many species ranked below the top 1,000 of the Species Ranking who needed to take the safety of their species into consideration.","Feng Qing would ask the Bloodians for fighters but would not report the exact production volume of resources of that Class 2 world to them.","The people Feng Qing sent would work with Fan Lou to store away the most precious of the resources. Even if he had to pay the Bloodians under the table, he would still be able to earn astronomical profits!","After Feng Qing left Kong Huan’s palace, she punched another stone pillar in a fit of fury.","The instant her fist collided with the stone pillar, the alluring image of a beautiful fox appeared behind her. Cracks even appeared on the foundation of the stone pillar.","Bright red blood with flecks of pink appeared on Kong Huan’s fist.","Kong Mu was so frightened that she hurriedly went up to Kong Huan.","“Lordess, no matter how angry you are, you can’t hurt yourself! Feng Qing is outright bullying us. Do you think we need to have a discussion with the Elders about this?","“Don’t forget that the Snow-Covered Fox species has been trying to form ties with us in the hopes that we will relocate the Alluring Foxes to the North Universe.","“They promise that the Alluring Foxes will gain a seat in Glow Evoking Palace’s parliament within the next 400 years! That will give the Alluring Foxes a similar status in the North Universe to what we currently hold in the East Universe!”","Kong Mu was Kong Huan’s aide and knew a lot of information.","Normally, Kong Mu would not say this much. But this time, there was no avenue for Kong Huan to vent her overwhelming anger. If she did not demonstrate her value, it was highly possible that Kong Huan would vent her anger on her!","Kong Huan’s eyes flashed when she heard what Kong Mu said, and she began thinking deeply.","The Snow-Covered Foxes of the North Universe had extended their first invitation to the Alluring Foxes more than 200 years ago. This matter had been the cause of many debates during the Alluring Foxes’ meetings. However, they always decided against the migration.","This was not because the Snow-Covered Foxes’ terms were not tempting, but because there were many uncertain factors to moving away from a universe they had settled so well into and lived in for so long.","If the Alluring Foxes moved to the North Universe, they would essentially be betraying Honor Absent Palace and would never be able to return to the East Universe.","However, the Alluring Foxes’ roots had always been in the East Universe.","But now, the Alluring Foxes were under threat from the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","Given the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves’ style, using the Bloodians as a successful threat once would lead to them repeating this method.","Kong Huan could represent the Alluring Foxes as a member of the Honor Absent Palace’s parliament because she possessed a special divine kingdom ability—it allowed her to use her energy to block the detection of world wills.","This divine kingdom ability did not have any use during combat, so Kong Huan had yet to utilize it.","However, she could use this divine kingdom ability to head to the Class 2 world first.","In the past, she hesitated to undertake this task because if her actions were exposed, not only would Honor Absent Palace impose punishment, but it would also lead to the implication of all the Alluring Foxes!","But now, she wanted to use her divine kingdom ability to enter the Class 2 world ahead of the others.","This idea had popped into her mind because she now saw the Snow-Covered Foxes as a safety net for the Alluring Foxes.","The Snow-Covered Foxes were almost permanently part of the top 100 of the North Universe’s Species Ranking. At their prime, they made it to 19th on the Species Ranking and left snow wherever they went.","The Snow-Covered Foxes had taken in other fox-species from other universes in the past. All of these fox-species had become their dependent species.","This was a similar relationship to the one between the Light Wind Wolves and Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","Those that became the Snow-Covered Foxes’ dependent species were all living in relative comfort.","The Alluring Foxes were more attractive to fox-species lifeforms than other lifeforms.","While the Alluring Foxes were communicating with the Snow-Covered Foxes, it was likely that they would be treated favorably.","“Kong Mu, go and contact the Elders so we can hold a meeting. Also, send people to visit the Snow-Covered Fox envoy. I will personally arrange the personnel that will be heading to the Class 2 world. You don’t have to worry about this matter anymore!”","Kong Mu was unaware of Kong Huan’s divine kingdom ability.","But now, Kong Huan wanted to hold a meeting with the Elders and contact the Snow-Covered Fox envoy. Was she going to take her up on her suggestion?","This filled Kong Mu with delight. If Kong Huan truly used her suggestion, she would definitely be handsomely rewarded in the future.","It was said that the Snow-Covered Foxes were all tall and charismatic men with hair more luscious than that of other fox-species.","If she managed to marry one of the Snow-Covered Foxes, her future would be a bright one!","Once Kong Huan decided to become one of the Snow-Covered Foxes’ dependent species, she stopped fearing the Bloodians.","Although the Bloodians’ might was notorious across the four universes, the Bloodians in the East Universe did not have close connections with the dependent species in the other universes.","The Bloodians prioritized bloodline. This did not refer to the bloodline of all the Bloodians but the legacy of a powerful bloodline.","When the Bloodians hunted other species, they worked as a team. Internally, they functioned as a family.","The Bloodians of the East Universe did not want the Bloodians of other universes to leave their bloodlines in the East Universe as it would taint their bloodline.","The infighting within the Bloodians was that of competing bloodlines.","The Bloodians of the North Universe did not possess as much power as the Snow-Covered Foxes.","The Snow-Covered Foxes’ Frozen physiques allowed them to summon snow that effectively countered the Bloodians’ blood-type enchantments.","Half of the Alluring Foxes’ Elders wanted to migrate while the other half wanted to continue developing in the East Universe.","Kong Huan had been supporting the side that wanted to remain in the East Universe.","If she told the Elders about how the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were threatening them and that the Bloodians were involved, the Elders who wanted to stay would definitely change their minds.","Now, Kong Huan needed to come up with a way to use her own power to capture all the resources from the Class 2 world and bring them with her to the North Universe.","The resources would be able to help the Alluring Foxes with their development and could also be used as gifts to earn the favor of the Snow-Covered Foxes. This would allow the Alluring Foxes to be protected by the Snow-Covered Foxes in the North Universe and improve their standard of living."]},{"number":2770,"title":"Chapter 2770 Arrival of the Visitors From the Sky Beyond the Clouds","paragraphs":["2770 Arrival of the Visitors From the Sky Beyond the Clouds","“Lordess Kong Huan, I will go and contact the Elders now and hold a meeting. I will also liaise with the Snow-Covered Fox envoy! I was present when we greeted him, so I am somewhat acquainted with him.”","When Kong Mu saw the expression on Kong Huan’s face, she knew that Kong Huan had made her decision.","Hence, Kong Mu was now doing her best to claim resources for herself.","If she represented the Alluring Foxes and liaised with the Snow-Covered Fox envoy, she would be able to stand out.","Even if she did not manage to seduce the envoy, she would be able to leave a deep impression on him. This would allow her to tap into this connection once she went to the North Universe.","The envoy’s journey to another universe highlighted his significant status among the Snow-Covered Foxes.","Kong Huan cast a glance at Kong Mu, fully aware of the plan unfolding in her mind.","Each Alluring Fox could be characterized as egotistic.","Kong Mu aspired to represent the Alluring Foxes in engaging with the envoy, hoping to establish a meaningful connection.","However, her status fell short, not reaching the level that would qualify her to interact with the envoy directly.","Typically, only a direct descendant of the Alluring Foxes could liaise with the Snow-Covered Fox envoy.","Surprisingly, Kong Huan not only didn’t oppose Kong Mu’s proposal but also intended to endorse her.","Kong Mu, a closely nurtured subordinate, belonged to Kong Huan’s circle of profits within the Alluring Foxes.","Discontent among many Alluring Foxes toward Kong Huan had risen in recent years. Her membership in the Honor Absent Parliament hadn’t brought substantial profits to the Alluring Foxes.","Kong Huan was aware of that.","This was not because she did not want to contribute to the Alluring Foxes but because Honor Absent Palace had been extremely messy in recent years. There were always bigshots fighting with each other. Kong Huan was afraid that trying to obtain profits for the Alluring Foxes would result in her becoming embroiled in the conflict.","Stability was key to survival in such a complex environment.","This was in spite of there constantly being members of the Alluring Foxes who used this as an excuse to attack her.","Previously, Kong Huan did not agree to migrate to the North Universe because she was worried that doing so would destabilize her position.","In the East Universe, she was a member of the Honor Absent Parliament. But when they went to the North Universe, there was a high likelihood that another Alluring Fox would become a member of the Glow Evoking Parliament.","Kong Huan did not plan on using Kong Mu to get closer to the Snow-Covered Fox envoy. After all, he was not one of the true decision-makers.","In order to secure her position in the North Universe, she would have to form close ties with the Snow-Covered Foxes’ main members.","Aside from making use of the Alluring Foxes’ current resources, Kong Huan also intended to leverage the resources she collected from the Class 2 world.","Kong Huan’s divine kingdom ability allowed her to hide from the detection of world wills and escape their restraints.","She could use her power freely when she arrived at the Class 2 world.","Someone from the Sky Beyond the Clouds searching a Class 2 world was against regulations.","If they employed too much power and caused the world to collapse, Honor Absent Palace would be targeted by the factions from the other three universes. The bigshots from Honor Absent Palace would never permit something like this to happen.","The last time something like this happened, five members of Honor Absent Parliament were kicked out.","This time, even if Feng Qing sought help from the Bloodians, the latter would not provide help that was beyond World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","In Kong Huan’s eyes, such power was not worth mentioning.","In order to cover her tracks, Kong Huan decided to kill all the people who were going to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. This would include Fan Lou, who had betrayed her.","Kong Huan wanted to crush all of Fan Lou’s bones and scatter them in one of the Class 2 world’s volcanoes. This was the only way to quench the hatred in her heart!","Kong Huan took out a ring with an outdated design and a pink and purple stone embedded in it.","When she held the ring with both hands, Kong Huan’s body disappeared instantly, and the ring clattered onto the table’s surface.","The ring shook lightly a moment later, and Kong Huan’s body reappeared.","Kong Huan placed the ring on her finger with satisfaction.","This ring made from World Wall Crimson Gold and Mirage Stone was truly perplexing. The World Wall Crimson Gold would create a stable space that teleportation could not destabilize. Mirage Stone was a gem that the Alluring Foxes in the Sky Beyond the Clouds often used as an accessory. The female Alluring Foxes used them as accessories or wore them in their hair.","If the warrior she dispatched was wearing a ring with a Mirage Stone, no one would bat an eyelid.","Kong Huan could hide in the ring and follow the warrior to the Class 2 world.","Once she fully investigated the Class 2 world, Kong Huan would swoop in to attain victory and obtain all the resources in that Class 2 world!","Collecting all the resources from a Class 2 world was difficult. It would take a long time for Kong Huan to do it all on her own.","In her eyes, every person on the team was labor that she could use. Regardless of whether these people had hidden resources away, the resources would all end up being owned by her once she eliminated them!","...","Kong Huan returned to the Alluring Foxes’ base and participated in a meeting of the inner circle.","Kong Mu had been interacting with the Snow-Covered Fox envoy. She was ready at any moment to receive an order from Kong Huan and seal a partnership with the Snow-Covered Foxes.","Almost 200 years had passed since Han Rong left the North Universe and came to the East Universe.","Envoys like him had to return to give a report every 300 years.","At first, Han Rong assumed that nothing would come out from this trip to the East Universe. Yet, right as he was due to return, he received such a piece of good news.","There were not many members of the Snow-Covered Foxes. They were able to achieve a high ranking on the Species Ranking because all their adult members possessed exceptional power.","Powerful species like them that also had a small population liked to take in dependent species and use them to increase their power.","The more dependent species an envoy roped in for the Snow-Covered Foxes, the higher their status would be.","Han Rong had his eye on four fox-species in the East Universe. Three of them had turned him down. The Alluring Foxes were the only ones who had yet to firmly express their rejection.","Han Rong could sense that the Alluring Foxes were leading him on.","Under normal circumstances, Han Rong would typically venture farther to explore additional fox-species instead of lingering around the Alluring Foxes. Exploring distant regions might lead him to the discovery of even more fox-species.","Yet, Han Rong held great expectations for the Alluring Foxes. They possessed all the captivating qualities of a fox, and other foxes were naturally drawn to them. This allure targeted the senses rather than the intellect.","If he managed to bring the Alluring Foxes to the North Universe, they would undoubtedly stand out amidst the myriad dependent species of the Snow-Covered Foxes. There was even a possibility that a prominent Snow-Covered Fox elite might consider taking one of the Alluring Foxes as a mate to continue their bloodline. To the Snow-Covered Foxes, a potent dependent species held the same value as another elite member of their own kind.","Regardless of how strong the dependent species were, they would receive protection from the Snow-Covered Foxes.","The special fox-species were the ones that truly attracted the attention of the Snow-Covered Foxes.","The Alluring Foxes could be considered one such special fox-species.","Since the Alluring Foxes were initiating contact with him, it meant that they were open to the idea of moving to the North Universe.","Han Rong had already been waiting for almost 200 years. He could handle waiting for a little while more. This was so long as the Alluring Foxes gave him an answer before he returned home.","Han Rong could tell that the Alluring Foxes wanted to negotiate with him. However, he would not make it easy for them because the Snow-Covered Foxes did not give much authority to their envoys.","Han Rong could not promise much.","If he was unable to fulfill his promises, the Alluring Foxes would riot once they migrated to the North Universe. This would affect his reputation among the Snow-Covered Foxes.","There were a few envoys who had given false promises and had been hounded by the dependent species who wanted to collect on the promises made.","Han Rong was relatively friendly to Kong Mu after finding out she was only Kong Huan’s aide.","However, Han Rong did not host her personally.","Powerful species prioritized status.","Han Rong felt that Kong Mu did not deserve to liaise with him.","Han Rong would not use force on the Alluring Foxes before they migrated to the North Universe. But once they went there, not only would the Alluring Foxes have to keep their heads down, but their backs had to be bent too!","If the Alluring Foxes were obedient and had a few exceptional individuals, they could receive the favor of the Snow-Covered Foxes’ top level. This would also inflate the Alluring Foxes’ status.","It was possible that even he would have to end up trying to curry favor with them!","...","When Kong Huan left the Alluring Foxes’ base and headed to Honor Absent Palace she took two warriors with her.","Kong Huan’s expression was extremely sour.","Although she had facilitated the decision to move the Alluring Foxes from the East Universe to the North Universe, she realized that her status was a shadow of what it used to be.","The other branches of the Alluring Foxes were becoming increasingly brazen.","If they were fighting back against her for no reason, she could suppress them without holding back.","However, they had found a legitimate reason. The other branches had members whose bloodlines had reached the Alluring Bone grade.","The Alluring Bone bloodline would extend the Alluring Fox’s charms past the superficial appearance.","It was said that beauty was in the bones and not the skin.","Once they reached the Alluring Bones grade, the Alluring Fox’s aura would be renewed.","Kong Huan’s bloodline was pinnacle Alluring Bones.","Kong Huan was unable to find a reason to suppress the branch bloodlines because they had gained confidence and power from their improved bloodlines. If she tried to suppress them, it would seem as though Kong Huan’s branch was petty. This was unbecoming behavior for a superior!","Kong Huan pondered over how she would manage the Alluring Foxes in the future.","She needed to have perfect control over the Alluring Foxes before they went to the North Universe. This way, the Alluring Foxes would be united when they arrived at the North Universe.","...","In the Radiance Federation, the sky was clear, and the weather was perfect. Wisps of clouds flowed through the sky, occasionally clustering into clumps before quickly evaporating by the sun’s rays.","It was difficult to maintain self-discipline when the weather was this hot and the Radiance citizens were all on summer vacation.","The Radiance Federation’s sea trade had been fully established. Hence, the Radiance citizens who had recovered from the trauma of the dead spirits crisis were now riding boats to travel and visit the other cities.","In the past, only spirit qi professionals were capable of crossing cities. The regular people rarely had the opportunity to leave the city where they lived.","But now that the boats had replaced the Island Whales and the seas were safe, travel became a pastime that regular people could enjoy.","The economic growth of the Radiance Federation’s cities was propelled by travel. Cities boasting unique environments, where the production of feys and spiritual ingredients was relatively low, emerged as popular tourism hotspots.","Lin Yuan felt a sense of accomplishment as he listened to Wen Yu describe this occurrence.","He held the belief that within the next three to five years, or at most a decade, tourism would extend beyond a handful of cities in one federation and span across various federations.","Aside from tasting good food and enjoying beautiful scenery, experiencing culture was also an important part of tourism. Scholars valued culture far more than food and scenery.","...","After the white-clothed followers took over the harbor in the Startling Lines Continent, the harbor’s management became organized.","The people from other federations also realized that the Great Lush Federation did not have any authority to manage the harbor. As a result, they stopped trying to curry favor with Jin Qianxun.","Jin Qianxun was slightly disappointed by this, but he was also glad. He was glad that Luo Lan’s warning had allowed him to save his own life.","In order to express his gratitude to Luo Lan, Jin Qianxun promised her substantial private benefits. However, she did not accept them.","She resisted not because she lacked interest in his offer but because she understood Lin Yuan’s desire for a balanced distribution of power among the Divine Wood, Great Lush, and Iron Hammer Federations. Lin Yuan aimed to prevent scenarios where the Great Lush Federation could form exclusive alliances with the Iron Hammer Federation. Knowing his intentions, she saw no reason for actions that might upset him.","...","When Spring and Summer first started following Lin Yuan around, they did not think much of life in the main world. They did not think that a Class 2 world’s culture could be overly impressive.","But after tasting Liu Jie’s delicacies, Spring and Summer became slaves to gourmet food.","Slowly, they assimilated to life in the Radiance Federation.","There were many things that might seem unacceptable at first that could be slowly accepted after giving them a shot.","After learning that Sky City was a faction that Lin Yuan had built personally, the two of them even donned Sky City’s uniform.","...","After promoting Wen Yu to an S-rank spirit qi professional, Lin Yuan did the same with Liu Jie.","From now on, Liu Jie could continuously evolve Elegance’s grade and quality and strengthen his insect-species carcinoma feys!","As Lin Yuan contemplated visiting the Moon Empress to potentially elevate her spirit qi professional rank, he discerned a sudden shift in the auras of Spring and Summer.","Their attention was fixed on the domed roof above them!"]},{"number":2771,"title":"Chapter 2771 Slaughter Riding on the Abyss Beast!","paragraphs":["2771 Slaughter Riding on the Abyss Beast!","Lin Yuan looked up to the distance where Spring and Summer’s gazes were now fixed.","Lin Yuan was rather nervous.","He was used to relying on himself for everything and had become accustomed to his own style of handling matters.","But now, he needed to rely on Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter to take on the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds. He was not capable of taking them on.","Hence, he would have no choice but to accept the final result, regardless of what it was.","Despite knowing that the four of them would never lie to him and had already given him their assurances, Lin Yuan still could not calm down.","After all, the invasion of the main world by the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds jeopardized the survival of the main world.","Spring soon shifted her gaze away from the distance and smiled at Lin Yuan. “Lord Saint, the people from the East Universe are riding an Abyss Beast. Only people from Honor Absent Palace are capable of using teleporting Abyss Beasts as a mode of transportation.","“Aside from Honor Absent Palace, the other factions might be capable of capturing the Abyss Beasts but are unable to tame them.","“Winter has used his aura to lock onto the Abyss Beast. Once the Abyss Beast arrives in this Class 2 world, it will be captured along with all the lifeforms riding on it. You will be able to control all of them!","“Unlike your expectations, it won’t be an obvious conflict. It will be akin to the spirit-fire experts from your world taking control of D-rank spirit qi professionals. It won’t cause a fuss at all!”","Spring had likened Winter to a spirit-fire expert and the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds as D-rank spirit qi professionals. It was clear that despite not knowing how powerful these people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds were, Spring was not concerned by them in the slightest.","The people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds were aware that there was more than one World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform in this Class 2 world. Hence, the lifeforms from the Sky Beyond the Clouds who had come to the main world had to possess World Emperor/Divine Kingdom power, at the very least!","Spring’s attitude allowed Lin Yuan to relax significantly.","Suddenly, Lin Yuan felt clear energy fluctuations coming from the distance.","However, it did not take long before this energy was enveloped and blocked by other energy torrents.","Winter’s soul voice was transmitted to Lin Yuan’s mind a moment later.","“Lord Saint, I have already helped you to capture all the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Are you going to interrogate them yourself?”","Winter paused before continuing. “There is internal strife among these people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Many of them were killed before I took control of them. Only 17 of them are still alive.”","Lin Yuan’s eyes flashed when he heard that. It seemed that the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds saw the main world as a slab of mouth-watering meat that they were all eager to gobble up! As a result, some of them lost patience during the journey and eliminated their rivals.","Lin Yuan’s guess was right.","However, the conflict that had taken place on the Abyss Beast’s back was not the result of a carefully premeditated plan but an accident.","Before the departure...","Feng Qing, having taken Fan Lou under his wing, didn’t permit him unrestricted freedom. Recognizing the significance of Fan Lou’s secrets, Feng Qing securely kept him by his side. Fan Lou was only granted permission to depart when it was time for him to guide the group to the Class 2 world.","Feng Qing blocked all other members of the Honor Absent Parliament who sought to explore the Class 2 world and dispatched individuals to reach out to Fan Lou.","Feng Qing had contacted the Bloodians, and they sent two outstanding World Emperor/Divine Kingdom experts to help him.","Feng Qing checked these two experts’ strength himself. Once he ascertained that their strength met his standards, Feng Qing finally set all his worries to rest.","The only other person who was aware of this, Kong Huan, had also sent people to help him.","Feng Qing did not believe that the Alluring Foxes were capable of causing impactful problems.","Earlier...","Fan Lou had been in a very good mood of late.","He never expected he would one day become a member of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","Feng Qing had visited Kong Huan on his behalf. This cruel ex-mistress of his would no longer come after him.","According to Feng Qing, as long as things went well, he would be able to remain by Feng Qing’s side as his close aide.","He would have a much easier time working for a member of the Honor Absent Parliament like Feng Qing than working as a Boundary Patrol Envoy.","Boundary Patrol Envoys often encountered danger while they were patrolling the Class 1, 2, and 3 worlds.","With so many members of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team dead, Fan Lou could not help but feel an aversion to being a Boundary Patrol Envoy. He did not want to become the next sacrificial lamb who lost his life while searching the lower worlds.","Due to the fact that a Class 2 world’s world wills had strong repulsion, the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds intentionally chose a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Abyss Beast, which had an acceptable level of power for a Class 2 world.","Since Fan Lou was the only guide, there was no point in sending more Abyss Beasts when he could only ride on one.","The Alluring Foxes were aware that Fan Lou had betrayed Kong Huan. The two Alluring Fox warriors came from the same branch as Kong Huan and were not courteous toward Fan Lou at all. They verbally insulted him numerous times.","Fan Lou did not comment on this.","In truth, he still deeply feared the Alluring Foxes. After all, he had been working for them for so many years.","But now that the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had acknowledged his identity, despite not being a main member, he was still a relative whom Feng Qing had personally recruited.","Fan Lou could endure the two Alluring Foxes’ verbal insults, but the two Chaos Wind Demon Wolves accompanying him could not.","The Bloodians didn’t intervene in the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves’ conflicts with other species solely due to their strong connection. Instead, it was their disdain for the Alluring Foxes’ unrestrained auras.","A dog’s behavior was a reflection of its owner.","It was not a secret in the East Universe that the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had the Bloodians’ protection. The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves would never have been able to break free from the Moon-Worshiping Wolves without their help.","By continuing to pick fights with the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves despite knowing this, the Alluring Foxes were disrespecting the Bloodians.","When did the Alluring Foxes become so daring?","Normally, the Alluring Foxes had better control over their tempers.","However, these two Alluring Foxes were harboring too much displeasure against Fan Lou. Moreover, they knew that the Alluring Foxes intended to migrate to the North Universe and saw no need to remain courteous toward the East Universe’s native factions.","The two Alluring Foxes never expected the Bloodians to strike.","Compared to other divine-kingdom experts, the Bloodians possessed unparalleled combat power.","The two Alluring Foxes were no match for them. Hence, they were soon grievously injured by the Bloodians.","The two Alluring Foxes had no idea that Kong Huan was hiding in the ring.","However, Kong Huan knew what was happening outside of the ring.","It went without saying that Kong Huan could not allow these two Alluring Foxes from her branch to die. This operation was far too important, and one of the two warriors chosen was Kong Huan’s direct relative.","Hence, Kong Huan had no choice but to abandon her original plan and save the two Alluring Foxes from the Bloodians, thereby exposing herself.","In order to prevent news of this from reaching the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Kong Huan had no choice but to kill all the lifeforms on the Abyss Beast.","Once she rode the Abyss Beast back to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, she would need to think about whether to eliminate this Abyss Beast.","Kong Huan’s appearance startled the two Bloodians.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves looked at Fan Lou suspiciously. They could not help but suspect that he was still involved with Kong Huan and was deceiving the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","Kong Huan did not say much after making her appearance. She immediately demonstrated her power and killed one of the Bloodians while heavily injuring the other.","The experts from other species who had arrived at the Class 2 world were just bystanders, taken aback by the sudden presence of Kong Huan, a member of the Honor Absent Parliament. They hadn’t anticipated she would start killing.","They were about to arrive at the boundary where the influence of the Class 2 world’s world wills began. Was Kong Huan not worried that releasing her power would cause the Class 2 world to collapse?","In spite of the questions and admonishments, Kong Huan did not hold back.","She continued even when they reached the boundary where the influence of the Class 2 world’s world wills began.","Kong Huan looked at the two severely injured Alluring Foxes behind her. She only relaxed when she felt certain that their lives were not in any danger.","These two juniors in her branch harbored the highest hopes of advancing their bloodline to the Alluring Bones grade. Kong Huan, aware that she would be present to supervise, had tasked them with the mission as part of their training.","Kong Huan knew that the Alluring Foxes’ self-healing capabilities were inferior to those of other species. Her plan was to wait until they reached the Class 2 world before seeking resources to address injuries.","Before Feng Qing approached Kong Huan on his behalf, Fan Lou speculated on various ways Kong Huan might seek revenge. However, even in his worst-case scenario, he never foresaw her arrival on the Abyss Beast bound for the Class 2 world.","Kong Huan even dared to kill the Bloodians supporting the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves. There was no question she would not hesitate to kill him!","Fan Lou was frozen with fear.","With his knowledge of Kong Huan’s power, Fan Lou did not have any thoughts of resisting.","Kong Huan did not rush into attacking Fan Lou. If she killed him so quickly, she would be letting him off too easily! She intended to take her time dealing with him once they arrived at the Class 2 world.","The most pressing matter at hand was to take control of all the other experts on the Abyss Beast. Once they arrived at the Class 2 world and these people fled, it would be difficult to search for all of them!","After killing so many members of other species, the others would never obediently come to her when she tried searching for them!","Since that was the case, Kong Huan decided to do her best to kill as many experts on the Abyss Beast as possible before they arrived at the Class 2 world.","She might not be able to control the experts from other species, but she could form a trade with this World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Abyss Beast.","Abyss Beasts were akin to slaves. As long as she promised this Abyss Beast sufficient profits, it would not mind betraying its old master.","But whether she eventually fulfilled her promise would depend on her mood.","Kong Huan rarely had the opportunity to kill since becoming a member of the Honor Absent Parliament.","This slaughter had reignited the viciousness within her.","Fan Lou fell into despair as he watched Kong Huan’s mindless slaughter.","He was about the same distance from Kong Huan as the two dead Bloodians had been.","Kong Huan’s reason for not killing him yet was obvious.","Fan Lou did not dare to think about all the ways in which Kong Huan would be torturing him.","Kong Huan was strong enough to threaten the life of this Abyss Beast, which quickly agreed to her request. It created a shield around itself to prevent the warriors from other species from fleeing once they arrived.","More and more experts fell to the bloodshed, and Kong Huan had used up the majority of her physical energy.","She fully relaxed when she saw the more than ten heavily injured fallen experts.","Kong Huan looked up, her eyes shooting deadly glares.","When Kong Huan laid her eyes on Fan Lou, he fell to his knees in fright.","At that instant, everything was cemented and frozen by a certain might.","Kong Huan realized she could not move a single muscle in her body while she was shrouded in this might.","A few flakes of snow landed on the Abyss Beast and every lifeform was on its back. All of their bodies were covered in a layer of ice-like snow.","A thought formed in Kong Huan’s mind before she lost consciousness.","Even if the individuals from Honor Absent Palace colluded and used their full strength, they would not be able to generate this level of power. How could such a powerful lifeform exist in this Class 2 world? Why didn’t this Class 2 world’s world wills break because of this lifeform’s power?","...","After receiving the transmission of Winter’s soul voice, Lin Yuan was silent for a moment before he said, “Spring, send a soul transmission to Winter on my behalf. Tell him to bring all the captured experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds to Epoch God Palace. We will leave for Epoch God Palace immediately!”"]},{"number":2772,"title":"Chapter 2772 The Moon Empress’ Breakthrough!","paragraphs":["2772 The Moon Empress’ Breakthrough!","Normally, it would be much more convenient for Lin Yuan if Winter brought the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds to the Radiance Federation or even the Startling Lines Continent.","However, he chose not to do so because he was still worried.","If the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds escaped Winter’s control, it would unleash destruction upon the Radiance Federation and Startling Lines Continent.","Lin Yuan had World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys now and knew how shocking and terrifying their strength could be. It was possible that one misstep would result in an explosion of might that decimated half of the Radiance Federation.","Lin Yuan had accepted his identity as the Saint, so Epoch God Palace could also be regarded as his residence. It was undeniably more appropriate to address the invaders there.","After receiving Lin Yuan’s instruction, Spring immediately contacted Winter.","From this matter, Spring gained a better understanding of how important the Class 2 world was to Lin Yuan. She also began to value the Class 2 world even more.","Perhaps Lin Yuan felt an affection for this Class 2 world itself and not just a specific group of its inhabitants. This was an affection that Spring could not understand.","In a complex environment like the Sky Beyond the Clouds, few species staked their claim on territory and were worshiped by other species.","Most roamed around like nomads. It was difficult for them to breed affection for a specific location because they were mostly guided by opportunities and blessings when they moved around. Hence, the various species were more fond of opportunities and areas of blessing.","Winter was not concerned by the internal conflict that had taken place among the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Hence, he only mentioned that this event had taken place but did not describe the scene on the Abyss Beast’s back in detail.","Spring thought things through much more thoroughly than Winter did and had also been with Lin Yuan the longest out of the four of them. She knew that Lin Yuan liked to have control over everything.","Hence, she intentionally asked more questions.","After comprehending the situation, Spring said, “Lord Saint, the people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds arrived in this Class 2 world riding on a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Abyss Beast. Due to the special properties of world wills, the Class 2 world will only be able to accept World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeforms at the very most.","“If lifeforms beyond Intermediate Divine Kingdom arrive here, they will be in conflict with the world wills and could cause the world to crumble. Hence, these people should only be of the Intermediate Divine Kingdom level. But if they all had this level of power, a fight wouldn’t have broken out.","“Someone used their divine kingdom ability to escape the repulsion of the world wills. This means their power has reached the Pinnacle Higher Divine Kingdom level. It was this person who killed 3/4 of the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds.”","Lin Yuan looked surprised when he heard that. But soon, he asked Spring anxiously, “This person is using their divine kingdom ability to block the world wills. Will they affect the world wills if they stop using their divine kingdom ability?”","Lin Yuan was the most concerned about the main world’s safety.","Spring nodded seriously.","“You’re correct. If that person ceases using their divine kingdom ability and unleashes their full power, the world will soon succumb!","“Fortunately, she maintained her divine kingdom ability until captured by Winter. It’s probable she ventured into the Class 2 world in search of potential treasures. She must be unaware that you’re the catalyst for the birth of faeries and the emergence of World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeforms here. She wouldn’t consider destroying this world until securing the treasures.","“Additionally, as per the agreement among the four universes, members from higher-class worlds aren’t permitted to harm lower-class worlds.","“Once Winter takes control of her, he can employ his aura to conceal her from the world wills’ detection, even if she ceases using her divine kingdom ability. It’s akin to the centuries we spent waiting for you when this was a Class 1 world, using our aura to elude the world wills’ notice.”","Lin Yuan laid all his worries to rest when he heard what Spring said.","It was likely that World Emperor/Pinnacle Higher Divine Kingdom experts held considerable status in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","This level of power suited the magnitude that Lin Yuan wanted to control.","Apart from this expert, Lin Yuan was also very interested in the other invaders who were still alive.","Lin Yuan finally had the opportunity to interact with lifeforms from the Sky Beyond the Clouds in close proximity.","Recently, Lin Yuan had been investigating his body composition.","He had discovered that he could not only help feys and spirit qi professionals to increase their strength, but it could also absorb and temper the bloodlines of various species to strengthen them within his body. This would enable the bloodlines to improve continuously.","When Lin Yuan circulated a bloodline he had absorbed, he could even take on some of its properties.","This was similar to the mermaid bloodline.","Before Lin Yuan activated his body composition, he assumed that the mermaid bloodline was suppressing his original human bloodline.","But now that he had awakened the Body of All Spirits, the mermaid bloodline had become subordinate to his Body of All Spirits and was a tool he could utilize.","If the dead dimensional lifeforms did not have such an inferior bloodline, Lin Yuan would have absorbed their bloodline.","Most of the invaders from the Sky Beyond the Clouds had been killed.","They all came from different species, so Lin Yuan could extract their bloodlines and select the best few to absorb and temper in his body.","Lin Yuan called the Moon Empress before he left for Epoch God Palace. However, the call was answered by Mystic Moon.","Once he picked up the call, Lin Yuan could sense there was something off about Mystic Moon. The latter was a laid-back sort of person and interacting with him was a form of enjoyment.","Now, all the danger in the main world had been eliminated, and it was unlikely that Mystic Moon was unaware of the situation in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","For Mystic Moon to be this tense, it could only be because the Moon Empress was experiencing problems.","Lin Yuan’s expression turned stern as he asked, “Uncle Mystic, is Master in some sort of trouble? If she is, you can just tell me!”","Mystic Moon was still tense, but his expression was slightly more relaxed than before.","“Young Lord, the Moon Empress is in seclusion. She is trying to use Forage Moon’s power to reach the spirit-fire level.","“Forage Moon’s power can be directly applied on the Moon Empress. However, only a few years have passed since the Moon Empress awakened her birth horoscope. It isn’t safe for her to use Forage Moon’s power to try to reach the spirit-fire level now. There is a high chance that her roots will be damaged. But I can’t persuade her to do otherwise!”","Mystic Moon understood the Moon Empress’ temper and character. He knew that she felt an urgent desire to increase her power.","Mystic Moon did not dare to ask Lin Yuan to persuade the Moon Empress to give up on the idea of breaking through to the spirit-fire level. However, he had already expressed the message he wanted to get across.","He hoped that the Moon Empress could achieve a breakthrough but did not want her to be in any peril.","Currently, given the state of the main world and Radiance Federation, there was no need for the Moon Empress to put herself through any danger. Now that the main world had entered a period of peace, there was no storm that the Moon Empress needed to address by increasing her power.","This was unlike in the past when the Freedom Federation was constantly targeting the Radiance Federation, or when the main world was facing the dead spirits crisis, which threatened to destroy the entire main world.","Considering the Moon Empress’s ability, if she chose to slow down, she could ignite her spirit fire in the future.","Lin Yuan reflected on how fortunate it was that he had reached out to the Moon Empress; this call held immense importance.","This was particularly crucial because Lin Yuan could use his body composition to elevate the ranks of other spirit qi professionals.","The thought of the Moon Empress facing any danger troubled him. His affection for her was as strong as that for Chu Ci, differing only in the nature of that affection.","“Uncle Mystic, how long has Master been in seclusion? Will I affect her negatively if I go and see her now?”","Lin Yuan had spoken to the Moon Empress on the phone two days ago. Hence, she could not have been in seclusion for too long.","The biggest concern one had while in seclusion was being disturbed.","If the Moon Empress had been in seclusion for more than two days, Lin Yuan would need to think twice before he went to see her.","Mystic Moon hurriedly said, “Young Lord, the Moon Empress decided to go into seclusion today. Less than two hours have passed.”","Lin Yuan used the Ethereal Jellyfish’s Node Transportation to transport himself to the Radiant Moon Palace’s inner palace.","...","Mystic Moon was currently in Radiant Moon Palace’s inner palace.","Once Mystic Moon saw Lin Yuan, he hung up the call.","Lin Yuan knew that as the Moon Empress’ subordinate, Mystic Moon would not do anything that crossed the line and displeased her. Otherwise, he would have already tried to talk the Moon Empress out of this.","“Uncle Mystic, is Master in the quiet room at the Moonlight Gallery’s end?”","Mystic Moon nodded and was about to greet Lin Yuan when the latter’s body flashed and disappeared from the inner palace.","After passing through the Moonlight Gallery to the door of the quiet room, Lin Yuan knocked lightly on the door twice.","Without waiting for a response, Lin Yuan said, “Master, I remember you mentioning it would take at least eight years for Forage Moon to temper the energy in the six moons. It’s unlikely that you have fully tempered the energy in the moons.","“If you try to use the energy in Forage Moon to break through, you might break your birth horoscope! I wish that you would come out of seclusion!”","Lin Yuan knew how strong-headed the Moon Empress was. Hence, he did not mention he could help with her breakthrough.","Despite being in the quiet room, the Moon Empress had sensed Lin Yuan’s presence from the moment he arrived at the inner palace.","At that moment, the Moon Empress was overcome by a very strange feeling. She had just been reproached by her disciple. Yet, she did not dislike this feeling.","It was true that she wanted to increase her power as quickly as possible. However, she was not a reckless person.","While in the quiet room, the Moon Empress had been sensing Forage Moon’s state and mulling over her choice.","With the supply of resources from Lin Yuan, the Moon Empress had finished tempering the energy in the six moons in advance. Now, even if she used the energy in Forage Moon to set her spirit fire alight, a mistake would damage her roots but would not break her birth horoscope like Lin Yuan had said.","Regardless of how brash the Moon Empress was, she would not do anything that harmed her roots.","When she heard the anxiousness in Lin Yuan’s voice, the Moon Empress sighed and pulled open the door of the quiet room.","With this sigh, she not only gave up on the idea of using Forage Moon to break through but also acknowledged that despite being Lin Yuan’s Master, she was now trailing further and further behind him.","Henceforth, even with her endless lifespan, it would be difficult for the Moon Empress to catch up to her disciple.","The Moon Empress smiled lovingly at Lin Yuan.","“Little Yuan, since you don’t want me to put myself in danger, I won’t do it!”","Lin Yuan was relieved when he heard this.","Since the Moon Empress said that she was not going to put herself in danger, it would be the truth. She would never lie to him.","After a moment of silence, Lin Yuan placed his hand on the Moon Empress’ hand.","Lin Yuan’s action stunned the Moon Empress. He was always extremely respectful toward her and never put on such displays of affection.","Before the Moon Empress could think too much of this, she sensed a stream of energy flowing from Lin Yuan’s hand into her body.","The Moon Empress realized that as Lin Yuan injected energy into her body, her power grew continuously.","This energy would enable her to temper her birth horoscope.","Before the Moon Empress could marvel at Lin Yuan’s amazing ability, she hurriedly pulled her hand away and frowned as she asked, “Little Yuan, will you harm your body’s energy by doing this?","“I know you have your secrets. Your power suddenly broke through to pinnacle birth horoscope, and your roots are even stronger than mine. But regardless of what happens or who it is, I don’t want you to do anything that will harm yourself!”","Lin Yuan smiled faintly.","Despite being in the middle of something as beneficial as improving her power, the Moon Empress was still able to put Lin Yuan first and worry about him.","Lin Yuan was not at all surprised by this. Nonetheless, he was very touched.","Liu Jie and Wen Yu had said similar things in the past.","Lin Yuan was the creator of resources and would not harm himself to help his companions as it would affect his creation of resources.","However, nothing that Lin Yuan was doing now would affect him in any way!","“Master, helping you to break through won’t negatively affect me in any way. In fact, it might even help me!","“One of my secrets is my body composition. There are some matters I need to go and handle now. Once I return, not only will I help you set your spirit fire alight, but I will also help you break through to an even higher level so you can become a true World Emperor/Divine Kingdom expert!”"]},{"number":2773,"title":"Chapter 2773 Exclusive Skill: Tentacle Sacrifice Antenna Formation!","paragraphs":["2773 Exclusive Skill: Tentacle Sacrifice Antenna Formation!","Lin Yuan spoke extremely calmly.","When he placed his palm on the Moon Empress’ hand, he could sense that the energy in the Moon Empress’ body had improved slightly because of his body composition.","He had left his palm on the Moon Empress’ palm for tens of seconds. Yet, it was already enough for Lin Yuan to sense such a thing. He believed that if he left his hand on hers for a few weeks, he would be able to improve her level.","After helping the Moon Empress to set her spirit fire alight, Lin Yuan could try to help her open up her divine kingdom in the future.","As long as he could help the Moon Empress become a divine-kingdom expert, Lin Yuan would even be willing to spend a few years of his time.","When Lin Yuan helped Wen Yu and Liu Jie to raise their spirit qi professional ranks, he noticed that his own energy improved as well.","Lin Yuan experienced the same thing when he helped the Moon Empress to improve her level.","Since he possessed such capabilities, it went without saying he would help his Master first!","It was more important for Liu Jie and Wen Yu to evolve their feys’ grades and qualities than to raise their spirit qi professional ranks.","On the other hand, it would be difficult for the Moon Empress’ feys to evolve anytime soon. Hence, it was more important for the Moon Empress to focus on increasing her own power.","Eventually, both humans and feys needed to open up their divine kingdoms.","However, humans needed to go through the birth-horoscope and spirit-fire levels before they reached the Divine Kingdom level, while feys needed to pass through Sovereign XII in order to reach World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","The stronger and more knowledgeable one was, the more one’s perception would be broadened.","Lin Yuan had discovered more knowledge in the past month than he had in the past two to three years.","Lin Yuan spoke calmly, but his words were as shocking as strikes of lightning to the Moon Empress—this revelation went beyond the Moon Empress’ comprehension.","He had also done many things in the past that shocked the Moon Empress.","Regardless of how many resources he supplied, even if he had taken control of the five dimensional worlds, combined the five dimensional worlds with the main world, as well as promoted the Class 1 world to Class 2, the Moon Empress was able to comprehend all of this.","However, what Lin Yuan just said overhauled all the knowledge the Moon Empress had acquired since childhood.","Lin Yuan could use his body composition to raise a spirit qi professional’s rank without any cost. If the words had not come out of Lin Yuan’s mouth, the Moon Empress would never have believed such a statement.","The Moon Empress had just personally experienced the energy increasing in her body.","She blinked and forced herself to accept this fact.","The Moon Empress could not help but feel that this was absurd.","The experts in the main world were all stuck at a set level. This included the experts from the Radiance and Freedom Federations’ royalty and the 12 aristocratic families of the Azure Federation.","All of them had to put their lives at risk when they attempted to break through. A few had accidentally died during the process of the breakthrough.","But this new reality allowed the Moon Empress to see that the effort of all these experts could be accomplished by Lin Yuan with ease.","The Moon Empress suddenly realized why Lin Yuan had managed to gain so much power and was even able to take control of the five dimensional worlds.","Lin Yuan did not know what the Moon Empress was thinking. If he did, he would feel rather vexed because he did not know how to go about explaining himself.","His current accomplishments were not strongly related to his body composition. All along, he had been relying on Morbius.","He was starting to realize the usefulness of his body composition now that he had awakened his birth horoscope and body composition.","At present, his body composition was just as useful as Morbius!","“Little Yuan, if you have anything to attend to, go and take care of it now. If that’s the case, I can spend all my time governing the Radiance Federation and main world. I will do my best to achieve my previous 30-year goal in ten years!”","Lin Yuan smiled at the Moon Empress. “Master, aside from your own level, I will also help you to evolve your feys’ grades and qualities!”","...","Lin Yuan used the Ethereal Jellyfish’s Node Transportation to depart from the Radiant Moon Palace and headed in the direction of Epoch God Palace.","He could not leave the invaders from the Sky Beyond the Clouds alone for too long because he planned on making use of them.","Since he was going to make use of them, he would definitely allow them to return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. If they remained there for too long, it would draw suspicion from their factions.","From the moment Lin Yuan made contact with the invaders, he would begin his strategy against the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ East Universe!","Spring maintained communication with Winter while following Lin Yuan on his journey.","When she heard that the strongest of the invaders was a World Emperor/Pinnacle Higher Divine Kingdom Alluring Fox, an amused expression appeared on her face.","When did the Alluring Foxes become so destitute they were even willing to send people to search a Class 2 world?","To Spring’s memory, the Alluring Foxes were brimming with power. They were even stronger than what was regarded as the limit for fox-species lifeforms.","Not only were the Alluring Foxes attractive to other fox-species lifeforms, but they could also mesmerize other species.","However, Spring’s memory was from many epochs ago.","It was likely that the Alluring Foxes had declined in power over time!","Spring believed it was necessary for her to refresh her knowledge of the Sky Beyond the Clouds through these invaders.","The Alluring Foxes valued Kong Huan’s divine kingdom ability to escape the detection of world wills. Kong Huan herself significantly valued her divine kingdom ability as well.","However, Spring and Winter felt that this divine kingdom ability could only be used as a functional-type ability and did not have any special potential.","“Lord Saint, one of the individuals Winter caught is from a very powerful species. You can try to use your body composition to temper this species’ bloodline. If you improve this species’ bloodline, you will gain an advantage against many species.”","Lin Yuan looked interested, as Spring rarely gave him recommendations. He could tell that despite humbling herself in front of him, Spring was innately arrogant!","A species that was recommended by Spring had to be exceptional!","Ever since Lin Yuan awakened his body composition and discovered its uniqueness, he decided to make use of it to increase his power.","...","The Radiance Federation was very far away from Epoch God Palace, and Lin Yuan rested multiple times in between. It took him some time before he finally arrived at Epoch God Palace.","The Ethereal Jellyfish had yet to comprehend a Willpower Rune and evolve to Fantasy Breed.","By using the Ethereal Jellyfish’s abilities more often, Lin Yuan was helping it to comprehend a Willpower Rune.","Upon reaching Epoch God Palace, the Ethereal Jellyfish swiftly comprehended a Willpower Rune. Its once diminutive form, now a radiant red, hovered in the air, bearing little resemblance to its previous self that could rest atop Lin Yuan’s head.","Contrary to its ethereal nature, the jellyfish indeed possessed weight. If it were to rest on Lin Yuan’s head now, his neck might struggle under the burden, and its delicate tentacles could easily enshroud his entire body.","A luminous silver Willpower Rune materialized beside the Ethereal Jellyfish.","Lin Yuan could feel a compelling force emanating from this silver rune as if it were a central core drawing the surrounding space toward itself.","Before Lin Yuan could carefully examine the Willpower Rune, it entered the Ethereal Jellyfish’s body.","The Ethereal Jellyfish had evolved from Diamond X/Legend to Fantasy Breed.","Its size did not change, but it now had many more tentacles than before.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the Ethereal Jellyfish.","[Fey Name]: Ethereal Jellyfish","[Fey Species]: Ulmaridae/Floating Jellyfish","[Fey Grade]: Diamond (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Spatial","[Fey Quality]: Fantasy I","Abilities:","[Tentacle Node]: By breaking its tentacles, the broken tentacles are treated as a spatial node.","[Node Teleportation]: By sensing a spatial node, it would transport targets toward a certain spatial node.","[Node Activation]: The spatial teleportation marked by the Tentacle Node will be activated, and the target of the activated node will be teleported to other Tentacle Nodes or towards itself. Tentacle Node would be invalidated after the teleportation.","[Dissociate Catch]: When the Ethereal Jellyfish is traveling through various dimensions, it can catch some of the spatial energy in the different dimensions and condense them into spatial crystals.","[Main Tentacle]: A main tentacle will grow from the Ethereal Jellyfish’s body. When a large amount of spatial energy is supplied to the main tentacle, it will fall off. The fallen main tentacle can create a Space Tunnel anywhere that connects to the Ethereal Jellyfish’s location.","[Spatial Shift]: The energy in a specified area can be rounded up. When the Ethereal Jellyfish lights up and goes to another dimension, the energy from the specified area can be brought to the other dimension.","Exclusive Skill:","[Space Tunnel]: Break off a large number of tentacles or fuse the tentacles with spatial spiritual materials in the space to form a special long-distance space passageway. When there are three long-distance space passageways, one of them has to be removed before a new one can be set up.","[Tentacle Sacrifice Antenna Formation]: Form an antenna formation from all the tentacle nodes. When the tentacle nodes are sacrificed, the energy can be used as a guide to the antenna formation. Once the guide has been accepted, the spatial energy will freeze the surrounding space, and one will cross through space to return to the antenna formation.","At first, Lin Yuan did not have high hopes for the Ethereal Jellyfish’s new exclusive skill. After all, with all his experience of nurturing powerful feys, they usually only gained powerful exclusive skills when their quality evolved.","However, the Ethereal Jellyfish’s Fantasy Breed exclusive skill, Tentacle Sacrifice Antenna Formation, stunned Lin Yuan!","In an instant, he came up with a way to use Tentacle Sacrifice Antenna Formation.","Lin Yuan had a few methods to bring the dead back to life, but all of them came at extremely high costs.","Lin Yuan could not use them when Sky City’s white-clothed followers died.","Lin Yuan greatly valued abilities that could increase the white-clothed followers’ chances of survival.","These white-clothed followers had been recruited into Sky City and were also a part of Sky City. Lin Yuan needed to ensure their safety when they were loyally carrying out tasks for Sky City.","Tentacle Sacrifice Antenna Formation led Lin Yuan to think of an online game he played in his past life. It was very similar to the checkpoints and revival points in the game.","The cost of using Tentacle Sacrifice Antenna Formation was only one of the Ethereal Jellyfish’s tentacles.","Even when it was still only a Normal fey, the Ethereal Jellyfish’s ability to produce tentacles was very strong.","Now, as the Ethereal Jellyfish’s quality increased, it had twice the number of tentacles than before!","After communicating with the Ethereal Jellyfish, Lin Yuan found out that regrowing all the tentacles took two weeks. If he could obtain thousands of tentacles in two weeks, it would be sufficient for his daily use.","Even without life-saving methods, Sky City’s white-clothed followers would be able to use the Tentacle Nodes to return to the antenna formation while they were out on missions.","Lin Yuan would set up Tentacle Sacrifice Antenna Formation on Sky Sea’s back. This would allow it to be mobile and could be shifted to whichever location best suited Lin Yuan’s plan.","Tentacle Sacrifice Antenna Formation once again added to Sky City’s establishment on Sky Sea’s back.","Lin Yuan would collect as many Tentacle Nodes as he could while he was in the main world and store them away.","In the past, Lin Yuan did not plan on taking the white-clothed followers with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds as they would not be able to survive there at their current level. If they went, they would only become living targets.","But now, Lin Yuan could use his body composition to strengthen them and increase their power to suit his needs. As a result, the white-clothed followers would become a source of support for his operation in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Among all the feys Lin Yuan had contracted, he provided the least resources to the Ethereal Jellyfish.","This was because the Ethereal Jellyfish was just like the Acid Corrosion Queen Bee in that it needed to comprehend a Willpower Rune from nature.","Before it comprehended a Willpower Rune, its power would not increase regardless of how many resources it had.","But now that it had comprehended a Willpower Rune, Lin Yuan could use his resources to increase its overall power.","Spring was also observing the Ethereal Jellyfish and was amazed by its exclusive skill.","Spring thought, Only a fey nurtured by Lord Saint can gain such an exclusive skill when it is only Fantasy Breed!","Lin Yuan looked at the nearby Four Seasons Mountain and shrugged, raising his own spirits. He could finally begin putting his plan for the Sky Beyond the Clouds into action!"]},{"number":2774,"title":"Chapter 2774 You Don’t Have the Right to Work with Us!","paragraphs":["2774 You Don’t Have the Right to Work with Us!","When Autumn sensed Lin Yuan’s aura, he immediately came to greet him.","Autumn’s expression changed slightly when he saw Spring next to Lin Yuan. He could tell that Lin Yuan favored Spring the most out of his four followers. This might be because Spring had spent the most time with him.","Once Lin Yuan saw Spring as his closest and most trusted servant, his trust in her would only deepen.","This made Autumn rather jealous of Spring. However, jealousy was the end of it.","Before Lord Saint reincarnated, Spring had also spent the most time by his side.","“Lord Saint, Winter is watching the people from the East Universe. Do you want to go and see them together, or should I bring them to you one by one?”","Lin Yuan was silent for a moment. “Take me to see the invaders from the Sky Beyond the Clouds. I will select a few of them who I will then see individually.”","Meeting with the invaders individually would allow him to better size them up and take control of them. It would also be more convenient for him to glean the information he wanted.","When there were many people in the same environment, it would be inconvenient to discuss some things.","But before he spoke to them individually, he needed to discern which one of them was deserving of a private conversation with him.","Lin Yuan did not want to waste too much time on these minor lackeys.","Although all of them were from the Sky Beyond the Clouds and came from different species, Lin Yuan was not interested in learning about the inner workings of their species.","Winter had proved his power by taking control of these experts.","With Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter by his side, Lin Yuan did not have to watch where he stepped when he headed to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and began his development. Thanks to the protection of such martial force, Lin Yuan would quickly accumulate might in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Autumn hurriedly began leading the way. He believed that these mere World Emperor/Intermediate Divine Kingdom experts did not deserve the honor of meeting with Lin Yuan.","On the other hand, Spring admired Lin Yuan’s style of doing things. Although this was a reincarnation of Lord Saint, the soul of Lin Yuan’s previous life had merged with his current one from the moment he stepped out of the Returning Saint Pool.","Spring was the first of the four to begin following Lord Saint.","But by the time she began following him, he was already the esteemed Saint. He was also the most mysterious of the six figures.","Hence, Spring had not had the opportunity to see how the Saint had risen to his prime in his youth.","But now, Spring was getting a glimpse of the Saint’s youth in Lin Yuan.","Guided by Autumn, Lin Yuan soon arrived at the entrance of Winter’s palace.","Winter was keeping the invaders prisoner in his palace.","The moment Lin Yuan stepped into Winter’s palace, his gaze fell on the totem on the wall illustration behind the throne.","He was very familiar with the depictions on the totem.","At the center of the totem was a majestic figure with an enormous ring behind him. Lin Yuan had seen this ring in his subconscious when he awakened Morbius. The two were basically exact copies of each other.","Around this majestic figure’s wrist and neck was the same Morbius ring as the one that Lin Yuan was currently wearing.","Every single fey around the figure matched the ones that Lin Yuan had contracted and was nurturing.","It was no wonder that Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter were certain at first glance that he was the Saint.","Autumn and Winter were just as respectful toward the totem behind the throne as they were toward Lin Yuan. The two of them kept their heads low and did not look directly at the totem on the wall.","Autumn pointed at the long corridor at the side and said, “Lord Saint, once you pass through this corridor you will be able to reach the remote hall where the East Universe’s people are imprisoned!”","Lin Yuan walked over to the remote hall.","As the corridor leading to the remote hall was at the back of the main hall, Lin Yuan’s shoulder brushed against the totem on the wall when he passed.","At that moment, it was as though the totem connected with his birth horoscope, and it lit up.","The previously faceless majestic figure took on Lin Yuan’s features.","In the past, Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter bowed down and prayed whenever the totem changed in any way.","Now that they had found Lin Yuan and were following him, the totem on the wall was no longer as important as it used to be.","In Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter’s eyes, the totem on the wall represented their longing and reverence for Lin Yuan. But now, their longing and reverence had been transferred to the living Lin Yuan.","When Winter spotted Lin Yuan, he hurriedly bowed before pointing at the 100-odd figures on the ground. The snow covering the figures vanished.","The figures were devoid of life.","“Lord, this is the exact scene as I encountered it on the Abyss Beast’s back. These people were all killed by this Alluring Fox.”","Winter shifted his gaze onto Kong Huan while she spoke.","His glare frightened Kong Huan to the point she reverted to her original form.","A slender and lithe fox with pink and faintly purplish-red fur was now crouched on the ground, its expression terror-stricken. Its ten long tails waved around restlessly.","It had an inexplicable charm.","Normally, such charm had a large impact on birth-horoscope experts like Lin Yuan.","However, Spring had blanketed Lin Yuan in her aura so Kong Huan would not have the opportunity to affect Lin Yuan.","In truth, Kong Huan was already petrified to the point she no longer had any courage.","Winter’s power exceeded Kong Huan’s imagination, and she regretted coming to this Class 2 world. If she had not stubbornly made the trip to this Class 2 world, she would have fallen into such peril.","She could have remained in Honor Absent Palace as a member of the Honor Absent Parliament, basking in the worship of millions of lifeforms.","Yet, she was now captured by these people, and it was uncertain if she would be able to hold onto her life.","It was clear that this young man was the one who called the shots in the group.","When she sensed Spring and Winter’s hostile auras directed at her, Kong Huan did her best to retract her aura.","From the way that Spring and Winter were protecting his young man, Kong Huan could be certain that this young man was not strong.","While she was trying to come up with a way to plead for mercy, the young man’s pleasant voice sounded. “I heard that you are a member of the Alluring Foxes. The two flirty fellows next to you should also be Alluring Foxes, right?”","Faced with Lin Yuan’s question, Kong Huan hurriedly nodded before saying in a respectful tone, “My Lord, they are indeed Alluring Foxes. My Lord, from the moment I saw you, I felt a desire to submit to you. If there is anything that you want to know, feel free to ask me. I won’t hold anything back!”","Lin Yuan was slightly dumbfounded when he heard what Kong Huan said. Her way of currying favor was much too crude.","She had the desire to submit to him from the moment she saw him?","If Spring and Winter were not sufficiently strong, he would already have been killed by this Alluring Fox.","However, this strongest member of the Alluring Foxes was clever enough to comprehend his objective immediately.","Lin Yuan always liked clever people.","Kong Huan was trying to find a way to save her life. She had no idea her attitude had already received a positive review from Lin Yuan.","Kong Huan was not the only one present who was alive.","Lin Yuan asked everyone present, “There should be a leader among you. Step forward so I can take a look at you!”","Lin Yuan was certain that the leader was not Kong Huan, who was the strongest in the group. If she was the leader, there would be no need for her to unleash a massacre on the Abyss Beast’s back.","While Lin Yuan was asking his questions, he could sense that Kong Huan was only interested in protecting the two Alluring Foxes.","He intended to give the leader of the group an opportunity.","If the leader of the group had the courage to step forward, it would show that they were responsible despite not being the strongest in the group.","If the person did not step forward after his call, Lin Yuan would not make use of this leader in his future plans.","Once Lin Yuan spoke but before the others could shift their gazes toward Fan Lou, the latter raised a shaky hand and said solemnly, “My Lord, I am the guide sent by Honor Absent Palace. I am under orders to search your world! I am also the leader of a Boundary Patrol Team. This Class 2 world is under my jurisdiction.”","At this point, Fan Lou paused before saying seriously, “My Lord, do you intend on remaining in this Class 2 world? I am sure the appearance of the faeries and World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys are all linked to you. I am willing to submit to you. Once I submit to you, I will help you to cover up everything that happens in this Class 2 world. I won’t reveal anything to anyone!”","Lin Yuan looked at Fan Lou with surprise.","Fan Lou had likely guessed from Spring and Winter’s strength they were not natives of this world. Rather, they had just come to this Class 2 world early on.","Fan Lou had introduced his background, implying it would be able to bring him convenience.","It could be said that Fan Lou was much smarter than Kong Huan when it came to fighting for his life in a dangerous situation. He could also accurately guess what Lin Yuan wanted.","It was clear that Kong Huan’s massacre had nothing to do with Fan Lou.","When Lin Yuan controlled his subordinates, he liked to create an environment where they could compete on equal footing. If any of them made a mistake, another would report the mistake to Lin Yuan as a means of dealing a blow to their rival.","Lin Yuan looked around at the rest who were present and saw that they all looked timid.","Once Fan Lou stepped forward, none of them tried to engage him in conversation, not even the Bloodian.","As Lin Yuan was about to instruct Autumn to bring Fan Lou and Kong Huan to see them later, a robust man beside Fan Lou interjected, “My Lord, I am a Chaos Wind Demon Wolf. The guide is part of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves’ dependent species and is under our control.","“If you need to speak with Fan Lou about anything, you can speak with me first! The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves are very willing to work with you!”","Feng Huan was Feng Xuan’s relative and represented the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves in this operation because he was one of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves’ strongest World Emperor/intermediate Divine Kingdom warriors.","Furthermore, he was there on behalf of Feng Xuan to watch Fan Lou.","Feng Qing trusted Fan Lou greatly and did not think he could cause any significant problems.","However, Feng Xuan did not trust Fan Lou. If Fan Lou could betray Kong Huan, he could do the same to Feng Qing. Moreover, there was an abundance of resources in this Class 2 world, and Fan Lou had ample opportunities to embezzle the resources.","At the end of the day, Fan Lou was not a Chaos Wind Demon Wolf and would not put their profits first.","Feng Xuan would like nothing better than for Fan Lou to make a mistake. Once he made an error, Feng Qing would not be able to keep him by his side. At that point, Feng Xuan would have one less competitor with whom he had to fight for Feng Qing’s attention.","Feng Xuan knew that Feng Qing cared a lot about fortune and luck. If Feng Qing encountered any issues while Fan Lou was by his side, Feng Qing would attribute the problem to Fan Lou.","Then, Feng Xuan would be able to topple Fan Lou.","Fan Lou did not speak after Feng Huan spoke because the latter had spoken the truth. He was indeed a member of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves now. Everyone there could attest to that. There was no point in him trying to rebuke what Feng Huan said. Rather, it would cause him to come across as insincere.","Fan Lou was very worried that Lin Yuan would choose to speak with Feng Huan instead.","It was likely that only the few who had the right to speak with this young man would be able to keep their lives.","If the young man chose Feng Huan, Fan Lou would lose his chance at survival.","There were no issues with what Feng Huan had said, but Kong Huan could not help but purse her lips when she heard those words.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were truly wildly arrogant.","It was unlikely that even the first descendant of the Moon-Worshiping Wolves would have the right to speak with this young man. What right did the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves have to work with this young man?","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had backing from the Bloodians. Yet, the young man seemed unfazed by any potential trouble from the Bloodians, as he didn’t even bother to give the Bloodian present a lingering glance. If he cared about what the Bloodians had to say, he would have let them speak.","If one did not know one’s place at such a time, one would not deserve to live!","Lin Yuan did not continue the conversation with Feng Huan. Rather, he turned to look at Kong Huan. “Since this member of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves has presented his identity, why don’t you tell me about them? I would also like to know how the Alluring Foxes see the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves!”"]},{"number":2775,"title":"Chapter 2775 Bloodline Absorption!","paragraphs":["2775 Bloodline Absorption!","Lin Yuan did not say this because he truly wanted to understand the relationship between the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves and Alluring Foxes. Rather, he wanted to give Kong Huan and Fan Lou the chance to assert their dominance.","As the saying went, “Kill the chicken to scare the monkey.”","Given that Kong Huan had the courage to attack the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves’ members, it showed that they were not to be feared! Otherwise, Kong Huan would have restrained herself.","Moreover, the truly powerful species from the Sky Beyond the Clouds would not brazenly break the rules just to search for resources in a Class 2 world. A powerful species would have more sources from which they could search for resources.","The more powerful the species, the more ties they would have.","Feng Huan glanced at the heavily injured Bloodian numerous times. This gave Lin Yuan reason to believe that the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were under the Bloodians.","Lin Yuan was not interested in getting to know a species that hid behind another species.","There was no species that Kong Huan hated more than the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","Feng Qing had caused Kong Huan to suffer an enormous humiliation. This was an unbearable insult to her.","If the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves did not have the Bloodians supporting them, Kong Huan would have insisted on battling it out with Feng Qing.","But now that Lin Yuan was asking about the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves, this was a very good chance for Kong Huan. She could use the opportunity to suppress and smear the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","One message could be interpreted in many ways depending on how it was expressed.","Kong Huan was well-versed in the art of speaking.","“My Lord, the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves are traitors who betrayed the Moon-Worshiping Wolves almost 10,000 years ago.","“Have you heard of the Moon-Worshiping Wolves? Their internal power fell. As a result, the overall power of the species diminished. When the Moon-Worshiping Wolves were on the brink of losing all power, the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves, a branch species at the time, detached themselves from them.","“It would be fine if the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had only been the Moon-Worshiping Wolves’ dependent species. However, a few of their members had already married into the Moon-Worshiping Wolves.","“I was the one who propped up Fan Lou, the guide for this operation. However, the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves used dirty tricks to steal him away. He is now an official member of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves. If they did not have the support of the Bloodians, they would be no match for the Alluring Wolves!”","The Moon-Worshiping Wolves had not gone after the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves because they had linked themselves to the Bloodians.","Occasionally, fights in the Sky Beyond the Clouds led to the extinction of a few species.","However, the species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds could thrive because many other species cracked and became divided.","The division of species was not a big deal.","However, Kong Huan spun her words in a way that made the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves seem like a despicable species.","However, Fan Lou could not rebuke Kong Huan.","Firstly, it was true he used to serve Kong Huan. Hence, the background of her claims was true.","Moreover, Fan Lou was still terribly afraid of Kong Huan.","Given the current circumstances, there was no way the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves could continue to protect him.","This young man’s attitude toward Kong Huan made it obvious he regarded her as the most valuable of the group.","Feng Huan’s face flushed when he heard what Kong Huan said. He was about to speak when a terrifying aura enveloped him and paralyzed his movements.","Winter frowned and looked at Feng Huan.","Lin Yuan was currently in the middle of asking them questions. By interrupting Lin Yuan before he posed a question to him, Feng Huan was disrespecting Lin Yuan.","As Lin Yuan’s follower, there was no way that Winter would permit such disrespect.","Winter’s body composition allowed him to sense that Kong Huan was telling the truth. Although she was bending the message, the statements were facts nonetheless.","Winter did not feel any negative emotions toward species that split off.","There were many species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds that split off from their main species and eventually rose up to attain even greater power.","However, a species like this that attached itself to another faction after splitting off from its original species constricted its own development and prevented itself from gaining prominence.","Winter despised species like these, but there were a fair number of them in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan knew that Spring and Winter were capable of discerning truth from lies.","When Spring nodded at him, Lin Yuan knew that Kong Huan was telling the truth.","But it was always more convenient for him to discern the truth for himself rather than depending on others.","Lin Yuan intended to strengthen the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom once he was done asking his questions to Kong Huan and Fan Lou. The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s spores would then be able to judge if World Emperor/Divine Kingdom experts were telling the truth!","Given the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s power, its spores would not have much of an effect on Kong Huan and Fan Lou even if they did not put up any resistance.","Once Lin Yuan was done asking Kong Huan his questions, he ignored the rest of the invaders.","Instead, he turned his gaze to Winter and asked, “Winter, do you think any of these species’ bloodlines are worth nurturing?”","Although Lin Yuan had seen the invaders, he did not know much about the situation in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. More often than not, asking Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter for their opinions was better than doing research on his own.","Winter had already guessed that Lin Yuan would use his Body of All Spirits to nurture more bloodlines.","Using the Body of All Spirits to nurture bloodlines took time. Each time a bloodline was abandoned, all the time that had gone into nurturing it would be wasted.","Hence, recommending a bloodline to Lin Yuan was extremely important to Winter.","After a moment of silence, Winter said seriously, “My Lord, if you would like to nurture a bloodline, the Alluring Fox, Bloodian, and Burning Demon bloodlines are all worth considering. As for the other bloodlines, it will be easy to find better alternatives in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","“The Bloodians have various variations of their main bloodline, making the bloodlines significantly diverse. The two Bloodian warriors they dispatched for this mission possess bloodlines closely aligned to the original one, which is considered the most authentic. Extracting their bloodlines eliminates the need to replace them for nurturing a different one upon reaching the Sky Beyond the Clouds.”","Lin Yuan nodded and looked at the three Alluring Foxes, Bloodian, as well as the dead Burning Demon.","Before Lin Yuan spoke, Spring said seriously, “Lord Saint, I will help you to extract the bloodlines. Once I’ve extracted them, I will bring over the two individuals you have selected! As for the others, you can decide what to do with them once you are done speaking to the two!”","Lin Yuan really liked how thoughtful Spring was. She always thought one step ahead of him and could understand what he wanted.","When he was in the Radiance Federation, Summer was also by his side. When it came to such matters, Summer was no match for Spring.","Lin Yuan’s Body of All Spirits did not require much bloodline energy in order to absorb bloodlines. Hence, extracting the bloodlines would not have much of an effect on Kong Huan and the others.","Moreover, if he extracted too many bloodlines at once, his Body of All Spirits would be contaminated.","...","Lin Yuan went to the main palace and sat down on the throne.","The totem on the wall behind the chair became increasingly clearer. Soon, the entire totem lit up with a reddish-bronze light.","Morbius’ voice echoed in Lin Yuan’s mind. “Partner, I can sense that my body is being filled up with power, which is coming from the totem on the wall. I want to take some time to absorb this energy. Partner, I might need you to stay here for a little longer.”","Morbius rarely asked Lin Yuan for anything.","Since Morbius could absorb the energy from the totem on the wall, there was no reason for Lin Yuan to turn Morbius down.","Lin Yuan really hoped that Morbius would be able to evolve its roots.","As his lifelong fey, Morbius’ accumulation of energy also strengthened Lin Yuan’s power.","Lin Yuan remembered Spring and Winter mentioning that there was a totem on the wall of all four of their palaces.","Once Morbius absorbed all the energy in the wall illustration, Lin Yuan would head to the other three palaces to see if Morbius could also absorb the energy from the wall illustrations there.","Lin Yuan was not in the main palace for long before Spring brought him three crystal bottles. These three crystal bottles contained three strange types of energy.","In the main world, the best way to extract bloodlines was to temper the essence blood in the lifeform. However, this method would result in the extracted bloodline containing impurities.","Spring had used her own body composition to extract the bloodlines of Kong Huan and the rest. Spring’s body composition had filtered out the impurities for Lin Yuan, ensuring the purity of these three bloodlines.","First, Lin Yuan received the crystal bottle that contained the Burning Demon bloodline and held it in his palm.","In an instant, Lin Yuan could sense that the Burning Demon bloodline felt extremely affectionate toward him.","Lin Yuan circulated his energy and absorbed the Burning Demon bloodline into his body with ease.","Spring said softly, “Lord Saint, this Burning Demon is weak, and its bloodline level is low. However, the Burning Demon bloodline is straightforward and doesn’t have as many variations and branches as the Bloodians. Once you begin nurturing the Burning Demon bloodline, fire elements will no longer be able to harm you. Rather, they will enhance you.","“There are also many abyss demons that can control flames in your Class 2 world. The abyss demons are able to control flames because of the lotus-species lifeform you have taken control of.","“On the other hand, the Burning Demons’ ability to control flames comes from their own bloodline. The Burning Demons are a very elite type of lifeform.”","Lin Yuan thought, So the abyss demons are also an enormous species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","It was just as Spring said. The abyss demons could control flames because the Abyss Wombs produced by the Abyss Red Lotus had been infected by its aura.","Now that the abyssal world had fused with the main world, there was no Abyss Red Lotus to infect the Abyss Wombs.","The fire-elemental energy in the Abyss Wombs decreased continuously. As a result, the newly born abyss demons had lost the ability to wield fire-elemental energy in combat and only had a body that was highly resistant to fire-elemental energy.","After thousands of years passed, once all the fire-elemental energy had disappeared from within the Abyss Wombs, the abyss demons would revert to their original forms.","Lin Yuan felt that taking control of and nurturing a bloodline to gain resistance to and benefit from a type of elemental energy was a very good thing.","In this regard, the Burning Demon bloodline could be equated to the mermaid bloodline.","After absorbing the Burning Demon bloodline, Lin Yuan picked up the crystal bottle that contained the Bloodian bloodline and began absorbing it.","The Bloodians’ bloodline was highly capable of infecting the bloodlines of other lifeforms. High-class Bloodians would use their own bloodlines to infect and take control of other lifeforms, turning them into their slaves.","Their bloodline was one of the main reasons the Bloodians were so feared by other species. If they were infected by the Bloodians’ bloodline during combat, it would be difficult to solve this issue even if they won the fight.","Yet, in Lin Yuan’s hands, the Bloodian bloodline was very tame and submitted to his body composition.","After absorbing the Burning Demon bloodline, Lin Yuan’s body would light up with a fiery glow when he activated it. Lin Yuan’s eyes would also turn faintly orange.","This was because the Burning Demon bloodline was not strong.","The two Bloodian bloodlines that Spring had extracted were of a much higher level than that of the Burning Demon bloodline.","Lin Yuan’s eyes turned blood-red, and his hair also changed from black to crimson.","The bright red hair fell past his shoulders, giving him a devilishly elite air.","Lin Yuan could sense that his physical strength increased exponentially when he tapped into the Bloodian bloodline.","Lin Yuan casually took out a piece of radium steel and gripped it lightly. It buckled under his grip, changing its shape.","Lin Yuan used a little strength, and the hard metal began seeping through his fingers.","The improvement in his physical strength made Lin Yuan very interested in this bloodline, so he decided to strengthen it first.","The Bloodians could take control of bloodlines, and their bodies were powerful. It was no wonder that the mermaids were no match for them.","Just like the mermaid bloodline, the Bloodian bloodline had numerous distinct levels.","Lin Yuan could not be bothered with these complicated levels. To him, the bloodlines were nothing more than tools. All he needed to do was make use of those tools.","Now, all that was left was the Alluring Fox bloodline.","Both Spring and Winter had praised the Alluring Fox bloodline, piquing Lin Yuan interest.","However, rather than taking control of the Alluring Fox bloodline to mesmerize other fox-species and lifeforms, Lin Yuan believed that the boost and resistance to flames and the blood-type enchantments and physical strength boost from the other two bloodlines were much more beneficial!","While Lin Yuan was absorbing the Alluring Fox bloodline, Spring spoke."]},{"number":2776,"title":"Chapter 2776 Bloodline: Alluring Soul Grade!","paragraphs":["2776 Bloodline: Alluring Soul Grade!","“Lord Saint, most of the Alluring Fox bloodline was extracted from Kong Huan’s body. When I extracted her bloodline, she told me its level is the most elite of all the experts in her species! Her bloodline has reached pinnacle Alluring Bones and is only one step away from reaching Alluring Soul!”","In spite of its eliteness, Lin Yuan did not experience any difficulty absorbing the Alluring Fox bloodline.","But once Lin Yuan absorbed it, 10 long pinkish-red tails emerged from his back.","They were even wider and more graceful than Kong Huan’s own when she was in her original form.","Lin Yuan’s long black hair slowly faded to a light peachy pink. His hair reached his knees, and there were flecks of gold and purplish-red within the pink. It was as though the underside of the hair had been highlighted.","A pair of animal ears sprouted from the top of his head, and his eyes turned crystalline pinkish-purple.","Lin Yuan’s handsome features softened and became more alluring.","At that moment, Spring felt that Lin Yuan could be perfectly described as a charming natural beauty.","After assimilating the Alluring Fox bloodline, Lin Yuan began to feel the full extent of its enhancing effects.","Interestingly, the Alluring Fox bloodline not only captivated fox-species lifeforms but also stirred affection in cat-species lifeforms toward him.","Additionally, it bolstered his resistance to charm, shielding him from external influences.","Thanks to the Alluring Fox bloodline’s support to his soul and spirit, Lin Yuan gained immunity to various negative effects of soul- and spirit-targeting curses.","Remarkably, when it came to these capabilities, the Alluring Fox bloodline proved to be on par with, if not stronger than, the formidable Bloodian bloodline!","Lin Yuan finally understood why Spring and Summer had so strongly recommended the Alluring Fox bloodline to him.","It was like the bloodline of kings that dominated all other lifeforms.","Unfortunately, evolving the Alluring Fox bloodline in the Sky Beyond the Clouds proved to be exceptionally challenging for unknown reasons.","Lin Yuan held the belief that the pinnacle Alluring Bones bloodline faced difficulty in dominating the most potent fox-species lifeforms and failed to appeal strongly to other cat-species lifeforms.","The Alluring Foxes could consider themselves fortunate for not becoming the pets of other fox- and cat-species lifeforms.","However, if the Alluring Fox bloodline could be successfully evolved, its standing on the Species Ranking would experience a significant boost!","Spring had mentioned the Snow-Covered Foxes to Lin Yuan.","Spring had not heard of the Snow-Covered Foxes before. Yet, they occupied a spot in the top 100 ranks of the East Universe’s Species Ranking. There was no way that Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter would be unaware of such a species if they existed while they were in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Given that Spring had not heard of them, it meant that the Snow-Covered Foxes had only risen to power in the last few epochs.","Kong Huan had mentioned that the Alluring Foxes intended to migrate to the North Universe to become the Snow-Covered Foxes’ dependent species.","Lin Yuan felt that a species that knew how to seek protection was a smart one.","However, due to the special characteristics of the Alluring Foxes, it was challenging for them to become a dependent species.","Without a powerful source of support, the Alluring Foxes would likely become playthings to the Snow-Covered Foxes as well as the other dependent species.","There were no restraints when it came to fighting between the species of the Sky Beyond the Clouds. The powerful species did not need any reason to destroy the weaker ones.","Lin Yuan sensed that his Alluring Fox bloodline had indeed reached pinnacle Alluring Bones, and there was only a weak wall obstructing the bloodline from the next step in its evolution. Lin Yuan could sense that this wall could be broken with one tiny push.","Lin Yuan circulated the energy in his bloodline to temper the Alluring Fox bloodline.","Once he injected his energy into the Alluring Fox bloodline, it became active and began hacking at the thin wall.","Lin Yuan could sense that the attacks from the Alluring Fox bloodline were causing the wall to weaken.","If this trajectory persisted, the energy in his body would be able to help the bloodline to evolve.","Now that he had confirmed this, Lin Yuan concentrated on activating his body composition.","While he was strengthening the Alluring Fox bloodline, his charm intensified, and Spring found it difficult to keep her eyes off of him.","Charm was an influence that came from the bloodline and manifested through the body. The less impurities in the body, the stronger the manifestation of charm.","Lin Yuan’s Body of All Spirits had enabled him to become the Source of All Spirits and his body could naturally boost other bloodlines.","Hence, despite the fact that both Lin Yuan and Kong Huan’s bloodlines were at pinnacle Alluring Bones, his ability to mesmerize other fox-species and cat-species lifeforms was much stronger than hers!","All of a sudden, Spring sensed that Lin Yuan’s aura had changed.","The charm of Alluring Bones did not come from the appearance but was kept within the body. Nonetheless, the body was the source.","But now, all the charm in Lin Yuan’s body had been concealed and stored in his soul. As a result, the charm no longer manifested through the surface.","If the two types of charm were compared, the Alluring Bones bloodline was akin to the ape stage of evolution, while the Alluring Soul bloodline was already at the homosapien stage!","Lin Yuan’s peachy pink hair that fell to his knees was shortened so that it only reached his waist. The color also became lighter, and the curls had golden hues.","Given that his charm was all concealed within his soul now, Lin Yuan’s appearance was very clean.","His purplish-pink eyes took on a more crystalline beauty.","Spring could not help but marvel that his current appearance could not only mesmerize other fox-species and cat-species lifeforms but also have a significant effect on other species.","The Alluring Bones bloodline in Lin Yuan’s body had only just evolved to Alluring Soul. But thanks to Lin Yuan’s Body of All Spirits, it had reached higher Alluring Soul.","It was said that during the golden age of the Alluring Foxes, the High Priest’s bloodline had broken through past Alluring Soul.","The evolution of the High Priest’s bloodline had required the help of all the Alluring Foxes. But to Lin Yuan, evolving the bloodline was not a difficult task at all.","The Alluring Foxes were a species that prioritized bloodline.","Now that Lin Yuan’s bloodline had reached Alluring Soul grade, it would be extremely easy for him to take control of Kong Huan by brandishing his bloodline.","However, as Spring came to learn more about Lin Yuan, she discovered that he liked everything to be done with certainty. Hence, he would never just rely on his bloodline to take control of Kong Huan.","In Spring’s eyes, this was a virtue.","Using one’s bloodline to take control of other bloodlines involved the bloodline suppressing the bloodlines of other species, thereby attaining their loyalty.","Unlike the demon insects, not every species’ bloodline afforded them as strong of a controlling power over their peers.","If he used his bloodline to take control of Kong Huan, she would be able to betray him once she decided to turn her back on the Alluring Foxes.","Lin Yuan sensed his current state.","After the evolution of the Alluring Fox bloodline, he noticed that his spirit and soul were much more resistant to negative effects than before.","Lin Yuan needed to use his own energy in order to use the Body of All Spirits to evolve a bloodline. Hence, before taking control of a bloodline, he needed to ensure there were sufficient merits that warranted its use. Otherwise, it would be a waste of his energy.","Morbius was currently absorbing the energy on the wall illustration.","Lin Yuan would need to remain in Epoch God Palace for four months at least.","Lin Yuan sat on the throne and pondered for a moment before he said, “Spring, go and bring these two people over to me. What do you think I should do to ensure their loyalty when I take control of them?”","Lin Yuan had never interacted with World Emperor/Divine Kingdom experts before and did not know if they could swear on their Willpower and Law Runes like spirit qi professionals and feys could.","Spring smiled and said, “Lord Saint, despite recently awakening your birth horoscope, your divine kingdom has swiftly integrated with a sacred mountain, boasting unparalleled accommodation capabilities.","“Utilize your divine kingdom to absorb theirs, leaving your distinct imprint on their divine kingdoms. Employ your fountain of faith to bind their fountains, gaining control over their power sources. While their lives may not be within your grasp, their obedience is assured.”","Spring guessed what Lin Yuan was thinking. When spirit qi professionals swore on their Law and Willpower Runes, they were being restrained by the world wills.","However, once divine-kingdom experts opened their divine kingdoms, they were able to use their divine kingdoms to fight back against the world wills. Hence, swearing on Law Runes and Willpower Runes might work for other lifeforms but no longer worked for them.","In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, power was everything. There were countless experts who put their lives on the line in their pursuit of power. Some species even ran themselves into the ground because of this.","The Alluring Foxes were the best example of that.","It was likely that the High Priest that evolved past Alluring Soul had encountered some issues and might have even died.","Otherwise, the Alluring Foxes would never have fallen down such a spiral!","Lin Yuan relaxed when he heard what Spring said.","He would only allow the two of them to return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds once he found a way to take full control of them.","If the two were allowed to return and they brought disaster back to the main world, it would be too late for Lin Yuan to regret his decision!","But now, he could use his divine kingdom to take control of the two of them. Lin Yuan believed that experts from a place as complicated as the Sky Beyond the Clouds would treasure power over their own lives.","Lin Yuan had always known that his divine kingdom was very special.","He had only been a D-rank spirit qi professional when he opened his divine kingdom.","Spring said that his divine kingdom had fused with a sacred mountain. What was a sacred mountain?","After a moment of silence, Lin Yuan decided not to ask more questions.","As his power continued to grow, he would eventually gain the answers to many of his questions.","Soon, Kong Huan and Fan Lou appeared in front of him.","Lin Yuan gazed down at the two of them and could clearly sense the fear they felt toward him. This fear came from their fear of his power, as well as their unfamiliarity with him.","They still could not figure out how experts like Spring and Winter could exist in a Class 2 world!","Kong Huan was the strongest expert in the group. She had revealed her objective during Winter’s preliminary questioning.","Kong Huan wanted to kill all the other experts who had come to the main world from the Sky Beyond the Clouds, aside from the other Alluring Foxes, so she could occupy all the resources in the main world.","As the leader of the Boundary Patrol Team in charge of the main world, Fan Lou had the best understanding of the main world. He had leveraged this to join the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves and successfully elevated his status in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Fan Lou used to be Kong Huan’s subordinate but had betrayed her. As such, the two of them were now bitter enemies, and Kong Huan wanted nothing more than to see him dead.","But now that they were both prisoners, they had no choice but to try to get along with each other.","Due to the differences in their stances and the enmity between them, they would both jump at the chance to undermine each other.","However, neither would agree to work with their captor without first discussing it with each other.","“How long did the two of you plan on searching this Class 2 world before returning to the Sky Beyond the Clouds?”","This was the question that Lin Yuan most wanted the answer to.","But to Fan Lou and Kong Huan, it sounded as though Lin Yuan was interrogating them.","Previously, Kong Huan was always the one to speak first. But this time, Fan Lou reacted first and said, “My Lord, we didn’t set a deadline because we don’t know much about this Class 2 world. We only need to return before all the abyssal space energy in the Abyssal Beast’s body is depleted.”","Fan Lou understood the circumstances. All their lives were in the hands of this young man.","This young man was not showing Kong Huan any special favor, so he had the right to compete with Kong Huan for this young man’s favor.","This young man’s two subordinates were unbelievably powerful. Evidently, this young man was a bigshot from one of the Sky Beyond the Clouds’s top factions.","There was a chance that he might not be from the East Universe!","Kong Huan’s power was insignificant in the face of such a bigshot.","Fan Lou needed to do his best to leave a good impression on this young man. A good start would be to answer all the questions he had.","Lin Yuan looked at Spring as he did not know how long it would take for all the abyssal space energy in the Abyssal Beast to run out.","Spring hurriedly explained, “Lord Saint, given a regular level of activity, it would take at least two years and four months for all the energy in the Abyssal Beast’s body to be depleted.”","Lin Yuan could not help but remember Spring mentioning that the experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds went into seclusion for hundreds or even thousands of years. There were also many of them that only emerged hundreds of thousands of years later!","Two years and four months was nothing to lifeforms from the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Moreover, given the difference in the flow of time between the Sky Beyond the Clouds and the main world, two years and four months in the main world was the equivalent of around two months in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Since there was so much time left, there was no need for Lin Yuan to rush.","He was going to visit all four palaces so Morbius could absorb the energy in the walls.","Hence, he would allow Kong Huan and Fan Lou to tell him all about the current East Universe!","When Lin Yuan traveled from the main world to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, his arrival point was the boundary of the East Universe.","When you knew yourself and your enemy, you could fight a hundred battles without fearing defeat.","Hence, Lin Yuan believed that it was imperative for him to gain an understanding of the East Universe."]},{"number":2777,"title":"Chapter 2777 The Hand That Reached Into the North Universe!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2777 The Hand That Reached Into the North Universe!","Kong Huan and Fan Lou had the same sentiments toward Lin Yuan.","In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Kong Huan was always able to keep Fan Lou under her thumb. Even if he had become a relative of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves, she could still strike at him if the opportunity arose.","Everything came down to evidence.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves would not try to persecute the Alluring Foxes over a dead man. The dead had no value.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves had to pay the Bloodians handsomely to obtain their help.","But now, Kong Huan did not feel superior in the slightest—","she needed to compete with Fan Lou for this young man’s trust.","Kong Huan had kept Fan Lou by her side all this time because of his competency and his ability to bring her amusement.","When it came to currying favor and bringing amusement, Kong Huan had to admit that she was no match for Fan Lou.","She was born into the main branch of the Alluring Foxes and possessed outstanding talent from a young age. She evolved faster than the rest of her species. Her upbringing had been smooth sailing, and she never needed to try to please anyone else.","Kong Huan looked delighted when Lin Yuan said he wanted to hear about the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Since she was of a higher level than Fan Lou, she possessed more information than him.","Kong Huan would not mind revealing some secrets if she could trade them for her survival.","But it went without saying she would prefer not to reveal information about the Alluring Foxes unless Lin Yuan asked her about it directly. Regardless of where she was or what danger she was in, Kong Huan put her species first. This was the difference between her and Fan Lou.","Fan Lou was now a relative of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves and was valued by Feng Qing. However, he only saw them as a safe haven where he could take shelter.","If Fan Lou was able to seek support from the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves, he would do everything he could to get into Feng Qing’s good books and raise his status among the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","But if Feng Qing and the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were unable to protect him, Fan Lou would not feel too much guilt over betraying them.","Fan Lou needed to compete with Kong Huan while figuring out Lin Yuan’s objective.","If Lin Yuan did not mind that he and Kong Huan lacked power and were willing to take them in, Fan Lou would do anything to grab onto the opportunity.","Unlike Kong Huan, he did not have the Alluring Foxes backing him up.","This situation was not only dangerous but was also a possible opportunity for Fan Lou.","“Since we have time, the two of you can tell me everything you know about the Sky Beyond the Clouds! If you find that the other person’s information isn’t accurate, you can point it out. I have always liked subordinates who are able to prove their value to me. If the two of you are able to prove your value, I will be willing to offer you an opportunity.”","Lin Yuan already intended to let Kong Huan and Fan Lou live and to make them work for him. There was no need to hide his plans.","Under the threat of death, the two of them would definitely tell him everything they knew in order to live.","However, if he paid out the pros and cons for them clearly, they would be inclined to hold back some information about the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","From Fan Lou and Kong Huan’s descriptions, Lin Yuan gained a general understanding of the situation in the East Universe.","Spring was also listening to Kong Huan and Fan Lou’s descriptions. She realized that the East Universe had changed significantly over the last few epochs!","The only thing that had not changed was that Honor Absent Palace was still the dominant faction.","Kong Huan thought about the Snow-Covered Fox envoy from the North Universe liaising with the Alluring Foxes and felt she needed to tell Lin Yuan about this.","She hoped he could guide her in the right direction regarding this matter.","At that moment, Kong Huan was unsure if moving the Alluring Foxes to the North Universe was still the right decision.","The reason for their move to the North Universe was that Kong Huan did not want to be bothered by Feng Qing.","Additionally, the Bloodians were always looming over the Alluring Foxes.","Kong Huan believed that an entity of Lin Yuan’s level would surely return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds once he was done exploring this Class 2 world.","Asking Lin Yuan about decisions that concerned the Alluring Foxes was also a way of demonstrating subordination.","“My Lord, the Alluring Foxes have been communicating with the Snow-Covered Fox envoy recently. According to our plan, we will be moving from the East Universe to the North Universe soon. The Snow-Covered Foxes promised me a seat in the parliament there.”","Lin Yuan’s lips curled upward.","Kong Huan was very smart and guessed his objective.","By saying this, Kong Huan was signaling she would lead all the Alluring Foxes to submit to him.","After Lin Yuan went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would begin developing in the East Universe.","However, there was no need for the Alluring Foxes to remain in the East Universe. They could not bring Lin Yuan any benefits by remaining there.","Once they went to the North Universe, the Alluring Foxes would become his eyes there and help him gain insight into the North Universe.","Rather than staying in the East Universe, the North Universe might be a more beneficial environment for the Alluring Foxes.","Lin Yuan was silent for a moment before he said, “Your bloodline has reached pinnacle Alluring Bones. It won’t be difficult to evolve your bloodline.”","Kong Huan looked astonished when she heard what Lin Yuan said.","It was true that her bloodline was pinnacle Alluring Bones. But what did he mean by it not being difficult to evolve her bloodline? She had been stuck at pinnacle Alluring Bones for a very long time, and there was no Alluring Fox with a more elite bloodline.","Kong Huan had absolute confidence in her bloodline. Otherwise, she would not have been recommended as the Alluring Foxes’ representative member of the Honor Absent Parliament.","“My Lord, you might not be aware of this, but the Alluring Fox bloodline is more difficult to evolve than the bloodlines of other species. I have the most elite bloodline of all the Alluring Foxes in the past hundreds of thousands of years! I will only have the opportunity to evolve if I somehow encounter a giant lucky break!”","Lin Yuan did not bother to explain. Instead, he circulated his Alluring Fox bloodline in his body.","Lin Yuan’s appearance changed in an instant.","The bloodline power flowing out of Lin Yuan’s body stupefied Kong Huan. She stared at him in shock. Based on his aura and state, she could be certain that his bloodline had reached pinnacle Alluring Soul. Moreover, his Alluring Soul bloodline had extremely solid roots.","Just what was happening?","Kong Huan could also sense that Lin Yuan’s bloodline came from her own. Otherwise, she would not feel such an intimacy toward his bloodline aura.","When Kong Huan first saw Lin Yuan, she was certain that he knew nothing about the Alluring Foxes.","Could it be that the bloodline in Lin Yuan’s body was related to the bloodline that the female expert named Spring had extracted from her?","His bloodline had broken through the wall and successfully evolved to Alluring Soul grade in such a short time!","Kong Huan finally believed that Lin Yuan would be able to evolve her bloodline.","She hurriedly knelt, lowered her body to the ground, and said with respect and anticipation, “My Lord, if you can help my bloodline to evolve, I will be of great help to you once I take the Alluring Foxes to the North Universe!”","Kong Huan was not the type to make promises easily, especially in such situations. As an Alluring Fox, she was well aware of the attraction that her bloodline had on other fox-species and beast-type lifeforms.","She might not be able to use the Alluring Soul bloodline to seduce the upper echelon of the Snow-Covered Foxes, but she would still be able to mesmerize other powerful dependent species and gain their protection!","Kong Huan had suggested leaving for the North Universe because she believed that Lin Yuan wanted her to do so.","Even if she did not head to the North Universe and the Alluring Foxes continued developing in the East Universe, evolving her bloodline would definitely elevate her position as a member of the Honor Absent Parliament.","Fan Lou became extremely anxious when he heard the conversation between Kong Huan and Lin Yuan.","He had come with Kong Huan to tell Lin Yuan about the situation in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. However, his status was lower than that of Kong Huan, and there were many things about Honor Absent Palace he did not know. This gave Kong Huan the chance to seize the lead.","Now, Kong Huan was clinging to and forming a connection with Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan had Kong Huan’s bloodline in his body. This made Fan Lou feel as though he would be abandoned by Lin Yuan at any time.","This thought was a wake-up call to Fan Lou, and he brought out the information he believed would be the most useful to Lin Yuan.","“My Lord, how long do you intend on staying in this Class 2 world? I will remain as a Boundary Patrol Envoy even after I return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. If you intend to continue nurturing faeries or evolving feys in this Class 2 world, I can help you to keep the news under wraps so no one finds out about what is happening in this Class 2 world.”","Lin Yuan’s eyes flashed.","It was true he intended to remain in the main world for some time. While he was in the main world, not only would he evolve his own feys but would also increase the strength of those around him, followed by their feys’ grades.","Hence, it was likely that another World Emperor/Divine Kingdom expert would appear in the main world soon.","Lin Yuan was concerned that if the commotion from the evolutions was not hidden, there would be a second, third, or even more groups of visitors from the Sky Beyond the Clouds. At that point, the main world would become a giant target.","Once Lin Yuan left the main world, it would have no one to protect it!","If Fan Lou could use his identity as a Boundary Patrol Envoy to cover up any activities in the main world, it would save Lin Yuan a lot of trouble.","With someone as intelligent as Fan Lou, Lin Yuan believed he could help him gain access to Honor Absent Palace and become a member of the Honor Absent Parliament. This would allow Lin Yuan to obtain classified information from within Honor Absent Palace.","Otherwise, once Kong Huan moved to the North Universe, Lin Yuan would lose a set of eyes within Honor Absent Palace!","“Not bad. That is exactly what I need you to do! I will ask Spring to check your bloodline. Then, I’ll give you some resources to slowly nurture your bloodline.”","Fan Lou was overjoyed.","Lin Yuan said that because he intended to keep him around and would not kill him.","Fan Lou was well aware of the bloodline in his body. His original bloodline was lacking. Currently, the strongest bloodline in his body was the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf bloodline.","When he returned to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would also have to return to Feng Qing’s side.","If he strengthened his bloodline, his position among the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves would also improve.","But from Spring’s words, Fan Lou could tell that Lin Yuan was not interested in the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","At that point, Fan Lou heard Lin Yuan say, “There is still one Bloodian who is alive. The other one in the team has died. It will be difficult to explain their deaths when you return.","“I will take control of that Bloodian so that when he returns to the Sky Beyond the Clouds with you, he will communicate with the Bloodians on your behalf and allow you to gain their protection! This will not only elevate your position among the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves but will also allow you to become the bridge between the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves and Bloodians!","“Everything depends on effort. There is nothing that cannot be achieved. It’s possible that with my help, you will become a member of the Honor Absent Parliament.”","While Lin Yuan was speaking to Fan Lou, he could clearly sense Fan Lou had always acted cautiously and timidly. A person with such a manner of action had predictable potential.","In a complex environment like the Sky Beyond the Clouds, time could easily erode a lifeform’s ambition.","Lin Yuan’s words were meant to expand Fan Lou’s mind and give him hope for the future. This would also allow Fan Lou to understand the benefits that could come from dutifully sticking by Lin Yuan’s side.","After speaking to Kong Huan and Fan Lou, Lin Yuan told Kong Huan to stay behind.","Kong Huan’s heart was filled with excitement and anticipation as she watched Lin Yuan walk over to her from the throne.","Once her bloodline evolved from pinnacle Alluring Bones to Alluring Soul, she would not only be able to lead the Alluring Foxes toward a new future but would also be able to suppress the various branches and fortify her control over the Alluring Foxes!","Lin Yuan did not place his hand on Kong Huan’s body immediately to refine her bloodline with the Body of All Spirits.","Unlike in the past, Lin Yuan no longer hid his secret weapons in the main world. This was because there was nothing in the main world that could endanger him.","But once he went to the unknown environment that was the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan would need to do his best to ensure that his secret weapons were not exposed.","Lin Yuan asked Kong Huan in a low voice, “What type of resources do you usually need to refine your bloodline?”","Kong Huan hurriedly replied, “My Lord, the best way for lifeforms like us that use spirit qi as our main source of energy to evolve our bloodline is to absorb pure spirit qi. The spirit qi will nourish and refine our bloodlines.","“Although other methods will also be able to evolve our bloodlines, they always come with drawbacks. A light consequence would be our bloodline being unable to evolve any further in the future. A serious consequence would be our bloodlines becoming contaminated or the emergence of harmful mutations.”"]},{"number":2778,"title":"Chapter 2778 Above Divine Kingdom!","paragraphs":["2778 Above Divine Kingdom!","Kong Huan did not understand why Lin Yuan asked her such a question.","It was evident that Spring had extracted her bloodline to give to Lin Yuan, so he should have realized this after examining the bloodline.","Frankly, Kong Huan could have replied to Lin Yuan with her first two statements. She only added the two statements at the end because she did not want Lin Yuan to use a special method to forcefully evolve her bloodline. She did not want to suffer any negative side effects after doing so.","The inability to advance her bloodline was already torture to Kong Huan. It left her no choice but to make do with the current benefits that her bloodline brought her. She could not compete with the new Alluring Foxes, who were born with more excellent bloodlines.","If her luck got any worse and her bloodline ended up being contaminated, she would have to grapple with her bloodline backfiring on her.","Having one’s bloodline backfire on oneself was no joking matter! She would get off easy if her body deteriorated. But in the worst-case scenario, she would become a monster that was neither fox nor demon!","The Sky Beyond the Clouds was very accommodating. If an expert could not thrive in one universe, they could move to another universe to jumpstart their development. This was just like how the Alluring Foxes could move to the North Universe to seek a new source of support.","If Lin Yuan was going to use a technique that affected her potential in order to forcefully evolve her bloodline, Kong Huan would prefer to keep her bloodline at pinnacle Alluring Bones.","It was possible she would encounter an opportunity in the future that enabled her to evolve.","Nonetheless, these were all Kong Huan’s personal wishes. At the end of the day, she could not call the shots on her future developments.","After hearing this, Lin Yuan now understood that the resources needed by the lifeforms in the main world and Sky Beyond the Clouds were relatively similar.","As such, if he supplied Kong Huan with spirit qi crystals, her bloodline would be able to evolve within two years.","With this thought, Lin Yuan lifted his hand, and a spirit qi crystal appeared in his hand.","Lin Yuan tossed the spirit qi crystal at Kong Huan and asked, “If you are provided with spirit qi of such purity, how long will it be before your bloodline evolves?”","It was true that Lin Yuan had a certain level of understanding of the Sky Beyond the Clouds. However, his understanding of most matters was only superficial. Hence, he needed to hear from the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ lifeforms in order to confirm his ideas.","For example, he now needed to confirm with Kong Huan how many spirit qi crystals she needed in order to evolve her bloodline from pinnacle Alluring Bones to Alluring Soul. But the next time he encountered a similar situation, he would know how many spirit qi crystals to offer in the negotiation.","When Lin Yuan took out the spirit qi crystal, Kong Huan did not know what it was.","As Morbius’ grade increased, the spirit qi crystals produced by the Pure Land of Bliss increased in concentration of spirit qi. Their ability to hide the aura of the spirit qi within also improved. Unless one’s body made contact with the spirit qi crystal, it would be very difficult to discover the spirit qi crystal’s effects.","Lin Yuan saw this as a positive.","If the spirit qi crystal’s value was obvious, any faction would try to use it as a bargaining chip during their negotiations.","Once Kong Huan’s hand touched the spirit qi crystal, her body shuddered.","Lin Yuan had asked her how many spirit qi crystals she needed in order to evolve her bloodline, but she could not give him a definitive answer before absorbing its spirit qi. This was because she had never absorbed such pure spirit qi before in her life.","“My Lord, I need to absorb the spirit qi crystal before coming up with an exact number. Once I’ve absorbed it and estimated the extent to which my bloodline has improved, I will be able to estimate a calculation.”","Lin Yuan nodded and replied, “Then you can go ahead and absorb it now! But before I give you more spirit qi crystals, you have to allow me to place my divine kingdom’s imprint on your divine kingdom and merge your fountain of faith with mine!”","The meaning behind Lin Yuan’s words was clear. He wanted to have complete and utter control over Kong Huan.","Kong Huan had already expected Lin Yuan to make such a request.","This was a humiliating act, and there were very few people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds who would agree to it.","Kong Huan had not even asked Fan Lou to swear his loyalty to her through his divine kingdom when she first took control of him. Otherwise, he would never have been able to betray her!","If Lin Yuan had made this request outright from the beginning, Kong Huan might not have agreed. After all, unlike Fan Lou, who was indecisively shifting between her and Feng Qing, she had the pride of an expert. Hence, she could not easily throw her pride aside to curry favor with others.","But now, Lin Yuan was giving her the chance to evolve her bloodline. On top of that, he was offering such pure spirit qi.","Based on the resources that Lin Yuan was offering, Kong Huan could guess the level of power that Lin Yuan wielded.","If he did not possess a large volume of such pure spirit qi, he would never be willing to give her the chance to use it. She was nothing more than a captive.","Lin Yuan was very generous. Kong Huan believed that he would definitely be able to bring enormous blessings to the Alluring Foxes.","Moreover, Lin Yuan possessed the Alluring Soul bloodline, which inconspicuously influenced Kong Huan and made it very difficult for her to say no to him.","There were plenty of potential benefits, and nothing worse could come out of this.","Kong Huan immediately said, “My Lord, I can swear my loyalty to you on my divine kingdom even if I don’t absorb the spirit qi crystal!”","To Kong Huan’s memory, Lin Yuan was not strong. He had not even reached the level of being able to open his divine kingdom.","But since he had made such a request, it meant he had already opened his divine kingdom.","Kong Huan thought, This Lord I’m about to pledge my loyalty to must be a sly fox who likes to hide his true power to deceive others.","Kong Huan could not think of any other reasons.","She summoned a miniature version of her divine kingdom from her soul.","A kingdom shrouded in amber light appeared in front of Lin Yuan. It looked like an intricate model.","When Lin Yuan looked closer at the divine kingdom, he realized he could look at its details by directing his spiritual energy at one of its parts.","Lin Yuan suddenly discovered that Kong Huan’s divine kingdom had deriviated to a considerable extent but it did not have any holy spirits.","Lin Yuan never expected his divine kingdom level to exceed that of a Divine Kingdom expert by such a large extent!","Kong Huan could sense that Lin Yuan was investigating her divine kingdom.","As the owner of the divine kingdom, Kong Huan had the ability to destroy Lin Yuan’s spiritual energy that was infesting her divine kingdom. Not only did she not do this, but she intentionally put her divine kingdom on display as well.","Kong Huan was very proud of the development of her divine kingdom.","Once Lin Yuan finished looking through Kong Huan’s divine kingdom, he asked, “Your divine kingdom has already reached the Higher Divine Kingdom level. How long will it take before your divine kingdom advances?”","Suddenly, Kong Huan did not know how to reply to Lin Yuan.","Faith power was needed to evolve one’s divine kingdom. The purer the faith that another lifeform felt toward one, the more faith power they would supply.","The species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds sought faith more than resources.","The Snow-Covered Foxes took in many dependent species from various universes because they wanted to obtain the dependent species’ faith power.","Faith power would only arise when a lifeform truly submitted to another lifeform. Hence, it was very difficult to obtain faith power by force.","Around 20,000,000 years ago, one of the Bloodians’ branches had gone down the wrong path. They had been powerful and captured weaker branches by force before using various extreme tactics to force these weaker branches to give up their faith power.","At first, using force to extract faith power had been effective. But as time went on, the forcefully extracted faith power had affected the roots of these Bloodians and led to the demise of these once-famous Bloodians.","After this incident, there were no more instances of unorthodox methods being used to obtain faith power.","The Alluring Foxes had a substantial internal conflict. Kong Huan’s influence had significantly diminished, so she obtained faith power at a much slower rate than before.","The Sky Beyond the Clouds’ districts had a pyramid structure. The more powerful the species, the easier it would be for them to obtain faith power.","The weaker species would not dare to nurture dependent species in the same carefree manner that the powerful species did.","If a species had a number of dependent species that did not match their power, it would not be long before trouble struck!","Given the circumstances, if she had not met Lin Yuan, Kong Huan believed that she would not be able to evolve her divine kingdom even after hundreds of thousands of years passed.","Even evolving to Pinnacle Divine Kingdom was a goal nowhere in sight, much less evolving above the Divine Kingdom level!","But now that she met Lin Yuan, if her bloodline could reach Alluring Soul grade, there would be no Alluring Fox that could touch her position.","Once the Alluring Foxes went to the North Universe, she would be able to use her Alluring Soul bloodline to flourish. Her Divine Kingdom level might be able to evolve after a few tens of thousands of years. As for above the Divine Kingdom level, she could not dream of reaching that level even if her bloodline reached Alluring Soul grade.","Kong Huan truthfully told Lin Yuan about her situation, and he nodded.","However, his furrowed brow did not relax.","When Spring saw this, she guessed that Lin Yuan wanted to obtain information from Kong Huan’s answers.","Spring thought a little deeper and guessed that Lin Yuan wanted to ask what was after the Divine Kingdom level.","Spring told Lin Yuan through her soul voice, “Lord Saint, after the Divine Kingdom level, there is the Holy Spirit level. The most basic requirement for the Holy Spirit level is the presence of a holy spirit that manages the divine kingdom on the owner’s behalf. Once one reaches the Holy Spirit level, one will have the right to venture out of the Sky Beyond the Clouds!”","When Lin Yuan heard this, not only did his eyebrows not relax, but they were furrowed even deeper.","At that moment, Lin Yuan realized that his divine kingdom was utterly disorderly! His divine kingdom already had a holy spirit!","Technically, he was already a Holy Spirit expert.","However, his true power was only at the birth horoscope level.","Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter had never asked about his divine kingdom and did not know the exact circumstances of his divine kingdom. Otherwise, they would already have mentioned the level above the Divine Kingdom level to him.","There was no way that having such a divine kingdom could be a bad thing.","Lin Yuan had already accepted his status as the Saint. It was likely that this was a gift left behind by his previous life.","Going forward, Lin Yuan was going to attempt to use his fountain of faith to find ways to take control of the fountains of faith of other Divine Kingdom experts.","He could show his uncertainty to Kong Huan because his bloodline was sufficient to induce her submission.","However, there was no way that he could show his uncertainty to Fan Lou. When it came to someone like Fan Lou, who was always seeking out the most powerful entities, he could only keep Fan Lou in line by putting on as strong of a front as he could!","Lin Yuan’s spiritual energy landed on Kong Huan’s fountain of faith, and he circulated his divine kingdom.","In an instant, powerful faith power burst out from Lin Yuan’s fountain of faith and enveloped Kong Huan’s fountain of faith.","Without Lin Yuan having to do anything, his fountain of faith left an imprint on Kong Huan’s fountain of faith.","With this imprint, Lin Yuan could use his fountain of faith to seal off all the faith power in Kong Huan’s fountain of faith.","The instant Lin Yuan activated his divine kingdom to control Kong Huan, she sensed a special aura from his divine kingdom. A moment later, Kong Huan felt certain that this was the aura of a holy spirit!","There were Holy Spirit experts in the Honor Absent Palace, and Kong Huan had sensed the aura of holy spirits in the past, so she was not unfamiliar with it.","Since she sensed the aura of a holy spirit, it meant that Lin Yuan had to be a Holy Spirit expert at the very least. It also was possible he was even more powerful. This was because the holy spirit aura she sensed from his divine kingdom was even stronger than any holy spirit aura she had sensed in the past.","The faith power in Lin Yuan’s fountain of faith was extremely pure. Kong Huan was very curious to find out how he had obtained such pure faith power.","Just how many dependent species did he have to take in to attain such pure faith power?","Lin Yuan did not know what Kong Huan was thinking. If he did, he would mumble to himself, “Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter have provided way too much faith power to me!”","The faith power from the four of them had caused the volume of faith power in Lin Yuan’s fountain of faith to multiply many times."]},{"number":2779,"title":"Chapter 2779 Morbius’ Transformation!","paragraphs":["2779 Morbius’ Transformation!","This was why Lin Yuan possessed such rich and abundant faith power.","However, it was not only related to Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter. Even without them, Lin Yuan’s faith power would still be far greater and purer than that of Kong Huan!","In Kong Huan’s eyes, a Class 2 world was insignificant. However, Lin Yuan’s faith power came from the humans, sea clans, and feys of this Class 2 world!","Lin Yuan had saved the main world when it was only a Class 1 world.","Ever since he became the Moon Empress’ disciple, his trajectory had continued climbing upward, and he received the idolization of all the youths in the Radiance Federation. It was then that Lin Yuan first began accumulating faith power.","Lin Yuan was a young hero in the Radiance Federation who had saved Millstone Town.","The faith power that he had accumulated on every step of his journey was extremely pure.","The dots of faith in the fountain of faith that represented people who first began worshiping him had only grown brighter.","It was very unlikely for such pure faith to exist in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan had used Morbius’ Klein Hub to enter the marsh world and open up new lands. In the process, he discovered the marsh world’s secrets and used the Abundance Treasure Tree to take control of all the lifeforms in the marsh world.","The lifeforms from the marsh world provided Lin Yuan with solid faith power that only grew with time.","Even if the new dimensional lifeforms felt animosity toward humans, Lin Yuan was never their target, and they continued to see him as a god. After being taught by the older generation of dimensional lifeforms, all of them became Lin Yuan’s believers.","The same situation took place in the abyssal, water, alien insect, and subterranean worlds.","Lin Yuan collected the dimensional worlds’ faith by taking control of them. On the other hand, he collected faith from the main world and sea clans by saving them.","Lin Yuan’s method of collecting faith power could not be replicated by other lifeforms.","Firstly, no one else had Lin Yuan’s body composition or Morbius. They also did not have the identity of the Saint. Hence, they were unable to create as many miracles.","When Lin Yuan saw Kong Huan’s amazed expression, he felt that it would be better for him to collect faith power from Class 1, 2, and 3 worlds instead of the Sky Beyond the Clouds. It would be easier for him to collect faith power from these worlds, and the faith power would also be purer.","The Endless Gems existed in the dimensional worlds.","However, Morbius needed to use its root power to combine the Endless Gems to create treasures like the Abundance Treasure Tree, Earth Source Cube, and Tide Herb Treasure Conch. Even if others got their hands on one or two Endless Gems, they would not be able to use the treasures to take control of the dimensional worlds.","Previously, Lin Yuan was unaware of this. He only found out by accident after speaking to Spring.","Now that her fountain of faith had Lin Yuan’s imprint, Kong Huan was Lin Yuan’s subordinate.","As Lin Yuan’s subordinate, Kong Huan began absorbing the spirit qi crystal.","As the pure spirit qi entered her body, Kong Huan closed her eyes happily.","At that moment, Kong Huan felt as though she was at a summer festival and had just taken a sip of a cold drink.","She could clearly sense that his pure spirit qi was beneficial for her body.","It could be said that this was the first time she was feeling her bloodline improve at such a rapid rate.","When she was done absorbing the spirit qi crystal, Kong Huan began telling Lin Yuan about the state of her body, “My Lord, given my current state, my bloodline will be able to evolve after I absorb another 7,500 spirit qi crystals!”","Lin Yuan nodded.","7,500 spirit qi crystals were not a large amount to him, and he could offer it with ease.","Lin Yuan did not hesitate to take out a brocade box that contained around 8,000 spirit qi crystals. He handed these spirit qi crystals to Kong Huan.","“I will give you around 500 extra spirit qi crystals. Use these spirit qi crystals and evolve your bloodline as quickly as possible. If you have any other needs, you can tell them to me directly.”","When Kong Huan heard what Lin Yuan said, she bowed to him with delight. “My Lord, the Alluring Foxes and I will be relying on you to nurture us in the future!”","Power and strength had undeniable benefits. This allowed Lin Yuan to acquire Kong Huan.","Currently, Kong Huan could be described as being devoted to Lin Yuan.","After Spring led Kong Huan away, she led Fan Lou in.","Fan Lou’s body currently contained the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf bloodline. He had even consumed the Light Wolf Fruits, but the Light Wind Wolf bloodline could not compete with the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf bloodline.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were able to take in so many wolf species as dependent species in the East Universe because they were sufficiently capable.","The Chaos Wind Demon Wolf bloodline came from the Moon-Worshiping Wolf bloodline. In the past, the Moon-Worshiping Wolves were a high and mighty species. They even had a Holy Spirit expert once.","If the Moon-Worshiping Wolves did not end up clashing with that faerie, they would never have fallen so far!","Faeries looked after their own and were domineering. Any species that threatened Faerie Institution’s overall profits would immediately be subdued by Faerie Institution.","There were factions in the past that were displeased with Faerie Institution. However, regardless of how they felt, none dared to express their unhappiness.","The demise of the Moon-Worshiping Wolves had opened the opportunity for Faerie Institution to rise up.","Fan Lou’s bloodline was not worth nurturing.","At first, Winter wanted to nurture Fan Lou and awaken the Moon-Worshiping Wolf bloodline. However, this would cost far too many resources. Fan Lou was not worth all those resources.","Lin Yuan nurtured his subordinates so they could provide him with profits. If the cost exceeded the profits, it would be a foolish endeavor.","Kong Huan was an Alluring Fox and could call the shots among them. She was their mouthpiece. If she did not possess considerable status among the Alluring Foxes, she would not have been chosen as the member of the Honor Absent Parliament.","Fan Lou did not have much potential that was worth developing. Hence, there was no need to put as much emphasis on nurturing him as on Kong Huan.","As long as he was promised some benefits, he would follow Lin Yuan around like an obedient puppy.","Kong Huan had mentioned that Fan Lou had betrayed her for the sake of profits. She was the one who had nurtured and given him his start.","Spring and Winter could not feel any positive feelings toward someone like this who abandoned their previous leader.","If anyone tried to convince them to abandon Lin Yuan, Spring and Winter would never agree.","Fan Lou was nervous and anxious as he faced Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan said, “You should be familiar with Kong Huan. She is now my subordinate. Are you interested in becoming my subordinate as well?","“If you become my subordinate, I can promise that you’ll be able to take over Kong Huan’s position as a member of the Honor Absent Parliament. What do you think?”","Fan Lou was over the moon.","Becoming a member of the Honor Absent Parliament was a pipe dream for Fan Lou. He never dared to have such aspirations in the past.","Once he became a member, he would be able to use his bloodline to develop his species.","Fan Lou was aware that his bloodline was extremely weak. But once he became a member of the Honor Absent Parliament, he would be able to join his bloodline to that of a powerful female lifeform to improve the bloodline of his offspring. Through this, his descendants’ bloodlines would become better and continue to pass on the improved bloodline.","Fan Lou never dared to dream of such a luxury.","But now, Lin Yuan’s promise stirred up his ambitions considerably. Fan Lou knew that if he wanted to obtain benefits, he would have to buckle down and work hard for Lin Yuan.","Hence, Fan Lou said sincerely, “My Lord, if there’s anything you need, just let me know. I will definitely do all I can to meet your requests. I won’t disappoint you!”","Lin Yuan nodded with satisfaction when he heard what Fan Lou said.","Fan Lou was the guide to the main world. It would be difficult for him to explain what had happened now that Kong Huan had killed so many people.","If Feng Qing wanted to escape persecution and continue to be valued by Feng Qing when he returned to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would have to bring back useful resources with him. Otherwise, once he returned, he would have no choice but to wait to be eliminated.","Fan Lou felt that he needed to tell Lin Yuan about all this.","The resources that he would have to show Feng Qing once he returned to the Sky Beyond the Clouds would also have to come from Lin Yuan.","After listening, Lin Yuan waved his hands and said, “I will prepare the resources you will need when you return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. As for what you will say when you return, that’s up to you! With your intelligence, I shouldn’t have to teach you. The two Alluring Foxes will back you up. I am sure that given your relationship with the Alluring Foxes, no one will be suspicious of you if they support your claim.”","Lin Yuan did not give Fan Lou any promises and managed to use his fountain of faith to take control of him.","Not only was Fan Lou not upset over losing his freedom, but he was even happier than he was before. In his eyes, he had found an even stronger source of support.","It was true that Lin Yuan had also promised Fan Lou benefits.","Apart from giving him the chance to become a member of the Honor Absent Parliament, Lin Yuan also promised to give him more resources whenever he made a contribution or performed well in his tasks.","Lin Yuan did not give Fan Lou any benefits now, but his promises were extremely attractive. When Fan Lou received these resources, he could do many things that he was unable to do in the past.","Lin Yuan did not spend too long talking to Fan Lou. The two of them had already told Lin Yuan about the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Rather than speaking to Fan Lou, Lin Yuan could learn more information by speaking to Kong Huan.","The leader of a Boundary Patrol Team did not hold much sway in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Fan Lou’s true function was to use his identity as the captain of a Boundary Patrol Team to hide the evolution of feys in the main world.","...","Epoch God Palace on Four Seasons Mountain was maintained by Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter’s strength and was long ready to be evolved into a faerie.","Lin Yuan did intend to evolve Four Seasons Mountain into a faerie.","Based on its roots, Four Seasons Mountain’s roots could not be compared to that of Begin Lady back when it was the Gaea Begin River.","Lin Yuan had reason to suspect that once Four Seasons Mountain evolved into a faerie, it would immediately be born as a higher faerie.","Lin Yuan had been communicating with Begin Lady and had an understanding of the faerie bloodline. In his subsequent conversations with Spring, he now knew the implication of a faerie that was born with a high-class bloodline.","Almost all the elites of Faerie Institution were born as higher faeries.","Lin Yuan would need Fan Lou to cover up the evolution of his feys, the evolution of Sky City’s members’ feys, and the commotion caused by the Four Seasons Mountain’s evolution into a faerie.","...","Time flew by, and Lin Yuan finished going through all four palaces of Epoch God Palace.","As Morbius continuously absorbed the energy in Epoch God Palace, its roots became increasingly stronger.","Lin Yuan had been maintaining contact with Liu Jie, Wen Yu, the Moon Empress, and the rest. Otherwise, all of them would be worried about him disappearing for four to five months.","Lin Yuan did not have anything else to do and began drawing up his plans for Sky Beyond the Clouds.","His body composition could help spirit qi professionals raise their ranks, and he would be able to increase the power of his subordinates and companions very quickly. He could evolve feys by just throwing resources at them.","All the white-clothed followers’ feys were Bronze/Legend when they contracted them. With such a good foundation, their potential was boundless.","While Lin Yuan was in Epoch God Palace for the past four to five months, many humans and sea clan experts had gathered in the Startling Lines Continent.","Based on their backgrounds, they were housed in six newly built cities.","The six cities were now filled with spirit qi professionals who were waiting for Lin Yuan to help their feys evolve.","To Lin Yuan, these six cities were treasure troves of resources.","Under Mang Shui’s management, the manor in the north district had devolved into chaos.","The six cities were managed by the white-clothed followers and operated smoothly.","It went without saying that issues did arise. However, if the provokers did not learn their lesson after being warned by the white-clothed followers, they would be punished by having their faction’s ration of resources reduced.","After catching a few perpetrators and making an example out of them, even the biggest of troublemakers forced themselves to get along amicably with the others.","Almost all of the resources in the main world were supplied by the Radiance Federation.","If any faction stopped obtaining resources from the Radiance Federation, they would soon be left in the dust and never be able to recover.","...","Just as Lin Yuan felt that it was about time for Morbius to be done absorbing the last of the energy from the wall in Autumn’s palace, he felt his wrist grow hot.","Morbius lit up with a reddish-bronze light, and Morbius’ voice appeared in his head."]},{"number":2780,"title":"Chapter 2780 The Moon Empress’ Upgrade!","paragraphs":["2780 The Moon Empress’ Upgrade!","“Partner, it turns out that all my root energy was left here after I reincarnated alongside you! While I was absorbing the power, my memory recovered. I am about to fully unlock myself!","“This time, I will have to sleep for a few years. This slumber won’t affect the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s abilities, and it will be able to continue functioning as usual. The Spirit Lock spatial zone will only begin to transform once I awake from my slumber and inject my energy into it!”","At this point, Morbius paused.","Now that Morbius had recovered its memory, it was feeling many different emotions while speaking to Lin Yuan.","Its heart ached inexplicably for Lin Yuan.","Back then, it was this friend who had stepped forward and taken on the duty of being the rescuer.","Luckily, the sacred mountain merged with Lin Yuan’s soul when he reincarnated. Otherwise, the Saint’s reincarnation would not have taken place smoothly. Without the protection from the sacred mountain, Lin Yuan’s spiritual energy and soul could have been damaged during the reincarnation process.","If that had happened, Morbius would have chosen to end its own life.","But if it had done that, it would not have been able to meet and accompany Lin Yuan in his life.","Before it recovered its memory, Lin Yuan was Morbius’ closest companion. This did not change even now that it had recovered its memory!","Morbius knew that once it absorbed all this energy and was restored to its complete state, its abilities would improve tremendously.","At that time, it would be of even more help to Lin Yuan during their journeys.","However, this impending slumber would last for a few years, and Morbius would miss Lin Yuan while it was asleep.","With the memories from their previous life, Morbius felt as though it was reuniting with Lin Yuan.","Morbius knew that Lin Yuan had decided not to recover the memories from his past life.","Morbius did not think that this was a bad idea. He would only be able to break through without being affected by anything else and carve out a new path for himself if he was unencumbered by his past life’s memories.","If Lin Yuan accepted the previous Saint’s memories, he would inevitably be affected by these memories in the future.","It was possible that the paths Lin Yuan took in this life would allow him to reach unprecedented heights that went beyond that of his previous life.","The spirit fountain on the sacred mountain’s peak had transformed into Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom while the sacred mountain itself had fused with Lin Yuan’s body and was now a part of him.","Now that Morbius had recovered its memories, it could clearly sense that only Lin Yuan’s Body of All Spirits could merge perfectly with the sacred mountain and absorb all of its energy to nourish himself.","If the sacred mountain was paired with the other individuals, they might be able to use their bodies to absorb the sacred mountain by force, but it was highly probable that its energy would cause their bodies to mutate.","Going forward, if there was anything that Lin Yuan did not know, he would not have to ask Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter. Morbius could answer all the questions he had that pertained to basic knowledge.","As the Totem God, Morbius was always by the Saint’s side and knew more than Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter, who were only followers.","The three bloodlines that Lin Yuan had just used the Body of All Spirits to attain were decent and worth nurturing. Moreover, Lin Yuan already had the mermaid bloodline. As such, Lin Yuan’s physique had powerful combat abilities.","Lin Yuan’s heart skipped a beat when he heard that.","It was good news that Morbius had evolved after absorbing the energy in the wall illustrations. However, it would have to go into slumber for such a long time!","Ever since Morbius joined him, they had never been apart for more than a year. Morbius was not only his friend but also his shadow.","Lin Yuan was now used to discussing all his issues with Morbius. During their conversations, Lin Yuan could not only assess his decisions objectively, but Morbius would also offer new insights and perspectives.","Morbius sensed that Lin Yuan was feeling reluctant. In its semi-tangible form, Morbius appeared next to Lin Yuan and hugged him tightly.","“Partner, a temporary parting is necessary for a better union in the future.","“Judging by how things are going now, you should be preparing to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds by the time I awake. You will only be able to better protect our current world by heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and amassing power.","“Once the Abyss Beast returns, many people will become suspicious that so many members lost their lives in this Class 2 world. It’s true that Fan Lou will be able to hide the subsequent evolutions of feys, but once the other species become suspicious, they can send people secretly to the main world to investigate it.","“Suspicion and curiosity will convince the wealthy species to pay the price in exchange for searching for the truth. Unless you remain in this Class 2 world forever, such incidents could happen at any time!","“Once you arrive at the Sky Beyond the Clouds and gain sufficient power, you will be able to protect the Class 2 world. With your power looming over the Class 2 world, no one will dare to cause trouble for it.","“Additionally, once you leave, this Class 2 world will return to a state of peace. It is your presence that led to the creation of so many fantastical tales about this world. This world is lucky to be the host of your reincarnated life!”","Morbius was speaking objectively. It believed that without Lin Yuan, this world would be a regular Class 1 world.","Given that there were spirit-fire experts in this world, it would not be conquered by the dimensional worlds. As it continued to develop, there would be more and more spirit-fire experts as well. It was possible that they would eventually have been able to take over the dimensional worlds.","Of the five dimensional worlds, the abyssal world’s changes were the most largely attributed to Lin Yuan.","The changes in the alien insect world were due to the demon insects.","As Keira continued to develop the alien insects, she could have used them to awaken herself and subsequently proliferate the demon insects! Once the demon insects expanded, even a few spirit-fire experts would be no match for them. As such, if that happened, it was likely that the conflict would lead to the widespread death of the main world’s lifeforms.","Given that the demon insects had taken over the Class 1 world’s civilization, they would eventually try to promote the world to Class 2 on behalf of the original lifeforms.","That was the original playbook for this Class 2 world.","It was Lin Yuan’s presence that put the world on a different course.","Lin Yuan shook his head gently. He did not think that this world was lucky to host his reincarnation. Rather, he believed that he was the lucky one.","If he had not been born into this Class 1 world, he would never have met Chu Ci, the Moon Empress, Auntie Zhang, Uncle Li, Liu Jie, Wen Yu, and the rest of his friends. To Lin Yuan, these relationships were his most precious treasures.","Power made one strong, but it was not meant to allow one to recklessly break the rules. Instead, its purpose was to enable one to protect those who were precious to them. Relationships were the only thing that a person could possess for eternity.","After releasing each other from the hug, Lin Yuan said, “Partner, don’t worry about anything and go and sleep. By the time you awake, it should be time for us to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!”","Lin Yuan did not agree with what Morbius said about this world being lucky to have hosted his reincarnation. But he did agree with what Morbius said about him not being able to remain in the main world forever.","Lin Yuan’s protection of the main world should not limit his development.","It was true that he could only improve his protection of the main world by making a name for himself in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The experts from the Sky Beyond the Clouds were able to come to the main world on the Abyss Beast. This meant that Lin Yuan could do the same to return to the main world in the future.","...","Once Morbius fell asleep, Lin Yuan left for the Startling Lines Continent to begin collecting resources.","Spring remained at Epoch God Palace to watch over the visitors from the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan had given Kong Huan and Fan Lou permission to decide what to do with the visitors from the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Winter would wait until Kong Huan and Fan Lou had left with the rest of the visitors before going to the Radiance Federation to meet up with Lin Yuan.","Once he was done collecting resources and returned to the Radiance Federation, Lin Yuan would begin helping the Moon Empress, Cold Moon, Mystic Moon, and the rest to increase their strength.","When the Moon Empress went with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, she would definitely take Cold Moon and Mystic Moon with her.","With the Moon Empress’ current power, she would not be able to offer Lin Yuan much help in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","In truth, the Moon Empress’ current power could not hold a candle to that of Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan currently had four World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys. If these four feys decided to unleash mayhem, they could easily destroy this Class 2 world.","The Moon Empress might not be able to help Lin Yuan, but she was far more capable than Wen Yu when it came to governance.","Governance was an ability that was built up through time and experience. Most of Wen Yu’s skills were taught to her by Mystic Moon.","Mystic Moon was skilled at internal governance, while Cold Moon was skilled at external governance. External governance involved far more tasks, while internal governance was more complex.","Cold Moon was just as capable as Mystic Moon. In fact, she was more decisive than him when it came to handling issues.","When Cold Moon went with them to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Liu Jie could be left by her side for some time.","Sky City would only grow stronger in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, and Lin Yuan’s current pool of management talent was far from sufficient. He badly needed the Moon Empress’ help.","Lin Yuan could be certain that the Moon Empress would not hide any selfish intentions while helping him.","...","After the recent storm, the main world had entered a period of true peace.","Lin Yuan greatly enjoyed this peace.","Prior to this peace, Lin Yuan had been far too busy for far too long.","The trip to the Startling Lines Continent to collect spirit qi crystals went extremely smoothly, and another small mountain of spirit qi crystals now sat in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope got to work again. It was not just the main world that had undergone substantial changes. The same went for the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","...","Once Lin Yuan returned to the Radiance Federation, he went directly to the Radiant Moon Palace and handed the Moon Empress a fey storage box that contained 300,000 spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan said seriously, “Master, hold onto these spirit qi crystals. Don’t distribute them. Instead, use them to increase the power of your own feys! Try to evolve your feys to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom at the same time that you reach the Divine Kingdom level!”","Lin Yuan always kept his circumstances in check and was aware of the limitations. It would not be a good thing for World Emperor/Divine Kingdom experts to appear in the world when it was only a Class 2 world.","When Lin Yuan helped a lifeform to increase its power to the point that it exceeded the power of this world, this lifeform would be at the peak of the world. In such an event, it was highly possible that the lifeform’s mindset would change toward a negative trajectory. Possession of unrestrained power always clouded the mind.","Before Lin Yuan left the main world, he would help all the members of the Radiance Federation’s royalty to reach the spirit-fire level and give them a Divine Kingdom human weapon.","Red Thorn had stored away all the corpses of the invaders from the Sky Beyond the Clouds. It would use the Tongue of Relinquish to take control of these lifeforms.","With Red Thorn’s current power, it was difficult for it to use the Tongue of Relinquish to take control of World Emperor/intermediate Divine Kingdom experts, and it was unknown how much time would be needed to accomplish such a thing.","However, it would not be long before Lin Yuan increased Red Thorn’s power.","Once Red Thorn reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, it would be easy for it to take control of these World Emperor/Intermediate Divine Kingdom lifeforms.","The Moon Empress reached out and received the spatial equipment from Lin Yuan.","“Little Yuan, I will do my best to increase my power as soon as possible. I only hope that my meager power will be of help to you in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!”","Lin Yuan said earnestly, “Master, once we get to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, I will leave you in charge of managing Sky City while Wen Yu will support you. Most of Wen Yu’s abilities were taught to her by Mystic Moon. If you manage Sky City, Wen Yu will be able to learn more from Mystic Moon. That will give me more assurance!”","Lin Yuan wanted to develop Sky City but was not focused on its management. He preferred to be the creator of resources rather than the manager of a faction.","As the City Lord, Lin Yuan had always been a mouthpiece in name, while most of the heavy lifting of management fell on the shoulders of Wen Yu and Liu Jie.","When they departed, Sky City would surely strengthen rapidly. Wen Yu and Liu Jie alone would not be enough to hold down the fort.","Moreover, Wen Yu and Liu Jie were very prideful.","If Lin Yuan found another group of capable people from the Sky Beyond the Clouds to help manage Sky City, Wen Yu and Liu Jie would not only be indignant but would also grow doubtful.","Lin Yuan did not want such a thing to happen.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie would not feel any displeasure if the Moon Empress was the one to take over Sky City’s management.","The Moon Empress was stunned when she heard what he said. She never expected Lin Yuan to trust her with such an important matter.","The Moon Empress was always worried she would not be able to help Lin Yuan. Despite being his Master, she seemed to fulfill no crucial role in his life.","But now that she knew what she could do for Lin Yuan, the Moon Empress was elated. “Don’t worry, Little Yuan. Once we get to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, I will definitely do my best to help you manage Sky City!”"]},{"number":2781,"title":"Chapter 2781 Purple Afterglow’s Beauty Dispersion!","paragraphs":["2781 Purple Afterglow’s Beauty Dispersion!","The Moon Empress now felt at ease and could use Lin Yuan’s resources to evolve her feys without worries.","He had helped Liu Jie and Wen Yu to increase their strength extremely quickly, but helping the Moon Empress was a slow and long operation.","...","Eight months went by.","When the Moon Empress emerged from the quiet room, she was a pinnacle spirit-fire expert.","Lin Yuan did not help her break through to the Divine Kingdom level because Fan Lou had yet to return to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and could not help hide the accompanying signs of the evolution.","If he helped her break through now, it would attract more invaders from the Sky Beyond the Clouds to come to the main world to cause trouble. That would be very bad news!","Lin Yuan’s feys had also been breaking through continuously. Even Purple Afterglow, who never used to work hard, suddenly became diligent.","With the sea of resources provided by Morbius, it evolved from Suzerain/Myth II to Sovereign/Pinnacle Creation within eight months. It was now only a step away from reaching Immortal Breed.","Out of all the feys absorbing these outstanding resources, Purple Afterglow’s rate of evolution was the quickest. After all, unlike Green Vine, Lin Yuan’s other feys could not absorb energy and transform it into their own energy.","If Lin Yuan could use his body composition to evolve his feys, he could enable them to undergo a series of breakthroughs in a very short span of time.","The Moon Empress gently lifted her hands and sensed the new power flowing through her body.","A bittersweet feeling filled her heart.","Firstly, from the method that Lin Yuan used to increase her power, the Moon Empress realized that her previous increases in power had been minuscule.","All Lin Yuan did was place his hand on hers, and her power skyrocketed.","Previously, trying to awaken her birth horoscope had almost cost her her life.","The other members of royalty were unaware of the method by which Lin Yuan was helping her increase her power. If they found out, it was likely they would also feel a sense of bitter surrealness about their previous experiences of increasing their power.","Lin Yuan fully understood how the Moon Empress was feeling.","This was similar to his previous life when players promised themselves they would not spend money on cheat codes in a game, only to find out eventually that the players who spent their days grinding away and working hard were nothing more than entertaining fodder for the players that did spend money!","At that moment of realization, even the most strong-willed and passionate players would choose to give up on the game.","If Lin Yuan had not taken control of the marsh world and used the Samsara Realm Dictators to keep the Mirror God and God of Fools in check, the Radiance Federation would not have been able to fend off an attack from them.","Now, she had gone beyond spirit fire and was at pinnacle spirit fire.","It would not be long before Lin Yuan helped the Divine Kingdom level, a concept she had never even heard of in the past.","At that time, it was likely that the spirit-fire level would seem insignificant!","“Little Yuan, you’ve been here all this time helping me evolve. You must have many things to attend to. Go ahead and do them! I also need time to sense and experience my current power. Currently, I feel as though this power doesn’t belong to me.”","Lin Yuan chuckled.","This was exactly how he felt when he first awakened his birth horoscope. But it did not take him too long to adjust and become comfortable with his increased power.","It was true that there were many things that Lin Yuan needed to do.","Now that he had increased the Moon Empress’ power, Lin Yuan would go on to help Liu Jie and Wen Yu to increase their power.","During the past eight months, Lin Yuan’s own power had increased substantially as well. The stronger the person whose power he helped increase, the greater the feedback of energy he would obtain.","From this, Lin Yuan could see a path to rapid power growth.","...","After exiting the Radiant Moon Palace, Lin Yuan heard Purple Afterglow’s voice in his head.","Purple Afterglow was urging Lin Yuan to help it increase its power. He felt he needed to have a proper talk with Purple Afterglow so he could learn what had caused it to change its lazy ways and become as diligent as it was now!","Lin Yuan released Purple Afterglow.","This was one of the rare occasions where Purple Afterglow appeared before Lin Yuan in its human form. It had a pitiful and pleading expression hanging off its handsome countenance.","Lin Yuan was in no rush to ask Purple Afterglow his question because it was still talking to him in his head.","Lin Yuan first used True Data to check on Purple Afterglow.","[Fey Name]: Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly","[Fey Species]: Flash-butterfly species/scaled-butterfly species","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Spiritual/Soul","[Fey Quality]: Creation IX","Abilities:","[Flashing Scale Dance]: Its images will be formed from the scale powder released into the air. It will be able to flash back and forth between itself and the formed images. While it is traveling, it can absorb energy from its surroundings to quicken the production of scale powder.","[Scale Light Butterfly Image]: Scale powder in the wings will be used to refract light. When light fills its reflection, its charm will be boosted, and it will gain absolute control over butterfly-species feys.","[Beautiful God Hallucination]: When a target is being attracted and sees one as a beautiful god, one will be able to adjust according to the target’s features and pick a lifeform to turn into the target’s definition of unsightliness. If the target and the lifeform have a positive connection, it will disappear momentarily. If they do not have a positive connection, the target will attack the lifeform.","[Species Praised Beauty]: When attracting a target and receiving its worship, the target’s species will also be affected and instinctively feel positively about the Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly.","[Beautiful God Cutting Wings]: Flap its wings to produce sequential cutting attacks. A special Beautiful God Engraving will be formed on the target’s body. Every engraving requires 16 cutting attacks to be formed. The target with a formed Beautiful God Engraving will trigger its own emotions to the greatest extent. Anything related to energy will be prevented from moving in and out of the target’s body.","[Beauty Assessment Plundering]: When one’s beauty stupefies a species and takes over that species’ assessment of beauty, it can set the standard with its beauty and become the definition of beauty for that species. Besides itself, the species would not see any other lifeform as beautiful. It would not detest and be repulsed by lifeforms that previously met their standards of beauty.","[Beauty Dispersion]: When other feys feel love for it, their amazement and recognition of its beauty will turn into a special scale powder that can be used to increase the power of other butterfly-species lifeforms. (This is only effective on butterfly-species lifeforms with inferior bloodlines.)","Exclusive Skill:","[Scale Powder Halo]: The scale powder has strong reflective abilities, and the target that lays eyes on the scale powder will be affected by the reflection. The target will start to feel dizzy and experience temporary blindness.","[Soul Beauty Goddess]: By activating the power of the spirit and soul, the beauty will be increased to a limitless level. The target will be attracted and fall in love. The target will want everything of the object of its love on its body, and the target will want to collect everything connected to the object of its love.","[Beauty Reaches Every Species]: Each time it receives the recognition of a species and becomes their standard of beauty, its charm would be eternally strengthened.","[Extreme Mesmerization]: When the mesmerizing ability is used on an entity, it can give up its scale powder in exchange for boosting its mesmerizing ability.","When he saw the data, Lin Yuan could guess the reason for Purple Afterglow’s anxiousness.","Love was the reason!","The last time that Lin Yuan checked Purple Afterglow’s data, it had only been a Suzerain/Myth fey. But now, it was Sovereign X/Creation IX.","Purple Afterglow had only gained one new ability and exclusive skill. The new ability Beauty Dispersion would allow Purple Afterglow to utilize other lifeforms’ recognition of its beauty to create a special scale powder that could rapidly boost the power of other butterfly-species lifeforms.","It was likely that Purple Afterglow wanted to create as much of this scale powder as possible to improve the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","There was a limiting clause to Purple Afterglow’s use of its scale powder to strengthen the bloodline and power of other butterfly-species feys.","However, this limiting clause was not much of a restraint to Purple Afterglow.","It was unlikely that a butterfly-species fey with a superior bloodline to Purple Afterglow could be found in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, much less the main world!","Spring had seen Purple Afterglow and had felt incredulous at its existence. Spring saw Purple Afterglow’s bloodline as a miracle.","She confirmed that there were very few butterfly species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds that could compete with Purple Afterglow’s bloodline.","Now that Purple Afterglow’s power had increased, it could gather as many dependent species as it wanted in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The Sovereign ability, Beauty Dispersion, could be considered a functional-type ability. Meanwhile, Lin Yuan felt that the Creation Breed exclusive skill, Extreme Mesmerization, was a combat-type exclusive skill.","It significantly increased Purple Afterglow’s ability to mesmerize an entity. This meant that Purple Afterglow’s ability to mesmerize targets in combat had grown stronger.","In the past, when Purple Afterglow was still very weak, it could only use its scale powder to cause targets to lose their ability to sense elements.","But after the many evolutions that it had undergone, Purple Afterglow’s abilities now centered around mesmerization.","Extreme Mesmerization significantly increased Purple Afterglow’s combat abilities. It could now use mesmerization to take control of and kill targets.","Purple Afterglow was madly in love with its partner.","As its de facto father, Lin Yuan could not refuse such a request.","Lin Yuan said, “Purple Afterglow, focus on increasing your own power for now. Later, I will prioritize evolving you to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom. You will be just as powerful as the Jasmine Lily and Blackie!","“Once we get to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, you can collect dependent species freely. The Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s power won’t be lagging either! If you are in a rush to increase the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s power, it will be much easier for me to help to increase its power than for you to do it!”","Purple Afterglow hurriedly expressed to Lin Yuan that it wanted to use its own abilities to increase the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s power.","...","After soothing Purple Afterglow, Lin Yuan returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion.","He had yet to reveal the fact that he could use his body composition to raise the ranks of spirit qi professionals.","After he was done helping Wen Yu and Liu Jie to increase their power, he intended to contact Zong Ze, Gu Lang, Xia Qing, Gao Feng, and the rest to ask if they wanted to venture to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","In the past, he never considered Zong Ze, Gu Lang, Gao Feng, and the rest when he made his plans to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","This was because they lacked power and because he was unable to help them become powerful enough to handle the journey that he was going to embark on.","But now that he had gained such abilities, it went without saying he could begin taking them into consideration!","Wen Yu and Liu Jie already heard Lin Yuan’s news.","Not long ago, they had been overjoyed at becoming S-rank spirit qi professionals.","Yet now, Lin Yuan was giving them the chance to become experts who were as powerful as the Moon Empress! This was an opportunity they had never even dared to dream of in the past!","The stronger they became, the more they would be able to accomplish.","When they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, they would only be able to help Lin Yuan manage the new subordinates they gathered if they themselves possessed great power.","If Lin Yuan’s new subordinates were much stronger than them, Liu Jie and Wen Yu would run into many issues while managing them.","While Liu Jie and Wen Yu were both eager to increase their power, Wen Yu allowed Liu Jie to go first. This was because she knew that his yearning to increase his power was stronger than her own.","...","While Lin Yuan was helping Liu Jie to increase his power, Winter watched Kong Huan, the two Alluring Foxes, and Fan Lou climb onto the Abyss Beast’s back before departing to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","When Kong Huan and Fan Lou were first captured by Lin Yuan, they had been bitter enemies. Kong Huan hated Fan Lou for betraying her while Fan Lou was terrified that she had ill intent toward him and would seize any opportunity to kill him!","But now, the two of them knew that they were both under Lin Yuan’s control and could not lay a hand on each other. As such, they decided to work together and had a collaborative relationship.","When they returned to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, they would watch each other’s backs and do their best to ensure that everything went smoothly!","Kong Huan would create some issues that would shift the attention of the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ factions away from Fan Lou and this Class 2 world."]},{"number":2782,"title":"Chapter 2782 Heart Mushroom Disrupts Heaven!","paragraphs":["2782 Heart Mushroom Disrupts Heaven!","Next, Kong Huan would lead the Alluring Foxes in following the Snow-Covered Fox envoy to the North Universe, where they would make a new home for themselves.","Previously, Kong Huan felt some trepidation toward the migration to the North Universe. She was concerned that once they went there, they would be at the mercy of the Snow-Covered Foxes and be reduced to puppets.","But now that her bloodline had evolved from pinnacle Alluring Bones to Alluring Soul, Kong Huan was confident that her bloodline was strong enough to enable the Alluring Foxes to stand firmly on their own despite being linked to the Snow-Covered Foxes!","Confidence came from power. Kong Huan’s current state exemplified this statement to the tee!","However, an increase in power was not the only thing that led to increased confidence. Fan Lou was currently feeling even more confident than Kong Huan.","Now that they were Lin Yuan’s subordinates, he no longer feared her in the slightest!","If they encountered issues, Fan Lou would use the excuse of Kong Huan being stronger to dump all the responsibility on her to handle!","The two of them had not seen Lin Yuan before they left. However, Winter spoke on behalf of Lin Yuan and told Kong Huan to look out for Fan Lou when they returned to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Winter said this because he knew Kong Huan still felt resentful toward Fan Lou.","Furthermore, with Kong Huan’s current status in the East Universe, it was easy for her to help Fan Lou secure his position as the captain of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team.","Fan Lou needed to continue holding this position to help Lin Yuan protect the Class 2 world.","Winter knew just how important this Class 2 world was to Lin Yuan.","Winter never expected Fan Lou to use his words to threaten Kong Huan, however!","Fan Lou was sure that not only would Kong Huan not be angered by his actions but would even do her best to help him.","In the past, given Kong Huan’s temper, she would never have tolerated Fan Lou.","But now, she had developed an extremely high level of tolerance for him.","This tolerance came from a change in Kong Huan’s mindset.","She was no longer bothered by Fan Lou. Rather, she had set her sights on broader ambitions!","Kong Huan’s head was filled with thoughts about how she could develop the Alluring Foxes.","Fan Lou’s bloodline had not been extracted, and Lin Yuan had not given him any spirit qi crystals. It was clear that he had no intention to invest in Fan Lou, so the latter would inevitably become a peripheral figure in Lin Yuan’s circle.","At that time, she could eliminate Fan Lou if she still wanted to do so.","However, Kong Huan felt that even when the time came, she would be uninterested in wasting her time and energy on an insignificant character like Fan Lou. Targeting him would only prove to others that she was petty.","...","Kong Huan had already decided to leave the East Universe. When an explanation needed to be given, Kong Huan took responsibility for almost everything and every issue.","This caused her status in the Honor Absent Parliament to be lowered, and she was reduced to a minor role.","Normally, there was nothing that Kong Huan cared more about than her position in the Honor Absent Parliament.","But now, this was meaningless to her.","In order to not draw suspicion to herself, Kong Huan acted utterly downtrodden during the meeting.","Fan Lou and Kong Huan’s deception managed to deceive the majority.","However, a small group of people could not shake their suspicions.","Almost all the resources that Kong Huan and Fan Lou brought back went toward compensating the other members of parliament.","Meanwhile, Fan Lou gave Feng Qing the private resources that he had prepared.","Winter had handed Fan Lou and Kong Huan the main world’s resources. They came off as both precious but not overly stunning.","Kong Huan and Fan Lou stated that they had emptied the Class 2 world of all its resources.","Even those who remained suspicious did not continue to pay attention to an empty Class 2 world.","However, Kong Huan and Fan Lou still followed the plan and caused some issues to distract the other members of the Honor Absent Parliament.","Kong Huan tried to assassinate Fan Lou. The assassination was never meant to succeed. Both Kong Huan and Fan Lou were aware of this.","However, Kong Huan’s assassination attempt on Fan Lou was the best way to express her hatred toward him. This would remove all suspicion that Fan Lou had betrayed Feng Qing and rejoined Kong Huan.","In order to hammer the nail into the coffin, Kong Huan injured Fan Lou’s roots.","After all, Feng Qing would heal Fan Lou’s injured roots.","She did not use her bloodline power to attack Fan Lou, as these injuries healed easily.","Her assassination attempt on Fan Lou was enough for the latter to secure Feng Qing’s trust.","Kong Huan paid a significant price for her assassination attempt—the Bloodians supporting the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves gave the Alluring Foxes a warning.","Kong Huan knew that the Alluring Foxes were going to leave for the North Universe very soon.","Now that the day was almost upon them, Kong Huan felt a twinge of reluctance to leave the East Universe! This was where she was born and raised.","Kong Huan still had more than 5,000 of the spirit qi crystals Lin Yuan had given her. She intended to use them to increase the power of the young Alluring Foxes in her branch.","...","At first, Feng Qing had suspected that Fan Lou had rejoined Kong Huan.","Even if he believed that Fan Lou brought him luck, Feng Qing was unwilling to continue using a suspicious subordinate.","On this trip that was led by Fan Lou, the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf warriors and two Bloodians died in the abyss.","During the return journey, the Abyss Beast had been grievously injured and died shortly after arriving in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","However, there had been no abyssal pirates in the East Universe’s vicinity in the past few years. There was no reason to explain how a lone Abyss Beast was suddenly ambushed by an abyssal pirate.","However, Kong Huan’s assassination attempt on Fan Lou fully squashed all of Feng Qing’s suspicions. If he had not stepped in to stop her, Fan Lou would have died at her hands.","As such, there was no need for him to continue suspecting Fan Lou.","Moreover, Fan Lou had secretly brought back a large stash of resources for him. These resources were sufficient to move Feng Qing!","If Fan Lou had any traitorous intentions, he could have hidden these resources away. Why would he still hand them over? Many of these resources could be used to increase one’s power!","Feng Qing was increasingly satisfied with Fan Lou and personally helped him to heal his injuries.","Subsequently, he enabled Fan Lou to once again be appointed as the captain of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team. He also sent two Chaos Wind Demon Wolf warriors to guard Fan Lou’s residence before making a personal trip to Kong Huan’s palace to give her a stern warning and ensure she would stop pursuing Fan Lou.","When he was speaking with Kong Huan, she bickered and picked on him like she always did. But for some reason, Feng Qing found it very difficult to become angry at her, and he could not help but lower his tone when he spoke to her.","Moreover, in spite of her fury, Kong Huan decided not to pursue the matter.","From a certain perspective, the Alluring Foxes were the victims.","Feng Qing did not realize that after just one meeting with Kong Huan, he began to stand in her shoes and consider things from her perspective.","...","Winter used his body composition to produce a jade that was cold to the touch. He had told Fan Lou to crush this jade if he encountered any issues. If he managed to be reappointed as the captain of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team and could hide the happenings in the main world, he must inject his own energy into the jade. Winter would be able to sense all of this!","Wen Yu’s Thoughts Letter Paper could send messages to and from all areas of the main world. However, it was impossible to use it to send messages between the main world and the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Even if the Elemental Paper was World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, it would be difficult for it to break past the main world’s world wills, as well as the abyss that surrounded the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Winter sensed that Fan Lou had injected his energy into the gem and immediately informed Lin Yuan of this.","By now, Lin Yuan had helped Wen Yu and Liu Jie reach pinnacle spirit fire. Liu Jie’s Insect Queen and Wen Yu’s Elemental Paper were also using spirit qi crystals to evolve.","Lin Yuan remembered that Purple Afterglow wanted to increase its power and had planned on evolving it into World Emperor/Divine Kingdom first.","However, Purple Afterglow was currently accompanying the Kill Food Sky Butterfly, which had consumed Purple Afterglow’s scale powder and was evolving its bloodline. Purple Afterglow wanted to wait until the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s bloodline had evolved before it increased its strength.","Lin Yuan always saw Purple Afterglow as his son and gladly tolerated his exaggerated devotion.","Hence, Lin Yuan decided to nurture the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom first.","At first, Lin Yuan only used the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to interrogate other lifeforms as it could discern whether the lifeforms were telling the truth or if they were lying.","But once the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom gained Heart Mushroom Sky Questioning, its function now exceeded just that of interrogation. At crucial moments, it could help Lin Yuan escape from sticky situations and ask the world wills for a way to benefit from his current circumstances!","This exclusive skill caused Lin Yuan to see the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom as a foundational fey. Otherwise, given all of Lin Yuan’s feys, nurturing it would not be such a priority!","Lin Yuan summoned the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom had been absorbing spirit qi crystals and the elemental pearls that were cultivated by the Deposit Vegetable Pods.","Now, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom had reached Sovereign X/Creation IX.","From this, Lin Yuan could tell that for feys, evolving from Sovereign to High Sovereign and from Creation Breed to Immortal Breed were large obstacles that were extremely challenging to overcome!","Purple Afterglow was also stuck at the same grade and quality.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s size remained the same even after it evolved to Sovereign/Creation and attached itself to Lin Yuan’s sleeve, right above the Source Sand.","Because of its small size, the complex patterns on its body could not be seen clearly by the naked eye.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom.","[Fey Name]: Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom","[Fey Species]: Parasitic fungus species/flaming fungus species","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Fire","[Fey Quality]: Creation IX","Abilities:","[Seeping Flames]: The flames will seep into the target’s mind, spirit, and soul through the heart and brain. The spirit and soul will begin to burn. If the flames begin to die out, it can absorb the energy from the heart and brain to reignite itself.","[Body-Penetrating Flames]: When burning the mind, spirit, and soul, the flames will also burn the body. The damage will be translated from the elemental form to the physical. Before the fire in its mind, spirit, and soul was extinguished, the flames afflicting the body will continue to cause harm.","[Thought-Separating Flames]: When burning the target’s mind, spirit, and soul, if the target’s mind, spirit, and soul have any thoughts or feelings linked to another lifeform, the thoughts would become a guide that allows the flames to extend.","[Strengthened Spores]: The fungi produced will be strengthened and be able to absorb and take control of more energy. The fungi will be deeply rooted in the target’s soul and be more difficult to remove.","[Truth Colony]: When questioning a target, the precise answers given will grow a truth colony. When the colony absorbs energy, it will grow into a truth mushroom. When the truth mushroom is fed to a target, the target will be forced to tell the truth, making it easier to obtain true answers to questions.","[False Colony]: When questioning a target, every lie told by the target will produce a false colony. When the false colony absorbs energy, it will grow into a false mushroom. When the false mushroom is fed to a target, the target will be unable to break while questioning, preventing them from answering questions.","[Interrogation Soul Flames]: After confirming that the target has made more than three false statements, the target can be asked a question, and the soul with fungi rooted in it will be sacrificed. The target will have to tell the truth through the voiced spirit form.","[Truth and Lie Temptation]: Each time truth and lie are discerned, it can store the sincerity and falseness. The sincerity can be used to boost its soul and defend it against temptation abilities. The falseness can be used to boost its temptation abilities and strengthen its ability to tempt targets.","Exclusive Skill:","[Honesty Reflects the Heart]: The spores will host themselves deep within the target’s spirit and soul and determine the genuineness of the target’s exterior.","[Crumbled Parasitic Cycle]: The bacterial strain will be sacrificed. After being sacrificed, the energy around it will crumble, along with other energy-containing entities.","[Heart Mushroom Sky Questioning]: When a judgment cannot be made on an issue, one can be staked to question the sky and ask for a positive solution.","[Heart Mushroom Disrupts Heaven]: When other life forms use various methods to ask the world wills for answers, it can use its energy to disrupt the world wills and prevent the world wills from answering other life forms. Alternatively, it can incite the world wills to give wrong answers.","Lin Yuan could not see the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s appearance clearly after its evolution. Hence, he placed all his attention on its new ability and exclusive skill.","When its new exclusive skill, Heart Mushroom Disrupts Heaven appeared, Lin Yuan’s hopes for the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom expanded. It could be said that Lin Yuan would not be surprised at whatever abilities it went on to attain!","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s new ability and exclusive skill brought Lin Yuan significant surprise and happiness.","This was especially due to the Creation Breed exclusive skill, Heart Mushroom Disrupts Heaven!"]},{"number":2783,"title":"Chapter 2783 Divine Kingdom Ability [Reverse Colony]!","paragraphs":["2783 Divine Kingdom Ability [Reverse Colony]!","Heart Mushroom Disrupts Heaven would allow the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to block heavenly intervention. When other lifeforms prayed to the heavens for answers, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom would disrupt their reception of the answers or even incite the world wills to lie to them.","If an enemy’s search for answers was blocked or falsified by the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom, it could cause the enemy to go down a path of ruin with no return!","At crucial moments, this ability would allow the enemy to lose their will to resist.","Aside from Heart Mushroom Disrupts Heaven, the Sovereign ability, Truth and Lie Temptation, was also extremely useful to Lin Yuan.","While the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom was discerning truth and lies, Truth and Lie Temptation would allow it to use sincerity to boost its own soul and strengthen its resistance to temptation abilities while using falseness to boost its temptation abilities.","Lin Yuan’s alluring and temptation abilities were extremely strong with the Alluring Soul Alluring Fox bloodline in his body. His abilities might exceed Alluring Soul’s if he had sufficient falseness to boost him.","Lin Yuan was very satisfied with the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s new ability and exclusive skill.","Lin Yuan was now going to use his body composition to evolve the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom.","Winter had already received the news that Fan Lou would be able to cover up the happenings in this Class 2 world. Hence, Lin Yuan no longer needed to worry about restricting himself.","Lin Yuan removed the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom from his sleeve and circulated the energy in his body.","A sea of energy gathered around the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s body.","During this process, Lin Yuan took out a large number of fire-element heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","These fire-element heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls, nurtured by the Deposit Vegetable Pods, were close to transforming into elemental dolls with 100% purity. They were sufficient to be used to nurture the pinnacle Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom.","It did not take long for Lin Yuan’s nurturing to lead the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s evolution.","Lin Yuan was in seclusion in the Return from Faraway Mansion and planned to evolve the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom, Purple Afterglow, and Rememberling.","Additionally, he wanted to strengthen and refine the Merciful Star Peony. After all, it could utilize constellations to temper itself and improve its body composition.","Lin Yuan felt he needed to pay attention to the nurturing of this fey the Moon Empress had given him.","The Body of All Spirits could improve his body composition by taking control of bloodlines. However, the enhancement effects would disappear once the bloodlines were swapped out.","For example, the Bloodian bloodline could significantly improve Lin Yuan’s physique. When Lin Yuan triggered it, he could even crush radium. However, all his strength would vanish when he swapped to the Alluring Fox or Burning Demon bloodlines.","On the other hand, when the Merciful Star Peony strengthened his body, he would maintain the powerful physique regardless of which bloodline he was utilizing. This shielded Lin Yuan from external risks.","Previously, Lin Yuan did not nurture the Merciful Star Peony because he obtained it far later than his other feys. By that time, he was fully focused on trying to take control of all the dimensional worlds.","Hence, despite the benefits that the Merciful Star Peony could bring him, Lin Yuan had not had the time to nurture it carefully. He had contracted it with his own spiritual energy. He would never do such a thing if it was not excellent in its own right.","...","Time flew by.","During the days that Lin Yuan was nurturing the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom, Wen Yu and Liu Jie managed all the matters related to Sky City while trying to get used to their increased power.","Now, both of them were top experts of their time.","While they adjusted themselves to their new power, they used Lin Yuan’s resources to evolve their feys. Elegance and the Elemental Paper’s grade and quality also increased rapidly.","...","A month passed.","Lin Yuan used the Ethereal Jellyfish’s Node Transportation to travel from the Return from Faraway Mansion to the air above the sea just outside the Radiance Federation’s territory.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom had evolved to Sovereign/Pinnacle Spirit Fire and was only a step away from World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","Lin Yuan only needed to spend another hour or two injecting energy into the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom, and its grade would evolve.","It would not be appropriate to evolve the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom in the Radiance Federation’s Royal Capital. After all, even with Spring’s protection, the commotion caused by its evolution would be far too eye-catching.","There was no need for Lin Yuan to get the Radiance citizens involved.","The main world had only just overcome the dead spirits crisis. It could not handle any changes.","Lin Yuan knew how important stability and happiness were to the Radiance citizens.","As Lin Yuan continued to circulate the energy in his body, a large amount of pure spirit qi was injected into the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s body.","Finally, after being enabled by Lin Yuan’s body composition, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom successfully evolved.","A strong energy flowed out from the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom and called out to the world wills.","Spring easily stopped the world wills from affecting the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom, and it soon burst out with a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom aura.","After its evolution, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s size did not change. The complicated patterns on its cap intertwined as stunningly beautiful images. However, these images were difficult to see clearly with the naked eye and looked like a mass of black.","Lin Yuan checked on the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom again. He was very excited to see the divine kingdom ability it had gained.","[Fey Name]: Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom","[Fey Species]: Parasitic fungus species/flaming fungus species","[Fey Type]: Fire","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","Certainly! Here’s an edited version of the manuscript following the Chicago Manual of Style:","[Seeping Flames]: The flames will seep into the target’s mind, spirit, and soul through the heart and brain. The spirit and soul will begin to burn. If the flames begin to die out, they can absorb the energy from the heart and brain to reignite themselves.","[Body-Penetrating Flames]: When burning the mind, spirit, and soul, the flames will also burn the body. The damage will be translated from the elemental form to the physical. Before the fire in its mind, spirit, and soul is extinguished, the flames afflicting the body will continue to cause harm.","[Thought-Separating Flames]: When burning the target’s mind, spirit, and soul, if the target’s mind, spirit, and soul have any thoughts or feelings linked to another lifeform, those thoughts will become a guide that allows the flames to extend.","[Strengthened Spores]: The fungi produced will be strengthened and able to absorb and take control of more energy. The fungi will be deeply rooted in the target’s soul and more difficult to remove.","[Truth Colony]: When questioning a target, the precise answers given will grow a truth colony. When the colony absorbs energy, it will grow into a truth mushroom. When the truth mushroom is fed to a target, the target will be forced to tell the truth, making it easier to obtain true answers to questions.","[False Colony]: When questioning a target, every lie told by the target will produce a false colony. When the false colony absorbs energy, it will grow into a false mushroom. When the false mushroom is fed to a target, the target will be unable to break while questioning, preventing them from answering questions.","[Interrogation Soul Flames]: After confirming that the target has made more than three false statements, the target can be asked a question, and the soul with fungi rooted in it will be sacrificed. The target will have to tell the truth through the voiced spirit form.","[Truth and Lie Temptation]: Each time truth and lie are discerned, it can store the sincerity and falseness. The sincerity can be used to boost its soul and defend it against temptation abilities. The falseness can be used to boost its temptation abilities and strengthen its ability to tempt targets.","[Truth Soil]: The spores will change the soil beneath them and imbue it with truth power. When other plant-type feys are planted in this soil imbued with truth power, they will absorb the energy within and produce truth fruits.","[False Soil]: The spores will change the soil beneath them and imbue it with false power. When other plant-type feys are planted in this soil imbued with false power, they will absorb the energy within and produce false fruits.","Exclusive Skill:","[Honesty Reflects the Heart]: The spores will host themselves deep within the target’s spirit and soul and determine the genuineness of the target’s exterior.","[Crumbled Parasitic Cycle]: The bacterial strain will be sacrificed. After being sacrificed, the energy around it will crumble, along with other energy-containing entities.","[Heart Mushroom Sky Questioning]: When a judgment cannot be made on an issue, one can be staked to question the sky and ask for a positive solution.","[Heart Mushroom Disrupts Heaven]: When other lifeforms use various methods to ask the world wills for answers, it can use its energy to disrupt the world wills and prevent the world wills from answering other lifeforms. Alternatively, it can incite the world wills to give wrong answers.","[Heavenly Will Shield]: It will trigger heavenly will and direct it towards a target. The heavenly will will be used to shield a target’s aura and prevent it from being detected.","[Endless Curse Generation]: When the main body is destroyed, it can be reincarnated through any spore. The imprint in the spore will be used to recover its memories from before its death. At the point of its death, it will place a curse on a target. When the truth is told, the curse will lower the target’s lifespan. But when a lie is told, it will reduce the target’s soul energy.","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Reverse Colony]: Truth and false power will join together to create a special colony. Once the colony is fully formed, it will turn into a reverse spirit mushroom. The reverse spirit mushroom will need to absorb spirit qi to grow. The purer the spirit qi absorbed, the better the effects of the reverse spirit mushroom. When being interrogated, consuming the reverse spirit mushroom will cause the opposite effect to take place during the interrogation.","The World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s data appeared in front of Lin Yuan.","Before it reached Myth Breed, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom was only a fey meant for interrogation. But after reaching Myth Breed, its abilities involved using heavenly will to detect and shield, as well as manipulate truth and lies.","Before obtaining Truth Soil and False Soil, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom could only obtain truth and false energy by continuously questioning lifeforms.","Lin Yuan did not have the time to use the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom to collect truth and false energy continuously.","Hence, its abilities had been restricted.","But with Truth Soil and False Soil, everything was different now. The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom could now obtain truth and false energy through interrogation.","It could then inject the truth and false energy into its spores and alter soil. Subsequently, the plant-type feys that were grown on such soil would produce fruits that contained truth and false power.","Lin Yuan could harvest these fruits to obtain a large amount of truth and false power. He could then use this truth and false power to activate the ability Truth and Lie Temptation.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s Immortal Breed exclusive skill, Heavenly Will Shield, would be able to use heavenly will to support a target and shield it from detection. If other targets wanted to investigate the target that was being protected by Heavenly Will Shield, they would have to suppress the world wills.","The world wills of Lin Yuan’s Class 2 world were not strong.","The effects of Heavenly Will Shield’s effectiveness would supersede the world wills.","The Sky Beyond the Clouds’ East Universe was like a large world and had its own world wills.","When they went to the East Universe, the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom could try to tap into the East Universe’s world wills. However, this would come at a higher cost.","As for the Eternal Breed exclusive skill, Endless Curse Generation, it could be seen as a self-preservation exclusive skill. The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom no longer had to fear death.","With the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s current power, it could produce billions of spores with ease.","It could place its spores in various locations. Hence, it would be able to revive in multiple locations after its death.","When the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom was by Lin Yuan’s side, it was almost impossible for it to be in any danger of dying.","This was unless Lin Yuan used the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom as a weapon and used its death to place a powerful curse on a target.","In life, one always needed to answer questions from others.","Once the curse of Endless Curse Generation was placed, the answerer would be significantly affected regardless of whether they answered with the truth or a lie!"]},{"number":2784,"title":"Chapter 2784 Purple Afterglow’s Divine Kingdom!","paragraphs":["2784 Purple Afterglow’s Divine Kingdom!","If they answered with the truth, their lifespan would decrease. Although World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeforms had very long lifespans, they would not be able to triumph over the continuous reduction of their lifespans.","If they answered with a lie, their soul energy would diminish.","Once a lifeform’s soul was harmed, it would entail a grievous root injury.","The stronger the lifeform, the more challenging it would be for them to heal from a soul injury.","Hence, when powerful lifeforms suffered soul injuries, most of them would decide to negotiate with their opponents rather than continue battling it out.","If they continued battling it out despite suffering soul injuries, it would mean that the two parties were either irreconcilable enemies or fighting over profitable resources. The profits had to exceed the impact of the soul injuries.","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s divine kingdom ability, Reverse Colony, was a rare production-type one.","The colonies would eventually form reverse spirit mushrooms.","However, the reverse spirit mushrooms would not grow in the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s divine kingdom. They needed to be nourished by pure spirit qi to become ripe.","After they were consumed, a person’s words would be reversed, and right and wrong would be reversed.","The divine kingdom ability that only seemed to help one tell lies actually had implications that went beyond this superficial effect.","Sky City’s main members would all have to understand a certain number of Sky City’s secrets.","If they were caught by an enemy, the enemy could use a special method to judge if they were telling the truth, regardless of how loyal they were to Sky City and how hard they tried to safeguard Sky City’s secrets.","One such example of a technique was the Sin Cleansing Weeping Willow that was planted in the Sin Cleansing Pool.","There would be a fair number of such feys in the Sky Beyond the Clouds as well!","The Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom was one of these feys as well.","Once Sky City’s members consumed the reverse spirit mushrooms, they would be able to truly evade the enemies’ methods and prevent Sky City’s information from being leaked.","This ability was extremely useful for Sky City’s development.","Now that he had evolved the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom, Lin Yuan had five World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys.","Purple Afterglow had helped the Kill Food Sky Butterfly to increase its power, and its bloodline had improved substantially.","According to Purple Afterglow, the Kill Food Sky Butterfly’s bloodline had transformed and now exceeded the historically highest-recorded level of a butterfly-species fey from the main world.","This made Lin Yuan curious, and he told Purple Afterglow to rush back to the Return from Faraway Mansion with the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly preferred to interact with Lin Yuan, Wen Yu, Liu Jie, and the rest in its human form rather than its original form.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly was extremely respectful toward Lin Yuan.","This was not just because the Kill Food Sky Butterfly and Purple Afterglow had become a couple.","Lin Yuan was Purple Afterglow’s contractor, and the Kill Food Sky Butterfly respected Lin Yuan as a father.","Lin Yuan was also the one who nurtured the Kill Food Sky Butterfly from the Kill Food Worm to its current self.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly did not have many memories from when it had been the Kill Food Worm, despite being Suzerain/Myth then.","This was a common affliction for butterfly-species feys. They only developed their brains when they were in their cocoons. Prior to that, they were mostly driven by instinct.","When Lin Yuan saw the Kill Food Sky Butterfly, he used True Data to check on it.","With Purple Afterglow’s help, the Kill Food Sky Butterfly had successfully reached Immortal Breed. It was not far from Eternal Breed, and its grade had also reached High Sovereign.","This rate of power increase was extremely high for the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly had only been with Lin Yuan for a few years. But in that time, its quality had evolved from Myth Breed to Immortal Breed.","Aside from the Kill Food Sky Butterfly, Purple Afterglow was also surrounded by a group of the Sky Fragrance Beauty Butterflies, which never stopped trying to curry favor with Purple Afterglow. However, it was obvious that Purple Afterglow was uninterested in them.","Purple Afterglow had used almost all of the scale powder that came from Beauty Dispersion on the Kill Food Sky Butterfly.","The Kill Food Sky Butterfly had transformed into the Sky-Killing Execution Butterfly.","It had comprehended a Strength Law and was a butterfly-species fey that would wield incredible strength.","During its bloodline transformation, the Sky-Killing Execution Butterfly’s wings were evolved. Now, when it spread its wings, it could cleave an opening in the sky and cause the space to vibrate.","Hence, when the Sky-Killing Execution Butterfly flew, it would sense the spatial energy around it. As time passed, the Sky-Killing Execution would have hope of taking control of spatial energy!","The Sky-Killing Execution Butterfly was very satisfied with its increase in power and was brimming with love for Purple Afterglow.","Now, the Sky-Killing Execution Butterfly’s grade was slightly higher than that of Purple Afterglow.","When Lin Yuan saw this, he smiled and said, “Purple Afterglow, you have to hurry up and increase your power! If you continue to remain stuck at Sovereign/Immortal, you won’t be able to use Beauty Dispersion to continue helping your wife increase her power and grade!","“Aren’t you in a rush to increase your power? Why don’t I take this opportunity to evolve you, Blackie, and the Jasmine Lily to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom?”","In a rare occurrence, a serious expression appeared on Purple Afterglow’s face.","Lin Yuan realized that a serious Purple Afterglow was much more charismatic than a laid-back Purple Afterglow!","The main world was currently in a state of peace. Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter’s spiritual energy were sufficient to cover the entire main world and keep watch on what happened in the main world.","Purple Afterglow knew that its wife could not be idle.","Since it was going to accompany Lin Yuan into seclusion for some time, it sent the Sky-Killing Execution Butterfly out to explore the Radiance Federation. It could also use the time to quickly evolve its grade and quality.","After Lin Yuan sent Sky-Killing Execution Butterfly away, Purple Afterglow changed into its original form.","In an instant, a purple cloud of mist appeared in Lin Yuan’s breeding room.","The patterns on Purple Afterglow’s body pierced through the cloud of mist-like rays of light.","As the butterfly flapped its wings, it emanated a soul-stealing and astonishing beauty that Lin Yuan could not describe!","Even a person who did not have many desires would form the habit of gazing upon Purple Afterglow after one glance at it.","Purple Afterglow was not large. It was only around the size of two of Lin Yuan’s palms. When it landed on Lin Yuan’s hand, it just managed to cover his palm.","Lin Yuan took a deep breath and circulated the energy in its body.","Powerful pure spirit qi gathered around Purple Afterglow and entered its body.","Lin Yuan could clearly sense Purple Afterglow’s happiness at being nourished by the spirit qi.","The cloud of purple mist expanded. The movement of mist caused the cloud to change shape, and it resembled ever-changing weather!","Lin Yuan evolved Purple Afterglow while enjoying the view. It could be said that Purple Afterglow’s evolution was the most enjoyable time that Lin Yuan had spent nurturing a fey.","Many of Lin Yuan’s feys, such as Purple Afterglow, Blackie, and Rememberling’s bloodlines, had all gone beyond that of the main world.","However, none of them belonged to a species and were unique entities.","Lin Yuan’s body composition could absorb bloodlines, so he wondered if he should absorb Purple Afterglow and Blackie’s bloodlines.","He believed their bloodlines would be beneficial for him.","When it came to matters Lin Yuan could not be sure of, he decided to ask Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter about them once he was done nurturing Purple Afterglow.","There were many matters Lin Yuan did not need to ponder over himself because he could find the answers to many questions by asking Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter. There was no need for him to search for the answers on his own.","When Lin Yuan clearly sensed the wall in Purple Afterglow’s body, Lin Yuan knew that its grade was about to evolve.","Lin Yuan concentrated on circulating the energy in his body to help Purple Afterglow evolve its grade.","Just as it was about to break through the wall, a large amount of brilliant purple light began exploding out from Purple Afterglow’s body.","As the purple light continued to shine, Lin Yuan felt as though he had been transported to a territory where only truly magical creatures could exist.","Purple Afterglow continued to transform while ensconced in the light.","In Lin Yuan’s eyes, the current Purple Afterglow could already be described as the most beautiful thing in the world.","But once Lin Yuan glimpsed the evolved Purple Afterglow, he suddenly realized the previous Purple Afterglow had been ordinary.","It was like a kid who had only ever seen other kids but was now witnessing a regular-sized adult for the first time. Inevitably, the kid would think that it was looking at a giant! But once an actual giant appeared, the regular-sized adult would seem short by comparison.","Purple Afterglow’s transformation elevated Lin Yuan’s definition of beauty.","Compared to Purple Afterglow’s current appearance, Lin Yuan was more concerned with Purple Afterglow’s abilities, exclusive skills, and kingdom ability.","Based on Lin Yuan’s previous understanding of Purple Afterglow’s abilities, its beauty and abilities were linked.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Purple Afterglow.","[Fey Name]: Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly","[Fey Species]: Flash-butterfly species/scaled-butterfly species","[Fey Grade]: World Emperor (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Spiritual/Soul","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","[Silence Scale Powder]: Special scale powder with the ability to silence is released, and any target that comes into contact with the scale powder will be unable to use spiritual power abilities. The scale powder will also be absorbed into the target’s spiritual power. Each time the target uses spirit qi, their spirit qi will end up cracking.","[Flashing Scale Dance]: Its images will be formed from the scale powder released into the air. It will be able to flash back and forth between itself and the formed images. While it is traveling, it can absorb energy from its surroundings to quicken the production of scale powder.","[Scale Light Butterfly Image]: Scale powder in the wings will be used to refract light. When light fills its reflection, its charm will be boosted, and it will gain absolute control over butterfly-species feys.","[Beautiful God Hallucination]: When a target is being attracted and sees one as a beautiful god, one will be able to adjust according to the target’s features and pick a lifeform to turn into the target’s definition of unsightliness. If the target and the lifeform have a positive connection, it will disappear momentarily. If they do not have a positive connection, the target will attack the lifeform.","[Species Praised Beauty]: When attracting a target and receiving its worship, the target’s species will also be affected and instinctively feel positively about the Purple Afterglow Beauty Goddess Butterfly.","[Beautiful God Cutting Wings]: Flap its wings to produce sequential cutting attacks. A special Beautiful God Engraving will be formed on the target’s body. Every engraving requires 16 cutting attacks to be formed. The target with a formed Beautiful God Engraving will trigger its own emotions to the greatest extent. Anything related to energy will be prevented from moving in and out of the target’s body.","[Beauty Assessment Plundering]: When one’s beauty stupefies a species and takes over that species’ assessment of beauty, it can set the standard with its beauty and become the definition of beauty for that species. Besides itself, the species would not see any other lifeform as beautiful. It would not detest and be repulsed by lifeforms that previously met their standards of beauty.","[Beauty Dispersion]: When other feys feel love for it, their amazement and recognition of its beauty will turn into a special scale powder that can be used to increase the power of other butterfly-species lifeforms. (This is only effective on butterfly-species lifeforms with inferior bloodlines.)","[Feathered Insect Command]: It will have stronger mesmerization effects on insects and lifeforms with wings. Insects and lifeforms with wings will also easily begin worshipping it.","[Beautiful Spirit Transformation]: All other lifeforms’ recognition of its beauty will be sealed in and used to transform its body. It will also use its dreams as a weapon to take control of the faith, spirit, and soul of other species.","Exclusive Skill:","[Scale Powder Halo]: The scale powder has strong reflective abilities, and the target that lays eyes on the scale powder will be affected by the reflection. The target will start to feel dizzy and experience temporary blindness.","[Soul Beauty Goddess]: By activating the power of the spirit and soul, the beauty will be increased to a limitless level. The target will be attracted and fall in love. The target will want everything of its object of love on its body, and the target will want to collect everything connected to the object of its love.","[Beauty Reaches Every Species]: Each time it receives the recognition of a species and becomes their standard of beauty, its charm would be eternally strengthened.","[Extreme Mesmerization]: When the mesmerizing ability is used on an entity, it can give up its scale powder in exchange for boosting its mesmerizing ability.","[Butterfly Bloodline Gift]: A part of its bloodline will be gifted to other lifeforms and allow them to gain some traits of its bloodline. The bloodlines of other butterfly-species feys will be activated to a greater extent.","[Spirit Arrival Application]: Choose a lifeform that has received its gift. The lifeform’s life will be sacrificed. It will temporarily be able to use the lifeform’s body as a medium to arrive (The duration of arrival is related to the concentration of bloodline in the lifeform’s body).","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Beauty Seal]: Make a judgment about beauty. It will assign a value to every lifeform’s level of beauty. If other lifeforms’ beauty value is lower than its own, it can use its divine kingdom to seal the other lifeform’s divine kingdom (Only a maximum of two entities can be sealed. When sealing the two entities, it will not be able to use any other ability apart from its divine kingdom ability)."]},{"number":2785,"title":"Chapter 2785 Sovereign/Creation Rememberling!","paragraphs":["2785 Sovereign/Creation Rememberling!","Lin Yuan found the Sky-Questioning Flaming Heart Mushroom’s abilities to be fearsome.","Take Feathered Insect Command, for example. It could increase the mesmerization effects on insects and lifeforms with wings, causing them to easily begin worshiping Purple Afterglow.","With Purple Afterglow’s beauty—Beauty Reaches Every Species, Species Praised Beauty, and Beautiful God Hallucination—it had no problems leaving a positive impression on other lifeforms.","Feathered Insect Control could not only be seen as an ability that raised Purple Afterglow’s mesmerization abilities but also as an ability that could potentially enable it to become the king of insects and avian-type feys!","The feys more closely related to Purple Afterglow’s bloodline would also be affected by Purple Afterglow’s mesmerization to a larger extent.","At first, Lin Yuan believed that Purple Afterglow could collect many butterfly species as its dependent species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","But now, it seemed that it was not just butterflies—insect and winged species would also be affected by Purple Afterglow’s mesmerization.","This meant that Purple Afterglow would have no trouble collecting many dependent species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, obtaining an extremely large amount of faith power.","Once a fey reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, it could not depend solely on pure spirit qi to increase its power. Aside from pure spirit qi, it also needed to obtain faith power to develop its divine kingdom.","Purple Afterglow’s divine kingdom would evolve the fastest among all of Lin Yuan’s feys. Not even Green Vine could compare with Purple Afterglow.","Meanwhile, Beautiful Spirit Transformation was even more amazing than Feathered Insect Command.","Beauty came from other lifeforms’ recognition of its beauty. It was an objective perception and could not be used as energy. However, Purple Afterglow was able to use beauty as its weapon and seal the recognition of its beauty in its body. It would then use the beauty that was sealed in its body to control the faith, spirit, and soul of other lifeforms.","Given Lin Yuan’s experience, the ability to control spirit and soul was not new or particularly rare. However, this was the first time Lin Yuan heard of a lifeform that could use its ability to control the faith of other lifeforms and species. It could be said that this ability surpassed Lin Yuan’s horizons.","Purple Afterglow’s strength was proven through this ability that could surpass Lin Yuan’s horizons.","Even Spring, who was helping Purple Afterglow fend off the world wills, could not help but be astounded.","However, Spring’s astonishment did not last for too long because Purple Afterglow was a fey Lin Yuan had evolved. In Spring’s eyes, it was impossible for such a fey not to turn out to be spectacular!","In its evolution to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, Purple Afterglow gained not only two new abilities but also two new exclusive skills, Butterfly Bloodline Gift and Spirit Arrival Application.","Butterfly Bloodline Gift involved Purple Afterglow giving a portion of its bloodline to other butterfly-species feys, allowing them to gain a part of its own bloodline. Purple Afterglow could then use its extremely elite butterfly-species bloodline to trigger and activate the bloodline levels of other butterfly-species feys.","An exclusive skill like that could be seen as a support-type one. Purple Afterglow would deplete its own butterfly-species bloodline to help other butterfly-species feys.","Each time this exclusive skill was used, Purple Afterglow’s bloodline would be affected, and it would take time to heal.","But with Spirit Arrival Application, everything was different. Purple Afterglow could arrive through the butterfly-species feys that it controlled with its bloodline. It was as though the butterfly-species feys’ bodies had become the mediums through which Purple Afterglow would arrive.","There were two benefits to arriving through Spirit Arrival Application.","Firstly, Purple Afterglow could rush to the battlefield in the nick of time regardless of its starting location.","Secondly, once Purple Afterglow arrived, it would not be affected after the butterfly-species medium died.","Nonetheless, Spirit Arrival Application was not without its drawbacks. Once it was used, the butterfly-species fey it was attached to would die. Additionally, the duration of the application was also limited. This was related to Purple Afterglow’s bloodline concentration in the butterfly-species fey’s body.","Purple Afterglow’s abilities were fully dependent on its mesmerization of targets. If these abilities were used, it would only take an instant for them to come into effect.","Hence, the butterfly-species feys that Purple Afterglow used as mediums to arrive only needed to contain a faint amount of its bloodline.","The butterfly-species feys that Purple Afterglow injected a large amount of its bloodline into did not need to be sacrificed for Spirit Arrival Application.","Purple Afterglow’s abilities were sufficient to prove how cruel it was toward other butterfly-species feys.","In truth, feys that subscribed to the law of the jungle would not be overly concerned with other lifeforms. In the world of feys, only lifeforms that were more powerful than others could afford to show pity to them.","The feys that liked to show pity to other lifeforms would find it difficult to survive in the main world, much less in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","At that moment, Purple Afterglow said, “Yuan, I am going to use my butterfly bloodline to nurture the 14 Sky Fragrance Beauty Butterflies. They come with abilities to serve other lifeforms and are very compatible with my bloodline! If I ever need to use Spirit Arrival Application, using these Sky Fragrance Beauty Butterflies will incur the lowest cost.”","Lin Yuan did not turn Purple Afterglow down. The 14 Sky Fragrance Beauty Butterflies were gifts from the Moon Empress. But she had only given them to him to use to pull his fey carriage.","The Sky Fragrance Beauty Butterflies’ talent was limited. If Purple Afterglow had not used its bloodline to nurture them, their power would be stuck at Creation Breed.","Purple Afterglow was willing to use its bloodline to give them an opportunity. They should be grateful to it.","Moreover, even if they were nurtured through Butterfly Bloodline Gift, there was no guarantee they would have to be sacrificed for Spirit Arrival Application.","Spirit Arrival Application would only be used if Lin Yuan was in danger. If Lin Yuan was truly in danger, the Sky Fragrance Beauty Butterflies might not survive even if they were not sacrificed to Spirit Arrival Application.","Currently, Lin Yuan did not know how to appraise Purple Afterglow’s divine kingdom ability.","Lin Yuan had heard of the phrase: “Acting aggressively due to a sense of superiority that came from beauty.”","This was the feeling Lin Yuan got from Purple Afterglow’s Beauty Seal. It would make a judgment about beauty and assign a value to the beauty of every lifeform. As long as the lifeform’s beauty was lower than that of Purple Afterglow, the latter would use its divine kingdom ability to seal the other party’s divine kingdom ability.","An extreme exchange of one for another.","With Purple Afterglow’s Beauty Seal, Lin Yuan could dissolve the threat of an enemy’s divine kingdom ability.","In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, divine kingdom abilities were seen as secret weapons.","Once an enemy’s divine kingdom ability was neutralized, they would inevitably be filled with terror.","Purple Afterglow’s divine kingdom ability was very similar to Gao Feng’s sacred source lifeform. The value was determined by the strength of the enemy’s divine kingdom ability.","Spring praised Purple Afterglow’s Beauty Seal more than once.","Spring brought up Kong Huan as an example. If any other lifeform on the Abyss Beast’s back had a divine kingdom ability similar to that of Purple Afterglow, they could have sealed off Kong Huan’s divine kingdom ability. At that point, Kong Huan would be rejected by the world wills and would have no choice but to retreat.","Kong Huan did not dare to become the cause for a Class 2 world’s collapse. If such a thing happened, she would have to pay an enormous price or even be jailed and punished.","If that happened, all the Alluring Foxes would be implicated and unable to head to the North Universe. Not even the Snow-Covered Fox envoy would be able to help!","Lin Yuan’s first reaction was not to praise Purple Afterglow’s power but to feel glad that none of the lifeforms on the Abyss Beast’s back had a divine kingdom ability similar to Purple Afterglow’s.","Based on Lin Yuan’s understanding of Kong Huan, Lin Yuan noticed she was not the type who thought a lot about the consequences when she acted. If she were, she would not have come to this Class 2 world and committed such acts!","Once a person in the middle of a raving fit was provoked, it was difficult for them to stop and think of the consequences. If they could do so, they would not be in the middle of a raving fit!","This especially applied to the two Alluring Foxes in the same branch as Kong Huan. The latter would do anything to ensure their safety.","At first, Lin Yuan wanted to continue evolving Rememberling.","It had been working very hard and had reached Sovereign/Creation.","Lin Yuan summoned Rememberling and checked on it using True Data.","[Fey Name]: Praying Universe Soul Whale","[Fey Species]: Soul whale-species/single-horned whale-species","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Soul","[Fey Quality]: Creation IX","Abilities:","[Soul Knot]: When faced with the body of a dead target, singing the whale song will combine all the hidden souls in the body and awaken the soul within the target. If there is enough soul in the target’s body, the memories in the soul will be activated.","[Whale Fantasy]: When faced with an attack, the body can be turned into soul power and spread out into the surroundings. This will be able to dodge any attack. When heavily injured, the soul will attach itself to the closest object. Once out of danger, the soul can re-solidify into its original form.","[Singing Soul]: The soul energy will be spent, and the soul’s past experiences will be recited. This will help to recover the soul’s memories.","[Whale Soul Tears]: After consuming the fragments of the soul and draining the energy within them, the energy can be released through the eyes as sacred items and be used to heal and nourish souls.","[Sacred Whale Song]: When the sacred whale song is sung, curses placed on the soul will be broken. The impurities in the soul will also be cleansed.","[Whale Horn Piercing Crystal]: The whale horn will pick out souls hidden within non-lifeforms. The Remembrance Soul Whale’s soul energy will begin to mold the soul pieces until they solidify into crystals that cannot be returned back into the main body.","[Soul Universe Guide]: The whale horn can communicate with and make prayers to the universe. The collected souls can be guided to its side, and universe power will be used to guide the souls while protecting them and preventing them from dissipating.","[Soul Ability Protection]: The whale horn will be used to plead to the universe for power that will add to its own soul power. Its soul power will be used to protect the target’s soul and soul body to prevent the soul body from being destroyed and dissipating.","Exclusive Skill:","[Burning Soul New Life]: By using spiritual ingredients full of soul power, the soul energy can be directed to and solidified in the soul. The soul energy can be used to recover damaged souls and return them to whole.","[Soul Remember Gift]: By combining with the collected dead souls, the dead souls will eventually become soul imprints once they are completely absorbed. When the soul imprint is applied to a lifeform of the same species, the lifeform’s comprehension ability will be raised, and they will be able to comprehend willpowers and laws more easily.","[Universe Prayer]: Cry out in unison with the universe space through its own bloodline. This will earn the chance to communicate with the universe space. After sincerely praying, the whale’s tears will be the guide that calls the universe’s thoughts and wills to it as a form of direct compensation.","[Gather Soul Conversion]: A type of energy will be fastened. The absorbed soul will be converted into this type of energy. The body can then absorb this type of energy and use it to strengthen itself.","Before Lin Yuan had the chance to be amazed by Rememberling’s new abilities and exclusive skill, Lin Yuan received a reply from Zong Ze, Gu Lang, and the rest.","They had just finished their training in the vicinity of the Dead Spirits Wells.","All of them were disciples of royalty, and Chef Supreme, the Bamboo Monarch, Iron Prison, and Long Lamplight had all made the same decision. They wanted to use this method to ensure that their disciples remembered how the sixth epoch came to be.","Furthermore, it was true they could increase their power rapidly by training in the vicinity of the Dead Spirits Wells.","Even the simulated Class 5 dimensional rifts could not compare to the dangers of the Dead Spirits Wells.","Aside from increasing their power, the Radiance Federation’s royalty also prioritized the training of their disciples’ characters. Power alone was not enough to shoulder the mindset that came with possessing power.","This kind of power would not only give rise to uncertainty about whether the Radiance Federation was going down the right path but would likely also lead to harmful impacts on the Radiance Federation.","Mang Shui’s incident was a warning not only to Tian Feng but also to the rest of the Radiance Federation’s royalty. They were now surer than ever that personality and character were more important than power!"]},{"number":2786,"title":"Chapter 2786 Old Friends Reunited!","paragraphs":["2786 Old Friends Reunited!","The Dead Spirits Wells were built in the Radiance Federation’s various cities. The ones around the Royal Capital were the toughest to tackle.","The members of royalty who sent their disciples to the Dead Spirits Wells to train also gave them ample measures to save themselves. This was because they were concerned that accidents would befall Zong Ze, Gu Lang, Gao Feng, and the rest while they were in that dangerous environment.","As Iron Prison’s disciple, Long Tao was also sent to the Dead Spirits Well at the beginning.","However, he was not only Iron Prison’s disciple but also the head of Coiling Dragon’s Valley. His father had officially passed on the position to him a year ago.","As Coiling Dragon’s Valley’s new head, Long Tao had things to do daily. Iron Prison could understand that.","The disciples of aristocratic families always placed their family’s honor above all else.","There were many times that Long Tao wanted to chase his dreams. However, his dreams were eventually all grounded by reality before they could take off.","The instant he took on the role of the head of Coiling Dragon’s Valley, Long Tao sensed the pressure that his father and grandfather felt.","Although he had cultivated many helpers and could delegate trivial tasks, he needed to make decisions on serious matters and also needed to remain in contact with the other elders.","The elders who used to get along well with Long Tao now regarded him differently. As a result, friction arose.","In order for a powerful faction to develop along the right trajectory, it could not follow the direction of a single individual. The elders existed to watch over Long Tao’s utilization of his power and support him so that he could be a better leader of Coiling Dragon’s Valley and the Long family.","When Lin Yuan heard what Long Tao said, he could not help but think that it was a pity. Given Long Tao’s talent and hard work, he should not be restricted to this Class 2 world.","However, he had clearly made his choice and decided his future path.","All Lin Yuan could do was wish him the best.","With Long Tao managing Coiling Dragon’s Valley, the faction would definitely be able to prosper in the main world.","Long Tao was using his means to help his family.","Given Lin Yuan’s understanding of Zong Ze, Gu Lang, Gao Feng, and Xia Qing, the latter would decide to remain in the Radiance Federation to protect it, regardless of how badly she wanted to go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. She might take over her grandfather’s role a few decades later.","Gao Feng did not have any lofty ambitions, nor did he have a burning passion for increasing his power. He preferred to enjoy life. Moreover, it was said that Gao Feng now had a girlfriend. It was almost impossible he would decide to go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The only people who would possibly be going to the Sky Beyond the Clouds were Zong Ze and Gu Lang.","Lin Yuan had interacted the most with Zong Ze and knew that Zong Ze had an intense craving for battle. Hence, the Sky Beyond the Clouds would be the best place for him to exist. In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Zong Ze could increase his power endlessly and battle against powerful enemies. Zong Ze would definitely want to accompany Lin Yuan there.","Lin Yuan could just discuss the matter of the Sky Beyond the Clouds with Zong Ze and Gu Lang.","Lin Yuan would need a few trustworthy helpers in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Zong Ze and Gu Lang were not only powerful but also possessed decent management abilities.","Lin Yuan intended to take some time to see, given the provision of opportunities, the extent to which Zong Ze and Gu Lang’s management abilities could be unleashed. They might be able to surprise him!","Lin Yuan looked at the messages from Zong Ze, Gu Lang, Gao Feng, and the rest on the Thoughts Letter Paper and responded to them.","[Lin Yuan]: All of you have just finished training. Why don’t we gather together? But this time, we won’t prepare our own food. I heard that after reopening after the end of the dead spirits crisis, the Spirit Food Pavilion is even busier than before. Why don’t we go there to eat? That is Zong Ze’s territory, and he knows all our tastes, so he’ll also know what to order.","Ever since Liu Jie’s power reached pinnacle spirit fire, he was fully focused on Elegance’s increase in power.","After communicating with Keira, Lin Yuan finally found what she had been trying to help Liu Jie to obtain. He was going to use this gathering to tell Liu Jie the news and make his day.","Regardless of whether Gao Feng, Xia Qing, Long Tao, and the rest decided to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, Lin Yuan would help them to increase their strength.","If they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, they would become the companions who explored new worlds with him.","If they did not want to go and stayed behind as the main world’s protectors, Lin Yuan would still be able to trust their characters and dispositions. They would not step out of line even if their strength was increased.","In the past, Lin Yuan and Zong Ze were the ones who decided when and where the gatherings were held.","The previously suspended Spirit Food Pavilion had been renovated and was no longer managed by Xia Chen. Instead, Li Changlin had taken over.","This change was not because Xia Chen had not done a good job of managing the Spirit Food Pavilion but because, after attaining an endless lifespan, Chef Supreme gained a new understanding of the words’ to wash a pig was a waste of both water and soap’.","In spite of all the time that Chef Supreme had put into nurturing Li Changlin, the latter was unable to stand on his own two feet. As such, Chef Supreme decided to stop putting Li Changlin on the spot and allow him to do what he wanted to do.","Li Changlin’s culinary skills were passable, and it went without saying that he was capable of managing Spirit Food Pavilion.","Chef Supreme felt that, regardless of what happened, Li Changlin would not be able to fail at such a simple matter as managing the Spirit Food Pavilion!","It turned out that Li Changlin and his management of the Spirit Food Pavilion indeed did not disappoint Chef Supreme.","In the past, the Spirit Food Pavilion’s menu consisted only of Kitchen Fragrance Palace’s 300 dishes.","Chef Supreme had established his Creation Master path through his cooking, and the 300 dishes were suitable for nurturing feys and combining spiritual ingredients.","There were numerous skills that were not suited for cooking delicacies. Xia Chen was aware of this.","However, in order to express his respect toward his Master, he stubbornly carried on with these methods during his management of the Spirit Food Pavilion.","After Li Changlin took over, he got rid of these complicated techniques that did nothing to help with the food’s flavor. Nothing was more important than flavor and the building of a complementary nutrition profile.","Lin Yuan also wanted to visit the Spirit Food Pavilion to support Li Changlin.","In truth, Lin Yuan had not tasted Li Changlin’s cooking in a long time. It was the best food that Lin Yuan had ever eaten.","Zong Ze was very happy when he saw that Lin Yuan wanted to eat at the Spirit Food Pavilion.","[Zong Ze]: Okay, let’s go to the Spirit Food Pavilion now! Allow me to be in charge of ordering this time. I know all of your tastes. I will go and give Senior Brother a heads-up. Ah Yuan, he has been waiting for you for a long time. His skills at cooking red-braised meat have improved significantly of late.","Lin Yuan and Zong Ze’s conversation on the Thoughts Letter Paper could be seen by Wen Yu, Liu Jie, Xia Qing, and the rest.","All of them were greatly looking forward to this gathering.","During the last gathering, they had all been under immense pressure.","This time, they were all free of pressure and could properly catch up and enjoy their time together!","...","When Li Changlin received Zong Ze’s message, he made a beeline for the kitchen and put on his chef’s uniform.","Zong Ze had said that they would only be ordering after they arrived. However, Li Changlin called Zong Ze every three minutes to rush him. Eventually, Zong Ze became so frustrated that he ordered over the phone!","Chef Supreme took Zong Ze in when he was very young. However, Zong Ze did not have a close relationship with his Senior Brother, Li Changlin.","For almost as long as Zong Ze could remember, Li Changlin was absent after eloping with his Senior Sister. He only returned to Kitchen Fragrance Palace with Senior Sister a few years ago. It was only then that Zong Ze and Li Changlin began forming a bond.","Li Changlin treated Zong Ze exceedingly well. However, Zong Ze could sense that Li Changlin was clearly closer with Lin Yuan.","...","All of them were punctual people. When the time for the meal arrived, they were all present and waiting outside the room that Zong Ze and Li Changlin had set aside for them.","When Li Changlin saw Lin Yuan, his eyes welled up with tears.","The independent and resilient boy who had to struggle to make ends meet while taking care of his sister had come so far! Li Changlin was both happy and proud of Lin Yuan.","Li Changlin did not express his feelings often. But this time, he could not help but stretch out his arms toward Lin Yuan.","“Little Yuan, you are much taller and buff now! Let me see if I can still lift you up! Auntie Zhang’s fey is currently on the cusp of transforming its bloodline. Otherwise, she would have definitely come here to see you!”","Li Changlin, who used to be Lin Yuan’s neighbor, would lift him up and shake him whenever he pushed his wheelchair into Lin Yuan’s shop. This expressed his affection for Lin Yuan and was also his way of proving his strength. Despite being wheelchair-bound, he was still a real man!","Lin Yuan always had the soul of a mature adult in him. He was never a child, so he used to dislike Li Changlin’s way of displaying his friendliness.","But now, Lin Yuan walked over to Lin Yuan with sincerity written all over his face.","Lin Yuan was very thankful to Li Changlin for taking care of him and Chu Ci in the past. The food he would occasionally bring them was only a small portion of the care he provided. He had also helped Lin Yuan to advertise his store and encouraged other neighbors to patronize the store. Otherwise, with Lin Yuan having to consume medicine daily, there was no way he could have saved up so many Radiance dollars to buy a fey for Chu Ci.","Li Changlin’s care for Lin Yuan was exemplified through daily deeds.","He had also been Lin Yuan’s parents’ comrade in battle. They had asked him to take care of Lin Yuan and Chu Ci.","Li Changlin’s care for Lin Yuan was an extension of his parents’ love for him.","When he saw all the friends by Lin Yuan’s side, one of whom was his Junior Brother, Li Changlin waved his hands and said, “All your food has been ordered. Given your spirit qi professional ranks, you need to take in more energy daily. I will add more dishes for you!”","Li Changlin did not linger and returned to the kitchen.","If he remained there, he would interfere with their conversations. As a senior, Li Changlin was well aware of his circumstances and which lines not to cross.","Lin Yuan’s question was of paramount importance. He could ask after the meal was done.","During the meal, the group caught each other up with what was happening in their lives.","As Lin Yuan listened to Zong Ze, Gu Lang, Xia Qing’s experiences training near the Dead Spirits Wells and the growth and transformations they had experienced, he could not help but think, Maybe it’s just as Zong Ze, Gu Lang, and Xia Qing are saying. They were sent to the Dead Spirits Wells to train because Chef Supreme, the Bamboo Monarch, and the rest hope that they will remember this epoch and not forget how the fifth epoch shifted to the sixth epoch.","It’s likely that Master also thought this way when she decided to keep the Dead Spirits Wells in the main world.","The wine flowed, and dish after dish was consumed.","Even Wen Yu was stuffed.","Lin Yuan cleared his throat and said seriously, “We haven’t sat together and talked about our dreams in a long time.","“The last time we were together was a few years ago in the Return from Faraway Mansion. Back then, the dead spirits crisis and Radiance Hundred Sequence selection were about to begin. We weren’t thinking about the future at all. Now, we are all gathered together and have time. Why don’t we talk about our dreams?”","Zong Ze, Gu Lang, Xia Qing, Gao Feng, and the rest glanced at each other.","It was common for young people to discuss their dreams when they were gathered together.","Back then, Lin Yuan had been 18 or 19 years old, while Zong Ze, Gu Lang, Xia Qing, and the rest were just over 20 years old.","But now, they were all fully grown adults. Gao Feng was the oldest at 27 years old.","All of them had their accomplishments. However, some had achieved more than others.","While they were discussing their dreams, those who were doing better could not help but feel proud and want to show off.","However, it was true that Lin Yuan could help anyone achieve their dreams.","All of them knew that the Radiance Federation’s resources were supplied by Lin Yuan.","Apart from the Radiance Federation, Lin Yuan also provided resources to the entire main world. He was the one who allowed the main world to change and develop.","Zong Ze said seriously, “My dream is to constantly increase my power and fight passionately. While I’m increasing my power, I will protect those I need to protect and hold up the responsibilities I need to undertake.”","Zong Ze spoke resolutely, just like he had done a few years ago during the Guard Ye Banquet.","Gu Lang was silent for a moment before he said with a smile, “It just so happens that I have the same dreams as Zong Ze! But rather than combat, I am more interested in becoming stronger!","“I am less enthusiastic about raising my Creation Master class than I am about increasing my power. So, Zong Ze has always been one step ahead of me in terms of Creation Master abilities!”","Gao Feng and Xia Qing’s dreams aligned with Lin Yuan’s guesses.","However, Lin Yuan had not expected love to change a person this much.","Gao Feng had a girlfriend, but they were not married. Yet, he was already coming up with plans to take his future wife and children on vacation around the world and enjoy life as a family man."]},{"number":2787,"title":"Chapter 2787 Divine Kingdom Ability: [Soul Spirit Harbor]!","paragraphs":["2787 Divine Kingdom Ability: [Soul Spirit Harbor]!","Even in his past life, Lin Yuan understood one fact of life: everyone had their own aspirations. They all had different ambitions, and no ambition was better than another.","Zong Ze and Gu Lang’s eyes lit up when they heard that.","The two of them had made many guesses, but this was the first time they were receiving verbal confirmation from Lin Yuan about the existence of a world beyond the main world.","It could be said that Zong Ze and Gu Lang immediately became interested in heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Brilliant fireworks also exploded in Xia Qing’s gaze. However, she quickly suppressed her excited gaze and looked down at the Radiance Federation’s ground.","Gao Feng looked as though he was just here to join in the fun.","Gao Feng was the first to speak. “I am aware of my own talent. I have never had much passion for increasing my power. In my younger days, I wanted to increase my power because my father forced me to do so. After I became a disciple, Master began supervising my growth.","“But finally, there is no one to supervise me, and I can kick back and enjoy life! I don’t think going to the Sky Beyond the Clouds is for me.”","Everyone here knew that, in spite of Gao Feng’s joking and friendly tone, he was not this apathetic about increasing his power.","He also worked hard for the sake of increasing his power.","During the battle against the Freedom Federation, he had been willing to go all out for its sake.","Gao Feng had not completely given up now either.","However, because of his choice, his increase in power would be much slower than before.","Currently, there was already a large gap between his power and that of the rest.","Zong Ze shot Gao Feng a look of exasperation.","“Ah Feng, Ah Yuan is giving you a chance. You have to think it through properly! Otherwise, even if you come to regret your decision, there won’t be anything you can do about it!”","It was impossible for Lin Yuan to chase after them continuously to ask about their dreams. This was the only chance. Once they passed up on it, they would never be able to reach the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Going to a wider world would be far better than maintaining the status quo in the Radiance Federation. There was a limit to one’s advancement in the main world. They would only be able to achieve new breakthroughs by going to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","“I am willing to go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds! But will I have the chance to battle there?” Zong Ze asked.","Lin Yuan smiled. “There are thousands of species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. As long as you want to battle, you will be able to find someone to do it with.","Zong Ze took note of what Lin Yuan said.","Lin Yuan shook his head. “The exact time hasn’t been decided. However, it will be at least a few years later. There isn’t a rush to go. If you really intend to go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, you can still remain in the main world for some time.”","Lin Yuan could see the longing in Xia Qing’s eyes and asked her seriously, “Xia Qing, what do you think?”","Xia Qing was silent for a moment. She looked as though she had made a resolute decision and said, “Lin Yuan, I have decided to stay behind to protect the Radiance Federation.”","When Lin Yuan heard what Xia Qing said, he said seriously, “I just said that the main world where we live is only a very small part of the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","“Not long ago, invaders arrived in this Class 2 world. Luckily, they have been dealt with. If we go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and make a name for ourselves, we will be able to better protect the main world!","“Xia Qing, I am sure you can understand my meaning. There are sufficient people to protect the main world. You don’t have to lend your strength to them!”","Lin Yuan spoke straightforwardly because this would help Xia Qing with her decision.","It was true that Lin Yuan’s words gave Xia Qing significant motivation. However, she eventually still shook her head. “Lin Yuan, I have decided to stay. I trust that the few of you will be enough to protect our world! I will stay here. It’ll also allow me to spend more time with Grandfather.”","Xia Qing knew that her grandfather had formed a contract with the Lifespan Mouse and attained an endless lifespan. She really wanted to stay with him to do her part as his granddaughter.","Just like Lin Yuan’s only remaining blood relative was Chu Ci, Xia Qing’s only remaining blood relative was her grandfather. He was the man who had dedicated his entire life to the Radiance Federation, to the point that he had even tied his soul to the land.","Frankly, Lin Yuan also intended to extend his offer to An He, but the latter had yet to return from training.","Given Lin Yuan’s understanding of An He, it was unlikely that An He would be willing to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","An He was as laid back as Gao Feng.","Now that all of them had made their decisions, Lin Yuan did not continue to discuss this matter.","Before Lin Yuan left, he invited Zong Ze and Gu Lang to visit the Return from Faraway Mansion soon.","Lin Yuan intended to help the two of them to increase their powers first.","He would wait until he was about to leave the main world before helping Xia Qing, Gao Feng, and the others who were staying behind in the main world to increase their strength.","Once Lin Yuan returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion, Lin Yuan immediately began nurturing Rememberling.","Rememberling’s grade increased continuously. Eventually, it became a World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform.","After its evolution, Rememberling’s appearance remained relatively unchanged. However, its aura of starlight and mysticism intensified, and special patterns appeared on its horn. These patterns had the power to trigger a living soul.","Rememberling was a lifeform that could piece souls together. However, it had only ever pieced together the souls of the dead. Now, it could do the same for the living.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Rememberling.","[Fey Name]: Praying Universe Soul Whale","[Fey Grade]: World Emperor (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Soul","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","Abilities:","[Soul Knot]: When faced with the body of a dead target, singing the whale song will combine all the hidden souls in the body and awaken the soul within the target. If there is enough soul in the target’s body, the memories in the soul will be activated.","[Whale Fantasy]: When faced with an attack, the body can be turned into soul power and spread out into the surroundings. This will be able to dodge any attack. When heavily injured, the soul will attach itself to the closest object. Once out of danger, the soul can re-solidify into its original form.","[Singing Soul]: The soul energy will be spent, and the soul’s past experiences will be recited. This will help to recover the soul’s memories.","[Whale Soul Tears]: After consuming the fragments of the soul and draining the energy within them, the energy can be released through eyes as sacred items and be used to heal and nourish souls.","[Sacred Whale Song]: When the sacred whale song is sung, curses placed on the soul will be broken. The impurities in the soul will also be cleansed.","[Whale Horn Piercing Crystal]: The whale horn will pick out souls hidden within non-lifeforms. The Remembrance Soul Whale’s soul energy will begin to mold the soul pieces until they solidify into crystals that cannot be returned to the main body.","[Soul Universe Guide]: The whale horn can communicate with and make prayers to the universe. The collected souls can be guided to its side, and universe power will be used to guide the souls while protecting them and preventing them from dissipating.","[Soul Ability Protection]: The whale horn will be used to plead to the universe for power that will add to its soul power. Its soul power will be used to protect the target’s soul and soul body to prevent the soul body from being destroyed and dissipating.","[Soul Spirit Extraction]: Evaluate a lifeform’s soul energy. With the sacrifice of the same grade and type of bloodline as the other party, their soul can be extracted and contained.","[Restricted Soul Sensing]: Dissect the imprisoned soul of the living or dead to use the aura to locate a lifeform with a similar bloodline.","Exclusive Skills:","[Burning Soul New Life]: By using spiritual ingredients full of soul power, the soul energy can be directed to and solidified in the soul. The soul energy can be used to recover damaged souls and return them to whole.","[Soul Remember Gift]: By combining with the collected dead souls, the dead souls will eventually become soul imprints once they are completely absorbed. When the soul imprint is applied to a lifeform of the same species, the lifeform’s comprehension ability will be raised, and they will be able to comprehend willpowers and laws more easily.","[Universe Prayer]: Cry out in unison with the universe space through its own bloodline. This will earn the chance to communicate with the universe space. After sincerely praying, the whale’s tears will be the guide that calls the universe’s thoughts and wills to it as a form of direct compensation.","[Gather Soul Conversion]: A type of energy will be fastened. The absorbed soul will be converted into this type of energy. The body can then absorb this type of energy and use it to strengthen itself.","[Soul Tide Whirlpool]: Its soul will form a high-speed whirlpool. This whirlpool will be able to increase the response rate of its own soul and increase the concentration of soul power.","[Soul Level Blessing]: Once the soul of an expert is obtained, the expert’s soul can be used to bless a lifeform of the same type. The lifeform will be able to increase its level quickly, and its soul will be strengthened. Divine Kingdom Abilities:","Divine Kingdom Ability:","[Soul Spirit Harbor]: It will merge with the environment. Once merged, it will be able to gather all the soul energy in the environment and store the soul energy in its own sea of souls.","When Lin Yuan saw Rememberling’s new abilities and exclusive skills, he felt as though he had discovered a gem.","Lin Yuan did not check Rememberling’s abilities in detail before it evolved to Sovereign/Creation.","But now that he was looking at all the abilities, he noticed that the exclusive skill, Gather Soul Conversion, and divine kingdom ability, Soul Spirit Harbor, could be connected.","Soul Spirit Harbor would allow Rememberling to collect all the souls of the dead in the world and store them safely in its own soul.","Meanwhile, Gather Soul Conversion allowed Rememberling to fasten a certain type of energy before turning souls into that energy and absorbing the energy through the body.","Faith power immediately came to Lin Yuan’s mind.","Rememberling could collect souls from all around it and turn the souls into faith power that it would use to evolve itself. This meant that it would be able to use Gather Soul Conversion and Soul Spirit Harbor to rapidly evolve its own divine kingdom and grade.","Perhaps, Rememberling was the fey that increased its power the fastest!","Due to the dead spirits crisis, most of the souls in the main world were gone.","However, there were plenty of burial grounds in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The Sky Beyond the Clouds had existed for far longer than the main world.","Once Rememberling used Soul Spirit Harbor, countless souls would gather around it.","Soul Tide Whirlpool would allow Rememberling to speed up his soul sea and absorb the soul energy quicker.","Moreover, the whirlpool could increase the rate of response between Rememberling and its ability to gather soul energy. Once its ability to gather soul energy was strengthened, its own soul’s defensive abilities would be elevated.","With these two exclusive skills and divine kingdom ability, it was possible that Rememberling would be able to evolve to the Holy Spirit level soon.","After all, once a lifeform reached the Divine Kingdom level, the evolution of its divine kingdom was solely dependent on its faith power. The quantity of faith power required was determined by the level of the divine kingdom.","Additionally, Rememberling’s abilities allowed its functions to expand significantly.","Soul Universe Guide could be paired with Soul Ability Protection.","When Rememberling used its horn to communicate with the universe and pray to it, the universe power would support its soul power.","The universe power would not only protect the souls that had been guided to it, but its own faith power could also be used to protect the souls and soul bodies of targets. With this double layer of protection, they could effectively prevent soul bodies from being destroyed and dissipating.","A shattered soul body was very fragile. This also applied to an expert’s shattered soul body.","From the patterns on Rememberling’s horn, Lin Yuan could sense its ability to control the living.","This was related to Rememberling’s Soul Spirit Extraction, whose effects were aimed at the souls of the living.","As long as a similar grade and type of bloodline as that of the target was sacrificed to the universe, Rememberling would be able to extract the target’s soul and imprison it."]},{"number":2788,"title":"Chapter 2788 Expedition to the North Universe!","paragraphs":["2788 Expedition to the North Universe!","Soul Spirit Extraction targeted the souls of the living and could be regarded as a deadly move.","In the Sky Beyond the Clouds, bloodline was very precious, and it was exceedingly difficult to evolve the bloodline.","It was basically impossible for experts to be able to sacrifice bloodlines that were of the same type as their own.","If there was a faction or person in the Sky Beyond the Clouds that could make that sacrifice, they would also have other means to kill their targets.","But to Lin Yuan, bloodline was not something that was difficult to get his hands on. Regardless of how elite the bloodline was, he would be able to nurture it through his Body of All Spirits.","When he faced powerful enemies, the bloodlines he had nurtured for the longest could be used to take control of his opponent’s souls.","This not only allowed him to defeat his enemies but also placed immense pressure on them. Once their lives were in his hands, Lin Yuan believed that even the strongest holy spirit would be willing to trade secrets and information for its own life.","Soul Spirit Extraction could be linked with Restricted Soul Sensing and Soul Level Blessing.","Restricted Soul Sensing could dissect the living or dead soul that had been imprisoned before using it to locate a holy spirit with the same bloodline.","With just Restricted Soul Sensing, Lin Yuan would be able to locate an entire species. This would prevent any member of a species that Lin Yuan was trying to capture or eliminate from slipping out of his grasp.","If a species from the Sky Beyond the Clouds, like the one Kong Huan belonged to, found out about this ability, they would definitely begin to quake in terror.","This ability could strike fear into species with small numbers.","Once Kong Huan found out about this ability, she would know that if she ever made an enemy out of Lin Yuan, he would be able to capture any Alluring Fox and imprison their souls using Rememberling.","Under Rememberling’s control, Lin Yuan could find all the Alluring Foxes. If he wanted to wipe out the Alluring Foxes, none of them would be able to escape, and the species would be rendered extinct!","Soul Spirit Extraction allowed Rememberling to target experts while Soul Level Blessing allowed it to create experts.","Once Rememberling imprisoned the soul of an expert, it would be able to use the expert’s soul to bless other members of its species. The other members of its species would be able to utilize this expert’s soul to increase their strength. Their souls would also be strengthened.","When Lin Yuan took control of a species, he could use this method to eliminate the uncooperative and disobedient experts before using their souls to nurture the members of the species he had chosen. This would allow him to quickly gain full control over the species.","...","While Lin Yuan was nurturing Rememberling, Fan Lou and Kong Huan were both experiencing a multitude of events in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Fan Lou was now the apple of Feng Qing’s eye.","Fan Lou did not give himself this status. It was determined by the way he was viewed by the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","Feng Qing saw Fan Lou as his lucky charm. Feng Qing did not distribute the Class 2 world’s resources brought back by Fan Lou to the rest of the species. Instead, he used them to continuously increase his own power. Through this, Feng Qing’s bloodline had improved considerably.","Once Feng Qing began viewing Fan Lou as his lucky charm, his attitude toward Fan Lou improved. This made Feng Xuan seethe with envy.","Yet, there was nothing that Feng Xuan could do about it.","Unless Fan Lou committed a serious error and angered Feng Qing, he would be stuck under Fan Lou for the foreseeable future!","Feng Xuan had made attempts to change the circumstances.","When he was alone with Feng Qing, he threw in some comments to undermine Fan Lou.","However, not only did Feng Qing not believe him, but even sternly warned him not to discriminate against Fan Lou. As a result, Feng Qing did not dare to continue targeting Fan Lou.","He was only able to climb to his current position because of Feng Qing’s cultivation and rewards. If Feng Qing chose to abandon him, he would lose all of his power and have to return to the ranks of the rest of the species.","It was unlikely that he would have a good time among the other members of the species.","The members of the species were used to currying favor with the strong while scorning the weak. When he was favored by Feng Qing, many of them flocked to him. These same people would return to trample over him once he lost his power.","Feng Xuan could only watch as Fan Lou strove for more success.","Despite only having a small amount of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolf bloodline, he was a rising star among the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves because of the rewards he received from Feng Qing. Many of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves were falling over themselves to earn his favor.","Fan Lou did not become blinded by arrogance because of the rewards he received from Feng Qing.","He was polite to those who tried to curry favor with him and would help them as much as he could.","Fan Lou was well aware he was not working for Feng Qing but for the Lord in the Class 2 world.","After witnessing Spring and Winter’s strength, not even Feng Qing could impress Fan Lou anymore.","Fan Lou was doing what he was doing now in order to improve his standard of living and hide his true motives.","This was also so he could do an even better job as the captain of the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team.","In the past, in order to secure the protection of the team’s members, Fan Lou had distributed a significant portion of power to the team members.","But now, he took back all the authority and began controlling the Sixth Boundary Patrol Team with an iron fist.","The territory where Lin Yuan’s Class 2 world existed was solely watched and managed by Fan Lou.","Fan Lou could sense that there were lifeforms in Lin Yuan’s world that were being evolved to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom. This caused him to be even more awed by Lin Yuan’s strength.","It was extremely difficult to evolve a Class 2 world’s native lifeforms to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","With Fan Lou’s success, his residence was expanded to more than ten times its original size and was moved to an area with even more resources.","In the past, the most precious resource that Fan Lou could get his hands on was a weak spirit ore mine. But now, he would not even look twice at a weak spirit ore mine.","The rewards that Feng Qing gave Fan Lou allowed him to have a far better life than most of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","...","Compared to Fan Lou, Kong Huan’s experience was much more of a roller coaster ride.","By now, Kong Huan had led the Alluring Foxes in their departure to the North Universe.","Before she left for the North Universe, Kong Huan attempted to assassinate Fan Lou once again in order to cement the relationship they were trying to project.","It seemed as though she was helping Fan Lou, but this was also her way of showing her loyalty to Lin Yuan.","Once she was done with her assassination attempt, Kong Huan organized all of the Alluring Foxes’ resources and sold the assets they would not be able to take with them.","By using her evolved bloodline, Kong Huan mesmerized the many Light Wind Wolves and robbed their treasure vault. She did this so that she could obtain even more resources and would not have to worry about a lack of resources during their development in the North Universe.","But to the rest of the world, Kong Huan’s actions would be seen as her revenge on the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves who protected the Light Wind Wolves.","Many members of Honor Absent Palace were shocked by Kong Huan and the Alluring Foxes’ departure to the North Universe.","It had already been an anomaly for Kong Huan to obtain a seat on the Honor Absent Parliament as an Alluring Fox.","Given the power of the Alluring Foxes, they would never be able to achieve such treatment in the North Universe, whose living conditions were far harsher than those of the East Universe.","It was likely that the Alluring Foxes were going to the North Universe because they had been invited by the Snow-Covered Foxes.","The Snow-Covered Foxes had been making contact with various fox species across the four universes and inviting them to become their dependent species. Many fox species had accepted the offer because of the Snow-Covered Foxes’ power.","If the Snow-Covered Foxes had only invited a few fox species to become their dependent species, they would be able to protect all of them. However, they had invited more than a thousand species.","Not only would these species have to earn the favor of the Snow-Covered Foxes, but they would also have to compete endlessly amongst themselves.","The Alluring Foxes’ decision was too abrupt and illogical.","It caused some to think that they were fleeing far away to escape the threat of the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves.","Apart from the Chaos Wind Demon Wolves, the Bloodians were also putting pressure on the Alluring Foxes.","Once the Bloodians placed a target on the Alluring Foxes’ back, there was a high probability that they would attack them.","The Bloodians eliminated tens of species from the East Universe every century.","The species that lacked power all did their best to get on the Bloodians’ good side. They did not dare to engage the Bloodians in any conflict for fear of becoming a target.","The Alluring Foxes were already targeted by the Bloodians, and they lacked the power to take the Bloodians on. Hence, leaving the East Universe was an option they had to consider taking.","Once Kong Huan decided to lead the Alluring Foxes in following the Snow-Covered Fox envoy to the North Universe and become the Snow-Covered Foxes’ dependent species, she stopped bothering about what she was leaving behind.","When she left, Kong Huan did not feel a shred of sadness. Rather, she saw the North Universe as a place where the Alluring Foxes would be able to prosper.","The Alluring Foxes were not battling alone now. They had a powerful source of support!","Kong Huan’s bloodline had evolved from pinnacle Alluring Bones to beginner Alluring Soul.","She could clearly sense the benefits of her evolved bloodline.","Before her bloodline evolved, she would never have had the courage to go to the Light Wind Wolves’ treasure vault on her own to rob it, nor would she have been able to mesmerize the Light Wind Wolf experts to ensure she was successful.","Kong Huan’s branch had always been the dominant one amongst the Alluring Foxes.","But recently, a few of the young Alluring Foxes from other branches had discovered their talent and became rebellious.","It was only after the other Alluring Foxes found out that Kong Huan’s bloodline had reached the Alluring Soul grade they no longer dared to act disrespectfully toward her.","With just her bloodline, Kong Huan managed to quell all defiant thoughts from the other bloodlines.","The bloodline was above all to the Alluring Foxes. Kong Huan did not have to worry that the other branches were only pretending to submit to her.","The Alluring Foxes had always passed down a rule left behind by their ancestors. Only the Alluring Fox with the strongest bloodline could lead the species.","If another Alluring Fox managed to attain a stronger bloodline, Kong Huan would be willing to submit to them as well.","...","Kong Huan did not know much about the Snow-Covered Foxes. Hence, on this trip, she never stopped asking the Snow-Covered Fox envoy questions in the hopes of learning more information that would help the Alluring Foxes settle into the North Universe.","The Snow-Covered Fox envoy had guided many fox species from the East Universe to the North Universe.","Usually, he would not give away too much about the circumstances in the North Universe.","It was true that most of the fox species who went to the North Universe would not have to worry about their safety because they had the Snow-Covered Foxes’ protection.","However, these fox species would not receive many opportunities because such opportunities mostly went to the Snow-Covered Foxes.","The dependent species’ living conditions were fully dependent on the Snow-Covered Foxes’ moods and whims.","If any of the Snow-Covered Fox elites were attracted to any member of a dependent species and were willing to take them in as a concubine, the concubine’s species would immediately receive an inflation in status.","Most of the Snow-Covered Foxes’ dependent species’ status was related to their power.","But once a member caught the eye of a Snow-Covered Fox elite, their species would receive better treatment than the others, regardless of how weak the species was.","If a dependent species saw itself as powerful and affected other dependent species under the Snow-Covered Foxes’ protection, they would be eliminated by the Snow-Covered Foxes!","It went without saying that it was not appropriate to tell the fox species who were headed to the North Universe to become the Snow-Covered Foxes’ dependent species about all this.","Kong Huan had been muffling her bloodline.","She only revealed a small portion of it now in front of the Snow-Covered Fox envoy to seduce him.","The Alluring Fox bloodline had strong seduction effects on fox species. Once they were mesmerized, the targets would not be able to sense the effects. They would only know they now felt attracted to the Alluring Foxes.","This Snow-Covered Fox envoy had met with Kong Mu. He had acknowledged she was very pretty but had not felt any special feelings toward her.","Yet, now in his interaction with Kong Huan, he felt the pricks of love. Instinctively, he wanted to make Kong Huan happy.","It was clear that this Alluring Fox was not being overly friendly with him and was also asking about the North Universe.","However, this Snow-Covered Fox envoy felt overwhelmed by his attraction and found it difficult to restrain himself!","During the journey, the Snow-Covered Fox envoy never stopped trying to gain Kong Huan’s favor and frequently expressed his love for her. He even claimed to want to marry her once they joined the Snow-Covered Foxes.","The Snow-Covered Fox envoy admitted he was not a member of the elite, but his status was not low either. As long as he made sufficient contributions, he would be able to become an elite in the future!","While the Snow-Covered Fox envoy candidly expressed his love for Kong Huan, he completely missed the derision in her eyes."]},{"number":2789,"title":"Chapter 2789 Divine Kingdom Ability: [Battleground Angel]!","paragraphs":["2789 Divine Kingdom Ability: [Battleground Angel]!","If this were in the past, Kong Huan would not have hesitated to accept the Snow-Covered Fox envoy’s love.","Once she married this Snow-Covered Fox envoy, she would be able to receive true protection and coverage that would not only benefit her but all the Alluring Foxes.","Until now, Kong Huan had only heard rumors about the Snow-Covered Foxes.","Based on the Snow-Covered Foxes’ ranking on the Species Ranking, it was not difficult to guess just how powerful they were.","But now, she had managed to use her Alluring Soul bloodline to seduce this Snow-Covered Fox envoy easily and turn him into her tool.","Now, Kong Huan only saw this Snow-Covered Fox envoy as a tool she could use as she pleased.","Who would want to marry a tool?","Kong Huan was very confident she would be able to use her Alluring Soul bloodline to mesmerize more Snow-Covered Foxes into becoming her tools.","She would also be able to use her bloodline to attract the Snow-Covered Fox elites.","Moreover, attracting the Snow-Covered Fox elites did not mean that she had to marry them.","The Snow-Covered Foxes were considered a small species when compared to the other top 100-ranked species in the North Universe.","But to the Alluring Foxes, they were an enormous species with a messy internal structure. The elites both worked together and saw each other as rivals.","Given these circumstances, if she were bonded to a member of the Snow-Covered Fox elites through marriage, it would indeed enable her to receive his protection. However, it would also cause the Alluring Foxes to become implicated if this member of the elite fell.","Hence, Kong Huan had to think things through carefully.","“When the Alluring Foxes arrive at the North Universe, I will praise you in front of Sir Light Graceful Fox. I will tell him you are very enthusiastic about becoming the Snow-Covered Foxes’ dependent species and volunteered to come to the North Universe!”","This Snow-Covered Fox envoy was part of Light Graceful Fox’s faction. Although he could not receive rewards from Light Graceful Fox, he could gain an audience with him.","Light Graceful Fox liked the fox species that volunteered to join the Snow-Covered Foxes. He believed they had taste and were well-behaved. He disliked the fox species that came to the North Universe and began putting on airs.","In truth, dependent species were servants.","How could servants put on airs in front of bigshots of other universes?","The Snow-Covered Foxes would not do charity for nothing. There were many fox species who had failed to be compliant and had been taught painful lessons.","The love he felt for Kong Huan was unexplained.","Among the Snow-Covered Foxes, the inferior members rarely recklessly discussed their superiors.","The Snow-Covered Fox envoy hesitated to answer Kong Huan’s question.","When Kong Huan saw this, she whined coquettishly before circulating her Alluring Soul bloodline and repeating her question.","It was only then that the Snow-Covered Fox envoy answered her question and even told her of all of Light Graceful Fox’s likes and dislikes.","“It’s true. Sir Light Graceful Fox is arrogant and likes the submissive dependent species. He never treats the noncompliant dependent species well. When you come with me to join the Snow-Covered Foxes, you will have to find shelter in Sir Light Graceful Fox’s camp.”","Kong Huan listened intently to this Snow-Covered Fox envoy as he introduced Light Graceful Fox.","She now knew that there were 16 fox leaders, and each of them had more than ten envoys. These envoys would be sent out to the various universes to search for dependent species. Once they found them, they did not have to be acknowledged by all the Snow-Covered Foxes but would become akin to the private assets of the fox leader.","Cold sweat began dripping down Kong Huan’s back when she heard that.","The envoy’s words now were completely different from his previous claims.","The Snow-Covered Foxes’ gathering of the fox species was seen as them trying to protect the fox species, and they were highly revered for this. Almost every fox species that had been pushed into a corner in a certain universe would think of joining the Snow-Covered Foxes.","But in reality, the Snow-Covered Foxes were the true devils.","A fox leader’s dependent species was linked to the profits they received.","It was clear that the Snow-Covered Foxes were taking in dependent species to strengthen themselves. It was unsurprising that species that used this method of development could grow increasingly and endlessly stronger.","Despite her bloodline having reached Alluring Soul, Kong Huan still became apprehensive. There was no way that her beginner Alluring Soul bloodline would be able to mesmerize Light Graceful Fox.","Once they arrived at the North Universe, the Alluring Foxes would be in Light Graceful Fox’s hand.","Kong Huan could use her bloodline to take control of this envoy and return to the East Universe.","But if she returned to the East Universe, she would have to face the threat of the Bloodians. The Chaos Wind Demon Wolves would definitely also try to take revenge on the Alluring Foxes for the Light Wind Wolves.","Frankly, these would not be enough to cause the Alluring Foxes to fall.","Nonetheless, Kong Huan did not do so because going to the North Universe and developing the Alluring Foxes was a task Lin Yuan had given her. There was no way Kong Huan could go against Lin Yuan’s order.","Even if she defied Lin Yuan, an expert who at the very least had reached the Holy Spirit level, he still had two bodyguards who were definitely above the Holy Spirit level!","She could only ask Lin Yuan for help if she and the Alluring Foxes ran into trouble. If everything went smoothly, she would not be able to ask Lin Yuan for resources.","Winter had not only given Fan Lou a jade, but he had also given one to Kong Huan.","If she paid the appropriate price, she could use her soul to communicate with Winter through the jade.","Lin Yuan had provided numerous resources, meaning he definitely had a plan to use her in the future.","Kong Huan was going to roll with the punches. When they were in the North Universe, she would develop the Alluring Foxes carefully while seeking out opportunities.","At first, Kong Huan believed she would be able to gain the Snow-Covered Fox elites’ acknowledgment due to her bloodline.","But now, she preferred not to stand out immediately and catch Light Graceful Fox’s attention. She did not want to be seen as a present Light Graceful Fox could use to ameliorate the relationships between the fox leaders. Once she received such a label, she would be leashed to the Light Graceful Fox’s elites forever, and the Alluring Foxes would be shamed.","...","Lin Yuan did not know about Kong Huan and Fan Lou’s circumstances.","It was true that they were two tools in his toolbox. However, Lin Yuan was in the main world and did not need to use these two tools yet.","Lin Yuan had spent the past two days evolving the Merciful Star Peony.","The Merciful Star Peony needed to absorb moonlight to evolve its grade. Hence, it could not evolve quickly, even with Lin Yuan’s help.","Luckily, Lin Yuan was not in a rush.","Zong Ze and Gu Lang arrived at the Return from Faraway Mansion as agreed. Lin Yuan told them about how he could use his body composition to promote the ranks of spirit qi professionals.","Zong Ze and Gu Lang were astonished by this. When Liu Jie and Wen Yu saw this, they released their pinnacle spirit-fire aura.","The two of them were only one step away from reaching the Divine Kingdom level.","In terms of aura, their auras were even stronger than the Bamboo Monarch and Chef Supreme’s.","Firstly, neither Zong Ze nor Gu Lang doubted what Lin Yuan said. Moreover, Wen Yu and Liu Jie’s auras were the best evidence for Lin Yuan’s words. Hence, Zong Ze and Gu Lang had no reason not to believe him.","Zong Ze and Gu Lang had felt that there was something off about Liu Jie and Wen Yu’s auras during their meal.","Now, they finally knew the reason.","After Lin Yuan told Zong Ze and Gu Lang about the situation, he did not rush to help them increase their strength. Instead, he told them to stay in the Return from Faraway Mansion for a while.","Lin Yuan intended to evolve the Merciful Star Peony and Wen Yu’s Elemental Paper first so the Elemental Paper could reach World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","The Elemental Paper’s increase in power would not only allow for improved delivery of messages but would also increase the speed of resource flow in the main world. Once the Elemental Paper was evolved, it would be easier to deliver resources from the Radiance Federation to the rest of the main world.","...","A month passed in a flash.","The Merciful Star Peony had reached Suzerain/Myth, and the Elemental Paper had broken through to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom and had attained its own divine kingdom ability.","[Fey Name]: Elemental Paper (Bouquet of Flowering Cranes)","[Fey Species]: Elemental-species/paper species","[Fey Grade]: World Emperor (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Wood","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","[Dance of Paper]: Transform the body into a piece of paper that is immune to physical attacks. However, it is especially vulnerable to elemental attacks. The paper has teleporting power. The teleportation can be used every three seconds and has a radius of 20 kilometers.","[Paper Crane’s Promise]: The paper will be stacked to form a paper crane that can send messages. The paper crane will be engraved with the aura of the person receiving the message. If a person other than the receiver touches the paper crane, it will burst into flames. The paper crane has teleporting power that is 30 times more powerful than that of Dance of Paper.","[Thoughts Letter Paper]: The paper will absorb the target’s blood and form a temporary contract with the target. The people holding the Thoughts Letter Paper will be able to communicate with each other using their thoughts, as their thoughts will automatically appear as words on the paper. The people holding the Thoughts Letter Paper will be able to read the words together.","[Faceless Paper]: An imaginary paper will appear in front of the target, and it can take the shape of the target’s appearance. As long as the Elemental Paper is not destroyed, the imaginary paper will be undamaged even if the target is killed.","[Paper Flower Funeral]: The paper will be folded into a flower that will form an imprint when it lands on a target. Even if the target is hidden, cloned, or affected by elements, the paper flower imprint can be used to sense the target’s location.","[Paper of Ten Thousand Forms]: The paper can pretend to be a person, fey, mountain, city, sea, or even sky. While in the imitation state, the entities hidden behind the paper can enjoy absolute defense.","[Paper World Carrier]: Its own body will become a carrier for other entities. The entities can be restructured to enter the paper world. When portions of the paper are broken apart, the entities stored within will be released. The paper carrier can be used to transport entities through Paper Crane’s Promise.","[Folded Paper Abundant Entities]: A lifeform’s aura will be imprinted on the paper. The paper will be folded into the shape of the lifeform and will have the ability to think independently. (The folded paper will detect and possess the lifeform’s spiritual energy and soul, gaining an imitation fate).","[Absolute Paper World]: A special paper will create a world. The paper world can be used to store various items and will be unaffected by spatial abilities. As long as the paper world is undamaged, the items inside will be absolutely safe.","[Stripped Official Paper]: The official paper will be printed on a lifeform’s body. When the official paper leaves the lifeform’s body, it will take with it the target’s disguise, leaving the target in its original appearance.","Exclusive Skills:","[Hear Heaven’s Secrets]: The contractor will become a book of secrets linked to the flying piece of paper. When the book’s pages are turned, any knowledge within can be transferred to the flying piece of paper.","[Truth Form Paper]: While the paper is flying around, soul power can be used to form a piece of paper that can investigate the truth. When questioning a target, the paper will be folded into a flower if the target is telling the truth, and it will break apart if the target is lying.","[Floating World Ever-Changing]: One’s body will be separated. As long as a piece of paper still exists, the owner of the paper can be revived through the remaining piece of paper.","[Loading Paper Summon Return]: The paper that has left it will be activated, and the energy within it will be burned. The paper and all that are in contact with them will return to it.","[Imperial Paper Blessing]: Sacrifices and paper will be forfeited to bless a certain entity. Karma will ensure that the matters go smoothly. The sacrifices will only be used up once it is assured that the matter has been successfully achieved.","[Memorize Paper Coffin]: Official paper will form a paper coffin. The items stored in the paper coffin will be suspended and unaffected by the passage of time.","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Battleground Angel]: The paper will form wings. Each piece of paper will be able to uncover any hidden information on a battleground. All information within the battleground will be revealed, and orders can be issued with full knowledge of the battleground’s information.","Lin Yuan carefully scanned through the Elemental Paper’s new abilities, exclusive skills, and divine kingdom ability.","He was very satisfied with the Elemental Paper’s evolution. Even after reaching World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, it was still an excellent functional-type fey."]},{"number":2790,"title":"Chapter 2790 Liu Jie’s Opportunity","paragraphs":["2790 Liu Jie’s Opportunity","When it was Suzerain/Myth, the Elemental Paper’s functions were mainly centered around collecting, blocking, hiding information, and delivering resources.","The Elemental Paper had the most comprehensive functions of all the Myth Breed feys that Lin Yuan knew.","Faceless Paper and Thoughts Letter Paper were still Sky City’s key treasures.","The white-clothed followers all put on the same face when they were out on operation. This prevented them from conspiring privately.","But now, although the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Elemental Paper’s abilities had not changed much, its new abilities could help Lin Yuan take on battle circumstances at crucial moments.","For example, Folded Paper Abundant Entities first imprinted the aura of a lifeform on the folded paper. The paper would encapsulate the aura of the lifeform and take the form of the lifeform.","Normally, imitations were seen through because they did not have intelligence. Hence, they could be exposed when they interacted with others.","When Folded Paper Abundant Entities took the form of lifeforms, it would not only be capable of independent thought but would also have spiritual energy and a soul.","This radical imitation was capable of deceiving even the most outstanding interrogator. It would also be able to deceive most of the factions in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Even the most detailed technique of interrogation would not investigate a lifeform’s soul or spiritual energy but its fate veins.","At World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, fate was no longer something that was out of reach. Powerful lifeforms could even use their divine kingdom abilities to displace the fate of other experts. However, it went without saying that doing so came at a heavy price.","Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter had told Lin Yuan a lot about the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Lin Yuan had also asked Fan Lou and Kong Huan many questions while they were describing the East Universe to him.","Now, Lin Yuan had a general understanding of the East Universe and no longer had to feel his way around blindly.","The Elemental Paper’s Folded Paper Abundant Entities could be used in many situations, but especially when a lifeform needed to be used as a lure.","Absolute Paper World involved the Elemental Paper creating a special paper to produce a small world. The paper world could store items and would be unaffected by spatial energy.","It would be a small matter if the paper world was just affected by spatial energy. But if the enemy used a special method to target the items being stored and expel them from the paper world, the stored items would be pushed out into the abyss.","Currently, there were star pirates roaming most of the outskirts of the universes. Only a few of the star pirates were capable of robbing the large species, and most of them depended on a livelihood of picking up trash. They made a living from picking up the items disposed of from the spatial equipment. Occasionally, they were even able to earn a tidy sum.","Spring had already told Lin Yuan that regardless of how well spatial equipment like fey storage boxes were made, they would become useless in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Although there was still spatial equipment made from spatial ingredients, factions with sufficient power usually chose different methods of storing items.","Every powerful species had to grapple with items that were previously stored in their spatial equipment being expelled.","However, methods to ensure safe access were rare.","Lin Yuan intended to search for such methods in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","But now, the Elemental Paper’s new ability solved this issue for Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan felt that Stripped Official Paper could be paired extremely well with Truth Form Paper.","Truth Form Paper involved producing a special type of official paper and assessing whether a target’s answer was true or false. If the target answered truthfully to a question, the paper would be folded into a flower. But if the target answered with a lie, the paper would be shredded.","Stripped Official Paper was used when a target was deemed to be telling a lie or if the target was wearing a disguise. The paper would cover the target’s body and absorb the target’s disguise. When the paper was stripped from the target, it would take the target’s disguise away with it.","Normally, interrogation techniques exerted pressure on the target or used coercion to force the target to tell the truth. These abilities were effective but were also passive. If the target was unwilling to answer, there was nothing the other party could do about it.","However, Stripped Official Paper used a proactive method to remove the target’s disguise. This lowered the difficulty of the interrogation. Even the targets with the tightest lips would not be able to hide their secrets.","Compared to the new abilities, the Elemental Paper’s new exclusive skills were more remarkable.","Loading Paper Summon Return was very similar to the Ethereal Jellyfish’s ability.","The Ethereal Jellyfish used itself as a core and could summon lifeforms that made contact with its tentacle nodes to its side.","The Elemental Paper’s Loading Paper Summon Return could do the same.","Official paper that had special functions, such as the Faceless Paper and Thoughts Letter Paper, could be affected by Loading Paper Summon Return.","This allowed the Elemental Paper to become Sky City’s other core.","All of Sky City’s members would receive a Faceless Paper and Thoughts Letter Paper. At key moments, they would become life-preservation methods for them.","If a faction had more cores, they would be undeniably stronger than if they only had one core.","The Immortal exclusive skill, Imperial Paper Blessing, could predict fortune and misfortune.","The Elemental Paper would first produce a special imperial paper. But to do so, sufficient energy had to be sacrificed.","The imperial paper’s original intention was to bless targets and use karma to increase the success rate of the target’s subsequent progress. However, the sacrifices would only be used up when it was assured that the matter was completed successfully. Otherwise, only the imperial paper would be used up.","When Lin Yuan had grand plans and was unsure if they would be successful, he could ask Wen Yu to use Imperial Paper Blessing once to predict if the matter could be completed safely.","There were many matters in which safety was not determined by Lin Yuan’s abilities but rather by the quantity of manpower.","When Sky City ventured into the Sky Beyond the Clouds for development, the faction would only grow stronger.","Lin Yuan could not deploy his full force in every task. Instead, he could only send a portion of them.","The Elemental Paper’s Eternal Breed exclusive skill, Memorize Paper Coffin, could be seen as a life-preservation and storage ability.","In response to Lin Yuan’s question, Wen Yu had mentioned that the paper coffin formed by the Elemental Paper was very weak and could easily break when impacted by external force. Alternatively, it could be viewed as a controlling-type ability.","If anyone on their side was in danger during a battle and on the brink of death, they could be placed in the Memorize Paper Coffin in a suspended state, unaffected by the passage of time. Even if their injuries could only be addressed a long time later, they would still be able to remain alive.","Some special resources decayed and rotted despite being stored in airtight spaces, making them impossible to preserve.","But in the coffin, time would come to a standstill.","Hence, these resources would not encounter such issues.","These resources were not common, and bloodlines could be considered one of them.","This was why Spring had given Lin Yuan the bloodlines to absorb immediately after extracting them.","Bloodline power would lose its effectiveness after being stored for a prolonged period. Although it would still have some effects, they would be highly discounted.","When factions traded bloodlines in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, they always used items such as the Memorize Paper Coffin.","Similar to the Thoughts Letter Paper and Faceless Paper, the Memorize Paper Coffin could be produced repeatedly. However, it cost far more energy to make the Memorize Paper Coffin than it did to make the Faceless Paper and Thoughts Letter Paper.","The Memorize Paper Coffin’s special characteristics enabled it to have many uses within Sky City.","Lin Yuan had only sent Kong Huan, the two Alluring Foxes, and Fan Lou back to the Sky Beyond the Clouds. Winter had not extracted the bloodline power from the corpses because the bloodline power could not be easily stored, and Lin Yuan did not intend to absorb them.","Once the bloodline power was extracted from the corpses, their energy would be affected.","Lin Yuan was going to instruct Red Thorn to turn these corpses into Divine Kingdom weapons.","In truth, Winter felt that the value of these experts came from the bloodline power they possessed.","Winter used to possess treasures that could store bloodline power, but they had rotted away in time.","Otherwise, the four of them would not have had to cultivate a mountain.","Once Lin Yuan saw Memorize Paper Mountain, he immediately thought of the invaders from the Sky Beyond the Clouds who were still alive.","Lin Yuan intended to ask Wen Yu to use the Elemental Paper to create a Memorize Paper Coffin, which he would give to Winter. The latter would then extract the invaders’ bloodlines and store them as combat resources.","Rather than its abilities and exclusive skills, Lin Yuan was most interested in the Elemental Paper’s divine kingdom ability, Battleground Angel.","In the past, Wen Yu could only remain backstage and could not participate in combat.","However, Battleground Angel would change that.","During combat, paper that could carry information would form wings on her back, enabling her to know everything about the battle and understand every facet of information.","This ability would not make much of an impact in a small battle, but in a large battle, it would be a force to be reckoned with.","Regardless of how many people were in the battle, Wen Yu would have full control over the situation and be able to issue organized and effective orders.","Frankly, Wen Yu did not have the strongest combat strategy abilities in Sky City. This title went to Bai Qinghuan.","Lin Yuan could use Connected Tails to link Wen Yu and Bai Qinghuan together during combat so Wen Yu could pass on information to Bai Qinghuan. The latter would use the information she received to issue orders.","Lin Yuan was not the only one who was satisfied with the evolution of the Elemental Paper. Wen Yu was just as pleasantly surprised.","After Lin Yuan helped Wen Yu evolve the Elemental Paper, Wen Yu dove back into facilitating the flow of resources in the main world.","In a month, the Elemental Paper had reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","However, the Merciful Star Peony’s grade evolution was very slow because it needed to absorb power from the constellations. Furthermore, it had yet to comprehend a Willpower Rune. Nurturing the Merciful Star Peony could not be rushed.","...","Liu Jie was next in line to increase his power.","He longed to increase his power just as much as Zong Ze and Gu Lang did.","The higher Elegance’s grade, the stronger its combat power would be. As Elegance continued to evolve, its insect army would become increasingly fearsome. It would also be able to control an even larger insect army.","Lin Yuan found it difficult to imagine the power Liu Jie would attain once Elegance reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom. He was unsure if, at that time, he would still be able to hold his own against Liu Jie with just his feys!","Liu Jie’s current strength did not come from just Elegance but also the fairies.","Liu Jie produced the fairies by using the Firefly Demon Fetuses to induce the transformation of insect-species carcinoma feys.","Alas, they had only obtained 12 of the Firefly Demon Fetuses from Yin Lin. These 12 Firefly Demon Fetuses had both given him a new opportunity and restrained him at the same time.","If Liu Jie could turn all the insect-species carcinoma feys he controlled into fairies, his power would skyrocket.","Ever since Lin Yuan took control of the dimensional worlds, he had been mulling over the dimensional world where the Firefly Demon Fetuses came from. He wanted to find out the truth behind this source-type item. Hence, he had sent out the Samsara Realm Dictators to search for them.","After questioning various Samsara Realm Dictators, he learned that none of them had heard of the Firefly Demon Fetuses.","From this, Lin Yuan knew that the species that produced the Firefly Demon Fetus had to be very rare.","So far, Lin Yuan’s best guess was that the Firefly Demon Fetus came from the alien insect world. The marsh world was also possible. The alien insect world’s main inhabitants were insects, and insects also made up a large portion of the lifeforms in the marsh world.","Previously, the Freedom Federation had used the Firefly Demon Fetuses to target the Radiance Federation. The Freedom Federation wanted to use theμ to wreak havoc in the Radiance Federation.","At that time, a Class 6 marsh dimensional rift had opened in the Freedom Federation, and Lin Yuan had been fully focused on the alien insect and marsh worldσ.","It never crossed his mind that the Firefly Demon Fetuses could actually come from the subterranean world.","Hollow Earth was a powerful Land Imp who had joined Lin Yuan’s camp. However, he had not had many opportunities to interact with Lin Yuan directly.","Previously, he had been pushed to the brink by Bai Qinghuan.","Nonetheless, he always regarded Lin Yuan’s words as sacred law.","When Hollow Earth realized that the Firefly Demon Fetuses came from the Mineral Heart Demon Sandfly, he began silently collecting the Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies.","He did not inform the other subterranean Dictators of this information."]},{"number":2791,"title":"Chapter 2791 Elegance’s Death Echo!","paragraphs":["2791 Elegance’s Death Echo!","Hollow Earth brought the Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies and Firefly Demon Fetuses he had collected to Lin Yuan.","He had already reached the Afterlife Realm and could be considered the strongest subterranean Dictator.","The only other candidate who stood a chance against him was Rock Underworld. Both of them had received the Earth’s Sacred Fruit.","Mountain Furrow, who had not received the Earth’s Sacred Fruit, was less powerful than them.","If not for the fact that the two of them were certain that Lin Yuan would not be increasing Mountain Furrow’s power, they would be doing all they could to keep him down.","Being a Land Imp, Hollow Earth was much cleverer than Mountain Furrow and Rock Underworld.","Previously, Lin Yuan had assigned Hollow Earth to work with Bai Qinghuan, so he had worked as her assistant. He had followed her directions to organize the army of Land Imps to fix the dimensional wall that had since been damaged and ordered to be deconstructed.","Since he had been working under Bai Qinghuan, he had had no choice but to listen and endure whatever she said or did.","Being ordered around by a mere slip of a girl and having millions of Land Imps in his team wiped out had caused Hollow Earth to lose his authority among the other Land Imps.","Although these Land Imps would not go so far as to riot against him, this situation still did not sit right with Hollow Earth.","Luckily, Lin Yuan eventually punished Bai Qinghuan for this.","Lin Yuan had placed him in command of the project to take down the dimensional wall. Bai Qinghuan had only been there to assist him.","This allowed Hollow Earth to know that Lin Yuan did care about how he felt. Just knowing this was enough for Hollow Earth. He was not petty enough to try to regain his authority and reputation at the expense of Bai Qinghuan.","Given that Lin Yuan had previously allowed Bai Qinghuan to take charge of such an important matter, it showed how much he valued her. In the future, she was sure to be one of his prominent aides.","Lin Yuan’s actions were meant to comfort him while also taking Bai Qinghuan down a peg.","Hollow Earth had heard a piece of news from Bai Qinghuan, which was that there was a high chance Lin Yuan would be leaving this world for a higher-level world.","If this news were true, this world would undergo many changes.","The gears in Hollow Earth’s head began turning.","He believed that it was unfeasible to expect Lin Yuan to take him with him.","Although he had reached the Afterlife Realm, there were many other Dictators.","Now that the dimensional worlds had combined with the main world, everyone was accumulating power much faster than they used to.","It was likely that the Dictators would be staying behind in the main world to watch over it in Lin Yuan’s stead.","Lin Yuan would definitely issue many tasks or even lay down various rules for them before he left.","Hollow Earth expected all of them.","Without outstanding talent, the mediocre could reign.","All of them would have to follow Lin Yuan’s orders. However, the Dictators would definitely try to rank each other and fight over power.","Hollow Earth badly wanted to be able to distinguish himself.","Establishing a good relationship with Lin Yuan could only benefit him. It would not only enable him to receive benefits but also allow him to be directly appointed to a position with Lin Yuan’s trust.","Otherwise, Hollow Earth would never put so much effort and hard work into searching for these specific resources.","...","Lin Yuan was delighted when Hollow Earth found and presented him with the more than ten Firefly Demon Fetuses. He knew just how much Liu Jie’s power would grow with these Firefly Demon Fetuses.","Liu Jie could turn more than ten other insect-species carcinoma feys into fairies. He might even be able to continuously evolve them to the point of reaching World Emperor/Divine Kingdom!","These fairies were no longer insect-species carcinoma feys. They were just like any other fey.","By contracting Elegance, Liu Jie was unable to form contracts with any other fey.","The Firefly Demon Fetuses broke this shackle and opened up a bright future for Liu Jie.","Furthermore, after presenting him with the Firefly Demon Fetuses, Hollow Earth followed this up with more than 20 Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies.","The Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies were not a well-regarded insect-species lifeform in the subterranean world.","They were extremely capable of searching for mineral hearts and would immediately begin consuming them upon discovering them.","However, they were rather weak.","The Mineral Heart Demon Sandfly was venomous, so even if a powerful Apostle consumed them, they would not be able to absorb the Mineral Heart Demon Sandfly’s energy. Rather, they would be inflicted with the venom, and their bodies would go numb.","The subterranean world’s lifeforms viewed the Mineral Heart Demon Sandfly as an enormous waste of resources and would kill any that they came across.","There were very few Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies that could mature to the point of producing source-type items.","The Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies usually lived in groups. Once one group was exterminated, there would be no Mineral Heart Demon Sandfly to be found within a thousand-meter radius. The source-type items produced by the Mineral Heart Demon Sandfly were also considered to be inauspicious and were usually damaged, drowned, or buried the moment they were discovered.","As a result of this, none of the Dictators expected the source-type item produced by the Mineral Heart Demon Sandfly to be what Lin Yuan had been asking them to search for.","After Hollow Earth handed the Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies to Lin Yuan, he was unafraid of the news spreading.","All he had to do was to be the first to help Lin Yuan.","If, instead, he tried to stop others from trying to help Lin Yuan, he would be taking the low road, and there was a high chance that Lin Yuan would become displeased with him.","...","Lin Yuan used True Data to carefully examine the Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies.","Once he was done, he decided to keep a few with him so that he could slowly nurture them.","Then, he would send out an order to the subterranean Dictators so they could pass on the message to the Apostles. Every single subterranean Apostle was to lead their subordinates to any mine they could find to search for the Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies.","The Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies were challenging to nurture. Lin Yuan did not have many mineral hearts available to feed the Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies to enable them to mature to the point of being able to produce the source-type items in order to harvest them.","The subterranean world was only so large. It would not be difficult to find more of the Firefly Demon Fetuses.","He only needed to stock up on a few more Firefly Demon Fetuses, and they would be sufficient to meet Liu Jie’s needs.","Even if Liu Jie needed more in the future, Lin Yuan could just nurture the Mineral Heart Demon Sandflies he had stored away.","Liu Jie was already very satisfied with his current increase in power. He was no longer as downtrodden and unconfident as he used to be.","But once he saw the Firefly Demon Fetuses that Lin Yuan was handing to him, Liu Jie could not help but begin trembling in excitement.","“Lin... Lin Yuan, these...”","Liu Jie was so overcome by excitement that he began to stutter.","Seeing the state that Liu Jie was in, Lin Yuan reached out and patted his shoulder as he said with a smile, “Big Brother Liu, these are not all of the Firefly Demon Fetuses. I will be collecting more for you in the future!","“You can use them to turn all the insect-species carcinoma feys under Elegance’s control into fairies before beginning to nurture them. From now on, you won’t have to be troubled by having to choose which insect-species carcinoma fey to transform! I have already prepared the resources you will need to nurture the fairies.”","While he spoke, Lin Yuan handed Liu Jie two fey storage boxes containing the resources prepared for Liu Jie.","Liu Jie solemnly stored away the resources.","“Lin Yuan, I am done organizing the white-clothed followers’ tasks in the Startling Lines Continent. You have given me so many of the Firefly Demon Fetuses. I intend to go into seclusion for some time to nurture them.”","Lin Yuan said seriously, “The Empress Core of All Insects evolves its grade very quickly. With these Firefly Demon Fetuses, the insect-species carcinoma feys just need to be transformed into fairies!","“The most important part is still Elegance’s combination of abilities! If these insect-species carcinoma feys aren’t nurtured properly, and their abilities deviate from what you were expecting, you will still be able to stop nurturing them and nurture other insect-species carcinoma feys instead. However, you can’t be careless with Elegance’s abilities!”","Liu Jie raised his hand and summoned Elegance.","Elegance had reached Sovereign X/Creation IX. Its three pairs of wings were a sign that its fairy bloodline had evolved.","“Lin Yuan, I have already given Elegance a few insect-species feys’ genetic models to consume. Elegance already has new abilities! Moreover, the exclusive skills it gained from its evolutions also suit my combat style very well.”","While Liu Jie was speaking, Liu Jie used True Data to check on Elegance.","[Fey Name]: Insect Queen","[Fey Species]: Insect-species/fairy-species","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Spiritual","[Fey Quality]: Creation IX","Abilities:","[Execution Blade Insect]: Eight hooked insect legs will grow out of the body. The sense of taste, smell, and mouth will be degraded. The insect legs have an extremely strong sensing ability. The sharp end of the hooked legs has mouths that are connected to the inner organs. When the legs pierce a target, the mouths will emerge and break through anything hard within the target’s body.","[Vibrating Armor Ladybug]: Its back will open and have a strong defense against attacks. Its back will also start to vibrate violently and reflect physical attacks. If targeted by elemental attacks, the vibrating back would be able to dodge a portion of the elemental damage.","[Flowing Plasma Electricity Insect]: The insect will spit out large amounts of plasma that will start to flow. The flowing plasma will have a strong, paralyzing effect. It will cause long-lasting electric-related damage to the target.","[Electromagnetic Chrysalis]: In a chrysalis state, it will be able to speed up the rate of accumulation of the plasma. The plasma will be quickly released. In the moth state, it will be able to use plasma to manipulate electromagnetic fields and control targets from a distance away.","[Lonely Night Hurricane Moth]: By flapping its wings, it will be able to generate strong winds that it can manipulate to attack a target. Its wings will produce a special scale powder that will be able to blend perfectly with the night or camouflage in the day.","[Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly]: It can boost other insect-species lifeforms and increase their speed, strength, defense, and store of energy. When necessary, it can become a shield and take on a deadly attack on behalf of one of the feys it has boosted.","[Curse Explosion Brain Insect]: It will be hosted in the brain of an insect and supply energy to that insect’s brain to increase the brain’s intelligence. It will be able to issue orders to the insect-species lifeforms in the vicinity. Once the insect’s brain is no longer active, it will automatically explode. The shocks of the explosion will place curses on the insects in the surroundings, causing them to go into a frenzy.","[Fortress Floating Insect]: An enormous insect body will be able to carry a large number of insects. The light insect body will be able to move rapidly in the air. Insects can be stored and released.","Exclusive Skills:","[Blast Recovery]: The Insect Queen will select a portion of the insects it produces and explode them. The explosion timings can be adjusted based on the positions of the insects. After the blast, the Insect Queen will regain some of the protein and spiritual power.","[Swarm Frenzy]: When the insect swarm is in a frenzied state, its speed will skyrocket. In the frenzied state, the insect swarm will be bloodthirsty and be able to replenish their vitality using the blood within the target.","[Death Echo]: Each time an insect dies, an echo will resonate back to the Insect Queen. With every 100 echoes, the rate at which the Insect Queen produces protein will be raised, increasing the rate at which insects are produced.","[Main Body Split]: Half of the energy will be depleted to split the body. The split body will possess the same insect-producing abilities as the main body (the current bloodline will only allow for three splits).","When Lin Yuan last checked Elegance’s data, it had only been Diamond X/Fantasy V.","Lin Yuan had given the six Six Treasures Cloud Dragonflies to Liu Jie. Before that, Liu Jie had been unable to confirm Elegance’s Diamond ability. Elegance could not reach Myth Breed before its Diamond ability was confirmed.","At that point, it had almost been time for the Radiance Hundred Sequence selection.","Lin Yuan had been anxious to evolve Shiny and had not witnessed Elegance’s evolution.","But now, Liu Jie was telling Lin Yuan that Elegance’s Myth Breed exclusive skill was Death Echo.","Death Echo was very similar to Blast Recovery.","However, Blast Recovery required Elegance to trigger the insects’ explosions and retrieve the energy and protein. This would cause Elegance’s rate of insect production to fall during the battle.","However, Death Echo did not require Elegance’s conscious effort.","As long as the insects died, Elegance would automatically receive an echo. Once there were 100 echoes, Elegance would not only receive additional protein, but the rate at which it produced insects would also be raised.","The rate at which Elegance produced insects was linked to its power. It was the crux of Elegance’s abilities!"]},{"number":2792,"title":"Chapter 2792 Divine Kingdom Ability: [Unyielding Insect Spirit]!","paragraphs":["2792 Divine Kingdom Ability: [Unyielding Insect Spirit]!","Liu Jie had been trying to come up with a way to increase the rate at which Elegance produced insects.","Elegance’s current rate of insect production was very fast. However, it was still unable to complete the insect army formation in a short span of time.","As a result, Elegance was greatly restricted during battle, and it caused Elegance to only be suited for formation battles.","However, skirmishes were much more common in the wild than formation battles. Skirmishes were the most common form of battle in the wild.","Liu Jie had attempted many methods with little success.","He had even tried searching for suitable insect-species lifeforms in the hopes of using their abilities to speed up Elegance’s rate of insect production. However, he never managed to find such insect-species lifeforms.","Death Echo finally gave Elegance the possibility of rapidly producing insects during skirmishes.","Next came Main Body Split. It referred to Elegance using half of the energy in its body to split itself. Its split selves would also be able to produce insects.","This exclusive skill increased the rate at which Elegance produced insects.","Although it required a large amount of Elegance’s energy to be sacrificed, it would not be difficult for Elegance to recover its energy. Many of the insect-species carcinoma feys Liu Jie controlled could serve such a function.","The splitting effects of Main Body Split were linked to Elegance’s bloodline. Given the current strength of Elegance’s bloodline, Main Body Split would only allow Elegance to split its body three times.","After splitting its body three times, Elegance could produce insects at four times its current rate. This would allow it to build its formation very quickly when it was in battle.","Death Echo and Main Body Split both raised Elegance’s combat abilities.","This was not the first time that Lin Yuan was amazed by Elegance’s power.","Given that Elegance could attain abilities and exclusive skills that were so complementary to it during its evolutions, it meant that Elegance’s potential for combat was terrifyingly powerful!","In the past, Liu Jie was always conflicted about which abilities to choose whenever he evolved Elegance. He always ended up seeking Lin Yuan’s opinion.","But now, he no longer did this because he was affirmed in the path he would take. Hence, he knew what choices to make.","Lin Yuan felt that Elegance’s Suzerain and Sovereign abilities were all excellent choices.","Elegance had absorbed the Curse Explosion Brain Insect and Fortress Floating Insect, neither of which Lin Yuan had previously heard of.","Evidently, the information on these two insect-species feys had never appeared on Star Web. If they had, it was impossible Lin Yuan would not have heard of them before.","Wen Yu had been using the Elemental Paper’s Hear Heaven’s Secrets to help Liu Jie search the main world for insect-species lifeforms. It was likely that the Curse Explosion Brain Insect and Fortress Floating Insect had been discovered during this search.","When the Curse Explosion Brain Insect was hosted in the brain of an insect-species lifeform, it would supply energy to the host and increase its intelligence. This would increase the host’s ability to think critically. It could then issue orders to the same type of insect-species lifeforms.","This strengthened the organization and management of the insect army, thereby lightening Elegance and Liu Jie’s load.","Now, when Liu Jie and Elegance were commandeering the army of insects, they would no longer have to carefully issue every order and watch over the insects. Instead, the army of insects could carry out Liu Jie’s instructions perfectly.","More importantly, when the Curse Explosion Brain Insect’s host died and the insect brain was no longer active, the Curse Explosion Brain Insect would automatically explode. The explosion would place curses on the surrounding insects and cause them to enter a state of frenzy.","A frenzied state was a ferocious form of controlling ability that caused the target to attack everything around it.","Although this would cause the frenzied target to attack the insect army, it would also be unable to defend itself. This would allow the insect army to attack the target effectively. The insect army was unafraid of taking hits and getting injured.","Once the insect army died, it would not only be able to help recover Elegance’s energy but could also resonate echoes that increased the rate at which Elegance produced insects.","By selecting the Curse Explosion Brain Insect as Elegance’s ability, Liu Jie had strengthened his organization of the insect army as well as their combat abilities. It was a perfect choice!","On the other hand, the Fortress Floating Insect was a stronger functional-type ability than the Curse Explosion Brain Insect.","The Fortress Floating Insect substantially increased Elegance’s maneuverability.","The Fortress Floating Insect was an enormous insect that could float in the sky. It was filled with gasses, making it extremely light and capable of moving quickly through the air.","If, during combat, the enemy’s side bolstered their power, Elegance could send out the Fortress Floating Insect across far distances to provide aid.","If Liu Jie needed to instruct Elegance to establish combat in different areas, the Fortress Floating Insect could be used to send troops to even the most far-flung areas.","Previously, Lin Yuan had been busy when Liu Jie was trying to set up and coordinate Elegance’s abilities. Otherwise, despite having his own ideas, Liu Jie would still have sought Lin Yuan’s opinion.","Liu Jie was about to introduce the new insects that he intended Elegance to consume when Lin Yuan waved his hand dismissively.","“Big Brother Liu, Elegance has reached Sovereign X/Creation IX. You know better than me what abilities and exclusive skills it should pick in the future. You don’t need to ask me for my opinion anymore.","“Going forward, whenever Elegance evolves, you can just pick an insect and feed it to Elegance. Elegance won’t be able to continue increasing its grade unless its abilities are decided.”","Liu Jie smiled and nodded.","It was true that he had already chosen Elegance’s next evolution ability.","Liu Jie had carefully pondered over his decision.","If Lin Yuan had given a different opinion, Liu Jie would have felt a pang of regret even if he followed Lin Yuan’s decision.","But now that Lin Yuan was leaving the decision fully up to him, Liu Jie could make all the decisions regarding his feys.","Liu Jie was very thankful for Lin Yuan’s trust in him, and he was looking forward to seeing Lin Yuan’s reaction to his decision. He believed that Lin Yuan would be satisfied with his decision.","Lin Yuan waved at Elegance, and it landed on his palm.","Lin Yuan circulated the energy in his body and began helping Elegance evolve. He put all his effort into circulating the energy in his body, and Elegance’s grade shot up.","Liu Jie remained by Lin Yuan’s side. Each time Elegance’s grade evolved, Liu Jie fed it an insect-species fey.","Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter remained in the Return from Faraway Mansion, and the four of them worked together to protect the mansion.","Among the four of them, Autumn had spent the least amount of time with Lin Yuan and was anxious to demonstrate what he could do.","Spring, Summer, and Winter did not try to compete with Autumn.","Autumn helped Elegance fend off the repulsion of the world wills and the trials of evolution.","Meanwhile, Elegance successfully evolved into a pinnacle eight-winged fairy.","In terms of its bloodline, Elegance’s bloodline had exceeded that of Red Thorn and Silver Corona. It now had the top fairy bloodline in the main world.","However, Lin Yuan knew that this was only temporary.","Red Thorn had evolved three grades in succession. It was only to be expected that its bloodline would evolve significantly.","Silver Corona and Red Thorn were both accumulating power and were at eight-wings.","Once they reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, they would become ten-winged fairies at the very least. It was possible they could even bring Lin Yuan even more surprises!","Lin Yuan saw Liu Jie’s expression of deep thought and knew that Liu Jie was sensing the divine kingdom ability Elegance had obtained after reaching World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Elegance.","[Fey Name]: Insect Queen","[Fey Species]: Insect-species/fairy-species","[Fey Grade]: World Emperor (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Source/Spiritual","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","[Execution Blade Insect]: Eight hooked insect legs will grow out of the body. The sense of taste, smell, and mouth will be degraded. The insect legs have an extremely strong sensing ability. The sharp end of the hooked legs has mouths that are connected to the inner organs. When the legs pierce a target, the mouths will emerge and break through anything hard within the target’s body.","[Vibrating Armor Ladybug]: Its back will open and have a strong defense against attacks. Its back will also start to vibrate violently and reflect physical attacks. If targeted by elemental attacks, the vibrating back would be able to dodge a portion of the elemental damage.","[Flowing Plasma Electricity Insect]: The insect will spit out large amounts of plasma that will start to flow. The flowing plasma will have a strong, paralyzing effect. It will cause long-lasting electric-related damage to the target.","[Electromagnetic Chrysalis]: In a chrysalis state, it will be able to speed up the rate of accumulation of the plasma. The plasma will be quickly released. In the moth state, it will be able to use plasma to manipulate electromagnetic fields and control targets from a distance away.","[Lonely Night Hurricane Moth]: By flapping its wings, it will be able to generate strong winds that it can manipulate to attack a target. Its wings will produce a special scale powder that will be able to blend perfectly with the night or camouflage in the day.","[Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly]: It can boost other insect-species lifeforms and increase their speed, strength, defense, and store of energy. When necessary, it can become a shield and take on a deadly attack on behalf of one of the feys it has boosted.","[Curse Explosion Brain Insect]: It will be hosted in the brain of an insect and supply energy to that insect’s brain to increase the brain’s intelligence. It will be able to issue orders to the insect-species lifeforms in the vicinity. Once the insect’s brain is no longer active, it will automatically explode. The shocks of the explosion will place curses on the insects in the surroundings, causing them to go into a frenzy.","[Fortress Floating Insect]: An enormous insect body will be able to carry a large number of insects. The light insect body will be able to move rapidly in the air. Insects can be stored and released.","[Protein Millipede]: It will reproduce to create a large amount of insect protein. The insect protein can be supplied to other targets. While producing egg protein, it will inject a special venom into the insects. Once it dissolves in the body of other insects, absorbing the rich liquid will allow it to recover its depleted energy.","[Revival Death Insect]: When many insects die, and their souls have not been used, they can be revived. The dead insects will turn into dead spirits. Although they will not follow the Insect Queen’s orders directly, they will follow the Revival Death Insect’s orders.","Exclusive Skills:","[Blast Recovery]: The Insect Queen will select a portion of the insects it produces and explode them. The explosion timings can be adjusted based on the positions of the insects. After the blast, the Insect Queen will regain some of the protein and spiritual power.","[Swarm Frenzy]: When the insect swarm is in a frenzied state, its speed will skyrocket. In the frenzied state, the insect swarm will be bloodthirsty and be able to replenish their vitality using the blood within the target.","[Death Echo]: Each time an insect dies, an echo will resonate back to the Insect Queen. With every 100 echoes, the rate at which the Insect Queen produces protein will be raised, increasing the rate at which insects are produced.","[Main Body Split]: Half of the energy will be depleted to split the body. The split body will possess the same insect-producing abilities as the main body (the current bloodline will only allow for four splits).","[Gene Transform Fairy]: It will use the special insect genes in its body to support the fairy bloodline and nurture fairies. The fairies will be linked to its genes, and their bloodlines will boost its own bloodline. The fairies’ bloodlines can be evolved individually. When necessary, the fairy bloodlines can be absorbed to allow its own bloodline to break through.","[Forceful Reincarnation]: When dealt with a lethal attack and on the brink of death, it can inject its soul into its muscles to forcefully nurture a fetus. When sufficient energy is supplied to the fetus, the fetus will be reincarnated into a new body.","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Unyielding Insect Spirit]: When the insects it nurtures die, their souls can be collected in the divine kingdom as long as they have fought valiantly in battle. When the divine kingdom’s aura is released, the divine kingdom’s aura will allow the insect spirits to become even braver. These insect spirits will be able to provide the Insect Queen with faith power in the same way lifeforms do.","Faith power was now a common power that Lin Yuan used.","However, it is still completely foreign to Liu Jie. He had yet to try using faith power.","Hence, it was likely Liu Jie did not understand the benefits of Elegance’s Unyielding Insect Spirit.","Lin Yuan smiled at Liu Jie and said, “Big Brother Liu, Elegance has reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom and has attained an impressive divine kingdom ability!”"]},{"number":2793,"title":"Chapter 2793 Before the Journey to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2793 Before the Journey to the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Lin Yuan was always very serious when it came to nurturing feys.","If Elegance’s divine kingdom ability could not make the cut, Lin Yuan would never say what he said, regardless of how much he wanted to comfort Liu Jie.","He was truly impressed by Elegance’s divine kingdom ability!","Elegance’s divine kingdom ability could not only increase the insect army’s overall combat power but could also help Elegance quickly increase its power.","Unyielding Divine Kingdom would allow the souls of the insects Elegance produced to enter its divine kingdom after they died. The souls in the divine kingdom could support the insect army and enable them to become more ferocious when Elegance released its divine kingdom aura. The insect souls could also provide a large amount of faith power.","From his conversations with Kong Huan and Fan Lou, Lin Yuan realized that most of the Divine Kingdom experts in the Sky Beyond the Clouds had a very difficult time increasing their power because they struggled to obtain pure faith power.","After Elegance’s insects died, their souls would enter the divine kingdom.","Only one insect might not be able to provide Elegance with much faith power. But at the very least, the faith power would be pure.","Moreover, as it engaged in more and more battles, more insects would die, and more insect souls would gather in the divine kingdom.","Accordingly, Elegance would also be able to obtain faith power at an increasing rate.","When he saw that Liu Jie still looked uncertain after hearing what he said, Lin Yuan began to explain, “Big Brother Liu, your fey has reached the Divine Kingdom level and needs to absorb faith power to continue increasing its power. This will also apply to you once you break through past pinnacle spirit fire.","“Faith power is the building brick that Divine Kingdom experts use to increase their power. With the dead insects, Elegance’s divine kingdom will be able to accumulate faith power swiftly. This will allow Elegance to continue increasing its power quickly even now that it has reached the divine kingdom.","“When other lifeforms reach the Divine Kingdom level, they need to come up with ways and means to get their hands on faith power.”","Lin Yuan was going to the Sky Beyond the Clouds because of his World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys. He needed to create an incubator for them in which they would be able to obtain faith power.","Although Lin Yuan could give them his own faith power, he had his own needs for faith power and could not give it away liberally to help his feys increase their power.","Lin Yuan’s words were beyond Liu Jie’s comprehension. He tried his best to understand what Lin Yuan was saying and had a basic understanding of the concept of faith power.","Lin Yuan intended to tell Genius all that he knew about faith power so Genius could use Connected Tails to relay the information to all the main members of Sky City. This would enable them to become aware of how they could continue increasing their power after they reached the Divine Kingdom level.","Once Liu Jie digested Lin Yuan’s words, he looked at Lin Yuan seriously and asked, “Lin Yuan, what do you think of Elegance’s two new abilities?”","Lin Yuan had used True Data to check on Elegance and was aware of its new abilities.","In order to better demonstrate Elegance’s new abilities, Liu Jie instructed Elegance to produce the Protein Millipede and Revival Death Insect.","The Protein Millipede was an enormous insect that was almost 1,300 meters long. It was extremely rare for an insect to grow to such a size.","Once the Protein Millipede appeared, it began moving its head and tail vigorously in tandem.","It did not take long for the Protein Millipede to produce a large number of yellowish-green eggs that attached themselves to the surface of the Protein Millipede.","If a person with agoraphobia saw the Protein Millipede now, goosebumps would immediately rise all over their skin.","Lin Yuan had seen his fair share of gross sights while evolving his feys. He even found Red Thorn’s eyes to be cute.","However, he could not stand the sight of the wiggling egg-covered Protein Millipede.","In order to help the Protein Millipede to speed up the rate at which it produced the insect eggs, Liu Jie instructed Elegance to produce a few of the Vibrating Armor Ladybugs.","Once the Vibrating Armor Ladybugs were created, they dutifully lay down beside the Protein Millipede and exposed their soft bellies.","The Protein Millipede began chomping on the Vibrating Armor Ladybug’s abdomens.","The Vibrating Armor Ladybugs let out howls of pain as the softest part of their bodies were bitten and eaten away. However, they did not resist in the slightest.","Once the Vibrating Armor Ladybugs completely lost all signs of life, the Protein Millipede began absorbing the fluids within their bodies before producing even more insect eggs.","The Protein Millipede used its tail to gather all the insect eggs and deliver them to Elegance’s cavity. In an instant, Elegance was replenished with a sea of protein.","During combat, Elegance only needed to nurture a few more of the Protein Millipedes so they could continuously produce protein for it. This would allow Elegance to create insects endlessly. It would not have to be worried about encountering a powerful enemy during combat that significantly cut down the size of the insect army.","Liu Jie was shocked that Liu Jie had been able to find such an insect-species fey. It was very suitable for Elegance.","Lin Yuan knew that there were many powerful insects.","However, to Liu Jie, what was important was not the strength of the insects that Elegance used as its abilities but their overall compatibility.","Once the Vibrating Armor Ladybugs’ corpses were absorbed to the point that only their shells were left, Elegance released energy fluctuations that brimmed with a death aura toward the grayish-black shells, turning them into dead spirits.","However, the insect souls also changed.","The insect souls that were changed into dead spirits could not enter the divine kingdom through Unyielding Insect Spirit. However, they could be used to supplement Elegance’s army of insects rapidly.","They significantly increased the insect army’s strength. It would not be an exaggeration to say that the strength was multiplied numerous times.","The only drawback was that the insect dead spirits would not be able to listen to Elegance’s orders. They would only listen to the Revival Death Insect’s orders.","Luckily, Elegance could control the Revival Death Insect and could use it to control the insect dead spirits.","The insect dead spirits would be used as cannon fodder that protected the safety of the army of insects.","After Elegance’s bloodline evolved to four wings, Main Body Split increased from three splits to four splits.","Additionally, Elegance had obtained two new exclusive skills, Gene Transform Fairy and Forceful Reincarnation.","Gene Transformation Fairy would allow Elegance to inject its own fairy bloodline into insects that had its genes. The insect genes and its own fairy bloodline would be combined to nurture fairies. These fairies could be evolved to aid the army of insects that Elegance produced.","Once the Execution Blade Insect, Vibrating Armor Ladybug, Flowing Plasma Electricity Insect, Electromagnetic Chrysalis, Lonely Night Hurricane Moth, Six Treasures Cloud Dragonfly, Curse Explosion Brain Insect, Fortress Floating Insect, Protein Millipede, and Revival Death Insect were turned into fairies, the 10 fairies would be able to individually increase their strength, thereby strengthening 10 of Elegance’s abilities.","Aside from increasing Elegance’s power, its fairy bloodline would also evolve at 10 times its current rate.","While Elegance was evolving its bloodline, it could re-absorb the fairy bloodline within these 10 genes that had transformed into fairies. This would strengthen its bloodline and enable its bloodline to break through.","When Elegance reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, its bloodline was only higher-eight-wings. Given the circumstances, it was almost impossible for its bloodline to evolve to 10 wings.","However, with Gene Transformation Fairy, Elegance now stood a chance of producing 10 wings.","Elegance Forceful Reincarnation could be seen as an extremely powerful life-preservation exclusive skill.","When Elegance was in a near-dead state, regardless of the issues its body had, it could forcefully inject its soul into the fetus it produced.","This not only gave Elegance the chance to flee and save its life but also allowed it to escape negative influences, such as curses, poison, and parasites.","Liu Jie only needed to supply sufficient energy to the fetus, and it would grow into a new body.","Elegance’s soul was no different from its original body.","“Big Brother Liu, I am so happy that you have found your own battle system and style. For now, use the Firefly Demon Fetuses to transform the insect-species carcinoma feys into fairies and increase their strength.","“Also, spend more time helping Sky City. I will also be increasing the white-clothed followers. You have always been the one managing the white-clothed followers. Once the white-clothed followers’ strength increases abruptly, it’s inevitable that their mindsets will change.","“You will need to contain such thoughts! You have to ensure that they don’t cause any trouble because of this change in mindset. If they cause trouble as a result of their power increase, you can eliminate them.","“Sky City is willing to waste resources, but we have to guarantee that every white-clothed follower has upstanding character and values!”","Lin Yuan spoke with utmost seriousness.","For a faction, the usual culprits that hindered their development were internal decay and tumors.","When the white-clothed followers’ strength increased this time, it would also be Lin Yuan’s way of testing them.","These white-clothed followers needed to overcome this test before Lin Yuan took them with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","With Liu Jie’s intelligence, he immediately understood Lin Yuan’s meaning.","Lin Yuan did not want him to focus on managing the white-clothed followers because Sky City absolutely needed him to perform this task. Rather, there were plenty of people who wanted to contribute to Sky City and demonstrate their capabilities to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan expressed this concern because he feared that Liu Jie’s decision to enter seclusion for the transformation of the insect-species carcinoma feys into fairies could potentially impact his authority and influence in Sky City.","If he could not manage and put a lid on the white-clothed followers’ attitudes before they ballooned beyond control due to their power increase, it was likely they would begin questioning his might once he came out of seclusion.","“Don’t worry, Lin Yuan. Under my management, the white-clothed followers won’t cause a single problem! If you want to nurture these white-clothed followers, I will instruct them accordingly so that they understand Sky City’s regulations before their strength increases.”","...","After Liu Jie left, Lin Yuan began increasing Zong Ze and Gu Lang’s strength.","Lin Yuan even took a trip to the Radiant Moon Palace to help the Moon Empress break through past pinnacle spirit fire. She was now a Divine Kingdom expert.","When the Moon Empress became a Divine Kingdom expert, she sensed a large amount of faith power gathering within her divine kingdom. The faith power nourished her newly formed divine kingdom.","...","The main world was currently developing rapidly.","Time flew by, and the main world’s development had exceeded the level of a Class 2 world.","Nonetheless, the main world was still a Class 2 world that had only recently been promoted.","Lin Yuan had no idea whether 10 or 20 years had passed since he began helping Zong Ze and Gu Lang to increase their strength.","In terms of human years, Lin Yuan was now more than 35 years old. However, given his lifespan, he had only just taken the first step of his life journey.","At first, Lin Yuan had also intended to form a contract with the Lifespan Mouse.","However, Lin Yuan had awakened his body composition in the Epoch God Palace’s Returning Saint Pool. There was no longer a need to use the Lifespan Mouse to increase his lifespan!","The Body of All Spirits allowed Lin Yuan to increase his lifespan each time he absorbed a new bloodline, enabling him to break through human limitations.","Despite a decade passing, Lin Yuan’s appearance had not changed in the slightest. Rather, his eyes had become even brighter and more charismatic.","Lin Yuan thought, ‘It won’t be long before Morbius wakes up.’","For the past decade, Lin Yuan could see Morbius daily but could not communicate with it.","Lin Yuan really missed this friend who had accompanied him from his lowest point and along his journey of achieving success.","Once Morbius woke up, Lin Yuan would lead his group in heading to Epoch God Palace. They would pass through the tunnel created by Epoch God Palace to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan had not rested even for a moment in the past 10 years.","Aside from helping people increase their strength, he also helped the main world bolster its foundation.","In the past 10 years of helping people to increase their strength, Lin Yuan’s own strength had increased from pinnacle birth horoscope to higher spirit fire.","When he reached the spirit-fire level, Lin Yuan truly managed to produce the spirit fire!","Given that he already had his divine kingdom and a holy spirit, lighting his spirit fire now seemed ludicrous. However, that was Lin Yuan’s current condition.","...","After the past decade of development, the main world had fully stabilized.","The dead spirits crisis had indeed pushed the main world from the fifth epoch to the sixth epoch. However, the trauma had not been overly impactful.","Nonetheless, it did leave a deep brand on the main world.","...","At that moment, someone knocked on Lin Yuan’s door.","A graceful woman with waist-length hair walked in. This was Wen Yu.","Wen Yu used to have short hair, but she had grown it out. With her long hair, she looked more capable than before.","Wen Yu had undeniable credit for the main world’s rapid development in the past 10 years.","Sky City had undergone its fastest phase of development during the past decade, and Wen Yu had fulfilled the role of Sky City’s manager. She was Lin Yuan’s unshakable second-in-command."]},{"number":2794,"title":"Chapter 2794 The Evolved Floating Island Whale!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2794 The Evolved Floating Island Whale!","The Moon Empress had joined Sky City ten years ago.","Most of Sky City’s members were natives of the Radiance Federation.","Twenty years ago, the Moon Empress was one of only three Class 5 Creation Masters in the Radiance Federation. She was also a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty.","She was like a goddess to the members of Sky City.","The Moon Empress was a figure that stood even above the summit, protecting the entire Radiance Federation.","More importantly, she was Lin Yuan’s Master. Even Lin Yuan, the City Lord of Sky City, was highly respectful toward her.","Wen Yu’s influence in Sky City could surpass that of the Moon Empress because she indeed possessed outstanding capabilities and kept Sky City in perfect order. Furthermore, the Moon Empress had intentionally lowered her position and allowed Wen Yu and Liu Jie to take center stage.","Wen Yu’s position in Sky City was always built on her abilities.","However, in terms of abilities, the Moon Empress were much stronger than those of Wen Yu.","The Moon Empress managed the Radiance Federation on behalf of the Spacetime Elder and had held up the Radiance Federation during its darkest hour.","In spite of the immense pressure, the Moon Empress managed the Radiance Federation perfectly.","Before the pressure was lifted, Lin Yuan entrusted the Moon Empress with the job of protecting the main world’s other federations.","Lin Yuan always liked to manage from the backseat. He would only step in to expend his effort to solve the real challenges.","However, Lin Yuan only managed the big picture and never focused on the trivial kinks.","The Moon Empress handled all the subsequent details in Lin Yuan’s stead.","If Wen Yu were in the Moon Empress’ position, she would not even have been able to shoulder the pressure of managing the Radiance Federation, much less the entire main world!","This was why Mystic Moon continued to teach Wen Yu various things even now.","After all, Wen Yu was still a young person who was around Lin Yuan’s age.","Unlike Lin Yuan, Wen Yu had not lived two lives.","But in terms of perspective, Wen Yu had grown just as much as Lin Yuan had.","Liu Jie had never been able to compete with Wen Yu when it came to maturity.","The Moon Empress handled the rear and helped Wen Yu to address the issues she did not have the energy to see to.","The addition of Moon Empress allowed Sky City’s speed of management to multiply.","Mystic Moon and Cold Moon were the Moon Empress’ two Moon Envoys.","The Moon Empress would be going with Lin Yuan to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, and it went without saying that Cold Moon and Mystic Moon would be going as well.","Liu Jie and Wen Yu had taken up the posts of one mainly handling the external while the other handled the internal.","Wen Yu was Sky City’s manager, while Liu Jie was akin to Sky City’s general.","In the Radiant Moon Palace, Cold Moon was the one who handled the external, and there were many things that she could teach Liu Jie.","Although Liu Jie was Night Leaning Moon’s disciple, she did not hold back anything from Liu Jie.","Night Leaning Moon had only been teaching Liu Jie how to increase his power. But once Liu Jie’s power reached the Divine Kingdom level, there was no longer much that Night Leaning Moon could teach him.","Night Leaning Moon was now fully focused on protecting the Radiance Federation.","The Spirit Guards had been expanded as Night Leaning Moon had recruited numerous members of the Radiance Hundred Sequence.","Night Leaning Moon had always seen the dimensional lifeforms as opportunities and disasters for humans. The two could coexist in the main world without any issues.","While the humans utilized the dimensional lifeforms, they also needed to stay on guard against the dimensional lifeforms to prevent them from causing damage to the main world.","Although the dead spirits crisis had passed, there were still numerous lifeforms in the main world that had mutated after being infected.","These feys that had been infected by death aura were extremely contagious, and the Spirit Guards needed to search for and eliminate all of them. Otherwise, they would attack the adventurers in the world. They might even infect other feys and cause them to go insane.","In the past few years, the outskirt towns of the Radiance Federation had suffered attacks from fey waves.","If Night Leaning Moon had not made advance preparations and stationed the Spirit Guards to guard the towns, these small towns would have been devoured soon after the dead spirits crisis ended.","Ever since the dead spirits crisis disappeared, Night Leaning Moon had not focused on Liu Jie.","All of the Radiance Federation’s royalty were aware of the Sky Beyond the Clouds’ existence.","Night Leaning Moon had felt extremely sorrowful when she learned that the Moon Empress was about to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Night Leaning Moon and the Moon Empress had grown up together. They became acquainted when they were young, accompanied each other, grew up together, and until now, walked down their paths together.","However, Night Leaning Moon did not choose to go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","The Moon Empress would head there to protect the Radiance Federation.","Night Leaning Moon was well aware of the strength of her abilities. She had never been able to measure up to the Moon Empress.","Even if the Moon Empress did not rely on her power in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, she would utilize her intelligence.","There was no reason for her to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and become a burden to juniors like Liu Jie, Lin Yuan, and Wen Yu.","Her abilities might not be sufficient for the Sky Beyond the Clouds, but she could play her role in the main world as a member of the Radiance Federation’s royalty. She could protect the Radiance Federation or even the entire main world!","...","Since Night Leaning Moon was not focused on Liu Jie, Cold Moon began telling Liu Jie about her experiences in the spare time she had when she was not teaching Chu Ci. She mainly concentrated on telling him how to command his subordinates and issue directives.","As a superior, issuing directives was an art. Once a superior made an error, there was a high chance they would immediately lose all their formidability.","Liu Jie had grown extremely quickly in the past ten years. Lin Yuan was very glad to watch Liu Jie grow.","...","In the past ten years, there was no doubt that the busiest member of Sky City was Hu Quan.","Hu Quan had been developing the Spirit Lock spatial zone and building Sky City on Sky Sea’s back.","Due to Morbius’ grade evolution, the Spirit Lock spatial zone had enlarged again.","In the past ten years, Hu Quan had finished constructing the space that used to be half the size of the Xia Region.","The frame of the structure on Sky Sea had been announced to be completed a year ago.","The majestic city on Sky Sea’s back would become the base camp that accompanied Lin Yuan in exploring the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","After spending the past few years in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Sky Sea had also evolved.","Lin Yuan had not intentionally helped Sky Sea to increase its power in the past ten years.","By just absorbing the spirit qi in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, Sky Sea had evolved from Suzerain/Myth to Suzerain/Pinnacle Creation.","For an enormous creature like Sky Sea, this rate of evolution was fast enough.","However, this was far from being enough to meet Lin Yuan’s needs.","Sky Sea had to reach World Emperor/Divine Kingdom before Lin Yuan went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan would need to use his resources to enable Sky Sea’s power to continue evolving there.","Otherwise, Sky Sea’s existence would become Sky City’s weakness. Not only would it be incapable of protecting Sky City, but it would become a weak point when enemies were attacking Sky City.","Lin Yuan entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone and immediately saw Sky Sea floating in the sky.","Sky Sea sensed Lin Yuan’s presence and quickly reached the sky above Lin Yuan with a flap of its enormous wing.","Lin Yuan looked up, and he had to admit that the sight of the majestic Sky Sea was breathtaking!","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Sky Sea.","[Fey Name]: Floating Island Whale","[Fey Species]: Large-winged-whale-species/","island-whale-species.","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Water/Wind","[Fey Quality]: Creation IX","Abilities:","[Whale Blood Screen]: Set fire to the essence blood inside its body and form a screen that can protect everything on its back.","[Water Vapor Whale Feelers]: Transform its feelers into water vapor and use them to gather nutrients from the environment to recover itself.","[Whale Spout Empowerment]: Through the blowhole in its head, it can shoot out energy from its energy and supply it to entities with compatible bodies to replenish their energy or fix them up in other ways.","[Lashing Spirit Tail Wings]: After being nourished by pure spirit qi, the wings and tail will be covered with a skin that can filter out spirit qi. With every movement of the wings and tail, the spirit qi can be directed to its back to increase the concentration of spirit qi on its back.","[Flesh Solidification]: An additional mouth that is connected to the additional stomach will grow below the blowhole. The metal and rocks that enter the additional stomach will strengthen the flesh during the contraction and expansion of the additional stomach. The solidified flesh will not affect the growth of the whale’s bones.","[Whale’s Breath]: Gather energy that is compatible with its body and shoot it out at a target. Before the target escapes the breath’s lock, the breath will lock and track the target.","[Floating Whale Sinks]: When the things and lifeforms on the whale’s back are dying, a mournful cry of grief will be released. The sky will be like the ocean, and its body and soul will be the price paid to protect all the beings on its back.","[Sinking Whale Becomes Life]: When Floating Whale Sinks is used, its bloodline will combine with the whale bones. While the whale bones are being upgraded, they will produce a fetus, and the fetus will take on its current bloodline.","Exclusive Skill:","[Floating Island Secret Realm]: By swallowing wind-elemental energy, a special space will be opened within the whale’s abdomen. The higher the purity of the wind-elemental energy, the larger the space will be. However, the space will not exceed twice the size of the body. By swallowing water-elemental energy, the flesh will gain powerful fusion abilities that will enable the fats to stick to any lifeform, dead or alive, and drain nutrients from them. The purer the water-elemental energy, the stronger the fusion ability will be.","[Knotted Life Cohabitation]: Pick a lifeform on its back to fuse and share its life with. Before its life comes to an end, the target will not die. Before the target dies, it will be able to continue living even if it sustains a serious injury.","[Accommodating Territory Transformative Environment]: A territory can be subsumed into its body, and the body will become a part of this territory. The entities on its body can also be placed anywhere on this territory. The root power of the surroundings can be used to nourish the body and allow the body to be acknowledged by the environment.","[Sea Sky Stance]: As the ruler of the sea and sky, it will be able to change the stance of the sky and sea. It will use the stance to defend against enemies. When energy is absorbed from the sky and sea, it will be able to continuously recover its injuries (Anything joined to it will also suffer the same damage).","After Sky Sea evolved, it obtained new abilities and exclusive skills.","Lin Yuan was very surprised by Sky Sea’s newest ability, Sinking Whale Becomes Life. It came from Floating Whale Sinks and was a self-preservation ability.","To Lin Yuan, Floating Whale Sinks was an ability he would not use unless he did not have any other choice.","Floating Whale Sinks involved Sky Sea singing a woeful song when the lifeforms and entities on its back died. It would view the sky as the deep sea and give up its life to revive the entities and lifeforms.","It was an ability akin to saving the world. One would revive one’s protected target regardless of the cost, even if it meant death.","But with Sinking Whale Becomes Life, playing the hero would not result in a tragic sacrifice. Instead, there was the chance to continue the legacy of one’s bloodline.","However, if Sky Sea used its soul as the price to sing its woeful song, the only result would be death, even if its bloodline was extended by Sinking Whale Becomes Life.","Furthermore, Sky Sea’s fetus that Lin Yuan nurtured would not be Sky Sea but a completely new Floating Island Whale!","Sky Sea’s ability caused Lin Yuan to recall what the Moon Empress had said.","When facing a powerful enemy, being a protector came with sacrifice.","There were countless unnamed heroes in the Radiance Federation’s history. The Moon Empress had told Lin Yuan this when the dead spirits crisis began.","The Moon Empress had mentioned that because she had been prepared to do the same.","Although Lin Yuan had not said this, he had silently made the same decision when he took on Tower Canon. He had been ready to shoulder all the risks of safeguarding the Radiance Federation’s peace.","Lin Yuan had started walking down the path that he used to admire others for doing.","The Island Whales’ abilities were largely linked to its wills. This was Sky Sea’s choice.","If there was really the need to use Floating Whale Sinks, Sky Sea would use the ability even if Lin Yuan tried to stop it.","Sky Sea also gained a new exclusive skill, Sea Sky Stance.","Sky Sea was the Heavenly Family Fey of the sky and sea and had the ability to control both of them.","The Heavenly Family Cottage had a ranking for the Heavenly Family Feys’ abilities.","Sky Sea and Gray were the most powerful feys in the entire Heavenly Family Cottage. One of them controlled weather phenomena, while the other controlled the sky and sea. They did not lose out to the Mother of Bloodbath, who controlled the sun, and Purple Love, who controlled the constellations.","Sea Sky Stance was proof of Sky Sea’s control over the sea and sky.","Normally, the sea and sky’s stances could speed up Sky Sea’s movements.","But when facing enemies, it would allow Sky Sea to protect its vicinity while restraining enemies. More importantly, Sea Sky Stance was also a strong endurance ability."]},{"number":2795,"title":"Chapter 2795 Foggy Weather and Weather Transformation Seal!","paragraphs":["Chapter 2795 Foggy Weather and Weather Transformation Seal!","Sea Sky Stance allowed Sky Sea to absorb energy from the sky and sea. This extraction of energy was continuous and sustained Sky Sea.","Even if Sky Sea did not consume food for energy, it would still be sustained for a very long time.","When the endurance effects of Sea Sky Stance were paired with Water Vapor Whale Feelers, Sky Sea could take in energy freely from the air.","If Sky Sea was in a battle, it was inevitable that the entities stuck to its body would be damaged.","Sea Sky Stance allowed Sky Sea to continuously provide energy to the entities and repair them.","Lin Yuan smiled and waved at Sky Sea.","Sky Sea responded by flapping its wings.","When Hu Quan saw Lin Yuan, he smiled and walked over to him before saying happily, “Young Master, a few years must have passed since you last entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone. Now that you’re here, what do you think of this paradise that I’ve built? Does it meet your expectations?”","Hu Quan had always called the Spirit Lock spatial zone a paradise.","Lin Yuan did not have to worry when it came to Hu Quan. For the past few years, he had been helping the Radiance Federation’s royalty and the white-clothed followers to increase their powers. Meanwhile, he allowed Hu Quan to oversee the Spirit Lock spatial zone fully.","Hu Quan had been working himself to the bone these past few years. He had wanted to give Lin Yuan a surprise the next time he entered the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Hu Quan asked himself if he had put his full effort into this celestial space and the building of Sky City on Sky Sea’s back. He was very happy with the fruits of his labor.","Not only had he poured effort into this endeavor, but almost all the spiritual ingredients he used were the rarest and most precious ones that he could imagine.","Lin Yuan did not respond to Hu Quan immediately.","Lin Yuan had only just arrived at the Spirit Lock spatial zone. If he answered Hu Quan without surveying the results of his efforts over the past few years, he would only be placating Hu Quan.","Lin Yuan looked through and around the area before smiling and giving Hu Quan a thumbs-up.","“Uncle Hu, you’ve done an even better job of building the Spirit Lock spatial zone than I expected!”","Lin Yuan first became acquainted with Hu Quan because he wanted to ask Hu Quan to build the sandalwood longevity fish tank.","Hu Quan was very skilled at building a singular item intricately. Despite the years that had passed and all of the growth that he had achieved, this remained his specialty.","However, he had also improved at coordinating complex pieces of scenery.","Every part of this space and scene was extremely intricate. Yet, they did not look messy when put together. Rather, they exuded a natural cohesiveness.","Hu Quan’s face lit up with elation when he heard Lin Yuan’s sincere praise.","Hu Quan had been working so hard at leading the team and building the Spirit Lock spatial zone and Sky City on Sky Sea solely so he could receive Lin Yuan’s affirmation.","At that moment, a crane cry rang out from the Spirit Lock spatial zone’s sky, and clouds gathered around Lin Yuan.","When Lin Yuan saw this, he knew that Gray had sensed his presence and was here to see him.","Hu Quan had always been astonished at how and where Lin Yuan managed to find these mystical feys.","Hu Quan was on good terms with Gray, and he often asked Gray for help to create certain weather. As thanks, he and the other Spirit Craftsmen would play with it.","“Young Master, I am done building Sky City on Sky Sea’s back. I have carefully carved all of the interior’s decorations. If you want to redo the interior environment, you can add some fortuitous ornaments. I haven’t planted the weather-producing plant-type feys that Gray absorbs on Sky Sea’s back. Gray can never sit still, and this paradise struggles to keep up with Gray’s energy levels.”","When Lin Yuan heard Hu Quan say this, he knew that Hu Quan and Gray got along extremely well.","In truth, Lin Yuan did not mistreat Gray.","Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter were sufficiently powerful to deal with the invaders.","With Fan Lou on guard in the Sky Beyond the Clouds, it was impossible that there would be other invaders.","Nonetheless, one could never be too careful.","Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter needed to watch over various areas of the main world and did not have time to play with Gray.","If the four of them did not keep an eye on Gray and the latter caught the eye of invaders or the main world, serious trouble would follow!","Gray’s Sovereign/Creation power was still a ways away from the top experts in the main world.","The top experts in the main world were unaware of the relationship between Lin Yuan and Gray.","The Heavenly Family Cottage had been formed and had managed to collect so many Heavenly Family Feys because young Heavenly Family Feys had to face far too many risks.","Before the Heavenly Family Cottage was established, many Heavenly Family Feys had lost their lives before reaching maturity.","Even after the Heavenly Family Cottage’s establishment, there were still Heavenly Family Feys that were killed before they reached maturity.","If Purple Love could not read the stars to help her uncover the culprits and subsequently enact furious revenge on them, the number of Heavenly Family Feys in the main world would have fallen to less than half of its original quantity.","“Uncle Hu, for now, focus on moving the weather-producing plant-type feys onto Universe’s back! Universe can use its ability to plant the weather-producing plant-type feys in its flesh as well as speed up their growth.”","While he spoke, Lin Yuan felt a weight land in his arms. He lifted his arms and hugged Gray tightly. In truth, Lin Yuan had not had such close contact with Gray in a few years.","The last time he paid attention to Gray, it had only just comprehended a Willpower Rune and evolved to Fantasy Breed. Now it had reached Sovereign/Creation IX.","If Gray was given another few years, it would be able to absorb sufficient weather to naturally reach Immortal.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Gray.","[Fey Name]: Sky Clouded Crane","[Fey Species]: Crane species/Red Crane species","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Natural","[Fey Quality]: Creation IX","Abilities:","[Cloudy Weather]: The body will present itself as a cloud and will be compatible with any weather. The body can absorb the weather. Once the weather is absorbed into the cloud, it will become a new ability. No new abilities will come from evolution.","[Radiance of a Clear Day]: In an area covered by clouds or after changing the weather to that of clear skies, all life forms in the area will be stamped with a clear weather imprint. Friendly life forms’ light-type abilities will generate more damage, while enemies will sustain sunstroke, burning, and other negative effects.","[Darkness of a Cloudy Day]: In an area covered by clouds or after changing the weather to that of a cloudy day, all life forms in the area will be stamped with a cloudy weather imprint. Friendly life forms’ dark-type abilities will generate more damage, while enemies will suffer confusion, fear, and other negative effects.","[Frozen Snowy Day]: In an area covered by clouds or after the weather has changed to become snowy, all life forms will be branded with the snowy weather imprint. Friendly life forms will produce more powerful ice-type attacks, and water-type abilities can also become ice-type. Enemies will be frozen and numbed and experience other negative effects. Fire-type effects will also become less effective.","[Roar of a Windy Day]: In an area covered by clouds or after changing the weather to windy weather, all life forms in the area will be stamped with a windy weather imprint. Friendly life forms’ wind-type abilities will generate more damage, while enemies will experience reverse currents, wind pressure, and other negative effects.","[Judgment of Thunder Weather]: An area covered by clouds or transformed into cloudy weather will be branded with a thunder weather imprint. When thunder hits friendly life forms, their ability to cause damage will increase. When thunder hits enemies, they will feel numbness and other related negative effects.","[Fusion of Rainbow Weather]: Cloudy weather will turn into rainbow weather. The rainbow weather can promote the fusion of other weather and allow them to coexist.","[Foggy Day’s Coverage]: Cloudy weather will change into foggy weather. Simultaneously, a cloudy weather imprint will be placed on life forms in the area. Friendly targets will effectively hide their presence in the fog, while enemies will be hit with a series of negative effects, such as blindness and dizziness.","Exclusive Skill:","[Jade Contract]: Condense every type of weather absorbed into jade. The jade will adorn the feathers. Once the weather turns into a jade decoration, the cloud will no longer carry the aura of that weather. However, when the jade decoration is activated, every type of weather will turn into a jade beast.","[Body of Weather]: The body will comprehend the construction of natural phenomena it controls and produce them accordingly. These natural phenomena can aid other targets, so they will receive double empowerment regardless of the weather they are experiencing.","[Abandon Weather Reincarnation]: When severely injured or in a near-dead state, it will immediately give up one of the weather it controls and instantly return to full health (after the ability is used, the weather can be taken control of again. However, regaining the abandoned weather will require accumulation and will not change the respective ability).","[Weather Transformation Seal]: Gather all the weather it has under its control and create a seal full of weather power. It will be used to suppress a target. Under the weather seal, friendly targets will receive comprehensive boosting from weather-related elemental power.","Gray now had a new ability, Foggy Day’s Coverage.","After the dead spirits crisis ended, the main world was shrouded in fog for some time due to the presence of death aura. It was during this time that Gray absorbed weather from the outside world and attained this ability.","The territory formed by this ability would allow friendly targets to hide within the fog while enemies would suffer negative effects such as blindness and dizziness.","It could be said that Foggy Day’s Coverage was more useful to Sky Sea than the other weather phenomena.","It allowed Gray to cover Sky Sea’s body better as well as everything that was on it.","Although the blindness and dizziness effects were not strong, they could still affect enemies to a certain extent. As such, it was considered a dynamic controlling ability.","Due to Cloudy Weather, Gray could not gain a new ability each time it evolved like other feys could.","Gray’s abilities were related to the weather phenomena it absorbed.","When Gray absorbed another weather phenomenon and obtained another ability, it would not only improve Jade Contract’s combat power and the support effects of Body of Weather but would also be extremely useful for the two new exclusive skills, Abandon Weather Reincarnation and Weather Transformation Seal.","Abandon Weather Reincarnation would allow Gray to recover from injuries and return to full health by sacrificing one of its weather phenomena when facing a powerful enemy and in a near-dead state.","It was said that cats had nine lives.","Gray currently controlled seven types of weather phenomena. With Abandon Weather Reincarnation, Gray essentially had seven lives.","It was a powerful life-preservation ability.","The key point was that after a weather phenomenon was sacrificed to Abandon Weather Reincarnation, the weather phenomenon could be accumulated again without affecting Gray’s potential.","Gray’s attacking power mostly came from Jade Contract. Hence, Gray’s combat power was somewhat lacking.","However, Weather Transformation Seal’s appearance allowed Gray to gain a powerful combat technique to use against enemies.","By gathering all the energy from the weather together, Gray had essentially gained the ability to trigger its maximum power.","By combining all the weather phenomena into a weather seal, targets could be suppressed, while its own side would be comprehensively boosted by all the elemental power related to weather.","There was no question that this boost would be gargantuan.","Gray’s abilities encompassed elemental energy related to light, darkness, ice, wind, and thunder.","There were very few Heavenly Family Feys that could be simultaneously boosted by five types of elemental power.","Lin Yuan thought, Why don’t I evolve Sky Sea and Gray to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom simultaneously?","Aside from these two, Dark Blue’s power could also be increased.","Dark Blue, Sky Sea, and Gray formed a system.","Now that Lin Yuan had awakened the Body of All Spirits, the value of Dark Blue’s mermaid bloodline was no longer as significant to him.","Frankly, the bloodlines Lin Yuan controlled were just as powerful as the mermaid bloodline. Some were at an even higher level!","Although Dark Blue’s bloodline boost was no longer effective for Lin Yuan, it could not be denied that Dark Blue was one of Lin Yuan’s strongest feys. After all, Dark Blue was the only one of Lin Yuan’s feys that needed to absorb 12 Willpower Runes to evolve to Fantasy Breed!"]},{"number":2796,"title":"Chapter 2796 Whale World Piety!","paragraphs":["2796 Whale World Piety!","Dark Blue could not evolve quickly because it needed to comprehend Willpower Runes from top-grade strange water.","For the past decade, Dark Blue had absorbed countless types of strange water. Yet, it only just managed to comprehend 12 Willpower Runes.","Every pillar of water that made up Dark Blue’s body contained its own will and could be regarded as an individual entity. There was no difference between contracting Dark Blue and contracting 12 water-elemental feys.","Every will that Dark Blue controlled had been carefully selected. It could be said that Dark Blue’s 12 wills were perfectly complementary.","Dark Blue’s growth potential was extremely large. Aside from every pillar of water controlling its own top-grade strange water characteristic, they also possessed individual mermaid bloodlines.","The mermaid bloodlines in the pillars of water could be continuously evolved.","If Lin Yuan was willing to help Dark Blue evolve every pillar of water’s mermaid bloodline, they would eventually transform into elemental mermaids. When Lin Yuan controlled Dark Blue, the 12 pillars of water would transform into 12 mermaid thearchs who would guard Sky Sea.","In order to perfect Sky Sea’s system, the priority would be to increase Sky Sea, Gray, and Dark Blue’s strength.","However, it was not as simple to increase their strength as it was to increase the strength of Lin Yuan’s other feys.","Dark Blue needed to absorb not only pure spirit qi but also a large amount of pure water-elemental energy to evolve. Sky Sea needed to absorb both water- and wind-elemental energy. Gray needed to absorb weather phenomena.","Lin Yuan would need a year or two to perfect Sky Sea’s system.","There was no way he could spend a year or two in the Spirit Lock spatial zone.","Moreover, remaining in the Spirit Lock spatial zone would not benefit Sky Sea, Gray, and Dark Blue’s evolutions.","They had been cooped up in the Spirit Lock spatial zone, and it was time for them to go out to breathe fresh air!","To the north of the Radiance Federation was their border with the Barren Sea. There were many islands scattered around the area. These islands were impoverished and were not only uninhabited by humans but also had very few feys living there.","Lin Yuan did not want to allow Sky Sea to be exposed to the main world’s lifeforms.","Despite Lin Yuan being so powerful now that he had even saved the main world numerous times, he would never expose Sky City’s lair, which was also about to be used as his vehicle in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","If Sky Sea was seen swimming around in the sky, it would cause terror and hysteria among the main world’s lifeforms. Furthermore, Lin Yuan did not want this information to be leaked.","If Sky Sea was anchored on an uninhabited island and was hidden by Gray, it would be unlikely for anyone to discover its existence unless experts specifically tried looking for it.","There were many things that Lin Yuan was keeping under wraps, not just for his own protection but also for the safety of the main world.","An interrogator did not need to utter a single word to their target to find out the truth!","Before Morbius woke up, Lin Yuan would enter a period of seclusion.","Genius and Chimey were the first feys Lin Yuan acquired.","The two of them started from the plainest conditions and had now opened paths that had never existed in history.","Chimey needed to absorb the energy from the strange flames in the Phoenix Perching Chinese Parasol Tree to increase its power.","In order for Genius to evolve, it needed to accumulate sufficient spiritual energy and produce enough life-preserving tails before pleading with the heavens and the earth for wills.","Top-grade strange flames were the peak in the main world.","However, according to Kong Huan and Fan Lou, there were higher-level flames in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","It was clear that the Sky Beyond the Clouds was more suitable for Genius and Chimey’s future evolutions.","The wills in the Sky Beyond the Clouds were much stronger than the wills in the main world, a mere Class 2 world.","When Genius went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, it would undoubtedly be able to obtain more mystical wills from the heavens and the earth.","Once he became certain of this, Lin Yuan was in no rush to increase Chimey and Genius’ powers. He even intentionally restrained their evolutions.","...","When Lin Yuan arrived at a deserted island near the Barren Sea, he released Sky Sea and Gray.","The two Heavenly Family Feys really liked to explore and experience nature.","Once the two of them were released, they exploded with happiness.","Sky Sea did somersaults in the sky and occasionally dove into the sea, causing the surface of the sea to be tumultuously disturbed continuously.","When Lin Yuan saw this, he felt guilty and sad.","When they went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would no longer restrain Gray and Sky Sea’s living space.","Lin Yuan allowed the two of them to play for a few days. He would release Dark Blue once the two of them had their fill of fun.","Lin Yuan waved at the two of them and took out chests filled with water- and wind-type heavenly-maiden-grade elemental pearls.","Each of these jade-textured Phoebe Zhennan boxes could fit exactly 10,000 elemental pearls.","The Wind Speed Rapid Antelope had already carefully separated elemental pearls in the chests based on their purity.","Lin Yuan opened the wings made by the Source Sand and flew onto Sky Sea’s back.","Next, he placed his hand on Sky Sea’s back and concentrated on circulating his energy to inject pure spirit qi into its body.","Unexpectedly, Lin Yuan’s expression soon changed slightly.","This change occurred because he discovered it was more difficult to evolve Sky Sea’s grade and quality than he had anticipated.","This difficulty was likely related to Sky Sea’s bloodline.","Sky Sea needed tens or even hundreds of times the energy that other feys required to evolve.","Lin Yuan always felt that he had stocked up on a substantial amount of elemental pearls.","However, now that Lin Yuan was evolving Sky Sea and Dark Blue simultaneously, he suddenly realized there could never be enough of something like elemental pearls. Regardless of how many there were, they could be used up swiftly!","...","Lin Yuan made several trips to the Startling Lines Continent to collect spirit qi crystals.","The investments he made in the main world provided him with even greater returns, and he could collect a harvest periodically.","However, no one could replace Lin Yuan in helping the spirit qi professionals increase their strength and collect their World Grace to turn them into spirit qi crystals. Lin Yuan had to do it on his own.","Morbius’ Pure Land of Bliss was required to turn the absorbed World Grace into spirit qi crystals.","Lin Yuan could never hand Morbius over to someone else, even if they were Wen Yu or Liu Jie!","Luckily, Lin Yuan could travel to and return from the Startling Lines Continent very quickly with the Ethereal Jellyfish’s Node Transportation.","When Lin Yuan was at the pinnacle birth horoscope, it only took him around a month to evolve feys from Sovereign/Creation to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","But now, he had reached the pinnacle spirit fire.","With the increase in his power, his Body of All Spirits was also strengthened.","Now, he only needed a little over ten days to evolve a Sovereign/Creation fey to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","...","Surprisingly, Lin Yuan spent more than a year on the remote island evolving Sky Sea.","He once again felt the same feeling of pushing himself to his limits that he felt when Sky City was first established.","He did not waste the year and a half!","Sky Sea had finally reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom!","Sky Sea was already an enormous creature. But after its grade and quality continuously increased, its size had also multiplied by several times.","The old Sky Sea was only around the size of the wing of the current Sky Sea.","The Sky City that Hu Quan had built on Sky Sea also seemed smaller.","Luckily, Sky Sea had Floating Island Secret Realm, allowing it to protect Sky City. Otherwise, Sky City would probably have been torn apart when Sky Sea grew larger.","When the energy fluctuations that represented faith energy appeared, Lin Yuan knew that Sky Sea had successfully evolved.","Lin Yuan was very curious about the exclusive skills and divine kingdom ability that the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom Sky Sea had obtained.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Sky Sea.","[Fey Name]: Floating Island Whale","[Fey Species]: Large-winged-whale-species/island-whale-species.","[Fey Grade]: World Emperor (1/10)","[Fey Type]: Water/Wind","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","[Whale Blood Screen]: Set fire to the essence blood inside its body and form a screen that can protect everything on its back.","[Water Vapor Whale Feelers]: Transform its feelers into water vapor and use them to gather nutrients from the environment to recover itself.","[Whale Spout Empowerment]: Through the blowhole in its head, it can shoot out energy from its energy and supply it to entities with compatible bodies to replenish their energy or fix them up in other ways.","[Lashing Spirit Tail Wings]: After being nourished by pure spirit qi, the wings and tail will be covered with skin that can filter out spirit qi. With every movement of the wings and tail, the spirit qi can be directed to its back to increase the concentration of spirit qi on its back.","[Flesh Solidification]: An additional mouth that is connected to the additional stomach will grow below the blowhole. The metal and rocks that enter the additional stomach will strengthen the flesh during the contraction and expansion of the additional stomach. The solidified flesh will not affect the growth of the whale’s bones.","[Whale’s Breath]: Gather energy that is compatible with its body and shoot it out at a target. Before the target escapes the breath’s lock, the breath will lock and track the target.","[Floating Whale Sinks]: When the things and life forms on the whale’s back are dying, a mournful cry of grief will be released. The sky will be like the ocean, and its body and soul will be the price paid to protect all the beings on its back.","[Sinking Whale Becomes Life]: When Floating Whale Sinks is used, its bloodline will combine with the whale bones. While the whale bones are being upgraded, they will produce a fetus, and the fetus will take on its current bloodline.","[Sea Sky Exchange]: Exchange the sea or sky of the current environment to either turn the sky into the sea or the sea into the sky. (The change in the environment is foundationally related to the strength of the world wills’ acknowledgment)","[World Roots Consume]: Consume and digest the world’s root power. The world’s root power will be used to strengthen itself and enable the whale’s back and abdomen’s secret realm to gain the same grade of conception power as that of the world’s roots.","Exclusive Skills:","[Floating Island Secret Realm]: By swallowing wind-elemental energy, a special space will be opened within the whale’s abdomen. The higher the purity of the wind-elemental energy, the larger the space will be. But the space will not exceed twice the size of the body. By swallowing water-elemental energy, the flesh will gain powerful fusion abilities that will enable the fats to stick to any lifeform, dead or alive, and drain nutrients from them. The purer the water-elemental energy, the stronger the fusion ability will be.","[Knotted Life Cohabitation]: Pick a lifeform on its back to fuse and share its life with. Before its life comes to an end, the target will not die. Before the target dies, it will be able to continue living even if it sustains a serious injury.","[Accommodating Territory Transformative Environment]: A territory can be subsumed into its body, and the body will become a part of this territory. The entities on its body can also be placed anywhere on this territory. The root power of the surroundings can be used to nourish the body and allow the body to be acknowledged by the environment.","[Sea Sky Stance]: As the ruler of the sea and sky, it will be able to change the stance of the sky and sea. It will use the stance to defend against enemies. When energy is absorbed from the sky and sea, it will be able to continuously recover its injuries (Anything joined to it will also suffer the same damage).","[Whale’s Extension]: When energy is at its maximum, some of the bloodline can be sacrificed to produce a fetus with the same bloodline. (The fetus will take on the same characteristics but will not have the same abilities and exclusive skills)","[Faith Gift]: Give some of the accumulated faith power to other lifeforms. If given to whales that it produced on its own, the faith power will not be depleted. If given to targets with unrelated bloodlines, the faith power will be used up at differing degrees.","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Whale World Nurturing]: All the faith power gained by the lifeforms in the space on its back and abdomen will be used to nurture it based on different proportions. The faith power will then either be turned into its own faith power or given to other targets to be absorbed.","When Lin Yuan saw Sky Sea’s new abilities and exclusive skills, he was shocked by them. But once he saw its divine kingdom ability, true astonishment bloomed on his face.","A question appeared in his mind. Are all World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys this powerful?!"]},{"number":2797,"title":"Chapter 2797 All Water Surging Tides!","paragraphs":["2797 All Water Surging Tides!","Lin Yuan felt that every one of his World Emperor/Divine Kingdom feys attained unique abilities, all extremely effective in their respective areas.","The rate of absorption of faith power was related to the World Emperor/Divine Kingdom lifeform’s subsequent evolution in grade and quality.","If every World Emperor/Divine Kingdom fey was this powerful, Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter might not be able to shield him from all storms in the Sky Beyond the Clouds!","Spring was currently standing in midair and helping Sky Sea to defend against the world wills.","When she saw Lin Yuan’s expression, Spring hurriedly bowed to him and said, “Lord Saint, I am willing to dispel your concerns and solve your troubles! If there is anything that’s bothering you, please do tell me about them!”","Lin Yuan told Spring about his thoughts.","Lin Yuan would never share these concerns with Spring if he had only just become acquainted with her.","But now, they had known each other for decades, and Lin Yuan was very familiar with her.","He had noticed that Spring was helping him with almost every task.","With Spring, Summer, Autumn, and Winter by his side, Lin Yuan was afforded a lot of convenience. It also allowed Lin Yuan to do many things in the past ten years that he would not have been able to accomplish on his own.","When Spring heard Lin Yuan’s concerns, she blinked a few times. She was momentarily at a loss about what to say.","In spite of her immense respect for Lin Yuan, she could not help but think, Lord Saint, you are really underestimating your resources and body composition!","Every spirit qi crystal that Lin Yuan used the Totem God to produce could lead to the start of a war in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","It was true that Spring would normally try to flatter Lin Yuan. But when she complained about him to herself, she did not try to flatter him at all.","None of the direct descendants of the top 100 species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds were capable of possessing and using such an abundance of resources to increase their power.","Moreover, all of Lin Yuan’s feys received his resources when they were at their weakest. By laying down such solid foundations, they steadily and reliably grew into eventual powerhouses.","Aside from the provision of resources, Lin Yuan also used his Body of All Spirits to evolve his feys.","The resources that feys used to increase their strength would directly affect the abilities, exclusive skills, and divine kingdom abilities they gained.","Hence, it would only be strange if Lin Yuan’s feys did not gain powerful abilities, exclusive skills, and divine kingdom abilities.","Once Spring explained all this to Lin Yuan, he nodded in understanding.","The white-clothed followers were the best example of this.","But when the Bronze/Legend feys Lin Yuan gave them were nurtured, they gained abilities once they reached Gold grade.","It turned out that this gap became even more obvious once feys reached the Divine Kingdom level.","This realization strengthened Lin Yuan’s resolution to provide his new feys with only the best foundations.","Among all of his feys, Lin Yuan had injected the most resources into Sky Sea. This was true from the time he contracted it.","Sky Sea’s abilities, exclusive skills, and divine kingdom abilities lived up to the resources that Lin Yuan had invested.","In the past year, Sky Sea had gained two new abilities. One was Sea Sky Exchange, and the other was World Roots Consume.","Sea Sky Exchange was another manifestation of its Heavenly Family Fey power.","Sky Sea could use its Heavenly Family Fey abilities to control the surrounding environment. The control it exerted was related to the strength and acknowledgment of the world wills.","Lin Yuan did not know how strong Sky Sea’s control would be in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","But in the main world, its control extended to the Barren Sea and the sky above it.","If Sky Sea wanted to, it could exchange the sea’s environment and turn it into the sky, or vice versa.","Normally, feys had environments that did not suit their combat styles or were unable to take shelter in.","When feys that flew in the sky landed in the sea, they did not have to attack each other as all parties would be seriously affected.","The same went for feys that lived in the sea when they arrived in an aerial environment. If feys that lived in the deep sea were brought to an aerial environment, the pressure would cause their bodies to bloat and eventually lead to death.","Sea Sky Exchange was an ability that was suitable for combat and not only had support but also powerful combat functions.","An ability like this was very suitable for Sky Sea, the Heavenly Family Fey controlling the sky and sea.","World Roots Consume gave Sky Sea the ability to consume and digest the root power of a world.","When Lin Yuan conquered Tower Canon, Spring had helped him to obtain the root power of the dead world.","Special techniques could be used to extract world power.","Sky Sea could use root power to strengthen itself!","It was clear just how formidable Sky Sea’s body was.","Sky Sea could not only use the root power to strengthen itself but could also enable the secret realm on its back and in its abdomen to have the same level of conception as the root power. This conception ability allowed it to create a world of its own.","With the root power, the lifeforms on its back and in its abdomen could reproduce.","In the future, the feys that Lin Yuan planted on Sky Sea’s back and in its abdomen would not only grow by absorbing the energy supplied by Sky Sea but could also evolve naturally after being nurtured by the root power of a world.","World Roots Consume could be perfectly paired with Whale World Piety!","Once the lifeforms on Sky Sea’s back and abdomen reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom, they would be able to collect faith power.","A certain fraction of the faith power they gained would be supplied to Sky Sea.","Although the total volume of faith power would not change as Sky Sea would only be gaining the faith power attained by other lifeforms, there would be differences in quality.","This was just like how one bomb would only be able to blow up one mound of dirt. But hundreds or thousands of bombs would together be able to level a mountain.","Whale World Piety had the ability to gather faith power.","Sky Sea could choose to absorb this faith power. But before it did so, it would need to sacrifice the faith power that had been supplied to it.","The sacrifice would entail the depletion of a proportion of its faith power.","Although this would cause the overall quantity of faith power to fall, it would use the limited amount of faith power to nurture a powerful entity.","Moreover, Sky Sea could not only absorb the faith power that was supplied to it but could also inject it into other lifeforms instead to strengthen them.","This was very similar to its exclusive skill, Faith Gift!","When Sky Sea injected faith power into targets with unrelated bloodlines, the faith power would be depleted. However, if injected into the whales that it produced, the faith power would not be depleted.","Hence, it was clear that using the gathered faith power to nurture whales it produced on its own would be the best option!","This could be perfectly paired with Sky Sea’s new exclusive skill, Whale’s Extension.","When Sky Sea had sufficient energy in its body, it could use up a portion of its bloodline to create fetuses that shared its bloodline. It was guaranteed that the fetuses would also be Floating Island Whales and not Island Whales.","It was difficult for any fey to recover their bloodline.","However, Lin Yuan possessed precious resources and the Body of All Spirits that could replenish Sky Sea’s bloodline.","Thus, Sky Sea could produce whales without suffering any consequences and subsequently evolve their strength through Faith Gift.","It went without saying that Faith Gift also had its limitations.","Once the fetuses produced by Sky Sea hatched, they would take on its characteristics but not its abilities and exclusive skills.","Nonetheless, the whales produced by Sky Sea would still be able to carry out their duties with regard to Sky City.","In the year that Lin Yuan had spent nurturing Sky Sea, Dark Blue had also improved substantially.","With Lin Yuan’s provision of water-elemental energy, Dark Blue had evolved from Fantasy Breed to Creation Breed. However, its grade had yet to reach Sovereign.","If a comparison was made, Dark Blue’s grade evolved faster than that of Gray!","The 12 pillars of water around Dark Blue that were formed by law power had transformed into miniature mermaids, circling Dark Blue’s main body. Although the bloodline power in Dark Blue’s main body had yet to reach king-class, it was not far off.","The mermaids around it all had intermediate mermaid bloodlines.","Dark Blue’s mermaid bloodline was faint, but Lin Yuan could inject mermaid bloodline energy into it to enable it to evolve.","It could be said that when it came to bloodline, Dark Blue’s future was limitless!","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Dark Blue.","[Fey Name]: Moving Source Water (Mermaid Disorientation)","[Fey Species]: Source genus/Sacred Source Species","[Fey Grade]: Suzerain (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Water","[Fey Quality]: Creation IV","Abilities:","[Flowing]: The water will rush rapidly, and the energy from the water can allow it to flow in any location.","[Halted Flow]: Separating from the main body and turning all the water-element energy in the body into raging energy that shoots towards the target.","[Faith Water]: Change faith power into a warm stream of water that can nurture other lifeforms using faith power. Faith Water can increase the rate at which faith power heals and replenishes the lifeform and slow down the faith power in larger bodies. Faith Water can also be used to draw back faith power that was given out, along with any additional faith power gained by the target.","[Faith Application]: The owner can be combined with the Moving Source Water and use all the power in the Moving Source Water. The owner can also inject faith power into the Moving Source Water to increase the strength of the Moving Source Water’s abilities.","[Faith Gift or Robbery]: The Moving Source Water can inject the faith power in its body into targets that can possess faith power to bolster them. It can also steal the right to control faith power from the bodies of targets with weaker faith power.","[Water Vein Block]: Use its bloodline energy to trigger its water-elemental energy that is not in its vicinity. The water-elemental energy will take on the water characteristics under its control and gather them closely together to form a block.","[Faith Shackle]: Link its bloodline power to a target with a similar bloodline. The target’s bloodline will be sealed away. If, together, they have greater bloodline power than that of the target, the target will lose the ability to accept and manipulate the faith power in its body.","Exclusive Skills:","[Power Water Soul]: Choose a power and condense it into the soul of the Moving Source Water. Any power can be chosen, but the choice cannot be undone. The power will affect the Moving Source Water’s future abilities and exclusive skills. When the Moving Source Water receives a certain level of feedback from the power, the Moving Source Water can comprehend any Willpower Rune according to the water-elemental characteristics in its body.","[Undepleted Clean Water]: The water-elemental energy it controls will have powerful resistance to other elements and will not be depleted. In a contaminated environment or when facing an ability with contamination effects, it can ensure the purity of the water-elemental energy under its control.","[Disorientation Water Territory]: Its water-elemental energy and bloodline power will fill up an environment and enable the water-elemental energy in the environment to have the ability to block auras and energy fluctuations, thereby disorienting enemy targets in the area.","[All Water Surging Tides]: The water-elemental energy in its body will be compared to the water-elemental energy in the surrounding environment. If the purity of its water-elemental energy is higher than that of the environment, it can extract the water-elemental energy of the environment to heal its wounds and replenish its depleted energy."]},{"number":2798,"title":"Chapter 2798 Morbius Awakens!","paragraphs":["2798 Morbius Awakens!","Dark Blue had gained two new abilities: Water Vein Block and Faith Shackle.","Water Vein Block activated Dark Blue’s bloodline energy. The stronger Dark Blue’s bloodline was, the more potent this ability’s effects would be.","Dark Blue used its bloodline power to trigger water-elemental energy and combined it with the water attributes under its control.","The block around Sky Sea not only provided Sky Sea with mobility through the water attributes, but it could also defend Sky Sea.","Dark Blue, Sky Sea, and Gray protected the main institute of Sky City together. Sky Sea was the vessel, Gray provided concealment, and Dark Blue covered defense.","Water Vein Block improved Dark Blue’s ability to carry out its defense duty.","As for Faith Shackle, Faith Application, and Faith Gift or Robbery, they were all the same type of abilities.","Dark Blue had gained the ability to control faith power when it reached Gold grade. As its grade continued to evolve, its ability to control faith power also grew stronger.","Both Faith Application and Faith Gift or Robbery tapped into Dark Blue’s utilization of its faith power.","Faith Shackle allowed Dark Blue to be linked to a target with the same bloodline power. The two parties’ faith power would be added together before being compared to another target. If the combined faith power was greater than that of the target, the target would lose the ability to receive and manipulate the faith power in its body.","At the Divine Kingdom level, the feys’ abilities were linked to their manipulation of faith power. Additionally, many of their abilities and exclusive skills relied on faith power as well.","If Faith Shackle only linked Dark Blue to another mermaid, the ability’s value would be greatly discounted because the strongest mermaid in Lin Yuan’s camp was Dazzling Silver.","Lin Yuan did not intend to take Samsara Realm mermaids like Dazzling Silver, Blue Umber, Light Green Umber, and Red Beauty to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","After the main world was linked to the dimensional worlds, the mermaids became another one of the main world’s species, and emperor-class mermaids like Dazzling Silver, Light Green Umber, Blue Umber, and Red Beauty needed to protect their species.","If Lin Yuan took the water world’s mermaids’ strongest pillars of strength with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, the mermaids might be able to continue living peacefully in the main world at first. But as time continued to pass, they would eventually go extinct.","Lin Yuan had the mermaid bloodline in his body and was a mermaid thearch who had received the worship of the mermaids. He did not want to see such a thing happen.","Lin Yuan’s mermaid bloodline came from Dark Blue. It could use Faith Shackle to link its faith power to that of Lin Yuan and use his faith power to seal the target’s faith power.","Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom was very different from the divine kingdoms of other experts.","Lin Yuan’s divine kingdom contained an enormous amount of faith power. If it was used to seal targets, even pinnacle Divine Kingdom lifeforms would be no match for him.","This was a very powerful technique for restraining enemies.","Dark Blue’s exclusive skill, Power Water Soul, enabled Dark Blue to absorb 12 types of Willpower Runes. It could be said that Power Water Soul gave Dark Blue endless potential.","Dark Blue’s other three exclusive skills were just as impressive as Power Water Soul.","Undepleted Clean Water allowed Dark Blue to use its water-elemental energy to become extremely resistant to other water-elemental energy. It would no longer be affected by other elements in special environments. Additionally, its water-elemental energy would no longer be used up unnecessarily.","Dark Blue would no longer be affected by other elemental abilities. However, it would be able to restrain the other elements that used to affect it.","In an environment with curses, poison, or contamination, Dark Blue would be immune to such defilement.","An elemental-type fey was the most afraid of its body becoming tainted.","This self-cleansing ability was a self-preservation ability for Dark Blue.","Disorientation Water Territory also involved Dark Blue using its elemental power. It would use its water-elemental energy to block the aura within the territory. It could also cover the internal energy fluctuations.","When enemies entered this area, they would become disoriented. In its disoriented state, the target would lose the ability to move. This would make it easier for Sky Sea to use the abilities on its back to eliminate the target.","This ability would not be very useful against stronger experts than Dark Blue. However, it would be very effective against groups.","As opposed to Undepleted Clean Water and Water Disorientation Territory, Lin Yuan was more interested in All Water Surging Tides, which could be seen as Dark Blue’s endurance ability. However, it was far from being as simple as an endurance ability.","This exclusive skill required Dark Blue to compare its body’s water-elemental energy with its environment.","It would only be able to absorb the water-elemental energy in the environment if its water-elemental energy was purer than that of the environment.","It could use the water-elemental energy in the surroundings to heal its injuries and replenish its depleted energy.","If this exclusive skill appeared for other feys, it would be virtually useless because there were very few other feys that could be confident that their water-elemental energy would be purer than that of the environment.","Elemental energy only took up a small proportion in the bodies of flesh feys. Comparing the elemental energy in their body to that of the environment would cause them to come up against many obstacles. It would be very easy for them to be interrupted by other feys’ abilities.","The water-elemental energy in Dark Blue’s body was close to 100% purity. Even if it was affected by other powerful water-type feys, the water-elemental energy in its body would still be stronger than the environment’s.","Gray’s rainy day weather and the water elemental aura spewed from Sky Sea’s body nourished Dark Blue daily. As a result, Dark Blue was almost never in an uncomfortable environment.","Dark Blue’s main duty was to defend Sky Sea.","When the outside world attacked Dark Blue, it could use All Water Surging Tides to heal its injuries effectively.","Lin Yuan once again took out numerous resources and gave them to Dark Blue and Gray.","He then left Spring behind to watch Dark Blue, Gray, and Sky Sea while he returned to the Radiance Federation.","This was because, once Lin Yuan was done nurturing Sky Sea, Morbius woke up.","Since Lin Yuan did not ask Morbius to spirit-lock new feys, its grade had not changed.","However, its appearance had changed drastically.","Morbius on Lin Yuan’s wrist had been completely redesigned.","The indentations meant to be filled with the Endless Gems had disappeared. In their place were simple totems and designs that changed constantly. If the totem patterns were closely examined, one would see that they were forming shapes of many of the world’s entities.","There were six new indentations below the bracelet. They were empty, just like when Lin Yuan had just contracted Morbius.","Morbius’ voice echoed in Lin Yuan’s ear.","The way Morbius’ voice was transmitted to him took Lin Yuan by surprise.","Normally, Morbius communicated with him through his soul. This was the first time that Morbius was communicating with him in real life.","Lin Yuan looked up and saw a young man with the same features as his own, wearing a rust-colored half-armor, standing in front of him.","At that moment, Lin Yuan suddenly felt as though he was looking into a mirror.","However, upon closer look, it could be seen that this young man, who greatly resembled him, had cold and sharp eyes. These were very different from Lin Yuan’s own eyes.","When Morbius saw Lin Yuan looking at it, it walked forward and hugged him before saying gently yet coldly, “Partner, after all these years apart, I am finally awake!”","Lin Yuan’s tone was one of delight as he said, “Morbius, you were completely silent. I thought you were going to sleep for even longer! After waking up this time, you can finally change into human form!”","Morbius could sense the joy in Lin Yuan’s voice and smiled.","“Partner, you have been collecting spirit qi crystals from the main world and working so hard on your own. Now, you don’t need to work so hard alone. I can go to help you! I can finally change into human form and no longer need to appear as a soul. I can now carry out tasks in your stead! You can divert your effort and energy into more important things.”","Lin Yuan could be concerned about anyone, but he would never be concerned about Morbius. To him, Morbius was as good as a clone.","If Morbius represented him to head to the Startling Lines Continent to help the lifeforms evolve and harvest spirit qi crystals, it would be extremely good news for Lin Yuan!","However, regardless of whether Morbius was able to help him harvest spirit qi crystals, Lin Yuan would have to go to the Radiance Federation in person.","Now that Morbius was awake, Lin Yuan was prepared to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Since the dead spirits crisis, the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting had not been held in a long time.","For the past ten years, every member of the Astronomical Parliament had grown to varying degrees.","Lin Yuan felt it was high time to hold an Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting.","Liu Jie had helped Wen Yu, Gu Lang, Zong Ze, and the rest of his friends increase their strength, as well as the strength of the Radiance Federation’s royalty.","However, Lin Yuan had not helped any of the members of the Astronomical Parliament increase their strength, even members like Su Yiren and Bei Xu, whom he intended to take with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Lin Yuan did this because he wanted to give them time to grow.","After all the growth they had gone through, they were now clearer about the choices they were going to make.","Lin Yuan never felt that the members of the Astronomical Parliament he nurtured needed to follow in his footsteps.","Take Yin Lin as an example; she was the daughter of the Azure Cloud Leopard family. She was an undeniable elite. Later, she became an Azure Envoy, thereby becoming a key part of the Azure Federation’s future.","She needed to consider carefully before deciding whether she would be heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","If she went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, she might be able to return to the main world, but she would not be able to do so for a very long time.","If Yin Lin truly wanted to head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, she would have to cut off all her ties to the main world.","More than ten years had passed. It was likely that Yin Lin had made her decision about whether she was leaving or staying.","This Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting would be both a welcoming of the members and also a goodbye to the members who would not be going to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","...","When Lin Yuan went to the Radiance Federation, the first thing he did was visit the Moon Empress.","Lin Yuan never verbally expressed his respect toward the Moon Empress. Rather, he demonstrated it through his actions.","Lin Yuan only returned to the Return from Faraway Mansion half a day after staying in the Radiant Moon Palace.","Wen Yu and Liu Jie were waiting there.","When Wen Yu made the suggestion, she knew that Lin Yuan would agree to hold the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting.","While the members of the Astronomical Parliament were communicating with Wen Yu, even Su Yiren, who was the most composed of the group, asked Wen Yu for information.","Wen Yu knew that Su Yiren and the rest were afraid Lin Yuan would abandon them when he departed.","Lin Yuan had been too busy in the past ten years. Hence, his communication with Wen Yu and Liu Jie was no longer as intimate as it used to be.","Thus, it was inevitable for the members of the Astronomical Parliament who relied on Lin Yuan to lose a sense of security.","After all, they were not like Liu Jie and Wen Yu, who were the backbone of Sky City and were helping Lin Yuan to manage Sky City. The two of them knew Lin Yuan would take them with him to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","However, Su Yiren, Bei Xu, and the rest did not have this confidence.","Wen Yu had yet to respond to their covert questions because it should be Lin Yuan who made the decision and not her.","Wen Yu would never make a decision on Lin Yuan’s behalf.","In truth, Wen Yu could not be fully certain of Lin Yuan’s decision.","Lin Yuan did have the ability to help spirit qi professionals increase their strength, but he had yet to use this ability on Sky City’s other members.","It was likely that this Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting would allow many of Lin Yuan’s decisions to come to light.","Among the Astronomical Parliament’s members, Wen Yu believed that Lin Yuan would most likely take only Su Yiren, Bei Xu, and Luo Lan with him.","If this was more than ten years ago, Wen Yu would only be certain that Peace and Ta Lei would not be heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","But now, she had added Yin Lin, Bu Po, and Wo Lun to the list.","For Yin Lin, it was because she had become increasingly focused on the Azure Federation. She was stuck between her family’s honor and responsibility. Hence, she had no choice but to make such a decision.","As one grew older, they also matured. Yin Lin was no exception.","In terms of her decision-making, Yin Lin was becoming increasingly similar to Xia Qing.","Wen Yu greatly respected Yin Lin’s decision, albeit it would cause her to lose the opportunity to transform.","Bu Po’s obsession with his sister was becoming clearer by the day. If he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would definitely ask Lin Yuan to take his sister as well.","Unfortunately, Bu Po’s sister did not have any spirit qi professional potential and was a regular person.","Bu Po had once asked Wen Yu for a Lifespan Mouse for his sister, but Wen Yu had turned him down."]},{"number":2799,"title":"Chapter 2799 Listen’s Growth!","paragraphs":["2799 Listen’s Growth!","It was likely that Bu Po’s life goal would be to live peacefully in the main world with his sister.","A regular person had a lifespan of around 130 years. Bu Po still had around 80 to 90 years of life left to enjoy with his sister.","Bu Po was currently the ruler of the Spirit Mother Federation.","From previous matters, Lin Yuan learned that the Spirit Mother Federation had been under Tarot Round Table’s control.","After Lin Yuan killed all the Tarot members, there was nothing in the Spirit Mother Federation that could restrict Bu Po.","If Bu Po was willing to give resources to his sister, she might be able to use the previous spiritual ingredients to live to 200 years of age.","Once Bu Po’s sister came to the end of her lifespan, it was likely that Bu Po would want to go to the Sky Beyond the Clouds with Lin Yuan.","However, it was impossible for Lin Yuan to wait until then for Bu Po.","As for Wo Lun, he was completely focused on constructing boats.","At first, Wo Lun remained in the Radiance Federation to upgrade the fleet of boats continuously. It was only when the boats were upgraded to a certain degree that Wo Lun pivoted to building his own fleet.","For the past few years, Wo Lun had spent his time traveling everywhere. He had not forgotten his original dream and was still a passionate sailor.","Given his personality, it was more suitable for him to remain in the main world than head to the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Wo Lun’s knowledge about building boats was very useful in the main world. But once he went to the Sky Beyond the Clouds, he would lose the direction he could develop toward.","Peace had indeed experienced growth in the past few years, but her growth was restricted to the Green Continent Federation.","In the past few years, she had secretly reached out to Lin Yuan for help twice. Both times, he had decided to help her.","With Lin Yuan’s help, the Green Continent Federation had managed to gain a stable footing in the main world. But as for where it was going in the future, it would fully depend on Peace’s governance and the federation’s luck!","Once Ta Lei expanded Thick Soil City, he could no longer continue carrying out the duties of the City Lord on his own.","Lin Yuan had sent Qin Lun to help and support Ta Lei.","Lin Yuan would be bringing both Qin Lun and Qin Yu to the Sky Beyond the Clouds and had already helped Qin Lun reach the birth horoscope level.","It was likely that Lin Yuan would give Ta Lei new tasks during this Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting.","This was not because Lin Yuan had any negative opinions against Ta Lei.","Rather, with Ta Lei’s lack of abilities and talent, Lin Yuan would have to come up with alternative arrangements for the entire Thick Soil City once he took Qin Lun away.","Thick Soil City was vital to the entire Startling Lines Continent.","Lin Yuan had thought about nurturing Ta Lei.","While Qin Lun helped Ta Lei manage Thick Soil City, he also became Ta Lei’s role model.","Unfortunately, Ta Lei was unable to rise to the occasion.","Rather than being a ruler, Ta Lei was more suited to concentrating on being a Creation Master.","Ta Lei really liked doing research about Creation Master information and was very skilled at it.","Wen Yu liked to think and consider deeply when she approached any issue.","Liu Jie did not think too much because he felt it was fully up to Lin Yuan about who he was going to take with him. As such, the decisions were solely up to him.","The Astronomical Parliament’s members were not of much help to Lin Yuan. Rather, they were the ones who attained endless opportunities from him.","Peace and Ta Lei were restricted by their abilities and could not create any value for Lin Yuan in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","...","Wen Yu did not hold the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting immediately after Lin Yuan returned. Rather, she first sent out an announcement to the Astronomical Parliament’s members so they could be prepared.","This would also make it easier for them to interact with Lin Yuan when the meeting began.","They would be holding the next Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting in the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Wen Yu would abandon the members in the main world, and they would no longer be able to hold their contracts to the north star constellation seats.","Lin Yuan intended to properly rest in the Return from Faraway Mansion for a few days.","He had expended an enormous amount using his body composition to evolve Sky Sea.","In the past year or so, Lin Yuan had not rested apart from sleeping and eating.","...","Lin Yuan only rested for a day before he received a message from Long Tao on the Thoughts Letter Paper.","[Long Tao]: Ah Yuan, I have already given a new batch of the dragon lungs to Listen. Dark Clouds Bird Shrine has also prepared the essence blood of various phoenix-species feys. The dragon lungs weigh more than two tonnes. After this batch of dragon lungs, I won’t be able to provide you with a new batch for a long time!","Long Tao had been working with Lin Yuan for a long time.","In order to increase Shiny’s power as soon as possible, Lin Yuan had provided Long Tao with numerous resources during their partnership. This increased the scale of Long Tao’s cultivation of dragon-species feys.","The lungs of dragon-species feys were the best when they were young. It was also during that period they contained the most energy.","Hence, Long Tao slaughtered the dragon-species feys once they reached that age.","Long Tao had cultivated a batch of standard dragon-species feys. Once he slaughtered them, it would be a few years before he could cultivate a new batch of such dragon-species feys.","Listen had been helping Lin Yuan communicate with Long Tao ever since he returned to the Radiance Federation.","When Lin Yuan read he would be able to obtain over 200 tonnes of dragon lungs and that Dark Clouds Bird Shrine would definitely provide him with a considerable amount of phoenix blood, he knew that Shiny would be able to increase its power quickly once it absorbed them.","Lin Yuan intended to take these two days of rest to nurture the Sovereign/Creation Shiny.","...","Lin Yuan arrived at the breeding room and released Shiny.","At that moment, Shiny was much more heroic than it was when it was Myth Breed. With each flap of its wings, it gave off an inexplicable air of elegance and strength.","Feys with the Barren bloodline had a unique aura of sharpness and carnage. No other feys had such an aura.","Lin Yuan highly valued a fey like Shiny that represented the legacy of the Radiance Federation. Otherwise, he would not have held back from increasing Shiny’s power just because he lacked suitable dragon lungs and phoenix blood.","Lin Yuan used True Data to check on Shiny.","[Fey Name]: Golden Wings","[Fey Species]: Barren-species/feather-winged-species","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Wind","[Fey Quality]: Creation IX","Abilities:","[Snapped Neck Falling Death]: When its sharp claws make contact with a target, the target’s neck will be snapped. At the same time, the Golden Wings will extract the target’s soul and absorb it into its feathers. The soul will imbue the storm patterns on the feathers with intelligence.","[Flowing Wind Claws]: When the wind elements in the Golden Wings’ feathers are released into the environment, it will be able to control the surrounding winds and manipulate them to attack its opponent. The attacked target will feel as if it is being slashed by claws. After attacking a target, the Golden Wings will also be able to inject wind-elemental energy into its target through explosions and cause double the amount of damage.","[Rapid Wind Whistle]: By flapping its wings to activate wind-elemental energy, it will simultaneously let out a roar that causes both physical and elemental damage to a designated target. A headwind will also lower the target’s speed. Each time a headwind is released, its own speed will be increased.","[Hurricane Added Protection]: A vicious hurricane shield will be added to its own body. Every time elemental damage is inflicted on it, the hurricane shield will absorb the damage before reflecting it. The hurricane shield can also absorb wind-elemental energy from the surroundings to replenish the wind-elemental energy in its body.","[Folded Wings Wind Valley]: With the Golden Wings at the center, an environment charged with wind-elemental energy will be formed. Wind-elemental energy will be continuously produced in this environment. When it makes a sacrifice to this territory, the wind-elemental energy will be absorbed into its bloodline and trigger a one-time explosion.","[Disappearing Wind Attack]: Its body will be combined with wind elements. Even a slight breeze will be enough for it to hide within. While it is hiding in the wind, it will be immune to damage as long as the wind remains.","[Revived Seasonal Winds]: The wind elements’ state will be changed. The wind elements will gain powerful healing abilities. Targets will be healed wherever the winds exist. They will continue to heal as long as the wind does not stop moving.","[Swift Wind Death]: The sharpness of wind elements will be activated. The wind elements will change into wild winds that will continuously attack the target until the target has been ground to pieces. The sharpness of the wind elements will have Flowing Wind Claws’ tearing effects and Snapped Neck Falling Death’s bone-breaking effects.","Exclusive Skill:","[Unset State]: When interacting with another fey, the Golden Wings can copy the fey’s exclusive skill and triggered abilities. Unset State will then turn into the copied exclusive skill and triggered ability. The abilities can only be switched out once every lunar cycle.","[Wind’s Descendant]: By placing itself as the heart of all wind elements, it will become the eye of a hurricane and control all surrounding wind elements. It will become the master, while all other winds will become its disciples.","[Summoning Wind Changing Spirit]: Use wind elements to accommodate other elemental energy and turn them into vassals of the wind elements. In extreme environments, the accommodated elemental energy can change its attributes and allow it to become better affiliated with the environment, as well as use elemental attacks of different types.","[Whirling Wind Compression]: Use the energy in its body to compress and coordinate wind-elemental energy. The wind elements will be tightly locked together and will resonate. Its ability to control wind elements will be stronger than that of the natural environment, and it will become stronger at controlling wind elements in different environments. The power of its abilities and exclusive skills related to wind will also be strengthened.","Shiny had gained a new ability called Swift Wind Death and an exclusive skill called Whirling Wind Compression.","Swift Wind Death strengthened Shiny’s attacking abilities.","Shiny’s previous abilities were too balanced and caused Shiny’s combat abilities to be weaker than those of traditional feys with the Barren bloodline.","But now, Swift Wind Death’s existence raised Shiny’s combat abilities.","Swift Wind Death triggered the sharpness of wind elements. While continuously attacking targets, it would have the tearing effects of Flowing Wind Claws and the bone-breaking effects of Snapped Neck Falling Death.","Hence, when Swift Wind Death was attacking targets, it would cause targets to suffer attacks on different levels. It was considered an all-rounded combat skill.","Whirling Wind Compression could be seen as an ability that comprehensively boosted Shiny.","Whirling Wind Compression involved Shiny using its abilities to compress wind elements and improve their quality. Hence, all of Shiny’s wind-related abilities would be boosted. This would enable every single one of Shiny’s abilities and exclusive skills to become stronger!","Shiny could be seen as the model standard of a fey with comprehensive abilities.","However, as Lin Yuan’s power grew, functional-type feys became increasingly important to him.","When Lin Yuan contracted feys, he tried his best to contract functional-type ones.","Shiny’s Unset State allowed it to become a functional-type fey. It used Unset State to replicate the ability Sacrifice and was considered a life-preservation technique for Lin Yuan.","After letting Shiny out, Lin Yuan played with it for a while.","He had just arranged the dragon lungs and phoenix blood in the breeding room for Shiny when Listen arrived at the Return from Faraway Mansion.","In the past ten years, Lin Yuan had increased Listen’s power to the Divine Kingdom level and Listen’s three feys had reached World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","Although Listen was not one of Sky City’s three main pillars of support, he was just as valuable as Liu Jie and Wen Yu.","Listen was the one who organized and generated all of Sky City’s resources.","Back then, in preparation for the dead spirits crisis, the Radiance Federation had immediately organized all the materials needed to build the defense bases and sent them to the right locations.","This also applied to the construction of the dimensional wall.","This organization of resources allowed Lin Yuan to carry out many tasks smoothly.","Without someone like Listen working for him, Lin Yuan would never be able to be a hands-off manager.","In the past decade, Lin Yuan had not only increased his strength but also his abilities.","After the dead spirits crisis ended, there were many messy and starving federations in the main world. A large-scale death of their populations was avoided because Listen had sent out the Soldier Ration Radishes to them.","When Listen saw Lin Yuan, he bowed and said seriously, “Young Master, Long Tao gave me a batch of resources for you to use to nurture Shiny. I have brought them with me.”","Listen had not seen Lin Yuan in almost two years.","Listen was always aware of his position before Lin Yuan and saw himself as his servant.","Listen handed the fey storage box containing the dragon lungs and phoenix blood to Lin Yuan.","Lin Yuan received the Diamond fey storage box before patting Listen’s shoulder. “Listen, we will be heading to the Sky Beyond the Clouds soon. That will be your new battleground. For now, distribute the resources I’m about to give you before taking a good rest!”","Listen looked touched when he heard what Lin Yuan said.","Logically, now that Lin Yuan was about to leave the main world, he should be doing all he could to collect the main world’s resources for his own use. However, Lin Yuan did not do so. Instead, he was going to give the main world one last boost before he left.","Lin Yuan’s spirit had never changed, regardless of when they first met or now that he had risen to the peak of the main world. His soul was just as clean as it had always been."]},{"number":2800,"title":"Chapter 2800 Sacred Golden Wind Nest!","paragraphs":["2800 Sacred Golden Wind Nest!","Listen was Lin Yuan’s manager when it came to resources. He knew better than anyone how Lin Yuan’s resources were allocated.","If Lin Yuan had given him these resources, he would have been able to turn them into unimaginable riches.","Listen asked himself if he could do the same if he were in Lin Yuan’s position, and he knew that he could not.","His fate was changed when he swore to Lin Yuan on his Willpower Rune.","At that time, he had been blindly trying to keep the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce afloat.","At that time, the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce had not even been a rising faction and had been under the thumb of the Zheng family’s third lineage.","His life had even been endangered.","It was all because his ancestors had bought a large piece of land near the shallow sea that hindered the Zheng family’s third lineage’s development.","After Listen joined Lin Yuan’s camp and watched Lin Yuan’s growth, he became fully aware of how Sky City had grown step by step into such a gargantuah entity under Lin Yuan’s management.","Back then, Lin Yuan had been hiding the fact that he was the Moon Empress’ disciple and hat single-handedly helped him to take on the Zheng family.","During that process, Lin Yuan had done a lot for him.","This was because the Zheng family had also been connected to the top faction Connected Beast Park.","Listen did not believe that he was valuable enough to warrant taking on a top faction.","All that he had today came from Lin Yuan.","Listen never denied his talent.","But without the opportunities that came from Lin Yuan, he would never be able to accomplish such training with his own abilities.","Listen was genuinely grateful to Lin Yuan. Because of Lin Yuan, Listen’s horizons were continuously expanded, and his dreams were continuously broadened.","At first, he wanted to continue developing the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce. Then, he wanted to develop the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce from a veteran to a top faction. Now, he wanted to expand the Listening Heron Chamber of Commerce beyond the Radiance Federation’s borders.","He started by helping Lin Yuan organize the Startling Lines Continent’s resources. Eventually, he began allocating the resources of the entire main world. Now, Lin Yuan was setting his sights on the Sky Beyond the Clouds.","Listen was very willing to help Lin Yuan overcome obstacles in the Sky Beyond the Clouds and be the best subordinate he could be.","“There are some federations with very problematic internal affairs. These problems are the real reasons for their terrible conditions. Some of these issues are linked to the foundations of these federations and can’t be fixed manually. These federations will eventually disappear into history. The Green Island Federation that you asked me to look after is also experiencing such problems.”","Lin Yuan had indeed asked Listen to look after the Green Continent Federation. However, Lin Yuan did not understand its true condition.","Lin Yuan was busy every day and did not have the energy to spend on other matters.","Lin Yuan nodded at Listen to signal to him to continue talking.","The Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting was going to be held tomorrow.","Listen did not have a good impression of Peace. He saw her as a classic black sheep.","At first, Wen Yu had helped Peace a few times. Then, he helped her several times too. However, she did not improve in the slightest. Peace also participated in the Major Federation Union meetings of recent years.","The Moon Empress had given the federations advice during the Major Federation Meetings, but it was clear that Peace had not taken the Moon Empress’ words to heart.","At first, the Green Continent Federation had encountered geographic issues that restricted their development.","Later, the Green Continent Federation moved into a better area and started relying on a federation with a Class 5 Creation Master.","Peace intentionally revealed her relationship with Lin Yuan.","Regardless of whether she did it to protect the Green Continent Federation, this crossed the line in Listen’s mind.","If Peace had not done this, the Green Continent Federation’s land would already have been taken over by the surrounding federations.","All of the main world’s federations had offered themselves to Lin Yuan. The same went for the Green Continent Federation.","However, the Green Continent Federation not only worshipped Lin Yuan but also Peace.","Peace was still the self-proclaimed Green Continent Goddess.","Listen knew a significant amount about the Broiling Rock Continent’s situation.","In a location where water was scarce, water sources were linked to survival.","Peace could use her own abilities to create water.","But now, the area where the Green Continent Federation was located experienced rain frequently.","It was a joke that Peace was continuing to call herself the Green Continent Goddess!","Listen always felt that Peace let Lin Yuan down.","Lin Yuan sighed in regret to himself when he heard Listen describe the situation.","As someone who had experience, Lin Yuan felt that Peace’s problems were linked to a lack of proper education. Lin Yuan chatted idly with Listen for a while. Liu Jie prepared lunch specially for Listen.","Liu Jie and Wen Yu had become increasingly impressed with Listen over the years. They had a very good relationship with each other.","Listen immediately began distributing the resources while Lin Yuan took the dragon lungs and phoenix blood with him back to the breeding room to continue nurturing Shiny.","It was only with dragon lungs, phoenix blood, and wind-elemental energy that Shiny’s absorption of spirit qi quickened.","With the support from Lin Yuan’s body composition, Shiny’s power grew quickly.","At first, Lin Yuan only intended to evolve Shiny to a certain extent and continue evolving it after the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting.","During the nurturing process, Lin Yuan suddenly realized that Shiny’s bloodline had changed.","This meant that Shiny’s bloodline could be evolved.","The lower a fey’s grade, the easier it would be for its bloodline to mutate.","It was difficult for a fey’s bloodline to continue mutating once its power reached Suzerain/Creation.","Once such an opportunity appeared, it had to be grabbed. Otherwise, it would slip away extremely easily.","Hence, Lin Yuan decided to push back the Astronomical Parliament parliamentary meeting and focus on Shiny’s evolution first!","During Shiny’s evolution, its appetite was not affected because of the evolution. Instead, the evolution of its bloodline required a large amount of energy, and its consumption of food increased.","Lin Yuan saw that every single one of Shiny’s feathers had turned translucent.","Lin Yuan had conducted experiments and found out that the feathers that were enveloped by rapidly moving winds not only did not lower Shiny’s defensive abilities but raised its defensive and attacking abilities.","Shiny’s size had not changed significantly, but its claws had become sharper.","The golden gusts of wind around the claws were a form of extremely high-level wind elements. It was a technique that came from Shiny’s transformation of its bloodline.","Lin Yuan evolved Shiny to World Emperor/Divine Kingdom.","Spring helped Lin Yuan to complete Shiny’s evolution.","Lin Yuan looked at Shiny that was enveloped in wind and used True Data to check on it.","Morbius had already reached the Startling Lines Continent and was helping Lin Yuan to collect spirit qi crystals.","Although Morbius was not by his side, Lin Yuan could still use its abilities.","[Fey Name]: Golden Wings","[Fey Species]: Barren-species/feather-winged-species","[Fey Grade]: Sovereign (10/10)","[Fey Type]: Wind","[Fey Quality]: Elementary Divine Kingdom","[Divine Kingdom Grade]: Miniature","Abilities:","[Snapped Neck Falling Death]: When its sharp claws make contact with a target, the target’s neck will be snapped. Simultaneously, the Golden Wings will extract the target’s soul and absorb it into its feathers. The soul will imbue the storm patterns on the feathers with intelligence.","[Flowing Wind Claws]: When the wind elements in the Golden Wings’ feathers are released into the environment, it will be able to control the surrounding winds and manipulate them to attack its opponent. The attacked target will feel as if it is being slashed by claws. After attacking a target, the Golden Wings will also inject wind element into its target through explosions, causing double the amount of damage.","[Rapid Wind Whistle]: By flapping its wings to activate wind-elemental energy, it will simultaneously emit a roar that inflicts both physical and elemental damage on a designated target. A headwind will also lower the target’s speed. Each time a headwind is released, its own speed will increase.","[Hurricane Added Protection]: A vicious hurricane shield will be added to its own body. Every time elemental damage is inflicted on it, the hurricane shield will absorb the damage before reflecting it. The hurricane shield can also absorb wind-elemental energy from the surroundings to replenish the wind-elemental energy in its body.","[Folded Wings Wind Valley]: With the Golden Wings at the center, an environment charged with wind-elemental energy will be formed. Wind-elemental energy will be continuously produced in this environment. When it makes a sacrifice to this territory, the wind-elemental energy will be absorbed into its bloodline and trigger a one-time explosion.","[Disappearing Wind Attack]: Its body will be combined with wind elements. Even a slight breeze will be enough for it to hide within. While it is hiding in the wind, it will be immune to damage as long as the wind remains.","[Revived Seasonal Winds]: The wind elements’ state will change. The wind elements will gain powerful healing abilities. Targets will be healed wherever the winds exist. They will continue to heal as long as the wind does not stop moving.","[Swift Wind Death]: The sharpness of wind elements will be activated. The wind elements will change into wild winds that will continuously attack the target until the target has been ground to pieces. The sharpness of the wind elements will have Flowing Wind Claws’ tearing effects and Snapped Neck Falling Death’s bone-breaking effects.","[Elemental Sword Feathers]: All the feathers will be elementalized. The pure elemental traits in the feathers will be activated. When the feathers are attacked and damaged, the wind flowing in the environment will naturally replenish the feathers. The feathers can be shot into the outside world and will have penetrating effects.","[Sacred Golden Wind]: All the wind elements under its control will be transformed into sacred gold wind. The sacred gold wind will go beyond the regular elemental state. The lowest elemental state will have damaging and immunity effects.","Exclusive Skill:","[Unset State]: When interacting with another fey, the Golden Wings can copy the fey’s exclusive skill and triggered abilities. Unset State will then turn into the copied exclusive skill and triggered ability. The abilities can only be switched out once every lunar cycle.","[Wind’s Descendant]: By placing itself as the heart of all wind elements, it will become the eye of a hurricane and control all of the surrounding wind elements. It will become the master, while all other winds will become its disciples.","[Summoning Wind Changing Spirit]: Use wind elements to accommodate other elemental energy and turn them into vassals of the wind elements. In extreme environments, the accommodated elemental energy can change its own attributes and allow it to become better affiliated with the environment as well as use elemental attacks of different elemental types.","[Whirling Wind Compression]: Use the energy in its body to compress and coordinate wind-elemental energy. The wind elements will be tightly locked together and will resonate. Its ability to control wind elements will be stronger than that of the natural environment, and it will become stronger at controlling wind elements in different elements. The power of its abilities and exclusive skills related to wind will also be strengthened.","[Golden Wind Enters Body]: The sacred golden wind will be absorbed into the body and be used to change the body. The sacred wind will transform into commanding wind elements and will be able to suppress all inferior wind elements. In the transformed state, it will be able to comprehensively increase its energy and the characteristics it controls.","[Wind Territory Release]: The sacred golden energy will be released into the surrounding environment. The environment filled with the sacred golden wind will be under its control, and the wind territory under its control will suppress lifeforms of other types. Each suppressed target will lead to an increase in the wind speed of the sacred golden wind in the wind territory.","Divine Kingdom Abilities:","[Sacred Golden Wind Nest]: A large nest of faith power will be created in the divine kingdom. The sacred golden wind can be released from the body in the nest and condensed into sacred golden wind crystals.","Lin Yuan frowned slightly when he saw Shiny’s data.","The description of Shiny’s divine kingdom ability, Sacred Golden Wind Nest, was far too simple.","Although Sacred Golden Wind Nest was a production-type divine kingdom ability and was considered a highly treasured divine kingdom ability, Lin Yuan was uncertain of the value of the sacred golden wind crystals.","When Spring was done helping Shiny to fend off the world wills, she said to Lin Yuan in amazement, “Lord Saint, I never expected your Barren beast to be given such an opportunity! Sacred Golden Wind is an extremely rare element of utmost purity.","“Absolutely pure elements won’t be eroded and can nourish any wind-type lifeform. It is considered a treasure of the highest form. It will do wonders for the bloodline evolutions of wind-type bird-species lifeforms.","“If you are willing to use your fey to create a large number of sacred golden wind crystals, you will definitely be able to create a thriving bird species in the Sky Beyond the Clouds. The bird species might not be able to make it into the top 100 of the Species Ranking immediately, but it will definitely enter the top 1,000!”"]}]);
